  "npc.wentworth.here_you_are_26": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_27": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.well_can_i_28": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.would_you_like_29": "Would you like to change your platinum coins into gold or crystal?",
  "npc.wentworth.how_many_platinum_30": "How many platinum coins would you like to change into gold?",
  "npc.wentworth.how_many_crystal_31": "How many crystal coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.wentworth.well_can_i_32": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_33": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.so_you_would_34": "So you would like me to change ",
  "npc.wentworth.here_you_are_35": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_36": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.well_can_i_37": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_38": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.so_you_would_39": "So you would like me to change ",
  "npc.wentworth.here_you_are_40": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_41": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.well_can_i_42": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.how_many_crystal_43": "How many crystal coins would you like to change into platinum?",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_44": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.so_you_would_45": "So you would like me to change ",
  "npc.wentworth.here_you_are_46": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.sorry_you_do_47": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.well_can_i_48": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.willard.thank_you_i_1": "Thank you, I appreciate it. Don't forget to mention the package to Snake.",
  "npc.woblin.you_bring_me_1": "You bring me Old Nasty?",
  "npc.wyda.you_brought_me_1": "You brought me a cookie?",
  "npc.wyda.arrr_here_we_2": "Arrr... here we go again.... do you have a #$*§# blood herb for me?",
  "npc.wyda.you_have_no_3": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.wyda.well_its_a_4": "Well, it's a welcome change from all that gingerbread ... AHHH HOW DARE YOU??? FEEL MY WRATH!",
  "npc.wyda.thank_you_sooo_5": "Thank you -SOOO- much! No, I really mean it! Really! Here, let me give you a reward...",
  "npc.wyda.thank_you_sooo_6": "Thank you -SOOO- much! No, I really mean it! Really! Ah, you know what, you can have this old thing...",
  "npc.wyda.no_you_dont_7": "No, you don't have any...",
  "npc.wyrdin.do_you_have_1": "Do you have the papers I asked you for with you?",
  "npc.wyrdin.oh_marvellous_please_2": "Oh marvellous, please excuse me. I need to read this text immediately. Here, take this small reward of 500 gold pieces for your efforts.",
  "npc.wyrdin.ive_heard_some_3": "I've heard some odd rumours about this new dwarven outpost. But tell me, what has the Edron academy to do with Farmine?",
  "npc.wyrdin.im_not_sure_4": "I'm not sure if I'm in the mood to talk about that matter again. Or do you have anything that might change my mind?",
  "npc.wyrdin.hm_you_are_5": "Hm, you are right, we are at the forefront of knowledge and innovation. Our dwarven friends could learn much from one of our representatives.",
  "npc.wyrdin.sighs_okay_sending_6": "<sighs> Okay, sending some trader there won't hurt. I hope it will be worth the effort, though.",
  "npc.wyrdin.what_do_you_7": "What do you mean the druids of Carlin could provide the service as well? They are incompetent imposters! I will not allow them to ruin our reputation! I'll send some trader with supplies right away!",
  "npc.wyrdin.hm_you_are_8": "Hm, you are right, we are at the forefront of knowledge and innovation. Our dwarven friends could learn much from one of our representatives.",
  "npc.wyrdin.wrong_word_9": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.xelvar.right_now_i_1": "Right now I am sort of {recruiting} people.",
  "npc.xelvar.you_already_talked_2": "You already talked with me.",
  "npc.xelvar.ok_so_listen_3": "Ok, so listen. Your help is needed. That is if you're the hero type. Our ... {partners} need some help in urgent matters.",
  "npc.xelvar.i_guess_the_4": "I guess the time of secrecy is over now. Well, we have an old alliance with another underground dwelling race, the {gnomes}.",
  "npc.xodet.so_you_ask_1": "So you ask me for a {",
  "npc.xodet.what_i_have_2": "What? I have already gave you one {",
  "npc.xodet.sorry_you_arent_3": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.xodet.here_you_are_4": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.xodet.of_course_just_5": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.xorlosh.hmmmm_you_could_1": "Hmmmm, you could indeed help me. See this mechanism? Some son of a rotworm put WAY too much stuff on this elevator and now it's broken. I need 3 gear wheels to fix it. You think you could get them for me?",
  "npc.xorlosh.holy_mother_of_2": "HOLY MOTHER OF ALL ROTWORMS! You did it and they are of even better quality than the old ones. You should be the first one to try the elevator, just jump on it. See you my friend.",
  "npc.xorlosh.that_would_be_3": "That would be great! Maybe a blacksmith can forge you some. Come back when you got them and ask me about your mission.",
  "npc.xorlosh.the_book_about_4": "The book about tunnelling is in the library which is located in the north eastern wing of Beregar city.",
  "npc.yalahari.so_you_have_1": "So you have killed the plague carriers. Have you also retrieved the research papers? ",
  "npc.yalahari.this_will_teach_2": "This will teach these fishmen who is the ruler of that area. You have earned yourself a special privilege. But we will talk about that when we speak about your next mission. ",
  "npc.yalahari.your_failure_is_3": "Your failure is an outrage! I think we have to talk about the missions you have accomplished so far. ",
  "npc.yalahari.now_we_will_4": "Now we will have power we truly deserve!...",
  "npc.yalahari.so_do_you_5": "So do you want to side with me |PLAYERNAME|? ",
  "npc.yalahari.great_work_take_6": "Great work, take this outfit and you are able to open the door to the reward room.",
  "npc.yalahari.impressive_indeed_someone_7": "Impressive indeed! Someone with your skills will quickly raise in our ranks of helpers. You have great potential, and if you are upfor further missions, just ask for them. ",
  "npc.yalahari.i_knew_that_8": "I knew that you were smart enough to make the right decision! Your next mission will be a special one! ",
  "npc.yaman.shove_off_little_1": "Shove off, little one! Humans are not welcome here, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.yaman.be_greeted_human_2": "Be greeted, human |PLAYERNAME|. How can a humble djinn be of service?",
  "npc.yaman.do_you_want_3": "Do you want to trade Boots of haste for Enchanted Chicken Wing?",
  "npc.yaman.do_you_want_4": "Do you want to trade 4 Warrior Helmet for Warrior Sweat?",
  "npc.yaman.do_you_want_5": "Do you want to trade 2 Royal Helmet for Fighting Spirit",
  "npc.yaman.do_you_want_6": "Do you want to trade 3 Fire Sword for Magic Sulphur",
  "npc.yaman.i_trade_enchanted_7": "I trade Enchanted Chicken Wing for Boots of Haste, Warrior Sweat for 4 Warrior Helmets, Fighting Spirit for 2 Royal Helmet Magic Sulphur for 3 Fire Swords",
  "npc.yaman.you_brought_cookies_8": "You brought cookies! How nice of you! Can I have one?",
  "npc.yaman.here_you_are_9": "Here you are.",
  "npc.yaman.sorry_but_you_10": "Sorry but you don't have the item.",
  "npc.yaman.you_have_no_11": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.yaman.you_see_good_12": "You see, good deeds like this will ... YOU ... YOU SPAWN OF EVIL! I WILL MAKE SURE THE MASTER LEARNS ABOUT THIS!",
  "npc.yaman.im_sorry_but_13": "I'm sorry, but you don't have Malor's permission to trade with me.",
  "npc.yana.if_you_have_1": "If you have any gold tokens with you, let's have a look! These are my offers.",
  "npc.yana.there_it_is_2": "There it is.",
  "npc.yana.im_sorry_but_3": "I'm sorry but it seems you don't have enough ",
  "npc.yana.you_dont_have_4": "You don't have enough capacity. You must have ",
  "npc.yana.your_decision_come_5": "Your decision. Come back if you have changed your mind.",
  "npc.yasir.tje_hari_ku_1": "Tje hari ku ne finjala. {Ariki}?",
  "npc.yasir.soso_yana_shakes_2": "Soso yana. <shakes his head>",
  "npc.zalamon.what_newzz_do_1": "What newzz do you bring? Did you find any cluezz about zzeir whereaboutzz? ",
  "npc.zalamon.ah_you_have_2": "Ah you have returned. I azzume you already found zzome itemzz to build a proper dizzguizze? ",
  "npc.zalamon.zzo_you_finished_3": "Zzo... you finished him. Show me hizz head, will you? ",
  "npc.zalamon.you_azzembled_zze_4": "You - azzembled zze zzeptre? Hand it out, give it to me, will you? ",
  "npc.zalamon.ah_i_zzee_5": "Ah I zzee. You are ready for your mizzion and waiting for me to create and mark zze crate? ",
  "npc.zalamon.zze_emperor_of_6": "Zze emperor of zze dragonzz hazz tranzzformed himzzelf into an undead creature to lazzt for all eternity, to cheat deazz. Hizz corruption flowzz to zzozze he bound, and from zzem to zzozze zzey bound, and from zzem into zze land.",
  "npc.zalamon.be_warned_zze_7": "Be warned. Zze mountain pazzezz have been dezzerted for zzeveral weekzz now. No one made it acrozz and I fear you won't meet a zzingle friendly zzoul up zzere.",
  "npc.zalamon.exzztraordinary_we_are_8": "Exzztraordinary. We are mozzt fortunate to have zzezze documentzz in our handzz now. Zzizz would zzertainly help me to build an effective rezzizztanzze. Will you give zzem to me? ",
  "npc.zalamon.ive_marked_itzz_9": "I've marked itzz location on your map. Go and find out what happened zzere. In zze pazzt it wazz known azz zze Temple of Equilibrium. ",
  "npc.zalamon.zzizz_izz_not_10": "Zzizz izz not hizz head but clearly belonged to zze keeper. I - I am imprezzed. You can go now. Leave me alone for a zzecond. ",
  "npc.zalamon.finally_at_lazzt_11": "Finally. At lazzt. Zze zzeptre izz - ourzz. Ourzz of courzze. A weapon we should uzze wizzely for our cauzze. I need a zzecond or two. Do you leave me already? ",
  "npc.zarifan.tell_methe_first_1": "...Tell me...the first... magic word.",
  "npc.zarifan.yes_yes_friendship_2": "Yes... YES... friendship... now... second word?",
  "npc.zarifan.yes_yes_friendship_3": "Yes... YES... friendship... lives... now third word?",
  "npc.zarifan.continue_with_your_4": "...continue with your mission...",
  "npc.zebron.hmmm_would_you_1": "Hmmm, would you like to play for {money} or for a chance to win your own {dice}?",
  "npc.zebron.i_am_sorry_2": "I am sorry, but you don't have so much money.",
  "npc.zebron.ok_here_we_3": "Ok, here we go ... ",
  "npc.zebron.ok_here_we_4": "Ok, here we go ... 6! You have won a dice, congratulations. One more game?",
  "npc.zebron.so_you_care_5": "So you care for a civilized game of dice?",
  "npc.zebron.i_thought_so_6": "I thought so. Okay, I will roll a dice. If it shows 6, you will get five times your bet. How much do you want to bet?",
  "npc.zebron.hehe_good_choice_7": "Hehe, good choice. Okay, the price for this game is 100 gold pieces. I will roll a dice. If I roll a 6, you can have my dice. Agreed?",
  "npc.zebron.i_am_sorry_8": "I am sorry, but I accept only bets between 1 and 99 gold. I don't want to ruin you after all. How much do you want to bet?",
  "npc.zebron.i_am_sorry_9": "I am sorry, but you don't have so much money.",
  "npc.zebron.ok_here_we_10": "Ok, here we go ... ",
  "npc.zebron.ok_here_we_11": "Ok, here we go ... 6! You have won ",
  "npc.zebron.oh_come_on_12": "Oh come on, don't be a child.",
  "npc.zirella.by_the_way_1": "By the way, 'quest' is a keyword that many NPCs react to, especially those which have tasks for you. So darling, about that {quest}... are you listening?",
  "npc.zirella.thank_you_so_2": "Thank you so much for your kindness. I'm an old woman and I desperately need firewood for my oven. Could you please help me?",
  "npc.zirella.youre_such_a_3": "You're such a treasure. In the forest south of here, there are {dead trees} without any leaves. The first thing you have to do is search for one, {okay}?",
  "npc.zirella.splendid_once_youve_4": "Splendid, once you've found one, 'Use' it to break a branch from it. Did you understand that so far?",
  "npc.zirella.good_so_after_5": "Good... so after you broke a branch, please push it here and select 'use with'. That will turn your mouse cursor into crosshairs. Then left-click on my cart. {Alright}?",
  "npc.zirella.to_push_the_6": "To push the branch, drag and drop it on the grass by holding the left mousebutton and moving the cursor to where you want to throw the branch. Just push it near my cart before you 'Use' it, {alright}?",
  "npc.zirella.oh_you_deserve_7": "Oh, you deserve it. You really have earned some experience! Also, you may enter my little house now and take what's in that chest beside my bed. Good {bye} for now!",
  "npc.zirella.well_then_i_8": "Well then, I hope you find nice and dry branches for me! Good {bye}!",
  "npc.zizzle.you_made_it_1": "You made it! Az zoon az you are prepared, I will brief you for your nexzt mizzion. ",
  "npc.zoltan.ah_yenny_the_1": "Ah, Yenny the Gentle was one of the founders of the druid order called Crunor's Caress, that has been originated in her hometown Carlin.",
  "npc.zoltan.a_quite_undruidic_2": "A quite undruidic order of druids they were, as far as we know. I have no more enlightening knowledge about them though.",
  "npc.zoltan.i_cannot_believe_3": "... I cannot believe my eyes. You retrieved this hat from Ferumbras' remains? That is incredible. If you give it to me, I will grant you the right to wear this hat as addon. What do you say?",
  "npc.zoltan.i_bow_to_4": "I bow to you, player, and hereby grant you the right to wear Ferumbras' hat as accessory. Congratulations!",
  "npc.zoltan.sorry_you_dont_5": "Sorry you don't have the Ferumbras' hat.",
  "npc.zoltan.this_task_is_6": "This task is only available for male players who don't already have the addon.",
  "npc.zoltan.stop_bothering_me_7": "Stop bothering me. I am a far too busy man to be constantly giving out awards.",
  "npc.zoltan.what_the_hell_8": "What the hell are you talking about?",
  "npc.zora.do_you_want_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.zora.here_it_is_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.zora.you_dont_have_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.ztiss.you_are_ztill_1": "You are ztill a captive and your life is forfeit. Zere might be a way for you to ezcape if you agree to {work} for my mazter.",
  "npc.zumtah.you_are_searching_1": "You are searching for the way out? Do you want to go home? Are you homesick, nostalgic, allergic? I am sorry. You will stay. Muhahahaha. Haha. Are you giving up then?",
  "npc.zumtah.a_what_i_2": "A what? I don't even know what you're talking about, human. If you aren't just giving up - will you kindly change the topic please?",
  "npc.zumtah.haha_no_no_3": "Haha, no! No. Why don't you just stop asking me that and start enjoying your stay here?",
  "npc.zumtah.oh_you_mean_4": "Oh, you mean - if I have ever been out of here in those 278 years? Well, I - I can't remember. No, I can't remember. Sorry.",
  "npc.zumtah.no_i_really_5": "No, I really can't remember. I enjoyed my stay here so much that I forgot how it looks outside of this hole. Outside. The air, the sky, the light. Oh well... well.",
  "npc.zumtah.its_you_why_6": "It's you, why did they throw you in here again? Anyway, I will just transform you once more. I also recovered your crate which will wait for you at the exit. There, feel free to go.",
  "npc.zumtah.ive_already_told_7": "I've already told you that you can't get out. What's the problem? Do you even see an exit?",
  "npc.zumtah.you_are_starting_8": "You are starting to get on my nerves. Is this the only topic you know?",
  "npc.zumtah.but_there_is_9": "But there is no escape, I said NO. You've already asked several times and my answer will stay the same. What is this? Are you trying to test me?",
  "npc.zumtah.muhahaha_where_i_10": "Muhahaha. Where? I can only see a dark cave with nothing than bones and a djinn in it. You mean that small hole there? Muhahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.pesky_persistent_human_11": "Pesky, persistent human.",
  "npc.zumtah.muhahaha_then_i_12": "Muhahaha. Then I will give you a test. How many years do you think have I been here? {89}, {164} or {278}?",
  "npc.zumtah.correct_human_and_13": "Correct human, and that is not nearly how high you would need to count to tell all the lost souls I've seen dying here. I AM PERPETUAL. Muahahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.wrong_answer_human_14": "Wrong answer human! Muahahaha.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.you_want_trip_1": "You want trip to Izzle of Zzao?",
  "npc.zurak_arena.you_need_permission_2": "You need permission to travel to.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.itzz_done_your_3": "It'zz done your travel to.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.zzoftzzkinzz_zzo_full_4": "Zzoftzzkinzz zzo full of fear.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.me_zzimple_ferryman_5": "Me zzimple ferryman. I arrange {trip} to Zzao.",
  "npc.zurak.you_want_trip_1": "You want trip to Izzle of Zztrife?",
  "npc.zurak.you_need_permission_2": "You need permission to travel to.",
  "npc.zurak.itzz_your_doom_3": "It'zz your doom you travel to.",
  "npc.zurak.zzoftzzkinzz_zzo_full_4": "Zzoftzzkinzz zzo full of fear.",
  "npc.zurak.me_zzimple_ferryman_5": "Me zzimple ferryman. I arrange {trip} to Izzle of Zztrife.",
  "npc.alwin.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.arnold.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.a_starving_dog.munch_1": "<munch>",
  "npc.aurita.then_not_1": "Then not.",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.so_be_it_1": "So be it!",
  "npc.bambi_bonecrusher.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.barbara.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.blossom_bonecrusher.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.busty_bonecrusher.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.christoph.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.then_not_1": "Then not.",
  "npc.demonguard.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.edron_guardsman.move_on_1": "Move on!",
  "npc.fenbala.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.harsky.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.jean_claude.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.stutch.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.taegen.then_not_1": "Then not.",
  "npc.warbert.take_this_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.bertram.oh_my_you_1": "Oh my! You look so great in your uniform! \\z\n\t\t\t\tYou archpostwomen are not only daring but also beautiful. \\z\n\t\t\t\tHere take it, that's the key you wanted. Just promise to visit me now and then!",
  "npc.canary.say_1": "This the our discord group link: {https://discordapp.com/invite/3NxYnyV}",
  "npc.alyxo.say_1": "Could you kill 3 bosses for me?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_2": "Come back as soon as you kill all 3 bosses.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_3": "Sorry, you do not have access.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_4": "Did you manage to face all 3 bosses?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_5": "I am very satisfied.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_6": "Sorry.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_7": "Could you help me with some more work?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_8": "Kill 300 members of the Fafnar cult, help me find Ivory Lyre and help me find an animal to stone.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_9": "Sorry.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_10": "Have you finished killing the 300 members of Fafnar's cult?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_11": "Thanks. You killed the 300 members of the Fafnar cult.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_12": "Sorry.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_13": "Did you manage to find Lyre?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_14": "Thanks. I was looking for Lyre for a long time.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_15": "Sorry.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_16": "Did you manage to find Small Tortoise?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_17": "Thanks. I was looking for Small Tortoise.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_18": "Sorry.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_19": "Do you want me to stone a small tortoise?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_20": "Here's your Small Petrified Tortoise.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_21": "Sorry.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_22": "Did you finish the 3 jobs I gave you?",
  "npc.alyxo.say_23": "Congratulations, you have completed the 3 jobs I gave you.",
  "npc.alyxo.say_24": "Sorry.",
  "npc.shimun.say_1": "Could you help me do a ritual?",
  "npc.shimun.say_2": "Here is the list with the missing ingredients to complete the ritual.",
  "npc.shimun.say_3": "Sorry.",
  "npc.shimun.say_4": "Did you bring all the materials I informed you about? ",
  "npc.shimun.say_5": "Thank you this stage of the ritual is complete.",
  "npc.shimun.say_6": "Sorry.",
  "npc.tefrit.say_1": "Could you help me do a ritual?",
  "npc.tefrit.say_2": "Here is the list with the missing ingredients to complete the ritual.",
  "npc.tefrit.say_3": "Sorry.",
  "npc.tefrit.say_4": "Did you bring all the materials I informed you about?",
  "npc.tefrit.say_5": "Thank you this stage of the ritual is complete.",
  "npc.tefrit.say_6": "Sorry.",
  "npc.saideh.say_1": " I would like you to visit the grave of our beloved hero Dayyan. His remains have to be reburied, because a horde of ogres controls this place. Do you want to start this holy mission?",
  "npc.saideh.say_2": "Well, I appreciate that. Good luck!",
  "npc.saideh.say_3": "Sorry.",
  "npc.tigo.say_1": "You are now one of us. Learn to endure this world's suffering in every facet and take delight in the soothing eternity that waits for the {purest} of us on the other side.",
  "npc.tigo.say_2": "Purification is but one of the difficult steps on your way to the other side. The {trial} of tar, sulphur and ice.",
  "npc.kallimae.say_1": "Some residents are in need of ingredients to finish a ritual. You can help?",
  "npc.kallimae.say_2": "Search for the NPCs Yonan, Narsai, Shimun and Tefrit.",
  "npc.kallimae.say_3": "Sorry.",
  "npc.kallimae.say_4": "Did you help some residents with ingredients?",
  "npc.kallimae.say_5": "Thanks. I need you to go to 4 places indicated by Goddess Bastesh.",
  "npc.kallimae.say_6": "Sorry.",
  "npc.kallimae.say_7": "Did you check all the points and bring the Symbol of Sun and Sea?",
  "npc.kallimae.say_8": "Thanks. Here is your reward.",
  "npc.kallimae.say_9": "Sorry.",
  "npc.yonan.say_1": "Could you help me do a ritual?",
  "npc.yonan.say_2": "Here is the list with the missing ingredients to complete the ritual.",
  "npc.yonan.say_3": "Sorry.",
  "npc.yonan.say_4": "Did you bring all the materials I informed you about? ",
  "npc.yonan.say_5": "Thank you this stage of the ritual is complete.",
  "npc.yonan.say_6": "Sorry.",
  "npc.yonan.say_7": "You have all parts of the famous Regalia of Suon! Only a few of them were ever forged, back in the times of the old empire. You are holding a very rare and precious treasure, my friend. ... As you have all four pieces, I could combine them into the full insignia. Shall I do this for you?",
  "npc.yonan.say_8": "Well then, let me have a look.",
  "npc.yonan.say_9": "Sorry, you dont have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_1": "The time has come, my child. I sense great spiritual wisdom in you and I shall grant you a sign of your progress, if you can fulfil my task.",
  "npc.chondur.say_2": "You have successfully passed the first task. If you can fulfil my second task, I will grant you a mask like the one I wear. Will you listen to the requirements?",
  "npc.chondur.say_3": "You must have the Shaman Outfit to proceed with this task.",
  "npc.chondur.say_4": "Good! Come back once you found a mandrake and collected 5 dworcish voodoo dolls.",
  "npc.chondur.say_5": "Have you gathered the mandrake and the 5 voodoo dolls from the dworcs?",
  "npc.chondur.say_6": "Have you gathered the 5 tribal masks and the 5 banana staves?",
  "npc.chondur.say_7": "I am proud of you, my child, excellent work. This staff shall be yours from now on!",
  "npc.chondur.say_8": "You don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_9": "Well done, my child! I hereby grant you the right to wear a shamanic mask. Do it proudly.",
  "npc.chondur.say_10": "You don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_11": "Maybe next time.",
  "npc.chondur.say_12": "You did bring all the items I requested, child. Good. Shall I travel to the spirit realm and try finding a stampor companion for you?",
  "npc.chondur.say_13": "You already have stampor mount.",
  "npc.chondur.say_14": "The evil cult has placed a curse on one of the captains here. I need at least five of their pirate voodoo dolls to lift that curse.",
  "npc.chondur.say_15": "Did you bring five pirate voodoo dolls?",
  "npc.chondur.say_16": "Sorry you don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_17": "Finally I can put an end to that curse. I thank you so much.",
  "npc.chondur.say_18": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.chondur.say_19": "This is really not advisable. Behind this barrier, strong forces are raging violently. Are you sure that you want to go there?",
  "npc.chondur.say_20": "Very good! <mumble> 'Your soul shall be protected!' Now, I need a fresh dead rat.",
  "npc.chondur.say_21": "You don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_22": "Very good! <chants and dances> 'You shall face black magic without fear!' Now, I need a fresh dead black sheep.",
  "npc.chondur.say_23": "You don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_25": "You don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_26": "Ten prayers for a blessed stake? Don't tell me they made you travel whole Tibia for it! Listen, child, if you bring me a wooden stake, I'll bless it for you. <chuckles>",
  "npc.chondur.say_27": "You don't have a wooden stake.",
  "npc.chondur.say_28": "Sorry, but I'm still exhausted from the last ritual. Please come back later.",
  "npc.chondur.say_29": "<mumblemumble> Sha Kesh Mar!",
  "npc.chondur.say_30": "You should not talk about things you don't know anything about.",
  "npc.chondur.say_31": "You mean, you are interested in a counterspell to cross the energy barrier on Goroma?",
  "npc.chondur.say_32": "Did you bring the fresh dead chicken?",
  "npc.chondur.say_33": "Did you bring the fresh dead rat?",
  "npc.chondur.say_34": "Did you bring the fresh dead black sheep?",
  "npc.chondur.say_35": "Hm. I don't think you need another one of my counterspells to cross the barrier on Goroma.",
  "npc.chondur.say_36": "Ah, thank you very much! I'll honour his memory.",
  "npc.chondur.say_37": "You don't have the necessary items.",
  "npc.chondur.say_38": "Ah, the energy barrier set up by the cult is maintained by lousy magic, but it's still effective. Without a proper counterspell, you won't be able to pass it.",
  "npc.herbert.say_1": "You would like Chantalle's letter? only if you are willing to pay a price. {gold} maybe?",
  "npc.herbert.say_2": "Are you willing to pay 1000 gold for this letter?",
  "npc.herbert.say_3": "Here you go kind sir.",
  "npc.malor.say_1": "Shove off, little one! Humans are not welcome here, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.malor.say_2": "Greetings, human |PLAYERNAME|. My patience with your kind is limited, so speak quickly and choose your words well.",
  "npc.malor.say_3": "You haven't finished your final mission yet. Shall I explain it again to you?",
  "npc.malor.say_4": "Have you found Fa'hradin's lamp and placed it in Malor's personal chambers?",
  "npc.malor.say_5": "There's no mission left for you, friend of the Efreet. However, I have a {task} for you.",
  "npc.malor.say_6": "Your choice.",
  "npc.malor.say_7": "Just do it!",
  "npc.malor.say_8": "There are still blue djinns everywhere! We can't let a single one of them live. I guess a start would be for you to kill 500 blue djinns and Marid. Will you assist us?",
  "npc.malor.say_9": "Come back when you kill 500 blue djinns and Marid.",
  "npc.malor.say_10": "Good, then show those pathetic Marid what you're made of.",
  "npc.romir.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.grombur.say_1": "Oh well, I liked Nokmir. He used to be a good dwarf until that day on which he stole the ring from {Rerun}.",
  "npc.grombur.say_2": "Yeah, he's the lucky guy in this whole story. I heard rumours that emperor Rehal had plans to promote Nokmir, but after this whole thievery story, he might pick Rerun instead.",
  "npc.grombur.say_3": "Got any dwarven brown ale?? I DON'T THINK SO....and Bolfana, the tavern keeper, won't sell you anything. I'm sure about that...she doesn't like humans... I tell you what, if you get me a cask of dwarven brown ale, I allow you to enter the mine. Alright?",
  "npc.grombur.say_4": "HOW?....WHERE?....AHHHH, I don't mind....SLUUUUUURP....tastes a little flat but I had worse. Thank you. Just don't tell anyone that I let you in.",
  "npc.grombur.say_5": "Haha, fine! Don't waste time and get me the ale. See you.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_1": "Hold your horses! First we need to get more {bait} fo' the sea serpent. Bring me the fish I requested and we can set sails immediately.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_2": "Ya wanna join the hunt fo' the {sea serpent}? Be warned ya may pay with ya life! Are ya in to it?",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_3": "You got any {baits} for me?",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_4": "A'right, wanna put out to sea?",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_5": "A'right, we are here to resupply our stock of baits to catch the sea serpent. Your first task is to bring me 5 fish they are easy to catch. When you got them ask me for the {bait} again.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_6": "Let's go fo' a {hunt} and bring the beast down!",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_7": "Excellent, now bring me 5 northern pike.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_8": "Excellent, now bring me 5 green perch.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_9": "Excellent, now bring me 5 rainbow trout.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_10": "Excellent, that should be enough fish to make the bait. Tell me when ya're ready fo' the {hunt}.",
  "npc.captain_haba.say_11": "The bait is ready, tell me if ya're ready to start the hunt.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_12": "My name is Haba, Captain Haba for ya little worm.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_13": "I ain't no pirate. Don't let yourself mislead by my pirate hat. I got it from a friend of mine.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_14": "Most o' my friends are dead the others don't like me anymore......well, seems there aren't many left.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_15": "What fo' godsake shall that be??",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_16": "Who are ya calling a barbarian?!? Watch your tongue here on board or you end up as fish fodder!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_17": "Dis is no passenger ship it's a WARship. I'm on hunting business.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_18": "Never heard of him. He is no captain that's for sure, otherwise I'd know him. I was on the sea for the last 20 years hunting this, this monster.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_19": "Yee, I've been chasing that monster for over 20 years now. I promise I'll bring it down!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_20": "It lets me forget the long years, the lost years. The years I was chasing after THAT monster, the sea serpent.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_21": "Ye, I command 'is ship!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_22": "Our last ship has been destroyed by the most evil creature of the ocean: the sea serpent. To continue our hunt, I've bought this ship here.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_23": "Never seen one.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_24": "I'm faithful - I'll catch that monster one day. Yes I will, as sure as my name is Captain Haba!!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_25": "On the high seas there is no queen. At least I didn't see her yet. Hararar!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_26": "On the high seas there is no king. At least I didn't see him yet. Hararar!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_27": "Arms, legs, head, whatever. I got injuries on almost every part of my body!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_28": "This is no shop boy, this is a warship!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_29": "We aren't even near that location! Wanna swim? Harharhar!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_30": "I know Marvik in Thais. He once helped me with a furuncle I had on my ...ahh, doesn't matter. He's a nice gran'pa, though!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_31": "My worst enemy is a huge sea serpent. I dunno when I started to follow it's trail. I'll kill it and if it's the last thing I'll do, I'll kill it!",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_32": "This is a ship and the captain is some kind o' leader, isn't he? <mumbles>..stupid..landlubber.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_33": "What fo' godsake shall that be??",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_34": "Seems that they are some sort o' druids fo' the Norseman.",
  "npc.captain_haba.stdmod_35": "I'm full of stories mate! Name a body part and I tell you the story what happened to it!",
  "npc.ceiron.say_1": "What are you thinking! I would never allow you to slay my beloved friends for the sake of your narcism. Only {Faolan} can grant you a fur like this one.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_2": "I know where the great wolf mother lives, but I will not tell that to just anyone. You have to earn my respect first. Are you willing to help me?",
  "npc.ceiron.say_3": "Right, I will keep my promise. Faolan roams Tibia freely, but her favourite sleeping cave is on Cormaya. I will now enchant you so you will be able to speak the wolf language.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_4": "Were you able to obtain a sample of the Griffinclaw?",
  "npc.ceiron.say_5": "Did you bring me a sample of water from the hydra cave?",
  "npc.ceiron.say_6": "Were you really able to collect 100 ounces of demon dust?",
  "npc.ceiron.say_7": "Have you really found my wolf tooth chain??",
  "npc.ceiron.say_8": "Have you lost my waterskin?",
  "npc.ceiron.say_9": "Alright then. Take this botanist's container and return to me once you were able to retrieve a sample. Don't lose patience!",
  "npc.ceiron.say_10": "Crunor be praised! The Griffinclaw really exists! Now, I will make sure that it will not become extinct. If you are ready to help me again, just ask me for a {task}.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_11": "Great! Here, take my waterskin and try to fill it with water from this special trickle. Don't lose my waterskin, I will not accept some random dirty waterskin.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_12": "Good work, |PLAYERNAME|! This water looks indeed extremely clear. I will examine it right away. If you are ready to help me again, just ask me for a {task}.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_13": "I'm very impressed, |PLAYERNAME|. With this task you have proven that you are on the right side and are powerful as well. If you are ready to help me again, just ask me for a {task}.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_14": "I'm very impressed, |PLAYERNAME|. With this task you have proven that you are on the right side and are powerful as well. If you are ready to help me again, just ask me for a {task}.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_15": "Thank you so much. I can't wait to wear it around my neck again, it was a special present from Faolan.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_16": "Crunor be praised! You found my beloved chain! |PLAYERNAME|, you really earned my respect and I consider you as a friend from now on. Remind me to tell you about {Faolan} sometime.",
  "npc.ceiron.say_17": "I can give you a new one, but I fear that I have to take a small fee for it. Would you like to buy a waterskin for 1000 gold?",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.stdmod_5": "The temple is built around the elves' holy tree. You can find it north of this harbour.",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.stdmod_6": "Finarfin is in charge of the bank. You can find him on the lowest floor of the depot.",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, instruments, furniture, spells and food here.",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_thelandil.stdmod_9": "The elves have constructed Ab'Dendriel mainly in and on trees. There is also a large underground cave system with shops, a prison and troll caves.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_1": "In exchange for a truly generous donation, I will offer a special outfit. Do you want to make a donation?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_2": "In that case, return to me once you made up your mind.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_3": "Take this armor as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_4": "Please make sure you have free slots in your store inbox.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_5": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_6": "You alread have that addon.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_7": "Take this helmet as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend. ",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_8": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_9": "You alread have that outfit.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_10": "You need to donate {armor} outfit first.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_11": "Take this boots as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend. ",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_12": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_13": "You alread have that outfit.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_14": "You need to donate {helmet} addon first.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_15": "So you wold like to donate 500.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear a unique armor?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_16": "So you would like to donate 250.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear unique helmet?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.say_17": "So you would like to donate 250.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear a unique boots?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_18": "I can promote you for 20000 gold coins. Do you want me to promote you?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_19": "Alright then, come back when you are ready.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_20": "I remember about those uniforms, they had a camouflage inlay so they could be worn the inside out too. I will send some color samples via mail to Mr. Postner.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_21": "The uniforms of our guards and soldiers are of unparraleled quality of course.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_22": "I am {Queen} Eloise. It is my duty to reign over this marvellous {city} and the {lands} of the north.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_23": "We women try to bring justice and wisdom to all, even to males.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_24": "I am Queen Eloise. For you it's 'My Queen' or 'Your Majesty', of course.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_25": "I don't care about gossip like a simpleminded male would do.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_26": "Soon the whole land will be ruled by women at last!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_27": "Thank you, I'm fine.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_28": "It's my humble domain.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_29": "Sell? Your question shows that you are a typical member of your gender!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_30": "We honor the gods of good in our fair city, especially Crunor, of course.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_31": "All citizens of Carlin are my subjects. I see them more as my childs, though, epecially the male population.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_32": "This beast scared my cat away on my last diplomatic mission in this filthy town.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_33": "He is the scourge of the whole continent!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_34": "The royal treasure is hidden beyond the grasps of any thieves by magical means.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_35": "Go and hunt them! For queen and country!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_36": "Visit the church or the townguards for help.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_37": "I will call for heroes as soon as the need arises again.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_38": "Our city is rich and prospering.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_39": "I don't want to talk about 'sewers'.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_40": "Dungeons are places where males crawl around and look for trouble.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_41": "Feel free to visit our town's magnificent shops.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_42": "Don't worry about time in the presence of your Queen.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_43": "We need the assistance of heroes now and then. Even males prove useful now and then.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_44": "The taxes in Carlin are not high, more a symbol than a sacrifice.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_45": "I am the Queen, the only rightful ruler on the continent!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_46": "Ask one of the soldiers about that.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_47": "Our enemies are numerous. We have to fight vile monsters and have to watch this silly king in the south carefully.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_48": "They dare to reject my reign over them!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_49": "Isn't our city marvellous? Have you noticed the lovely gardens on the roofs?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_50": "My subjects maintain many fine shops. Go and have a look at their wares.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_51": "Ask around about them.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_52": "The four major guilds are the Knights, the Paladins, the Druids, and the Sorcerers.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_53": "They haven't troubled our city lately. I guess, they fear the wrath of our druids.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_54": "The paladins are great hunters.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_55": "It's a shame that the High Paladin does not reside in Carlin.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_56": "The knights of Carlin are the bravest.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_57": "The sorcerers have a small isle for their guild. So if they blow something up it does not burn the whole city to ruins.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_58": "The druids of Carlin are our protectors and advisors. Their powers provide us with wealth and food.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_59": "Carlin is a center of the forces of good, of course.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_60": "The forces of evil have a firm grip on this puny city to the south.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_61": "The order, Crunor gives the world, is essential for survival.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_62": "Chaos is common in the southern regions, where they allow a man to reign over a realm.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_63": "A mans tale ... that means 'nonsense', of course.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_64": "If you want a reward, go and bring me something this silly King Tibianus wants dearly!",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_65": "A dusgusting organisation, which could be only created by men.",
  "npc.queen_eloise.stdmod_66": "It is said that he lives on a small island near Edron. Maybe the people there know more about him.",
  "npc.curos.say_1": "You come here to ask us to spare your people? This land has no tolerance for the weak, we have it neither. If you want us to consider you as useful for us, you'll have to prove it in a {test} of strength and courage. ",
  "npc.curos.say_2": "With the death of their leader, the rebels return to our camps one by one, deeply humiliated. It might be a wise decision to let a useful tool like you continue to exist.",
  "npc.izsh.say_1": "Oh yez, let me zee ze documentz. Here we go: zree cheztz filled wiz platinum, one houze, a zet of elite armor, and an unending mana cazket. Iz ziz correct?",
  "npc.angelina.say_1": "I will tell you a small secret now. My friend Lynda in Thais can create a blessed wand. Greet her from me, maybe she will aid you.",
  "npc.hjaern.say_1": "The spirits are at peace now. The threat of the chakoyas is averted for now. I thank you for your help. Perhaps you should ask Silfind if you can help her in some matters. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_2": "I have now no mission for you.",
  "npc.hjaern.say_3": "Do you bring frostheart shards for our spell?",
  "npc.hjaern.say_4": "Do you bring frostheart shards for our spell? ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_5": "Do you want to sell all your shards for 2000 gold coins per each? ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_6": "Take this. It might suit your Nordic outfit fine. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_7": "Take this. It might suit your Nordic outfit fine. From now on we only can give you 2000 gold pieces for each shard. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_8": "You want to sacrifice a cookie to the spirits?",
  "npc.hjaern.say_9": "This is good news. As I explained, travel to Helheim, seek the reason for the unrest there and then report to me about your mission. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_10": "Excellent, you collected 5 of them. If you have collected 5 or more, talk to me about your {reward}. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_11": "Excellent, you collected 10 of them. If you have collected 15 or more, talk to me about your {reward}. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_12": "Here your are. ",
  "npc.hjaern.say_13": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.hjaern.say_14": "In the name of the spirits I accept this offer ... UHNGH ... The spirits are not amused!",
  "npc.hjaern.say_15": "I see.",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_1": "Shove off, little one! Humans are not welcome here, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_2": "You know the code human! Very well then... What do you want, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_3": "You are still alive, |PLAYERNAME|? Well, what do you want?",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_4": "Did you find the thief of our supplies?",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_5": "Did you already talk to Alesar? He has another mission for you!",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_6": "After all, you're just a human.",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_7": "Finally! What is his name then?",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_8": "Then go to Carlin and search for him! Look for something that might give you a clue!",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_9": "Hmmm... I don't think so. Return to Thais and continue your search!",
  "npc.baa_leal.say_10": "Hmmm... I don't think so. Return to Thais and continue your search!",
  "npc.gorn.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.gorn.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.gorn.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_4": "I am selling equipment of all kinds. Do you need anything?",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_5": "The king supports Tibia's economy a lot.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_6": "Magic? Ask a sorcerer or druid about that.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_7": "I am Gorn. My goods are known all over Tibia.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_8": "It is exactly |TIME|. Maybe you want to buy a watch?",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_9": "This druids are nice people, you will find them in the east of the town.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_10": "Even the strong knights need my equipment on their travels though Tibia.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_11": "You can find him in the sorcerer guild.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_12": "She's the leader of the paladin guild.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_13": "Old Baxter was a rowdy, once. In our youth we shared some adventures and women.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_14": "Bah! Go away with this bozoguy.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_15": "Frodo is a jolly fellow.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_16": "We had a clash or two in the old days.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_17": "Even the strong knights need my equipment on their travels though Tibia.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_18": "That's a pretty one.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_19": "I hardly know the McRonalds.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_20": "You can find him in the sorcerer guild.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_21": "This Oswald has not enough to work and too much time to spread rumours.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_22": "He advices newcomers to buy at my store. I love that guy!",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_23": "Strong as an ox, could armwrestle a minotaur, I bet.",
  "npc.gorn.stdmod_24": "He owns the magic shop here. But be aware: The prices are enormous.",
  "npc.navigator.say_1": "Lhnjei gouthn naumpi! I know why you are here. I can {explain} everything.",
  "npc.navigator.say_2": "By entering this place, you have earned the right to learn what this is all about. This is a long story. Are you sure you want to hear this, {yes}?",
  "npc.navigator.say_3": "Do you have enough, can I stop?",
  "npc.navigator.say_4": "Then take this one. And remember: DO NOT TELL ANYONE ABOUT ME OR ANYTHING YOU HAVE HEARD HERE TODAY.",
  "npc.barbara.stdmod_1": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the queen greet with her title!",
  "npc.barbara.stdmod_2": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the queen greet with her title!",
  "npc.barbara.say_3": "Take this!",
  "npc.rata_mari.say_1": "Ok, have you brought me the cheese, I've asked for?",
  "npc.rata_mari.say_2": "I already gave you the report. I'm not going to write another one!",
  "npc.rata_mari.say_3": "No cheese - no report.",
  "npc.rata_mari.say_4": "Meep! Meep! Great! Here is the spyreport for you!",
  "npc.rata_mari.say_5": "No cheese - no report.",
  "npc.rata_mari.stdmod_6": "Your power of observation is stunning. Yes, I'm a rat.",
  "npc.fenbala.stdmod_1": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the queen greet with her title!",
  "npc.fenbala.stdmod_2": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the queen greet with her title!",
  "npc.fenbala.say_3": "Take this!",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_1": "I'm the officer responsible for this area. I give out missions, accept mission reports and oversee our defences.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_2": "It's good to be a gnome for sure!",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_3": "Now that's gnomish ingenuity given shape! Who but a gnome would come up with such a plan to defeat our enemies. ",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_4": "Sorry, but no! Your expertise could be put to better use elsewhere. You are desperately needed in the upper levels of the Spike. Report there immediately. ",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_5": "I can offer you several missions: to {deliver} parcels to our boys and girls in the battlefield, to get reports from our {undercover} gnomes, to do some {temperature} measuring and to {kill} some drillworms.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_6": " What mission do you want to report about: the {delivery} of parcels, the {undercover} reports, the {temperature} measuring or {kill} of drillworms?",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_7": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_8": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_9": "Gnowful! Deliver the four parcels to some of our far away outposts in the caverns.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_10": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_11": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_12": "Gnowful! Get three reports from our undercover agents posing as monsters in the caves around us.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_13": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_14": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_15": "Gnowful! Use the gnomish temperature measurement device to locate the hottest spot at the lava pools in the cave.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_16": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_17": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_18": "Gnowful! Just go out to the caves and kill at least seven drillworms.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_19": "That's not a valid mission name.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_20": "Sorry, you are not on the required minimum level [",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_21": "We need someone to bring four parcels to some of our far away outposts in the caverns. If you are interested, I can give you some more {information} about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_22": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_23": "Gnometastic! Here are the parcels. Regrettably, the labels got lost during transport; but I guess those lonely gnomes won't mind as long as they get ANY parcel at all.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_24": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_25": "Sorry, you are not on the required minimum level [",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_26": "Someone is needed to get three reports from our undercover agents posing as monsters in the caves around us. If you are interested, I can give you some more {information} about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_27": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_28": "Gnometastic! Get three reports from our agents. You can find them anywhere in the caves around us. Just keep looking for monsters that behave strangely and give you a wink.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_29": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_30": "Sorry, you are not on the required minimum level [",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_31": "Your task would be to use a gnomish temperature measurement device - short GTMD - to locate the hottest spot at the lava pools in the caves. If you are interested, I can give you some more information about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_32": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_33": "Gnometastic! Find the hottest spot of the lava pools in the caves. If you lose the GTMD before you find the hot spot, you'll have to get yourself a new one. Gnomux sells all the equipment that is required for our missions.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_34": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_35": "Sorry, you are not on the required minimum level [",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_36": "This mission will require you to kill some drillworms for us. If you are interested, I can give you some more {information} about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_37": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_38": "Gnometastic! You should have no trouble finding enough drillworms.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_39": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_40": "This mission will require you to kill some drillworms for us. If you are interested, I can give you some more {information} about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_41": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_42": "Gnometastic! You should have no trouble finding enough drillworms.",
  "npc.gnomargery.say_43": "Ok then.",
  "npc.fa_hradin.say_1": "Whoa! A human! This is no place for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Go and play somewhere else.",
  "npc.fa_hradin.say_2": "Aaaah... what have we here. A human - interesting. And such an ugly specimen, too... All right, human |PLAYERNAME|. How can I help you?",
  "npc.fa_hradin.say_3": "Looking for work, are you? Well, it's very tempting, you know, but I'm afraid we do not really employ beginners. Perhaps our cook could need a helping hand in the kitchen.",
  "npc.fa_hradin.say_4": "Did you already retrieve the spyreport?",
  "npc.fa_hradin.say_5": "Did you already talk to Gabel about the report? I think he will have further instructions for you.",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.say_1": "I'm aware what you are looking for. Usually I would rather devour you, but due to unfortunate circumstances, I need your {assistance}.",
  "npc.a_majestic_warwolf.say_1": "GRRRRRRRRRRRRR",
  "npc.a_majestic_warwolf.say_2": "I can see in your eyes that you are a honest and friendly person, |PLAYERNAME|. You were patient enough to learn our language and I will grant you a special gift. Will you accept it?",
  "npc.snake_eye.say_1": "So you're the delivery boy? Go ahead, but I warn you, it's quite heavy. You can take it from the box over there.",
  "npc.snake_eye.say_2": "Funny thing that everyone thinks we have forgers for fake documents here. But no, we don't. The best forger is old Ahmet in Ankrahmun.",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_1": "So you want to advance to a {Initiate} rank? Did you bring 500 demonic essences with you?",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_2": "So you want to advance to a {Dreamer} rank? Did you bring 1000 demonic essences with you?",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_3": "So you want to advance to a {Lord Protector} rank? Did you bring 1500 demonic essences with you?",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_4": "Please know that your decision is irrevocable. You will abandon the opportunity to join any order whose doctrine is incontrast to our own ...",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_5": "Do you still want to join our order?",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_6": "You advanced to {Initiate} rank! You are now able to use teleports of second floor of Knightwatch Tower.",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_7": "Come back when you gather all essences.",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_8": "You advanced to {Dreamer} rank!",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_9": "Come back when you gather all essences.",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_10": "You advanced to {Lord Protector} rank! You are now able to use teleports of fourth floor of Knightwatch Tower and to create addon scrolls.",
  "npc.the_dream_master.say_11": "Come back when you gather all essences.",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_1": "If you want anything, you should talk to Old Rock Boy over there. I do {collect} stuff, though. So just ask if you're interested in helping me.",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_2": "Have you got anything for me today?",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_3": "Have you got anything for me today?",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_4": "Great! Let me see. Amazing! I will take this, thank you!",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_5": "Great! Let me see. Amazing! I will take this, thank you!",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_6": "Great! Let me see. Amazing! I will take this, thank you!",
  "npc.rock_steady.say_7": "You dont have the required items!",
  "npc.guide_elena.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_elena.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_elena.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops - well, warehouses - spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the adventurer's guild, hunting grounds, quests and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_5": "The temple is pretty much in the middle of Venore. If you go south from this harbour, you can't miss it.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_6": "The bank as well as jewel stores can be found in the House of Wealth, in the north-eastern part of Venore. I can mark it on your map if you want.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_7": "You can buy almost everything here! Visit one of our warehouses for weapons, armors, magical equipment, spells, gems, tools, furniture and everything else you can imagine.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_9": "I will help you find your way in the buzzing city of Venore. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_10": "This trading city has been built directly over a swamp and basically stands on stone pillars. We have many large warehouses here. To speak of 'shops' would be an understatement.",
  "npc.guide_elena.stdmod_11": "I'm Elena, sweetheart. I love your name, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.charos.say_1": "Sorry, you have traveled a lot.",
  "npc.charos.say_2": "Goodbye traveler!",
  "npc.charos.say_3": "Sorry, I don't know about this place.",
  "npc.charos.say_4": "Sorry, I don't know about this place.",
  "npc.an_old_dragon_lord.say_1": "LEAVE THE DRAGONS' CEMETERY AT ONCE!",
  "npc.an_old_dragon_lord.say_2": "LEAVE THE DRAGONS' CEMETERY AT ONCE!",
  "npc.an_old_dragon_lord.say_3": "AHHHH THE PAIN OF AGESSS! I NEED MUSSSSHRROOOMSSS TO EASSSE MY PAIN! BRRRING ME MUSHRRROOOMSSS!",
  "npc.an_old_dragon_lord.say_4": "AHHH MUSHRRROOOMSSS! NOW MY PAIN WILL BE EASSSED FOR A WHILE! TAKE THISS AND LEAVE THE DRAGONSSS' CEMETERY AT ONCE!",
  "npc.a_fluffy_squirrel.stdmod_1": "Chh? Chhh?? <though you don't understand squirrelish, that one seems really excited>",
  "npc.bron.stdmod_1": "This... person... makes me want to... say something bad... must... control myself. <sweats>",
  "npc.bron.say_2": "Oh! He really said that? I am so proud of you, |PLAYERNAME|. These are really good news. Everything would be great... if only there wasn't this {person} near my house.",
  "npc.bron.say_3": "Fighting spirit? What am I supposed to do with this fi... - oh! I feel strange... ME MIGHTY! ME WILL CHASE OFF ANNOYING KIDS!GROOOAARR!! RRRRRRRRRRRRAAAAAAAGE!!",
  "npc.bron.say_4": "Have you really managed to fulfil the task and brought me 50 pieces of red cloth and 50 pieces of green cloth?",
  "npc.bron.say_5": "Oh, did you bring 10 rolls of spool of yarn for me?",
  "npc.bron.say_6": "Were you able to get hold of a flask with pure warrior's sweat?",
  "npc.bron.say_7": "You are indeed not only well educated, but also very courageous. I wish you good luck, you are my last hope.",
  "npc.bron.say_8": "Again, I have to thank you for your selfless offer to help me. I hope that Ajax can come up with something, now that he has experienced the power of words.",
  "npc.bron.say_9": "Thank you, my friend! Come back to me once you have collected 50 pieces of red cloth and 50 pieces of green cloth.",
  "npc.bron.say_10": "Terrific! I will start to trim it while you gather 10 rolls of spider silk. I'm sure that Ajax will love it.",
  "npc.bron.say_11": "I'm impressed! You really managed to get spool of yarn for me! I will immediately start to work on this shirt. Please don't forget to bring me warrior's sweat!",
  "npc.bron.say_12": "Good work, |PLAYERNAME|! Now I can finally finish this present for Ajax. Because you were such a great help, I have also a present for you. Will you accept it?",
  "npc.bron.say_13": "I have kept this traditional barbarian wig safe for many years now. It is now yours! I hope you will wear it proudly, friend.",
  "npc.alesar.say_1": "Shove off, little one! Humans are not welcome here, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.alesar.say_2": "What do you want from me, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.alesar.say_3": "Did you find the tear of Daraman?",
  "npc.alesar.say_4": "Don't forget to talk to Malor concerning your next mission.",
  "npc.alesar.say_5": "Then not.",
  "npc.alesar.say_6": "As I expected. You haven't got the stone. Shall I explain your mission again?",
  "npc.alesar.say_7": "As I expected. You haven't got the stone. Shall I explain your mission again?",
  "npc.alesar.say_8": "I'm sorry, but you don't have Malor's permission to trade with me.",
  "npc.gnomewart.say_1": "Just take the teleporter over there to the south and follow the hallway. At the end of the hallway you'll find a teleporter. Step on it and you are done!",
  "npc.gnomewart.say_2": "You have passed the test and are ready to create your soul melody. Talk to Gnomelvis in the east about it.",
  "npc.gnomewart.say_3": "Your endurance will be tested here when the time comes. For the moment please continue with the other phases of your recruitment.",
  "npc.gnomewart.say_4": "You have passed the test. If you consider what huge feet you have to move it's quite impressive.",
  "npc.eustacio.say_1": "I am Eustacio. At your service.",
  "npc.eustacio.say_2": "It's just the time to make a fortune.",
  "npc.eustacio.say_3": " I am an aspiring businessman, who thrives to climb the ladder of success in the Venorean society.",
  "npc.gnominus.say_1": "Your examination is quite easy. Just step through the green crystal apparatus in the south! We will examine you with what we call g-rays. Where g stands for gnome of course ...",
  "npc.gnominus.say_2": "Afterwards walk up to Gnomedix for your ear examination.",
  "npc.gnominus.say_3": "I provide the population with some fresh alcohol-free mushroom {beer}!",
  "npc.gnominus.say_4": "Do you want some mushroom beer for 10 gold?",
  "npc.gnominus.say_5": "Don't be afraid. It won't hurt! Just step in!",
  "npc.gnominus.say_6": "And here it is! Drink it quick, it gets stale quite fast!",
  "npc.gnominus.say_7": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.gnominus.say_8": "Come back later.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_1": "So you want to advance to a {Hyaena} rank? Did you bring 500 demonic essences with you?",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_2": "So you want to advance to a {Death Dealer} rank? Did you bring 1000 demonic essences with you?",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_3": "So you want to advance to a {Dread Lord} rank? Did you bring 1500 demonic essences with you?",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_4": "You advanced to {Hyaena} rank! You are now able to use teleports of second floor of Knightwatch Tower.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_5": "Come back when you gather all essences.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_6": "You advanced to {Death Dealer} rank!",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_7": "Come back when you gather all essences.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_8": "You advanced to {Dread Lord} rank! You are now able to use teleports of fourth floor of Knightwatch Tower and to create addon scrolls.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.say_9": "Come back when you gather all essences.",
  "npc.gnomespector.say_1": "Don't be afraid. It won't hurt! Just step in!",
  "npc.tony.say_1": "Uhm, report, eh? <slowly gives a clumsy description of recent problems>. ",
  "npc.tony.say_2": "You can {pass} either to the {Arena Quarter} or {Foreigner Quarter}. Which one will it be?",
  "npc.zirella.say_1": "By the way, 'quest' is a keyword that many NPCs react to, especially those which have tasks for you. So darling, about that {quest}... are you listening?",
  "npc.zirella.say_2": "Thank you so much for your kindness. I'm an old woman and I desperately need firewood for my oven. Could you please help me?",
  "npc.zirella.say_3": "You're such a treasure. In the forest south of here, there are {dead trees} without any leaves. The first thing you have to do is search for one, {okay}?",
  "npc.zirella.say_4": "Splendid, once you've found one, 'Use' it to break a branch from it. Did you understand that so far?",
  "npc.zirella.say_5": "Good... so after you broke a branch, please push it here and select 'use with'. That will turn your mouse cursor into crosshairs. Then left-click on my cart. {Alright}?",
  "npc.zirella.say_6": "To push the branch, drag and drop it on the grass by holding the left mousebutton and moving the cursor to where you want to throw the branch. Just push it near my cart before you 'Use' it, {alright}?",
  "npc.zirella.say_7": "Oh, you deserve it. You really have earned some experience! Also, you may enter my little house now and take what's in that chest beside my bed. Good {bye} for now!",
  "npc.zirella.say_8": "Well then, I hope you find nice and dry branches for me! Good {bye}!",
  "npc.corym_servant.say_1": "You don't have enough, return when could you bring 20 of rare earth to me.",
  "npc.siflind.say_1": "I heard you have already helped our cause. Are you interested in another mission, even when it requires you to travel to a distant land?",
  "npc.siflind.say_2": "Well done. The termites caused just the distraction that we needed. Are you ready for the next step of my plan?",
  "npc.siflind.say_3": "You saved the lives of many innocent animals. Thank you very much. If you are looking for another mission, just ask me.",
  "npc.siflind.say_4": "Our warriors need a more potent yet more secure berserker elixir to fight our enemies. To brew it, I need several ingredients. The first things needed are 5 bat wings. Bring them to me and Ill tell you the next ingredients we need.",
  "npc.siflind.say_5": "Do you have the 5 bat wings I requested?",
  "npc.siflind.say_6": "The second things needed are 4 bear paws. Bring them to me and Ill tell you the next ingredients we need.",
  "npc.siflind.say_7": "Do you have the 4 bear paws I requested?",
  "npc.siflind.say_8": "The next things needed are 3 bonelord eyes. Bring them to me and Ill tell you the next ingredients we need.",
  "npc.siflind.say_9": "Do you have the 3 bonelord eyes I requested?",
  "npc.siflind.say_10": "The next things needed are 2 fish fins. Bring them to me and Ill tell you the next ingredients we need.",
  "npc.siflind.say_11": "Do you have the 2 fish fins I requested?",
  "npc.siflind.say_12": "The last thing needed is a green dragon scale. Bring them to me and Ill tell you the next ingredients we need.",
  "npc.siflind.say_13": "Do you have the green dragon scale I requested?",
  "npc.siflind.say_14": "I have now no mission for you.",
  "npc.siflind.say_15": "Do you want to buy a jug for 1000 gold?",
  "npc.siflind.say_16": "Here you are.",
  "npc.siflind.say_17": "Good! Now listen. To protect the animals there, we have to harm the profit of the hunters. Therefor, I ask you to ruin their best source of earnings. Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.siflind.say_18": "So let's proceed. Take this vial of paint. Travel to Tyrsung again and ruin as many pelts of baby seals as possible before the paint runs dry or freezes. Then return here to report about your mission. ",
  "npc.siflind.say_19": "Thank you very much.",
  "npc.siflind.say_20": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.siflind.say_21": "Thank you very much.",
  "npc.siflind.say_22": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.siflind.say_23": "Thank you very much.",
  "npc.siflind.say_24": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.siflind.say_25": "Thank you very much.",
  "npc.siflind.say_26": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.siflind.say_27": "Thank you very much. This will help us to defend Svargrond. But I heard young Nilsor is in dire need of help. Please contact him immediately.",
  "npc.siflind.say_28": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.siflind.say_29": "You want to buy animal cure for 400 gold coins?",
  "npc.siflind.say_30": "Im out of stock.",
  "npc.siflind.say_31": "Here you go.",
  "npc.siflind.say_32": "You dont have enough of gold coins.",
  "npc.aruda.say_1": "I would never have guessed that.",
  "npc.aruda.say_2": "Oh, sorry, I was distracted, what did you say?",
  "npc.aruda.say_3": "Oh, I just remember I have some work to do, sorry. Bye!",
  "npc.aruda.say_4": "Take some time to talk to me!",
  "npc.aruda.say_5": "Well ... I have met him for a little while .. but this was nothing serious.",
  "npc.aruda.say_6": "I remember that grapes were his favourites. He was almost addicted to them.",
  "npc.aruda.say_7": "Thank you very much. How kind of you to care about me. I am fine, thank you.",
  "npc.aruda.say_8": "Sorry, I have nothing to sell.",
  "npc.aruda.say_9": "I do some work now and then. Nothing unusual, though. So I have plenty time to chat. If you are interested in any topic just ask me.",
  "npc.aruda.say_10": "I am Aruda.",
  "npc.aruda.say_11": "I am a little sad, that you seem to have forgotten me, handsome. I am Aruda.",
  "npc.aruda.say_12": "Yes, that's me!",
  "npc.aruda.say_13": "Oh, I like it, how you say my name.",
  "npc.aruda.say_14": "Please don't be so rude to look for the time if you are talking to me.",
  "npc.aruda.say_15": "I am deeply sorry, I can't help you.",
  "npc.aruda.say_16": "UH! What a terrifying topic. Please let us speak about something more pleasant, I am a weak and small woman after all.",
  "npc.aruda.say_17": "What gives you the impression, I am the kind of women, you find in sewers?",
  "npc.aruda.say_18": "You should ask about that in one of the temples.",
  "npc.aruda.say_19": "The king, that lives in this fascinating castle? I think he does look kind of cute in his luxurious robes, doesn't he?",
  "npc.aruda.say_20": "He is soooo strong! What muscles! What a body! Did you ask him for a date?",
  "npc.aruda.say_21": "He is soooo strong! What muscles! What a body! On the other hand, compared to you he looks quite puny.",
  "npc.aruda.say_22": "He is a little simple minded but always nice and well dressed.",
  "npc.aruda.say_23": "He should really sell some stylish gowns or something like that. We Tibians never get some clothing of the latest fashion. It's a shame.",
  "npc.aruda.say_24": "I don't understand this lonely monks. I love company too much to become one. Hehehe!",
  "npc.aruda.say_25": "Oh, isn't he funny? I could listen to him the whole day.",
  "npc.aruda.say_26": "As far as I know, he is working in the castle.",
  "npc.aruda.say_27": "I am a little shy and so don't hear many rumors.",
  "npc.aruda.say_28": "Oh, you little devil, stop talking like that! <blush>",
  "npc.aruda.say_29": "I know only little about weapons. Can you tell me something about them, please?",
  "npc.aruda.say_30": "I believe that love is stronger than magic, don't you agree?",
  "npc.aruda.say_31": "Oh, sorry, I have to hurry, bye!",
  "npc.aruda.say_32": "I would like to visit the beach more often, but I guess it's too dangerous.",
  "npc.aruda.say_33": "I love this castle! It's so beautiful.",
  "npc.aruda.say_34": "Powerful sorcerers frighten me a little.",
  "npc.aruda.say_35": "I personally think it's inappropriate for a woman to become a warrior, what do you think about that?",
  "npc.aruda.say_36": "Druids seldom visit a town, what do you know about druids?",
  "npc.aruda.say_37": "I like brave fighters like him.",
  "npc.aruda.say_38": "Oh, he is sooooo cute!",
  "npc.aruda.say_39": "I like dogs, the little ones at least. Do you like dogs, too?",
  "npc.aruda.say_40": "Oh, I am just a girl and know nothing about magic swords and such things.",
  "npc.aruda.say_41": "I ... don't know someone named like that.",
  "npc.aruda.say_42": "Yenny? I know no Yenny, nor have I ever used that name! You have mistook me with someone else.",
  "npc.paulie.say_1": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.paulie.say_2": "Sorry, but you can't deposit that much.",
  "npc.paulie.say_3": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.paulie.say_4": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.paulie.say_5": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.paulie.say_6": "Please tell me how much gold it is you would like to deposit.",
  "npc.paulie.say_7": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.paulie.say_8": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.paulie.say_9": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.paulie.say_10": "As you wish. Is there something else I can do for you?",
  "npc.paulie.say_11": "Are you sure you wish to withdraw ",
  "npc.paulie.say_12": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.paulie.say_13": "Please tell me how much gold you would like to withdraw.",
  "npc.paulie.say_14": "Are you sure you wish to withdraw ",
  "npc.paulie.say_15": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.paulie.say_16": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.paulie.say_17": "The customer is king! Come back anytime you want to if you wish to {withdraw} your money.",
  "npc.paulie.say_18": "How many platinum coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.paulie.say_19": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_20": "Here you are.",
  "npc.paulie.say_21": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_22": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.paulie.say_23": "Would you like to change your platinum coins into gold or crystal?",
  "npc.paulie.say_24": "How many platinum coins would you like to change into gold?",
  "npc.paulie.say_25": "How many crystal coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.paulie.say_26": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.paulie.say_27": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_28": "Here you are.",
  "npc.paulie.say_29": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_30": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.paulie.say_31": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_32": "Here you are.",
  "npc.paulie.say_33": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_34": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.paulie.say_35": "How many crystal coins would you like to change into platinum?",
  "npc.paulie.say_36": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_37": "Here you are.",
  "npc.paulie.say_38": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_39": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.paulie.say_40": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_41": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.paulie.say_42": "How many crystal coins would you like to change into platinum?",
  "npc.paulie.say_43": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_44": "So you would like me to change ",
  "npc.paulie.say_45": "Here you are.",
  "npc.paulie.say_46": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.paulie.say_47": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.gregor.say_1": "Sorry but I don't have anything for you at the moment.",
  "npc.gregor.say_2": "Sorry, but our tasks are only for premium warriors.",
  "npc.gregor.say_3": "You mean you would like to prove that you deserve to wear such a helmet?",
  "npc.gregor.say_4": "Your current task is to bring me 100 perfect behemoth fangs, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.gregor.say_5": "Your current task is to retrieve the helmet of Ramsay the Reckless from Banuta, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.gregor.say_6": "Your current task is to obtain a flask of warrior's sweat, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.gregor.say_7": "Your current task is to bring me royal steel, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.gregor.say_8": "Please talk to Sam and tell him I sent you. I'm sure he will be glad to refine your helmet, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.gregor.say_9": "You've already completed the task and can consider yourself a mighty warrior, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.gregor.say_10": "Have you really managed to fulfil the task and brought me 100 perfect behemoth fangs?",
  "npc.gregor.say_11": "You're not serious asking that, are you? They come from behemoths, of course. Unless there are behemoth rabbits. Duh.",
  "npc.gregor.say_12": "Did you recover the helmet of Ramsay the Reckless?",
  "npc.gregor.say_13": "These pesky apes steal everything they can get their dirty hands on.",
  "npc.gregor.say_14": "Were you able to get hold of a flask with pure warrior's sweat?",
  "npc.gregor.say_15": "Warrior's sweat can be magically extracted from headgear worn by a true warrior, but only in small amounts. Djinns are said to be good at magical extractions.",
  "npc.gregor.say_16": "Ah, have you brought the royal steel?",
  "npc.gregor.say_17": "Royal steel can only be refined by very skilled smiths.",
  "npc.gregor.say_18": "Bah. Then you will have to wait for the day these helmets are sold in shops, but that will not happen before hell freezes over.",
  "npc.gregor.say_19": "Alright then. Come back to me once you have collected 100 perfect behemoth fangs.",
  "npc.gregor.say_20": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.gregor.say_21": "Lying is not exactly honourable, |PLAYERNAME|. Shame on you.",
  "npc.gregor.say_22": "I'm deeply impressed, brave Knight |PLAYERNAME|. I expected nothing less from you. Now, please retrieve Ramsay's helmet.",
  "npc.gregor.say_23": "There is no need to rush anyway.",
  "npc.gregor.say_24": "Lying is not exactly honourable, |PLAYERNAME|. Shame on you.",
  "npc.gregor.say_25": "Good work, brave Knight |PLAYERNAME|! Even though it is damaged, it has a lot of sentimental value. Now, please bring me warrior's sweat.",
  "npc.gregor.say_26": "There is no need to rush anyway.",
  "npc.gregor.say_27": "Lying is not exactly honourable, |PLAYERNAME|. Shame on you.",
  "npc.gregor.say_28": "Now that is a pleasant surprise, brave Knight |PLAYERNAME|! There is only one task left now: Obtain royal steel to have your helmet refined.",
  "npc.gregor.say_29": "There is no need to rush anyway.",
  "npc.gregor.say_30": "Lying is not exactly honourable, |PLAYERNAME|. Shame on you.",
  "npc.gregor.say_31": "You truly deserve to wear an adorned helmet, brave Knight |PLAYERNAME|. Please talk to Sam and tell him I sent you. I'm sure he will be glad to refine your helmet.",
  "npc.gregor.say_32": "There is no need to rush anyway.",
  "npc.dalbrect.say_1": "You have recovered my brooch! I shall forever be in your debt, my friend!",
  "npc.dalbrect.say_2": "What? You want me to examine a brooch?",
  "npc.dalbrect.say_3": "What are you talking about? I am too poor to be interested in jewelry.",
  "npc.dalbrect.say_4": "I should have known better than to ask for an act of kindness in this cruel, selfish, world!",
  "npc.dalbrect.say_5": "Then stop being a fool. I am poor and I have to work the whole day through!",
  "npc.dalbrect.say_6": "I should have known better than to ask for an act of kindness in this cruel, selfish, world!",
  "npc.charles.say_1": "Do you seek a shortcut passage to {Thais} for 100 gold, to {Edron} for 90 gold, to {Liberty Bay} for 20 gold or to {Yalahar} for 200 gold?",
  "npc.charles.say_2": "Set the sails and good luck to us!",
  "npc.charles.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_4": "I'm sorry but I don't sail there.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_5": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_6": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_7": "Where do you want to go - {Thais}, {Darashia}, {Venore}, {Liberty Bay}, {Ankrahmun}, {Yalahar} or {Edron?}",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_8": "Where do you want to go - {Thais}, {Darashia}, {Venore}, {Liberty Bay}, {Ankrahmun}, {Yalahar} or {Edron?}",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_9": "Im the captain of the Poodle, the proudest ship on all oceans.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_10": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_11": "That's where we are.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_12": "It's Charles.",
  "npc.charles.stdmod_13": "I'm sorry, but we don't serve the routes to the Ice Islands.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.say_1": "Seeds to give life to strong trees, blooming and proud. The {intruders} robbed us from them.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.say_2": "The intruders appeared in the blink of an eye. Out of thin air, as if they came from nowhere. They overrun the glade within ours and drove away what was remaining from us within the day.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.say_3": "The purest water flows through this well. For centuries we concealed it, for other beings to not lay their eyes on it.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.say_4": "Take care, guardian.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.say_5": "Phials for the purest water from our sacred well. They are finely crafted and very fragile. We keep a small supply up here around the well. Probably the only thing the intruders did not care for.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.say_6": "I already handed a cage to you. If you are in need of another one, you will have to return to me later.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.stdmod_7": "My name is now known only to the wind and it shall remain like this until I will return to my kin.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.stdmod_8": "I was a guardian of this glade. I am the last one... everyone had to leave.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.stdmod_9": "This glade's time is growing short if nothing will be done soon.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.stdmod_10": "Take care, guardian.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.stdmod_11": "Cruel beings. Large and monstrous, with a single eye, staring at their prey. ",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat4.say_1": "I'm not sure if you know what you are doing but anyway. Your name is?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat4.say_2": "Alright |PLAYERNAME|. Vocation?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat4.say_3": "Sorry, you need Form 145 to get Form 356. Come back when you have it",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat4.say_4": "You are better than I thought! Congratulations, here you are: Form 356!",
  "npc.jeronimo.say_1": "In our website enter in {Events} => {Events Shop}.",
  "npc.jeronimo.say_2": "You want buy {",
  "npc.jeronimo.say_3": "So... what you want?",
  "npc.jeronimo.say_4": "You don't have enough bar's.",
  "npc.jeronimo.say_5": "You bought {",
  "npc.jeronimo.say_6": "You don't have enough bar's.",
  "npc.hireling.say_1": "Sorry, but you don't have enough capacity.",
  "npc.hireling.say_2": "Sorry, you don't have enough room on your inbox.",
  "npc.hireling.say_3": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.hireling.say_4": "Very well. You may choose one of the following: {chilli con carniphila}, {svargrond salmon filet}, {carrion casserole}, {consecrated beef}, {roasted wyvern wings}, {carrot pie}, {tropical marinated tiger}, or {delicatessen salad}.",
  "npc.hireling.say_5": "Alright, let me astonish you. Shall I?",
  "npc.hireling.say_6": "Which specific meal would you like? Choices are: {chilli con carniphila}, {svargrond salmon filet}, {carrion casserole}, {consecrated beef}, {roasted wyvern wings}, {carrot pie}, {tropical marinated tiger}, or {delicatessen salad}.",
  "npc.hireling.say_7": "Yay! I have the ingredients to make a skill boost dish. Would you rather like to boost your {magic}, {melee}, {shielding}, or {distance} skill?",
  "npc.hireling.say_8": "Alright then, ask me for other {services}, if you want.",
  "npc.hireling.say_9": "Sorry, but you must choose a valid skill class. Would you like to boost your {magic}, {melee}, {shielding}, or {distance} skill?",
  "npc.hireling.say_10": "I'm sorry, but that's not a valid food option. Please choose from: {chilli con carniphila}, {svargrond salmon filet}, {carrion casserole}, {consecrated beef}, {roasted wyvern wings}, {carrot pie}, {tropical marinated tiger}, or {delicatessen salad}.",
  "npc.hireling.say_11": "Here are the items for the category ",
  "npc.hireling.say_12": "As you wish!",
  "npc.hireling.say_13": "In my youth I dreamt to wield it! Now I wield the broom of... brooming. I guess that's the next best thing!",
  "npc.hireling.say_14": "What an uncivilised place without any culture.",
  "npc.hireling.say_15": "I'll keep an eye open for it when cleaning up the things you brought home!",
  "npc.hireling.say_16": "Are you sure you want me to go back to my lamp?",
  "npc.hireling.say_17": "As you wish!",
  "npc.hireling.say_18": "Are you sure you want me to go back to my lamp?",
  "npc.hireling.say_19": "Alright then, I will be here.",
  "npc.hireling.say_20": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.sven.say_1": "A true barbarian is something special among our people. Everyone who wants to become a barbarian will have to pass the barbarian {test}.",
  "npc.sven.say_2": "Do you have some honey with you?",
  "npc.sven.say_3": "Alright, we are even!",
  "npc.sven.say_4": "You don't have enough. Bring me the money and I will forget about it.",
  "npc.sven.say_5": "Good, for this honeycomb I allow you 20 sips from the mead bucket over there. Talk to me again about barbarian mead if you have passed the test.",
  "npc.sven.say_6": "Alright, it's your choice. If you regret your decision and want to be a barbarian again, talk to me about the {barbarian} test.",
  "npc.sven.say_7": "Alright, it's your choice. If you regret your decision and want to be a barbarian again, talk to me about the {barbarian} test.",
  "npc.dove.say_1": "Oh no! I knew that day would come! I am slightly above the allowed weight and if you can't supply me with some grapes to slim down I will get fired. Do you happen to have some grapes with you? ",
  "npc.dove.say_2": "Oh thank you! Thank you so much! So listen ... <whispers her measurements> ",
  "npc.dove.say_3": "Oh, you don't have it.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_1": "I would never have guessed that.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_2": "Oh, sorry, I was distracted, what did you say?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_3": "Oh, I just remember I have some work to do, sorry. Bye!",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_4": "Take some time to talk to me!",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_5": "Well ... I have met him for a little while .. but this was nothing serious.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_6": "I remember that grapes were his favourites. He was almost addicted to them.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_7": "Thank you very much. How kind of you to care about me. I am fine, thank you.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_8": "This is the continent you are currently visiting. You will find vast, dry steppes here as well as high mountains, the river Nykri and the big city {Issavi}.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_9": "Issavi is the capital of {Kilmaresh}, also called the Golden City. This city has a motto: An open gate for those of peace. This means, anyone is welcome here as long as they respect our laws, be it humans, elves, minotaurs or even a medusa.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_10": "I am Aruda.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_11": "I am a little sad, that you seem to have forgotten me, handsome. I am Aruda.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_12": "Yes, that's me!",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_13": "Oh, I like it, how you say my name.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_14": "Please don't be so rude to look for the time if you are talking to me.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_15": "I am deeply sorry, I can't help you.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_16": "UH! What a terrifying topic. Please let us speak about something more pleasant, I am a weak and small woman after all.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_17": "What gives you the impression, I am the kind of women, you find in sewers?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_18": "You should ask about that in one of the temples.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_19": "The king, that lives in this fascinating castle? I think he does look kind of cute in his luxurious robes, doesn't he?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_20": "He is soooo strong! What muscles! What a body! Did you ask him for a date?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_21": "He is soooo strong! What muscles! What a body! On the other hand, compared to you he looks quite puny.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_22": "He is a little simple minded but always nice and well dressed.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_23": "He should really sell some stylish gowns or something like that. We Tibians never get some clothing of the latest fashion. It's a shame.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_24": "I don't understand this lonely monks. I love company too much to become one. Hehehe!",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_25": "Oh, isn't he funny? I could listen to him the whole day.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_26": "As far as I know, he is working in the castle.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_27": "I am a little shy and so don't hear many rumors.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_28": "Oh, you little devil, stop talking like that! <blush>",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_29": "I know only little about weapons. Can you tell me something about them, please?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_30": "I believe that love is stronger than magic, don't you agree?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_31": "Oh, sorry, I have to hurry, bye!",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_32": "I would like to visit the beach more often, but I guess it's too dangerous.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_33": "I love this castle! It's so beautiful.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_34": "Powerful sorcerers frighten me a little.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_35": "I personally think it's inappropriate for a woman to become a warrior, what do you think about that?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_36": "Druids seldom visit a town, what do you know about druids?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_37": "I like brave fighters like him.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_38": "Oh, he is sooooo cute!",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_39": "I like dogs, the little ones at least. Do you like dogs, too?",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_40": "Oh, I am just a girl and know nothing about magic swords and such things.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_41": "I ... don't know someone named like that.",
  "npc.guard_saros.say_42": "Yenny? I know no Yenny, nor have I ever used that name! You have mistook me with someone else.",
  "npc.servant_sentry.stdmod_1": "Our. Master. Is. Gone. You. Can. Not. Visit. Him! We. Stand. {Sentry}!",
  "npc.servant_sentry.stdmod_2": "{Master}. Conducted. Experiments. Great. Problems. You. Must. Go!",
  "npc.servant_sentry.stdmod_3": "{Slime}. Dangerous. We. Have. It. Under. Control. ... We. Will. Stand. {Sentry}.",
  "npc.servant_sentry.say_4": "The. {Slime}. Has. Entered. Our. {Master}. Has. Left! We. Must. {Help}.",
  "npc.servant_sentry.say_5": "Defeat. {Slime}. We. Will. Why. Did. You. Kill. Us? Do. You. Want. To. Rectify. And. Help?",
  "npc.servant_sentry.say_6": "Then. Take. This. Gobbler. Always. Hungry. Eats. Slime. Fungus. Go.",
  "npc.morgan.say_1": "Ahh. So Duncan sent you, eh? You must have done something really impressive. Okay, take this fine sabre from me, mate.",
  "npc.morgan.say_2": "Thank you for delivering my letter to Eremo. I have no more missions for you.",
  "npc.morgan.say_3": "You already have this outfit!",
  "npc.morgan.say_4": "Great! Simply bring me 100 iron ore and one royal steel and I will happily {forge} it for you.",
  "npc.morgan.say_5": "Alright! As a matter of fact, I have one in store. Here you go!",
  "npc.morgan.say_6": "You do not have all the required items.",
  "npc.morgan.say_7": "You already have this outfit!",
  "npc.morgan.say_8": "Great! Simply bring me 100 Iron Ore and one Crude Iron and I will happily {forge} it for you.",
  "npc.morgan.say_9": "Alright! As a matter of fact, I have one in store. Here you go!",
  "npc.morgan.say_10": "You do not have all the required items.",
  "npc.morgan.say_11": "What would you like me to forge for you? A {knight's sword} or a {warrior's sword}?",
  "npc.morgan.say_12": "Alright, we will see. Here, take this letter and deliver it safely to old Eremo on Cormaya.",
  "npc.percybald.say_1": "I hope you learnt your role! I'll tell you a line from the script and you'll have to answer with the corresponding line! Ready?",
  "npc.percybald.say_2": "How dare you? Are you mad? I hold the princess hostage and you drop your weapons. You're all lost!",
  "npc.percybald.say_3": "Too late puny knight. You can't stop my master plan anymore!",
  "npc.percybald.say_4": "What's this? Behind the doctor?",
  "npc.percybald.say_5": "Haha! You may not fear for your own life, but how about hers!?",
  "npc.percybald.say_6": "Grrr!",
  "npc.percybald.say_7": "You're such a monster!",
  "npc.percybald.say_8": "Ah well, I think you passed the test! Here is your disguise kit! Now get lost, fate awaits me!",
  "npc.percybald.say_9": "Ok, ok. You've got this one right! Ready for the next one?",
  "npc.percybald.say_10": "No no no! That is not correct!",
  "npc.percybald.say_11": "Ok, ok. You've got this one right! Ready for the next one?",
  "npc.percybald.say_12": "No no no! That is not correct!",
  "npc.percybald.say_13": "Ok, ok. You've got this one right! Ready for the next one?",
  "npc.percybald.say_14": "No no no! That is not correct!",
  "npc.percybald.say_15": "Ok, ok. You've got this one right! Ready for the next one?",
  "npc.percybald.say_16": "No no no! That is not correct!",
  "npc.percybald.say_17": "Ok, ok. You've got this one right! Ready for the next one?",
  "npc.percybald.say_18": "No no no! That is not correct!",
  "npc.percybald.say_19": "Ok, ok. You've got this one right! Ready for the next one?",
  "npc.percybald.say_20": "No no no! That is not correct!",
  "npc.percybald.say_21": "In exchange for a generous donation of gold and silver tokens, I can offer you a special outfit. Would you like to donate?",
  "npc.percybald.say_22": "If you haven't made up your mind, please come back when you are ready.",
  "npc.percybald.say_23": "Take this armor as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend!",
  "npc.percybald.say_24": "You do not have enough tokens to donate that amount.",
  "npc.percybald.say_25": "You already have that addon.",
  "npc.percybald.say_26": "Take this shield as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend.",
  "npc.percybald.say_27": "You do not have enough tokens to donate that amount.",
  "npc.percybald.say_28": "You already have that outfit.",
  "npc.percybald.say_29": "You need to donate the {armor} outfit first.",
  "npc.percybald.say_30": "Take this crown as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend.",
  "npc.percybald.say_31": "You do not have enough tokens to donate that amount.",
  "npc.percybald.say_32": "You already have that outfit.",
  "npc.percybald.say_33": "You need to donate the {shield} addon first.",
  "npc.percybald.say_34": "Would you like to donate 15,000 silver tokens and 12,500 gold tokens for a unique red armor?",
  "npc.percybald.say_35": "Would you like to donate 7,500 silver tokens and 6,250 gold tokens for a unique shield?",
  "npc.percybald.say_36": "Would you like to donate 7,500 silver tokens and 6,250 gold tokens for a unique crown?",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_1": "Me put name away name long ago. Now only blind prophet of ape people are.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_2": "Me is who in dreams speak to holy banana. Me divine the will of banana.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_3": "Me {prophet} and {guardian} is.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_4": "Me is who in dreams speak to holy banana. Me divine the will of banana.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_5": "Me guard the forbidden land behind the great palisade. If any want to enter, he must ask me for transport.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_6": "Me guard the forbidden land behind the great palisade. If any want to enter, he must ask me for transport.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_7": "Good ape he is. Has to work hard to make other apes listen but you helped a lot.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_8": " Our holy ancestor he is. Big as mountain. Lizards say they built palisade to keep him but we not believe ... We think Bong palisade built to have peace from pesky lizards. We respect peace of Bong, keep people away from forbidden land.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_9": " The lizards evil and vengeful are. Ape people on guard must be.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_10": "Our people a lot to learn have. One day we might live in peace with you hairless apes, who knows.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_11": "Me not know. Me seldom have visions of not banana related objects.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.stdmod_12": "Hairless apes strange people are. ",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.say_13": "You want me to transport you to forbidden land?",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.say_14": "Take care!",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.say_15": "You are not worthy to be transported there yet.",
  "npc.the_blind_prophet.say_16": "Wise decision maybe.",
  "npc.marina.say_1": "Um. You mean, you really want me to touch that gooey spider silk just because you need yarn? Well... do you think that I'm pretty?",
  "npc.marina.say_2": "Okay... a deal is a deal, would you like me to create a {spool of yarn} from {10 pieces of spider silk}?",
  "npc.marina.say_3": "Did you bring me the 50 honeycombs I requested and do you absolutely admire my beauty?",
  "npc.marina.say_4": "<giggles> I think he has a crush on me. Well, silly man, it is only for his own good. This way he can get accustomed to TRUE beauty. And I won't give him up anymore now that he is mine.",
  "npc.marina.say_5": "Is that the best you can do? A true Djinn would have done something more poetic.",
  "npc.marina.say_6": "Well, everyone would say that in your position. Do you think that I'm really, absolutely the most stunning being that you have ever seen?",
  "npc.marina.say_7": "Oh goodie! Thank you! Okay... I guess since my fingers are sticky now anyway, I will help you. From now on, if you bring me {10 pieces of spider silk}, I will create one {spool of yarn}.",
  "npc.marina.say_8": "You don't have enough honey.",
  "npc.marina.say_9": "Ew... gooey... there you go.",
  "npc.marina.say_10": "You don't have the required items.",
  "npc.marina.stdmod_11": "Sorry, I don't have a spare comb. I lost my favourite one when diving around in Calassa.",
  "npc.storkus.say_1": "So they've sent another one? I just hope ye' better than the last one. Are ye' ready for a mission?",
  "npc.storkus.say_2": "Fine, you're done! Ye' should talk to me about your {mission} again now.",
  "npc.storkus.say_3": "Have ye' killed the vampire lord? Because ye' have no his ring.",
  "npc.storkus.say_4": "Would ye' like to give me vampire tokens?",
  "npc.storkus.say_5": "Would ye' like to give me vampire tokens?",
  "npc.storkus.say_6": "Would ye' like to give me vampire tokens?",
  "npc.storkus.say_7": "Would ye' like to give me vampire tokens?",
  "npc.storkus.say_8": "Would ye' like to give me vampire tokens?",
  "npc.storkus.say_9": "Would ye' like to give me vampire tokens?",
  "npc.storkus.say_10": "Ye' brought the token needed to advance to the first vampire hunter rank. I consider that a fluke, but still, congrats! Let me share some of my experience with ye'.",
  "npc.storkus.say_11": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_12": "Ye' brought the four tokens needed to advance to the second vampire hunter rank. Pretty lucky ye' are! Let me share some of my experience with ye'.",
  "npc.storkus.say_13": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_14": "Ye' brought the five tokens needed to advance to the third vampire hunter rank. Wow, you're pretty determined! Let me share some of my experience with ye'.",
  "npc.storkus.say_15": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_16": "Ye' brought the ten tokens needed to advance to the fourth vampire hunter rank. You're absolutely painstaking! Let me share some of my experience with ye'.",
  "npc.storkus.say_17": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_18": "Ye' brought the thirty tokens needed to advance to the fifth vampire hunter rank. You're completely obliterative, kid! Let me share some of my experience with ye'.",
  "npc.storkus.say_19": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_20": "Ye' brought the fifty tokens needed to advance to the last vampire hunter rank. Now that's something. You're razing-amazing! Let me share some of my experience and a little something with ye'!",
  "npc.storkus.say_21": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_22": "As they might have told ye', I'm a vampire hunter. If ye' want to be of any help, ye' can assist me with some of my tasks and bring me 20 ounces of vampire dust. This gives me some time to concentrate on a bigger project.",
  "npc.storkus.say_23": "Ye' don't have enought tokens.",
  "npc.storkus.say_24": "As they might have told ye', I'm a vampire hunter. If ye' want to be of any help, ye' can assist me with some of my tasks and bring me 20 ounces of vampire dust. This gives me some time to concentrate on a bigger project.",
  "npc.taegen.say_1": "Then not.",
  "npc.jack.say_1": "Gesundheit! Are you alright? Did you... want to tell me something by that?",
  "npc.jack.say_2": "What have you done? What are all these pieces of furniture doing here? Those are ugly at best and - hey! Stop! Leave the wallpaper alone! Alright, alright! Just tell me, why are you doing this? Who's behind all this?",
  "npc.jack.say_3": "WHAT?? No way, I ask you again - you DID tell me the TRUTH here... right?",
  "npc.jack.say_4": "So that's it? Really?",
  "npc.jack.say_5": "Yeah, yeah... so what are you still doing here? I guess I... will have to seek out this Spectulus now, see what he has to say. There is nothing left for me in this place.",
  "npc.jack.say_6": "I... was... sculpting sulky sculptures. For all my life. Until you came in here and DESTROYED MY MASTERPIECE. Go away. I don't like you.",
  "npc.lukosch.say_1": "Do you want to purchase a weekly ticket for the ore wagons? With it you can travel freely and swiftly through Kazordoon for one week. 250 gold only. Deal?",
  "npc.lukosch.say_2": "Your weekly ticket is still valid. Would be a waste of money to purchase a second one",
  "npc.lukosch.say_3": "Here is your stamp. It can't be transferred to another person and will last one week from now. You'll get notified upon using an ore wagon when it isn't valid anymore.",
  "npc.lukosch.say_4": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.lukosch.say_5": "No then.",
  "npc.alwin.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.cael.say_1": "Oh! That sounds fascinating. Have you found a Tome of Knowledge for me to read?",
  "npc.cael.say_2": "Oh! That sounds fascinating. Have you found a new Tome of Knowledge for me to read?",
  "npc.cael.say_3": "Oh! That sounds fascinating. Have you found a new Tome of Knowledge for me to read?",
  "npc.cael.say_4": "I'm sorry I'm busy. Speak with Ongulf to get some missions!",
  "npc.cael.say_5": "Oh! That sounds fascinating. Have you found a Tome of Knowledge for me to read? I have the feeling though that I can only share some of my experience with you now. Is that alright with you?",
  "npc.cael.say_6": "I'm sorry I'm busy. Speak with Ongulf to get some missions!",
  "npc.cael.say_7": "Thank you! I look forward to reading this interesting discovery of yours and learn a few things about {Zao}.",
  "npc.cael.say_8": "Thank you! I look forward to reading this interesting discovery of yours and learn a few things about {Zao}.",
  "npc.cael.say_9": "Thank you! I look forward to reading this interesting discovery of yours and learn a few things about {Zao}. Let me share some experience with you.",
  "npc.cael.say_10": "You dont have one!",
  "npc.cael.say_11": "I've learnt more about the {lizard} culture. It's really fascinating.",
  "npc.cael.say_12": "I've learnt more about the {minotaur} culture. It's really fascinating.",
  "npc.cael.say_13": "I've learnt more about the {Draken} culture by now. It's really fascinating.",
  "npc.cael.say_14": "I've learnt something interesting about a certain {food} that the lizardmen apparently prepare.",
  "npc.cael.say_15": "I've learnt something interesting about a city called {Zzaion}.",
  "npc.cael.say_16": "I've learnt a few things about the primitive {human} culture on this continent.",
  "npc.cael.say_17": "I've learnt something interesting about the Zao {steppe}.",
  "npc.cael.say_18": "I've learnt a few things about an illness, or how I prefer to call it, {corruption} of this land.",
  "npc.cael.say_19": "I've learnt something interesting about the Draken {origin}.",
  "npc.cael.say_20": "This book actually IS about Zao. Not about the continent, but about the mythical {founder} of the lizard dynasty.",
  "npc.cael.say_21": "I've learnt something interesting about {dragons} and their symbolism.",
  "npc.cael.say_22": "The last tome contained a lot of information about status symbols and insignia - such as {thrones} - and reveals some of the power structures in Zao.",
  "npc.cael.say_23": "I've learnt many things from your books. Still, I guess that's just a fragment of what I could still discover about this interesting continent.",
  "npc.cael.say_24": "Have you brought me a red lantern for a dragon statue?",
  "npc.cael.say_25": "Let's put this little lantern here.. there you go. I wrap it up for you, just unwrap it in your house again!",
  "npc.cael.say_26": "You don't have a red lantern.",
  "npc.cael.say_27": "Have you brought me a piece of red cloth? I can make that throne for you if you want. But remember, I won't do that all the time - so try and don't destroy it, okay?",
  "npc.cael.say_28": "Let's put this cloth over the seat.. there you go. I wrap it up for you, just unwrap it in your house again!",
  "npc.cael.say_29": "You don't have a red cloth.",
  "npc.cael.say_30": "Oh, wow! Now THAT is an interesting relic! Can I have that serpent crest?",
  "npc.cael.say_31": "Oh, wow! Now THAT is an interesting relic! Can I have that tribal crest?",
  "npc.cael.say_32": "You don't have a Warmaster Outfit or the crest to get the Addons.",
  "npc.cael.say_33": "Thank you! Let me reward you with something I stumbled across recently and which might fit your warmaster outfit perfectly.",
  "npc.cael.say_34": "You don't have a crest or already have this Outfitaddon.",
  "npc.cael.say_35": "Thank you! Let me reward you with something I stumbled across recently and which might fit your warmaster outfit perfectly.",
  "npc.cael.say_36": "You don't have a crest or already have this Outfitaddon.",
  "npc.cael.say_37": "Sorry, I don't have items to trade now.",
  "npc.hal.say_1": "Hicks! I... I... <he is obviously drunk and his report more than confusing>. ",
  "npc.hal.say_2": "You can {pass} either to the {Arena Quarter} or {Alchemist Quarter}. Which one will it be?",
  "npc.svenson.say_1": "Do you want to buy a heavy ball for 123 gold?",
  "npc.svenson.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.svenson.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.svenson.stdmod_4": "Do you want to sail ",
  "npc.svenson.stdmod_5": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.svenson.stdmod_6": "Where do you want to go? To {Tibia}, {Senja} or {Vega}?",
  "npc.svenson.stdmod_7": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.svenson.stdmod_8": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.demonguard.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.bertha.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.bertha.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.bertha.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.bertha.stdmod_4": "I sell equipment for your adventure! Just ask me for a {trade} to see my wares.",
  "npc.frosty.say_1": "You already have this sleigh!",
  "npc.frosty.say_2": "For a ",
  "npc.frosty.say_3": "Nasty creatures especially their queen that sits frozzen on her throne beneath this island.",
  "npc.frosty.say_4": "Here you are.",
  "npc.frosty.say_5": "You do not have needed items!",
  "npc.frosty.say_6": "Just tell me which {sleigh} you want to know more about.",
  "npc.frosty.say_7": "Come back when you get these items.",
  "npc.frosty.say_8": "Come back when you get these items.",
  "npc.frosty.stdmod_9": "Well why didn't you say that rightaway, if you give me such a skull I can give you one of my {sleighs}.",
  "npc.frosty.stdmod_10": "Always trying to eat my nose!",
  "npc.frosty.stdmod_11": "Always trying to eat my nose!",
  "npc.umar.say_1": "Whoa! A human! This is no place for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Go and play somewhere else.",
  "npc.umar.say_2": "|PLAYERNAME|! How's it going these days? What brings you {here}?",
  "npc.umar.say_3": "You already have the permission to enter Ashta'daramai.",
  "npc.umar.say_4": "Are you sure? You pledge loyalty to king Gabel, who is... you know. And you are willing to never ever set foot on Efreets' territory, unless you want to kill them? Yes?",
  "npc.umar.say_5": "I don't believe you! You better go now.",
  "npc.umar.say_6": "This isn't your war anyway, human.",
  "npc.umar.say_7": "This isn't your war anyway, human.",
  "npc.denominator.say_1": "Ready to {start}?",
  "npc.denominator.say_2": "Wrong. SHUT DOWN.",
  "npc.denominator.say_3": "Correct. {Next} question?",
  "npc.denominator.say_4": "SHUT DOWN.",
  "npc.denominator.say_5": "Correct. {Next} question?",
  "npc.denominator.say_6": "Wrong. SHUT DOWN.",
  "npc.denominator.say_7": "Correct. {Last} question?",
  "npc.denominator.say_8": "Wrong. SHUT DOWN.",
  "npc.denominator.say_9": "Tell me the correct number?",
  "npc.denominator.say_10": "Wrong. SHUT DOWN.",
  "npc.denominator.say_11": "Correct. The lower door is now open. The druid of Crunor lies.",
  "npc.denominator.say_12": "SHUT DOWN.",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_1": "I am a great and famous actor! Not a princess, at all. I was only PRETENDING to be a princess. But try explaining that to those stupid pirates.",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_2": "Stage acting was a waste of my immense talent. Not only am I a born leader, my talent is more profitable when it is used for conning people.",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_3": "Stage acting was a waste of my immense talent. Not only am I a born leader, my talent is more profitable when it is used for conning people.",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_4": "He was always a fool with a heart too soft to become a feared pirate.",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_5": "Me playing a princess was just part of a cunning plan we had.",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_6": "If you find some way to release me I might even let you live as reward! So you'd better do your best or I'll kill you!",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_7": "How dare you? I left to rot in this dirty cell and you have nothing better to do than chit chat?",
  "npc.a_bearded_woman.stdmod_8": "YOU .. YOU .. You are as good as dead! I will get you! Do you hear me? I will have your head! On a platter!",
  "npc.tehlim.say_1": "I warn you, those trolls are WAY more dangerous than the usual kind. Alone, I can't do anything for my brothers. Find a way to the trolls' hideout and rescue my brothers. Are you willing to help me?",
  "npc.tehlim.say_2": " Great! I hope you find my brothers. Good luck!",
  "npc.duncan.say_1": "You're talking about my sabre? Well, even though you earned our trust, you'd have to fulfill a task first before you are granted to wear such a sabre.",
  "npc.duncan.say_2": "I need a new quality atlas for our captains. Only one of the best will do it. I heard the explorers society sells the best, but only to members of a certain rank. You will have to get this rank or ask a high ranking member to buy it for you.",
  "npc.duncan.say_3": "Did you get an atlas of the explorers society as I requested?",
  "npc.duncan.say_4": "You did some impressive things. I think people here start considering you as one of us. But these are dire times and everyone of us is expected to give his best and even exceed himself. Do you think you can handle that?",
  "npc.duncan.say_5": "Did you rescue one of those poor soon-to-be baby tortoises from Nargor?",
  "npc.duncan.say_6": "Are you up to the task which I'm going to give you and willing to prove you're worthy of wearing such a sabre?",
  "npc.duncan.say_7": "Have you gathered 100 eye patches?",
  "npc.duncan.say_8": "Have you gathered 100 peg legs?",
  "npc.duncan.say_9": "Have you gathered 100 hooks?",
  "npc.duncan.say_10": "Good! Come back to me once you have gathered 100 eye patches.",
  "npc.duncan.say_11": "Good job. Alright, now bring me 100 peg legs.",
  "npc.duncan.say_12": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.duncan.say_13": "Nice. Lastly, bring me 100 pirate hooks. That should be enough to earn your sabre.",
  "npc.duncan.say_14": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.duncan.say_15": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.duncan.say_16": "Indeed, what a fine work... the book I mean. Your work was acceptable all in all.",
  "npc.duncan.say_17": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.duncan.say_18": "A real tortoise egg ... I guess you are more accustomed to rescue some noblewoman in distress but you did something goodtoday.",
  "npc.duncan.say_19": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.duncan.say_20": "Then no.",
  "npc.duncan.say_21": "Then no.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_1": "Very good. But now you need the Ring of Secret Thoughts back in order to extract the Ambassador's memories.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_2": "You found the Ring of Secret Thoughts! Well done! Now give it to the Ambassador as a present. He's a peacock and will accept such a precious gift for sure. As soon as he wears it, his memories will be stored in the ring.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_3": "I'm willing to admit that I need help. And the help of someone who is not from {Issavi} at that. But the task could be dangerous and you would become embroiled in the politics and court intrigues of {Kilmaresh}. Will you help me anyhow?",
  "npc.eshaya.say_4": "This is the proof we need! Very well done! You have to report this to our {Empress}. She will grant you an audience now.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_5": "You haven't completed your mission yet. Keep searching!",
  "npc.eshaya.say_6": "I don't know whether you are experienced in such things. If not, you could ask somebody who is. But I'm not sure where in Issavi you should look to hire a thief.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_7": "I guess claiming back a present would be a bit suspicious. You'll have to find another way. I resent thinking about theft but sometimes, desperate times call for desperate measures.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_8": "You got the ring back? Very well done! Now search for the memories that will prove the Ambassador's treason. I don't know much about ancient artefacts but you could ask the librarian in the palace. I'm sure he knows something helpful.",
  "npc.eshaya.say_9": "Good luck on your audience with the Empress. May Kilmaresh prosper.",
  "npc.cillia.say_1": "The exhibition is not for free. You have to pay 50 Gold to get in. Next please!",
  "npc.cillia.say_2": "And here we go!",
  "npc.cillia.say_3": "Then not.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.say_1": "You want trip to Izzle of Zzao?",
  "npc.zurak_arena.say_2": "You need permission to travel to.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.say_3": "It'zz done your travel to.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.say_4": "Zzoftzzkinzz zzo full of fear.",
  "npc.zurak_arena.say_5": "Me zzimple ferryman. I arrange {trip} to Zzao.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.say_1": "Alright, you delivered the parcel. So what is the password Thanita told you?",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.say_2": "I am not sure if I should be glad now or not but anyway ... you will get a password so I will know if you just threw it away or actually delivered it. Here is the parcel. See you ....or not.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.say_3": "That's right. Here is your reward some elementary arrows. You did pretty well on your mission!",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_4": "Salutations, commoner |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_5": "We are in constant training and in perfect health.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_6": "I am the general of the queen's army. I don't have time to explain this concept to you.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_7": "Our family has been serving the Carlin army since countless generations!",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_8": "Our family has been serving the Carlin army since countless generations!",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_9": "She is one of my beloved sisters and serves Carlin as a town guard.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_10": "HAIL TO QUEEN ELOISE, OUR NOBLE {LEADER}!",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_11": "Queen Eloise is a fine leader for our fair town, indeed!",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_12": "The army protects the defenceless males of our {city}. Our elite forces are the {Green Ferrets}.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_13": "Our city blends in with the nature surrounding it. Our {druids} take care of that.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_14": "They are our main magic support and play a major role in our battle {tactics}.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_15": "Our tactic is to kiss.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_16": "K.I.S.S.! Keep It Simple, Stupid! Complicated tactics are too easy to be crushed by a twist of fate.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_17": "Our elite forces are trained by rangers and druids. In the woods they come a close second to elves.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_18": "Join what?",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.stdmod_19": "Sorry, we don't recruit foreigners. Maybe you can join if you prove yourself in a mission for the queen.",
  "npc.edron_guardsman.say_1": "Move on!",
  "npc.the_beggar_king.say_1": "So I guess you are the one that the magistrate is sending to look after us, eh? ",
  "npc.the_beggar_king.say_2": "You need some quests then come and talk with me again.",
  "npc.the_beggar_king.say_3": "Yeah. No one has seen it and lived to tell the tale. People are missing and sometimes there are {traces} of blood or someone heard a scream, but that's all. We have no idea if the killer is a man or a beast, but there is something out there",
  "npc.the_beggar_king.say_4": "Some of the more daring of us tried to follow the tracks that were left, but they always lost the trail close to the {abandoned sewers}, in the east of the sewer system.",
  "npc.razan.say_1": "My turban? Eh no, you can't have it. Only oriental weapon masters may wear it after having completed a difficult task.",
  "npc.razan.say_2": "You mean, you would like to prove that you deserve to wear such a turban?",
  "npc.razan.say_3": "Excellent! Come back to me once you have collected 100 pieces of ape fur.",
  "npc.razan.say_4": "That is a shameless lie.",
  "npc.razan.say_5": "What a pity.",
  "npc.bozo.say_1": "Wow, your stupidity would be pride and joy for every fool. You've already applied as a member. Let's rather talk about your current mission.",
  "npc.bozo.say_2": "Do you wish to become a jester and join the fools guild?",
  "npc.bozo.say_3": "I'm sure it suits you well.",
  "npc.bozo.say_4": "No, you aren't! Why do only fools apply for the fools guild?",
  "npc.bozo.say_5": "Eeeek! What have you done?? These pies are crawling with bugs! Those must be the infamous parcel bugs! Get some new pies at once you wannabe fool, and this time without any bugs!",
  "npc.bozo.say_6": "No, you don't! Why do only fools apply for the fools guild?",
  "npc.bozo.say_7": "Too bad, I'm convinced you have it in you.",
  "npc.bozo.say_8": "You won't be successful in the fool's world with such an attitude.",
  "npc.bozo.say_9": "You wasted the disguise?? Why do only fools apply for the fools guild? Here... try again, but be wittier this time.",
  "npc.bozo.say_10": "Oh boy, why do only fools apply for the fools guild?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_11": "I wanted to become a sorcerer, too, but I was overqualified!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_12": "I wanted to become a druid, too, but I was overqualified!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_13": "I wanted to become a paladin, too, but I was overqualified!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_14": "I wanted to become a knight, too, but I was overqualified!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_15": "The good thing about them is that they can't be at two places at the same time.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_16": "I wonder if they love my water squirt flowers as much as all other plants.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_17": "They are the king's favourites, because they know how to 'bow'.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_18": "Did you notice that old knights have their scars just on their backs?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_19": "A fitting place for a {jester}. I guess there are worse {jobs} around.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_20": "Bozo: Nah, no jests about His Royal Highness.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_21": "I rarely leave the castle. It's really stressful to be as popular as me.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_22": "This castle is my home. A fitting place for a jester and all other fools. Feel welcome.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_23": "I'm a jester, not a doctor!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_24": "My name is Bozo. But it's more than a name, it's a lifestyle for me!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_25": "That's me: Bozo, the jester!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_26": "Ever since the first guild was created, there is a great demand of jesters and fools to join them.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_27": "Sell? Hmm, I know a little about magic and by chance I can sell you a truly unusual {weapon}.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_28": "I know some 'monstrous' jokes!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_29": "I know the newest jokes in tibia.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_30": "Thank you, I'm fine, the gods are with me.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_31": "Pheeew! That sounds disgusting! Are you a cook at Frodo's?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_32": "Don't feed the necromants.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_33": "Are we talking about Noodles?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_34": "Are we talking about Noodles?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_35": "Hey, the little one is almost as funny as me!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_36": "Better don't mess with sorcerers!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_37": "She's pretty but too serious for my taste.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_38": "Humourless old guy! Once, he turned me into a frog for painting his distasteful cave in pink.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_39": "A man of steel with a stomach of wax. Never offer him a beer!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_40": "He's my baby brother. If you tell him I sent you, he will grant you an extra spell or two.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_41": "He sells spell scrolls each day at midnight, but you have to address him that very second.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_42": "I better make no jokes about THIS matter.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_43": "Did you know that he sells a 'power axe of doom' now? Run and buy it, he only has got three in store.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_44": "He would make a fine jester, too.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_45": "I know a lot of monster jokes. Just tell me a monster's name, come on.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_46": "Why are the experienced heroes quicker than others? ... The demons love fast food!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_47": "Where do ghouls buy their robes? ... In a boooohtique!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_48": "Why do dragons breathe fire? ... They ate too many sorcerers in chilli sauce!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_49": "Why do orcs have green skin? ... They ate at Frodo's!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_50": "How many eyes does a cyclops have? ... One for each IQ point they have!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_51": "If you believe half the rumours he's spreading, you will get in a lot of trouble.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_52": "If you are a bad jester, you get a chance to visit them now and then.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_53": "What do all little minotaurs want to become when they are grown-ups? ... Cowboys, of course!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_54": "Why do trolls live underground? ... Because there are so many pks on the surface!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_55": "Why are bonelords so ugly? ... Because their mom and dad were bonelords, too!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_56": "Why does the rat have a wooden leg? ... Because it is a former pirate!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_57": "Why did the spider cross the road? ... Because it ... oh you already know this one!?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_58": "I had a cousin named like that.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_59": "He died some years ago.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_60": "Isn't he the author of the book 'Fun with Demons'?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_61": "He is kind of a father figure to me. Of course he denies all kinship to me.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_62": "He's a smart one. I heared he hid in a foreign country as the first bugs showed up.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_63": "I am not foolish enough to believe in the existence of this weapon.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_64": "Oh, I saw some demon carvings in the dungeons as I hid there after a little joke on old Stutch.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_65": "Yes, they showed demons, seven actually, dancing around a sword! In something like a flaming pit.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_66": "Ah, don't ask me! Usually mages and mystics know more about such stuff.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_67": "I'm the royal jes ... uhm ... the royal tax-collector! Do you want to pay your taxes?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_68": "Come back, when you have enough money.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_69": "Thank you very much. I will have a drink or two on your health!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_70": "Well, perhaps later.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_71": "I actually know some spells! Do you want to learn how to 'lessen your load' for 200 gold?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_72": "Come back, when you have enough money.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_73": "Here you are, I already lessened your load.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_74": "You don't know what offer you are missing!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_75": "Do you want to buy a 'mace of the fury' for 250 gold?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_76": "Come back, when you have enough money.",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_77": "And here it is, it suits you well!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_78": "You dont know what offer you have passed!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_79": "Uh, go away!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_80": "Do you want to kiss me?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_81": "Uh, oh! ... I am seeing stars!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_82": "Pah, I didn't want to kiss you anyway!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_83": "Well, women don't behave necessarily in a ladylike way just because they dress like one!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_84": "Has any man said to you that you're not only beautiful but also intelligent?",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_85": "This is a world of fantasy and full of surprises!",
  "npc.bozo.stdmod_86": "Well, think about it!",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_1": "Well, har har. Very funny. Come on, pick up the gold you just dropped.",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_2": "What? Whatever that is, it's not a port I sail to. ",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_3": "What? Whatever that is, it's not a port I sail to. ",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_4": "Changed your mind? Which city do you want to head to, ",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_5": "Changed your mind? Which city do you want to head to, ",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_6": "Errr... was that a foreign language? Could you just answer with a clear {yes} or {no}?",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_7": "Aw, come on! Talk to me in human words! {Yes}, {no}, or mention a city's name, that kind of stuff.",
  "npc.captain_dreadnought.say_8": "Aw, come on! Talk to me in human words! {Yes}, {no}, or mention a city's name, that kind of stuff.",
  "npc.wyda.say_1": "You brought me a cookie?",
  "npc.wyda.say_2": "Arrr... here we go again.... do you have a #$*§# blood herb for me?",
  "npc.wyda.say_3": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.wyda.say_4": "Well, it's a welcome change from all that gingerbread ... AHHH HOW DARE YOU??? FEEL MY WRATH!",
  "npc.wyda.say_5": "Thank you -SOOO- much! No, I really mean it! Really! Here, let me give you a reward...",
  "npc.wyda.say_6": "Thank you -SOOO- much! No, I really mean it! Really! Ah, you know what, you can have this old thing...",
  "npc.wyda.say_7": "No, you don't have any...",
  "npc.wyda.say_8": "I see.",
  "npc.lubo.say_1": "Sorry, the backpack I wear is not for sale. It's handmade from rare minotaur leather.",
  "npc.lubo.say_2": "Ah, right, almost forgot about the backpack! Have you brought me 100 pieces of minotaur leather as requested?",
  "npc.lubo.say_3": "Just in time! Your backpack is finished. Here you go, I hope you like it.",
  "npc.lubo.say_4": "Uh... I didn't expect you to return that early. Sorry, but I'm not finished yet with your backpack. I'm doing the best I can, promised.",
  "npc.lubo.say_5": "Sorry, but I can only make one backpack per person, else I'd have to close my shop and open a leather manufactory.",
  "npc.lubo.say_6": "Well, if you really like this backpack, I could make one for you, but minotaur leather is hard to come by these days. Are you willing to put some work into this?",
  "npc.lubo.say_7": "Alright then, if you bring me 100 pieces of fine minotaur leather I will see what I can do for you. You probably have to kill really many minotaurs though... so good luck!",
  "npc.lubo.say_8": "Sorry, but I don't run a welfare office, you know... no pain, no gain.",
  "npc.lubo.say_9": "Sorry, but that's not enough leather yet to make one of these backpacks. Would you rather like to buy a normal backpack for 10 gold?",
  "npc.lubo.say_10": "Great! Alright, I need a while to finish this backpack for you. Come ask me later, okay?",
  "npc.lubo.say_11": "I know, it's quite some work... don't lose heart, just keep killing minotaurs and you'll eventually get lucky. Would you rather like to buy a normal backpack for 10 gold?",
  "npc.lubo.say_12": "Ah yes, I remember my grandfather talking about that name. This house used to be an inn a long time ago. My family bought it from some of these flower guys.",
  "npc.lubo.say_13": "Oh, I mean druids of course. They sold the cottage to my family after some of them died in an accident or something like that.",
  "npc.lubo.say_14": "As far as I can remember the story, a pet escaped its stable behind the inn. It got somehow involved with powerful magic at a ritual and was transformed in some way.",
  "npc.lubo.say_15": "My grandpa told me, in the old days there were some behind this cottage. Nothing big though, just small ones, for chicken or rabbits.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_16": "I am selling equipment for adventurers. If you need anything, let me know.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_17": "This is Ruffy my dog, please don't do him any harm.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_18": "I sell torches, fishing rods, worms, ropes, water hoses, backpacks, apples, and maps.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_19": "I am Lubo, the owner of this shop.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_20": "Oh! I'm sorry, I sold the last one just five minutes ago.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_21": "My hat? Hanna made this one for me.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_22": "Oh, you sure mean this old story about the mage Dago, who lost two fingers when he conjured a dragon.",
  "npc.lubo.stdmod_23": "There are some strange stories about a magicians pet names. Ask Hoggle about it.",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.say_1": "So be it!",
  "npc.sinclair.say_1": "So, did you find anything worth examining? Did you actually catch a ghost?",
  "npc.sinclair.say_2": "So you have passed Spectulus' acceptance test. Well, I'm sure you will live up to that. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.say_3": "You already done this quest.",
  "npc.sinclair.say_4": "Talk research with spectulus to take some mission.",
  "npc.sinclair.say_5": "Good, now all you need to do is find a ghost, defeat it and catch its very essence with the cage. Once you have it, return to me and Spectulus and I will move it into our chamber device. Good luck, return to me as soon as you are prepared.",
  "npc.sinclair.say_6": "Go and use the machine in a dead ghost!",
  "npc.sinclair.say_7": "Good, of course you will also receive an additional monetary reward for your troubles. Are you fine with that?",
  "npc.sinclair.say_8": "Alright, let us see how many ghosts you caught!",
  "npc.sinclair.say_9": "You didnt catch the ghost pieces.",
  "npc.sinclair.say_10": " Alright you found something! Are you really finished hunting out there?",
  "npc.erayo.say_1": "Vescu gave you an assassin outfit? Haha. Noticed it lacks the head piece? You look a bit silly. Want my old head piece?",
  "npc.erayo.say_2": "Good. Start with the blue cloth. I'll wait.",
  "npc.erayo.say_3": "You don't have the required items.",
  "npc.erayo.say_4": "Maybe another time.",
  "npc.carlos.say_1": "Very well. Just choose an outfit and a colour combination that suits you. You can open this dialogue anytime by right-clicking on yourself and selecting 'Set Outfit'. Just try it and then talk to me again!",
  "npc.carlos.say_2": "You see, I'm quite hungry from standing here all day. Could you get me some {food}?",
  "npc.carlos.say_3": "Thank you! I would do it myself, but I don't have a weapon. Just kill a few rabbits or deer, loot food from them and bring me one piece of {meat} or ham, will you?",
  "npc.carlos.say_4": "Splendid. I'll be awaiting your return eagerly. Don't forget that you can click on the 'Chase Opponent' button to run after those fast creatures. Good {bye} for now!",
  "npc.carlos.say_5": "What's that delicious smell? That must be a piece of meat! Please hurry, simply ask me for a {trade} and I'll give you two gold pieces for it!",
  "npc.carlos.say_6": "Hmm. No, I don't think you have something with you that I'd like to eat. Please come back once you looted a piece of meat or a piece of ham from a rabbit or deer.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_1": "I have heard that it was recently planned to expand the Museum of Tibian Arts. In the course of these activities unexpected difficulties occurred.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_2": "That's simply a scientific sensation. It will provide me with lots of much needed knowledge!",
  "npc.dedoras.say_3": "There are rumors of a mysterious statue in the desert next to Darashia. Nobody really knows the meaning of it.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_4": "You brought incredible news. This book proves an invaluable clue!",
  "npc.dedoras.say_5": "You brought incredible news. This book proves an invaluable clue!",
  "npc.dedoras.say_6": "This is incredible! Thank you so much for digging out that hint!",
  "npc.dedoras.say_7": "Thank you so much for your efforts to provide this valuable piece of the puzzle!",
  "npc.dedoras.say_8": "Talk to Captain Charles in Port Hope. He told me that he once ran ashore on a small island where he discovered a small ruin. The architecture was like nothing he had seen before.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_9": "You're still searching for informations.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_10": "Are you interested in one or two addons to your battle mage outfit?",
  "npc.dedoras.say_11": "Very good! You gained the first addon to the battle mage outfit.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_12": "Very good! You gained the second addon to the battle mage outfit.",
  "npc.dedoras.say_13": "I provide two addons. For the first one I need you to bring me five sturdy books. For the second addon you need twenty epaulettes. Do you want one of these addons?",
  "npc.dedoras.say_14": "What do you have for me: the sturdy books or the epaulettes?",
  "npc.dedoras.stdmod_15": "I need the help of some competent {adventurers} to handle a threat to all creation.",
  "npc.dedoras.stdmod_16": "This leaves us with no choice but to take action into our own {hands}.",
  "npc.dedoras.stdmod_17": "I guess you know about the {background} and there is no need to tell you that the forces from beyond managed to acquire the parts of the godbreaker in a coup.",
  "npc.dedoras.stdmod_18": "The secret locations of the godbreaker {parts} were revealed and due to trickery, the minions of Variphor aquired all of them.",
  "npc.dedoras.stdmod_19": "Those pieces of knowledge come in several forms and shapes. For most I can give you more or less specific hints where to start your {search}.",
  "npc.dedoras.stdmod_20": "You have to {find} the veiled hoard of Zathroth, breach it and destroy the knowledge how to use the godbreaker.",
  "npc.busty_bonecrusher.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.palomino.say_1": "We can bring you to Venore with one of our coaches for 125 gold. Are you interested?",
  "npc.palomino.say_2": "Do you want to rent a horse for one day at a price of 500 gold?",
  "npc.palomino.say_3": "First get rid of those blood stains!",
  "npc.palomino.say_4": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.palomino.say_5": "Have a nice trip!",
  "npc.palomino.say_6": "You already have a horse.",
  "npc.palomino.say_7": "You do not have enough money to rent a horse!",
  "npc.palomino.say_8": "I'll give you one of our experienced ones. Take care! Look out for low hanging branches.",
  "npc.palomino.say_9": "Then not.",
  "npc.a_swan.say_1": "You need to deliver me like 5 feathers.",
  "npc.a_swan.say_2": "You are not on that mission.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_1": "If you have any {silver} tokens with you, let's have a look! Maybe I can offer you something in exchange.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_2": "With pleasure. <bows> I trade {token}s. There are several ways to obtain the {token}s I am interested in - killing certain bosses, for example. In exchange for a certain amount of tokens, I can offer you some first-class items.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_3": "Here's the deal, ",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_4": "Sorry, you don't have an unenchanted ",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_5": "Alright, come back if you have changed your mind.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_6": "Ah, very good. Now choose your addon: {first} or {second}.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_7": "Sorry, friend, but one good turn deserves another. You need to obtain the rift warrior outfit first.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_8": "Ah, excellent. Obtain the first addon for your rift warrior outfit.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_9": "Sorry, friend, you already have the first Rift Warrior addon.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_10": "Ah, excellent. Obtain the second addon for your rift warrior outfit.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_11": "Sorry, friend, you already have the second Rift Warrior addon.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_12": "Ah, very good. Now choose your addon: {first} or {second}.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_13": "Sorry, friend, but one good turn deserves another. You need to obtain the rift warrior outfit first.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_14": "Ah, excellent. Obtain the first addon for your rift warrior outfit.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_15": "Sorry, friend, but one good turn deserves another. Bring enough ",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_16": "Sorry, friend, you already have the first Rift Warrior addon.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_17": "Ah, excellent. Obtain the second addon for your rift warrior outfit.",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_18": "Sorry, friend, but one good turn deserves another. Bring enough ",
  "npc.cledwyn.say_19": "Sorry, friend, you already have the second Rift Warrior addon.",
  "npc.boozer.say_1": "Yessss! Now I only need to build my own small brewery, figure out the secret recipe, duplicate the dwarvish brew and BANG I'll be back in business! Here take this as a reward.",
  "npc.boozer.say_2": "Shush!! I don't want everybody to know what I am up to. Listen, things are not going too well, I need a new attraction. Do you want to help me?",
  "npc.boozer.say_3": "Good! Listen closely. Take this bottle and go to Kazordoon. I need a sample of their very special brown ale. You may find a cask in their brewery. Come back as soon as you got it.",
  "npc.eroth.say_1": "Have you ever heard of Elvenbane? It is the castle west of Ab'Dendriel which is inhabited by villains from all over the continent. Any support in this war is welcome. Are you willing to help?",
  "npc.eroth.say_2": "I heard the blow! The reflection must have caused a overcharge of magical energy leading to the contraction and the implosion. Just like I hoped! Please take this as a reward. Thank you very much.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_3": "I am the leader of the Cenath caste.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_4": "The Kuridai are aggressive and victims of their instincts. Without our help they would surely die in a foolish war.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_5": "Gods are for the weak. We will master the world on our own. We need no gods.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_6": "They lack the understanding of unity. We are keeping them together and prevent them from being slaughtered one by one.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_7": "We are the shepherds of our people. The other castes need our guidance.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_8": "Magic comes almost naturally to the Cenath. We keep the secrets of ages.",
  "npc.eroth.stdmod_9": "I can teach the spells 'magic shield', 'destroy field', 'creature illusion', 'chameleon', 'convince creature', and 'summon creature'.",
  "npc.sebastian.say_1": "Do you want to sail Nargor for 50 gold coins?",
  "npc.sebastian.say_2": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_1": "Great! A warm welcome to our newest member: |PLAYERNAME|! Ask me for a {task} if you want to go on a hunt.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_3": "You'll have to {join}, to get any {tasks}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_4": "You are ready to advance one rank in our society |PLAYERNAME|. Ask me for a {promotion} first.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_5": "You're lucky today. This time you'll get an experience reward and ",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_6": "You've three unfinished tasks running old chap. If you want to accept a new one, you have to delete one of your old ones. Do you want to delete a task?",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_7": "Alright, what would you like to hunt? {Crocodiles}, {badgers}, {tarantulas}, {carniphilas}, {stone golems}, {mammoths}, {gnarlhounds}, {terramites}, {apes}, {thornback tortoises} or {gargoyles}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_8": "You've three unfinished tasks running old chap. If you want to accept a new one, you have to delete one of your old ones. Do you want to delete a task?",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_9": "The spawn of pure evil must be erased from Tibia. You'll find demons lurking in the northern ruins of Edron as well as in some other deeper dungeons of Tibia. Slay 6666 demons for the greater good! Do you think you can handle this task?",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_10": "In this task you must defeat ",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_11": "The status of your current tasks is:\n",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_12": "You haven't started any task yet.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_13": "Congratulations, |PLAYERNAME|! You have gained the highest rank: 'Elite hunter'. If you haven't done yet, ask me for the {special} task.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_14": "You have not enough points for promotion.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_15": "You can choose between the {Snapper}, {Hide}, {Deathbine} and the {Bloodtusk}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_16": "You haven't started any task yet.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_17": "You haven't started any task yet.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_18": "You haven't started any task yet.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_19": "Are you sure you want to cancel this task?",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_20": "You currently killed 0/",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_22": "You have already started the task. Go find Tiquandas Revenge and take revenge yourself!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_23": "Great achievement, old chap! You are an outstanding hunter, no doubt about it!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_24": "This task is a very dangerous one. I want you to look for {Demodras'} hideout. It might be somewhere under the {Plains of Havoc}. Good luck, old chap, come back in one piece and ask me about the special task when you're done.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_25": "You have already started the special task. Find Demodras and kill it.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_26": "Jolly good show! You can cross swords with any creature in this world! I bow to you.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_27": "You have already finished all special tasks.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_28": "You currently killed ",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_29": "You currently killed 0/",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_30": "You have canceled the task ",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_31": "Speak to me again when you are done hunting",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_32": "You have already started the task. Go find Tiquandas Revenge and take revenge yourself!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_33": "Great achievement, old chap! You are an outstanding hunter, no doubt about it!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_34": "This task is a very dangerous one. I want you to look for {Demodras'} hideout. It might be somewhere under the {Plains of Havoc}. Good luck, old chap, come back in one piece and ask me about the special task when you're done.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_35": "You have already started the special task. Find Demodras and kill it.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_36": "Jolly good show! You can cross swords with any creature in this world! I bow to you.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_37": "You have already finished all special tasks.",
  "npc.zurak.say_1": "You want trip to Izzle of Zztrife?",
  "npc.zurak.say_2": "You need permission to travel to.",
  "npc.zurak.say_3": "It'zz your doom you travel to.",
  "npc.zurak.say_4": "Zzoftzzkinzz zzo full of fear.",
  "npc.zurak.say_5": "Me zzimple ferryman. I arrange {trip} to Izzle of Zztrife.",
  "npc.timothy.say_1": "Excellent! You will find Palimuth near the entrance of the city centre. Just ask him if you can assist him in a few missions.",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.say_1": "I guess I will stick around for a time to watch over the grave. After this final watch I will find peace, I can feel this. Thank you, human being. You redeemed me.",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.say_2": "I guess I will stick around for a time to watch over the grave. After this final watch I will find peace, I can feel this. Thank you, human being. You redeemed me.",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.say_3": "You are not on that mission.",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.say_4": "Then not.",
  "npc.gabel.say_1": "Whoa! A human! This is no place for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Go and play somewhere else.",
  "npc.gabel.say_2": "Welcome, human |PLAYERNAME|, to our humble abode.",
  "npc.gabel.say_3": "You haven't finished your final mission yet. Shall I explain it again to you?",
  "npc.gabel.say_4": "Have you found Fa'hradin's lamp and placed it in Malor's personal chambers?",
  "npc.gabel.say_5": "There's no mission left for you, friend of the Marid. However, I have a task for you.",
  "npc.gabel.say_6": "As you wish.",
  "npc.gabel.say_7": "Don't give up! May Daraman watch over you!",
  "npc.gabel.say_8": "Come back when you kill 500 green djinns or Efreet.",
  "npc.gabel.say_9": "All right. May Daraman bless your hunt, human.",
  "npc.berenice.say_1": "OH! So you have safely returned from Calassa! Congratulations, were you able to retrieve the logbook?",
  "npc.berenice.say_2": "The most important mission we currently have is an expedition to {Calassa}.",
  "npc.berenice.say_3": "Ah! So you have heard about our special mission to investigate the Quara race in their natural surrounding! Would you like to know more about it?",
  "npc.berenice.say_4": "Captain Max will bring you to Calassa whenever you are ready. Please try to retrieve the missing logbook which must be in one of the sunken shipwrecks.",
  "npc.berenice.say_5": "OH! So you have safely returned from Calassa! Congratulations, were you able to retrieve the logbook?",
  "npc.berenice.say_6": "Excellent! I will immediately inform Captain Max to bring you to {Calassa} whenever you are ready. Don't forget to make thorough preparations!",
  "npc.berenice.say_7": "Yes! That's the logbook! However... it seems that the water has already destroyed many of the pages. This is not your fault though, you did your best. Thank you!",
  "npc.christoph.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.elliott.say_1": "I'm glad to see you back alive and healthy. Did you find anything interesting that you want to {report}?",
  "npc.elliott.say_2": "The sewers need repair. You in?",
  "npc.elliott.say_3": "Elliott's keeps calling it that. It's just another job! You fixed some broken pipes and stuff? Let me check, {ok}?",
  "npc.elliott.say_4": "Good. Broken pipe and generator pieces, there's smoke evading. That's how you recognise them. See how you can fix them using your hands. Need about, oh, twenty of them at least repaired. Report to me or Jacob",
  "npc.elliott.say_5": "Good. Thanks, man. That's one vote you got for helping us with this. If you want to redo this task just say {abandoned sewers} to repeat it.",
  "npc.elliott.say_6": "You already reported this mission, go to the next.",
  "npc.maris.say_1": "The good thing about cookies is that they last for a long time. So they are well suited for a boat trip. I'll take some of those, okay?",
  "npc.maris.say_2": "It'd be better for you to leave now.",
  "npc.maris.say_3": "Let's try that stuff first - ARRRRRRHH! <coughs> That must have been the worst cookie I've ever eaten. Get off my ship.",
  "npc.maris.stdmod_4": "Do you want go to the ",
  "npc.maris.stdmod_5": "Alright then!",
  "npc.maris.stdmod_6": "I can take you to {Fenrock} and {Mistrock}!",
  "npc.maris.stdmod_7": "I am Maris, Captain of this ship.",
  "npc.maris.stdmod_8": "Stop mumbling and don't bug me.",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.say_1": "Hello hello! Did you bring those blood samples?",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.say_2": "You haven't got any blood.",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.say_3": "Hello hello! Did Hello hello! Well now, painted all those blood pagodas properly?",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.say_4": "Hello hell- oh, you've come for the scroll, haven't you?",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.say_5": "My heart bleeds to part from it. Here. Extend your hand - I'll just retrieve some blood from in exchange - HOLD STILL.",
  "npc.nor.say_1": "Here, take the memory crystal and leave immediately.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_1": "For your rank there are two missions available: {matchmaker} and golem {repair}. You can undertake each mission, but you can turn in a specific mission only once every 20 hours. ",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_2": "For your rank there are four missions available: {matchmaker}, golem {repair}, {spore} gathering and {grindstone} hunt. You can undertake each mission, but you can turn in a specific mission only once every 20 hours.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_3": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_4": "Gnomo arigato |PLAYERNAME|! You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your tokens and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_5": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_6": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_7": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_8": "Our gnomish crystal golems sometimes go nuts. A recent earthquake has disrupted the entire production of a golem factory. ... ",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_9": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_10": "Gnomo arigato |PLAYERNAME|! You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your tokens and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_11": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_12": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_13": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_14": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_15": "Gnomo arigato |PLAYERNAME|! You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your tokens and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_16": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_17": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_18": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_19": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_20": "Gnomo arigato |PLAYERNAME|! You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your tokens and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_21": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_22": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_23": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_24": "Which mission do you want to report: {matchmaker}, golem {repair}?",
  "npc.gnomeral.say_25": "Which mission do you want to report: {matchmaker}, golem {repair}, {spore} gathering or {grindstone} hunt?",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_1": "Do you really think you could bribe a hero like me with a meagre cookie?",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_2": "So you want to have the demon outfit, hah! Let's have a look first if you really deserve it. Tell me: {base}, {shield} or {helmet}?",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_3": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_4": "Well, you won't! Though it looks tasty ...What the ... WHAT DO YOU THINK YOU ARE? THIS IS THE ULTIMATE INSULT! GET LOST!",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_5": "I see.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_6": "Receive the base outfit, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_7": "You need to complete annihilator quest first, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_8": "Receive the shield, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_9": "The shield will only be granted to those adventurers who have finished the demon helmet quest, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_10": "Receive the helmet, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.avar_tar.say_11": "The helmet is for those who have hunted down all 6666 demons and finished the demon oak as well, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.battlemart.say_1": "I sell a selection of ",
  "npc.battlemart.say_2": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.trisha.say_1": "Are you talking about my spiky shoulder pad? You can't buy one of these. They have to be {earned}.",
  "npc.trisha.say_2": "I'm not sure if you are enough of a hero to earn them. You could try, though. What do you think?",
  "npc.trisha.say_3": "Before I can nominate you for an award, please complete your task.",
  "npc.trisha.say_4": "You did it! I have seldom seen a man as courageous as you. I really have to say that you deserve to wear a spike. Go ask Cornelia to adorn your armour.",
  "npc.trisha.say_5": "I thought so. Train hard and maybe some day you will be ready to face this mission.",
  "npc.trisha.say_6": "Excellent! Don't forget: Your first task is to bring me 100 hardened bones. Good luck!",
  "npc.trisha.say_7": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.trisha.say_8": "Why do men always lie?",
  "npc.trisha.say_9": "Don't give up just yet.",
  "npc.an_idol.say_1": "J-T B^C J^BXT°",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_1": "Two missions are available for your {rank}: crystal {keeper} and {spark} hunting. You can undertake each mission but you can turn in a specific mission only once each 20 hours. ...",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_2": "For your {rank} there are four missions avaliable: crystal {keeper}, {spark} hunting, monster {extermination} and mushroom {digging}. By the way, you {rank} now allows you to take aditional missions from {Gnomeral} in {Gnomebase Alpha}. ... ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_3": "You will have to repair some damaged crystals. Go into the Crystal grounds and repair them, using this harmonic crystal. Repair five of them and return to me. ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_4": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_5": "You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your {token} and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_6": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_7": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_8": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_9": "Take this extractor and drive it into a body of a slain crystal crusher. This will charge your own body with energy sparks. Charge it with seven sparks and return to me. ...",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_10": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_11": "You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your {token} and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_12": "You did not draw enough energy from Crystal Crushers or you have not asked for this task.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_13": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_14": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_15": "The wigglers have become a pest that threaten our resources and supplies. Kill 10 wigglers in the caves like the mushroon gardens or the truffles ground. {Report} back to me when you are done. ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_16": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_17": "You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your {token} and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_18": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_19": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_20": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_21": "Sorry, you will have to wait before you can undertake this mission again.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_22": "You did well. That will help us a lot. Take your {token} and this gnomish supply package as a reward. ",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_23": "You are not done yet.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_24": "You already have accepted this mission. Don't forget to {report} to me when you are done.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_25": "Sorry, you do have not have the required rank to undertake this mission.",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_26": "Which mission do you want to report: crystal {keeper}, {spark} hunting?",
  "npc.commander_stone.say_27": "Which mission do you want to report: crystal {keeper}, {spark} hunting, monster {extermination} or mushroom {digging}?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_1": "Firy steel it is. Need green ones' breath to melt. Or red even better. Me can make from shield. Lil' one want to trade?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_2": "Wait. Me work no cheap is. Do favour for me first, yes?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_3": "Me need gift for woman. We dance, so me want to give her bast skirt. But she big is. So I need many to make big one. Bring three okay? Me wait.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_4": "Good good! Woman happy will be. Now me happy too and help you.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_5": "Lil' one bring three bast skirts.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_6": "Lil' one bring three bast skirts?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_7": "Firy steel it is. Need green ones' breath to melt. Or red even better. Me can make from shield. Lil' one want to trade?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_8": "Wait. Me work no cheap is. Do favour for me first, yes?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_9": "Me need gift for woman. We dance, so me want to give her bast skirt. But she big is. So I need many to make big one. Bring three okay? Me wait.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_10": "Good good! Woman happy will be. Now me happy too and help you.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_11": "Lil' one bring three bast skirts.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_12": "Lil' one bring three bast skirts?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_13": "Very noble. Shiny. Me like. But breaks so fast. Me can make from shiny armour. Lil' one want to trade?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_14": "Cling clang!",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_15": "Firy steel it is. Need green ones' breath to melt. Or red even better. Me can make from shield. Lil' one want to trade?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_16": "Cling clang!",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_17": "Hellsteel is. Cursed and evil. Dangerous to work with. Me can make from evil helmet. Lil' one want to trade?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_18": "Cling clang!",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_19": "Good iron is. Me friends use it much for fight. Me can make from weapon. Lil' one want to trade?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_20": "Cling clang!",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_21": "Uh. Me can make some nasty lil' bolt from soul orbs. Lil' one want to trade all?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_22": "Cling clang! Me done good work today! Li'l one gets double bolts!",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.say_23": "Cling clang!",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_24": "I am smith.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_25": "Working steel is my profession.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_26": "Manny kinds of. Like {Mesh Kaha Rogh'}, {Za'Kalortith}, {Uth'Byth}, {Uth'Morc}, {Uth'Amon}, {Uth'Maer}, {Uth'Doon}, and {Zatragil}.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_27": "Most ancients use dream silver for different stuff. Now ancients most gone. Most not know about.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_28": "It's high steel called. Only lil' lil' ones know how make.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_29": "It's evil. Demon iron is. No good cyclops goes where you can find and need evil flame to melt.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_30": "Steel that is singing when forged. No one knows where find today.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_31": "Not good to make stuff off. Bad steel it is. But eating magic, so useful is.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_32": "Brightsteel is. Much art made with it. Sorcerers too lazy and afraid to enchant much.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_33": "Heartiron from heart of big old mountain, found very deep. Lil' lil ones fiercely defend. Not wanting to have it used for stuff but holy stuff.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_34": "Me parents live here before town was. Me not care about lil' ones.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_35": "Lil' lil' ones are so fun. We often chat.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_36": "One day I'll go and look.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_37": "Is one of elven family or such thing. Me not understand lil' ones and their business.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_38": "Is one of elven family or such thing. Me not understand lil' ones and their business.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_39": "I called Bencthyclthrtrprr by me people. Lil' ones me call Big Ben.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_40": "You shut up. Me not want to hear.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_41": "Do lil' one want to trade a fire sword?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_42": "Do lil' one want to trade a dragon shield?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_43": "Do lil' one want to trade a sword of valor?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_44": "Do lil' one want to trade a warlord sword?",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_45": "They were friend with me parents. Long before elves here, they often made visit. No longer come here.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_46": "Me not fight them, they not fight me.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_47": "Me wish I could make weapon like it.",
  "npc.a_sweaty_cyclops.stdmod_48": "Me people not live here much. Most are far away.",
  "npc.leeland.say_1": "Oh yes, that project the whole dwarven community is so excited about. I guess I already know why you are here, but speak up.",
  "npc.leeland.say_2": "Oh yes, that project the whole dwarven community is so excited about. I guess I already know why you are here, but speak up. Do you want to try again?",
  "npc.leeland.say_3": "Your pathetic whimpering amuses me. For this I grant you my assistance. But listen, one day I'll ask you to return this favour. From now on, you owe me one.",
  "npc.leeland.say_4": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.leeland.say_5": "The idea of a promising market and new resources suits us quite well. I think it is reasonable to send some assistance.",
  "npc.leeland.say_6": "Oh yes, that project the whole dwarven community is so excited about. I guess I already know why you are here, but speak up.",
  "npc.leeland.say_7": "Oh yes, that project the whole dwarven community is so excited about. I guess I already know why you are here, but speak up.",
  "npc.leeland.say_8": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.blossom_bonecrusher.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.palimuth.say_1": "I'm an Augur of the city of Yalahar. My special duty consists of coordinating the efforts to keep the city and its services running.",
  "npc.palimuth.say_2": "Did you bring me the vampiric crest?",
  "npc.palimuth.say_3": "So are you done with your work?",
  "npc.palimuth.say_4": "Did you get all the reports my superiors asked for? ",
  "npc.palimuth.say_5": "These are great news indeed. The people of Yalahar will be grateful. The Yalahari probably not, so take care of yourself. ",
  "npc.palimuth.say_6": "Rumours travel fast in Yalahar. So the Yalahari will soon have some new toys at their disposal. I strongly doubt this has any positive effect.",
  "npc.palimuth.say_7": "Oh no! So that's the reason for the quara attacks! I will do my best to close these sewage pipes. We will have to use other drains. ",
  "npc.palimuth.say_8": "You can be proud of your decision, my friend.",
  "npc.palimuth.say_9": "So do you want to side with me? ",
  "npc.palimuth.say_10": "Thank you very much. You have no idea how hard it was to find someone volunteering for that job. If you feel ready for further {missions}, just tell me.",
  "npc.palimuth.say_11": "Excellent! My superiors will be pleased to get these reports. I will for sure emphasise your efforts in this mission. Please come back soon to see if there are any more {missions} available for you. ",
  "npc.palimuth.say_12": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.palimuth.say_13": "You have no idea how much I hoped to hear that, my friend! But I have an urgent mission for you!",
  "npc.palimuth.say_14": "Great! Here, take this yalaharian addon in a return.",
  "npc.palimuth.say_15": "Come back when you do.",
  "npc.atrad.say_1": "You managed to deceive Erayo? Impressive. Well, I guess, since you have come that far, I might as well give you a task too, eh?",
  "npc.atrad.say_2": "I see you brought my stuff. Good. I'll keep my promise: Here's katana in return.",
  "npc.atrad.say_3": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.atrad.say_4": "Okay, listen up. I don't have a list of stupid objects, I just want two things. A behemoth claw and a nose ring. Got that?",
  "npc.atrad.say_5": "Good. Come back then you have BOTH. Should be clear where to get a behemoth claw from. There's a horned fox who wears a nose ring. Good luck.",
  "npc.tamoril.say_1": "The First Dragon? The first of all of us? The Son of Garsharak? I'm surprised you heard about him. It is such a long time that he wandered Tibia. Yet, there are some {rumours}.",
  "npc.tamoril.say_2": "It is told that the First Dragon had four {descendants}, who became the ancestors of the four kinds of dragons we know in Tibia. They perhaps still have knowledge about the First Dragon's whereabouts - if one could find them.",
  "npc.tamoril.say_3": "The names of these four are Tazhadur, Kalyassa, Gelidrazah and Zorvorax. Not only were they the ancestors of all dragons after but also the primal representation of the {draconic incitements}. About whom do you want to learn more?",
  "npc.tamoril.say_4": "What do you want to do, if you know about these mighty dragons' abodes? Go there and look for a fight?",
  "npc.ustan.say_1": "I had some cough syrup a while ago. It was stolen in an ape raid. I fear if you want more cough syrup you will have to buy it in the druids guild in carlin.",
  "npc.ustan.say_2": "Would you like to wear bear paws like I do? No problem, just bring me 50 bear paws and 50 wolf paws and I'll fit them on.",
  "npc.ustan.say_3": "Have you brought 50 bear paws and 50 wolf paws?",
  "npc.ustan.say_4": "Excellent! Like promised, here are your bear paws. ",
  "npc.shauna.say_1": "What do you think? I am the sheriff of Carlin.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_2": "No news are good news.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_3": "HAIL TO QUEEN ELOISE!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_4": "HAIL TO QUEEN ELOISE!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_5": "Just fine.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_6": "Would you like to buy the general key to the town?",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_7": "Yeah, I bet you'd like to do that! HO, HO, HO!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_8": "If they make trouble, I'll put them behind bars like all others.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_9": "If they make trouble, I'll put them behind bars like all others.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_10": "The Bonecrusher family is ideally suited for military jobs.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_11": "The Bonecrusher family is ideally suited for military jobs.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_12": "If you have a crime to report and clues, then do it, but don't waste my time.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_13": "If you have a crime to report and clues, then do it, but don't waste my time.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_14": "If you have a crime to report and clues, then do it, but don't waste my time.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_15": "If you have a crime to report and clues, then do it, but don't waste my time.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_16": "The castle is one of the safest places in Carlin.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_17": "Our people are fine and peaceful.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_18": "I bet they spy on us... not my business, however.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_19": "I scared this bigmouth so much that he left the town by night. HO, HO, HO!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_20": "The city is is a peaceful place, and it's up to me to keep it this way.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_21": "He is the guy responsible to keep the sewers working. Someone has to do such kind of jobs. I can't handle all the garbage of the city myself.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_22": "Rowenna is one of our local smiths. When you look for weapons, look for Rowenna.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_23": "Rowenna is one of our local smiths. When you look for weapons, look for Rowenna.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_24": "Cornelia is one of our local smiths. When you look for armor, look for Cornelia.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_25": "Cornelia is one of our local smiths. When you look for armor, look for Cornelia.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_26": "She has the sharpest eye in the region, I'd say.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_27": "Her peacefulness is sometimes near stupidity.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_28": "I worship Banor of course.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_29": "For me, he's the god of justice.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_30": "His cult is forbidden in our town.",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_31": "Wouldn't wonder if some males worship him secretly. HO, HO, HO!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_32": "I deal more with the human mosters, you know? HO, HO, HO!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_33": "Would certainly make a good butterknife. HO, HO, HO!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_34": "The only thing that rebels here now and then is the stomach of a male after trying to make illegal alcohol. HO, HO, HO!",
  "npc.shauna.stdmod_35": "For obvious reasons it's forbidden in our city.",
  "npc.aurita.say_1": "Then not.",
  "npc.sigurd.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.inigo.say_1": "I'm sorry, but I cannot let you go there, you'll get much better training here than on that ancient isle.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_1": "Brilliant! We need fine adventurers like you! If you are ready to learn, just ask me for a lesson. You can always ask for the differently coloured words - such as this one - to continue the lesson.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_2": "Brilliant! We need fine adventurers like you! If you are ready to learn, just ask me for a lesson. You can always ask for the differently coloured words - such as this one - to continue the lesson.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_3": "Only nonsense on your mind, eh?",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_4": "Thank you! Here is your reward.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_5": "HEY! You don't have so many!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_6": "Go and find some rats to kill!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_7": "Have you brought a dead rat to me to pick up your reward?",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_8": "Thank you! Here is your reward.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_9": "HEY! You don't have one! Stop playing tricks on me or I'll give you some extra work!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_10": "Go and find some rats to kill!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_11": "Do you have a suitable present box for me?",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_12": "THANK YOU! Here is a helmet that will serve you well.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_13": "HEY! You don't have one! Stop playing tricks on me or I'll give you some extra work!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_14": "Well, I would like to send our king a little present but I do not have a suitable box. If you find a nice box, please bring it to me.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_15": "You are pretty inexperienced. I think killing rats is a suitable challenge for you. For each fresh {dead rat} I will give you two shiny coins of gold.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_16": "For this remark I will wash your mouth with soap, young lady!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_17": "For this remark I will wash your mouth with soap, young man!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_18": "This is an island with {vocation} teachers. You can learn all about the different vocations there once you are level 8.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_19": "It's |TIME|, so you are late. Hurry!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_20": "My name is Seymour, but for you I am 'Sir' Seymour.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_21": "At least you know how to address a man of my importance.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_22": "I'm the master of this fine {academy}, giving {lessons} to my students.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_23": "Oh, which lesson did you want to attend again? Was it {Rookgaard}, {fighting}, {equipment}, {citizens}, the {academy} or the {oracle}?",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_24": "In a bank you can deposit your earned gold coins safely. Just go downstairs to {Paulie} and ask him to {deposit} your money.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_25": "Yes, depositing your money will keep it safe, so it is a good idea to store it in the bank. Of course, you can always withdraw it again.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_26": "Well, the {king} doesn't send troops anymore, the {academy} is dreadfully low on money, and the end of the world is pretty nigh. Apart from that I'm reasonably fine, I suppose.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_27": "Most of the citizens here are {merchants}. You can give me the name of any non-player character and I will tell you something about him or her.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_28": "Merchants buy and sell goods. Just ask them for a {trade} to see what they offer or buy from you.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_29": "Trolls are quite nasty monsters which you shouldn't face before level 3 or 4 depending on your {equipment}. Ask the bridge {guards} for their locations!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_30": "The guards {Dallheim} and {Zerbrus} protect our village from {monsters} trying to enter. They also mark useful {dungeon} locations on your map.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_31": "There are four vocations: {knights}, {paladins}, {sorcerers} and {druids}. You can choose your vocation once you are level 8 and have talked to the {oracle}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_32": "Sorcerers are talented elemental magicians. You will learn all about them once you are level 8 and reached the Island of {Destiny}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_33": "Knights are strong melee fighters. You will learn all about them once you are level 8 and reached the Island of {Destiny}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_34": "Druids are nature magic users and great healers. You will learn all about them once you are level 8 and reached the Island of {Destiny}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_35": "Paladins are swift distance fighters. You will learn all about them once you are level 8 and reached the Island of {Destiny}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_36": "We have a {weapon} and an {armor} shop south of the academy. {Equipment} such as {ropes} are sold to the north-west. {Potions} can be bought to the south. And then there are the {farms}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_37": "The world of Tibia is very large with tons of places to explore. Vast deserts, Caribbean islands, deep jungles, green meadows and jagged mountains await you!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_38": "The temple is the place to go when you are very low on {health} or poisoned. Ask {Cipfried} for a heal - he usually notices emergencies by himself.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_39": "Your current health is shown by the red bar on the right side. {Death} awaits you if it goes down to zero.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_40": "Dying in Tibia is painful, so try to avoid it. You will lose part of your {experience} points and also equipment. Make sure your {health} always stays up!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_41": "You gain experience when fighting {monsters}. You can take a look at your skill window to check your progress.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_42": "Good monsters to start hunting are {rats}. They live in the {sewers} below the village.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_43": "One entrance to the sewers is south of this {academy}. Look for a sewer grate, then use it to climb down.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_44": "The academy is the building you are standing in. We have a {library}, a {bank} and the room of the {oracle}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_45": "There are many books in the bookcases around you, unless some naughty kids stole them again. Read them for more and detailed information.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_46": "Don't go hunting without proper equipment. You need at least a suitable {weapon}, {armor}, {shield}, {rope} and {shovel}. A {torch} is also good as well as {legs}, a {helmet} and {shoes}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_47": "Make money by killing {monsters} and picking up their {loot}. You can sell many of the things they carry.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_48": "Once a monster is dead, you can select 'Open' on the {corpse} to check what's inside. Sometimes they carry {money} or other items which you can sell to {merchants}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_49": "You can even sell some corpses! For example, you can sell fresh dead rats to {Tom} the tanner or me. He also buys other dead creatures, just ask him for a {trade}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_50": "You definitely need a rope to progress in dungeons, else you might end up stuck. Buy one from {Al Dee} or {Lee'Delle}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_51": "A shovel is needed to dig some {dungeon} entrances open. 'Use' it on a loose stone pile to make a hole large enough to enter.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_52": "You should not descend into dungeons without proper {equipment}. Once you are all prepared, ask the bridge {guards} for suitable {monsters}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_53": "A torch will provide you with light in dark {dungeons}. 'Use' it to light it. You can buy them from {Al Dee} or {Lee'Delle}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_54": "Well, I could give you valuable {lessons} or some general {hints} about the game, or a small {quest} if you're interested.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_55": "The starter armor, a coat, does not protect you well. First of all, earn some money and try to get a sturdy leather armor from {Dixi}'s  or {Lee'Delle}'s shop. Simply ask for a {trade}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_56": "The starter weapon, a club, won't get you far. You should earn some {money} and buy a better weapon such as a sabre from {Obi}'s or {Lee'Delle}'s shop. Simply ask for a {trade}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_57": "A sturdy leather helmet is a good choice for a beginner. You can either buy it from {Dixi} and {Lee'Delle}, or, once you are strong enough, {loot} them from {trolls}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_58": "I fear you have to buy your first shield by yourself. A wooden shield from {Dixi} or {Lee'Delle} is a good choice.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_59": "Leather boots are basic shoes which will protect you well. You can either buy them from {Dixi} and {Lee'Delle}, or, once you are strong enough, {loot} them from {trolls}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_60": "Leather legs might be a good basic protection. You can buy them from {Dixi} or {Lee'Delle}. Or, once you are strong enough, hunt {trolls}. They sometimes carry them in their {loot}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_61": "Many monsters, such as rabbits or deer, are excellent food providers. You can also buy food from {Willie} or {Billy}, the farmers.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_62": "Paying for your Tibia account will turn it into a premium account. This means access to more areas and functions of the game as well as other neat features.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_63": "Hail to King Tibianus! Long live our king! Not that he cares for an old veteran who is stuck on this godforsaken island...",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_64": "Use a small health potion in case of emergencies to fill up around 75 health points. You can buy them at {Lily}'s shop. She also has {antidote} potions.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_65": "Some monsters poison you. To heal poison, use an antidote potion on yourself. Buy them at {Lily}'s store.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_66": "Rookgaard is the name of this {village} as well as of the whole {island}. It belongs to the kingdom of {Thais}, in our world which is called {Tibia}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_67": "The island is separated into a {premium} side and a non-premium side. On both sides you will find {dungeons}, but the premium side tends to be a little less crowded with other players.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_68": "The city of Thais is reigned by King Tibianus. Of course, there are many other cities but you will learn about them later.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_69": "The most important places in this village are the {temple}, the different {shops}, the {academy} and the {bridges}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_70": "There is a bridge to the north and one to the west which lead outside the village. You should only leave once you are well {equipped} and at least level 2.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_71": "You can leave for mainland once you are level 8. To do so talk to the {oracle}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_72": "You have to fight {monsters} to train your {skills} and {level}. If you lose {health}, eat {food} to regain it or use a {potion}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_73": "The more you fight with a weapon, the better will be your skill handling this weapon. Don't worry about that right now though, this will become important once you have a {vocation}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_74": "Once you gained enough experience for a level, you will advance. This means - among other things - more {health} points, a faster walking speed and more strength to carry things.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_75": "The farms are west of here. You can buy and sell {food} there which you need to regain {health}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_76": "To attack a rat, simply click on it in your battle list. Make sure that you have proper {equipment}, though! Also, I give you 2 gold coins for each {dead rat}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_77": "I personally don't have anything to trade, but you can ask {merchants} for a trade. That will open a window where you can see their offers and the things they buy from you.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_78": "Well, I could give you valuable {lessons} or some general {hints} about the game, or a small {quest} if you're interested.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_79": "Shall I try and take a guess at your destiny?",
  "npc.seymour.say_80": "Hmmm, let me look at you. You got that intelligent sparkle in your eyes and you'd love to handle great power - that must be a future sorcerer!",
  "npc.seymour.say_81": "Hmmm, let me look at you. You have an aura of great wisdom and may have healing hands as well as a sense for the powers of nature - I think you're a natural born druid!",
  "npc.seymour.say_82": "Hmmm, let me look at you. <missing message, destiny for paladin>!",
  "npc.seymour.say_83": "Hmmm, let me look at you. Strong and sturdy, with a determined look in your eyes - no doubt the knight profession would be suited for you!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_84": "Obi sells and buys {weapons}. You can find his shop south of the academy.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_85": "Norma has recently opened a bar here meaning she sells drinks and snacks. Nothing of importance to you, young student.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_86": "Oh, let's not talk about Loui.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_87": "A fine and helpful man. Without him, many new adventurers would be quite clueless.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_88": "This is Tom the tanner's mother. Other than that, I don't think she is of importance.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_89": "Al Dee has a general {equipment} store in the north-western part of the village. He sells useful stuff such as {ropes}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_90": "A traveller from the {main} continent. I wonder what brought her here. No one comes here of his own free will.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_91": "Billy is {Willie}'s cousin, but he has his farm on the {premium} side of the village.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_92": "Willie is a fine farmer, although he is short-tempered. He sells and buys {food}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_93": "A humble monk living in the {temple} south of here. He can heal you if you are wounded or poisoned.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_94": "Dixi sells and buys {armors}, {shields}, {helmets} and {legs}. You can find her shop south of the academy, just go up the stairs in {Obi}'s shop.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_95": "A mysterious druid who lives somewhere in the wilderness. He sells small health {potions} just like {Lily}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_96": "Lee'Delle's shop is in the western part of town, on the {premium} side. She sells everything cheaper.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_97": "In the southern part of town, Lily sells {potions} which might come in handy once you are deep in a dungeon and need {health}.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_98": "The oracle is a mysterious being just upstairs. It will bring you to the {Island of Destiny} to choose your {vocation} once you are level 8.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_99": "Yes, Paulie is very important. He is the local {bank} clerk.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_100": "Sir Seymour, yes, that's me.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_101": "Tom the tanner buys fresh {corpses}, minotaur leather and paws. Always good to make some {money} if you can carry the corpses there fast enough.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_102": "He's the guard on the north {bridge} and a great fighter. He can show you {monster} locations. Just ask him about monsters!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_103": "He's the guard on the west {bridge} and a great fighter. He can show you {monster} locations. Just ask him about monsters!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_104": "Sir Seymour, yes, that's me.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_105": "Tom the tanner buys fresh {corpses}, minotaur leather and paws. Always good to make some {money} if you can carry the corpses there fast enough.",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_106": "He's the guard on the north {bridge} and a great fighter. He can show you {monster} locations. Just ask him about monsters!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_107": "He's the guard on the west {bridge} and a great fighter. He can show you {monster} locations. Just ask him about monsters!",
  "npc.vescu.say_1": "Oh, two t-trolls. Hellooo, wittle twolls. <hicks>",
  "npc.vescu.say_2": "I wish there was like a {potion} which makes you sober in an instant. Dwarven rings wear off so fast. <hicks>",
  "npc.vescu.say_3": "It's so hard to know the exact time when to stop drinking. <hicks> C-could you help me to brew such a potion?",
  "npc.vescu.say_4": "Right. <hicks> Since you helped me to b-brew that potion and thus ensured the high quality of my work <hicks>, I'll give you my old assassin costume. It lacks the head part, but it's almost like new. Don't pretend to be me though, 'kay? <hicks>",
  "npc.vescu.say_5": "G-good. Go get them, I'll have a beer in the meantime.",
  "npc.vescu.say_6": "Next time you lie to me I'll k-kill you. <hicks> Don't think I can't aim well just because I'm d-drunk.",
  "npc.vescu.say_7": "Then not <hicks>.",
  "npc.vescu.say_8": "H-hurry up! <hicks> I have to start working soon.",
  "npc.sundara.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_1": "Whoa! A human! This is no place for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Go and play somewhere else.",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_2": "Hey! A human! What are you doing in my kitchen, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_3": "I already told you about the recipes I am missing, now please try to find a cookbook of the dwarven kitchen.",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_4": "Do you have the cookbook of the dwarven kitchen with you? Can I have it?",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_5": "Thanks again, for bringing me that book!",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_6": "Well, too bad.",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_7": "Too bad. I must have this book.",
  "npc.bo_ques.say_8": "Too bad. I must have this book.",
  "npc.armenius.say_1": "What kind of strange offer is this? You're actually offering me a cookie?",
  "npc.armenius.say_2": "It'd be better for you to leave now.",
  "npc.armenius.say_3": "Errrkss - coughcough - what the - heck did you put in there? Get out of my sight!",
  "npc.armenius.say_4": "Oh, the nerve. Sod off.",
  "npc.irmana.say_1": "Currently we are offering accessories for the nobleman - and, of course, noblewoman - outfit. Would you like to hear more about our offer?",
  "npc.irmana.say_2": "Especially for you, mylady, we are offering a pretty hat and a beautiful dress like the ones I wear. Which one are you interested in?",
  "npc.irmana.say_3": "Great! Since our accessories are hand-tailored designer pieces, of course they are not made for citizens with an empty wallet. Should I inform you about our payment policy?",
  "npc.irmana.say_4": "I'm very pleased to hear that! Which do you prefer - paying 150000 at once or 10000 for 15 times?",
  "npc.irmana.say_5": "Good, I have noted down your order. Once you have the money, please come back to pick up your accessory.",
  "npc.irmana.say_6": "Ah, are you here to pickup your accessory for 150000 gold pieces?",
  "npc.irmana.say_7": "Congratulations! Here is your brand-new accessory, I hope you like it. Please visit us again!",
  "npc.irmana.say_8": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.irmana.say_9": "Currently we are offering accessories for the nobleman - and, of course, noblewoman - outfit. Would you like to hear more about our offer?",
  "npc.irmana.say_10": "Especially for you, mylady, we are offering a pretty hat and a beautiful dress like the ones I wear. Which one are you interested in?",
  "npc.irmana.say_11": "Great! Since our accessories are hand-tailored designer pieces, of course they are not made for citizens with an empty wallet. Should I inform you about our payment policy?",
  "npc.irmana.say_12": "I'm very pleased to hear that! Which do you prefer - paying 150000 at once or 10000 for 15 times?",
  "npc.irmana.say_13": "Good, I have noted down your order. Once you have the money, please come back to pick up your accessory.",
  "npc.irmana.say_14": "Ah, are you here to pickup your accessory for 150000 gold pieces?",
  "npc.irmana.say_15": "Congratulations! Here is your brand-new accessory, I hope you like it. Please visit us again!",
  "npc.irmana.say_16": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.irmana.say_17": "Currently we are offering accessories for the nobleman - and, of course, noblewoman - outfit. Would you like to hear more about our offer?",
  "npc.irmana.say_18": "Especially for you, mylord, we are offering a fashionable top hat and a fancy coat like the one Kalvin wears. Which one are you interested in?",
  "npc.irmana.say_19": "Great! Since our accessories are hand-tailored designer pieces, of course they are not made for citizens with an empty wallet. Should I inform you about our payment policy?",
  "npc.irmana.say_20": "I'm very pleased to hear that! Which do you prefer - paying 150000 at once or 10000 for 15 times?",
  "npc.irmana.say_21": "Good, I have noted down your order. Once you have the money, please come back to pick up your accessory.",
  "npc.irmana.say_22": "Ah, are you here to pickup your accessory for 150000 gold pieces? Here is your nobleman coat. Enjoy!",
  "npc.irmana.say_23": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.irmana.say_24": "Currently we are offering accessories for the nobleman - and, of course, noblewoman - outfit. Would you like to hear more about our offer?",
  "npc.irmana.say_25": "Especially for you, mylord, we are offering a fashionable top hat and a fancy coat like the one Kalvin wears. Which one are you interested in?",
  "npc.irmana.say_26": "Great! Since our accessories are hand-tailored designer pieces, of course they are not made for citizens with an empty wallet. Should I inform you about our payment policy?",
  "npc.irmana.say_27": "I'm very pleased to hear that! Which do you prefer - paying 150000 at once or 10000 for 15 times?",
  "npc.irmana.say_28": "Good, I have noted down your order. Once you have the money, please come back to pick up your accessory.",
  "npc.irmana.say_29": "Ah, are you here to pickup your accessory for 150000 gold pieces? Here is your nobleman hat. Enjoy!",
  "npc.irmana.say_30": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.irmana.say_31": "You are not on that mission.",
  "npc.irmana.say_32": "A {Red Robe}! Great. Here, take this red piece of cloth, I don't need it anyway.",
  "npc.irmana.say_33": "Are you trying to mess with me?!",
  "npc.irmana.say_34": "A {Mystic Turban}! Great. Here, take this blue piece of cloth, I don't need it anyway.",
  "npc.irmana.say_35": "Are you trying to mess with me?!",
  "npc.irmana.say_36": "A 150 {Green Tunic}! Great. Here, take this green piece of cloth, I don't need it anyway.",
  "npc.irmana.say_37": "Are you trying to mess with me?!",
  "npc.irmana.say_38": "Alright. Here is the fur.",
  "npc.irmana.say_39": "Are you trying to mess with me?!",
  "npc.irmana.say_40": "Have you found a {Red Robe} for me?",
  "npc.irmana.say_41": "Have you found a {Mystic Turban} for me?",
  "npc.irmana.say_42": "Have you found {150 Green Tunic} for me?",
  "npc.chuckles.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.ajax.say_1": "YOURS? WHAT IS YOURS! NOTHING IS YOURS! IS MINE! GO AWAY, YES?!",
  "npc.ajax.say_2": "YOU STUPID! STUBBORN! I KILL YOU! WILL LEAVE NOW?!",
  "npc.ajax.say_3": "ARRRRRRRRRR! YOU ME DRIVE MAD! HOW I MAKE YOU GO??",
  "npc.ajax.say_4": "I GIVE YOU NO!",
  "npc.ajax.say_5": "Please? What you mean please? Like I say please you say bye? Please?",
  "npc.ajax.say_6": "Annoying kid. Bro hates him, but talking no help. Bro needs {fighting spirit}!",
  "npc.ajax.say_7": "If you want to help bro, bring him fighting spirit. Magic fighting spirit. Ask Djinn.",
  "npc.ajax.say_8": "Bron gave me present. Ugly, but nice from him. Me want to give present too. You help me?",
  "npc.ajax.say_9": "You bring 100 iron ore?",
  "npc.ajax.say_10": "You bring crude iron?",
  "npc.ajax.say_11": "You bring 50 behemoth fangs?",
  "npc.ajax.say_12": "You bring 50 lizard leather?",
  "npc.ajax.say_13": "Axe is done! For you. Take. Wear like me.",
  "npc.ajax.say_14": "Axe is not done yet!",
  "npc.ajax.say_15": "Oh. Easy. Okay. Please is good. Now don't say anything. Head aches. ",
  "npc.ajax.say_16": "Good. You get 100 iron ore first. Come back.",
  "npc.ajax.say_17": "Good! Now bring crude iron.",
  "npc.ajax.say_18": "Good! Now bring 50 behemoth fangs.",
  "npc.ajax.say_19": "Good! Now bring 50 lizard leather.",
  "npc.ajax.say_20": "Ah! All stuff there. I will start making axes now. Come later and ask me for axe.",
  "npc.guide_behil.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_behil.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_behil.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_5": "The temple is a few floors over the depot. Just walk up the numerous stairs there.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_6": "Muzir takes care of our bank business. His office is in the north-western part of the caliph's palace.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, furniture, spells and food here.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_9": "I'll show you around Darashia if you like. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_10": "Darashia is an oriental settlement ruled by Caliph Kazzan Ibn Gadral. We have a lot of shops, carpet travel and a rotworm plague, that sums it about up.",
  "npc.guide_behil.stdmod_11": "My name is Behil. Glad to be your guide.",
  "npc.chartan.say_1": "Mhm, what are you doing here. Who zent you? ",
  "npc.chartan.say_2": "Zo are you ready to get zomezing done?",
  "npc.chartan.say_3": "Zo? Did you find a way to reztore ze teleporter? ",
  "npc.beatrice.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.beatrice.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.beatrice.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.chrak.say_1": "I grant you ze permizzion to enter ze arena. Remember, you'will have to enter ze arena az a team of two. If you are not familiar wiz ze rulez, I can explain zem to you once again.",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_1": "If. You. Bring. Slime. Fungus. Samples. Fro-Fro-Fro-Frrrr*chhhhchrk*From. Other. Tower. You. Must. Be. The. Master. Are. You. There. Master?",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_2": "If. You. Bring. Slime. Fungus. Samples. Fro-Fro-Fro-Frrrr*chhhhchrk*From. Other. Tower. You. Must. Be. The. Master. Are. You. There. Master?",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_3": "You already have this outfit!",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_4": "You already have this outfit!",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_5": "I. Greet. You. Ma-Ma-Ma-ster! Did. You. Bring. Mo-Mo-Mo-M*chhhhrrrk*ore. Samples. For. Me. To-To-To. Analyse-lyse-lyse?",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_6": "Thank. I. Will. Start. Analysing. No-No-No-No*chhrrrk*Now.",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_7": "I. Greet. You. Ma-Ma-Ma-ster! Did. You. Bring. Mo-Mo-Mo-M*chhhhrrrk*ore. Samples. For. Me. To-To-To. Analyse-lyse-lyse?",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.say_8": "You do not have all the required items.",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_1": "May Fire and Earth bless you, stranger. What leads you to Beregar, the dwarven city?",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_2": "I always liked him and I still can't believe that he really stole that ring.",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_3": "Interesting. The fact that you have the ring means that Nokmir can't have stolen it. Combined with the information Grombur gave you, the case appears in a completely different light. ...",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_4": "Let there be justice for all. Nokmir is innocent and acquitted from all charges! And Rerun... I want him in prison for this malicious act!",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_5": "He's very ambitious and always volunteers for the long shifts.",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_6": "As you have proven yourself trustworthy I'm going to assign you a special mission. Are you interested?",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_7": "My son was captured by trolls? Doesn't sound like him, but if you say so. Now you want a reward, huh? ...",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_8": "Look at these dwarven legs. They were forged years ago by a dwarf who was rather tall for our kind. I want you to have them. Thank you for rescuing my son |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.say_9": "Alright then, come back when you are ready.",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.stdmod_10": "I can promote you for 20000 gold coins. Do you want me to promote you?",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.stdmod_11": "Alright then, come back when you are ready.",
  "npc.yalahari.say_1": "So you have killed the plague carriers. Have you also retrieved the research papers? ",
  "npc.yalahari.say_2": "This will teach these fishmen who is the ruler of that area. You have earned yourself a special privilege. But we will talk about that when we speak about your next mission. ",
  "npc.yalahari.say_3": "Your failure is an outrage! I think we have to talk about the missions you have accomplished so far. ",
  "npc.yalahari.say_4": "Now we will have power we truly deserve!...",
  "npc.yalahari.say_5": "So do you want to side with me |PLAYERNAME|? ",
  "npc.yalahari.say_6": "Great work, take this outfit and you are able to open the door to the reward room.",
  "npc.yalahari.say_7": "Impressive indeed! Someone with your skills will quickly raise in our ranks of helpers. You have great potential, and if you are upfor further missions, just ask for them. ",
  "npc.yalahari.say_8": "I knew that you were smart enough to make the right decision! Your next mission will be a special one! ",
  "npc.gnomally.say_1": "Our relations improve with every mission you undertake on our behalf. Another way to improve your relations with us gnomes is to trade in minor crystal tokens. ...",
  "npc.gnomally.say_2": "You are not even a recruit of the Bigfoots. Sorry I can't help you.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_3": "Do you really want to trade ",
  "npc.gnomally.say_4": "Do you need to buy any mission items?",
  "npc.gnomally.say_5": "Sorry, you don't have enough ",
  "npc.gnomally.say_6": "First make sure you have enough capacity to hold it.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_7": "First make sure you have enough space in your inventory.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_8": "How many tokens do you want to trade?",
  "npc.gnomally.say_9": "You don't have these many tokens.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_10": "Let us see if I have what you need.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_11": "As you like.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_12": "You don't have these many tokens.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_13": "Let us see if I have what you need.",
  "npc.gnomally.say_14": "As you like.",
  "npc.cassino.say_1": "If you want to play with me please come near me.",
  "npc.cassino.say_2": "Your bet is lower than the min {",
  "npc.undal.say_1": "So do you want to learn the {story} behind of this or rather talk about the {task} at hand? ",
  "npc.undal.say_2": "Do you prefer the {long} version or the {short} version?",
  "npc.undal.say_3": "The Nightmare Beast is slain. You have done well. The Courts of Summer and Winter will be forever grateful. For your efforts I want to reward you with our traditional dream warrior outfit. May it suit you well!",
  "npc.undal.say_4": "I already gave your task.",
  "npc.undal.say_5": "They are not literally keys but rather puzzles you have to solve or a secret mechanism you have to discover in order to open the Dream Doors. A parchment in the chest here can tell you more about it.",
  "npc.undal.say_6": "Are you interested in one or two addons to your dream warrior outfit?",
  "npc.undal.say_7": "You don't even have the outfit.",
  "npc.undal.say_8": "I provide two addons. For the first one I need you to bring me five pomegranates. For the second addon you need an ice shield. Do you want one of these addons?",
  "npc.undal.say_9": "What do you have for me: the {pomegranates} or the {ice shield}?",
  "npc.undal.say_10": "Very good! You gained the second addon to the dream warrior outfit.",
  "npc.undal.say_11": "You do not have enough items.",
  "npc.undal.say_12": "Very good! You gained the first addon to the dream warrior outfit.",
  "npc.undal.say_13": "You do not have enough items.",
  "npc.undal.say_14": "Sorry, I didn't understand.",
  "npc.emael.say_1": "Do you want to appropriately show off your boss trophies and buy an additional podium of vigour for 1000000 Gold?",
  "npc.emael.say_2": "Ah, I see you killed a lot of dangerous creatures. Here's your podium of vigour!",
  "npc.emael.say_3": "Please make sure you have free slots in your store inbox.",
  "npc.emael.say_4": "You don'\t have enough money.",
  "npc.emael.say_5": "You have not aquired enough knowledge in hunting big scary creatures.",
  "npc.emael.say_6": "Blessings on your hunts!",
  "npc.brewster.say_1": "The only person who might have some cough syrup is this druid Ustan. You find him in the tavern. Hmmm the tavern ... <hicks>",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_2": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_3": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_4": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_5": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_6": "No problem.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_7": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_8": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_9": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_10": "No problem.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_11": "I think you have forgotten to bring your stake, pilgrim.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_12": "Yes, I have been informed and haven't yet drunk enough to forget, so you can count yourself lucky. Are you prepared to <hicks> receive my line of the prayer?",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_13": "So receive my prayer: 'Your hand shall be guided - your feet shall walk in <hicks> harmony'. Now, take your stake to Tyrias in <hicks> Liberty Bay for the next line of the prayer. I shall let him know what he is to do.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_14": "I'll wait for you.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_15": "You should visit Tyrias in Liberty Bay now.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_16": "You have already received my line of the prayer. Don't make me do more work than necessary!",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_17": "A blessed stake? That's a <hicks> strange request. Maybe Quentin knows more, he is one of the oldest monks after all.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_18": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_19": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_20": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_21": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_22": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_23": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_24": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_25": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_26": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_27": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_28": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_29": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_30": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.brewster.stdmod_31": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_2": "Very good, we need heroes like you to go on a suici.....er....to earn respect of the authorities here AND in addition get a great reward for it. Are you interested in the job?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_3": "What? YOU DID IT?!?! That's...that's...er....<drops a piece of paper. You see the headline 'death certificate'> like I expected!! Here is your reward.",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_4": "Very nice, |PLAYERNAME|. That will push the trolls' forces back a little. Here is your reward!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_5": "Congratulations, you've fought well against the goblin plague. Thank you! Here is your reward!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_6": "Well done! Thanks to you the city is a bit safer. Here's your reward!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_7": "Very good job, |PLAYERNAME|. You've been a great help. Here's your reward!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_8": "Currently there is no new task I could entrust you with. However, you can repeat killing {goblins} or {trolls}. Which would you prefer?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_9": "Maybe you have noticed the numerous rotworms that burrowed under Edron. They're quite a pest. You look strong enough to be able to vanquish a few for us. Do you think you can kill 300 rotworms?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_10": "I'm pleased with your eagerness. To reach your goal, you have to kill the brown trolls and troll champions. Good luck!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_11": "Fine then! You can kill normal goblins as well as scavengers and assassins on the lower levels, but beware, they are a bit harder. Have a good hunt!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_12": "I'm pleased with your eagerness. To help you find the trolls' den, I mark both the entrance to the passage and their lair on your map. To reach your goal, you have to kill the normal brown trolls, but troll champions count too. Good luck!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_13": "Fine then! I'll show you the Goblin den on your map, here. Use the same passage you did when hunting for trolls. You can kill normal goblins as well as scavengers and assassins on the lower levels, but beware, they are a bit harder.",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_14": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to killing 150 goblins. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_15": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to repeat killing 100 trolls. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_16": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to killing 500 cyclops. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_17": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to killing 300 rotworms. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_18": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to killing 150 goblins. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_19": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to repeat killing 100 trolls. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_20": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to killing 500 cyclops. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.say_21": "Another option if you want to do a task for Edron would be to killing 300 rotworms. Would that suit your taste better?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.stdmod_22": "I am the governor of this isle, Edron, and grandmaster of the Knights of Banor's Blood.",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.stdmod_23": "LONG LIVE THE KING!",
  "npc.tim_the_guard.say_1": "Ah, well. Just this morning my new toothbrush fell into the toilet.",
  "npc.tim_the_guard.say_2": "What do you mean? Of course they will immediately send someone with extra long and thin arms to retrieve it! ",
  "npc.tim_the_guard.say_3": "Your humour might let end you up beaten in some dark alley, you know? No, I don't think someone could have prevented that accident! ",
  "npc.tim_the_guard.stdmod_4": "It's my duty to protect the city.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_1": "If you have passed the first six seals and entered the blue fires that lead to the chamber of the seal you might receive my {kiss} ... It will open the last seal. Do you think you are ready?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_2": "Are you prepared to receive my kiss, even though this will mean that your death as well as a part of your soul will forever belong to me, my dear?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_3": "You have already received my kiss. You should know better then to ask for it.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_4": "Your wish for a spectral dress is silly. Although I will grant you the permission to take one. My maidens left one in a box in a room, directly south of here.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_5": "Say... I have been longing for something for an eternity now... if you help me retrieve it, I will reward you. Do you consent to this arrangement?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_6": "Have you really brought me 50 holy orchids?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_7": "The Queen of the Banshee: Yessss, I can sense you have passed the seal of sacrifice. Have you passed any other seal yet?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_8": "You have not passed the seal of sacrifice yet. Return to me when you are better prepared.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_9": "The Queen of the Banshee: I sense you have passed the hidden seal as well. Have you passed any other seal yet?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_10": "You have not found the hidden seal yet. Return when you are better prepared.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_11": "The Queen of the Banshee: Oh yes, you have braved the plague seal. Have you passed any other seal yet?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_12": "You have not faced the plagueseal yet. Return to me when you are better prepared.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_13": "The Queen of the Banshee: Ah, I can sense the power of the seal of demonrage burning in your heart. Have you passed any other seal yet?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_14": "You are not filled with the fury of the imprisoned demon. Return when you are better prepared.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_15": "The Queen of the Banshee: So, you have managed to pass the seal of the true path. Have you passed any other seal yet?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_16": "You have not found your true path yet. Return when you are better prepared.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_17": "The Queen of the Banshee: I see! You have mastered the seal of logic. You have made the sacrifice, you have seen the unseen, you possess fortitude, you have filled yourself with power and found your path. You may ask me for my {kiss} now.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_18": "You have not found your true path yet. Return to meh when you are better prepared.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_19": "So be it! Hmmmmmm...",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_20": "You have spilled too much blood recently and the dead are hungry for your soul. Perhaps return when you regained you inner balance.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_21": "Listen... there are no blooming flowers down here and the only smell present is that of death and decay. I wish that I could breathe the lovely smell of beautiful flowers just one more time, especially those which elves cultivate. Could you please bring me 50 holy orchids?",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_22": "Thank you. I will wait for your return.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_23": "Thank you! You have no idea what that means to me. As promised, here is your reward... as a follower of Zathroth, I hope that you will like this accessory.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_24": "You need 50 holy orchid.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_25": "Then try to be better prepared next time we meet.",
  "npc.the_queen_of_the_banshees.say_26": "Perhaps it is the better choice for you, my dear.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_1": "Haha, that beard is - well, not fake, but there's a trick behind it. I noticed people tend to be more generous towards a poor gramps. Want to know my trick?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_2": "Have you brought me the 100 pieces of ape fur and 20000 gold pieces?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_3": "Hmm, I'm not done yet with your potion. But here, let me sprinkle a few drops of my own potion on your face... there you go. Now you just have to wait.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_4": "Aha! I can see it! Now that you've waited patiently without shaving, your beard is perfect! All thanks to my, err, potion. Yes. Goodbye!",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_5": "Hmm, it seems you need to wait a bit longer for the potion to take full effect. Please be patient.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_6": "Aha! I can see it! Now that you've waited patiently without shaving, your beard is perfect! All thanks to my, err, potion. Yes. Goodbye!",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_7": "Hmm, it seems you need to wait a bit longer for the potion to take full effect. Please be patient.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_8": "Oh, I'm sorry... I almost forgot! Okay, okay... here is your promised dress. I'm sure it will look so much better on you than on me- I mean, my, err, sister.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_9": "Great! Come back to me once you have the 100 pieces of ape fur and I'll do my part of the deal.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_10": "Ahh! Very good. I will start mixing the potion immediately. Come back later. Bye bye.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_11": "You do not have all the required items.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_12": "You do not have all the required items.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_13": "It seems you already have this addon, don't you try to mock me son!",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_14": "No, no. Our deal is finished, no complaining now, I don't have time all day. And no, you can't have my staff.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_15": "I said, no! Or well - I have a suggestion to make. Will you listen?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_16": "Good! Come back to me once you have retrieved my staff. Good luck.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_17": "Did you bring my favourite staff??",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_18": "Yes!! That's it! I'm so glad! Here, you can have my other one. Thanks!",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_19": "You do not have the staff.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_20": "You do not have the staff.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_21": "Sorry, but you need to have a premium account!",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_22": "Have you brought a cookie for the poor?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_23": "I need gold. Can you spare 100 gold pieces for me?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_24": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_25": "You haven't got enough money for me.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_26": "Thank you very much. Can you spare 500 more gold pieces for me? I will give you a nice hint.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_27": "Sorry, that's not enough.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_28": "Pah! I said 200 gold. You don't have that much.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.say_29": "Now you own the hot key.",
  "npc.hugo.say_1": "A new uniform for the post officers? I am sorry but my dog ate the last dress pattern we used. You need to supply us with a new dress pattern.",
  "npc.hugo.say_2": "It was ... wonderous beyond wildest imaginations! I have no clue where Kevin Postner got it from. Better ask him.",
  "npc.hugo.say_3": "By the gods of fashion! Didn't it do that I fed the last dress pattern to my poor dog? Will this mocking of all which is taste and fashion never stop?? Ok, ok, you will get those ugly, stinking uniforms and now get lost, fashion terrorist.",
  "npc.hugo.say_4": "Sorry, but my time is currently reserved for premium matters.",
  "npc.hugo.say_5": "I am so excited! This poor man's look will be an outfit like the world has never seen before.",
  "npc.hugo.say_6": "Sorry, but I am not done with the outfit yet. Venore wasn't built in a day.",
  "npc.hugo.say_7": "Eureka! Alas, the poor man's outfit is finished, but... to be honest... it turned out much less appealing than I expected. However, you can have it if you want, okay?",
  "npc.hugo.say_8": "I guess my vision wasn't that grand after all. I hope there are still people who enjoy it.",
  "npc.hugo.say_9": "Terrific! What are you waiting for?! Start right away gathering 20 pieces of brown cloth and come back once you have them!",
  "npc.hugo.say_10": "Here you go. Maybe you enjoy if after all.",
  "npc.hugo.say_11": "Argh! I guess this awesome idea has to remain unimplemented. What a pity.",
  "npc.hugo.say_12": "Do you want me to repeat the task requirements?",
  "npc.hugo.say_13": "Hurry! I am at my creative peak right now!",
  "npc.hugo.say_14": "Well, if you should change your mind, just ask me for the beggar outfit.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_1": "I am responsible for our war {missions}, to {trade} with seasoned soldiers and rewarding war {heroes}. You have to be rank 4 to enter the {warzones}.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_2": "As a war hero you are allowed to use the warzone teleporter one for free!",
  "npc.gnomission.say_3": "I can't let you enter the warzone teleporter one for free, unless you handle me a Deathstrike's snippet. But can still always use a red teleport crystal.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_4": "We've already talked about that.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_5": "As a war hero you are allowed to use the warzone teleporter three for free!",
  "npc.gnomission.say_6": "I can't let you enter the warzone teleporter two for free, unless you handle me an Abyssador's lash. But can still always use a red teleport crystal.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_7": "You need to defeat the first warzone boss to be able to get free access to the second warzone.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_8": "We've already talked about that.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_9": "As a war hero you are allowed to use the warzone teleporter second for free!",
  "npc.gnomission.say_10": "I can't let you enter the warzone teleporter three for free, unless you handle me a Gnomevil's hat. But can still always use a red teleport crystal.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_11": "You need to defeat the second warzone boss to be able to get free access to the third warzone.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_12": "We've already talked about that.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_13": "Fine, I grant you the permission to enter the warzones. Be warned though, this will be not a picnic. Better bring some friends with you. Bringing a lot of them sounds like a good idea.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_14": "You have already accepted this mission.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_15": "Sorry, you have not yet earned enough renown that we would risk your life in such a dangerous mission.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_16": "Only if you have killed 20 of our major enemies in the warzones I am allowed to trade with you.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_17": "You have already accepted this mission.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_18": "Sorry, you have not yet earned enough renown that we would risk your life in such a dangerous mission.",
  "npc.gnomission.say_19": "Only if you have killed 20 of our major enemies in the warzones I am allowed to trade with you.",
  "npc.xodet.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.xodet.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.xodet.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.xodet.say_4": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.xodet.say_5": "Ok then.",
  "npc.xodet.say_6": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.reed.say_1": "You have NO idea what we have to endure each day .. <gives a shocking and disturbing report>. ",
  "npc.reed.say_2": "You can {pass} either to the {Cemetery Quarter} or {Magician Quarter}. Which one will it be?",
  "npc.albinius.say_1": "The temple has been restored to its former glory, yet we strife to live and praise in the {Shaper} ways. Do you still need me to take some old {tomes} from you my child?",
  "npc.albinius.say_2": "You already offered enough tomes for us to study and rebuild this temple. Thank you, my child.",
  "npc.albinius.say_3": "Thank you very much for your contribution, child. Your first step in the ways of the {Shapers} has been taken.",
  "npc.albinius.say_4": "You need 5 heavy old tome.",
  "npc.albinius.say_5": "I understand. Return to me if you change your mind, my child.",
  "npc.albinius.say_6": "If you have some old shaper tomes I would {buy} them.",
  "npc.albinius.say_7": "I'm sorry, I don't buy anything. My main concern right now is the bulding of this temple.",
  "npc.albinius.say_8": "Do you wish to merge your rune parts into an astral shaper rune?",
  "npc.albinius.say_9": "I'm sorry but you lack the needed rune parts.",
  "npc.albinius.say_10": "As you wish.",
  "npc.albinius.say_11": "You may pass this portal if you have 50 fish as offering. Do you have the fish with you?",
  "npc.albinius.say_12": "Sorry, you first need to bring my Heavy Old Tomes or do the quest before continuing.",
  "npc.albinius.say_13": "Thank you for your offering. You may pass the Portal to the Powers of Ice now.",
  "npc.albinius.say_14": "I'm sorry, you don't have enough fish. Return if you can offer fifty of them.",
  "npc.albinius.say_15": "In this case I'm sorry, you may not pass this portal.",
  "npc.albinius.say_16": "You may pass this portal if you have 50 incantation notes as offering. Do you have the incantation notes with you?",
  "npc.albinius.say_17": "Sorry, first you need to bring my Heavy Old Tomes.",
  "npc.albinius.say_18": "Thank you for your offering. You may pass the Portal to the Powers of Holy now.",
  "npc.albinius.say_19": "I'm sorry, you don't have enough incantation notes. Return if you can offer fifty of them.",
  "npc.albinius.say_20": "In this case I'm sorry, you may not pass this portal.",
  "npc.albinius.say_21": "You may pass this portal if you have 50 marsh stalker feathers as offering. Do you have the marsh stalker feathers with you?",
  "npc.albinius.say_22": "Sorry, first you need to bring my Heavy Old Tomes.",
  "npc.albinius.say_23": "Thank you for your offering. You may pass the Portal to the Powers of Energy now.",
  "npc.albinius.say_24": "I'm sorry, you don't have enough marsh stalker feathers. Return if you can offer fifty of them.",
  "npc.albinius.say_25": "In this case I'm sorry, you may not pass this portal.",
  "npc.albinius.say_26": "You may pass this portal if you have 50 acorns as offering. Do you have the acorns with you?",
  "npc.albinius.say_27": "Sorry, first you need to bring my Heavy Old Tomes.",
  "npc.albinius.say_28": "Thank you for your offering. You may pass the Portal to the Powers of Earth now.",
  "npc.albinius.say_29": "I'm sorry, you don't have enough acorns. Return if you can offer fifty of them.",
  "npc.albinius.say_30": "In this case I'm sorry, you may not pass this portal.",
  "npc.albinius.say_31": "You may pass this portal if you have 50 pelvis bones as offering. Do you have the pelvis bones with you?",
  "npc.albinius.say_32": "Sorry, first you need to bring my Heavy Old Tomes.",
  "npc.albinius.say_33": "Thank you for your offering. You may pass the Portal to the Powers of Death now.",
  "npc.albinius.say_34": "I'm sorry, you don't have enough pelvis bones. Return if you can offer fifty of them.",
  "npc.albinius.say_35": "In this case I'm sorry, you may not pass this portal.",
  "npc.albinius.stdmod_36": "I am Albinius, a worshipper of the {Astral Shapers}.",
  "npc.albinius.stdmod_37": "Precisely time.",
  "npc.albinius.stdmod_38": "I find ways to unveil the secrets of the stars. Judging by this question, I doubt you follow my weekly publications concerning this research.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_1": "Oh, you want some work? You can help us, alright. Did you know that the people of the city think those rabbit feet are actually lucky charms?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_2": "You need to wait some hours to take another mission again or you are still on a mission.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_3": "Good to see you back. Now, did you bring us the lucky charms?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_4": "You need to wait some hours to take another mission again or you are still on a mission.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_5": "Ah there you are. So, did you repair all the broken structures?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_6": "You need to wait some hours to take another mission again or you are still on a mission.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_7": "You need to wait some hours to take another mission again or you are still on a mission.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_8": "You did it!! And I assume you took only what you needed? Heh. No, I know it. Because my men took the rest. Thanks for helping us, you did a very good job. In fact I have a little 'extra' for you here, thanks again.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_9": "You need to wait some hours to take another mission again or you are still on a mission.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_10": "Good, because that is exactly what you will help us with - getting more 'lucky charms'. If we won't get our hands on new charms in time, we will surely have to starve... during the autumn. That would be a hard time for all of us. So... you in?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_11": "Good hunt. That will be enough to help us uhm... get through the winter yes. Now if you want to help us getting even more lucky charms, you can always ask.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_12": "You do not have sufficient rabbit's foot.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.say_13": "Good, good. Do you remember the old saying? If it ain't broken, it was not made by us. Now, off you go!",
  "npc.lisander.say_1": "A cookie? Sure, is it for free?",
  "npc.lisander.say_2": "Whatever you have there, I think I don't want it.",
  "npc.lisander.say_3": "Errrkss - coughcough - what the - heck did you put in there? Get out of my sight!",
  "npc.lisander.stdmod_4": "Hold your tongue.",
  "npc.yaman.say_1": "Shove off, little one! Humans are not welcome here, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.yaman.say_2": "Be greeted, human |PLAYERNAME|. How can a humble djinn be of service?",
  "npc.yaman.say_3": "Do you want to trade Boots of haste for Enchanted Chicken Wing?",
  "npc.yaman.say_4": "Do you want to trade 4 Warrior Helmet for Warrior Sweat?",
  "npc.yaman.say_5": "Do you want to trade 2 Royal Helmet for Fighting Spirit",
  "npc.yaman.say_6": "Do you want to trade 3 Fire Sword for Magic Sulphur",
  "npc.yaman.say_7": "I trade Enchanted Chicken Wing for Boots of Haste, Warrior Sweat for 4 Warrior Helmets, Fighting Spirit for 2 Royal Helmet Magic Sulphur for 3 Fire Swords",
  "npc.yaman.say_8": "You brought cookies! How nice of you! Can I have one?",
  "npc.yaman.say_9": "Here you are.",
  "npc.yaman.say_10": "Sorry but you don't have the item.",
  "npc.yaman.say_11": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.yaman.say_12": "You see, good deeds like this will ... YOU ... YOU SPAWN OF EVIL! I WILL MAKE SURE THE MASTER LEARNS ABOUT THIS!",
  "npc.yaman.say_13": "Ok then.",
  "npc.yaman.say_14": "I see.",
  "npc.yaman.say_15": "I'm sorry, but you don't have Malor's permission to trade with me.",
  "npc.arnold.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.frafnar.say_1": "There is indeed something you could do for me. You must know, I'm in love with Bolfana. I'm sure she'd have a beer with me if I got her a chocolate cake. Problem is that I can't leave this door as I'm on duty. Would you be so kind and help me?",
  "npc.frafnar.say_2": "So did you tell her that the cake came from me?",
  "npc.frafnar.say_3": "Great! She works in the tavern of Beregar. It's situated in the western part of the city. Bring her a chocolate cake and tell her that it was me who sent it.",
  "npc.frafnar.say_4": "I hope your kidding 'cause I'll find out WHAT you've told her and I can get reeeeaaaalllly angry. I grant you access to the western part of the mine.....for NOW.",
  "npc.testserver_assistant.say_1": "There you have",
  "npc.testserver_assistant.say_2": "You can not take it anymore",
  "npc.testserver_assistant.say_3": "Here you are |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.testserver_assistant.say_4": "You have been blessed by all gods, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.testserver_assistant.say_5": "You can not take it anymore",
  "npc.ariella.say_1": "So you brought a cookie to a pirate?",
  "npc.ariella.say_2": "You mean my hat? Well, I might have another one just like that, but I won't simply give it away, even if you earned our trust. You'd have to fulfil a task first.",
  "npc.ariella.say_3": "Your task is to bring me the shirt of the Lethal Lissy, the sabre of Ron the Ripper, the hat of Brutus Bloodbeard and the eye patch of Deadeye Devious. Did you succeed?",
  "npc.ariella.say_4": "You know, we have plenty of rum here but we lack some basic food. Especially food that easily becomes mouldy is a problem. Bring me 100 breads and you will help me a lot.",
  "npc.ariella.say_5": "Are you here to bring me the 100 pieces of bread that I requested?",
  "npc.ariella.say_6": "Did you get a sample of the whisper beer from Carlin?",
  "npc.ariella.say_7": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.ariella.say_8": "How sweet of you ... Uhh ... OH NO ... Bozo did it again. Tell this prankster I'll pay him back.",
  "npc.ariella.say_9": "What a joy. At least for a few days adequate supply is ensured.",
  "npc.ariella.say_10": "Come back when you got all neccessary items.",
  "npc.ariella.say_11": "Thank you very much. I will test this beauty in privacy.",
  "npc.ariella.say_12": "Come back when you got the neccessary item.",
  "npc.ariella.say_13": "INCREDIBLE! You have found all four of them! |PLAYERNAME|, you have my respect. You more than deserve this hat. There you go.",
  "npc.ariella.say_14": "You do not have all the required items.",
  "npc.ariella.say_15": "I see.",
  "npc.ariella.say_16": "Alright then. Come back when you got all neccessary items.",
  "npc.alesar_functions.say_1": "Did you find the tear of Daraman?",
  "npc.alesar_functions.say_2": "Don't forget to talk to Malor concerning your next mission.",
  "npc.alesar_functions.say_3": "Then not.",
  "npc.alesar_functions.say_4": "As I expected. You haven't got the stone. Shall I explain your mission again?",
  "npc.alesar_functions.say_5": "As I expected. You haven't got the stone. Shall I explain your mission again?",
  "npc.a_beggar.say_1": "The guys from the magistrate sent you here, didn't they?",
  "npc.sarina.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.sarina.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.sarina.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.arito.say_1": "And what did they say?? Do I have to give up everything here? Come on tell me!!",
  "npc.arito.say_2": "These are great news!! Thank you for your help! I don't have much, but without you I wouldn't have anything so please take this as a reward.",
  "npc.captain_jack_rat.say_1": "There are two different routes. The dangerous one will be available once a day and it is likely that a seemonster will attack the ship once again. And a {safe} route that we can take directly there.",
  "npc.captain_jack_rat.say_2": "Do you want to take the safe route?",
  "npc.charlotta.say_1": "Oh, so you brought some gold from Eleonore to me?",
  "npc.charlotta.say_2": "Hmm, it seems that Eleonore does trust you. Perhaps she is even right. However. Since we need some help right now I guess we can't be too picky. Return to Eleonore and tell her the secret password: 'peg leg'. She will tell you more about her problem.",
  "npc.charlotta.say_3": "You don't have enough...",
  "npc.charlotta.say_4": "Then no.",
  "npc.gnome_trooper.say_1": "But you don't have it...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_1": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_2": "Come back when you have finished your job.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_3": "You got rid of a lot of corpses, very good. Now we have a realistic chance of pushing them back! Return to me later for more work if you want.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_4": "Noted. Get one of the gnomish devices from the container next to me and 'use' it on any diremaw corpses to effectively neutralise them. At least the gnomes told me this will work - good luck!",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_5": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_6": "You did a great job out there, the stuff will continue to grow, however. Return to me later for more work.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_7": "Noted. Now, get down there and rain some fire on them.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_8": "If you bring me any suspicious devices on creatures you slay down here, I'll make it worth your while by telling the others of your generosity. How many do you want to offer? ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_9": "Don't waste my time.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_10": "Done.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_11": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_12": "Done.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_13": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_14": "Done.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_15": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_16": "So you want to know what we all think about your deeds? What leader's opinion are you interested in, the {gnomes} (Gnomus), the {dwarves} (Klom Stonecutter) or the {scouts} (Lardoc Bashsmite)?",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_17": "So you want to know what we all think about your deeds? What leader's opinion are you interested in, the {gnomes} (Gnomus), the {dwarves} (Klom Stonecutter) or the {scouts} (Lardoc Bashsmite)?",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_18": "The gnomes are still in need of your help, member of Bigfoot's Brigade. Prove your worth by answering their calls! (",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_19": "The dwarves are still in need of your help, member of Bigfoot's Brigade. Prove your worth by answering their calls! (",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.say_20": "The scouts are still in need of your help, member of Bigfoot's Brigade. Prove your worth by answering their calls! (",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.stdmod_21": "Here's the situation: a tide of hazardous bugs, the gnomes named them {diremaws}, threatens our base. Then there is some kind of {growth} which seems connected to them somehow. We need to get rid of both.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.stdmod_22": "Bashsmite. That's all you need to know.",
  "npc.bambi_bonecrusher.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.vanys.say_1": "So do you want to learn the {story} behind of this or rather talk about the {task} at hand? ",
  "npc.vanys.say_2": "Do you prefer the {long} version or the {short} version?",
  "npc.vanys.say_3": "The Nightmare Beast is slain. You have done well. The Courts of Summer and Winter will be forever grateful. For your efforts I want to reward you with our traditional dream warrior outfit. May it suit you well!",
  "npc.vanys.say_4": "I already gave your task.",
  "npc.vanys.say_5": "They are not literally keys but rather puzzles you have to solve or a secret mechanism you have to discover in order to open the Dream Doors. A parchment in the chest here can tell you more about it.",
  "npc.vanys.say_6": "Are you interested in one or two addons to your dream warrior outfit?",
  "npc.vanys.say_7": "You don't even have the outfit.",
  "npc.vanys.say_8": "I provide two addons. For the first one I need you to bring me five pomegranates. For the second addon you need an ice shield. Do you want one of these addons?",
  "npc.vanys.say_9": "What do you have for me: the {pomegranates} or the {ice shield}?",
  "npc.vanys.say_10": "Very good! You gained the second addon to the dream warrior outfit.",
  "npc.vanys.say_11": "You do not have enough items.",
  "npc.vanys.say_12": "Very good! You gained the first addon to the dream warrior outfit.",
  "npc.vanys.say_13": "You do not have enough items.",
  "npc.vanys.say_14": "Sorry, I didn't understand.",
  "npc.tandros.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_5": "The temple is in the south-eastern part of town. If you exit the depot to the south and walk east - slightly south-east - you can't miss it.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_6": "Tesha is in charge of both the bank and the gem store. You can find her on the market pyramid. Just exit the depot on the north side and walk up the next pyramid.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, furniture, spells and food here.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_9": "I will help you to find your way around Ankrahmun. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_10": "Ankrahmun consists almost completely of pyramids. You can walk up and down those pyramids just like you'd climb up stairs. Most shops are on the upper floors.",
  "npc.guide_rahlkora.stdmod_11": "My name is Rahlkora. I'm a guide.",
  "npc.emma.say_1": "I am still a bit sceptical, but well, welcome to the girls brigade.",
  "npc.emma.say_2": "How unnecessarily complicated, but that's the way those Thaians are. In the end we got what we wanted and they can't do anything about it.",
  "npc.emma.say_3": "Bring me the spellbook.",
  "npc.emma.say_4": "I think the druids will be pleased to hear that the immediate threat has been averted.",
  "npc.emma.say_5": "Bring me the heart as proof.",
  "npc.emma.say_6": "Great! This blow strikes them where it hurts most: profit.",
  "npc.emma.say_7": "I hope our craftsmen can do something with this stuff. For me it makes hardly any sense.",
  "npc.emma.say_8": "You need to bring me those plans!",
  "npc.emma.say_9": "I will have this correspondence examined by our specialists. I am sure they are quite revealing.",
  "npc.emma.say_10": "Bring me back some hints or something!",
  "npc.emma.say_11": "I hope this old book will do those researches any good. Personally I see little use to proof some bloodlines after we cut all ties to Thais.",
  "npc.emma.say_12": "You need to bring us that book of family trees!",
  "npc.emma.say_13": "Please bring me proof of the mad technomancers defeat!",
  "npc.emma.say_14": "As you wish.",
  "npc.emma.say_15": "A man in the girls brigade? Come on this is hilarious, this is outright stupid, this is ... exactly what no one would expect. Mhm, on second thought the element of surprise might offset your male inferiority.",
  "npc.emma.say_16": "Don't try to fool me. We are perfectly aware to whom you are loyal.",
  "npc.emma.say_17": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.say_18": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.say_19": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.say_20": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.say_21": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.say_22": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.say_23": "Have you been successful?",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_24": "I am privileged to be in service of our beloved queen!",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_25": "We are proud people who fought hard for their freedom and won't allow others to oppress us again.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_26": "I am the head of Carlin's Girls Brigade, also known as CGB.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_27": "I am the head of Carlin's Girls Brigade, also known as CGB.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_28": "I am known as Emma.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_29": "The Thaians never got over the fact that we gained our independence. They do everything they can to hinder the prospering of our city.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_30": "Venore is a hellhole of evil. The trade barons' greed lets them plot against all other cities and even against each other.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_31": "Svargrond is an important project for our city. It's not a colony but many of our people live there alongside those barbarians. If everything works out fine, Carlin and Svargrond will both prosper.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_32": "Strange people with strange customs live in this city. Luckily, we rarely have to deal with them.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_33": "Darashia never bothers about the affairs of other cities.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_34": "It's just another Thaian puppet. Still, it is distant enough to stand a fair chance to get rid of Thais's oppression one day.",
  "npc.emma.stdmod_35": "The dwarfs of Kazordoon usually mind their own business. I wish all other cities would do the same.",
  "npc.arkulius.say_1": "I'm sorry this task is highly dangerous and I need experienced people for it.",
  "npc.arkulius.say_2": "AMAZING!! I'm going to start immediately with the research. If it turns out the way I expect it, Alverus will be revived soon!! Here, take this as a reward and try to collect more of this substance. I'll make you a good offer, I promise. ",
  "npc.arkulius.say_3": "Good, don't waste time! Come back here when you have the elemental object!",
  "npc.arkulius.say_4": "Good, don't waste time! Come back here when you have the elemental object!",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_5": "I'm Arkulius - Master of Elements, the headmaster of this academy.",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_6": "I have better things to do than helping you. See that ice statue over there? My dear friend Alverus needs to be revived!",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_7": "Time is an illusion and completely irrelevant to me.",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_8": "Weapons are for those people who aren't able to use their heads or better what's INSIDE their heads. No offence <coughs>.",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_9": "Yeye, I believe you almost feel like home among all those brainless creatures!",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_10": "Yeye, I believe you almost feel like home among all those brainless creatures!",
  "npc.tamerin.say_1": "You have kept your promise. Now, it's time to fulfil my part of the bargain. What kind of animals shall I raise? {Warbeasts} or {cattle}?",
  "npc.tamerin.say_2": "Thank you very much. As I said, as soon as you have helped me to solve both of my problems, we will talk about your mission. Have you killed {morik}?",
  "npc.tamerin.say_3": "Come back when you have the cure.",
  "npc.tamerin.say_4": "So be it!",
  "npc.tamerin.say_5": "So be it!",
  "npc.tamerin.say_6": "So he finally got what he deserved. As I said, as soon as you have helped me to solve both of my problems, we will talk about your {mission}.",
  "npc.tamerin.say_7": "Come back when you got rid with Morik.",
  "npc.tamerin.say_8": "I ask you for two things! For one thing, I need an animal cure and for another thing, I ask you to get rid of the gladiator Morik for me.",
  "npc.bolfona.say_1": "Is that for me?",
  "npc.bolfona.say_2": "So did you tell her that the cake came from me?",
  "npc.bolfona.say_3": "Err, thanks. I doubt it's from you. Who sent it?",
  "npc.bolfona.say_4": "Oh, I thought you have one.",
  "npc.bolfona.say_5": "Oh, Frafnar. That's so nice of him. I gotta invite him for a beer.",
  "npc.bolfona.say_6": "Never heard that name. Well, I don't mind, thanks for the cake.",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_1": "By now the cultists of the Shiron'Fal seem to have abandoned their search. But this is sadly no good news. It seems they gathered enough lich-knights to proceed with their {ultimate} plan.",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_2": "Sadly, I have no news yet. But I can give you information about the {locations} of the graves that we learned about. If you need more holy water just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_3": "Here is your second addon for your efforts!",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_4": "Here is your first addon for your efforts!",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_5": "Incredible! You averted a crisis that would have utterly crippled our defences aganist any other threat that is arising. Let me grant you the honor to be one of the hands of the inquisition alongside with the according outfit as a reward.",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_6": "Indeed you averted us a great danger! We will ever be greatful to you hand of the inquisition!",
  "npc.jack_springer.say_7": "You need to travel to the isle of the kings and end this threat before they raise king Zelos!",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_8": "I need your help in a matter of utmost {urgency}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_9": "The situation is complicated and it's even hard to say where to {start} best, just to describe it to you.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_10": "You see, several incidents in history can be traced back to a single {source}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_11": "Things get murkier the further you go down in history, but that's not even necessary. Even today we can discern a certain pattern in recent {events}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_12": "The recent rise of lycanthropy, the robbery of certain forbidden arcane texts and the vanishing of at least three dangerous individuals, targeted by the inquisition are just the tip of the {iceberg}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_13": "This outside force is moving behind the scenes since ages. Our research suggests that this force probably even {predates} the rise of humanity.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_14": "Well, we are sure that the puppeteer behind all these events is an organisation. So old that even its name, the Shiron'Fal, has lost its meaning, because the {language} it originates from is long dead.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_15": "Here is where you come into play. We could identify the most recent plot of the Shiron'Fal and already had some {clashes}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_16": "In our efforts to hinder their plot, we achieved mixed results at best. But now things are escalating fast and we have to {hurry}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_17": "Our resources are already stretched thin, so we need your help with the most recent {problem}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_18": "The legion tries to use a new form of twisted rituals to raise the bodies of well-known {knights}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_19": "These powerful undead were a terrible threat on their own but it seems even they are just part of some larger {scheme} that we cannot make out yet.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_20": "We are still working feverishly to uncover their goals but for now more imminent {threats} are at hand.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_21": "Death cultists of the Shiron'Fal are trying to locate the bodies of fallen knights and raise them in blasphemous {rituals}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.stdmod_22": "The churches of the gods worked hand in hand to supply us with the means to {purge} the graves of those knights.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_1": "I sell musical instruments of many kinds.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_2": "I sell lyres, lutes, drums, and simple fanfares.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_3": "Music is an attempt to condensate emotions in harmonies and save them for the times to come.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_4": "Time has its own song. Close your eyes and listen to the symphony of the seasons.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_5": "Everything is a song. Life, death, history ... everything. To listen to the song of something is the first step to understand it.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_6": "Everything is a song. Life, death, history ... everything. To listen to the song of something is the first step to understand it.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_7": "We are the most graceful of all races. We feel the music of the universe in our hearts and souls.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_8": "They could dig some halls for a big musical event, but they won't listen to me about that matter.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_9": "I bet they were great musicians.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_10": "That is some god the humans worship. Our pople are not interested in this gods anymore.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_11": "They are too loud and don't even understand the concept of a melody.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_12": "The other deraisim are too much concerned with mastering the nature so they don't listen to its music anymore.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_13": "The Cenath think they know the 'art' but the only true art is the music.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_14": "I went down to the mines and tried to lighten up their spirit, the foolish creatures did not listen to my songs, though.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_15": "Sorry, I don't feel like teaching magic today.",
  "npc.elvith.stdmod_16": "For the worst of crimes, criminals are cast into hellgate. It is said no one can return from there. Since it is not actually forbidden to enter hellgate, you might convince Elathriel to grant you entrance.",
  "npc.elvith.say_17": "Do you want to buy a poem scroll for 200 gold?",
  "npc.elvith.say_18": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.elvith.say_19": "Here it is.",
  "npc.norma.say_1": "Oh, you're back already? Did you bring a legion helmet, 100 chicken feathers and 50 honeycombs?",
  "npc.norma.say_2": "Pretty, isn't it? I made it myself, but I could teach you how to do that if you like. What do you say?",
  "npc.norma.say_3": "Okay, here we go, listen closely! I need a few things... a basic hat of course, maybe a legion helmet would do. Then about 100 chicken feathers... and 50 honeycombs as glue.That's it, come back to me once you gathered it!!",
  "npc.norma.say_4": "Aw, I guess you don't like feather hats. No big deal.",
  "npc.norma.say_5": "Sorry, but I can't see a legion helmet.",
  "npc.norma.say_6": "Sorry, but you don't enough chicken feathers.",
  "npc.norma.say_7": "Sorry, but you don't have enough honeycombs.",
  "npc.norma.say_8": "Great job! That must have taken a lot of work. Okay, you put it like this... then glue like this... here!",
  "npc.norma.say_9": "Maybe another time.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_10": "Well, my name is {Norma}.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_11": "I used to be a merchant, but being a barkeeper is so much more fun. It's been my dream since I was a little girl.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_12": "It's about |TIME|. Time just flies, doesn't it?",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_13": "To view the offers of a merchant, simply talk to him or her and ask for a {trade}. They will gladly show you their offers and also the things they buy from you.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_14": "I've never been better! I love my new {job}!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_15": "No sorry, I'm out of that business. Please ask {Obi} or {Lee'Delle} if you need a weapon.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_16": "As an adventurer, you should always have at least a {backpack}, a {rope}, a {shovel}, a {weapon}, an {armor} and a {shield}.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_17": "Ah, the monsters are far away. Let's party now!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_18": "If you really want to talk about dungeons, visit Dallheim on the bridge near my bar.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_19": "Ewww, I don't even want to think about the smell from the sewers right now!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_20": "Oooh, I wouldn't dare gossiping about the king. He might have his spies here somewhere, you know.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_21": "This is the world we live in, oh-oh-oh, and these are the hands we're given, oh-oh... oh, I'm sorry, I got carried away!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_22": "As a premium adventurer you have many advantages, you should check them out!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_23": "I serve the best drinks in town! What's it gonna be, lemonade? Wine? Milk? Beer? Just ask me for a {trade}!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_24": "The temple is a good place to visit if you're in urgent need for healing.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_25": "Well, the only help I could give you are some general {hints}. And a delicious {drink} along with it.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_26": "No sorry, I'm out of that business. Please ask {Al Dee} or {Lee'Delle} if you need equipment.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_27": "No sorry, I'm out of that business. Please ask {Dixi} or {Lee'Delle} if you need equipment.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_28": "Oh, would you like something to eat or drink? Ask me for a {trade} to see my offers!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_29": "<gets a dreamy look in her eyes>",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_30": "Al Dee treats his customers friendly, but he's badmouthing them once he had a few beers.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_31": "I'm curious about her adventures. She really should come here more often!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_32": "He got lucky when Willie and him played a game of dice about who gets to farm on which side of the river. Ever since, Willie holds a grudge against him.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_33": "Hehe, that guy doesn't pretend to be anyone that he isn't. He is what he is - rude, but honest.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_34": "Oh shush! It's kinda disgusting when he walks in here with animal blood on his hands!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_35": "What Seymour doesn't teach you is how much fun you can have here!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_36": "I invited her to my bar, but she refused. Oh well, it was worth a try!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_37": "I think that poor guy never gets a break from work. At least he never comes here.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_38": "That guy seriously needs some partying and a girlfriend.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_39": "The oracle is on the top floor of the academy. You should go there once you are level 8 to leave this island.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_40": "I think it's rather strange that he lives here with his granddaughter. No one's ever seen the parents of {Dixi}.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_41": "I hate that name, it sounds so boring. Almost like 'normal'. I think I should change my name to something more exciting. Like... Marylin! Oh, what a glamorous sound!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_42": "She told me that she dreams of leaving this island to go on a big adventure.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_43": "They tell me strange stories about him and some monsters in a hole. Weird!",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_44": "That girl thinks that she is soooo special and 'high society'. We used to be friends, but well, things change.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_45": "That's probably someone I'll never see in my bar.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_46": "<giggles> That monk with his holier-than-thou attitude hasn't anything against a good mug of wine now and then.",
  "npc.norma.stdmod_47": "If you listen to him, you could get the impression my little bar is the devil himself. He says he has more work now keeping drunken adventurers in than monsters out of the city. Such an exaggeration!",
  "npc.markwin.say_1": "No! The hornless have reached my city! BODYGUARDS TO ME!",
  "npc.markwin.say_2": "A letter from my Moohmy?? Do you have a letter from my Moohmy to me?",
  "npc.markwin.say_3": "You bring me ... a cookie???",
  "npc.markwin.say_4": "Uhm, well thank you, hornless being.",
  "npc.markwin.say_5": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.markwin.say_6": "I understand this as a peace-offering, human ... UNGH ... THIS IS AN OUTRAGE! THIS MEANS WAR!!!",
  "npc.markwin.say_7": "Hm ... good bye.",
  "npc.rachel.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.rachel.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.rachel.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.rachel.say_4": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.rachel.say_5": "Ok then.",
  "npc.rachel.say_6": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.jacob.say_1": "I'm glad to see you back alive and healthy. Did you find anything interesting that you want to {report}?",
  "npc.jacob.say_2": "The sewers need repair. You in?",
  "npc.jacob.say_3": "Elliott's keeps calling it that. It's just another job! You fixed some broken pipes and stuff? Let me check, {ok}?",
  "npc.jacob.say_4": "If you want to redo this task just say {abandoned sewers} to repeat it.",
  "npc.jacob.say_5": "Good. Broken pipe and generator pieces, there's smoke evading. That's how you recognise them. See how you can fix them using your hands. Need about, oh, twenty of them at least repaired. Report to me or Jacob",
  "npc.jacob.say_6": "Good. Thanks, man. That's one vote you got for helping us with this.",
  "npc.jacob.say_7": "You already reported this mission, go to the next.",
  "npc.karl.say_1": "Do you bring me a barrel of beer??",
  "npc.karl.say_2": "Do you want to buy a bottle of our finest whisper beer for 80 gold?",
  "npc.karl.say_3": "Three cheers for the noble |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.karl.say_4": "You don't have any barrel of beer!",
  "npc.karl.say_5": "Here. Don't take it into the city though.",
  "npc.karl.say_6": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.shiriel.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.say_1": "So be it! Here is my part of the sceptre. Combine it with the other parts on the altar of the Great Snake in the depths of this temple.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.say_2": "So be it! Here is my part of the sceptre. Combine it with the other parts on the altar of the Great Snake in the depths of this temple.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.say_3": "So be it! Here is my part of the sceptre. Combine it with the other parts on the altar of the Great Snake in the depths of this temple.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.say_4": "No deal then.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_5": "We are the {guardians}. We are all what is left from the glory of the past.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_6": "We are the keepers of this old temple and the guardians of its sacred {secrets}.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_7": "We are keepers of the {lore} of the Great {Snake} and we guard some of its {relics}.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_8": "The lore of the Great {Snake} is contorted like a snake. Although we feel you are touched by the snake's essence, you are not ready yet to receive the blessing of the deeper wisdom.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_9": "Once the powerful relics of the Great {Snake} were abundant. Most got lost to the ravages of time and our enemies. What is {left} is all the more precious.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_10": "We are the guardians. We are all what is left from the glory of the past.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_11": "What you call Banuta was once a centre of our civilisation and culture. We gave those {apes} so much, but they wanted more. In the end, the Great {Snake} used them as a tool to teach our people a painful but necessary lesson.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_12": "In their vanity our descendants thought they could use those false-born as servants. They paid a terrible price. Their downfall might only be temporary though if we can {redeem} our race in the eyes of the snake god.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_13": "Dragons are one of the greatest creations of the Great {Snake}. Yet, they are still distanced from the Great {Snake} and susceptible for {corruption} and the lies of the egg stealers.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_14": "There are many forms of corruption in this world. All of it is the work of the egg stealers who spread their taint. The creation hatched by the Great {Snake} was perfect without even the option of corruption.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_15": "Creatures from beyond. Greedy and traitorous, they stole parts of the world and of life for themselves. They corrupted the world by their deceptions and stole our {birthright}.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_16": "We were overthrown by those of who we vainly thought we could use for our advantage, even though we knew about the foulness of the false-born.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_17": "Everything that lacks scales is no true litter of the Great Snake. They are the corrupted kin of the egg stealers.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_18": "Such concepts are of little consequence for the dead.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_19": "They are a manifestation of the snake god's power. They are its avatars in some way.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_20": "We are the true-born. We are the children of the snake. But as children we have yet much to learn. One day we might take our rightful place in creation, but only if we prove {worthy}.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_21": "They are the false-born. They hatched from foul eggs - poisoned by the egg stealers. They are numerous and like a plague for the world.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_22": "This was once the centre of power of our religion. From here we ruled Tiquanda in the name of the snake god.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.stdmod_23": "We were not aware of another civilisation that was left. Only recently the awareness of the Great Snake touched us in our slumber and we learnt through visions of its other children.",
  "npc.bruce.say_1": "Well, .. <gives a short and precise report>.",
  "npc.bruce.say_2": "You can {pass} either to the {Alchemist Quarter} or {Cemetery Quarter}. Which one will it be?",
  "npc.santa_claus.say_1": "You can't get other present.",
  "npc.santa_claus.say_2": "Merry Christmas!",
  "npc.ivalisse.say_1": "Well, I hope you like it here. We tried to rebuild in the {Shaper}'s will. I am a bit preoccupied at the moment because of the absence of my {father}. I may not be the best of help currently, sorry.",
  "npc.ivalisse.say_2": "Besides my various {duties} in the temple, I also take care of visitors. Well, I would but right now I can't get my mind of how my {father}'s doing. I am sorry.",
  "npc.ivalisse.say_3": "Well, I hope you like it here. We tried to rebuild in the Shaper's will. I am a bit preoccupied at the moment because of the absence of my father. I may not be the best of help currently, sorry.",
  "npc.ivalisse.say_4": "You would? That's great! Thank you! If you can find my father, tell him I understand and that I really miss him!",
  "npc.ivalisse.say_5": "Oh nevermind, I am sorry I asked you for this.",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_6": "My {father}, can you tell me if he's alright?",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_7": "Alright then, you are very welcome to explore the temple!",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_8": "My name is Ivalisse.",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_9": "There is always time to make a change.",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_10": "Besides my various {duties} in the temple, I also take care of visitors. Well, I would but right now I can't get my mind of how my {father}'s doing. I am sorry.",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_11": " I help linking the portals of this temple to other ancient sites of the {Astral Shapers}.",
  "npc.ivalisse.stdmod_12": " I help linking the portals of this temple to other ancient sites of the {Astral Shapers}.",
  "npc.dermot.say_1": "You have a present for me?? Realy?",
  "npc.dermot.say_2": "Do you want to buy the dungeon key for 2000 gold?",
  "npc.dermot.say_3": "Thank you very much!",
  "npc.dermot.say_4": "Here it is.",
  "npc.dermot.say_5": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_6": "I am the magistrate of this isle.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_7": "Thats me.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_8": "I am Dermot, the magistrate of this isle.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_9": "Time is not important on Fibula.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_10": "You are at Fibula. This isle is not very dangerous. Just the wolves bother outside the village.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_11": "Oh, my god. In the dungeon of Fibula are a lot of monsters. That's why we have sealed it with a solid door.",
  "npc.dermot.stdmod_12": "Oh, my god. In the dungeon of Fibula are a lot of monsters. That's why we have sealed it with a solid door.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_1": "Hmm. You could be of assistance, I presume. I need several body parts. I will reward you adequately. Interested?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_2": "Ah hello, young friend! Did you bring me two ghoul snacks as requested?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_3": "Ah, young friend, I found a solution! Find me two {demonic skeletal hands}. That should do it. Now run along! Ask me for {mission} when you're done.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_4": "Ah hello again! You look as if you could, er, lend me a hand or two? Yes?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_5": "Yes, yes, hello. Tell me if you lost something. If not, do you have that stimulated brain with you?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_6": "Hello, hello. Let's come to the point - did you find me some intestines?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_7": "Ah hello! Well done there, I felt the old powers settling down. Now, {ready} to hallow the next altar?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_8": "Yes? Do you have the {scroll} piece? ",
  "npc.omrabas.say_9": "Ah, hello! I take it you have the next scroll piece for me, {yes}?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_10": "Hello - what? You have the {scroll} piece, you say?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_11": "Hello, young apprentice. Do you have that {scroll} piece from the priestess?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_12": "Don't keep me waiting. The last scroll piece - were you able to {restore} it?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_13": "Splendid! What? They're half gnawed! There are no hands! Hrmmm. Let me think of a solution. Ask me for a new {mission}.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_14": "You don't have two ghoul snacks.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_15": "Yes. Those will be adequate. Talk to me again if you want to continue with your next {mission}.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_16": "You don't have two demonic skeletal hands.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_17": "Ah... <sighs> Very good. Just say the word when you are ready for the next {mission}.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_18": "You don't have my heart.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_19": "Ah... <sighs> Very good. Just say the word when you are ready for the next {mission}.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_20": "You don't have the brain.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_21": "You don't have my intestine.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_22": "This is it! This is it! Well done, well done! And now, on to the {next} scroll piece, {yes}?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_23": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_24": "Indeed it is! The second scroll piece! Splendid! Here you go - for your trouble. And now, on to the {next} scroll piece, {yes}? ",
  "npc.omrabas.say_25": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_26": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_27": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_28": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_29": "What? Hack some off from a demon skeleton, of course! Now get moving.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_30": "Ah... <sighs> Very good. Just say the word when you are ready for the next {mission}.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_31": "You don't have my heart.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_32": "What? No bones around you say? Hrmmm. Wait. Check the skull heap here - that's right - hah! There! Now get to work!",
  "npc.omrabas.say_33": "Yes? Do you have the {scroll} piece?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_34": "Ah, hello! I take it you have the next {scroll} piece for me, {yes}?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_35": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_36": "Hello, young apprentice. Do you have that {scroll} piece from the priestess?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_37": "Hello, young apprentice. Do you have that scroll piece from the priestess?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_38": "Welcome, welcome! Finally! The last {scroll} piece.... you do have it, haven't you?",
  "npc.omrabas.say_39": "You don't have my scroll.",
  "npc.omrabas.say_40": "Chzzzz. wtf??@! leave.",
  "npc.the_librarian.say_1": "You don't need any instructions about the ring right now.",
  "npc.ongulf.say_1": "Excellent. Although we have no idea what awaits us in this foreign land, it is always good to know something more about our surroundings.",
  "npc.ongulf.say_2": "That's good news for sure. It will give our operation a new impulse. However, only if there is not some unexpected trouble ahead. Well, we'll talk about that when we discuss your next {mission}.",
  "npc.ongulf.say_3": "Shortly after you killed that creature, the others crumbled to dust and stone. I hope this incident does not foreshadow similar problems in our mines. However, for now I have other things to take care of and you have other {missions} to accomplish. ",
  "npc.ongulf.say_4": "You did an excellent job! With all this help Farmine will grow and prosper. While we put all available resources into building this base, I have another urgent {mission} for you.",
  "npc.ongulf.say_5": "Oh my. What a mess you have gotten yourself into. Well, at least you made it out alive. Whatever the value of a minotaur's promise might be, I guess that is the best we can get. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.say_6": "Oh my. What a mess you have gotten yourself into. Well, at least you made it out alive. Whatever the value of a minotaur's promise might be, I guess that is the best we can get. ...",
  "npc.lazaran.say_1": "Me people wanting {peace}. No war with others. No war with {little men}. We few. We weak. Need {help}. We not wanting make {war}. No hurt.",
  "npc.lazaran.say_2": "Oh! You found holy skull? In bone pile you found?! Thank Pandor you brought! Me can have it back?",
  "npc.lazaran.say_3": "You say you was to where sun is hot and burning? And where trees grow as high as mountain? And where Fasuon cries white tears? Me can't wait to see!! Can have holy skull back?",
  "npc.lazaran.say_4": "We been weak for too long! We prepare for great hunt. But still need many doings! You can help us?",
  "npc.lazaran.say_5": "You bring us big pot of strange water from little men?",
  "npc.lazaran.say_6": "Me people wanting peace. No war with others. No war with little men.",
  "npc.lazaran.say_7": "You mean you want help us?",
  "npc.lazaran.say_8": "You hero of our tribe if bring back holy skull!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_9": "Me thank you much! All wisdom safe again now.",
  "npc.lazaran.say_10": "You do not have it!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_11": "Here take holy skull. You bring where you think is good. See as much as possible! See where other people live!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_12": "We make big ritual soon and learn much about world outside. Me thank you many times for teaching us world. Very wise and adventurous you are!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_13": "The skull have not seen all yet!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_14": "We need to calm and make happy gods. Best go to Ulala. She is priest of us and can tell what needs doing.",
  "npc.lazaran.say_15": "We make big ritual soon and learn much about world outside. Me thank you many times for teaching us world. Very wise and adventurous you are!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_16": "You do not have the brown strange water!",
  "npc.lazaran.say_17": "Me have many small task, but also big {mission}. You say what want.",
  "npc.lazaran.say_18": "Many mighty monster rule land. We fight. We lose. We flee to mountain to hide.",
  "npc.lazaran.say_19": "We come and see little men. They like us, only very little. They having good weapon and armor, like the greens.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_1": "Eleonore ... Yes, I remember her... vaguely. She is a pretty girl ... but still only a girl and now I am in love with a beautiful and passionate woman. A true {mermaid} even.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_2": "Don't ask about silly missions. All I can think about is this lovely {mermaid}.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_3": "Ask around in the settlement where you can help out. If you have proven your worth I might have some missions for you.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_4": "I think that means 'mission accomplished'. Hehe. I guess that will put an end to their efforts to buy any alchemical substance from Edron.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_5": "You did it! Excellent!",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_6": "My pillow?? They know me all too well... <sigh> I've owned it since my childhood. However. Here, take it and convincehim that I am dead.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_7": "The mermaid is the most beautiful creature I have ever met. She is so wonderful. It was some kind of magic as we first met. A look in her eyes and I suddenly knew there would be never again another woman in my life but her.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_8": "I am deeply ashamed that I lacked the willpower to resist her spell. Thank you for your help in that matter. Now my head is once more free to think about our {mission}.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_9": "Ah, right! The pirate outfit! Here you go, now you are truly one of us.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_10": "Ahh, thank you, my friend! What would we do without you? Here, take this reward for your efforts. If you want to continue to help us killing pirates, just ask me about that {task}.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_11": "Go kill more pirates.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_12": "Do you, by chance, would like to kill pirates again for us?",
  "npc.raymond_striker.say_13": "Perfect. I know it sounds like a lot, but really, take your time. You won't do it for nothing, I promise.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_1": "Some annoying nightmarish creatures rove about in the tunnels underneath this island. They are threatening the members of my court and devastate the flora and fauna. They also threaten the natural balance. Would you go and fight them for me?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_2": "Have you defeated the nightmare monsters?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_3": "Have you found the moon mirror and freed the captured fairies?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_4": "Have you already found the starlight vial and the sun catcher?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_5": "Could you already gather the three lights?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_6": "Have you repaired the magical barrier? Is Feyrist safe?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_7": "Thank you again, mortal being! The fae will be forever grateful.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_8": "I knew you would be willing to help us. Kill two hundred of them as well as the terrible demon Kroazur who's leading them. That should bring some relief for the fae.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_9": "Thank you! You rendered a great favour to the fae courts and Feyrist alike. Would you help us with another problem?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_10": "You rendered a great favour to the fae courts and Feyrist alike. Would you help us with another problem?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_11": "You have to kill two hundred of nightmare creatures and the terrible demon Kroazur who's leading them. That should bring some relief for the fae.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_12": "Thank you, mortal being! Please keep the mirror. I think you may need it soon, because there is another problem. Would you help us again?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_13": "Please keep the mirror. I think you may need it soon, because there is another problem. Would you help us again?",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_14": "Please seek out the tainted fae, retrieve the artefact and free the captured fairies.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_15": "You have to catch the respective lights and store it in the corresponding vessel.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_16": "Thank you, mortal being! The fae will be forever grateful. Take this blossom bag as a little thank-you gift. Such blossoms grow on our trees just once in a decade, so they are quite rare.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_17": "If you charge all fifteen arcane sources with the respective light, Feyrist's protection will be ensured again.",
  "npc.maelyrra.say_18": "Then not.",
  "npc.zalamon.say_1": "What newzz do you bring? Did you find any cluezz about zzeir whereaboutzz? ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_2": "Ah you have returned. I azzume you already found zzome itemzz to build a proper dizzguizze? ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_3": "Zzo... you finished him. Show me hizz head, will you? ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_4": "You - azzembled zze zzeptre? Hand it out, give it to me, will you? ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_5": "Ah I zzee. You are ready for your mizzion and waiting for me to create and mark zze crate? ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_6": "Zze emperor of zze dragonzz hazz tranzzformed himzzelf into an undead creature to lazzt for all eternity, to cheat deazz. Hizz corruption flowzz to zzozze he bound, and from zzem to zzozze zzey bound, and from zzem into zze land.",
  "npc.zalamon.say_7": "Be warned. Zze mountain pazzezz have been dezzerted for zzeveral weekzz now. No one made it acrozz and I fear you won't meet a zzingle friendly zzoul up zzere.",
  "npc.zalamon.say_8": "Exzztraordinary. We are mozzt fortunate to have zzezze documentzz in our handzz now. Zzizz would zzertainly help me to build an effective rezzizztanzze. Will you give zzem to me? ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_9": "I've marked itzz location on your map. Go and find out what happened zzere. In zze pazzt it wazz known azz zze Temple of Equilibrium. ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_10": "Zzizz izz not hizz head but clearly belonged to zze keeper. I - I am imprezzed. You can go now. Leave me alone for a zzecond. ",
  "npc.zalamon.say_11": "Finally. At lazzt. Zze zzeptre izz - ourzz. Ourzz of courzze. A weapon we should uzze wizzely for our cauzze. I need a zzecond or two. Do you leave me already? ",
  "npc.asima.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.asima.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.asima.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.asima.say_4": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.asima.say_5": "Ok then.",
  "npc.asima.say_6": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.chrystal.say_1": "If its necessary ... <tells you her measurements>",
  "npc.lokur.say_1": "Your weekly ticket is still valid. Would be a waste of money to purchase a second one",
  "npc.lokur.say_2": "Do you want to purchase a weekly ticket for the ore wagons? With it you can travel freely and swiftly through Kazordoon for one week. 250 gold only. Deal?",
  "npc.lokur.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.lokur.say_4": "Here is your stamp. It can't be transferred to another person and will last one week from now. You'll get notified upon using an ore wagon when it isn't valid anymore.",
  "npc.lokur.say_5": "No then.",
  "npc.lokur.say_6": "Come on, I have no clue what they are. Better ask my armorer Kroox for such nonsense.Go and ask him for good ol' Lokurs measurements, he'll know.",
  "npc.gnomad.say_1": "I'm the gnomish tactical advisor for this area!",
  "npc.gnomad.say_2": "Ah you are amazed by our crystals, aren't you? Well, you have only seen a tiny fraction of what they are able to do.",
  "npc.gnomad.say_3": "In the last century mushrooms have become more and more important for producing raw materials and tools and less important for sustenance.",
  "npc.gnomad.say_4": "We gnomes are masters of growing and working crystals and we also mastered the raising of a variety of mushrooms for different purposes.",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.say_2": "You would be surprised how many things are washed ashore here. I trade ",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.stdmod_3": "I can help you buy trading stuff with you. Good for me, good for you. It's a win-win!",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.stdmod_4": "Have you noticed that I'm actually the only rock on this island with a proper job? Those lazy pebbleheads! I'm proud to announce: I'm a trader",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.stdmod_5": "I can help you buy trading stuff with you. Good for me, good for you. It's a win-win!",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.stdmod_6": "Have you noticed that I'm actually the only rock on this island with a proper job? Those lazy pebbleheads! I'm proud to announce: I'm a trader",
  "npc.guide_tiko.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_tiko.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_5": "The temple is in the north-eastern part of town, left of the depot. The priest there has a little alcohol problem, though. It's sad.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_6": "Our bank can be found one floor above the depot. Just talk to Ferks.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_7": "The shops here are very close to one another. I can mark them for you if you'd like.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_9": "I'll help you not to get lost in Port Hope. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_10": "The inhabitants of Port Hope are bravely facing the constant threat from the jungle. The town is built on pile dwellings and most shops are close to each other.",
  "npc.guide_tiko.stdmod_11": "I'm Tiko and your guide today. Have a good day!",
  "npc.aldo.say_1": "Do you want to repair your worn soft boots for 10000 gold coins?",
  "npc.aldo.say_2": "Sorry, you don't have the item.",
  "npc.aldo.say_3": "Sorry, you don't have enough gold.",
  "npc.aldo.say_4": "Here you are.",
  "npc.aldo.say_5": "Ok then.",
  "npc.guide_luke.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_luke.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_luke.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_4": "I can tell you all about the {town}, its {temple}, the {bank}, {shops}, {spell trainers} and the {depot}, as well as about the {world status}.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_5": "The temple is in the centre of Thais. Walk east from the harbour and pass by the {depot} until you reach the infamous crossroads, then turn south.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_6": "We have two bankers, Suzy and Naji. Naji is right in the depot. For Suzi, exit the {depot} to the west and walk south-west. Don't forget that I can {mark} important locations on your map.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_7": "You can buy {weapons}, {armor}, {tools}, {gems}, {magical} equipment, {furniture} and {food} here.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I {escort} newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_9": "I'm a guide, overworked and underpaid. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_10": "Thais is the oldest settlement in Tibia. You can hear its history whisper when walking through the streets. Beware of criminals, but else it's a fine city.",
  "npc.guide_luke.stdmod_11": "I'm Luke. No jokes, please, I heard them all!",
  "npc.perod.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.perod.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.perod.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_1": "Well, there is little where we need help beyond the normal tasks you can do for the city. However, there is one thing out of the ordinary where some {assistance} would be appreciated.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_2": "You already asked for a mission, go to the next.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_3": "It's nothing really important, so no one has yet found the time to look it up. It concerns the town's beggars that have started to behave {strange} lately.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_4": "They usually know better than to show up in the streets and harass our citizens, but lately they've grown more bold or desperate or whatever. I ask you to investigate what they are up to. If necessary, you may scare them away a bit.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_5": "Nice work, take your outfit.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_6": "You already have the outfit.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_7": "Receive the second addon.",
  "npc.ezebeth.say_8": "Receive the first addon.",
  "npc.miles_the_guard.say_1": "I'm fine. There's no trouble at all.",
  "npc.miles_the_guard.say_2": "Well, of course. We live in safety and peace.",
  "npc.miles_the_guard.say_3": "I think the gods are looking after us and their hands shield us from evil.",
  "npc.miles_the_guard.say_4": "I think the gods and the government do their best to keep away harm from the citizens.",
  "npc.miles_the_guard.stdmod_5": "It's my duty to protect the city.",
  "npc.karith.say_1": "The swamp spice will turn out very lucrative considering that it helps to make even the most disgusting dish taste good. Do you want a passage to Venore for 185 gold?",
  "npc.karith.say_2": "What's that? Bug milk? Hm, perhaps I can find some customers for that! ",
  "npc.karith.say_3": "Sand wasp honey? Hm, interesting at least!",
  "npc.karith.say_4": "Some special spice might be of value indeed.",
  "npc.karith.say_5": "I can hardly imagine that someone is interested in embalming fluid, but I'll give it a try.",
  "npc.karith.say_6": "Of course! Ivory! Its value is quite obvious.",
  "npc.karith.say_7": "This royal satin is indeed of acceptable quality.",
  "npc.karith.say_8": "I doubt that the esteemed Yalahari will indulge into something profane as rum. But who knows, I'll give it a try.",
  "npc.karith.say_9": "I doubt that these flowers will stay fresh and healthy forever. But if they do, they could be indeed valuable.",
  "npc.karith.say_10": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_11": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_12": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_13": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_14": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_15": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_16": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_17": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_18": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_19": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_20": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_21": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_22": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_23": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_24": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.karith.say_25": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.karith.say_26": "Don't waste my time.",
  "npc.karith.say_27": "Then no.",
  "npc.karith.stdmod_28": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.karith.stdmod_29": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.karith.stdmod_30": "I'm Karith. I don't belong to a caste any longer, and only serve the Yalahari.",
  "npc.karith.stdmod_31": "The city was a marvel to behold. It is certain that it have been the many foreigners that ruined it.",
  "npc.sholley.say_1": "Already clicked the body on the house Roswitha ?",
  "npc.oressa.say_1": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.oressa.say_2": "You do not need any healing right now.",
  "npc.oressa.say_3": "You do not need any healing right now.",
  "npc.oressa.say_4": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.oressa.say_5": "Tell me: Do you prefer to fight with {bow} and {spear}, or do you want to cast {magic}?",
  "npc.oressa.say_6": "So tell me, which {vocation} do you want to choose: {knight}, {sorcerer}, {paladin} or {druid}?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_1": "Are you saying that Gamel is a member of the rebellion?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_2": "Do you know what his plans are about?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_3": "Thank you! Take this ring. If you ever need a healing, come, bring the scroll, and ask me to {heal}.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_4": "Sorry, but you have none.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_5": "So be healed!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_6": "Sorry, you are not worthy!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_7": "Then I welcome you to the TBI. This is a great moment for you, remember it well. Talk to me about your missions whenever you feel ready.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_8": "I think they understood the warning the way it was meant. If not, you will have to visit Venore soon again. But for now it's settled.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_9": "I can only hope that this information are as valuable as we expected it. A good man died for them.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_10": "Please bring me some proof of his whereabouts.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_11": "I can only hope that this information are as valuable as we expected it. A good man died for them.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_12": "Please bring me some valuable information!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_13": "Ah yes, very interesting. Almost as I suspected. It's a good thing that we got those documents in our hands.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_14": "We need those intelligence reports, do whatever you need to do agent!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_15": "Now that Venore is of nearly no importance anymore, there is only Carlin left to deal with.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_16": "I already heard that our little trick worked quite well. Several officials of Carlin are already on their way to repair the damage done to their diplomatic efforts. It will not only cost them much money but also quite some time.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_17": "Here you are. Better don't loose it again.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_18": "You don't have enough money",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_19": "You have done superb work agent, I grant you the title of Top Agent! Here's a little gift you might find useful.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_20": "Please bring me proof of the mad technomancers defeat!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_21": "Then don't bother me with it. I'm a busy man.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_22": "Traitor!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_23": "As you wish.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_24": "That's terrible! Will you give me the crystal?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_25": "Tell me precisely what he asked you to do! It's important!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_26": "Do you need the healing now?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_27": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_28": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_29": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_30": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_31": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_32": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_33": "Have you fulfilled your current mission?",
  "npc.chester_kahs.say_34": "If you lost or wasted your disguise kit I can replace it. It will cost you 1000 gold though since you lost royal property. Is that ok for you?",
  "npc.ghorza.say_1": "Of course, just browse through my wares. You can also look at ",
  "npc.mortimer.say_1": "Do you want to join the explorer society?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_2": "Oh yes, an interesting topic. We had vivid discussions about this discovery. But what is it that you want?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_3": "The missions available for your rank are the {butterfly hunt}, {plant collection} and {ice delivery}.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_4": "The missions available for your rank are {lizard urn}, {bonelord secrets} and {orc powder}.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_5": "The missions available for your rank are {elven poetry}, {memory stone} and {rune writings}.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_6": "The explorer society needs a great deal of help in the research of astral travel. Are you willing to help?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_7": "Do you have some collected ectoplasm with you?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_8": "Did you bring the dress?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_9": "Oh, yes! Tell our fellow explorer that the papers are in the mail already.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_10": "The reports from Port Hope have already arrived here and our progress is astonishing. We think it is possible to create an astral bridge between our bases. Are you interested to assist us with this?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_11": "Did you get the requested pickaxe from Uzgod in Kazordoon?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_12": "Did you get the ice we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_13": "The mission asks you to collect some species of butterflies, are you interested?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_14": "Did you acquire the purple butterfly we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_15": "Did you acquire the blue butterfly we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_16": "Did you acquire the red butterfly we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_17": "In this mission we require you to get us some plant samples from Tiquandan plants. Would you like to fulfil this mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_18": "Did you acquire the sample of the jungle bells plant we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_19": "Use this botanist's container on a witches cauldron to collect a sample for us. Bring it here and report about your plant collection.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_20": "Did you acquire the sample of the witches cauldron we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_21": "Use this botanist's container on a giant jungle rose to obtain a sample for us. Bring it here and report about your plant collection.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_22": "Did you acquire the sample of the giant jungle rose we are looking for?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_23": "The explorer society would like to acquire an ancient urn which is some sort of relic to the lizard people of Tiquanda. Would you like to accept this mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_24": "Did you manage to get the ancient urn?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_25": "Have you found any proof that the pyramid was built by bonelords?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_26": "Did you acquire some of the orcish powder?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_27": "Did you acquire a copy of 'Songs of the Forest' for us?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_28": "Were you able to acquire a memory stone for our society?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_29": "Did you create a copy of the ancient runes as requested?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_30": "We will see if you can handle this simple task. Get the pickaxe from Uzgod in Kazordoon and bring it to one of our bases. Report there about the pickaxe.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_31": "Just in time. Sadly not much ice is left over but it will do. Thank you again.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_32": "*Sigh* I think the time is right to grant you another chance to get that ice. Hurry up this time.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_33": "A little bit battered but it will do. Thank you! If you think you are ready, ask for another butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_34": "A little bit battered but it will do. Thank you! If you think you are ready, ask for another butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_35": "That is an extraordinary species you have brought. Thank you! That was the last butterfly we needed.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_36": "Fine! Here take this botanist's container. Use it on a jungle bells plant to collect a sample for us. Report about your plant collection when you have been successful.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_37": "I see. It seems you've got some quite useful sample by sheer luck. Thank you! Just tell me when you are ready to continue with the plant collection.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_38": "Ah, finally. I started to wonder what took you so long. But thank you! Another fine sample, indeed. Just tell me when you are ready to continue with the plant collection.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_39": "What a lovely sample! With that you have finished your plant collection missions.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_40": "Yes, that is the prized relic we have been looking for so long. You did a great job, thank you.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_41": "You did it! Excellent! The scientific world will be shaken by this discovery!",
  "npc.mortimer.say_42": "You really got it? Amazing! Thank you for your efforts.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_43": "Excellent. This mission is easy but nonetheless vital. Travel to Ab'Dendriel and get the book.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_44": "Let me have a look! Yes, that's what we wanted. A copy of 'Songs of the Forest'. I won't ask any questions about those bloodstains.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_45": "In the ruins of north-western Edron you should be able to find a memory stone. Good luck.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_46": "A flawless memory stone! Incredible! It will take years even to figure out how it works but what an opportunity for science, thank you!",
  "npc.mortimer.say_47": "Excellent! Here, take this tracing paper and use it on the object you will find there to create a copy of the ancient runes.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_48": "It's a bit wrinkled but it will do. Thanks again.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_49": "Good! Take this container and use it on a ghost that was recently slain. Return with the collected ectoplasm and hand me that container ...",
  "npc.mortimer.say_50": "Don't lose the container. They are expensive!",
  "npc.mortimer.say_51": "Phew, I had no idea that ectoplasm would smell that ... oh, it's you, well, sorry. Thank you for the ectoplasm.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_52": "Good! Ask me for another mission.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_53": "Poor Ratha. Thank you for returning this skull to the society. We will see to a honourable burial of Ratha.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_54": "Come back when you find any information.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_55": "Marvellous! You brought a giant smith hammer for the explorer society!",
  "npc.mortimer.say_56": "No you don't.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_57": "It's always a sad day when we learn about the death of a member. But at least we learnt about his fate. Thank you, here is your reward.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_58": "Did it melt away?",
  "npc.mortimer.say_59": "Come back when you find any information.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_60": "Come back when you find one.",
  "npc.mortimer.say_61": "The explorer society is looking for a genuine giant smith hammer for our collection. It is rumoured the cyclopses of the Plains of Havoc might be using one. Did you by chance obtain such a hammer?",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_1": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_2": "Come back when you have finished your job.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_3": "I'l say I'm blown away but a Klom Stonecutter is not that easily impressed. Still, your got your hands dirt for us and I appreciate that.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_4": "Alright, good. Those things are strolling about and I ain't gonna have that. If it moves more than two legs, destroy it. If it moves legs and tentacles, destroy it again.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_5": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_6": "Come back when you have finished your job.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_7": "So you did it. Well, that won't be the last of 'em but this sure helps our situation down here. Return to me later if you want to help me again!",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_8": "So you did it. And you even made prisoners, the bonus is yours! Well, that won't be the last of 'em but this sure helps our situation down here. Return to me later if you want to help me again!",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_9": "Very well, now try to find some of their makeshift homes and tear'em down. There's bound to be some stragglers you can 'persuade' to surrender, eliminate any resistance. Get back here when you're done.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_10": "If you bring me any suspicious devices on creatures you slay down here, I'll make it worth your while by telling the others of your generosity. How many do you want to offer?",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_11": "Don't waste my time.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_12": "Done.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_13": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_14": "Done.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_15": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_16": "Done.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_17": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_18": "So you want to know what we all think about your deeds? What leader's opinion are you interested in, the {gnomes} (Gnomus), the {dwarves} (Klom Stonecutter) or the {scouts} (Lardoc Bashsmite)?",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_19": "So you want to know what we all think about your deeds? What leader's opinion are you interested in, the {gnomes} (Gnomus), the {dwarves} (Klom Stonecutter) or the {scouts} (Lardoc Bashsmite)?",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_20": "The gnomes are still in need of your help, member of Bigfoot's Brigade. Prove your worth by answering their calls! (",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_21": "The dwarves are still in need of your help, member of Bigfoot's Brigade. Prove your worth by answering their calls! (",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.say_22": "The scouts are still in need of your help, member of Bigfoot's Brigade. Prove your worth by answering their calls! (",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.stdmod_23": "Well, the biggest problem we need to address are the ever charging {subterraneans} around here. And on top of that, there's the threat of the Lost, who quite made themselves at {home} in these parts.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.stdmod_24": "Maintainin' this whole operation, the dwarven involvement 'course. Don't know about them gnomes but if I ain't gettin' those dwarves in line, there'll be chaos down here. I also oversee the {defences} and {counterattacks}.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.stdmod_25": "Klom Stonecutter's the name. ",
  "npc.iwar.say_1": "Nice. You like your picture, haa? Give me 10,000 gold and I will deliver it to the museum. Do you {pay}?",
  "npc.iwar.say_2": "Well done. The picture will be delivered to the museum as last as possible.",
  "npc.iwar.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.maryza.say_1": "Welcome to the Jolly Axeman, |PLAYERNAME|. Have a good time and eat some food!",
  "npc.maryza.say_2": "The cookbook of the famous dwarven kitchen. You're lucky. I have a few copies on sale. Do you like one for 150 gold?",
  "npc.maryza.say_3": "I'm sorry but I sell only one copy to each customer. Otherwise they would have been sold out a long time ago.",
  "npc.maryza.say_4": "No gold, no sale, that's it.",
  "npc.maryza.say_5": "Here you are. Happy cooking!",
  "npc.maryza.say_6": "I have but a few copies, anyway.",
  "npc.miraia.say_1": "Hehe, would you like to wear a pretty veil like I do? Well... I could help you, but you would have to complete a task first.",
  "npc.miraia.say_2": "You mean, you would like to prove that you deserve to wear such a veil?",
  "npc.miraia.say_3": "Let me cover my nose before I get this for you... Would you REALLY like to buy scarab cheese for 100 gold?",
  "npc.miraia.say_4": "Oh the last cheese molded? Would you like to buy another one for 100 gold?",
  "npc.miraia.say_5": "Excellent! Come back to me once you have collected 100 pieces of ape fur.",
  "npc.miraia.say_6": "That is a shameless lie.",
  "npc.miraia.say_7": "Here it is.",
  "npc.miraia.say_8": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.miraia.say_9": "What a pity.",
  "npc.miraia.stdmod_10": "I can offer you lemonade, camel milk, and water. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.miraia.stdmod_11": "Are you looking for food? I have bread, cheese, ham, and meat. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_1": "You can try to create {sword}s, {axe}s, {club}s, {bow}s, {crossbow}s and {spellbook}s.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_2": "The raw object is nothing but a pale of shadow of its potential. As unsafe and unpredictable the imporvement is, it might boot the powers of your item immensely. You can try to improve {sword}s, {axe}s, {club}s, {bow}s, {crossbow}s and {spellbook}s.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_3": "From time to time fate smiles upon those who take great risks and have strong dreams! If you have the {ingredients}, we can try to give the ultimate refinement to {sword}s, {axe}s, {club}s, {bow}s, {crossbow}s and {spellbook}s.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_4": "Do you want to create a crude umbral {blade} or crude umbral {slayer}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_5": "Do you want to improve a crude umbral {blade} or crude umbral {slayer}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_6": "Do you want to transform an umbral {blade} or umbral {slayer}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_7": "Do you want to create a crude umbral {axe} or crude umbral {chopper}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_8": "Do you want to improve a crude umbral {axe} or crude umbral {chopper}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_9": "Do you want to transform an umbral {axe} or umbral {chopper}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_10": "Do you want to spend your dream matter with those 25 clusters of {solace} and give a shot. {Yes} or {no}",
  "npc.eruaran.say_11": "Do you want to create a crude umbral {mace} or crude umbral {hammer}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_12": "Do you want to improve a crude umbral {mace} or crude umbral {hammer}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_13": "Do you want to transform an umbral {mace} or umbral {hammer}?",
  "npc.eruaran.say_14": "Something weird happened! You should contact a gamemaster.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_15": "Oh no! The process failed.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_16": "Sorry, you don't have the required ingredients.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_17": "Oh no! The process failed.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_18": "Something weird happened! You should contact a gamemaster.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_19": "Oh no! The process failed.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_20": "Something weird happened! You should contact a gamemaster.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_21": "Do you want to spend your umbral ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_22": "Do you want to spend your dream matter with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_23": "Do you want to spend your crude umbral bow with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_24": "Do you want to spend your umbral bow with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_25": "Do you want to spend your dream matter with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_26": "Do you want to spend your crude umbral crossbow with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_27": "Do you want to spend your umbral crossbow with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_28": "Do you want to spend your dream matter with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_29": "Do you want to spend your crude umbral spellbook with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_30": "Do you want to spend your umbral spellbook with ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_31": "Your dreams are strong, the creation was successful. Take your ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_32": "Something weird happened! You should contact a gamemaster.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_33": "Oh no! The process failed.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_34": "Sorry, you don't have the required ingredients.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_35": "Your dreams are strong, the improvement was successful. Take your ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_36": "Oh no! The process failed.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_37": "You do not have ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_38": "Something weird happened! You should contact a gamemaster.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_39": "Your dreams are strong, the transforming was successful. Take your ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_40": "Oh no! The process failed.",
  "npc.eruaran.say_41": "You do not have ",
  "npc.eruaran.say_42": "Something weird happened! You should contact a gamemaster.",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_43": "What addon you are looking? I need for first addon: {dream warden mask} and for second {dream warden claw}.",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_44": "To achieve the first dream addon you need to give me 1 dream warden mask. Do you have them with you?",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_45": "Alright then. Come back when you got all neccessary items.",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_46": "To achieve the second dream addon you need to give me 1 dream warden claw. Do you have them with you?",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_47": "Alright then. Come back when you got all neccessary items.",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.say_1": "Then not.",
  "npc.guide_davina.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_davina.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_davina.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_5": "The temple is just north west of the depot. You can't miss it.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_6": "Jefrey, our bank clerk, can be found inside the depot. Easy to find.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, furniture and food here.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_9": "Well, I'm a guide. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town. I do this for free, but I'm always happy about a small donation if you can spare some money.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_10": "This city has three main districts - a noble district, a merchant district and the slums. The class difference is clearly visible here. Most shops are in the merchant district. There are also large sugarcane plantations.",
  "npc.guide_davina.stdmod_11": "I'm Davina. Glad to help you today.",
  "npc.zora.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.zora.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.zora.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.zora.stdmod_4": "I sell equipment for your adventure! Just ask me for a {trade} to see my wares.",
  "npc.mr._west.say_1": "Indeed, I can see the benefits of a mutual agreement. I will later read the details and send a letter to your superior. ",
  "npc.mr._west.say_2": "Yes, for the sake of my life I'll accept those terms. I know when I have lost. Tell your master I will comply with his orders. ",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.stdmod_1": "'Alice the chalice'... Hmpf, of course I won't TELL you my name, I am UNDERCOVER! Now be quiet or they will hear you.",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.stdmod_2": "Well, I am drinking most of the time. Er, no I mean - trying to hold my fluids... ah, wait that came out wrong: I am doing research. Let's just keep it at that.",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.say_3": "Finally. That's what I... oh wait, you're still talking to me - you will blow my cover! What do you want? Oh wait, did my {daughter} send you? It has been some time now, indeed.",
  "npc.serafin.say_1": "Oh, no I don't sell cookies. Or, do you mean you'd like to give me one?",
  "npc.serafin.say_2": "It'd be better for you to leave now.",
  "npc.serafin.say_3": "COUGH?! What kind of a mean trick is that? Get out of my shop!",
  "npc.serafin.stdmod_4": "There's something about these words which makes me feel awkward. Or maybe it's you who causes that feeling. You better get lost.",
  "npc.kulag_the_guard.say_1": "You adventurers become more and more of a pest.",
  "npc.kulag_the_guard.say_2": "They should throw you all into jail instead of giving you all those quests and rewards an honest watchman can only dream about.",
  "npc.kulag_the_guard.stdmod_3": "It's my duty to protect the city.",
  "npc.jerom.say_1": "Thank you sooo much <sniffs>. Well, you know I lost everything, but recently I found this strange rope here. I don't need it, here take it!",
  "npc.jerom.say_2": "Great! Finally, some light at the end of the tunnel! Come back and ask me for the quest when you solved this mystery!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_3": "The only animal to catch there is the cobra and most people don't like to keep one as a pet.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_4": "Who wants such an animal as a pet?!?!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_5": "Those amazons denied making business with me. You know the reason?!? I tell you, the reason was that I am MALE! Ridiculous!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_6": "For sure, I would have offered cats!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_7": "He gave me the permission to open up a pet shop here. I paid him almost everything I got!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_8": "I made contact with Svargrond! A guy named Buddel wanted to sell me a three-headed dog. I haven't seen it yet, but imagine how much money I could make by breeding such a pet!!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_9": "I like it here, at least the town. I was warned that there are nasty creatures outside the town walls but I didn't expect anything to happen so close to town!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_10": "I was always good with animals. My parents had a farm, the McRonalds farm. Maybe you know it. Anyway, I had the idea that people may like to have animals as companions and so one led to another.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_11": "I'd go mad listening to this 'ribbit' the whole time. But each to his own!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_12": "I'm new here in Edron. I wanted to open up a pet shop. But now I'm ruined, uahahahaha <sniffs>.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_13": "I need to write a letter to the king. I'm not sure if those 2 million gold coins that Daniel Steelsoul demanded from me weren't too much.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_14": "I'm there from time to time, catching frogs. People like their bright colours.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_15": "My name is Jerom but no need to remember my name. All my belongings are destroyed and stolen. I'll be gone soon!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_16": "Raymond Striker offered me a contract to export parrots from Meriana but I won't need them anymore now that I'm ruined.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_17": "Not a very good spot to catch animals. At least no animals that pass off as pets.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_18": "Yesterday I would have said that I like all creatures of Tibia but TODAY my life has changed! When I catch this stinking troll!!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_19": "True, why not keep a rat as a pet! They can eat your trash, live inside your walls and you don't have to worry if one dies ! Could be a huge success....if I weren't ruined!!!!",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_20": "That would be a mission for a hero.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_21": "Well, I don't see any other way than going back to my home country now.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_22": "Good idea! Easy to catch and once the owner has been bitten, he can't sue me anymore, hehehe!!.... but wait....I forgot....I'm ruined, uahahahaha <sniffs>.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_23": "I never make profit in Thais and most of the time I get robbed. I stopped visiting Thais for business some years ago.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_24": "I don't have anything to earn a living with, everything is destroyed! Otherwise I could offer you pets.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_25": "I saw a troll rummaging in the remains of my house last night! I'm sure this creature is behind that! But I am too weak to take revenge.",
  "npc.jerom.stdmod_26": "I've been to town and on my way back I heard a deafening sound. Then I saw that the sound came from a huge rock smashing my house.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_1": "My name is Tom the tanner.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_2": "I'm the local {tanner}. I buy fresh animal {corpses}, tan them, and convert them into fine leather clothes which I then sell to {merchants}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_3": "{Dixi} and {Lee'Delle} sell my leather clothes in their shops.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_4": "That's my job. It can be dirty at times but it provides enough income for my living.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_5": "Do I look like a tourist information centre? Go ask someone else.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_6": "Help? I will give you a few gold coins if you have some fresh dead {animals} for me. Note the word {fresh}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_7": "Fresh means: shortly after their death.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_8": "Much to do these days.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_9": "Good monsters to start with are rats. They live in the {sewers} under the village of {Rookgaard}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_10": "Dungeons can be dangerous without proper {equipment}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_11": "You need at least a {backpack}, a {rope}, a {shovel}, a {weapon}, an {armor} and a {shield}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_12": "Sorry, I haven't been outside for a while, so I don't know.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_13": "Troll leather stinks. Can't use it.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_14": "I don't buy orcs. Their skin is too scratchy.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_15": "Are you crazy?!",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_16": "Nope, sorry, don't sell that. Go see {Al Dee} or {Lee'Delle}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_17": "Nope, sorry, don't sell that. Ask {Dixi} or {Lee'Delle}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_18": "Nope, sorry, don't sell that. Ask {Obi} or {Lee'Delle}.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_19": "I'm buying fresh {corpses} of rats, rabbits and wolves. I don't buy half-decayed ones. If you have any for sale, {trade} with me.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_20": "He's an apple polisher.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_21": "Now that's an interesting woman.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_22": "He's a better cook than his cousin {Willie}, actually.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_23": "I kinda like him. At least he says what he thinks.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_24": "He sticks his nose too much in books.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_25": "My mother?? Did you meet my mother??",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_26": "I don't have a problem with him.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_27": "Typical pencil pusher.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_28": "It's in the academy, just above Seymour. Go there once you are level 8 to leave this place.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_29": "He is such a hypocrite.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_30": "I like her beer.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_31": "She buys my fine leather clothes.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_32": "I wonder what spectacular monsters he has found.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_33": "Her nose is a little high in the air, I think. She never shakes my hand.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_34": "I wonder if he's angry because his potion monopoly fell.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_35": "I'm not what you'd call a 'believer'.",
  "npc.tom.stdmod_36": "He's okay.",
  "npc.tom.say_37": "I had some cough syrup a while ago. It was stolen in an ape raid. I fear if you want more cough syrup you will have to buy it in the druids guild in carlin.",
  "npc.tom.say_38": "Would you like to wear bear paws like I do? No problem, just bring me 50 bear paws and 50 wolf paws and I'll fit them on.",
  "npc.tom.say_39": "Have you brought 50 bear paws and 50 wolf paws?",
  "npc.tom.say_40": "Excellent! Like promised, here are your bear paws. ",
  "npc.tom.say_41": "You don't have all items.",
  "npc.melfar.say_1": "Yes, I can hear them even from here. It has to be a legion of beavers! I'll send the men to get the wood as soon as their gnawing frenzy has settled! You can report to Ongulf that men and wood will be on their way!",
  "npc.melfar.say_2": "If you place the beaver bait on trees on some strategic locations, we could let the beavers do the work and later on, I'll send men to get the fallen trees.",
  "npc.melfar.say_3": "Here you go.",
  "npc.melfar.say_4": "You dont have enough of gold coins.",
  "npc.melfar.say_5": "You want to buy a Flask with Beaver Bait for 100 gold coins?",
  "npc.melfar.say_6": "Im out of stock.",
  "npc.jean_claude.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.mother_of_jack.say_1": "What about him? He's downstairs as he always has been. He never went away from home any further than into the forest nearby. He rarely ever took a walk to Edron, did he?",
  "npc.mother_of_jack.say_2": "Thought so. Of course he wouldn't do anything wrong. And he went where? Edron. Hm. I can see nothing wrong with that. But... he wasn't there often, was he?",
  "npc.mother_of_jack.say_3": "What...? But he wasn't up to something, was he?",
  "npc.warbert.say_1": "Take this!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_1": "These are dire times for our people. Problems plenty are in this times. But me people not grant trust easy. Are you willing to prove you friend of ape people?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_2": "Oh, you brought me whisper moss? Good hairless ape you are! Can me take it?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_3": "Please hurry. Bring me whisper moss from dworc lair. Make sure it is from dworc lair! Take it yourself only! If you need to hear background of all again, ask Hairycles for {background}.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_4": "You brought me that cough syrup from human healer me asked for?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_5": "Little ape should be healthy soon. Me so happy is. Thank you again! But me suspect we in more trouble than we thought. Will you help us again?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_6": "You got scroll from lizard village in south east?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_7": "Ah yes, you read the signs in tomb? Good! May me look into your mind to see what you saw?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_8": "You still don't know signs on stone, go and look for it in tomb east in desert.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_9": "You bring Hairycles egg of hydra?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_10": "You brought Hairycles witches' cap from Fibula?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_11": "You do please Hairycles again, friend. Me hope madness will not spread further now. Perhaps you are ready for other mission.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_12": "Please destroy three casks in the complex beneath Banuta, so my people will come to senses again.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_13": "You brought hair of holy ape?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_14": "Get a hair of holy ape from forbidden land in east. Speak with blind prophet in cave.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_15": "Me know its much me asked for but go into the deepest catacombs under Banuta and destroy the monument of the serpent god.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_16": "No more missions await you right now, friend. Perhaps you want to check me offers for special friends... or shamanic powers.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_17": "Oh you bring cookie for old Hairycles?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_18": "Me truly proud of you, friend. You learn many about plants, charms and ape people. Me want grant you shamanic power now. You ready?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_19": "You already are shaman and doctor. Me proud of you.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_20": "You not have finished journey for wisdom yet, young human.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_21": "You look for food and rest.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_22": "You look for food and rest.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_23": "To become friend of ape people a long and difficult way is. We do not trust easy but help is needed. Will you listen to story of Hairycles?",
  "npc.hairycles.say_24": "Hairycles sad is now. But perhaps you will change mind one day.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_25": "Hairycles thought better of you.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_26": "Stupid, you no have the moss me need. Go get it. It's somewhere in dworc lair. If you lost it, they might restocked it meanwhile. If you need to hear background of all again, ask Hairycles for {background}.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_27": "Ah yes! That's it. Thank you for bringing mighty whisper moss to Hairycles. It will help but still much is to be done. Just ask for other mission if you ready.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_28": "Strange being you are! Our people need help!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_29": "No no, not right syrup you have. Go get other, get right health syrup.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_30": "You so good! Brought syrup to me! Thank you, will prepare cure now. Just ask for {mission} if you want help again.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_31": "Please hurry, urgent it is!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_32": "Me sad. Me expected better from you!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_33": "Good thing that is! Report about your mission when have scroll.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_34": "Me sad. Me expected better from you!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_35": "That's bad news. If you lost it, only way to get other is to kill holy serpents. But you can't go there so you must ask adventurers who can.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_36": "No! That not scroll me looking for. Silly hairless ape you are. Go to village of lizards and get it there on your own!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_37": "You brought scroll with lizard text? Good! I will see what text tells me! Come back when ready for other mission.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_38": "That's bad news. If you lost it, only way to get other is to kill holy serpents. But you can't go there so you must ask adventurers who can.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_39": "Good thing that is! Report about mission when you have read those signs.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_40": "Me sad. Me expected better from you!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_41": "Oh, so clear is all now! Easy it will be to read the signs now! Soon we will know what to do! Thank you again! Ask for mission if you feel ready.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_42": "Me need to see it in your mind, other there is no way to proceed.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_43": "You brave hairless ape! Get me hydra egg. If you lose egg, you probably have to fight many, many hydras to get another.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_44": "Me sad. Me expected better from you!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_45": "You not have egg of hydra. Please get one!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_46": "Ah, the egg! Mighty warrior you be! Thank you. Hairycles will put it at safe place immediately.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_47": "Please hurry. Hairycles not knows when evil lizards strike again.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_48": "Long journey it will take, good luck to you.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_49": "Me sad. Me expected better from you!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_50": "Not right mushroom you have. Find me a witches' cap on Fibula!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_51": "Incredible, you brought a witches' cap! Now me can prepare mighty charm of life. Yet still other {missions} will await you, friend.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_52": "Please try to find me a witches' cap on Fibula.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_53": "Hairycles sure you will make it. Good luck, friend.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_54": "Me sad. Please reconsider.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_55": "Hairycles proud of you. Go and find holy hair. Good luck, friend.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_56": "Me sad. Please reconsider.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_57": "You no have hair. You lost it? Go and look again.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_58": "Incredible! You got a hair of holy Bong! This will raise the spirit of my people. You are truly a friend. But one last mission awaits you.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_59": "You no have hair. You lost it? Go and look again.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_60": "Hairycles sure you will make it. Just use hammer on all that looks like snake or lizard. Tell Hairycles if you succeed with mission.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_61": "Me sad. Please reconsider.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_62": "Friend of the ape people! Take my gift and become me apprentice! Here is shaman clothing for you!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_63": "Come back if change mind.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_64": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.hairycles.say_65": "Thank you, you are ... YOU SON OF LIZARD!",
  "npc.hairycles.say_66": "I see.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_67": "Me great {wizard}. Me great doctor of {ape people}. Me know many plants. Me old and me have seen many things.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_68": "We see many things and learning quick. Merlkin magic learn quick, quick. We just watch and learn. Sometimes we try and learn.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_69": "Things not good now. Need helper to do {mission} for me people.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_70": "We be {kongra}, {sibang} and {merlkin}. Strange hairless ape people live in city called Port Hope.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_71": "Kongra verry strong. Kongra verry angry verry fast. Take care when kongra comes. Better climb on highest tree.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_72": "Sibang verry fast and funny. Sibang good gather food. Sibang know {jungle} well.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_73": "Merlkin we are. Merlkin verry wise, merlkin learn many things quick. Teach other apes things a lot. Making {heal} and making {magic}.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_74": "We see many things and learning quick. Merlkin magic learn quick, quick. We just watch and learn. Sometimes we try and learn.",
  "npc.hairycles.stdmod_75": "Jungle is dangerous. Jungle also provides us food. Take care when in jungle and safe you be.",
  "npc.torkada.say_1": "You need at least level 250 to start our mission.",
  "npc.torkada.say_2": "You already have accepted this mission.",
  "npc.torkada.say_3": "This expedition is here on an important {mission} for the inquisition",
  "npc.torkada.say_4": "Are you willing, to bring the fury of the inquisition to that foul place and eradicate all evil you find? Speak, {yes} or {no}?",
  "npc.torkada.say_5": "Ok then not.",
  "npc.ubaid.say_1": "Shove off, little one! Humans are not welcome here, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.ubaid.say_2": "What? You know the word, |PLAYERNAME|? All right then - I won't kill you. At least, not now.  What brings you {here}?",
  "npc.ubaid.say_3": "Still alive, |PLAYERNAME|? What brings you {here}?",
  "npc.ubaid.say_4": "You already pledged loyalty to king Malor!",
  "npc.ubaid.say_5": "Of course. Then don't waste my time and shove off.",
  "npc.ubaid.say_6": "Who do you think you are? A Marid? Shove off you worm!",
  "npc.ubaid.say_7": "So you pledge loyalty to king Malor and you are willing to never ever set foot on Marid's territory, unless you want to kill them? Yes?",
  "npc.ubaid.say_8": "Of course. Then don't waste my time and shove off.",
  "npc.ubaid.say_9": "Of course. Then don't waste my time and shove off.",
  "npc.padreia.say_1": "Do you want to buy a bottle of cough syrup for 50 gold?",
  "npc.padreia.say_2": "You MUST find that slime pool immediately or life here in Carlin will not be the same anymore.",
  "npc.padreia.say_3": "You did it! Even if only few of the Carliners will ever know about that, you saved all of their lives. Here, take this as a reward. Farewell!",
  "npc.padreia.say_4": "Maybe the guards have something to do for you or know someone who could need some help.",
  "npc.padreia.say_5": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.padreia.say_6": "Thank you. Here it is.",
  "npc.padreia.say_7": "Then no.",
  "npc.padreia.say_8": "Then the downfall of Carlin is inescapable. Please think about it. You know where to find me.",
  "npc.padreia.say_9": "Don't ask. They were only an unimportant footnote of history.",
  "npc.padreia.say_10": "They thought they had to bring Crunor to the people, if the people had not found Crunor on their own. To achieve this, they founded the inn called Crunor's Cottage, south of Mt. Sternum.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_11": "I am the grand druid of Carlin. I am responsible for the guild, the fields, and our citizens' health.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_12": "Every druid is able to learn the numerous spells of our craft.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_13": "Sorry, I don't teach spells for your vocation.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_14": "I am Padreia, grand druid of our fine city.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_15": "Time is just a crystal pillar - the centre of creation and life.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_16": "We are druids, preservers of life. Our magic is about defence, healing, and nature.",
  "npc.padreia.stdmod_17": "Sorcerers are destructive. Their power lies in destruction and pain.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_1": "It has been a while since I roamed the world of the living in a mortal shell.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_2": "I had many names in my live. The one that would be the most recognizable is probably the name Goshnar. Even that was an assumed name that I took when I left my mundane past behind.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_3": "Everything in my life was just a tool to further my goals. The brotherhood of bones was just a tool for me. As was everyone or everything. In the path I had chosen nothing mattered but me and my ambitions.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_4": "Necromancy was a passion at first, another tool while I amassed power and a crutch when my ambitions surpassed that what it could accomplish.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_5": "My demise did not meet me unprepared. As a powerful necromancer I had fettered my soul in the living world and the realms beyond. I had prepared for my return and was confident in my power.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_6": "My soul wandered the plains of Zarganash, waiting for my wards to power up. Waiting for my soul to be slowly pulled back and manifest in the world of the living once again. What I had not taken into consideration was peace.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_7": "I recognized the extent of my folly and failure. I decided not to return to the world of the living.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_8": "The only way I can get rid of them is to disperse them, to 'kill' them so to say. But they are tainted parts of myself and even going near them might endanger my sanity and stability. So all I can do is to ask you to do this daunting task.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_9": "I'm aware I have no right to ask and I have little to offer as a payment, but I ask you nonetheless. Will you face my fettered vices and destroy them for me?",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_10": "Thank you for accepting this burden.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_11": "You haven't killed Malice yet. You haven't killed Hatred yet. You haven't killed Spite yet. You haven't killed Cruelty yet. You haven't killed Greed yet.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_12": "My daughter was as ambitious as me, yet she lacked my intellect and my raw talent. She still was great and talented yet I sadly let her feel my disdain. One of the many errors that my way of hubris made me do.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_13": " I'm not aware of the fate of my linage. Neither I'm able to relate to the mortal world in that way. Each of us is an individual, not bound by ties of blood or herritage.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_14": "His avatar might be destroyed for now and it'd grip on Zarganash considerably weakened. Yet he burrowed to deep into the essence of this realm to be annihilated this easy.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_15": "I despised my followers for their petty agendas and for their limited vision of my own goals and personality.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_16": "I have cleansed you from the taints that you carried with you. You are now free from the burden that you should not have to bear.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.say_17": "You are not tainted by the darkness of the world. You are pure and free from the burdens that others carry.",
  "npc.dorian.say_1": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_2": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_3": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_4": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_5": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_6": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_7": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_8": "Have you finished your mission?",
  "npc.dorian.say_9": "What a fine material. That will be worth a coin or two. So far, so good. Ask me for another mission if you're ready for it.",
  "npc.dorian.say_10": "What an ugly vase. But who am I to question the taste of our customers? Anyway, I might have another mission in store for you.",
  "npc.dorian.say_11": "Excellent, that serves this fool right. I fear in your next mission, you'll have to get your hands dirty. Just ask me to learn more about it.",
  "npc.dorian.say_12": "That goblet is hardly worth all this trouble but we had to insist on our payment. However, I assume you are eager for more missions, so just ask.",
  "npc.dorian.say_13": "This little goldfish will bring us a hefty ransom! Just ask me if you're ready for another mission.",
  "npc.dorian.say_14": "Hm. Well, we could use some fresh blood. Ahum. Do you want to join the thieves guild, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.dorian.say_15": "Yes, I sell lock picks. Ask me for a trade.",
  "npc.brodrosch.say_1": "Your weekly ticket is still valid. Would be a waste of money to purchase a second one",
  "npc.brodrosch.say_2": "Do you want to purchase a weekly ticket for the ore wagons? With it you can travel freely and swiftly through Kazordoon for one week. 250 gold only. Deal?",
  "npc.brodrosch.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.brodrosch.say_4": "Here is your stamp. It can't be transferred to another person and will last one week from now. You'll get notified upon using an ore wagon when it isn't valid anymore.",
  "npc.brodrosch.say_5": "No then.",
  "npc.brodrosch.stdmod_6": "Do you want me take you to {Cormaya}, {Farmine} or to {Gnomprona}?",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_1": "I'm the officer responsible for this area. I give out missions, accept mission reports and oversee our defences.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_2": "We are the only protectors of the world against the enemies below. With small stature comes great responsibilities, as they say.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_3": "Sorry, but no! Your expertise could be put to better use elsewhere. Here awaits you no challenge. You are desperately needed in the deeper levels of the Spike. Report there immediately. ",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_4": "I can offer you several missions: to recharge our ghost {pacifiers}, to {release} the spiritual anger, to {track} an evil presence and to {kill} some demon skeletons.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_5": "What mission do you want to report about: recharging the ghost {pacifiers}, the {release} of the spiritual anger, about {tracking} an evil presence and the {killing} of demon skeletons?",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_6": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_7": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_8": "Gnowful! Take the resonance charger and use it on seven of the pacifiers in the cave.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_9": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_10": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_11": "Gnowful! Take the spirit shovel use it on four graves in the cave system.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_12": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_13": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_14": "Gnowful! Take the tracking device in the caves and locate the residual spirit energy.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_15": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_16": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_17": "Gnowful! Just go out to the caves and kill at least seven demon skeletons.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_18": "That's not a valid mission name.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_19": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_20": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_21": "Gnometastic! Take this resonance charger and use it on seven of the pacifiers in the cave. If you lose the charger, you'll have to bring your own. Gnomux sells all the equipment that is required for our missions.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_22": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_23": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_24": "Your task would be to use a spirit shovel to release some spirit's anger from graves that can be found all around here. If you are interested, I can give you some more information about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_25": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_26": "Gnometastic! Take this spirit shovel and use it on four graves in the cave system. If you lose the shovel you'll have to bring your own. Gnomux sells all the equipment that is required for our missions.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_27": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_28": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_29": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_30": "Gnometastic! Use this tracking device in the caves and locate the residual spirit energy. If you lose the tracking device, you'll have to bring your own. Gnomux sells all the equipment that is required for our missions.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_31": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_32": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_33": "We need someone to reduce the steadily growing number of demon skeletons in the caves. If you are interested, I can give you some more information about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_34": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_35": "Gnometastic! Just go out and kill them. You should find more of them than you like.",
  "npc.gnomilly.say_36": "Ok then.",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat3.say_1": "Tell me if you liked it when you come back. What is your name?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat3.say_2": "Alright |PLAYERNAME|. Vocation?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat3.say_3": "That's right, you can get Form 145 from me. However, I need Form 411 first. Come back when you have it.",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat3.say_4": "Well done! You have form 411!! Here is Form 145. Have fun with it.",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_1": "Do you already have 15 units of blue pollen with you?",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_2": "Ah! Did you bring me the peppermoon bell pollen I asked for?",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_3": "Ah! Well done! Now we shall proceed with the seance, yes?",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_4": "Ah! Well done! These 15 doses will suffice for now. Here, take this vote for your effort.",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_5": "No no no, I need 15 doses of freshly harvested pollen! Please, harvest those 15 doses yourself, to make absolutely sure you have first-rate quality. I am afraid nothing less will do.",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_6": "Splendid. Let me make the final preparations... There. Are you ready, too?",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_7": "Yes, take care, the gate is opening! Can you see a bright light?",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.say_8": "Ahhhhhhhh! ",
  "npc.muriel.say_1": "Indeed there is something to be done, but I need someone more experienced. Come back later if you want to.",
  "npc.muriel.say_2": "Excellent! Now I can try to put my theoretical thoughts into practice and find a cure for the symptoms of undead. Here, take this for your efforts.",
  "npc.muriel.say_3": "I am very glad you helped me, but I am very busy at the moment.",
  "npc.muriel.say_4": "I see you have the porcelain masks. Are you ready to exchange them for the first addon?",
  "npc.muriel.say_5": "I see you have the colourful feathers. Are you ready to exchange them for the second addon?",
  "npc.muriel.say_6": "You need the outfit and 3 porcelain masks or 50 colored feathers to get the festive costume accessories.",
  "npc.muriel.say_7": "Very good! You gained the first addon to the festive outfit.",
  "npc.muriel.say_8": "Oh, sorry but you don't have enough porcelain masks!",
  "npc.muriel.say_9": "Very good! You gained the second addon to the festive outfit.",
  "npc.muriel.say_10": "Oh, sorry but you don't have enough colourful feathers!",
  "npc.muriel.say_11": "I provide two addons. For the first one I need you to bring me three porcelain masks. For the second addon you need fifty colourful ostrich feathers. Do you want one of these addons?",
  "npc.muriel.say_12": "What do you have for me: the porcelain masks or the colourful feathers?",
  "npc.muriel.say_13": "I provide two addons. For the first one I need you to bring me three porcelain masks. For the second addon you need fifty colourful ostrich feathers. Do you want one of these addons?",
  "npc.muriel.say_14": "Ohh, then I need to find another adventurer who wants to earn a great reward. Bye!",
  "npc.stricken_soul.say_1": "Excellent... I hope they will haaaaaaunt my house no longer. What was your... naaaaaame again, tell me?",
  "npc.stricken_soul.say_2": "Yeeeees... you need to help meeeeeee. I want those ghosts gone... this is my home and I need it to teach my students. Will you take care of the... ghosts?",
  "npc.stricken_soul.say_3": "Sorry, I didn't understand.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_1": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_2": "Sorry, but you can't deposit that much.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_3": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.wentworth.say_4": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_5": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.wentworth.say_6": "Please tell me how much gold it is you would like to deposit.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_7": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.wentworth.say_8": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_9": "Sorry, but you can't deposit that much.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_10": "Sorry, but you can't deposit that much.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_11": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_12": "As you wish. Is there something else I can do for you?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_13": "Are you sure you wish to withdraw ",
  "npc.wentworth.say_14": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_15": "Please tell me how much gold you would like to withdraw.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_16": "Are you sure you wish to withdraw ",
  "npc.wentworth.say_17": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_18": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_19": "The customer is king! Come back anytime you want to if you wish to {withdraw} your money.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_20": "How many platinum coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_21": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_22": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_23": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_24": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_25": "Would you like to change your platinum coins into gold or crystal?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_26": "How many platinum coins would you like to change into gold?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_27": "How many crystal coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_28": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_29": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_30": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_31": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_32": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_33": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_34": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_35": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_36": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_37": "How many crystal coins would you like to change into platinum?",
  "npc.wentworth.say_38": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_39": "Here you are.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_40": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.wentworth.say_41": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_1": "Well, you could attempt the mission to become a recognised trader, but it requires a lot of travelling. Are you willing to try?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_2": "Have you managed to obtain a rare deer trophy for my customer?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_3": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_4": "Did you bring me the package?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_5": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_6": "Have you brought the cheese?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_7": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_8": "Have you brought the vase?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_9": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_10": "Have you brought a cheap but good crimson sword?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_11": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_12": "Have you brought me a gold fish??",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_13": "Ah, right. <ahem> I hereby declare you - one of my recognised traders! Feel free to offer me your wares!",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_14": "Fine. Then get a hold of that deer trophy and bring it to me while I'm in Svargrond. Just ask me about your mission.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_15": "Well done! I'll take that from you. <snags it> Come see me another day, I'll be busy for a while now. ",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_16": "Fine. Then off you go, just ask Willard about the 'package for Rashid'.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_17": "Great. Just place it over there - yes, thanks, that's it. Come see me another day, I'll be busy for a while now. ",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_18": "Okay, then please find Miraia in Darashia and ask her about the {'scarab cheese'}.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_19": "Mmmhh, the lovely odeur of scarab cheese! I really can't understand why most people can't stand it. Thanks, well done! ",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_20": "Okay, then please find {Briasol} in {Ab'Dendriel} and ask for a {'fine vase'}.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_21": "I'm surprised that you managed to bring this vase without a single crack. That was what I needed to know, thank you. ",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_22": "Okay, I'm curious how you will do with {Uzgod}. Good luck!",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_23": "Ha! You are clever indeed, well done! I'll take this from you. Come see me tomorrow, I think we two might get into business after all.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_24": "Thanks so much! I'll be waiting eagerly for your return then.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_25": "Thank you!! Ah, this makes my day! I'll take the rest of the day off to get to know this little guy. Come see me tomorrow, if you like.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_26": "I am a travelling trader. I don't buy everything, though. And not from everyone, for that matter.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_27": "I am Rashid, son of the desert.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_28": "Of course, old friend. You can also browse only armor, legs, shields, helmets, boots, weapons, enchanted weapons, jewelry or miscellaneous stuff.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_29": "Elves... I don't really trust them. All this talk about nature and flowers and treehugging... I'm sure there's some wicked scheme behind all this.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_30": "My beloved hometown! Ah, the sweet scent of the desert sands, the perfect shape of the pyramids... stunningly beautiful.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_31": "I have to go to Carlin once in a while, since the queen wishes to see my exclusive wares in regular intervals.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_32": "Cormaya? Not a good place to make business, it's way too far and small.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_33": "It's not the real thing, but almost as good. The merchants there claim ridiculous prices, which is fine for my own business.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_34": "Ah yes, Edron! Such a lovely and quiet island! I usually make some nice business there.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_35": "Too few customers there, it's not worth the trip.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_36": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_37": "I don't like being underground much. I also tend to get lost in these labyrinthine dwarven tunnels, so I rather avoid them.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_38": "When you avoid the slums, it's a really pretty city. Almost as pretty as the governor's daughter.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_39": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_40": "I like the settlement itself, but I don't set my foot into the jungle. Have you seen the size of these centipedes??",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_41": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_42": "I wish it was a little bit warmer there, but with a good mug of barbarian mead in your tummy everything gets a lot cosier.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_43": "I feel uncomfortable and rather unsafe in Thais, so I don't really travel there.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_44": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_45": "Although it's the flourishing trade centre of Tibia, I don't like going there. Too much competition for my taste.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_46": "It's almost time to journey on.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.stdmod_47": "Kings, queens, emperors and kaliphs... everyone claims to be different and unique, but actually it's the same thing everywhere.",
  "npc.rashid_custom.say_48": "Sorry, but you do not belong to my exclusive customers. I have to make sure that I can trust in the quality of your wares.",
  "npc.gate_guardian.say_1": "You want entranzzze to zzze zzzity?",
  "npc.gate_guardian.say_2": "Mh, zzzezzze paperzzz zzzeem legit, I have orderzzz to let you pazzz. Zzzo be it.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_1": "I'm responsible for the security and reward heroes to our cause. If you are looking for missions, talk to Gnomilly, Gnombold and Gnomagery.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_2": "I can sell special outfit parts. If your fame is high enough, you might be {worthy} of such a reward.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_3": "You are not worthy of a special reward yet.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_4": "You can acquire the {basic} outfit for 1000 Gold, the {first} addon for 2000 gold and the {second} addon for 3000 gold. Which do you want to buy?",
  "npc.gnommander.say_5": "You do not have enough level yet.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_6": "You already have that outfit.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_7": "Do you want to buy the basic outfit for 1000 Gold?",
  "npc.gnommander.say_8": "You do not have enough level yet.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_9": "You do not have the Cave Explorer outfit.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_10": "You already have that addon.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_11": "Do you want to buy the first addon for 2000 Gold?",
  "npc.gnommander.say_12": "You do not have enough level yet.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_13": "You do not have the Cave Explorer outfit.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_14": "You already have that addon.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_15": "Do you want to buy the second addon for 3000 Gold?",
  "npc.gnommander.say_16": "You do not have that money.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_17": "Here it is.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_18": "You do not have that money.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_19": "Here it is.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_20": "You do not have that money.",
  "npc.gnommander.say_21": "Here it is.",
  "npc.xelvar.say_1": "Right now I am sort of {recruiting} people.",
  "npc.xelvar.say_2": "You already talked with me.",
  "npc.xelvar.say_3": "Ok, so listen. Your help is needed. That is if you're the hero type. Our ... {partners} need some help in urgent matters.",
  "npc.xelvar.say_4": "I guess the time of secrecy is over now. Well, we have an old alliance with another underground dwelling race, the {gnomes}.",
  "npc.mirabell.say_1": "Oh you've heard about my excellent pies, didn't you? I am flattered. Unfortunately I'm completely out of flour. I need 2 portions of flour for one pie. Just tell me when you have enough flour for your pies.",
  "npc.mirabell.say_2": "For 12 pies this is 240 gold. Do you want to buy them?",
  "npc.mirabell.say_3": "Do you bring me the flour needed for your pies?",
  "npc.mirabell.say_4": "I think you are confusing the dust in your pockets with flour. You certainly do not have enough flour for 12 pies.",
  "npc.mirabell.say_5": "Excellent. Now I can start baking the pies. As you helped me, I will make you a good price for them.",
  "npc.mirabell.say_6": "You don't have enough money, don't try to fool me.",
  "npc.mirabell.say_7": "Without flour I can't do anything, sorry.",
  "npc.mirabell.say_8": "What are you? Some kind of fool?",
  "npc.mirabell.stdmod_9": "I can offer you beer, wine, lemonade and water. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.mirabell.stdmod_10": "Are you looking for food? I have bread, cheese, ham, and meat. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.jorge.say_1": "You just swapped 20 silver raid tokens for 1 ",
  "npc.jorge.say_2": "I'm sorry, I need at least 20 silver tokens for that. Please come back when you have them.",
  "npc.woblin.say_1": "You bring me Old Nasty?",
  "npc.myra.say_1": "This Tiara is an award by the academy of Edron in recognition of my service here.",
  "npc.myra.say_2": "Please ask about the 'outfit' first.",
  "npc.myra.say_3": "Well... maybe, if you help me a little, I could convince the academy of Edron that you are a valuable help here and deserve an award too. How about it?",
  "npc.myra.say_4": "Before I can nominate you for an award, please complete your task.",
  "npc.myra.say_5": "Go to the academy in Edron and tell Zoltan that I sent you, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.myra.say_6": "I don't have any tasks for you right now, |PLAYERNAME|. You were of great help.",
  "npc.myra.say_7": "That's a pity.",
  "npc.myra.say_8": "Fine! Let's start with the 70 bat wings. I really feel uncomfortable out there in the jungle.",
  "npc.myra.say_9": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_10": "Oh, did you bring the 70 bat wings for me?",
  "npc.myra.say_11": "Have you found 20 pieces of red cloth?",
  "npc.myra.say_12": "Were you able to retrieve 40 pieces of ape fur?",
  "npc.myra.say_13": "Did you convince the elves to give you 35 holy orchids?",
  "npc.myra.say_14": "Oh, did you bring 10 spools of spider silk yarn for me?",
  "npc.myra.say_15": "Have you found 60 lizard scales?",
  "npc.myra.say_16": "Were you able to get all 40 red dragon scales?",
  "npc.myra.say_17": "Have you collected 15 ounces of magic sulphur?",
  "npc.myra.say_18": "Have you gathered 30 ounces of vampire dust?",
  "npc.myra.say_19": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_20": "Thank you! I really needed them for my anti-wrinkle lotion. Now, please bring me 20 pieces of red cloth.",
  "npc.myra.say_21": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_22": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_23": "Great! This should be enough for my new dress. Don't forget to bring me 40 pieces of ape fur next!",
  "npc.myra.say_24": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_25": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_26": "Nice job, player. You see, I'm testing a new depilation cream. I guess if it works on ape fur it's good quality. Next, please bring me 35 holy orchids.",
  "npc.myra.say_27": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_28": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_29": "Thank god! The scent of holy orchids is simply the only possible solution against the horrible stench from the tavern latrine. Now, please bring me 10 rolls of spider silk yarn.",
  "npc.myra.say_30": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_31": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_32": "I appreciate it. My pet doggie manages to bite through all sorts of leashes, which is why he is always gone. I'm sure this strong yarn will keep him. Now, go for the 60 lizard scales!",
  "npc.myra.say_33": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_34": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_35": "Good job. They will look almost like sequins on my new dress. Please go for the 40 red dragon scales now.",
  "npc.myra.say_36": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_37": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_38": "Thanks! They make a pretty decoration, don't you think? Please bring me 15 ounces of magic sulphur now!",
  "npc.myra.say_39": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_40": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_41": "Ah, that's enough magic sulphur for my new peeling. You should try it once, your skin gets incredibly smooth. Now, the only thing I need is vampire dust. 30 ounces will suffice.",
  "npc.myra.say_42": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_43": "No, no. That's not enough, I fear.",
  "npc.myra.say_44": "Ah, great. Now I can finally finish the potion which the academy of Edron asked me to. I guess, now you want your reward, don't you?",
  "npc.myra.say_45": "Would you like me to repeat the task requirements then?",
  "npc.myra.say_46": "This Tiara is an award by the academy of Edron in recognition of my service here.",
  "npc.myra.say_47": "Go to the academy in Edron and tell Zoltan that I sent you, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.sandomo.say_1": "Oh, so you want a reward, hm? Well... let's see. What did you do for us - helping Mortis with his {repairs} and defended him?",
  "npc.sandomo.say_2": "Come back after you have done at least one of the tasks I talked you about.",
  "npc.sandomo.say_3": "You have ",
  "npc.sandomo.say_4": "I do not see inquisition gold registered in my book from you.",
  "npc.sandomo.say_5": "Ah yes, you currently have ",
  "npc.sandomo.say_6": "You do not seem to have enough inquisition gold yet to trade for clusters, as it's registered in my book.",
  "npc.sandomo.say_7": "You should tell me a real number.",
  "npc.sandomo.say_8": "You do not have enough inquisition gold for that, so far you can ask for up to ",
  "npc.sandomo.say_9": "Head to brother Maun if you are in need of basic supplies. He will help you - for a small fee.",
  "npc.sandomo.say_10": "Brother Maun is a valuable member of the Inquisition. He will help you out with supplies. Provided you can actually compensate of course.",
  "npc.flora.say_1": "Do you really want to enter the Glooth Fairy's hideout. There is no chickening out and I also have to charge one voting right! {Yes} or {no}?",
  "npc.flora.say_2": "Here you go!",
  "npc.flora.say_3": "Okay...",
  "npc.briasol.say_1": "Here it is.",
  "npc.briasol.say_2": "You don't have enought money.",
  "npc.santiago.say_1": "Oh, what's wrong? As I said, simply go to my house south of here and go upstairs. Then come back and we'll continue our chat.",
  "npc.santiago.say_2": "I've forgotten to tell you something. Of course I need proof that you killed cockroaches. Please bring me at least 3 of their legs. Good luck!",
  "npc.santiago.say_3": "I've forgotten to tell you something. Of course I need proof that you killed cockroaches. Please bring me at least 3 of their legs. Good luck!",
  "npc.santiago.say_4": "Great, please go to my house, just a few steps south of here. Upstairs in my room, you'll find a chest. You can keep what you find inside of it! Come back after you got it and greet me to talk to me again. {Yes}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_5": "Alright! Do you see the button called 'Quest Log'? There you can check the status of quests, like this one. {Bye} for now!",
  "npc.santiago.say_6": "Ah, no need to say anything, I can see it suits you perfectly. Now we're getting to the fun part, let's get you armed! Are you ready for some {action}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_7": "Oh, you don't wear it properly yet. You need to drag and drop it from your bag to your armor slot. Here, let me show you again. Is it a little {clearer} now?",
  "npc.santiago.say_8": "Oh no, did you lose my coat? Well, lucky you, I have a spare one here. Don't lose it again! Now we're getting to the fun part, let's get you armed! Are you ready for some {action}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_9": "I knew I could count on you. Here, take this good and sturdy weapon in your hand. Then go back to my house and down the ladder. Good luck, and {bye} for now!",
  "npc.santiago.say_10": "That's just great! Now you have more health points, can carry more stuff and walk faster. Talking about health, did you get {hurt} by those cockroaches?",
  "npc.santiago.say_11": "Really? You look fine to me, must have been just a scratch. Well, there are much more dangerous monsters than cockroaches out there. Take a look at your status bar. You have 155 Health right now. I'll show you something, {yes}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_12": "This is an important lesson from me - an experienced veteran fighter. Take this! Look at your status bar again. As you can see, you've lost health. Now I'll tell you how to heal that, {yes}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_13": "I knew you'd get it right away. You can loot food from many creatures, such as deer and rabbits. You can find them in the forest nearby. By the way... have you seen {Zirella}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_14": "Really?? She was looking for someone to help her. Maybe you could go and see her. She lives just to the east and down the mountain. So, thank you again and {bye} for now!",
  "npc.santiago.say_15": "This is an important lesson from me - an experienced veteran fighter. Take this! Look at your status bar again. As you can see, you've lost health. Now I'll tell you how to heal that, {yes}?",
  "npc.santiago.say_16": "I knew I could count on you. Here, take this good and sturdy weapon in your hand. Then go back to my house and down the ladder. Good luck, and {bye} for now!",
  "npc.santiago.say_17": "I knew you'd get it right away. You can loot food from many creatures, such as deer and rabbits. You can find them in the forest nearby. By the way... have you seen {Zirella}?",
  "npc.altar.say_1": "Prepare your offer and cling to the sanctitity of this place.",
  "npc.altar.say_2": "Five tainted hearts and five darklight hearts drowned in a worldly wealth of 50000000 gold pieces for the righteous. Are you prepared?",
  "npc.altar.say_3": "Sorry, you don't have all items.",
  "npc.altar.say_4": "Sorry, you don't have enough gold.",
  "npc.altar.say_5": "Your sacrifice has been accepted, mortal. Embrace your reward!",
  "npc.altar.say_6": "Ok then not.",
  "npc.tarak_sunken.say_1": "Do you want to go back to {Yalahar}?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_1": "Oh, my beloved ring! Have you found it and want to return it to me?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_2": "I would need some help in another matter. It is only a small errand. Are you interested?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_3": "Great, thank you! As promised, here are your 5 gold pieces. Is there ... anything left that you might want to discuss with me?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_4": "You have returned my ring and proven yourself as trustworthy. There is something I have to discuss with you. Are you willing to listen?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_5": "<blushes> Oh, he is so wonderful. A very special man with a special place in my heart.",
  "npc.eleonore.say_6": "I can't thank you enough for freeing my beloved Ray from that evil spell. I am still shocked that a mermaid could steal his love that easily.",
  "npc.eleonore.say_7": "Oh, thank you so much! Take this gold as a reward. ... which reminds me, I would need some help in another matter. It is only a small errand. Are you interested?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_8": "Thank you! It is not a difficult matter but a rather urgent one. I need to send some money to a person in town. Would you be willing to run this small errand for me?",
  "npc.eleonore.say_9": "I was hoping that you'd agree. Please deliver these 200 gold pieces to the herbalist Charlotta in the south-western part of the town. If you return from this errand, I will grant you 5 gold pieces as reward for your efforts.",
  "npc.eleonore.say_10": "Then no.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_1": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_2": "Sorry, but you can't deposit that much.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_3": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_4": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_5": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_6": "Please tell me how much gold it is you would like to deposit.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_7": "Would you really like to deposit ",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_8": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_9": "Sorry, but you can't deposit that much.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_10": "You do not have enough gold.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_11": "As you wish. Is there something else I can do for you?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_12": "Are you sure you wish to withdraw ",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_13": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_14": "Please tell me how much gold you would like to withdraw.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_15": "Are you sure you wish to withdraw ",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_16": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_17": "There is not enough gold on your account.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_18": "The customer is king! Come back anytime you want to if you wish to {withdraw} your money.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_19": "How many platinum coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_20": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_21": "Here you are.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_22": "Sorry, you do not have enough gold coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_23": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_24": "Would you like to change your platinum coins into gold or crystal?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_25": "How many platinum coins would you like to change into gold?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_26": "How many crystal coins would you like to get?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_27": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_28": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_29": "Here you are.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_30": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_31": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_32": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_33": "Here you are.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_34": "Sorry, you do not have enough platinum coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_35": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_36": "How many crystal coins would you like to change into platinum?",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_37": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_38": "Here you are.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_39": "Sorry, you do not have enough crystal coins.",
  "npc.plunderpurse.say_40": "Well, can I help you with something else?",
  "npc.julius.say_1": "Our nightly blood-sucking visitors put the inhabitants of Yalahar in constant danger. The worst thing is that anyone in this city could be a vampire. Maybe an outsider like you could help us. Would you try?",
  "npc.julius.say_2": "Hmm, I see, I see. That necklace is only a small indication though... I think I need another proof, just to make sure. Say... have you ever baked {garlic bread}?",
  "npc.julius.say_3": "I fear that will not do. Sorry.",
  "npc.julius.say_4": "I fear that will not do. Sorry.",
  "npc.julius.say_5": "Let me check - yes indeed, there's garlic in it. Now eat one, in front of my eyes. Right now! Say '{aaah}' when you've chewed it all down so that I can see you're not hiding it!",
  "npc.julius.say_6": "So, are you ready for your first real task?",
  "npc.julius.say_7": "Are you back with confirmed names of possible vampires?",
  "npc.julius.say_8": "Oh! You look horrible - I mean, rather weary. What happened? Who is the master vampire?",
  "npc.julius.say_9": "Well, there's one problem. How would I know I can trust you? You might be one of them... hm. Can you think of something really unlikely for a vampire? If you know a way to prove it to me, ask me about your {mission}.",
  "npc.julius.say_10": "Fine then. Talk to me again about your mission once you have the garlic bread. You can get holy water from a member of the inquisition.",
  "npc.julius.say_11": "Fine. Good luck! Talk to me again about your mission once you have confirmed the names of five suspects.",
  "npc.julius.say_12": "Alright, wait a moment. Tell me one name at a time so I can note them down carefully. Who is a suspect?",
  "npc.julius.say_13": "Well, you need to mix flour with holy water and use that dough on garlic to create a special dough. Bake it like normal bread, but I guarantee that no vampire can eat that. Are you following me?",
  "npc.julius.say_14": "I guess Armenius, Lisander, Maris, Ortheus and Serafin are all the names we can get for now. Let me think for a moment what we are going to do, talk to me about your mission again later.",
  "npc.julius.say_15": "No, no, I was asking for one of the names.",
  "npc.julius.say_16": "Very well. I think I can trust you now. Sorry that I had to put you through this embarassing procedure, but I'm sure you understand. So, are you ready for your first real task?",
  "npc.julius.say_17": "No, no, you didn't eat it! Vampire Brood! Say '{aaah}' once you have eaten the bread or get out of her instantly!",
  "npc.julius.say_18": "He really doesn't look like the man of the sea he pretends to be, does he? Noted down! Any other name?",
  "npc.julius.say_19": "You already reported that name. Any new ones?",
  "npc.julius.say_20": "Hm. You don't look so sure about that one. You should not report suspects that you did not confirm yourself! Any others?",
  "npc.julius.say_21": "I always thought that there is not really a poor beggar hidden under those ragged clothes. Noted down! Any other name?",
  "npc.julius.say_22": "You already reported that name. Any new ones?",
  "npc.julius.say_23": "Hm. You don't look so sure about that one. You should not report suspects that you did not confirm yourself! Any others?",
  "npc.julius.say_24": "Nice angelic name for a vampire. But he didn't escape your attention, well done. Noted down! Any other name?",
  "npc.julius.say_25": "You already reported that name. Any new ones?",
  "npc.julius.say_26": "Hm. You don't look so sure about that one. You should not report suspects that you did not confirm yourself! Any others?",
  "npc.julius.say_27": "Yes, that pale skin and those black eyes speak volumes. Noted down! Any other name?",
  "npc.julius.say_28": "You already reported that name. Any new ones?",
  "npc.julius.say_29": "Hm. You don't look so sure about that one. You should not report suspects that you did not confirm yourself! Any others?",
  "npc.julius.say_30": "Ahh, I always thought something was suspicious about him. Noted down! Any other name?",
  "npc.julius.say_31": "You already reported that name. Any new ones?",
  "npc.julius.say_32": "Hm. You don't look so sure about that one. You should not report suspects that you did not confirm yourself! Any others?",
  "npc.julius.say_33": "Then try harder.",
  "npc.julius.say_34": "Hm. You don't look so sure about that one. You should not report suspects that you did not confirm yourself! Any others?",
  "npc.julius.say_35": "Good. Don't play around with the spell, only use it when standing in front of those vampires. Come back and report to me about your progress later.",
  "npc.julius.say_36": "I see... so Armenius is the master, and the spell didn't even cause a scratch on him... Well, that went worse than expected. Let me think for a moment and then ask me about a mission again.",
  "npc.julius.say_37": "Getting cold feet, eh?",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_38": "I come from a family of {vampire} hunters, but to be honest, I'm more into the theoretic part and strategic planning.",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_39": "A better name would be Gomorrah, if you ask me.",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_40": "My name is Julius.",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_41": "Storkus? Oh yes, I know him. A long time ago we used to hunt together... sometimes.",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_42": "It's about time you showed the vampires that they should never bother the citizens again.",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_43": "Another vampire raid last night. But then again, that's nothing new.",
  "npc.julius.stdmod_44": "Well, I should be the one to thank you I guess.",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_1": "Hurray! For that I will give you my key for - hmm - let's say ... some apples. Interested?",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_2": "Mnjam - excellent apples. Now - about that key. You are sure want it?",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_3": "Get some more apples first!",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_4": "Really, really?",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_5": "Really, really, really, really?",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_6": "Then take it and get happy - or die, hehe.",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_7": "Then go away!",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_8": "You already know the secrets of mathemagics! Now go and use them to learn.",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_9": "But first tell me your favourite colour please!",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_10": "Very interesting. So are you ready to proceed in your lesson in mathemagics?",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_11": "So know that everything is based on the simple fact that 1 + 1 = 1!",
  "npc.a_prisoner.say_12": " I think you are not in touch with yourself, come back if you have tuned in on your own feelings.",
  "npc.sam.say_1": "Oh, Gregor sent you? I see. It will be my pleasure to adorn your helmet. Please give me some time to finish it.",
  "npc.sam.say_2": "Just in time, |PLAYERNAME|. Your helmet is finished, I hope you like it.",
  "npc.sam.say_3": "Please have some patience, |PLAYERNAME|. Forging is hard work!",
  "npc.sam.say_4": "I think it's one of my masterpieces.",
  "npc.sam.say_5": "Sorry, but without the permission of Gregor I cannot help you with this matter.",
  "npc.sam.say_6": "What? Are you telling me you found my old adventurer's backpack that I lost years ago??",
  "npc.sam.say_7": "My offers are weapons, armors, helmets, legs, and shields. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.sam.say_8": "What? You want to buy 2000 steel shields??",
  "npc.sam.say_9": "Have you signed the contract?",
  "npc.sam.say_10": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.sam.say_11": "I can't believe it. Finally I will be rich! I could move to Edron and enjoy my retirement! But ... wait a minute! I will not start working without a contract! Are you willing to sign one?",
  "npc.sam.say_12": "Fine! Here is the contract. Please sign it. Talk to me about it again when you're done.",
  "npc.sam.say_13": "You don't have a signed contract.",
  "npc.sam.say_14": "Excellent! I will start working right away! Now that I am going to be rich, I will take the opportunity to tell some people what I REALLY think about them!",
  "npc.sam.say_15": "Then no.",
  "npc.sam.say_16": "This deal sounded too good to be true anyway.",
  "npc.sam.stdmod_17": "I am the blacksmith. If you need weapons or armor - just ask me.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_5": "The temple can be found in one of the uptown districts. Look for stairs up from the lower city, you'll find the temple in the northwest of the upper city.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_6": "The First Oramond Bank is an important part of Rathleton, and is situated in the centre of the upper city. I can mark it on your map if you want.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_7": "You can buy almost everything here! Visit one of our shops for weapons, armors, magical equipment, spells, gems, tools, furnitureand everything else you can imagine.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_9": " I will help you find your way in the marvellous city of Rathleton. I can mark important locations on your map and give you someinformation about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_10": "This city is a modern marvel of progress. The city's wealth and industry is based on the famous glooth. The magistrate runs the city according to the wishes of its inhabitants.",
  "npc.guide_kunibert.stdmod_11": "I'm Kunibert, of course.",
  "npc.alexander.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.alexander.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.alexander.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.alexander.stdmod_4": "I'm selling runes, life rings, wands, rods and crystal balls. I also buy powerful spellbooks. If you like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.lurik.say_1": "Ah, you've just come in time. An experienced explorer is just what we need here! Would you like to go on a mission for us?",
  "npc.lurik.say_2": "You're not done yet...",
  "npc.lurik.say_3": "Have you retrieved the memory crystal?",
  "npc.lurik.say_4": "Give me some more time!",
  "npc.lurik.say_5": "Excellent. Just report about your mission when you got the memory crystal.",
  "npc.lurik.say_6": "Ah, great. Please give me some time to evaluate the information. Then talk to me again about your mission. ",
  "npc.gnomux.say_1": "I'm responsible for resupplying foolish adventurers with equipment that they may have lost. If you're one of them, just ask me about a {trade}. ",
  "npc.gnomux.say_2": "What could I say about gnomes that anyone would not know? I mean, we're interesting if not fascinating, after all.",
  "npc.gnomux.say_3": "I came here as a crystal farmer and know the Spike all the way back to when it was a little baby crystal. I admit I feel a little fatherly pride in how big and healthy it has become.",
  "npc.zizzle.say_1": "You made it! Az zoon az you are prepared, I will brief you for your nexzt mizzion. ",
  "npc.zizzle.say_2": "Now go to the north of Sleeping Dragon room, {dont need talk} with he!",
  "npc.barazbaz.say_1": "You need to kill the {The Ravager}, click on statue and then come here say {ritual}, {abandoned sewers}, {notebook} and after this find Roswitha and talk with she.",
  "npc.noodles.say_1": "<sniff><sniff>",
  "npc.noodles.say_2": "<sniff><sniff>",
  "npc.noodles.say_3": "<sniff><sniff>",
  "npc.noodles.say_4": "Woof!",
  "npc.noodles.say_5": "Woof!",
  "npc.noodles.say_6": "Meeep! Grrrrr! <spits>",
  "npc.myzzi.say_1": "I'm just a mere messenger and I'm here to find brave adventurers that might {help} my friends in this time of need.",
  "npc.myzzi.say_2": "Lady Alivar of the Summer Court and Lord Cadion of the Winter Court are in need of brave adventurers to avert a great {threat} for the whole world.",
  "npc.myzzi.say_3": "There are {entrances} to the hidden Courts of Summer and Winter in secluded places. You can find the portal to the Winter Court high in the mountains of Tyrsung and the portal to the Summer Court in the meadows of Feyrist. ...",
  "npc.myzzi.say_4": "So, are you willing to help in this time of need?",
  "npc.myzzi.say_5": "You are a true hero! Here, take my enchantment and you will be able to pass the portals. Now hurry, my friends are waiting.",
  "npc.myzzi.say_6": "What?!",
  "npc.lugri.say_1": "This skull shows that you are a true follower of Zathroth and the glorious gods of darkness. Are you willing to prove your loyalty?",
  "npc.lugri.say_2": "Is it your true wish to sacrifice a medusa shield to Zathroth?",
  "npc.lugri.say_3": "Is it your true wish to sacrifice a dragon scale mail to Zathroth?",
  "npc.lugri.say_4": "Is it your true wish to sacrifice crown legs to Zathroth?",
  "npc.lugri.say_5": "Is it your true wish to sacrifice a ring of the sky to Zathroth?",
  "npc.lugri.say_6": "Come back when you have slain 4000 necromancers and priestesses!",
  "npc.lugri.say_7": "Good job!",
  "npc.lugri.say_8": "Come back when you have slain 1000 necromancers and priestesses!",
  "npc.lugri.say_9": "You can't live without serving, can you? Although you are quite annoying, you're still somewhat useful. Continue killing Necromancers and Priestesses for me. 1000 are enough this time. What do you say?",
  "npc.lugri.say_10": "It will be a hard task which requires many sacrifices. Do you still want to proceed?",
  "npc.lugri.say_11": "Good decision, |PLAYERNAME|. Your first sacrifice will be a medusa shield. Bring it to me and do give it happily.",
  "npc.lugri.say_12": "Good. I accept your sacrifice. The second sacrifice I require from you is a dragon scale mail. Bring it to me and do give it happily.",
  "npc.lugri.say_13": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.lugri.say_14": "Good. I accept your sacrifice. The third sacrifice I require from you are crown legs. Bring them to me and do give them happily.",
  "npc.lugri.say_15": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.lugri.say_16": "Good. I accept your sacrifice. The last sacrifice I require from you is a ring of the sky. Bring it to me and do give it happily.",
  "npc.lugri.say_17": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.lugri.say_18": "Good. I accept your sacrifice. You have proven that you are a true follower of Zathroth and do not hesitate to sacrifice worldly goods. Thus, I will reward you with this headgear. ",
  "npc.lugri.say_19": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.lugri.say_20": "Good. Then go.",
  "npc.lugri.say_21": "Then no.",
  "npc.walter_the_guard.say_1": "I think there is a pickpocket in town.",
  "npc.walter_the_guard.say_2": "Well, sooner or later we will get hold of that delinquent. That's for sure.",
  "npc.walter_the_guard.say_3": "You can't tell by a person's appearance who is a pickpocket and who isn't. You simply can't close the city gates for everyone.",
  "npc.walter_the_guard.say_4": "If the gods had created the world a paradise, no one had to steal at all.",
  "npc.talphion.say_1": "DRESS FLATTEN? WHO WANTS ME TO FLATTEN A DRESS?",
  "npc.talphion.say_2": "A PRESS LANTERN? NEVER HEARD ABOUT IT!",
  "npc.talphion.say_3": "CHESS? I DONT PLAY CHESS!",
  "npc.talphion.say_4": "A PATTERN IN THIS MESS?? HEY DON'T INSULT MY MACHINE HALL!",
  "npc.talphion.say_5": "AH YES! I WORKED ON THE DRESS PATTERN FOR THOSE UNIFORMS. STAINLESS TROUSERES, STEAM DRIVEN BOOTS! ANOTHERMARVEL TO BEHOLD! I'LL SENT A COPY TO KEVIN IMEDIATELY!",
  "npc.uncle.say_1": "Then welcome to the family.",
  "npc.uncle.say_2": "I hope you did not make this little pest too nervous. He isn't serving us too well by hiding under some stone or something like that. However, nicely done for your first job.",
  "npc.uncle.say_3": "Ah, yes. This will be a most interesting lecture.",
  "npc.uncle.say_4": "Please bring me the file AH-X17L89.",
  "npc.uncle.say_5": "Does it not warm up your heart if you can bring a little joy to the people while doing your job? Well, don't get carried away, most part of your job is not warming up hearts but tearing them out.",
  "npc.uncle.say_6": "Good work getting rid of that nuisance.",
  "npc.uncle.say_7": "Fine, fine. This will serve us quite well. Ah, don't give me that look... you are not that stupid, are you?",
  "npc.uncle.say_8": "Come back when you've found the ring.",
  "npc.uncle.say_9": "Even if the present has not improved our relations, the weapons will enable the barbarians to put more pressure on Svargrond and Carlin. So in any case we profited from the present.",
  "npc.uncle.say_10": "Please bring me proof of the mad technomancers defeat!",
  "npc.uncle.say_11": "As you wish.",
  "npc.uncle.say_12": "Let's start with a rather simple job. There is a contact in Thais with that we need to get in touch again. Deliver this note to Gamel in Thais. Get an answer from him. If he is a bit reluctant, be 'persuasive'.",
  "npc.uncle.say_13": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy?",
  "npc.uncle.say_14": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy?",
  "npc.uncle.say_15": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy? Don't tell me you need another barrel of beer, though.",
  "npc.uncle.say_16": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy?",
  "npc.uncle.say_17": "I need you to locate a lost ring on the Isle of the Kings for me, get back to me once you have it.",
  "npc.uncle.say_18": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy?",
  "npc.uncle.say_19": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy?",
  "npc.uncle.say_20": "Do you have news to make old Uncle happy?",
  "npc.gareth.say_1": "If you like to, you can pay some gold to become a patron of the arts for this wonderful museum. The price is 10,000 gold. Your personal gain will be priceless. Do you want to {pay}?",
  "npc.gareth.say_2": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.gareth.say_3": "They want us to buy the picture back. Unfortunately this artefact is so important that I don't see an alternative. Please got to Iwar in Kazordoon and pay the money.",
  "npc.gareth.say_4": "So the rumours are true. How could this happen? I'll keep the picture at its place until we've got a replacement. Please fo to {Angelo} and ask him if he has a new artefact for our museum.",
  "npc.gareth.say_5": "You didn't investigate the pictures yet. Do your job and then come back.",
  "npc.gareth.say_6": "It is planned to extend the MOTA. But this will take time, because our workers have faced a little {problem}.",
  "npc.gareth.say_7": "You are a true patron of the arts! I have opened the construction site for you. Start your work right now!",
  "npc.xorlosh.say_1": "Hmmmm, you could indeed help me. See this mechanism? Some son of a rotworm put WAY too much stuff on this elevator and now it's broken. I need 3 gear wheels to fix it. You think you could get them for me?",
  "npc.xorlosh.say_2": "HOLY MOTHER OF ALL ROTWORMS! You did it and they are of even better quality than the old ones. You should be the first one to try the elevator, just jump on it. See you my friend.",
  "npc.xorlosh.say_3": "That would be great! Maybe a blacksmith can forge you some. Come back when you got them and ask me about your mission.",
  "npc.xorlosh.say_4": "The book about tunnelling is in the library which is located in the north eastern wing of Beregar city.",
  "npc.zarifan.say_1": "...Tell me...the first... magic word.",
  "npc.zarifan.say_2": "Yes... YES... friendship... now... second word?",
  "npc.zarifan.say_3": "Yes... YES... friendship... lives... now third word?",
  "npc.zarifan.say_4": "...continue with your mission...",
  "npc.zarifan.stdmod_5": "..what about {magic}..",
  "npc.thanita.say_1": "Impressive!! I could need someone like you here at the watchtower! Okay, the password you need to tell Bunny is ' password* '. Come back and visit me if you like to!",
  "npc.oliver.say_1": "Nobody knows the trouble I've seen .. <tells a quite detailed report>. ",
  "npc.oliver.say_2": "You can {pass} either to the {Factory Quarter} or {Sunken Quarter}. Which one will it be?",
  "npc.grof_the_guard.say_1": "I think it'll rain soon and I left some laundry out for drying.",
  "npc.grof_the_guard.say_2": "Yes I'm pretty sure they have failed to send the laundry police to take care of it, you fool.",
  "npc.grof_the_guard.stdmod_3": "It's my duty to protect the city.",
  "npc.theodore_loveless.say_1": "Oh my. Have you gotten an exquisite cigar for me, my young friend?",
  "npc.theodore_loveless.say_2": "Oh, then there must be a misunderstanding.",
  "npc.gnomaticus.say_1": "Shoot at the villain targets that will pop up. DON'T shoot innocent civilians since this will reset your score and you have to start all over. {Report} to me afterwards.",
  "npc.gnomaticus.say_2": "You are showing some promise! Now continue with the recruitment and talk to Gnomewart to the south for your endurance test!",
  "npc.gnomaticus.say_3": "Sorry you are not done yet.",
  "npc.gnomaticus.say_4": "You have nothing to report at all.",
  "npc.costello.say_1": "Do you want me to inspect a diary?",
  "npc.costello.say_2": "Who are you to demand holy water from the White Raven Monastery? Who sent you??",
  "npc.costello.say_3": "I already filled your vial with holy water.",
  "npc.costello.say_4": "Ahh, Amanda from Edron sent you! I hope she's doing well. So why did she send you here?",
  "npc.costello.say_5": "Thank you very much! From now on you may open the warded doors to the catacombs.",
  "npc.costello.say_6": "Uhm, as you wish.",
  "npc.costello.say_7": "By the gods! This is brother Fugio's handwriting and what I read is horrible indeed! You have done our order a great favour by giving this diary to me! Take this blessed Ankh. May it protect you in even your darkest hours.",
  "npc.costello.say_8": "I never heard that name and you won't get holy water for some stranger.",
  "npc.costello.say_9": "Ohh, why didn't you tell me before? Sure you get some holy water if it's for Amanda! Here you are.",
  "npc.costello.say_10": "Uhm, as you wish.",
  "npc.pemaret.say_1": "WOW! You have a marlin!! I could make a nice decoration for your wall from it. May I have it?",
  "npc.pemaret.say_2": "Yeah! Now let's see... <fumble fumble> There you go, I hope you like it!",
  "npc.pemaret.say_3": "You don't have the fish.",
  "npc.pemaret.say_4": "Then no.",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_5": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_6": "Maybe later.",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_7": "I'm a fisherman and I take along people to Edron. You can also buy some fresh fish.",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_8": "I'm a fisherman and I take along people to Edron. You can also buy some fresh fish.",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_9": "My fish is of the finest quality you could find. Ask me for a trade to check for yourself.",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_10": "It's a lovely and peaceful isle. Did you already visit the nice sandy beach?",
  "npc.pemaret.stdmod_11": "My name is Pemaret, the fisherman.",
  "npc.doubleday.say_1": "Very nice, there you go! Just bring me the printout from the probe after deploying it! You can request a new probing {device} or a new {detector} if you lose it - but it takes some time for me to get a new one ready so be careful with that stuff.",
  "npc.doubleday.say_2": "Hey, let's try to be reasonable here, alright? That's a bit too much for what you did, isn't it? It may seem that way but the number of votes I can offer isn't limitless.",
  "npc.doubleday.say_3": "Good, you just gained 1 genuine votes in the magistrate!",
  "npc.doubleday.say_4": "Alright, there you go - please, try to be more careful with my equipment next time!",
  "npc.doubleday.say_5": "Well, let's see, you helped me 1 times before exchanging any votes - how many votes do you want me to give you in exchange?",
  "npc.doubleday.say_6": "Well, let's see, you helped me 1 times before exchanging any votes - how many votes do you want me to give you in {exchange}?",
  "npc.doubleday.say_7": "Alright then, that's 2 vote(s) you want - I won't take them back, are you sure?",
  "npc.doubleday.say_8": "Alright then, that's 1 vote(s) you want - I won't take them back, are you sure?",
  "npc.doubleday.say_9": "You must wait until the detector is ready again.",
  "npc.habdel.say_1": "My scimitar? Yes, that is a true masterpiece. Of course I could make one for you, but I have a small request. Would you fulfil a task for me?",
  "npc.habdel.say_2": "Have you brought a mermaid's comb for Ishina?",
  "npc.habdel.say_3": "Brilliant! I will wait for you to return with a mermaid's comb then.",
  "npc.habdel.say_4": "No... that's not it.",
  "npc.habdel.say_5": "Yeah! That's it! I can't wait to give it to her! Oh - but first, I'll fulfil my promise: Here is your scimitar! Thanks again!",
  "npc.habdel.say_6": "Ah well. Doesn't matter.",
  "npc.habdel.stdmod_7": "I sell the finest weapons in town. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.richard.multiline_1": "I was a carpenter, back on Main. Wanted my own little shop. Didn't sit with the old man. \\z\n\t\t\t\t\tSo I shipped to somewhere else. Terrible storm.",
  "npc.richard.multiline_2": "Woke up on this island. Had to eat squirrels before the adventurers found me and took me in. End of story.",
  "npc.richard.multiline_3": "Only the best quality, I assure you. A rope in need is a friend indeed! Imagine you stumble into a rat \\z\n\t\t\t\t\thole without a rope - heh, your bones will be gnawed clean before someone finds ya!",
  "npc.budrik.say_1": "As I was just saying to the others, 'this brave fellow will bring me my mining helmet back' and here you are with it!! Here take my spare helmet, I don't need it anymore!",
  "npc.budrik.say_2": "We presume the hideout of The Horned Fox is somewhere in the south-west near the coast, good luck finding my mining helmet!",
  "npc.budrik.say_3": "Come back when you have slain {5000 minotaurs!}",
  "npc.budrik.say_4": "It was very decent of you to help me, and I am thankful, really I am, but now I have to get back to my duties as a foreman.",
  "npc.budrik.say_5": "Well, I could need help with that damn Horned Fox and his gang, but I guess since you are rather experienced, killing minotaurs would bore you to death. I'll wait for someone else. But thanks!",
  "npc.budrik.say_6": "Hum... what, {task}?",
  "npc.budrik.say_7": "I knew you have the guts for that task! We presume the hideout of The Horned Fox somewhere in the south-west near the coast. Good luck!",
  "npc.budrik.say_8": "Hussah! Let's bring war to those hoof-legged, dirt-necked, bull-headed minotaurs!! Come back to me when you are done with your {mission}.",
  "npc.budrik.say_9": "Zzz...",
  "npc.budrik.say_10": "Then no.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_11": "I'm the foreman of this {mine}.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_12": "We understand the ways of the earth like nobody else.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_13": "I'm a miner, not your mother. Go ask someone else.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_14": "The hideout of the Horned Fox is probably a dangerous if not lethal place for inexperienced adventurers. It is the source of all the {trouble} around here.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_15": "He is a minotaur who was kicked out of Mintwallin. He must have some kind of {hideout} nearby.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_16": "This is not an amusement park! Leave the miners and their drilling-worms alone and get out! We've already got enough {trouble} without you.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_17": "We occasionally come across nasty beasts in the deepest mines.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_18": "My name is Budrik Deepdigger, Son of Earth, from the Molten Rock.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_19": "The {Horned Fox} is leading his bandits in sneak attacks and raids on us.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_20": "You may enter the tunnel.",
  "npc.budrik.stdmod_21": "This is no funhouse. Leave the miners and their drilling-worms alone and get out! We have already enough trouble without you.",
  "npc.rabaz.say_1": "Well fantastic work, you gathered both samples! Now I can continue my work on the almanach, thank you very much for your help indeed. Can I take a look at my book please?",
  "npc.rabaz.say_2": "Yes? Yes! That's the enthusiasm I need! Remember to bring a sharp knife to gather the samples, plants - even mutated deformed plants - are very sensitive you know. Off you go and be careful out there, Zao is no place for the feint hearted mind you.",
  "npc.rabaz.say_3": "Oh, you don't have my book.",
  "npc.sinatuki.stdmod_1": "Chuqua jamjam!! Tiyopa Sinatuki?",
  "npc.sinatuki.say_2": "Jinuma, suvituka siq chuqua!! Nguraka, nguraka! <happily takes the food from you and gives you five glimmering crystals>",
  "npc.sinatuki.say_3": "Jinuma, suvituka siq chuqua!! Nguraka, nguraka! <happily takes the food from you>",
  "npc.sinatuki.say_4": "Kisavuta! <giggles>",
  "npc.sandra.say_1": "We have a special offer right now for depositing vials. Are you interested in hearing it?",
  "npc.sandra.say_2": "Would you like to get a lottery ticket instead of the deposit for your vials?",
  "npc.sandra.say_3": "Are you here to claim a prize?",
  "npc.sandra.say_4": "Pssht, not that loud. So they have sent you to get... the stuff?",
  "npc.sandra.say_5": "What?? How dare you?! I am a sorcerer of the most reknown academy on the face of this world. Do you think some lousy pirates could scare me? Get lost! Now! I will have no further dealings with the likes of you!",
  "npc.sandra.say_6": "Great! I've signed you up for our bonus system. From now on, you will have the chance to win the potion belt addon!",
  "npc.sandra.say_7": "Alright, thank you very much! Here is your lottery ticket, good luck. Would you like to deposit more vials that way?",
  "npc.sandra.say_8": "Sorry, but you don't have 100 empty flasks or vials of the SAME kind and thus don't qualify for the lottery. Would you like to deposit the vials you have as usual and receive 5 gold per vial?",
  "npc.sandra.say_9": "Congratulations! Here, from now on you can wear our lovely potion belt as accessory.",
  "npc.sandra.say_10": "Sorry, but you don't have your lottery ticket with you.",
  "npc.sandra.say_11": "Finally. You have no idea how difficult it is to keep something secret here. And you brought me all the crystal coins I demanded?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_1": "Sure, where else. Everyone likes to meet my master, he is a great demon, isn't he? Your name is ...?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_2": "How very interesting. I need to tell that to my master immediately. Please go to my colleagues and ask for Form 356. You will need it in order to proceed.",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_3": "Alright |PLAYERNAME|. Vocation?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_4": "Huhu, please don't hurt me with your ",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_5": "Form 411? You need Form 287 to get that! Do you have it?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_6": "Form 411? You need Form 287 to get that! Do you have it?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_7": "Oh, what a pity. Go see one of my colleagues. I give you the permission to get Form 287. Bye!",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_8": "Great. Here you are. Form 411. Come back anytime you want to talk. Bye.",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat1.say_9": "INCREDIBLE, you did it!! Have fun at Pumin's Domain!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_1": "Hahaha! Grarkharok take cloak from pretty girl. Then ... girl is swan. Grarkharok wants eat but flies away. Grarkharok not understand. Not need cloak, too many feathers. Give cloak to To ... Ta ... Tereban in Edron. Getting shiny coins and meat.",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_2": "Grarkharok already say everything! Not want talk! Go away!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_3": "Hrhrhrhr! Me no fear of human! Me Chief Grarkharok!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_4": "You help?? Human know troll lady for Grarkharok??",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_5": "Found lady for Grarkharok?!? Must be good-looking, hairy lady, yknow! Go find!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_6": "What name of troll lady??",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_7": "Gimme gimme! Yumyumyum! <BUUUURP>.",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_8": "You no have dead frog! Bring dead frog!!! Grarkharok hungry!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_9": "Gimme gimme! Yumyumyum! <BUUUURP>.",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_10": "You no have tasty snake! Bring tasty snake!!! Grarkharok hungry!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_11": "|PLAYERNAME|?!? Sound good! Bring troll lady to Grarkharok!! Here, give troll lady! Take take! Bring lady to Grarkharok for make tribe!! Now GO!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_12": "Have dead frog for Grarkharok??",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_13": "Have tasty snake for Grarkharok??",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_14": "Grarkharok angry now!! Want throw rock on human cave down hill again!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.say_15": "Huh?? No understand!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_16": "Me tribe in production! Only need troll lady!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_17": "Me no nothing! Need all money to make Grarkharok tribe!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_18": "Grarkharok like BOOM, BOOM sound! Go mountain, push rock and BOOM!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_19": "Like it?? Hope troll lady also like it!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_20": "Me no like human. Need quiet to make tribe! Only need troll lady!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_21": "Yeye, me stole chief club from Fragratosh, hrhrhrh! Now make me own tribe!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_22": "Fragratosh stupid. He chief of me old tribe. No frogs, no snakes, no smashing humans withrocks. Booooooring tribe! Now me make own tribe!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_23": "Grarkharok no listen to talk of stinky human! Lalalalalala! Like song? Grarkharok made!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_24": "You have what want! Go go, find lady so be Grarkharok tribe!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_25": "Me be Grarkharok!!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_26": "You say troll speak!! Hmmm, sound like south tribe! You know Ingortrak ?? He chief of big tribe in jungle! Good chief he is!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_27": "I Tem?!?!? No know! Maybe YOU Tem?",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_28": "Me be Grarkharok. No me name Job!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_29": "Tribe Grarkharok will rules Tibia! Me only need troll lady, then start tribe!",
  "npc.chief_grarkharok.stdmod_30": "Grarkharok destroy human cave down hill! Human away, my mission done,hrhrhrhrhr!",
  "npc.gnomelvis.say_1": "I'm the gnomish {musical} supervisor!",
  "npc.gnomelvis.say_2": "What you have to do is to find your soul melody. Use the harmonic crystals to deduce your soul melody. Every soul melody consists of seven sound sequences. ...",
  "npc.gnomelvis.say_3": "You will have to figure out your correct soul melody by trial and error.",
  "npc.gnomelvis.say_4": "Congratulations on finding your soul melody.",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_1": "Deep in the Tiquandian jungle a monster lurks which is seldom seen. It is the revenge of the jungle against humankind. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_2": "This monster, if slain, carries a rare root called Mandrake. If you find it, bring it to me. Also, gather 5 of the voodoo dolls used by the mysterious dworc voodoomasters. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_3": "If you manage to fulfil this task, I will grant you your own staff. Have you understood everything and are ready for this test?",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_4": "The dworcs of Tiquanda like to wear certain tribal masks which I would like to take a look at. Please bring me 5 of these masks. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_5": "Secondly, the high ape magicians of Banuta use banana staves. I would love to learn more about these staves, so please bring me 5 of them also. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_6": "If you manage to fulfil this task, I will grant you your own mask. Have you understood everything and are ready for this test?",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_7": "Good! Come back once you have collected 5 tribal masks and 5 banana staves.",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_8": "I shall grant you a sign of your progress as shaman if you can fulfil my task.",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_9": "Ohhhhh Mmmmmmmmmmmm Ammmmmgggggggaaaaaaa ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_10": "Aaaaaaaaaahhmmmm Mmmaaaaaaaaaa Kaaaaaamaaaa ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_11": "Brrt! I think it worked! It's a male stampor. I linked this spirit to yours. You can probably already summon him to you ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_12": "So, since we are done here... I need to prepare another ritual, so please let me work, child.",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_13": "I guess I cannot stop you then. Since you told me about my apprentice, it is my turn to help you. I will perform a ritual for you, but I need a few ingredients. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multiline_14": "Bring me one fresh dead chicken, one fresh dead rat and one fresh dead black sheep, in that order.",
  "npc.frosty.stdmod_8": "What about 'no' do you not understand, hrm? You are more annoying than any {percht} around here! Not to mention those bothersome {bunnies} who try to graw away my nose!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_2": "You have nothing to report.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.say_21": "Speak to me again when you are done hunting",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_80": "Well, like I told you before, I really think you got that spirit of a sorcerer in you. But of course it's completely up to you!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_81": "Well, like I told you before, I really think you got that spirit of a druid in you. But of course it's completely up to you!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_82": "Well, like I told you before, I really think you got that spirit of a paladin in you. But of course it's completely up to you!",
  "npc.seymour.stdmod_83": "Well, like I told you before, I really think you got that spirit of a knight in you. But of course it's completely up to you!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.stdmod_18": "I am the governor of this isle, Edron, and grandmaster of the Knights of Banor's Blood.",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.stdmod_19": "LONG LIVE THE KING!",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.stdmod_17": "Here's the situation: a tide of hazardous bugs, the gnomes named them {diremaws}, threatens our base. Then there is some kind of {growth} which seems connected to them somehow. We need to get rid of both.",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.stdmod_18": "Bashsmite. That's all you need to know.",
  "npc.arkulius.stdmod_4": "How dare you asking me this?!? I'm Arkulius - Master of Elements, the HEADMASTER of this academy!!",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.stdmod_1": "Have you noticed that I'm actually the only rock on this island with a proper job? Those lazy pebbleheads! I'm proud to announce: I'm a trader",
  "npc.rock_in_a_hard_place.stdmod_2": "No, you got it all wrong! I said I'm stuck between a rock and a hard place!",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.stdmod_19": "Well, the biggest problem we need to address are the ever charging {subterraneans} around here. And on top of that, there's the threat of the Lost, who quite made themselves at {home} in these parts.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.stdmod_20": "Maintainin' this whole operation, the dwarven involvement 'course. Don't know about them gnomes but if I ain't gettin' those dwarves in line, there'll be chaos down here. I also oversee the {defences} and {counterattacks}.",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.stdmod_21": "Klom Stonecutter's the name. ",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_21": "What addon you are looking? I need for first addon: {dream warden mask} and for second {dream warden claw}.",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_22": "To achieve the first dream addon you need to give me 1 dream warden mask. Do you have them with you?",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_23": "Alright then. Come back when you got all neccessary items.",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_24": "To achieve the second dream addon you need to give me 1 dream warden claw. Do you have them with you?",
  "npc.eruaran.stdmod_25": "Alright then. Come back when you got all neccessary items.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_1": "I was once known as the necromant king. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_2": "For some it was meant as a curse, others used the name with reverence. To me it was just another stepping stone, in a life that burned with ambition.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_3": "My ambitions were high and knew no limits. Mastery over life and death was but a milestone that I wanted to accomplish. In the end I aspired probably somewhat like godhood. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_4": "Though in hindsight even that wouldn't have been enough. There was a hunger in me that nothing could put to rest.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_5": "I was so convinced about my brilliance, my greatness, my destiny. And this hunger for more, it let me not have peace at any point in my life. I was always driven. There was no time to rest. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_6": "And there was no looking back. I never cared to remember my humble beginnings, what I had sacrificed to get where I was. All that I had left behind and that I had lost forever. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_7": "Now I see the bitter irony. I could bring back the dead, but I couldn't create second chances. I couldn't restore the truly important things that I had lost.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_8": "Zarganash was not a place without its dangers, but for a soul as powerful as mine, there was little threat at all. For the first time in my existence I had to stop running forward. I had to wait for things to fit into their places. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_9": "And me, who had seen things that horrible, they would have obliterated a lesser man's mind, finally took the time to look back. And what I saw was frightening in its own right. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_10": "A great tiredness overcame me. With the flames of my ambitions calming down for the first time since I could remember, all my aspirations and plans seemed to petty and futile. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_11": "Everything I had worked for and my plans for the things to come seemed pointless, and the things I had lost and never allowed myself to experience weighed heavily on my soul.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_12": "I talked to other souls, lost in Zarganash, and most of them seemed like mirrors to myself. Their faults, their shortcomings, the things that were important to them and the things they had lost. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_13": "It was all like miniature copies of my own grand plans and losses. It made me think. And the great tiredness weighed even more heavy on me. A weariness of the world, of the hunger that drove me.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_14": "Then I met a wise soul. A teacher that did not lecture. I never was impressed by anything but my own accomplishments. But the inner balance and peace of this soul, it did impress me. A lot. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_15": "I, who fancied myself to have been the epitome of knowledge, learned things that were entirely new to me. But this knowledge wasn't about power. It was about me.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_16": "I decided to stay here, even pass on into the great beyond at some point. Yet I still feel the pull of my fetters. I can faintly hear those who think they are my followers, calling to me.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_17": "And I feel others, many others who crave my powers and try to bring me back for their own gain.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_18": "Over my time in Zarganash I split away the parts of me that my worldly fetters were bound to. Yet I had to recognize that they are still a part of me and I'm bound to them. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_19": "The fetters and the efforts to call me back are empowering them. I feel them growing in strength and gaining awareness on their own. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_20": "They are beginning to feed not only on the fetters and incarnations but also on me. As I grow weaker, they grow more powerful over time.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_21": "You did it! For the first time I can feel free from the pull of my past. Now I'm free at last. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_22": "I might stay a while and teach other souls about the inner peace, but will eventually pass on. Thank you so much, my hero. My eternal gratitude and blessings will be with you!",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_23": "You will have to reach each of the negative parts of my personality that I split away. They are hidden deep in the depths of Zarganash and will have corrupted and twisted their surroundings into dangerous nightmares. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_24": "Even worse, you'll likely encounter minions of those who want to claim my soul as their prize for their own depraved reasons. You will have to destroy my shards to set me free.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_25": "I hated the world for its flaws and the reluctance of people to comply with my will. I was convinced I was destined for greatness and to change everything. Ordinary beings were far beneath me and my consideration. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_26": "All this opposition, all the wars were a nuisance on my way to greatness. I would have sacrificed the whole world to reach my goals.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_27": "Even in the lands of the dead, this one caused a stir. The dead were whispering his name. It made me feel jealous and angry at first, but at some point, after much self-reflection, I could recognize my own faults in the stories about him.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_28": "It was almost like looking into a mirror for the first time. However, he lived way later than me, and I never met his soul here, so I can't tell more about him.",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_29": "They called me the necromant king, in an act of reverence, but to me it was always more of a slander. To limit my greatness to this insignificant aspect was an insult to my ego. But I let it slip for the greater good. ...",
  "npc.flickering_soul.multiline_30": "I felt it was beneath me to correct them and I went along.",
  "npc.angus.say_1": "Do you want to join the explorer society?",
  "npc.angus.say_2": "Oh yes, an interesting topic. We had vivid discussions about this discovery. But what is it that you want?",
  "npc.angus.say_3": "You bring up this topic again? I don't think our talks make any sense unless you prove that you are a supporter of science. Do you have some proof for your dedication to science?",
  "npc.angus.say_4": "A whole new land is indeed very tempting. I can hardly imagine all the wonders that await us there. I doubt I could stop our explorers from going there even if I tried to.",
  "npc.angus.say_5": "For all I've heard, this is rather a barren isle than a whole new land. There are so many places to explore in this world, I won't send our best explorers on account of a rumour.",
  "npc.angus.say_6": "The missions available for your rank are the {butterfly hunt}, {plant collection} and {ice delivery}.",
  "npc.angus.say_7": "The missions available for your rank are {lizard urn}, {bonelord secrets} and {orc powder}.",
  "npc.angus.say_8": "The missions available for your rank are {elven poetry}, {memory stone} and {rune writings}.",
  "npc.angus.say_9": "The explorer society needs a great deal of help in the research of astral travel. Are you willing to help?",
  "npc.angus.say_10": "Do you have some collected ectoplasm with you?",
  "npc.angus.say_11": "The research on ectoplasm makes good progress. Now we need some spectral article. Our scientists think a spectral dress would be a perfect object for their studies ...",
  "npc.angus.say_12": "Have you acquired the spectral dress we need?",
  "npc.angus.say_13": "With the objects you've provided our researchers will make steady progress. Still we are missing some test results from fellow explorers ...",
  "npc.angus.say_14": "Oh, yes! Tell our fellow explorer that the papers are in the mail already.",
  "npc.angus.say_15": "The reports from Northport have already arrived here and our progress is astonishing. We think it is possible to create an astral bridge between our bases. Are you interested to assist us with this?",
  "npc.angus.say_16": "Did you get the requested pickaxe from Uzgod in Kazordoon?",
  "npc.angus.say_17": "Our finest minds came up with the theory that deep beneath the ice island of Folda ice can be found that is ancient. To prove this theory we would need a sample of the aforesaid ice ...",
  "npc.angus.say_18": "Did you get the ice we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_19": "The mission asks you to collect some species of butterflies, are you interested?",
  "npc.angus.say_20": "Did you acquire the purple butterfly we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_21": "This preparation kit will allow you to collect a blue butterfly you have killed ...",
  "npc.angus.say_22": "Did you acquire the blue butterfly we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_23": "This preparation kit will allow you to collect a red butterfly you have killed ...",
  "npc.angus.say_24": "Did you acquire the red butterfly we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_25": "In this mission we require you to get us some plant samples from Tiquandan plants. Would you like to fulfil this mission?",
  "npc.angus.say_26": "Did you acquire the sample of the jungle bells plant we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_27": "Use this botanist's container on a witches cauldron to collect a sample for us. Bring it here and report about your plant collection.",
  "npc.angus.say_28": "Did you acquire the sample of the witches cauldron we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_29": "Use this botanist's container on a giant jungle rose to obtain a sample for us. Bring it here and report about your plant collection.",
  "npc.angus.say_30": "Did you acquire the sample of the giant jungle rose we are looking for?",
  "npc.angus.say_31": "The explorer society would like to acquire an ancient urn which is some sort of relic to the lizard people of Tiquanda. Would you like to accept this mission?",
  "npc.angus.say_32": "Did you manage to get the ancient urn?",
  "npc.angus.say_33": "Have you found any proof that the pyramid was built by bonelords?",
  "npc.angus.say_34": "It is commonly known that orcs of Uldereks Rock use some sort of powder to increase the fierceness of their war wolves and berserkers ...",
  "npc.angus.say_35": "Did you acquire some of the orcish powder?",
  "npc.angus.say_36": "Did you acquire a copy of 'Songs of the Forest' for us?",
  "npc.angus.say_37": "Were you able to acquire a memory stone for our society?",
  "npc.angus.say_38": "Did you create a copy of the ancient runes as requested?",
  "npc.angus.say_39": "We will see if you can handle this simple task. Get the pickaxe from Uzgod in Kazordoon and bring it to one of our bases. Report there about the pickaxe.",
  "npc.angus.say_40": "Excellent, you brought just the tool we need! Of course it was only a simple task. However ...",
  "npc.angus.say_41": "So listen please: Take this ice pick and use it on a block of ice in the caves beneath Folda. Get some ice and bring it here as fast as you can ...",
  "npc.angus.say_42": "Just in time. Sadly not much ice is left over but it will do. Thank you again.",
  "npc.angus.say_43": "*Sigh* I think the time is right to grant you another chance to get that ice. Hurry up this time.",
  "npc.angus.say_44": "This preparation kit will allow you to collect a purple butterfly you have killed ...",
  "npc.angus.say_45": "A little bit battered but it will do. Thank you! If you think you are ready, ask for another butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.angus.say_46": "A little bit battered but it will do. Thank you! If you think you are ready, ask for another butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.angus.say_47": "That is an extraordinary species you have brought. Thank you! That was the last butterfly we needed.",
  "npc.angus.say_48": "Fine! Here take this botanist's container. Use it on a jungle bells plant to collect a sample for us. Report about your plant collection when you have been successful.",
  "npc.angus.say_49": "I see. It seems you've got some quite useful sample by sheer luck. Thank you! Just tell me when you are ready to continue with the plant collection.",
  "npc.angus.say_50": "Ah, finally. I started to wonder what took you so long. But thank you! Another fine sample, indeed. Just tell me when you are ready to continue with the plant collection.",
  "npc.angus.say_51": "What a lovely sample! With that you have finished your plant collection missions.",
  "npc.angus.say_52": "You have indeed the spirit of an adventurer! In the south-east of Tiquanda is a small settlement of the lizard people ...",
  "npc.angus.say_53": "Yes, that is the prized relic we have been looking for so long. You did a great job, thank you.",
  "npc.angus.say_54": "Excellent! So travel to the city of Darashia and then head north-east for the pyramid ...",
  "npc.angus.say_55": "You did it! Excellent! The scientific world will be shaken by this discovery!",
  "npc.angus.say_56": "You are a brave soul. As far as we can tell, the orcs maintain some sort of training facility in some hill in the north-east of their city ...",
  "npc.angus.say_57": "You really got it? Amazing! Thank you for your efforts.",
  "npc.angus.say_58": "Excellent. This mission is easy but nonetheless vital. Travel to Ab'Dendriel and get the book.",
  "npc.angus.say_59": "Let me have a look! Yes, that's what we wanted. A copy of 'Songs of the Forest'. I won't ask any questions about those bloodstains.",
  "npc.angus.say_60": "In the ruins of north-western Edron you should be able to find a memory stone. Good luck.",
  "npc.angus.say_61": "A flawless memory stone! Incredible! It will take years even to figure out how it works but what an opportunity for science, thank you!",
  "npc.angus.say_62": "Excellent! Here, take this tracing paper and use it on the object you will find there to create a copy of the ancient runes.",
  "npc.angus.say_63": "It's a bit wrinkled but it will do. Thanks again.",
  "npc.angus.say_64": "Good! Take this container and use it on a ghost that was recently slain. Return with the collected ectoplasm and hand me that container ...",
  "npc.angus.say_65": "Don't lose the container. They are expensive!",
  "npc.angus.say_66": "Phew, I had no idea that ectoplasm would smell that ... oh, it's you, well, sorry. Thank you for the ectoplasm.",
  "npc.angus.say_67": "Just in time! With this spectral article we can start the final phase of our research.",
  "npc.angus.say_68": "Good, just take this spectral essence and use it on the strange carving in this building as well as on the corresponding tile in our base at Northport ...",
  "npc.angus.say_69": "Poor Ratha. Thank you for returning this skull to the society. We will see to a honourable burial of Ratha.",
  "npc.angus.say_70": "Come back when you find any information.",
  "npc.angus.say_71": "Marvellous! You brought a giant smith hammer for the explorer society!",
  "npc.angus.say_72": "No you don't.",
  "npc.angus.say_73": "What a strange map. I wonder if any of our explorers recognises this coastal lines. However, you earned yourself another chance to convince me. Why do you think that Farmine would be interesting for us?",
  "npc.angus.say_74": "It's always a sad day when we learn about the death of a member. But at least we learnt about his fate. Thank you, here is your reward.",
  "npc.angus.say_75": "Did it melt away?",
  "npc.angus.say_76": "Come back when you find any information.",
  "npc.angus.say_77": "Come back when you find one.",
  "npc.angus.say_78": "The explorer society is looking for a genuine giant smith hammer for our collection. It is rumoured the cyclopses of the Plains of Havoc might be using one. Did you by chance obtain such a hammer?",
  "npc.angus.say_79": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.huntsman.say_1": "I hunt game of all sorts to earn a living. I respect the {balance} of nature though and take only as much as I need.",
  "npc.huntsman.say_2": "She is a bit overly concerned about that nature and balance stuff but she has a good heart. She is living in the woods between Carlin and Ab'Dendriel. I'll mark her hut on your map.",
  "npc.huntsman.say_3": "The white deer are somewhat sacred to the elves. Though their fur and antlers are rumoured to earn a decent amount of {gold} on the market, it's probably not worth the trouble.",
  "npc.huntsman.say_4": "Just between you and me, I heard a guy named {Cruleo} is offering some handsome cash for the trophies of a white deer.",
  "npc.huntsman.say_5": "He has a house in the wilderness. Just between Ab'Dendriel and the orcland. I'll mark his hut on your map.",
  "npc.huntsman.stdmod_6": "I'm just a simple {huntsman}.",
  "npc.huntsman.stdmod_7": "Sorry, I don't think telling a stranger your name is a smart thing to do.",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_1": "A bill? Oh boy so you are delivering another bill to poor me?",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_2": "Ok, ok, I'll take it. I guess I have no other choice anyways. And now leave me alone in my misery please.",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_3": "Uh? What do you want?!",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_4": "What? My hat?? Theres... nothing special about it!",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_5": "Stop bugging me about that hat, do you listen?",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_6": "Hey! Don't touch that hat! Leave it alone!!! Don't do this!!!!",
  "npc.a_strange_fellow.say_7": "Noooooo! Argh, ok, ok, I guess I can't deny it anymore, I am David Brassacres, the magnificent, so what do you want?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_1": "You bringing me draconian steel and obsidian lance in exchange for obsidian knife?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_2": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.uzgod.say_3": "You don't have these items.",
  "npc.uzgod.say_4": "True dwarven pickaxes having to be maded by true weaponsmith! You wanting to get pickaxe for explorer society?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_5": "Me don't sell crimson sword.",
  "npc.uzgod.say_6": "You telling me to forge one?! Especially for you? You making fun of me?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_7": "You got me brooch?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_8": "Me order book quite full is. But telling you what: You getting me something me lost and Uzgod seeing that your pickaxe comes first. Jawoll! You interested?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_9": "Good good. You listening: Me was stolen valuable heirloom. Brooch from my family. Good thing is criminal was caught. Bad thing is, criminal now in dwarven prison of dwacatra is and must have taken brooch with him ...",
  "npc.uzgod.say_10": "To get into dwacatra you having to get several keys. Each key opening way to other key until you get key to dwarven prison ...",
  "npc.uzgod.say_11": "Last key should be in the generals quarter near armory. Only General might have key to enter there too. But me not knowing how to enter Generals private room at barracks. You looking on your own ...",
  "npc.uzgod.say_12": "When got key, then you going down to dwarven prison and getting me that brooch. Tell me that you got brooch when having it.",
  "npc.uzgod.say_13": "Thanking you for brooch. Me guessing you now want your pickaxe?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_14": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.uzgod.say_15": "Ah, that's how me like me customers. Ok, me do this... <pling pling> ... another fine swing of the hammer here and there... <ploing>... here you have it!",
  "npc.uzgod.say_16": "Well. Thinking about it, me a smith, so why not. 1000 gold for your personal crimson sword. Ok?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_17": "Too expensive?! You think me work is cheap? Well, if you want cheap, I can make cheap. Hrmpf. I make cheap sword for 300 gold. Ok?",
  "npc.uzgod.say_18": "Cheap but good quality? Impossible. Unless... you bring material. Three iron ores, 250 gold. Okay?",
  "npc.a_dead_bureaucrat2.say_1": "Sure, you can get it from me. Here you are. Bye",
  "npc.gail.say_1": "I always feared that I lost her. And yet, all those years, I still had a gleam of hope. I'm devastated to learn about her fate - but at least I have certainty now. Thank you for telling me.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_1": "So you don't know it yet. This island, Grimvale, is affected by were-sickness. Many {pitiful}, who are stricken with the curse, dwell in the {tunnels} and caverns underneath the village and the nearby hurst.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_2": "Yes, pitiful. For they are savage beasts now who regularly come up from below to attack the village. But once they were inhabitants of Grimvale, before they {changed}.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_3": "Through a bite or even a scratch, you may be infected with the were-sickness. If that happens, there is little {hope} - until the next full moon you'll change into a were-creature, depending on the animal that hurt you.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_4": "There is a plant, the purple nightshade. It blossoms exclusively in the light of the full moon and only underground, where the full moon's light is falling through fissures in the surface. Only this plant's blossoms are able to defeat the {were-sickness}.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_5": "There are old legends about a subterranean temple that was once built in this area. Supposedly many {artefacts} are still hidden down there. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.say_6": "Yes, the story goes that there are ancient artefacts still hidden in the temple ruins, such as helmets in the form of wolven heads, for example. It is said that moonlight crystals are needed to enchant these artefacts.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_7": "Three of these blossoms should suffice to heal some afflicted persons. But if you bring more I'd be grateful, of course.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_8": "My name is Maeryn.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_9": "Yes, that's me.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_10": "I'm the protector of this little village. A bit of a self-proclaimed function, I admit, but someone has to watch over {Grimvale}. It is a {dangerous} place.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_11": "The small island you are standing on. For a long time it was a peaceful and placid place. But lately it has become more {dangerous}.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_12": "He's an experienced hunter and knows much about the woods, the animals that dwell there, and about the {werewolves}. He's devoted himself to finding out everything there is to know about the {Curse}.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_13": "Yes, my friend, werewolves. They dwell here on {Grimvale}, threatening our life. The were-sickness transforms peaceful villagers into savage beasts. We're not sure how this curse found its way into our small village. But undoubtedly it did.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_14": "She's an old druid. She's been living here on {Grimvale} since she was a little girl, just like me. She's very interested in were-creature body parts. If you find any, I'm sure she will love to trade with you.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_15": "He's basically a ferryman nowadays, but I remember when he was our village's leading fisherman. He offers a ferry service between Grimvale and Edron. You must have met him - he sailed you here.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_16": "You brought the wolven helmet, as i see. Do you want to change something?",
  "npc.maeryn.say_17": "So, which profession would you give preference to when enchanting the helmet: {knight}, {sorcerer}, {druid} or {paladin}?",
  "npc.maeryn.say_18": "And what would be your preferred weapon? {Club}, {axe} or {sword}",
  "npc.maeryn.say_19": "So this is your choice. If you want to change it, you will have to come to me again.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_20": "Message when player do not have quest.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_21": "So this is your choice. If you want to change it, you will have to come to me again.",
  "npc.maeryn.say_22": "Message when player do not have quest.",
  "npc.jondrin.say_1": "You already got the Necrometer.",
  "npc.jondrin.say_2": "Indeed I heard you did a good job out there. <sigh> I guess that means I can hand you one of our necrometers. Handle it with care.",
  "npc.haroun.say_1": "Whoa! A human! This is no place for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Go and play somewhere else.",
  "npc.haroun.say_2": "Be greeted, human |PLAYERNAME|. How can a humble djinn be of service?",
  "npc.haroun.say_3": "Do you want to trade Boots of haste for Enchanted Chicken Wing?",
  "npc.haroun.say_4": "Do you want to trade 4 Warrior Helmet for Warrior Sweat?",
  "npc.haroun.say_5": "Do you want to trade 2 Royal Helmet for Fighting Spirit",
  "npc.haroun.say_6": "Do you want to trade 3 Fire Sword for Magic Sulphur",
  "npc.haroun.say_7": "I trade Enchanted Chicken Wing for Boots of Haste, Warrior Sweat for 4 Warrior Helmets, Fighting Spirit for 2 Royal Helmet Magic Sulphur for 3 Fire Swords",
  "npc.haroun.say_8": "Here you are.",
  "npc.haroun.say_9": "Sorry but you don't have the item.",
  "npc.haroun.say_10": "Ok then.",
  "npc.haroun.say_11": "I'm sorry, human. But you need Gabel's permission to trade with me.",
  "npc.marvin.say_1": "You can't vote yet.",
  "npc.marvin.say_2": "How many of your x votes do you want to cast?",
  "npc.marvin.say_3": "Did I get that right: You want to cast 1 of your votes on funding the {archives}?",
  "npc.marvin.say_4": "Thanks, you successfully cast your vote. Feel free to continue gathering votes by helping the city! Farewell.",
  "npc.elathriel.say_1": "Here it is.",
  "npc.elathriel.say_2": "Come back when you have enough money.",
  "npc.elathriel.say_3": "Believe me, it's better for you that way.",
  "npc.barry.say_1": "Oh my, where to begin with .. <tells about the troubles he and his men have recently encountered>.",
  "npc.barry.say_2": "You can {pass} either to the {Magician Quarter} or {Sunken Quarter}. Which one will it be?",
  "npc.tarak_inner.say_1": "Do you want to travel to the {monument tower} for a 50 gold fee?",
  "npc.tarak_inner.say_2": "You don't have enought money.",
  "npc.carina.say_1": "Would you like to buy my precious necklace for 5000 gold?",
  "npc.carina.say_2": "Wha ... What??? Are you saying you've seen a mouse here??",
  "npc.carina.say_3": "Here you go kind sir.",
  "npc.carina.say_4": "There is no mouse here! Stop talking foolish things about serious issues!",
  "npc.carina.say_5": "IIIEEEEEK!",
  "npc.carina.say_6": "Thank goodness!",
  "npc.zebron.say_1": "Hmmm, would you like to play for {money} or for a chance to win your own {dice}?",
  "npc.zebron.say_2": "I am sorry, but you don't have so much money.",
  "npc.zebron.say_3": "Ok, here we go ... ",
  "npc.zebron.say_4": "Ok, here we go ... 6! You have won a dice, congratulations. One more game?",
  "npc.zebron.say_5": "So you care for a civilized game of dice?",
  "npc.zebron.say_6": "I thought so. Okay, I will roll a dice. If it shows 6, you will get five times your bet. How much do you want to bet?",
  "npc.zebron.say_7": "Hehe, good choice. Okay, the price for this game is 100 gold pieces. I will roll a dice. If I roll a 6, you can have my dice. Agreed?",
  "npc.zebron.say_8": "I am sorry, but I accept only bets between 1 and 99 gold. I don't want to ruin you after all. How much do you want to bet?",
  "npc.zebron.say_9": "I am sorry, but you don't have so much money.",
  "npc.zebron.say_10": "Ok, here we go ... ",
  "npc.zebron.say_11": "Ok, here we go ... 6! You have won ",
  "npc.zebron.say_12": "Oh come on, don't be a child.",
  "npc.harlow.say_1": "What the heck, stop bothering me with your questions.",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_2": "So you are saying you're looking for someone to take you to Vengoth?",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_3": "Oh well.",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_4": "I could do that, it's not far from here. I don't run a charity organisation, though. Tell you what. Give me 100 gold pieces, and me and my boat are yours for the trip. Okay?",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_5": "Oh well.",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_6": "Want me to bring you to Vengoth again for 100 gold?",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_7": "Oh well.",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_8": "I have a {job}, you know?",
  "npc.harlow.stdmod_9": "Well, I'm kind of a delivery man I guess. I take on small {transportation} jobs with my boat.",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.say_1": "Harharhar, landlubber, no no!! The correct command would be STRAIGHT. Remember that! Next, what you gonna say when you see something to left?",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.say_2": "Harharhar, landlubber, ya got it all wrong!! The correct command would be LARBOARD side. Don't forget that, 'kay? Last one, what you gonna say to me when ya see somethin' to the right?",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.say_3": "IS THAT ALL?!? SPEED UP, TIGHTEN THE MAINSAIL!!!",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.say_4": "Already got enough, huh? I kind o' expected that, landlubber! Let's head for Svargrond! Ready?",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.say_5": "Y' already wanna give up?? I should've known. I bring ya back to Svargrond, 'kay?",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.stdmod_6": "I'd go by myself and tear that beast's heart out if I were younger. I hope ya can do that for me. Now go and good luck to ya!",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.stdmod_7": "Ya're a coward, aren't ya? Prove that I'm wrong and get your lazy bones up to the lookout!!",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.stdmod_8": "Just ask me for a trade if you need a bait.",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.stdmod_9": "I can give ya a challenge to test if ya have the guts to be a real sailor. Go up to the lookout and remain there for 24 hours during a storm! Harharhar!",
  "npc.pukosch.say_1": "Do you want to purchase a weekly ticket for the ore wagons? With it you can travel freely and swiftly through Kazordoon for one week. 250 gold only. Deal?",
  "npc.pukosch.say_2": "Your weekly ticket is still valid. Would be a waste of money to purchase a second one",
  "npc.pukosch.say_3": "Here is your stamp. It can't be transferred to another person and will last one week from now. You'll get notified upon using an ore wagon when it isn't valid anymore.",
  "npc.pukosch.say_4": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.pukosch.say_5": "No then.",
  "npc.tereban_functions.say_1": "You are not on that mission.",
  "npc.tereban_functions.say_2": "Well, I need the parts of a sorcerer's robe, a paladin's bow, a knight's shield, and a druid's rod. If you cannot find one of them, ask me about it and I might provide you with some minor hints.",
  "npc.tereban_functions.say_3": "Thank you for your help!",
  "npc.tereban_functions.say_4": "I am relieved someone as capable as you will handle the task. Well, I need the parts of a sorcerer's robe, a paladin's bow, a knight's shield, and a druid's wand.",
  "npc.tereban_functions.say_5": "Oh my. I really hope you will change your mind.",
  "npc.rashid.say_1": "Well, you could attempt the mission to become a recognised trader, but it requires a lot of travelling. Are you willing to try?",
  "npc.rashid.say_2": "Have you managed to obtain a rare deer trophy for my customer?",
  "npc.rashid.say_3": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid.say_4": "Did you bring me the package?",
  "npc.rashid.say_5": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid.say_6": "Have you brought the cheese?",
  "npc.rashid.say_7": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid.say_8": "Have you brought the vase?",
  "npc.rashid.say_9": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid.say_10": "Have you brought a cheap but good crimson sword?",
  "npc.rashid.say_11": "So, my friend, are you willing to proceed to the next mission to become a recognised trader?",
  "npc.rashid.say_12": "Have you brought me a gold fish??",
  "npc.rashid.say_13": "Ah, right. <ahem> I hereby declare you - one of my recognised traders! Feel free to offer me your wares, just ask me for a {trade}!",
  "npc.rashid.say_14": "Fine. Then get a hold of that deer trophy and bring it to me while I'm in Svargrond. Just ask me about your mission.",
  "npc.rashid.say_15": "Well done! I'll take that from you. <snags it> Come see me another day, I'll be busy for a while now. ",
  "npc.rashid.say_16": "Fine. Then off you go, just ask Willard about the 'package for Rashid'.",
  "npc.rashid.say_17": "Great. Just place it over there - yes, thanks, that's it. Come see me another day, I'll be busy for a while now. ",
  "npc.rashid.say_18": "Okay, then please find Miraia in Darashia and ask her about the {'scarab cheese'}.",
  "npc.rashid.say_19": "Mmmhh, the lovely odeur of scarab cheese! I really can't understand why most people can't stand it. Thanks, well done! ",
  "npc.rashid.say_20": "Okay, then please find {Briasol} in {Ab'Dendriel} and ask for a {'fine vase'}.",
  "npc.rashid.say_21": "I'm surprised that you managed to bring this vase without a single crack. That was what I needed to know, thank you. ",
  "npc.rashid.say_22": "Okay, I'm curious how you will do with {Uzgod}. Good luck!",
  "npc.rashid.say_23": "Ha! You are clever indeed, well done! I'll take this from you. Come see me tomorrow, I think we two might get into business after all.",
  "npc.rashid.say_24": "Thanks so much! I'll be waiting eagerly for your return then.",
  "npc.rashid.say_25": "Thank you!! Ah, this makes my day! I'll take the rest of the day off to get to know this little guy. Come see me tomorrow, if you like.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_26": "I am a travelling trader. I don't buy everything, though. And not from everyone, for that matter.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_27": "I am Rashid, son of the desert.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_28": "Of course, old friend. You can also browse only armor, legs, shields, helmets, boots, weapons, enchanted weapons, jewelry or miscellaneous stuff.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_29": "Elves... I don't really trust them. All this talk about nature and flowers and treehugging... I'm sure there's some wicked scheme behind all this.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_30": "My beloved hometown! Ah, the sweet scent of the desert sands, the perfect shape of the pyramids... stunningly beautiful.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_31": "I have to go to Carlin once in a while, since the queen wishes to see my exclusive wares in regular intervals.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_32": "Cormaya? Not a good place to make business, it's way too far and small.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_33": "It's not the real thing, but almost as good. The merchants there claim ridiculous prices, which is fine for my own business.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_34": "Ah yes, Edron! Such a lovely and quiet island! I usually make some nice business there.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_35": "Too few customers there, it's not worth the trip.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_36": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_37": "I don't like being underground much. I also tend to get lost in these labyrinthine dwarven tunnels, so I rather avoid them.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_38": "When you avoid the slums, it's a really pretty city. Almost as pretty as the governor's daughter.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_39": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_40": "I like the settlement itself, but I don't set my foot into the jungle. Have you seen the size of these centipedes??",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_41": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_42": "I wish it was a little bit warmer there, but with a good mug of barbarian mead in your tummy everything gets a lot cosier.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_43": "I feel uncomfortable and rather unsafe in Thais, so I don't really travel there.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_44": "Um... I don't think so.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_45": "Although it's the flourishing trade centre of Tibia, I don't like going there. Too much competition for my taste.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_46": "It's almost time to journey on.",
  "npc.rashid.stdmod_47": "Kings, queens, emperors and kaliphs... everyone claims to be different and unique, but actually it's the same thing everywhere.",
  "npc.rashid.say_48": "Sorry, but you do not belong to my exclusive customers. I have to make sure that I can trust in the quality of your wares.",
  "npc.kroox.say_1": "Hm, well I guess its ok to tell you ... <tells you about Lokurs measurements> ",
  "npc.roswitha.say_1": "I'm sorry, but Harsin no longer lives here. He ordered a local named Quandon to transport all his stuff somewhere. I don't know where he moved, but Quandon should be able to help you with this information.",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_1": "I'd love to bring you back to Liberty Bay, but as you can see, my ship is ruined. I also hurt my leg and can barely move. Can you help me?",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_2": "Have you brought 30 pieces of wood so that I can repair the ship?",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_3": "Do you want to travel back to Liberty Bay?",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_4": "Good! Please return once you have gathered 30 pieces of wood.",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_5": "Excellent! Now we can leave this godforsaken place. Thank you for your help. Should you ever want to return to this island, ask me for a passage to Goroma.",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_6": "You don't have enough...",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.say_7": "Set the sails!",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.stdmod_8": "My name is Jack Fate from the Royal Tibia Line.",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.stdmod_9": "I'm the captain of this - well, wreck. Argh.",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.stdmod_10": "I'm the captain of this - well, wreck. Argh",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.stdmod_11": "This is where we are... the volcano island Goroma. There are many rumours about this place.",
  "npc.partos.say_1": "I won't talk about that.",
  "npc.partos.stdmod_2": "You mean that's a JAIL? They told me it's the finest hotel in town! THAT explains the lousy roomservice!",
  "npc.partos.stdmod_3": "You mean that's a JAIL? They told me it's the finest hotel in town! THAT explains the lousy roomservice!",
  "npc.partos.stdmod_4": "You mean that's a JAIL? They told me it's the finest hotel in town! THAT explains the lousy roomservice!",
  "npc.kazzan.say_1": "WAAAAAHHH!!!",
  "npc.kazzan.say_2": "Feel welcome in the lands of the children of the enlightened Daraman, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.kazzan.say_3": "Do you know the location of the djinn fortresses in the mountains south of here?",
  "npc.kazzan.say_4": "Well, I don't blame you for that. I am sure you did your best. Now we can just hope that peace remains. Here, take this small gratification for your effort to help and Daraman may bless you!",
  "npc.liane.say_1": "I have more urgent problem to attend then that. Those hawks are hunting my carrier pigeons. Bring me 12 arrows and I'll see if I have the time for this nonsense. Do you have 12 arrows with you? ",
  "npc.liane.say_2": "Great! Now I'll teach them a lesson ... For those measurements ... <tells you her measurements> ",
  "npc.liane.say_3": "Oh, you don't have it.",
  "npc.corym_ratter.say_1": "Recently the amount of delivered ores is decreasing. Could you find out the reason, why the situation has become worse?",
  "npc.corym_ratter.say_2": "Nice! I have opened the mine for you. But take care of you! The monsters of depth won't spare you.",
  "npc.skjaar.say_1": "I will give the key to the crypt only to the closest followers of my master. Would you like me to test you?",
  "npc.skjaar.say_2": "Before we start I must ask you for a small donation of 1000 gold coins. Are you willing to pay 1000 gold coins for the test?",
  "npc.skjaar.say_3": "All right then. Here comes the first question. What was the name of Dago's favourite pet?",
  "npc.skjaar.say_4": "You don't have enough money",
  "npc.skjaar.say_5": "Perhaps you knew him after all. Tell me - how many fingers did he have when he died?",
  "npc.skjaar.say_6": "Also true. But can you also tell me the colour of the deamons in which master specialized?",
  "npc.skjaar.say_7": "It seems you are worthy after all. Do you want the key to the crypt?",
  "npc.skjaar.say_8": "Here you are",
  "npc.nurik.say_1": "Excuse me, but I'm waiting for someone important!",
  "npc.nurik.say_2": "Wait a minute! Do I get that right? You're the owner of the dwarven bridge and you are willing to sell it to me??",
  "npc.nurik.say_3": "How splendid! Do you have the necessary documents with you?",
  "npc.nurik.say_4": "Oh my, oh my. I'm so excited! So let's seal this deal as fast as possible so I can visit my very own dwarven bridge. Are you ready for the transaction?",
  "npc.gnomus.say_1": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_2": "Come back when you have finished your job.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_3": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_4": "Come back when you have finished your job.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_5": "The other are already telling stories about you. Please return to me later if you want to help out some more!",
  "npc.gnomus.say_6": "I don't need your help for now. Come back later.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_7": "Come back when you have finished your job.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_8": "Thank you very much! With those structures mapped out we will be able to complete the puzzle in no time!",
  "npc.gnomus.say_9": "If you bring me any suspicious devices on creatures you slay down here, I'll make it worth your while by telling the others of your generosity. How many do you want to offer? ",
  "npc.gnomus.say_10": "Don't waste my time.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_11": "Done.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_12": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_13": "Done.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_14": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_15": "Done.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_16": "You don't have enough suspicious devices.",
  "npc.gnomus.say_17": "So you want to know what we all think about your deeds? What leader's opinion are you interested in, the {gnomes} (Gnomus), the {dwarves} (Klom Stonecutter) or the {scouts} (Lardoc Bashsmite)?",
  "npc.gnomus.stdmod_18": "If you're willing to help us, we could need an escort for arriving {ordnance}, help with {charting} the cave system and someone needs to get some heat {measurements} fast.",
  "npc.gnomus.stdmod_19": "My name is Gnomus.",
  "npc.gnomus.stdmod_20": "I'm the main gnomish contact for this base. I coordinate our efforts with those of the dwarves to ensure everything is running smoothly.",
  "npc.dukosch.say_1": "Do you want to purchase a weekly ticket for the ore wagons? With it you can travel freely and swiftly through Kazordoon for one week. 250 gold only. Deal?",
  "npc.dukosch.say_2": "Your weekly ticket is still valid. Would be a waste of money to purchase a second one",
  "npc.dukosch.say_3": "Here is your stamp. It can't be transferred to another person and will last one week from now. You'll get notified upon using an ore wagon when it isn't valid anymore.",
  "npc.dukosch.say_4": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.dukosch.say_5": "No then.",
  "npc.fenech.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.fenech.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.fenech.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_1": "You are searching for the way out? Do you want to go home? Are you homesick, nostalgic, allergic? I am sorry. You will stay. Muhahahaha. Haha. Are you giving up then?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_2": "A what? I don't even know what you're talking about, human. If you aren't just giving up - will you kindly change the topic please?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_3": "Haha, no! No. Why don't you just stop asking me that and start enjoying your stay here?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_4": "Oh, you mean - if I have ever been out of here in those 278 years? Well, I - I can't remember. No, I can't remember. Sorry.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_5": "No, I really can't remember. I enjoyed my stay here so much that I forgot how it looks outside of this hole. Outside. The air, the sky, the light. Oh well... well.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_6": "Oh yes, yes. I... I never really thought about how you creatures feel in here I guess. I... just watched all these beings die here. ...",
  "npc.zumtah.say_7": "Alright, as I said you are free now. There will not be an outside for the next three centuries, but you - go. ...",
  "npc.zumtah.say_8": "It's you, why did they throw you in here again? Anyway, I will just transform you once more. I also recovered your crate which will wait for you at the exit. There, feel free to go.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_9": "I've already told you that you can't get out. What's the problem? Do you even see an exit?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_10": "You are starting to get on my nerves. Is this the only topic you know?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_11": "But there is no escape, I said NO. You've already asked several times and my answer will stay the same. What is this? Are you trying to test me?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_12": "Muhahaha. Where? I can only see a dark cave with nothing than bones and a djinn in it. You mean that small hole there? Muhahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_13": "Pesky, persistent human.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_14": "Muhahaha. Then I will give you a test. How many years do you think have I been here? {89}, {164} or {278}?",
  "npc.zumtah.say_15": "Correct human, and that is not nearly how high you would need to count to tell all the lost souls I've seen dying here. I AM PERPETUAL. Muahahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.say_16": "Wrong answer human! Muahahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_17": "I wait. I wait for someone like you to come here. I wait for them to grow disconsolate. I wait for them to despair. And I wait for them to die. Muhahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_18": "I am Zumtah, Zumtah the impeccable, Zumtah the marvellous, Zumtah the... the... eternal.",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_19": "The land you are currently dwelling in, human. Don't you have any sense of your surroundings?",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_20": "I have seen many of them. I have seen many of them die. In here, with me. Perhaps you will be pleased to meet them. Not long and you will join their ranks. Muhaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_21": "Pesky creatures. Many of them have been brought here, many of them died here. Humans, lizards, beasts, they all die the same. Down here, with me. Muhahaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_22": "What? What do you mean by that?",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_23": "Hmm, an old one. I don't care much about politics or power, as here, he has none. Here, only I have power. Muhaha.",
  "npc.zumtah.stdmod_24": "What are you talking about, such things do not matter down here. Down here alone, isolated and broken. Muhaha.",
  "npc.rose.say_1": "Do you want to buy a Hydra Tongue for 100 gold?",
  "npc.rose.say_2": "Here you are. A Hydra Tongue!",
  "npc.rose.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.rose.say_4": "Then not.",
  "npc.amber.say_1": "Ah, you noticed my new accessory? Sorry, this one is not for sale. It's handmade from rare minotaur leather.",
  "npc.amber.say_2": "Ah, right, almost forgot about the backpack! Have you brought me 100 pieces of minotaur leather as requested?",
  "npc.amber.say_3": "Just in time! Your backpack is finished. Here you go, I hope you like it.",
  "npc.amber.say_4": "Uh... I didn't expect you to return that early. Sorry, but I'm not finished yet with your backpack. I'm doing the best I can, promised.",
  "npc.amber.say_5": "Sorry, but I can only make one backpack per person, else I'd have to close my shop and open a leather manufactory.",
  "npc.amber.say_6": "Well, if you really like this backpack, I could make one for you, but minotaur leather is hard to come by these days. Are you willing to put some work into this?",
  "npc.amber.say_7": "Alright then, if you bring me 100 pieces of fine minotaur leather I will see what I can do for you. You probably have to kill really many minotaurs though... so good luck!",
  "npc.amber.say_8": "Sorry, but I don't run a welfare office, you know... no pain, no gain.",
  "npc.amber.say_9": "Sorry, but that's not enough leather yet to make one of these backpacks. Would you rather like to buy a normal backpack for 10 gold?",
  "npc.amber.say_10": "Great! Alright, I need a while to finish this backpack for you. Come ask me later, okay?",
  "npc.amber.say_11": "I know, it's quite some work... don't lose heart, just keep killing minotaurs and you'll eventually get lucky. Would you rather like to buy a normal backpack for 10 gold?",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.say_1": "So I ask you: What is the name of the princess who fell in love with a Thaian nobleman during the regency of pharaoh Uthemath?",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.say_2": "That's right. Listen to the second question: Who is the author of the book ,The Language of the Wolves'?",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.say_3": "That's right. Listen to the third question: Which ancient Tibian race reportedly travelled the sky in cloud ships?",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.say_4": "That is correct. You satisfactorily answered all questions. You may pass and enter Gelidrazah's lair.",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.say_5": "I don't know what you are talking about.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_1": "Hmm, if you can spare a coin... we can talk. What do you say?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_2": "Persistent little nuisance, aren't we? Well, I like your spirit so I will tell you a secret. I may not look the part but I was once a {scientist}. The academy seemed to not like my... attitude and never actually invited me.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_3": "Indeed, I was one myself a long time ago. I may seem a little... distracted by now, but I was working on many important projects. I even created a device to... well, it will cost you another gold coin if you want me to tell you the whole story. You're in?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_4": "Well, if that is all you can spare... better keep it.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_5": "Alright, it seems you are serious about this. I will tell you about my device. Every night I looked up to the stars and wondered what worlds we would be able to find if we could just look where we wanted to. So... hey are you still listening?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_6": "Good, good. So eventually I found a way and invented a magic device I called the Lightboat. It was a large construction you could sit in and... well, judging by your looks you don't believe a word. Do you want to hear the story or not?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_7": "Fine. For years I gathered all the necessary items to build the device. I travelled, traded and took advantage of some rare opportunities. With luck and patience I eventually got every component I needed. Can you imagine the excitement I experienced?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_8": "And there I stood before my greatest invention. Door to unknown places, mysterious worlds... yet one of my components was flawed. A small crack in a vital element of my construction quickly led to the failure of the whole project. Still following?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_9": "The device was ultimately destroyed. I barely escaped the chaos with my life. My laboratory was shattered, as were all the components of the cursed device. With nothing left, I started to lead a new, different life. Do you know what that means?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_10": "Pah!! You have NO idea, leave me alone now.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_11": "Right... I'm glad everything was destroyed. I don't even know why I kept the remaining copy of the plans all those years... oh, did I say this aloud?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_12": "Yes, well... I do have one remaining copy of the plans. I will keep them as a... reminder. Such ill-fated devices only cause trouble and despair. Mankind would be better off, without them, right?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_13": "Ah, you think you are wise but you know nothing, nothing about science, nothing about the opportunities it offers... You will never understand scientists like me.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_14": "Well, to be honest, I envy him a little. He can continue his research in his laboratory. He still has working equipment... I sometimes read his publications. He is an able man, but completely on the wrong track... give these plans to him.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_15": "Mean, heartless... go and leave me be.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_16": "Well, whatever then...",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_17": "Then stop bothering me.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_18": "Your decision.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_19": "Yes and I, I... you mean what? Can't imagine? Well, then there is no purpose to continue telling you this story.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_20": "*mumbles*",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_21": "Thought so. It means starting anew, without any home, money or goal in your life. However, it also opens up opportunities... don't you agree?",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_22": "No, no, you are right, I should have tried to rebuild it, I should have been more careful, I should... ah, why did I even tell you this.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_23": "Phew... alright, it was nice talking to you.",
  "npc.shoddy_beggar.say_24": "Hm, maybe you are right. You could give these plans to someone who might be able to finish this project. Someone who will not make the mistakes I made. Someone... hm, do you know the astronomer Spectulus?",
  "npc.ruprecht.say_1": "So you want to exchange ",
  "npc.ruprecht.say_2": "Thank you, here is your 1 christmas token.",
  "npc.ruprecht.say_3": "You don't have a present bag.",
  "npc.ruprecht.say_4": "Thank you, here is your ",
  "npc.ruprecht.say_5": "You don't have enough of tokens.",
  "npc.ruprecht.say_6": "Come back when you are ready to trade some tokens!",
  "npc.alkestios.say_1": "Uhmn.. Maybe Ahmet in Ankrahmun can help we to fake this book.",
  "npc.alkestios.say_2": "The poachers are still chasing me. Please hurry and find a way to help me.",
  "npc.alkestios.say_3": "You have already started this mission.",
  "npc.alkestios.say_4": "Then not.",
  "npc.alkestios.stdmod_5": "Outside of our secret {realm} my siblings and I can't keep our true shape. If we want to travel other parts of the world, we must take over the bodies of animals. But we are causing them no harm and we just take control if necessary.",
  "npc.alkestios.stdmod_6": "We call it Feyrist and it is a secret, hidden place. Just few mortals get permission to enter it. A long time ago, we learned how to hide our realm from the outside world. Only if you gain our trust I will tell you how to reach it.",
  "npc.alkestios.stdmod_7": "We call ourselves the fae. Some name us nature spirits or peri but we prefer the former term. Most of us are rather reclusive and live peaceful lives in our secret realm. We only leave it in order to {protect} our home. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.stdmod_8": "We call ourselves the fae. Some name us nature spirits or peri but we prefer the former term. Most of us are rather reclusive and live peaceful lives in our secret realm. We only leave it in order to {protect} our home. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.stdmod_9": "I can sense a kind of dark energy lately. It is pervading this world, more and more every day. Yet I don't know where it arises from nor what we could do to dispel it.",
  "npc.alkestios.stdmod_10": "It is rather subversive, so most creatures won't sense it ... yet. But its corrosive power has already begun to affect my kind and our hidden realm in unpleasant ways.",
  "npc.henricus.say_1": "The churches of the gods entrusted me with the enormous and responsible task to lead the inquisition. I leave the field work to inquisitors who I recruit from fitting people that cross my way.",
  "npc.henricus.say_2": "Do you want to join the inquisition?",
  "npc.henricus.say_3": "You cannot get this blessing unless you have completed The Inquisition Quest.",
  "npc.henricus.say_4": "Do you want to buy the special flask of holy water for ",
  "npc.henricus.say_5": "You do not need this flask right now.",
  "npc.henricus.say_6": "Do you want to join the inquisition?",
  "npc.henricus.say_7": "Your current mission is to investigate the reliability of certain guards. Are you done with that mission?",
  "npc.henricus.say_8": "Your current mission is to destroy this coven. Are you done with that mission?",
  "npc.henricus.say_9": "Your current mission is to help the vampire hunter Storkus. Are you done with that mission? ",
  "npc.henricus.say_10": "Your current mission is to exorcise an evil being from a house in Liberty Bay. Are you done with that mission? ",
  "npc.henricus.say_11": "You need 20 of them.",
  "npc.henricus.say_12": "Destroy the shadow nexus using this vial of holy water and kill all demon lords.",
  "npc.henricus.say_13": "Your current mission is to destroy the shadow nexus in the Demon Forge. Are you done with that mission?",
  "npc.henricus.say_14": "So be it. Now you are a member of the inquisition. You might ask me for a {mission} to raise in my esteem.",
  "npc.henricus.say_15": "You haven't done your mission yet.",
  "npc.henricus.say_16": "Good, you've returned. Your skill in practical matters seems to be useful. If you're ready for a further mission, just ask. ",
  "npc.henricus.say_17": "You haven't done your mission with {Storkus} yet.",
  "npc.henricus.say_18": "Well, this was an easy task, but your next mission will be much more challenging. ",
  "npc.henricus.say_19": "You haven't done your mission with {Storkus} yet.",
  "npc.henricus.say_20": "Come back when you have destroyed the shadow nexus.",
  "npc.henricus.say_21": "You already have been blessed!",
  "npc.henricus.say_22": "You have been blessed by all of five gods!, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.henricus.say_23": "Come back when you have enough money.",
  "npc.henricus.say_24": "Here is your new flask!, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.henricus.say_25": "Come back when you have enough money.",
  "npc.henricus.say_26": "Fine, fine. You have proven that you can work efficiently. Still, only further missions will show if you are truly capable. Ask me for another mission if you're ready.",
  "npc.henricus.say_27": "You need bring me the witches' grimoire.",
  "npc.henricus.say_28": "Then no.",
  "npc.henricus.say_29": "Here is your demon hunter outfit. You deserve it. Unlock more addons by completing more missions.",
  "npc.henricus.say_30": "Here is your demon hunter outfit. You deserve it. Unlock more addons by completing more missions.!",
  "npc.henricus.say_31": "Here is the final addon for your demon hunter outfit. Congratulations!",
  "npc.henricus.say_32": "The priests of Fardos are often mystics who have secluded themselves from worldly matters. Others provide guidance and healing to people in need in the temples.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_33": "It's a shame that only a few paladins still use their abilities to further the cause of the gods of good. Too many paladins have become selfish and greedy.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_34": "Nowadays, most knights seem to have forgotten the noble cause to which all knights were bound in the past. Only a few have remained pious, serve the gods and follow their teachings.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_35": "Those who wield great power have to resist great temptations. We have the burden to eliminate all those who give in to the temptations.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_36": "The druids here still follow the old rules. Sadly, the druids of Carlin have left the right path in the last years.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_37": "The dwarfs are allied with Thais but follow their own obscure religion. Although dwarfs keep mostly to themselves, we have to observe this alliance closely.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_38": "The dwarfs are allied with Thais but follow their own obscure religion. Although dwarfs keep mostly to themselves, we have to observe this alliance closely.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_39": "Those elves are hardly any more civilised than orcs. They can become a threat to mankind at any time.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_40": "Those elves are hardly any more civilised than orcs. They can become a threat to mankind at any time.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_41": "Venore is somewhat difficult to handle. The merchants have a close eye on our activities in their city and our authority is limited there. However, we will use all of our influence to prevent a second Carlin.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_42": "Drefia used to be a city of sin and heresy, just like Carlin nowadays. One day, the gods decided to destroy this town and to erase all evil there.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_43": "Darashia is a godless town full of mislead fools. One day, it will surely share the fate of its sister town Drefia.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_44": "Demons exist in many different shapes and levels of power. In general, they are servants of the dark gods and command great powers of destruction.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_45": "Carlin is a city of sin and heresy. After the reunion of Carlin with the kingdom, the inquisition will have much work to purify the city and its inhabitants.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_46": "We can see his evil influence almost everywhere. Keep your eyes open or the dark one will lead you on the wrong way and destroy you.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_47": "The church of Crunor works closely together with the druid guild. This makes a cooperation sometimes difficult.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_48": "We owe to the gods of good our creation and continuing existence. If it weren't for them, we would surely fall prey to the minions of the vile and dark gods.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_49": "The churches of the gods united to fight heresy and dark magic. They are the shield of the true believers, while the inquisition is the sword that fights all enemies of virtuousness.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_50": "The churches of the gods entrusted me with the enormous and responsible task to lead the inquisition. I leave the field work to inquisitors who I recruit from fitting people that cross my way.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_51": "Belive on the gods and they will show you the path.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_52": "By edict of the churches I'm the Lord Inquisitor.",
  "npc.henricus.stdmod_53": "I'm Henricus, the Lord Inquisitor.",
  "npc.kevin.say_1": "You are not a member of our guild yet! We have high standards for our members. To rise in our guild is a difficult but rewarding task. Are you interested in joining?",
  "npc.kevin.say_2": "So you have finally made it! I did not think that you would have it in you ... However: are you ready for another assignment?",
  "npc.kevin.say_3": "Excellent, you got it fixed! This will teach this mailbox a lesson indeed! Are you interested in another assignment?",
  "npc.kevin.say_4": "You truly got him? Quite impressive. You are a very promising candidate! I think I have another mission for you. Are you interested?",
  "npc.kevin.say_5": "Do you bring all bones for our officers' safety fund at once?",
  "npc.kevin.say_6": "Splendid, I knew we could trust you. I would like to ask for your help in another matter. Are you interested?",
  "npc.kevin.say_7": "Once more you have impressed me! Are you willing to do another job?",
  "npc.kevin.say_8": "First you need to complete your current mission.",
  "npc.kevin.say_9": "Excellent! Another job well done! Would you accept another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_10": "Fine, fine. I think that should do it. Tell Hugo that we order those uniforms. The completed dress pattern will soon arrive in Venore. Report to me when you have talked to him.",
  "npc.kevin.say_11": "So Waldo is dead? This is grave news indeed. Did you recover his posthorn?",
  "npc.kevin.say_12": "You did it? I hope you did not catch a flu in the cold! Anyway, there's another mission for you. Are you interested?",
  "npc.kevin.say_13": "You have delivered that letter? You are a true postofficer. All over the land bards shallpraise your name. There are no missions for you left right now.",
  "npc.kevin.say_14": "There are no missions for you left right now. You already have the title of Archpostman.",
  "npc.kevin.say_15": "There are no missions for you left right now. But you are worthy indeed. Do you want to advance in our guild?",
  "npc.kevin.say_16": "So are you ready for another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_17": "So are you ready for another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_18": "So are you ready for another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_19": "Excellent! Another job well done! Would you accept another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_20": "Excellent! Another job well done! Would you accept another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_21": "You have made it! We have enough bones for the fund! You remind me of myself when I was young! Interested in another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_22": "You have made it! We have enough bones for the fund! You remind me of myself when I was young! Interested in another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_23": "You truly got him? Quite impressive. You are a very promising candidate! I think I have another mission for you. Are you interested?",
  "npc.kevin.say_24": "So are you ready for another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_25": "So are you ready for another mission?",
  "npc.kevin.say_26": "Oh yes, where did we get that from ...? Let's see, first ask the great technomancer in Kazordoon for the technical details. Return here afterwards.",
  "npc.kevin.say_27": "The mail with Talphion's instructions just arived. I remember we asked Queen Eloise of Carlin for the perfect colours. Go there, ask her about the UNIFORMS and report back here.",
  "npc.kevin.say_28": "The queen has sent me the samples we needed. The next part is tricky. We need theuniforms to emanate some odor that dogs hate.The dog with the best 'taste' in that field is Noodles,the dog of King Tibianus. Do you understand so far?",
  "npc.kevin.say_29": "Fine, fine. I think that should do it. Tell Hugo that we order those uniforms. The completed dress pattern will soon arrive in Venore. Report to me when you have talked to him.",
  "npc.kevin.say_30": "You are worthy indeed. Do you want to advance in our guild?",
  "npc.kevin.say_31": "You are worthy indeed. Do you want to advance in our guild?",
  "npc.kevin.say_32": "You are worthy indeed. Do you want to advance in our guild?",
  "npc.kevin.say_33": "You are worthy indeed. Do you want to advance in our guild?",
  "npc.kevin.say_34": "Hm, I might consider your proposal, but first you will have to prove your worth by doing some tasks for us. Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.kevin.say_35": "Excellent! Your first task will be quite simple. But you should better write my instructions down anyways. You can read and write?",
  "npc.kevin.say_36": "So listen, you will check certain tours our members have to take to see if there is some trouble. First travel with Captain Bluebear's ship from Thais to Carlin, understood?",
  "npc.kevin.say_37": "Excellent! Once you have done that you will travel with Uzon to Edron. You will find him in the Femor Hills. Understood?",
  "npc.kevin.say_38": "Fine, fine! Next, travel with Captain Seahorse to the city of Venore. Understood?",
  "npc.kevin.say_39": "Good! Finally, find the technomancer Brodrosch and travel with him to the Isle of Cormaya. After this passage report back to me here. Understood?",
  "npc.kevin.say_40": "Ok, remember: the Tibian mail service puts trust in you! Don't fail and report back soon. Just tell me about your {mission}.",
  "npc.kevin.say_41": "I am glad to hear that. One of our mailboxes was reported to be jammed. It is located on the so called 'mountain' on theisle Folda. Get a crowbar and fix the mailbox. Report about your mission when you have done so.",
  "npc.kevin.say_42": "For your noble deeds I grant you the title Assistant Postofficer. All Postofficers will charge you less money from now on. After every second mission ask me for an ADVANCEMENT. Your next task will be a bit more challenging. Do you feel ready for it?",
  "npc.kevin.say_43": "I need you to deliver a bill to the stage magician David Brassacres. He's hiding from his creditors somewhere in Venore. It's likely you will have to trick him somehow to reveal his identity. Report back when you delivered this bill.",
  "npc.kevin.say_44": "Ok, listen: we have some serious trouble with agressive dogs lately. We have accumulated some bones as a sort of pacifier but we need more. Collect 20 bones like the one in my room to the left and report here.",
  "npc.kevin.say_45": "You have collected all the 20 bones needed. Excellent! Now let's talk about further missions if you are interested.",
  "npc.kevin.say_46": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.kevin.say_47": "I grant you the title of postman. You are now a full member of our guild. Here have your own officers hat and wear it with pride.",
  "npc.kevin.say_48": "Since I am convinced I can trust you, this time you must deliver a valuable present to Dermot on Fibula. Do NOT open it!!! You will find the present behind the door here on the lower right side of this room.",
  "npc.kevin.say_49": "Ok. We need a new set of uniforms, and only the best will do for us. Please travel to Venore and negotiate with Hugo Chief acontract for new uniforms.",
  "npc.kevin.say_50": "Good. Go there and find out what taste he dislikes most: mouldy cheese, a piece of fur or abananaskin. Tell him to SNIFF, then the object. Show him the object and ask 'Do you like that?'.DONT let the guards know what you are doing.",
  "npc.kevin.say_51": "Good, so listen. Hugo Chief informed me that he needs the measurements of our postofficers. Go and bring me the measurements of Ben, Lokur, Dove, Liane, Chrystal and Olrik.",
  "npc.kevin.say_52": "From now on it shall be known that you are a grand postman. You are now a privilegedmember until the end of days. Most captains around the world have an agreement with our guild to transport our privileged members, like you, for less gold.",
  "npc.kevin.say_53": "Ok but your next assignment might be dangerous. Our Courier Waldo has been missing for a while. I must assume he is dead. Can you follow me so far?",
  "npc.kevin.say_54": "Find out about his whereabouts and retrieve him or at least his posthorn. He was looking for a new underground passage that is rumoured to be found underneath the troll-infested Mountain east of Thais.",
  "npc.kevin.say_55": "Thank you. We will honour this. Your next mission will be a very special one. Good thing you are a special person as well. Are you ready?",
  "npc.kevin.say_56": "From now on you are a grand postman for special operations. You are an honoured member of our guild and earned the privilege of your own post horn. Here, take it.",
  "npc.kevin.say_57": "So listen well. Behind the lower left door you will find a bag. The letters in the bag are for none other than Santa Claus! Deliver them to his house on the isle of Vega, {use} thebag on his mailbox and report back here.",
  "npc.kevin.say_58": "Excellent. Here is a letter for you to deliver. Well, to be honest, no one else volunteered. It's a letter from the mother of Markwin, the king of Mintwallin. Deliver that letter to him, but note that you will not be welcome there.",
  "npc.kevin.say_59": "I grant you the title of Archpostman. You are a legend in our guild. As privilege of your newly aquired status you are allowed to make use of certain mailboxes in dangerous areas. Just look out for them and you'll see.",
  "npc.kevin.say_60": "Your eagerness is a virtue, young one, but first let's talk about advancement",
  "npc.farhilorn_of_the_winter_court.say_1": "We allow able champions of all races to fight for our cause against the challenges of the {arena}. So are you interested? I'm not interested in fancy'wordplay, so a simple {yes} or {no} will suffice!",
  "npc.farhilorn_of_the_winter_court.say_2": "You are now able to enter the teleport.",
  "npc.farhilorn_of_the_winter_court.say_3": "As you wish.",
  "npc.farhilorn_of_the_winter_court.say_4": "This place has always been a site where the champions of summer and winter have clashed in battle. Over the centuries this spectacle has drawn many creatures here to watch, participate and indulge in less savory activities.",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.say_1": "Why are you asking, he didn't get himself into something again did he?",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.say_2": "Spelltolust?! That sounds awfully nasty! What was he doing there - are you telling me he lived an alternate life and he didn't even tell {mother}?",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.say_3": "What?! And what did he do there? Who did he visit there?",
  "npc.iskan.say_1": "So, do you want a passage to Nibelor my friend?",
  "npc.iskan.say_2": "Do you want to Nibelor?",
  "npc.iskan.say_3": "You are a friend of mine and the boys now. I tell you something. If you ever need to go to the isle of Nibelor, just ask me for a {passage}.",
  "npc.iskan.say_4": "I have now no mission for you.",
  "npc.iskan.say_5": "Sorry but I only give missions to those who are considered a true Barbarian. ",
  "npc.iskan.say_6": "Alright, we are even!",
  "npc.iskan.say_7": "You don't have enough. Bring me the money and I will forget about it.",
  "npc.iskan.say_8": "Sorry, first time you have to do a mission for me.",
  "npc.iskan.say_9": "Mhmm, you leave me no other choice than to inform the Jarl.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_10": "I run the dog sled service from this city to {Nibelor}.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_11": "I am Iskan.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_12": "I can bring you to Nibelor with the sled if you want to. Just ask for a {passage}.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_13": "This city seems to be growing every day. First, there have been only a few huts and now ... look around, houses everywhere.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_14": "Our people are very proud and honest. I guess that's more than most people can say about themselves and their people, right boys?",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_15": "I heard something about a ship crashing in the shelf ice between Nibelor and Grimlund. If I were you, I wouldn't go to chakoya terrain. It's pretty dangerous.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_16": "Nasty little beasts. Me and the boys had quite some bloody encounters with them on the ice.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_17": "The boys warn me in advance if a monster is around.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_18": "My boys did not like the guys that were travelling through our city, and I trust in their instincts. Isn't it so, boys?",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_19": "The yeti is real and dangerous.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_20": "I am not sure what to think about this new custom to accept foreigners as one of us after passing that test. But it's the Jarl's decision, not mine.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_21": "The raiders camps are far to the south. There are three of them. Small camp sites of raiding parties might be found almost anywhere though.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_22": "They are sometimes trying to catch me and the boys. Such fools, they will never get us. Right, boys?",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_23": "The boys can tell who's an enemy just by the smell.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_24": "Me and the boys care only about our own territory.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_25": "I guess their healing powers are almost as useful as those of our shamans.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_26": "I guess there are guys like me that have a talent to talk to dogs and there are guys like the shamans that have the talent to talk to spirits.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_27": "We don't need any kings or queens. Am I right, boys? Yeah, I am.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_28": "Sven the Younger is our current Jarl. For my standards he's still a puppy, but a smart one at least.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_29": "Yeah, where could it be. That's the question.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_30": "Easy, boys! Don't mention that name again. Makes the boys nuts, ye know?",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_31": "In my whole long life, I've not seen any sign of those gods the people of the south are constantly talking about.",
  "npc.iskan.stdmod_32": "The icy father. We know him all too well, am I right boys? He has claimed so many old friends in all those years. So many.",
  "npc.riddler.say_1": "Death awaits those who fail the test of the three seals! Do you really want me to test you?",
  "npc.riddler.say_2": "HOHO! Right again. All right. The final question of the first seal: Who was the first warrior to follow the path of the Mooh'Tah?",
  "npc.riddler.say_3": "Hmmm, so you think cheating will get you through that test? Then your final question of the first seal is: What is the meaning of life?",
  "npc.riddler.say_4": "HOHO! Lucky you. You have passed the first seal! So ... would you like to continue with the Seal of the Mind?",
  "npc.riddler.say_5": "As you wish, foolish one! Here is my first question: It's lighter then a feather but no living creature can hold it for ten minutes?",
  "npc.riddler.say_6": "That was an easy one. Let's try the second: If you name it, you break it.",
  "npc.riddler.say_7": "ARGH! You did it again! Well all right. Do you wish to break the Seal of Madness?",
  "npc.riddler.say_8": "GOOD! So I will get you at last. Answer this: What is your favourite colour?",
  "npc.riddler.say_9": "DAMN YOUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUU!",
  "npc.riddler.say_10": "WRONG!",
  "npc.riddler.say_11": "WRONG! Next time get your own answers. To hell with thee, cheater Sischfried!",
  "npc.riddler.say_12": "WRONG!",
  "npc.riddler.stdmod_13": "This tower, of course, silly one. It holds my {master'}s {treasure}.",
  "npc.riddler.stdmod_14": "His name is none of your business",
  "npc.riddler.stdmod_15": "I am guarding the treasures of the tower. Only those who pass the {test} of the three sigils may pass.",
  "npc.riddler.stdmod_16": "I am known as the riddler. That is all you need to know.",
  "npc.riddler.stdmod_17": "I am the guardian of the paradox tower.",
  "npc.riddler.stdmod_18": "The key of this tower! You will never find it! A malicious plant spirit is guarding it!.",
  "npc.freezhild.say_1": "Crate of weapons you say.. for me?",
  "npc.freezhild.say_2": "I'm wondering why you are doing this. Well, we accept the gift. Don't think that this makes you a friend though.",
  "npc.freezhild.say_3": "You don't have any crate of weapons!",
  "npc.ambassador_of_rathleton.say_1": "This is a very beautiful ring. Thank you for this generous present!",
  "npc.ambassador_of_rathleton.say_2": "Didn't you bring my gift?",
  "npc.ambassador_of_rathleton.say_3": "I don't need a present right now. Thank you.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_1": "Arrrrgh! A dirty paleskin! To me my children! Kill them my guards!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_2": "For eons he was trapped in an enchanted lamp by some ancient race. Now he's free to roam the world again. Although he cheated me I appreciate what he and his brethren will do to this world, now it's the time of the Djinn again!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_3": "You bring me a stinking cookie???",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_4": "I was waiting for this day! Take the lamp and let Malor feel my wrath!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_5": "I don't know your enemy, paleskin! Begone!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_6": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_7": "Well, I hope it stinks a lot. I like stinking cookies best ... BY MY THOUSAND SONS! YOU ARE SO DEAD HUMAN! DEAD!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.say_8": "I see.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_9": "I am Charkahn the Slayer! The immortal father of the {orcs} and master of this {hive}.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_10": "The orcs are the bearers of Blogs rage. This makes us the ultimate fighters and the most powerful of all races.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_11": "The orcs are the bearers of Blogs rage. This makes us the ultimate fighters and the most powerful of all races.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_12": "I can sense the presence and the feelings of my underlings and {minions}. I embrace the rage of the horde.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_13": "The orcish horde of this hive is under my control. I sense their emotions and their needs and provide them with the leadership they need to focus their hate and rage",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_14": "Hate and rage are the true blessings of Blog, since they are powerful weapons. They give the hive strength. I provide them with direction and focus.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_15": "The Raging One blessed us with his burning hate. We are truly his children and therefore {divine}.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_16": "To conquer, to destroy and to dominate. Orcs are born to rule the {world}.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_17": "One day I will rule the world, even when turned into a {slime}.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_18": "Pah! Don't mock me, mortal! This shape is a curse which the evil {djinn} bestowed upon me!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_19": "This cursed djinn king! I set him free from an enchanted {lamp}, and he {cheated} me!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_20": "Because I freed him he granted me three wishes. He was true to his word in the first two {wishes}.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_21": "He built this fortress over Uldrek's grave within a single night. Also, he granted me my second wish and gave me immortality. Test it and try to kill me if you want. Har Har!",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_22": "I wished to father more healthy and fertile children as any orc has ever done. But the djinn cheated me and made me a slime! Then he laughed at me and left for his abandoned fortress in the {Deathwish} Mountains.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_23": "His ancient fortress on Darama was deserted as the evil Djinn fled this world after his imprisonment. Now the time has come for the evil Djinns to return to their master although this will certainly awaken the {good Djinn} too.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_24": "I will not share anything more about that topic with you {paleskins}.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_25": "You are as ugly as maggots, although not quite as as tasty.",
  "npc.the_orc_king.stdmod_26": "This cursed djinn king! I set him free from an enchanted lamp, and he cheated me!",
  "npc.robson.say_1": "Do you want to buy a parcel for 15 gold?",
  "npc.robson.say_2": "Do you want to buy a label for 1 gold?",
  "npc.robson.say_3": "Sorry, that's only dust in your purse.",
  "npc.robson.say_4": "Fine.",
  "npc.robson.say_5": "Sorry, that's only dust in your purse.",
  "npc.robson.say_6": "Fine.",
  "npc.robson.say_7": "I knew I would be stuck with that stuff.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_1": "Well, I'm not a simple cook. I travel the whole Tibian continent for the most artfully seasoned {recipes} and constantly develop new ones.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_2": "You're interested in my recipes? Well. They are not for sale, but if you want to become my {apprentice}, I'll share my knowledge with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_3": "You can now cook any dish you want from this list: {Rotworm Stew, Hydra Tongue Salad, Roasted Dragon Wings, Tropical Fried Terrorbird, Banana Chocolate Shake, Veggie Casserole, Filled Jalapeno Peppers, Blessed Steak, Northern Fishburger, Carrot Cake, Coconut Shrimp Bake, Blackjack, Demonic Candy Balls, Sweet Mangonaise Elixir}.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_4": "Hmm. You look quite promising. Can't hurt to give it a try, I guess. Would you like to become my apprentice, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_5": "Fine, young human. Ask me for a {recipe} anytime and I'll teach you what I know.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_6": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_7": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_8": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_9": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_10": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_11": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_12": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_13": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_14": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_15": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_16": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_17": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_18": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_19": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_20": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_21": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_22": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_23": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_24": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_25": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_26": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_27": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_28": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_29": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_30": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_31": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_32": "Make sure that you have all the ingredients with you.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_33": "It seems you have already cooked this dish this year. Please come back next year in August.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_34": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to cook Rotworm Stew with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_35": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to prepare a Hydra Tongue Salad with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_36": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to prepare Roasted Dragon Wings with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_37": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to prepare a Tropical Fried Terrorbird with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_38": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to make a Banana Chocolate Shake with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_39": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to cook a Veggie Casserole with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_40": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to prepare Filled Jalapeño Peppers with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_41": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to prepare a Blessed Steak with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_42": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to make a Northern Fishburger with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_43": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to bake a Carrot Cake with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_44": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to prepare a Coconut Shrimp Bake with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_45": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to cook a Blackjack with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_46": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to make Demonic Candy Balls with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_47": "Did you gather all necessary ingredients to mix Sweet Mangonaise Elixir with me?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.say_48": "No?, come back when you are ready to cook.",
  "npc.hanna.say_1": "Pretty, isn't it? My friend Amber taught me how to make it, but I could help you with one if you like. What do you say?",
  "npc.hanna.say_2": "Oh, you're back already? Did you bring a legion helmet, 100 chicken feathers and 50 honeycombs?",
  "npc.hanna.say_3": "Pretty hat, isn't it?",
  "npc.hanna.say_4": "Okay, here we go, listen closely! I need a few things... a basic hat of course, maybe a legion helmet would do. Then about 100 chicken feathers... and 50 honeycombs as glue. That's it, come back to me once you gathered it!",
  "npc.hanna.say_5": "Aw, I guess you don't like feather hats. No big deal.",
  "npc.hanna.say_6": "Sorry, but I can't see a legion helmet.",
  "npc.hanna.say_7": "Sorry, but you don't enough chicken feathers.",
  "npc.hanna.say_8": "Sorry, but you don't have enough honeycombs.",
  "npc.hanna.say_9": "Great job! That must have taken a lot of work. Okay, you put it like this... then glue like this... here!",
  "npc.hanna.say_10": "Maybe another time.",
  "npc.hanna.stdmod_11": "I am a jeweler. Maybe you want to have a look at my wonderful offers.",
  "npc.hanna.stdmod_12": "I am Hanna.",
  "npc.peter.say_1": "A report? What do they think is happening here? <gives an angry and bitter report>. ",
  "npc.peter.say_2": "Pass the gate? If it must be. Are you headed for the {factory} or the former {trade quarter}?",
  "npc.peter.say_3": "Listen, I don't get paid enough to chat with citizens. Move on.",
  "npc.peter.say_4": "Be on your guard. Some people are nice, some... aren't.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_5": "There it's even more smelly than in the factory quarter. Smells a bit like rotten eggs.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_6": "You don't look as if you would last one second there.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_7": "One day I will walk into the office of my superior and announce my resignment. Probably not long from now.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_8": "Good idea. Go for a walk there. Preferably six feet down.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_9": "It's too noisy and smelly.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_10": "Go there if you wanna get beaten up.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_11": "Sergeant first class of the Yalaharian Guard Force. But I don't care about ranks and titles.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_12": "I can't stand those arrogant fools.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_13": "Leave me alone with your 'mission' unless you have precise orders from my superiors.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_14": "Peter.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_15": "That quara brood should be extinguished.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_16": "The leader of their pack is the biggest criminal among them all.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_17": "Count them yourself.",
  "npc.peter.stdmod_18": "You're here. So what?",
  "npc.gnomadness.say_1": "I can change your hazard level to spice up your hunt in the gardens. Your current level is set to ",
  "npc.gnomadness.say_2": "I'm sorry, I don't understand. What hazard level would you like to set?",
  "npc.gnomadness.say_3": "Your hazard level has been set to ",
  "npc.gnomadness.say_4": "You've achieved the necessary hazard level. As a reward, you've received the Noxious Ripptor mount and a primal bag.",
  "npc.gnomadness.say_5": "You can't set your hazard level higher than your maximum unlocked level.",
  "npc.yasir.say_1": "Me Yasir.",
  "npc.yasir.say_2": "Tje hari ku ne finjala. {Ariki}?",
  "npc.yasir.say_3": "Soso yana. <shakes his head>",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_1": "As far as I know it is a place of helish heat with bloodthirsty monsters of all kinds.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_2": "This sarcophagus seals the entrance to the caves down there. Only here you can get all the {materials} you need for a working compass of this kind. So no entrance here - no further magic compasses in Tibia. In theory.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_3": "On first glance, this cave does not look very spectacular, but the things you find in there, are. You have to know that this is the only place where you can find the respective materials to build the compass.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_4": "May I repair your compass if possible?",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_5": "You don't have the needed itens yet.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_6": "Here's your broken compass!",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_7": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_8": "You don't have the needed itens yet.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_9": "Done. Worry, the effect won't last forever!",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_10": "You're already with my bait!",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_11": "You cannot do that yet.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_12": "It was decided to collect all of the compasses, destroy them and throw them in the fiery depths of Tibia. I still have some of them here. I {sell} them for a low price if you want.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_13": "Would you like to buy a broken compass for 10.000 gold?",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_14": "Don't waste my time.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.say_15": "Sorry, I didn't understand.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_1": "You are back, how did the measurements go? Did you recognise anything of interest?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_2": "Alright, you look bright enough to fulfil my requests - at least you do not fall asleep while standing there. Ahem... I heard about a certain inventor who created a {magic device} to actually sail the {sea of light}. Will you help me find him?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_3": "You should find the beggar somewhere in Edron. Stay persistent, I'm sure he knows more than he wants to tell us.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_4": "o have you talked to the beggar? What did he tell you? Where are the plans...? Wh...? He did? He is?  You've already got the plans? Beautiful!! Amazing! Alright it will take some time to recapitulate these plans.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_5": "So have you talked to the beggar? What did he tell you? Where are the plans...? Wh...? He did? He is? You've already got the plans? Beautiful!! Amazing! Alright it will take some time to recapitulate these plans.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_6": "It will take some time to work out the initial problem of the device. Come back when I've found the component needed to finish it. Alright, B connects to D and another two nails marked with S go... hmmm.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_7": "...connects to N942. Alright!! That's it! I just finished a prototype device! And it looks like I figured out the initial failure. A very special crystal is needed for the device to work. Aren't you as curious as me to know what went wrong?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_8": "Did you enter the Lost Mines yet? They are west of Edron, close to the sea. You will also need a pick once you get to the crystal deposit.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_9": "Hm, so did you find a rare crystal? Show me... hey! That's not a rare crystal. What... where did you get that anyway? Please return to me with the right crystal.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_10": "Well, the only thing left to do would be to offer the crystal at the well of the collector. There must be a pedestal near the well, where you need to put your donation. Ha, do you think you could do that?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_11": "Found the well yet? Look on one of the ice isles near Carlin. I'm perfectly sure that the well with the pedestal is located on one of them. And be careful with the carrying device, I only have this one prototype.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_12": "So have you found the well and entered the lair? I hope you can find the {mirror crystal} in there. It is the only way to finish the {Lightboat}.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_13": "Put the mirror crystal into the special carrying device I gave you and bring it directly to me.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_14": "Do you have the mirror crystal? Unbelievable! Alright I will extract the crystal from the device myself, would you please give me the device with the crystal and step back?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_15": "After the debacle with the crystal, I started focussing on other things. There are also some {tasks} that still need to be done. If you can spare the time to continue helping me, it shall not be to your disadvantage. So are you in for another mission?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_16": "So you found him? Have you talked to {Jack} yet?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_17": "You're back from {Jack}! Mh, by the looks of your face I doubt our little redecoration project yielded any success. But I had an even better idea while you were gone - ready to give it another try?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_18": "So, did you talk to his family? Were you able to convince them?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_19": "Did you find out what hobby {Jack} has? Did you separate him from this activity? Only if he has a free mind, he can truly get back to his former self! Now all you need to do is talk to him again!",
  "npc.spectulus.say_20": "The device needs a special crystal. It's called {mirror crystal}. The inventor somehow damaged it - with fatal results. He had to give up, as no second crystal was left to try. I, however, know of another one... but are you up to the task?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_21": "One remaining mirror crystal is in the hands of a creature called the collector which collects all kinds of crystals. The only way to get access to its lair is to donate a very rare crystal to a secret well. I need you to get one, will you help me?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_22": "Good, because if you wouldn't do it... listen, this well is on one of the isles near Carlin. There you offer the crystal. Once you get access to its lair, find the collector and... convince it to give you the mirror crystal. Understood?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_23": "To collect the unbelievably rare, practically unique mirror crystal, you will need to use this special carrying device I developed. If you find the crystal, use it to store it and transport it safely to me. There is no second one.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_24": "Of course you are. And here we go. I have to ask some questions first. One: You aint afraid of no ghost, right?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_25": "Good. Two: You know that ghosts exist and/or have found and/or defeated one or more of them?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_26": "Good. Take this wand - we call it a spirit meter - and go to the graveyard I have marked on your map and take a few measurements on the graves.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_27": "Let me see the spirit meter. Hmmm... those are grave news you bring - uhm, you know what I mean. But this is awesome! Now I know for sure that the calibration is only some short bursts of magically enhanced energy away.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_28": "Yes? And he didn't remember anything? Not even me? That's not good. Then we will have to do everything ourselves. Are you ready to continue?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_29": "Ah well, let's forget about the scientific details - you will do just fine as long as you do exactly what I say. Ready for me to go on with your task?",
  "npc.spectulus.say_30": "Yes, maybe it was the right decision. Astronomical research is nothing for the faint-hearted.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_31": "Well, the... what? You... mean you're no longer interested? I see, well maybe I overestimated your spirit after all.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_32": "Alright, alright. You'll never find out the true secrets of life with such attitude, hm.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_33": "Come on, this is our only chance to finish the Lightboat.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_34": "Thought so. Well, no reason to be ashamed. I'll have to find help elsewhere now, though.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_35": "Come back if you made up your mind.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_36": "Hmpf. *mumbles*",
  "npc.spectulus.say_37": "Then off you go! Im sorry that I cannot offer you any further help but Im sure you will find support along your way. And - be careful. The sea can appear pitch black down there.",
  "npc.spectulus.say_38": "Excellent, excellent. The rumours pointed to the north of Tiquanda, a sunken temple probably half drowned in water. Return to me if you find anything interesting!",
  "npc.spectulus.say_39": "Then off you go! I'm sorry that I cannot offer you any further help but I'm sure you will find support along your way. And - be careful. The sea can appear pitch black down there.",
  "npc.cobra.say_1": "Begone! Hissssss! You bear not the mark of the cobra!",
  "npc.rehon.say_1": "By the Gods! You have the key to the cell! Thank you sooo much, mate. And now leave. I'll wait here until the air is clean and then I'm out of here.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_5": "The temple is near the shop area in the eastern part of the castle. Just go downstairs.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_6": "Our local bank clerk is called Ebenizer. You can find him north of the depot, near the food shop.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, furniture, spells and food here.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_8": "I'm your guide to the beautiful town Edron. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_9": "The town of Edron with its shops and facilities is built inside strong castle walls. Another remarkable building is the magic academy.",
  "npc.guide_jonathan.stdmod_10": "I'm Jonathan. Pleased to meet you.",
  "npc.ztiss.say_1": "You are ztill a captive and your life is forfeit. Zere might be a way for you to ezcape if you agree to {work} for my mazter.",
  "npc.a_starving_dog.say_1": "<munch>",
  "npc.chavis.say_1": "I am sorry, you didn't harvest enough roots. You need to harvest a bundle of at least five roots - and please try doing it yourself.",
  "npc.chavis.say_2": "Yes? You brought some juicy roots? How nice of you - that's one additional voice in the {magistrate} of {Rathleton} for you! ...",
  "npc.chavis.say_3": "Spend it wisely, though, put in a word for the poor, will ye? Sure you will.",
  "npc.chavis.say_4": "You don't have enough items.",
  "npc.chavis.say_5": "They are nutritious, cost nothing and are good for the body hair. If you can bring us bundles of five juicy roots each - we will make it worth your while for the {magistrate}.",
  "npc.chavis.say_6": "They act so important but it is us common people who keep things going. There is a lot you can do in this city to earn a right to vote in the magistrate, though. So keep an eye out for everyone who needs help.",
  "npc.shiantis.say_1": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.shiantis.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.shiantis.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.orockle.say_1": "You can help in the fight against the hive. There are several missions available to destabilise the hive. Just ask for them if you want to learn more. After completing many missions you might be worthy to get a reward.",
  "npc.orockle.say_2": "You could try to blind the hive, you might disrupt its digestion, you could gather acid or you can disable the swarm pores. ...",
  "npc.orockle.say_3": "So be it. Now you are a member of the inquisition. You might ask me for a mission to raise in my esteem.",
  "npc.shirith.say_1": "Do you want to buy a key for 50 gold?",
  "npc.shirith.say_2": "Here it is.",
  "npc.shirith.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.benjamin.say_1": "Oh they don't change that much since in the old days as... <tells a boring and confusing story about a cake, a parcel, himself and two squirrels, at least he tells you his measurements in the end> ",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_1": "Ohhhh. So... <lowers his voice> you know who sent you so I sail you to you know where. <wink> <wink> It will cost 50 gold to cover my expenses. Is it that what you wish?",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_2": "Sorry, my old ears can't hear you.",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_3": "<sigh> I knew someone else would claim all the treasure someday. But at least it will be you and not some greedy and selfish person. For a small fee of 200 gold pieces I will sail you to your rendezvous with fate. Do we have a deal?",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_4": "I have to admit this leaves me a bit puzzled.",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_5": "And there we go!",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_6": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_7": "And there we go!",
  "npc.captain_waverider.say_8": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.shirtalis_of_the_summer_court.say_1": "We allow able champions of all races to fight for our cause against the challenges of the {arena}. So are you interested? I'm not interested in fancy'wordplay, so a simple {yes} or {no} will suffice!",
  "npc.shirtalis_of_the_summer_court.say_2": "You are now able to enter the teleport.",
  "npc.shirtalis_of_the_summer_court.say_3": "As you wish.",
  "npc.shirtalis_of_the_summer_court.say_4": "This place has always been a site where the champions of summer and winter have clashed in battle. Over the centuries this spectacle has drawn many creatures here to watch, participate and indulge in less savory activities.",
  "npc.swolt.say_1": "Aaargh! Cael and his strange thoughts! He bugged me so long about the lizard culture that I eventually agreed to prepare that rice for you if you need it. I need one ripe rice plant to prepare ten rice balls. OK?",
  "npc.swolt.say_2": "You don't have a ripe rice plant. Thank fire and earth I was spared.",
  "npc.swolt.stdmod_3": "Well, you see me standing behind a bar. Selling drinks. Food. And stuff. Now try figuring out what I could be making a living of down here.",
  "npc.swolt.stdmod_4": "I can offer you bread, cheese, ham, or meat. And as drinks we serve beer and water. If you'd like to see what we have to offer, just ask me for a trade.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_1": "You find yourself inside the dragon's dream. You can {look} around or {go} into a specific direction. You can also {take} or {use} an object. Enter {help} to display this information at any time.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_2": "Advancing to the west, you recognise an increase of onyx on the ground.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_3": "You carefully lift the onyx attachment from its socket. It is lighter than you expected.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_4": "You return to the plateau in the east.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_5": "You wander to the south, passing large obelisks of emerald to your left and sprawling trees of topaz to your right. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_6": "As you rip the solid stand out of its socket and take it with you, the large gate opens with a deafening rumble. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_7": "You gasp at the size of the large open gate as you walk through to head further to the east.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_8": "You reach for a small solitary arrangement of combined small houses and put it in your pocket.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_9": "You take an emerald from the pile. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_10": "You return through the semi-translucent gate to the west. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_11": "You head back north to the plateau. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_12": "You travel east across several large emerald bluffs and edges. All sorts of gems are scattered alongside your path. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_13": "You take a rather large ruby out of a pile before you. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_14": "You head north passing countless stones in the crimson sea of stones beneath your feet.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_15": "Avoiding the bright light, you carefully put the attachment on top of the strange socket. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_16": "Your path to the north is open. You pass the gigantic gate wings to your left and right as you advance. After about an hour of travel you hear a slight rustling in the distance. You head further into that direction. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_17": "You travel all the way back down the dune and through the gate to the south. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_18": "You return to the crimson sea of rubies in the south. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_19": "You travel back to the plateau in the west. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_20": "Advancing to the west, you recognise an increase of onyx on the ground. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_21": "You continue travelling the barren sea of gemstones to the north. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_22": "You leave the massive open gate behind you and go to the west. ",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_23": "You carefully remove the sapphire from Bastesh's grasp.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_24": "You head back to the east and to the plateau.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_25": "You head back south to the site with the onyx lookout.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_26": "You return to the plateau in the east.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_27": "You put the stand into a small recess you find near the middle of the plateau.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_28": "As the ruby slips into the notch, the strong red of the stone intensifies a thousandfold. You fear to hurt your eyes and turn away immediately. The ray seems to be directed to the centre of the plateau with astounding precision.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_29": "As the sapphire slips into the notch, the deep blue of the stone intensifies a thousandfold. You fear to hurt your eyes and turn away immediately. The ray seems to be directed to the centre of the plateau with astounding precision.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_30": "As the emerald slips into the notch, the vibrant green of the stone intensifies a thousandfold. You fear to hurt your eyes and turn away immediately. The ray seems to be directed to the centre of the plateau with astounding precision.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.say_31": "I call you the wayfarer. You travelled through my dreams. You ultimately freed my mind. My mind accepted you and so will I.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_alexena.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_5": "The temple can be found in one of the uptown districts. Look for stairs up from the lower city, you'll find the temple in the northwest of the upper city.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_6": "The bank is on the left side of the depot. Eva will be at your service there.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, furniture, spells and food here.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_9": "I'll help you find your way through Carlin, the amazon town. I can mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_10": "This city is ruled by Queen Eloise with the help of her female brigade. We have a lot of shops here as well as the usual facilities like depot, temple and so on.",
  "npc.guide_alexena.stdmod_11": "I'm Alexena, at your service!",
  "npc.lorbas.say_1": "You want me to eat this cookie?",
  "npc.lorbas.say_2": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.lorbas.say_3": "Well, you don't mind if I play around with this antidote rune a bit ... UHHH, YOU LOU ... uhm that was so ... funny, haha ... ha. Mhm, you better leave now.",
  "npc.lorbas.say_4": "I see.",
  "npc.harsky.stdmod_1": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the king greet with his title!",
  "npc.harsky.stdmod_2": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the king greet with his title!",
  "npc.harsky.say_3": "Take this!",
  "npc.gamel.say_1": "I don't like the way you look. Help me boys!",
  "npc.gamel.say_2": "You have a letter for me?",
  "npc.gamel.say_3": "Oh well. I guess I am still on the hook. Tell your 'uncle' I will proceed as he suggested.",
  "npc.gamel.say_4": "You don't have any letter!",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_1": "In exchange for a truly generous donation, I will offer a special outfit. Do you want to make a donation?",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_2": "In that case, return to me once you made up your mind.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_3": "Take this armor as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend!",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_4": "Please make sure you have free slots in your store inbox.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_5": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_6": "You alread have that addon.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_7": "Take this helmet as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend. ",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_8": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_9": "You alread have that outfit.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_10": "You need to donate {armor} outfit first.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_11": "Take this boots as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend. ",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_12": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_13": "You alread have that outfit.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_14": "You need to donate {helmet} addon first.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_15": "So you wold like to donate 500.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear a unique armor?",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_16": "So you would like to donate 250.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear unique helmet?",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.say_17": "So you would like to donate 250.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear a unique boots?",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.stdmod_18": "I can promote you for 20000 gold coins. Do you want me to promote you?",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.stdmod_19": "Alright then, come back when you are ready.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_1": "I suggest you relax a bit with a fresh mushroom beer and we can talk after that. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_2": "Yes... Yes... <sigh>. We already talked about that. I can't remember if you have already tried the {test}, so lets get going.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_3": "We are hiring people to fight in our so called Bigfoot company against the foes of gnomekind. Are you interested in joining?",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_4": "What do you think describes gnomish society best? {A}) Ingenuity {B}) Bravery {C}) Humility {D}) All of the above.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_5": "What is the front part of a spear? Is it {A}) the pointed one. {B}) The blunt one. {C}) Whatever causes the most damage {D}) A spear is no weapon but a fruit that grows on surface trees.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_6": "What comes first? {A}) safety {B}) I {C}) duty {D}) George",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_7": "In case of emergency {A}) break glass {B}) break a leg {C}) have a break {D}) call a gnome?",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_8": "The greatest disaster I can imagine is ... {A}) to fail the gnomes {B}) a ruined mushroom pie {C}) accidentally hammering my finger {D}) having some work to do",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_9": "What would your favourite pet be? {A}) A Krazzelzak of course. {B}) An Uxmoff to be honest. {C}) Montpiffs were always my favourite. {D}) A Humdrella and nothing else!",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_10": "Why do you want to become a bigfoot? {A}) To become rich and famous. {B}) To become famous and rich. {C}) To become rich or famous. {D}) To serve the gnomish community in their struggle?",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_11": "Indeed an excellent and smart decision for an ungnomish lifeform. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_12": "A well thought out answer I have to admit. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_13": "Ah, we have a true warrior here I guess. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_14": "Fear not. We don't expect too much of you anyway. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_15": "Ha! A Krazzelzak would for sure fit someone like you! But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_16": "Wrong answer!",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_17": "Stop it! The test is over, you can ask me for your {results}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_18": "Although chances are the gnome will end up rescuing you instead, it is the attempt that counts. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_19": "I knew this question was too easy. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_20": "Wrong answer!",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_21": "That's the spirit! Initiative is always a good thing. Well most of the time. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_22": "You have no idea how many answer this question wrong. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_23": "That's the spirit! But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_24": "Wrong answer!",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_25": "Stop it! The test is over, you can ask me for your {results}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_26": "Of COURSE you wouldn't! NO ONE would! But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_27": "I can only hope that is your honest opinion. But let us continue with the test.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_28": "Oh, you silver tongued devil almost made me blush. But of course you're right. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_29": "How true. How true. *sigh* But fear not! We gnomes are here to help! But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_30": "That's just what I'd do - if I weren't a gnome already, that is. But let us continue with the {test}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_31": "Excellent! Well this concludes the test. Now let us see your {results}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_32": "Wrong answer!",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_33": "Stop it! The test is over, you can ask me for your {results}.",
  "npc.gnomerik.say_34": "Excellent! Now let us begin with the gnomish aptitude test. Just tell me when you feel ready for the {test}!",
  "npc.willard.say_1": "Thank you, I appreciate it. Don't forget to mention the package to Snake.",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_1": "Whoa! A human! This is no place for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Go and play somewhere else.",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_2": "<Sighs> Another {customer}! I've only just sat down! What is it, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_3": "You brought cookies! How nice of you! Can I have one?",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_4": "You have no cookie that I'd like.",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_5": "You see, good deeds like this will ... YOU ... YOU SPAWN OF EVIL! I WILL MAKE SURE THE MASTER LEARNS ABOUT THIS!",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_6": "I see.",
  "npc.nah_bob.say_7": "I'm sorry, human. But you need Gabel's permission to trade with me.",
  "npc.stutch.stdmod_1": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the king greet with his title!",
  "npc.stutch.stdmod_2": "MIND YOUR MANNERS COMMONER! To address the king greet with his title!",
  "npc.stutch.say_3": "Take this!",
  "npc.mazarius.say_1": "Ah, you have heard about my search for experienced help. And indeed your reputation for solving certain {problems} has preceded you.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_2": "My problems are, so to say, dire news for the whole world. <sigh> I don't want to confuse you with overly complicated and lengthy stories, so do you want to hear the {long} version or the {short}?",
  "npc.mazarius.say_3": "Good!, but I need 30 {demonic essences} to exchange with the demonic messenger for a ticket for you to enter the Abodes of Torments.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_4": "Do you have 30 demonic essences to offer to the demonic messenger?",
  "npc.mazarius.say_5": "Excellent! This will empower possibilty to create a breach is enough to let you pass into that hellish hiding place. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.say_6": "You don't have the demonic essences, back here when you get it.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_7": "Given the internal power plays amongst the Seven, they are the ideal keepers for individual parts of an powerful artefact. Not one of them would allow his compatriots to hold such a power, and neither would trust the other.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_8": "Ah, a good man and a competent aid.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_9": "I like the quietness and the climate. And admittedly it helped my studies not to be constantly disturbed by petitioners.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_10": "Thais has become a melting pot of some source. Yet whatever you melt, if the ingredients are corrupted, the outcome is always flawed.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_11": "Instead of banding together and starting to change something, they and Thais keep wasting resources in hostilities.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_12": "Edron has become as stagnant as the teachings in its academy. No new idea has been thought there for decades. The whole Edron is an example for what happens when humanity has become fat and lazy.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_13": "An almost laughable greed is persistent in that city. At least this makes knowledge and materials conveniently available to those who can match their prizes.",
  "npc.mazarius.say_14": "What?!",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_1": "We can bring you to Thais with one of our coaches for 125 gold. Are you interested?",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_2": "Do you want to rent a horse for one day at a price of 500 gold?",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_3": "First get rid of those blood stains!",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_4": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_5": "Have a nice trip!",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_6": "You already have a horse.",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_7": "You do not have enough money to rent a horse!",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_8": "I'll give you one of our experienced ones. Take care! Look out for low hanging branches.",
  "npc.appaloosa.say_9": "Then not.",
  "npc.ahmet.say_1": "The slayer of my enemies is my friend! For a mere 1000 gold I will create the documents you need. Are you interested?",
  "npc.ahmet.say_2": "Did you find my stuff?",
  "npc.ahmet.say_3": "I see: You want me to add an additional story to this book. A legend about how it brings ill luck to kill a white deer. I could do that, yes. It costs 5000 gold, however. Are you still interested?",
  "npc.ahmet.say_4": "And here they are! Now forget where you got them from.",
  "npc.ahmet.say_5": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.ahmet.say_6": "GREAT! If you ever need a job as my personal security guard, let me know. Here is the reward I promised you.",
  "npc.ahmet.say_7": "Come back when you find my stuff.",
  "npc.ahmet.say_8": "You need 5000 gps and book with ancient legends.",
  "npc.ahmet.say_9": "You are not in this mission.",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.say_1": "You already have access.",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.say_2": "You are willing to pay 5000000 gold pieces, then? There is no turning back after our... transaction is complete. Are you sure?",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.say_3": "Sorry, you don't have enough gold.",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.say_4": "The bargain has been made, the business is done.",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.say_5": "Ok then not.",
  "npc.noozer.say_1": "I was stationed in this cave to... guard something. Right now I am not even sure what that was.",
  "npc.noozer.say_2": "Then don't waste my time. I'm doing some important... business... here. Actually... where am I? If I find out, I will be even more angry than I am now. Out of my sight.",
  "npc.noozer.say_3": "I was on a mission, too - I guess. It was all quite blurry back then. Maybe I'll leave this place after I recovered completely. I have to find out what happened to me.",
  "npc.zoltan.say_1": "Ah, Yenny the Gentle was one of the founders of the druid order called Crunor's Caress, that has been originated in her hometown Carlin.",
  "npc.zoltan.say_2": "A quite undruidic order of druids they were, as far as we know. I have no more enlightening knowledge about them though.",
  "npc.zoltan.say_3": "... I cannot believe my eyes. You retrieved this hat from Ferumbras' remains? That is incredible. If you give it to me, I will grant you the right to wear this hat as addon. What do you say?",
  "npc.zoltan.say_4": "I bow to you, player, and hereby grant you the right to wear Ferumbras' hat as accessory. Congratulations!",
  "npc.zoltan.say_5": "Sorry you don't have the Ferumbras' hat.",
  "npc.zoltan.say_6": "This task is only available for male players who don't already have the addon.",
  "npc.zoltan.say_7": "Stop bothering me. I am a far too busy man to be constantly giving out awards.",
  "npc.zoltan.say_8": "What the hell are you talking about?",
  "npc.gnombold.say_1": "I'm the officer responsible for this area. I give out missions, accept mission reports and oversee our defences.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_2": "Gnomes have lived autonomous for so long that it still feels odd to work with strangers for many of us.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_3": "Sorry, but no! Your expertise could be put to better use elsewhere. Here awaits you no challenge. You are desperately needed in the deeper levels of the Spike. Report there immediately. ",
  "npc.gnombold.say_4": " I can offer you several missions: to gather geomantic {charges}, to {fertilise} the mushroom caves, to destroy monster {nests} and to {kill} some crystal crushers.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_5": "What mission do you want to report about: gathering the geomantic {charges}, the {fertilisation} of the mushroom caves, about destroying monster {nests} and the {killing} of crystal crushers?",
  "npc.gnombold.say_6": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_7": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_8": "Gnowful! Charge this magnet at three monoliths in the cave system. With three charges, the magnet will disintegrate and charge you with its gathered energies. Step on the magnetic extractor here to deliver the charge to us, then report to me.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_9": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_10": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_11": "Gnowful! Use the fertiliser on four gardener mushroom in the caves.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_12": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_13": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_14": "Gnowful! Step into the transformer and destroy eight monster nests.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_15": "You have not started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_16": "You have done well. Here, take your reward.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_17": "Gnowful! Just go out to the caves and kill at least seven crystalcrushers.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_18": "That's not a valid mission name.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_19": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnombold.say_20": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_21": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_22": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnombold.say_23": "Your mission would be to seek out gardener mushrooms in the caves and use some fertiliser on them. If you are interested, I can give you some more information about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnombold.say_24": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_25": "Gnometastic! And here is your fertiliser - use it on four gardener mushroom in the caves. If you lose the fertiliser you'll have to bring your own. Gnomux sells all the equipment that is required for our missions.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_26": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_27": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnombold.say_28": "Our mission for you is to step into the gnomish transformer and then destroy eight monster nests in the caves. If you are interested, I can give you some more information about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnombold.say_29": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_30": "Gnometastic! Don't forget to step into the transformer before you go out and destroy five monster nests. If your transformation runs out, return to the transformer to get another illusion.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_31": "Ok then.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_32": "Sorry, you are not on the required range of levels [",
  "npc.gnombold.say_33": "This mission will require you to kill some crystal crushers for us. If you are interested, I can give you some more information about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnombold.say_34": "You have already started that mission.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_35": "Gnometastic! You should have no trouble to find enough crystal crushers. Killing seven of them should be enough.",
  "npc.gnombold.say_36": "Ok then.",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_1": "Do you have the papers I asked you for with you?",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_2": "Oh marvellous, please excuse me. I need to read this text immediately. Here, take this small reward of 500 gold pieces for your efforts.",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_3": "I've heard some odd rumours about this new dwarven outpost. But tell me, what has the Edron academy to do with Farmine?",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_4": "I'm not sure if I'm in the mood to talk about that matter again. Or do you have anything that might change my mind?",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_5": "Hm, you are right, we are at the forefront of knowledge and innovation. Our dwarven friends could learn much from one of our representatives.",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_6": "<sighs> Okay, sending some trader there won't hurt. I hope it will be worth the effort, though.",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_7": "Well, it can't be wrong to be there when new discoveries are made. Also, all those soldiers of fortune that might travel there could turn out to be a good source of income for a magic shop. ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_8": "What do you mean the druids of Carlin could provide the service as well? They are incompetent imposters! I will not allow them to ruin our reputation! I'll send some trader with supplies right away!",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_9": "Hm, you are right, we are at the forefront of knowledge and innovation. Our dwarven friends could learn much from one of our representatives.",
  "npc.wyrdin.say_10": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.say_1": "Hello, brother. You come with a question to me, I believe?",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.say_2": "And what is it you want? Do you bring news from the undead, or do you seek a dark {artefact}?",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.say_3": "Hello, brother. You have finished the dance?",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.say_4": "Time is money, hurry.",
  "npc.hamish.multiline_1": "Small and deceptively friendly-looking island. Well, I used to study the plants and herbs here for my potions.",
  "npc.hamish.multiline_2": "Nowadays, I leave that to Oressa, she has a better way with that horrible wildlife here. \\z\n\t\t\t\tI prefer to distil potions in the quiet of my lab. \\z\n\t\t\t\tIf you need some potions, runes or other magic equipment, ask for a trade.",
  "npc.hamish.multiline_3": "Dawnport is not far off from the coast of the Tibian Mainland. Lots of cities, monsters, bandits, \\z\n\t\t\t\tbrigands, mean folk and people of low understanding with no sense of respect towards alchemical genius. \\z\n\t\t\t\t<mutters to himself>",
  "npc.hamish.multiline_4": "Ahem. Once you're level 8, you should be experienced enough to choose your definite vocation and leave \\z\n\t\t\t\tDawnport for Main - and Tibia definitely needs more skilled adventurers to keep those monsters in check \\z\n\t\t\t\twhich roam our lands!",
  "npc.hamish.multiline_5": "I wish I had thought of changing my name to that of a hero. Would have smoothed my way no end!",
  "npc.hamish.multiline_6": "Anyway, whatever he was before he joined, Tybald now fits the bill of the legendary hero. \\z\n\t\t\t\tHe even has a crush on lady Oressa. Cute. <chuckles>",
  "npc.terrence.say_1": "I'm not allowed to let just anyone pass. If you have proven your willingness and effort to participate in the fighting, I'm allowed to let you pass.",
  "npc.terrence.say_2": "Ahhhhhhhh! ",
  "npc.terrence.say_3": "You fought hard enough against the minotaurs. Since you've shown so much effort in our war, I'll let you pass through the gate.",
  "npc.eremo.say_1": "A letter from that youngster Morgan? I believed him dead since years. These news are good news indeed. Thank you very much, my friend.",
  "npc.pig.say_1": "Do you want to try to release me with a kiss?",
  "npc.pig.say_2": "Mhm Uhhh. Not bad, not bad at all! But you can still improve your skill a LOT.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_1": "Prey hunting tasks should reduce the number of certain monsters. And if you fulfil them successfully I will show my appreciation and give you some {rewards} in exchange of hunting task points.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_2": "You have already spent ",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_3": "Sorry, i have no offer to make for you today.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_4": "I have no outfit offer to make.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_5": "I have no mount offer to make.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_6": "I have no trophie offer to make.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_7": "I have no furniture offer to make.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_8": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_9": "Sorry, but you don't have enough slots on your inbox or capacity.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_10": "Sorry, but you don't have enough hunting task points.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_11": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_12": "Sorry, but you don't have enough slots on your inbox or capacity.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_13": "Sorry, but you don't have enough hunting task points.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_14": "You already have this outfit.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_15": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_16": "First you need to buy the base addon to unlock this addon.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_17": "You already have this addon.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_18": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_19": "Sorry, but you don't have enough hunting task points.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_20": "First you need to buy the base addon to unlock this addon.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_21": "You already have this addon.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_22": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_23": "Sorry, but you don't have enough hunting task points.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_24": "You already have this mount.",
  "npc.walter_jaeger.say_25": "Here you have it.",
  "npc.klaus.say_1": "Hmm, you look like a seasoned seadog. Kill Captain Ray Striker, bring me his lucky pillow as a proof and you are our hero!",
  "npc.klaus.say_2": "Do you have Striker's pillow?",
  "npc.klaus.say_3": "You DID it!!! Incredible! Boys, lets have a PAAAAAARTY!!!!",
  "npc.klaus.say_4": "Come back when you have his lucky pillow.",
  "npc.topsy.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.topsy.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.topsy.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.lynda.say_1": "Did you bring a sample of each wand and each rod with you?",
  "npc.lynda.say_2": "Did you obtain 10 ounces of magic sulphur?",
  "npc.lynda.say_3": "Were you actually able to retrieve the Necromancer's soul stone?",
  "npc.lynda.say_4": "Am I sensing enough holy energy from ankhs here?",
  "npc.lynda.say_5": "I'm glad to tell you that I have finished the ritual, player. Here is your new wand. I hope you carry it proudly for everyone to see..",
  "npc.lynda.say_6": "Please let me focus for a while, |PLAYERNAME|.",
  "npc.lynda.say_7": "Alright then. Come back to with a sample of all five wands and five rods, please.",
  "npc.lynda.say_8": "Thank you, that must have been a lot to carry. Now, please bring me 10 ounces of magic sulphur.",
  "npc.lynda.say_9": "Very good. I will immediately start to prepare the ritual and extract the elemental energy from the wands and rods. Please bring me the Necromancer's soul stone now.",
  "npc.lynda.say_10": "You have found a rarity there, |PLAYERNAME|. This will become the tip of your blessed wand. Please bring me 20 ankhs now to complete the ritual.",
  "npc.lynda.say_11": "The ingredients for the ritual are complete! I will start to prepare your blessed wand, but I have to medidate first. Please come back later to hear how the ritual went.",
  "npc.lynda.say_12": "A player with this name does not exist.",
  "npc.lynda.say_13": "You REALLY want to marry yourself? c'mon, be serious.",
  "npc.lynda.say_14": "As I said, you need a wedding ring and the wedding outfit box in order to marry.",
  "npc.lynda.say_15": "Since both of you are willing to marry, I accept to celebrate your marriage, go prepare yourself, and tell me when you are ready for the {celebration}",
  "npc.lynda.say_16": "Your partner didn't accept your proposal, yet",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_17": "Ok, let's keep it then.",
  "npc.lynda.say_18": "You don't have any pending proposal to be removed.",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_19": "Great! Marriages should be an eternal commitment.",
  "npc.lynda.say_20": "You aren't married to get a divorce.",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_21": "Would you like to get married? Make sure you have a wedding ring and the wedding outfit box with you.",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_22": "That's fine.",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_23": "And who would you like to marry?",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_24": "Is your soulmate and friends here with you for the celebration?",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_25": "Then go bring them here!",
  "npc.lynda.stdmod_26": "Good, let's {begin} then!",
  "npc.inkaef.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.inkaef.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.inkaef.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.faloriel.say_1": "So, the Librarian sent you. Well, yes, I have a vial of the hallucinogen you need. I'll give it to you for 1000 gold. Do you agree?",
  "npc.faloriel.say_2": "I don't have anything to offer you regarding a ring.",
  "npc.faloriel.say_3": "Great. Here, take it.",
  "npc.faloriel.say_4": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.khanna.say_1": "Sorry, you aren't a druid either a sorcerer.",
  "npc.khanna.say_2": "Here you are young adept, take care yourself.",
  "npc.khanna.say_3": "Ok then.",
  "npc.chantalle.say_1": "Oh my! You look so great in your uniform! You archpostmen are not only daring but also handsome. Here take it, that's the key you wanted. Just promise to visit me now and then!",
  "npc.chantalle.say_2": "Oh my, such a lovely necklace! Here take it, that's the key you wanted. Now let me admire my precious necklace alone.",
  "npc.chantalle.say_3": "I am sorry, I am not interested in your money. Maybe you should try your luck with Herbert, the postman instead.",
  "npc.cornelia.stdmod_1": "I run this armoury. If you want to protect your life, you better buy my wares.",
  "npc.cornelia.say_2": "Ah, you must be the hero Trisha talked about. I'll prepare the shoulder spikes for you. Please give me some time to finish.",
  "npc.cornelia.say_3": "I'm not done yet. Please be as patient as you are courageous.",
  "npc.cornelia.say_4": "Finished! Since you are a man, I thought you probably wanted two. Men always want that little extra status symbol. <giggles>",
  "npc.cornelia.say_5": "I'm selling leather armor, chain armor, and brass armor. Ask me for a {trade} if you like to take a look.",
  "npc.yana.say_1": "{Tokens} are small objects made of metal or other materials. You can use them to buy superior equipment from token traders like me.",
  "npc.yana.say_2": "Disrupt the Heart of Destruction, fell the World Devourer to prove your worth and you will be granted the power to imbue 'Powerful Strike', 'Powerful Void' and --'Powerful Vampirism'.",
  "npc.yana.say_3": "If you have any gold tokens with you, let's have a look! These are my offers.",
  "npc.yana.say_4": "I have creature products for the imbuements {strike}, {vampirism} and {void}. Make your choice, please!",
  "npc.yana.say_5": "There it is.",
  "npc.yana.say_6": "You don't have enough capacity. You must have ",
  "npc.yana.say_7": "Your decision. Come back if you have changed your mind.",
  "npc.telas.say_1": "I have heard only little about this mine. I am a bit absorbed in my studies. But what does this mine have to do with me?",
  "npc.telas.say_2": "You are starting this discussion again? Why should I listen to you this time, do you have anything to convince me to let you even try?",
  "npc.telas.say_3": "Well it sounds like a good idea to test my golems in some real environment. I think it is acceptable to send some of them to Farmine.",
  "npc.telas.say_4": "Well, of course my worker golems are quite usefull and it might indeed be a good idea to see who they operate on realistic conditions. I will send some to farmine soon.",
  "npc.telas.say_5": "Well, if the situation is that desperate I think it is possible to send some of the golems to help the poor dwarfs out of their misery.",
  "npc.telas.say_6": "Oh how nice of you. I might have misjudged you. So let us return to this matter of worker golems. Do you have any better arguments this time?",
  "npc.telas.say_7": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.ikassis.say_1": "The wolf's ghost has found peace. Thank you, human being. However, there is someone else who needs help: A sister of mine who's bereft of something very precious. You'll find her in the guise of a swan at a small river south-east of here.",
  "npc.ikassis.say_2": "You are not on that mission.",
  "npc.ikassis.say_3": "Then not.",
  "npc.bloodshade_rotten.say_1": "You already have started this quest.",
  "npc.jamesfrancis.say_1": "The minotaurs I faced in the cave are much stronger than the normal ones. What I were able to see before I had to flee: all of them seem to belong to a cult worshipping their god. Could you do me a {favour}?",
  "npc.jamesfrancis.say_2": "I'd like to work in this cave researching the minotaurs. But right now there are too many of hem and what is more, they are too powerful for me. Could you enter the cave and kill at least 50 of these creatures?",
  "npc.jamesfrancis.say_3": "Great job! You have killed at least 50 of these monsters. I give this key to you to open the door to the inner area. Go there and find out what's going on.",
  "npc.jamesfrancis.say_4": "Come back when you have killed enough minotaurs.",
  "npc.jamesfrancis.say_5": "Very nice. Return to me if you've finished your job.",
  "npc.ishina.say_1": "My jewelled belt? Of course I could make one for you, but I have a small request. Would you fulfil a task for me?",
  "npc.ishina.say_2": "Have you brought me a mermaid's comb?",
  "npc.ishina.say_3": "Yay! I will wait for you to return with a mermaid's comb then.",
  "npc.ishina.say_4": "No... that's not it.",
  "npc.ishina.say_5": "Yeah! That's it! I can't wait to comb my hair! Oh - but first, I'll fulfil my promise: Here is your jewelled belt! Thanks again!",
  "npc.ishina.say_6": "Oh... okay.",
  "npc.ishina.stdmod_7": "I am a jeweller. Maybe you want to have a look at my wonderful {offers}.",
  "npc.ishina.stdmod_8": "Well, I sell gems and {goblets}. If you'd like to see my offers, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.ishina.stdmod_9": "Ah, our newest import! We have golden goblets, silver goblets and bronze goblets. All of them have space for a hand-written dedication.",
  "npc.angelo.say_1": "The scientists are still missing? You just found some strange green shining mummies and a big oasis? I give you this analysis tool for the water of the oasis. Maybe that's the key. Could you bring me a sample of this water?",
  "npc.angelo.say_2": "Very good. Hopefully analysing this sample will get us closer to the solution of this mistery.",
  "npc.angelo.say_3": "Do you have the sample I asked you for?",
  "npc.angelo.say_4": "Thanks a lot. Let me check the result. Well, I think you need the counteragent. Please apply it to the oasis!",
  "npc.angelo.say_5": "What has happened? You applied the counteragent to the oasis and then it was destroyed by a sandstorm? Keep on investigating the place.",
  "npc.angelo.say_6": "Just get out of my way! You killed this beautiful creature. I have nothing more to say. Damn druid of Crunor!",
  "npc.angelo.say_7": "{Gareth} told you that there are rumours about fake artefacts in the MoTA? And it is your task to check that with a magnifier? I see. I don't need one right now, so you can have one of mine. You find one in the crate over there.",
  "npc.angelo.say_8": "So you found out that one artefact in the MoTA is fake? And {Gareth} sent you to me to get a new artefact as a replacement? Sorry, I hardly know you so I don't trust you. I won't help you with that!",
  "npc.angelo.say_9": "The project is called 'Sandy {Cave} Project' and is funded by the {MoTA}. Its goal is the investigation of this {cave}.",
  "npc.angelo.say_10": "MoTA is short for the recently founded Museum of Tibian Arts. We work together in close collaboration. New {results} are communicated to the museum instantly.",
  "npc.angelo.say_11": "We have no scientific results so far to reach our {goal}, because my workers aren't back yet. Should I be {worried}?",
  "npc.angelo.say_12": "Then I have to find out why they don't return. But I'm old and my back aches. Would you like to go there and look for my workers?",
  "npc.angelo.say_13": "Fantastic! Go there and then tell me what you've seen. I've opened the door for you. Take care of yourself!",
  "npc.angelo.say_14": "We don't know exactly why this cave has now exposed an entry via the {dark pyramid}. It seems that the cave already existed for a long time, however, without a connection to our world. Maybe some smaller earth movements have changed the situation.",
  "npc.angelo.say_15": "We don't know yet to wich extent the cave and the dark pyramid belong together. Thisi s what we try to find out. Maybe the history of this place has to be rewritten.",
  "npc.elane.say_1": "Oh, my winged tiara? Those are traditionally awarded after having completed a difficult {task} for our guild, only to female aspirants though. Male warriors will receive a hooded cloak.",
  "npc.elane.say_2": "So you are saying that you would like to prove that you deserve to wear such a hooded cloak?",
  "npc.elane.say_3": "I'm so excited! Have you really found my crossbow?",
  "npc.elane.say_4": "Did you bring me 100 pieces of lizard leather and 100 pieces of red dragon leather?",
  "npc.elane.say_5": "Were you able to get hold of 5 enchanted chicken wings?",
  "npc.elane.say_6": "Ah, have you brought one piece of royal steel, draconian steel and hell steel each?",
  "npc.elane.say_7": "That's the spirit! I hope you will find my crossbow, |PLAYERNAME|!",
  "npc.elane.say_8": "Yeah! I could kiss you right here and there! Besides, you're a handsome one. <giggles> Please bring me 100 pieces of lizard leather and 100 pieces of red dragon leather now!",
  "npc.elane.say_9": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.elane.say_10": "Good work, |PLAYERNAME|! That is enough leather for a lot of sturdy quivers. Now, please bring me 5 enchanted chicken wings.",
  "npc.elane.say_11": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.elane.say_12": "Great! Now we can create a few more Tiaras. If only they weren't that expensive... Well anyway, please obtain one piece of royal steel, draconian steel and hell steel each.",
  "npc.elane.say_13": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.elane.say_14": "Wow, I'm impressed, |PLAYERNAME|. Your really are a valuable member of our paladin guild. I shall grant you your reward now. Wear it proudly!",
  "npc.elane.say_15": "You don't have it...",
  "npc.elane.say_16": "Then no.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_17": "We are always looking for sniper gloves. They are supposed to raise accuracy. If you find a pair, bring them here. Maybe I can offer you a nice trade.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_18": "I am the leader of the Paladins. I help our members.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_19": "I am the leader of the Paladins. I help our members.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_20": "Paladins are great warriors and magicians. Besides that we are excellent missile fighters. Many people in Tibia want to join us.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_21": "Of course, we aren't as strong as knights, but no druid or sorcerer will ever defeat a paladin with a sword.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_22": "There are many magic spells and runes paladins can use.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_23": "Paladins are the best missile fighters in Tibia!",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_24": "I am a paladin, not a storyteller.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_25": "Every paladin profits from his vocation. It has many advantages to be a paladin.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_26": "We will help you to improve your skills. Besides I offer spells for paladins.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_27": "Harkath Bloodblade is the royal general.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_28": "Some paladins serve in the kings army.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_29": "He has some potential.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_30": "How spineless do you have to be to become a jester?",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_31": "The McRonalds are simple farmers.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_32": "He must have been skilled before he became the way he is now. Such a pity.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_33": "The alcohol he sells shrouds the mind and the eye.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_34": "One of the most important members of our guild. She makes all the bows and arrows we need.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_35": "He sells a lot of useful equipment.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_36": "He and his guildfellows lack the grace of a true warrior.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_37": "A fine warrior and a skilled general.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_38": "King Tibianus is a wise ruler.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_39": "A follower of evil that will get what he deserves one day.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_40": "Mhm, a little too nice for my taste. Still, it's amazing how she endures all those men stalking her, especially this creepy Oswald.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_41": "A skilled healer, that's for sure.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_42": "Just another arrogant sorcerer.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_43": "If there wouldn't be higher powers to protect him...",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_44": "A humble monk and a wise man.",
  "npc.elane.stdmod_45": "Strong man. But a little shy.",
  "npc.humgolf.say_1": "Bah, Farmine here, Farmine there. Is there nothing else than Farmine to talk about these days? Hrmpf, whatever. So what do you want?",
  "npc.humgolf.say_2": "You are here to apologise? Have you got anything that would make me reconsider my decision never to talk to you again about this subject?",
  "npc.humgolf.say_3": "Yeah, of course they can't do without my worms. Mining and worms go hand in hand. Well, in the case of the worms it is only an imaginary hand of course. I'll send them some of my finest worms.",
  "npc.humgolf.say_4": "Hah! Now you talk like a dwarf! That's the spirit! Of course you can have some of my worms. I'll send a bunch to Farmine as soon as possible.",
  "npc.humgolf.say_5": "Uh, how cute! Look how he's snapping for my fingers! You really know how to make an old dwarf happy! Well, so let's try again. Why do you think I should send my precious worms to Farmine?",
  "npc.humgolf.say_6": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_1": "Ah, I vaguely remember that our little allies were eager to build some base. So speak up, what do you want?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_2": "Do you have anything that might change my mind?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_3": "Indeed, indeed. Without the help of Thais, our allies stand no chance! Well, I'll send some money to support their cause.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_4": "In exchange for a truly generous donation, I will offer a special outfit. Do you want to make a donation?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_5": "In that case, return to me once you made up your mind.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_6": "Take this armor as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend!",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_7": "Please make sure you have free slots in your store inbox.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_8": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_9": "You alread have that addon.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_10": "Take this helmet as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend. ",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_11": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_12": "You alread have that outfit.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_13": "You need to donate {armor} outfit first.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_14": "Take this boots as a token of great gratitude. Let us forever remember this day, my friend. ",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_15": "You do not have enough money to donate that amount.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_16": "You alread have that outfit.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_17": "You need to donate {helmet} addon first.",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_18": "Ah, I vaguely remember that our little allies were eager to build some base. So speak up, what do you want?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_19": "So you wold like to donate 500.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear a unique armor?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_20": "So you would like to donate 250.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear unique helmet?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_21": "So you would like to donate 250.000.000 gold pieces which in return will entitle you to wear a unique boots?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.say_22": "Wrong Word.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_1": "What do you want to know? Something about the three different {difficulties}, the {general} rules or the {prices}? Maybe you also want to know what happens when you {die}?",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_2": "There are three difficulties: Greenhorn, Scrapper and Warlord. On each challenge you will be confronted with ten monsters increasing in strength.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_3": "There are three difficulties: Greenhorn, Scrapper and Warlord. On each challenge you will be confronted with ten monsters increasing in strength.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_4": "There are three difficulties: Greenhorn, Scrapper and Warlord. On each challenge you will be confronted with ten monsters increasing in strength.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_5": "That is the easiest way in our arena. The {fee} is 1000 gold. We were setting this up for of our children to challenge some easy monsters and train them for the future.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_6": "The most common difficulty for us. The {fee} is 5000 gold. So if you are experienced in fighting middle class monsters this is your challenge!",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_7": "Only the strongest among us will take this challenge. The {fee} is 10000 gold. If you pass that I promise you the respect of all citizens here. You will be a hero!",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_8": "The fee is either 1000, 5000 or 10000 gold for one try. Remember that if you {die}, it is YOUR problem and you won't be able to get back to your corpse and your backpack.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_9": "It would be better not to die! In every pit there is an emergency exit, the portal to the south. If you die in a pit... well... your corpse and backpack are gone, so you enter the arena at your own risk.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_10": "Basically you pay me a {fee}, and you are sent into an arena with 10 different stages. If you succeed you will be rewarded accordingly.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_11": "My job is to explain about the rules and to get the fee from the competitors.",
  "npc.halvar.stdmod_12": "Well I would rather call it an {Ultimate Challenge} than a mission.",
  "npc.halvar.say_13": "You already paid the fee, go and fight!",
  "npc.halvar.say_14": "So you agree with the {rules} and want to participate in the {challenge}? The {fee} for one try in {",
  "npc.halvar.say_15": "You've already completed the arena in all {difficulty levels}.",
  "npc.halvar.say_16": "As you wish! You can pass the door now and enter the teleporter to the pits.",
  "npc.halvar.say_17": "You do not have enough money.",
  "npc.halvar.say_18": "Come back when you are ready then.",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_1": "Ah, you're here to report about the {key} - any progress?",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_2": "Good. Just chat with the guys. Someone is bound to remember *something* about that key.",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_3": "The key to the dormitory! Finally! You're a real sleuth. Here's your reward.",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_4": "Ah, very good job. That should put a crimp in their activities. Here's your reward.",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_5": "Come back when you have slain {20 mountain trolls!}",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_6": "Ah, very good job. That should put a crimp in their activities. Here's your reward.",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_7": "Come back when you have slain {20 muglex clan footman!}",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_8": "Ah, very good job. That should put a crimp in their activities. Here's your reward.",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_9": "Come back when you have slain {20 minotaur bruisers!}",
  "npc.mr_morris.say_10": "You already done this task.",
  "npc.ulala.say_1": "Come back if you finished the dance.",
  "npc.ulala.say_2": "Please help tribe make Pandor happy! Did you bring us what I asked?",
  "npc.ulala.say_3": "Please find great crystal of Fasuon and pray there for his support!",
  "npc.ulala.say_4": "You prayed to Fasuon! Me saw ray of lights on mountain top! Beautiful it was. Me thank you for your help. Great hunt almost can't go wrong now!",
  "npc.ulala.say_5": "Krunus is God for plants and birth. He hidden in all that grows.",
  "npc.ulala.say_6": "Me thank you! Me will bring sacrifice for Pandor. He surely be pleased with our work. Well your work, but me won't tell him. Teehee.",
  "npc.ulala.say_7": "You do not have these things!",
  "npc.vascalir.say_1": "Welcome, adventurer |PLAYERNAME|. Thank you for offering your help - but you are already too experienced to start this quest. Just go on hunting monsters, you'll be better off that way.",
  "npc.vascalir.say_2": "|PLAYERNAME|, the only thing left for you to do here is to talk to the oracle above the academy and leave for the Isle of Destiny. Thanks again for your great work and good luck on your journeys!",
  "npc.vascalir.say_3": "Greetings, |PLAYERNAME|. Right now I don't need your help. I heard that Lily south-west of here requires assistance though.",
  "npc.vascalir.say_4": "Greetings, |PLAYERNAME|. Right now I don't need your help. You should pay a visit to Tom the Tanner. His hut is south-west of the academy!",
  "npc.vascalir.say_5": "You can find the vault if you go down the stairs in the northern part of the academy. The book should be in a large blue chest somewhere down there - I hope it's not burnt yet.",
  "npc.vascalir.say_6": "I think it's a good idea to go see Paulie before you leave the village again. Just go downstairs and to the right to find the bank.",
  "npc.vascalir.say_7": "|PLAYERNAME|, you need to discover the troll tunnel and find a way to make it collapse. Maybe you're able to use some of the trolls' tools. Make sure they can't enter the village via that tunnel anymore!",
  "npc.vascalir.say_8": "|PLAYERNAME|, the air smells like victory. Head into the orc fortress and vanquish Kraknaknork once and for all. Don't forget to take the items from below the academy!",
  "npc.vascalir.stdmod_9": "OK, dude!",
  "npc.vulturenose.say_1": "Hey, I rarely see a dashing pirate like you! Get in, matey!",
  "npc.vulturenose.say_2": "YOU WILL NOT PASS! Erm ... I mean you don't look like a true pirate to me. You won't get in.",
  "npc.gewen.say_1": "Your weekly ticket is still valid. Would be a waste of money to purchase a second one",
  "npc.gewen.say_2": "Do you want to purchase a weekly ticket for the ore wagons? With it you can travel freely and swiftly through Kazordoon for one week. 250 gold only. Deal?",
  "npc.gewen.say_3": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.gewen.say_4": "Here is your stamp. It can't be transferred to another person and will last one week from now. You'll get notified upon using an ore wagon when it isn't valid anymore.",
  "npc.gewen.say_5": "No then.",
  "npc.gewen.stdmod_6": "Never heard about a place like this.",
  "npc.gewen.stdmod_7": "Do you seek a ride to ",
  "npc.gewen.stdmod_8": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.gewen.stdmod_9": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, {Svargrond}, {Edron}, {Issavi}, {Zao}, {Femor Hills} or to {Marapur} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.tarun.say_1": "I hope you will find my brother.",
  "npc.tarun.say_2": "I thank you! This is more than I could hope!",
  "npc.tarun.say_3": "As you wish.",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_1": "Excellent! Now you may leave ziz area zrough ze teleporter to ze norz. It will bring you to a hidden boat. Ziz boat will take you to ze tournament izle. ...",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_2": "Zere you'll learn anyzing you need to know about ze great tournament.",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_3": "You are zmart for a zoftzkin, but before you begin to feel too zmart, you should know zat we will zeal our deal wiz you drinking a ztrong poizon zat will inevitably kill you if you want to trick me and not attend ze tournament. ...",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_4": "Zo are you ready to drink ziz poizon here?",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_5": "Zere iz a great tournament of ztrengz each decade. It determinez ze granted privilegez for zertain individualz of power for ze comming decade. ...",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_6": "My mazter wantz to zurprize hiz opponentz by an unexpected move. He will uze warriorz from ze outzide, zomeone zat no one can azzezz. ...",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_7": "One of ziz warriorz could be you. Or you could ztay here and rot in ze dungeon. Are you interezted in ziz deal?",
  "npc.ztiss.multi_8": "Ziz iz not for you to azk. I work for zomeone of immenze power. He haz an {offer} for you.",
  "npc.gerimor.say_1": "You have already fulfilled your job to my full satisfaction. The cults are investigated and the final boss is eliminated. I have nothing more for you to do. Fare you well!",
  "npc.gerimor.say_2": "You already done this mission.",
  "npc.gerimor.say_3": "Very nice! Come back if you have found what's going on in this cult.",
  "npc.gerimor.say_4": "You have not finished your work yet. Come back when you're done.",
  "npc.gerimor.say_5": "Here's your reward. Thank you and farewell!",
  "npc.gerimor.say_6": "What a pitty! You can come back, when ever you want, if you have changed your opinion.",
  "npc.guide_edna.say_1": "Would you like me to mark locations like - for example - the depot, bank and shops on your map?",
  "npc.guide_edna.say_2": "Here you go.",
  "npc.guide_edna.say_3": "Well, nothing wrong about exploring the town on your own. Let me know if you need something!",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_4": "Currently, I can tell you all about the town, its temple, the bank, shops, spell trainers and the depot, as well as about the world status.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_5": "The temple is just south west of here. Actually, it's a temple raft and the priestess is somewhat... meow... you'll see what I mean.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_6": "Our bank clerk Znozel is somewhat... special. You can find him north of this harbour and then to the right, past the tavern.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_7": "You can buy weapons, armor, tools, gems, magical equipment, furniture, spells and food here.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_8": "The depot is a place where you can safely store your belongings. You are also protected against attacks there. I escort newcomers there, but it's just north of here.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_9": "I'm the only feline guide in Tibia. I might not have fingers anymore, but with my paw I can still mark important locations on your map and give you some information about the town and the world status.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_10": "Yalahar is a very old city of gigantic size, consisting of a city centre and eight quarters. The beings that are closest to be called rulers of the city are the Yalahari.",
  "npc.guide_edna.stdmod_11": "I'm Jonathan. Pleased to meet you.",
  "npc.ortheus.say_1": "A cookie? Well... I have to admit I haven't had one for ages. Can I have it?",
  "npc.ortheus.say_2": "It'd be better for you to leave now.",
  "npc.ortheus.say_3": "Well thanks, it looks tasty, I'll just take a bi - COUGH! Are you trying to poison me?? Get out of here before I forget myself!",
  "npc.ortheus.say_4": "Wow. These polite young adventurers nowadays. Thank you.",
  "npc.ortheus.say_5": "Hmmm, you don't have tea with you.",
  "npc.ortheus.say_6": "Have you actually brought me a mug of tea??",
  "npc.ortheus.say_7": "What a pity.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_8": "I can't imagine a better place to live.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_9": "Though the city has seen better days, the quality of life is still much better than in most other cities.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_10": "Hm, good question. Maybe old, wise man?",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_11": "I'm used to being called old man. Simple as that.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_12": "I don't know what you're talking about.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_13": "Yes, it's a bit messy down there. Sorry.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_14": "Doesn't ring a bell.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_15": "He rarely comes here.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_16": "A man of the seas.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_17": "He used to visit me for a chat, but ever since that new tavern opened I haven't seen him much anymore.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_18": "He sometimes delivers fruit and vegetables to this quarter.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_19": "Though the city has seen better days, the quality of life is still much better than in most other cities.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_20": "I can't imagine a better place to live",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_21": "Whatever that's supposed to mean.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_22": "I don't have anything that I could give you as a reward. Guess you aren't so selfless after all, huh?",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_23": "They try to protect the city and do a decent job. Well - no, a poor job, I mean a poor job.",
  "npc.ortheus.stdmod_24": "You can bring me a mug of tea if you want to.",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_1": "CHILD! COME BACK WHEN YOU HAVE GROWN UP!",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_2": "YOU ALREADY HAVE A VOCATION!",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_3": "IN WHICH TOWN DO YOU WANT TO LIVE: {CARLIN}, {THAIS}, OR {VENORE}?",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_4": "IN WHICH TOWN DO YOU WANT TO LIVE: {CARLIN}, {THAIS}, OR {VENORE}?",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_5": "{KNIGHT}, {PALADIN}, {SORCERER}, OR {DRUID}?",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_6": "SO BE IT!",
  "npc.the_oracle.say_7": "THEN WHAT? {KNIGHT}, {PALADIN}, {SORCERER}, OR {DRUID}?",
  "npc.moe.say_1": "I guess I could do this, yes. But I have to impose a condition. If you bring me ten sphinx feathers I will steal this ring for you.",
  "npc.moe.say_2": "Thank you! They look so pretty, I'm very pleased. Agreed, now I will steal the ring from the Ambassador of Rathleton. Just be patient, I have to wait for a good moment.",
  "npc.moe.say_3": "If you bring me ten sphinx feathers, I will steal this ring for you.",
  "npc.moe.say_4": "You already delivered the feathers. Be patient while I steal the ring.",
  "npc.moe.say_5": "You're arriving at the right time. I have the ring you asked for. It was not too difficult. I just had to wait until the Ambassador left his residence and then I climbed in through the window. Here it is.",
  "npc.moe.say_6": "I will steal it, promised. I'm just waiting for a good moment.",
  "npc.moe.say_7": "I guess I could do this, yes. But I have to impose a condition. If you bring me ten sphinx feathers I will steal this ring for you.",
  "npc.moe.say_8": "You don't need this ring anymore.",
  "npc.moe.say_9": "I'm upset to accuse myself, the lyre is hidden in a tomb west of Kilmaresh.",
  "npc.moe.say_10": "You already know about the lyre's location.",
  "npc.canary.multiline_1": "The goal is for Canary to be an 'engine', that is, it will be \\z\n\t\t\t\t\ta server with a 'clean' datapack, with as few things as possible, \\z\n\t\t\t\t\tthus facilitating development and testing.",
  "npc.chondur.multi_1": "I guess I cannot stop you then. Since you told me about my apprentice, it is my turn to help you. I will perform a ritual for you, but I need a few ingredients. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_2": "Bring me one fresh dead chicken, one fresh dead rat and one fresh dead black sheep, in that order.",
  "npc.chondur.multi_3": "Ohhhhh Mmmmmmmmmmmm Ammmmmgggggggaaaaaaa ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_4": "Aaaaaaaaaahhmmmm Mmmaaaaaaaaaa Kaaaaaamaaaa ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_5": "Brrt! I think it worked! It's a male stampor. I linked this spirit to yours. You can probably already summon him to you ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_6": "So, since we are done here... I need to prepare another ritual, so please let me work, child.",
  "npc.chondur.multi_7": "Good! Come back once you have collected 5 tribal masks and 5 banana staves.",
  "npc.chondur.multi_8": "I shall grant you a sign of your progress as shaman if you can fulfil my task.",
  "npc.chondur.multi_9": "The dworcs of Tiquanda like to wear certain tribal masks which I would like to take a look at. Please bring me 5 of these masks. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_10": "Secondly, the high ape magicians of Banuta use banana staves. I would love to learn more about these staves, so please bring me 5 of them also. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_11": "If you manage to fulfil this task, I will grant you your own mask. Have you understood everything and are ready for this test?",
  "npc.chondur.multi_12": "Deep in the Tiquandian jungle a monster lurks which is seldom seen. It is the revenge of the jungle against humankind. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_13": "This monster, if slain, carries a rare root called Mandrake. If you find it, bring it to me. Also, gather 5 of the voodoo dolls used by the mysterious dworc voodoomasters. ...",
  "npc.chondur.multi_14": "If you manage to fulfil this task, I will grant you your own staff. Have you understood everything and are ready for this test?",
  "npc.lothar.multi_1": "The stampor in the back? She's my friend, but she came to me out of her own free will. I must admit I've never managed to tame any other stampor. ...",
  "npc.lothar.multi_2": "I heard that there's some sort of voodoo magic which would allow you to summon a stampor, but I'm not a voodoo expert, so I wouldn't know.",
  "npc.lothar.multi_3": "It is said that ferocious creatures once thrived on lush islands in the far northern sea. They died aeons ago when times of great cold came and formed the icy wastes of Svargrond as we know them today. ...",
  "npc.lothar.multi_4": "Travellers from the north have told stories of these creatures, watching them from within the ice in the deepest caves, still vigilant as if frozen in time. 'Ursagrodon' they called them. ...",
  "npc.lothar.multi_5": "With tinder and some kind of fireproof vessel, you could create a device to melt the ice surrounding their remains and see for yourself what this is all about.",
  "npc.lothar.multi_6": "Did you know that you can also create those by yourself? Trade a gold ingot with the sweaty cyclops in Ab'Dendriel for a cup of molten gold. If you use that on a fir tree, you have a small chance to get a golden fir cone. ...",
  "npc.lothar.multi_7": "Those are needed to impress the white deers that roam around Ab'Dendriel sometimes, but I'd wait until you are able to enrage one to make sure it has the necessary strength to carry you.",
  "npc.lothar.multi_8": "That's an interesting one, nothing like I have ever seen myself. What you describe is a device of which I heard that it grants literally 'complete' control over some sort of... artificial thing? ...",
  "npc.lothar.multi_9": "Well, if you ever happen to come about a stroke of luck and find such a thing - use it on an appropriate mount, it will probably be mechanical, driven by... something.",
  "npc.malor.multi_1": "You've met Fahim the Wise? That's good. I'm pretty sure it was easy to give him a nice beating. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_2": "If you should feel like killing blue djinns in our service again, just talk to me about that task.",
  "npc.malor.multi_3": "Well well, human. Not bad. I'm not surprised, since you have done acceptably well in the past. So I suppose I can ask you for another thing. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_4": "Seek out Fahim the Wise. A name which is utter mockery, since he's one of the stupidest Marid I've ever seen. He hides somewhere in Yalahar, probably afraid to come anywhere near Mal'ouquah. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_5": "I suggest you teach that joke of a djinn a lesson he won't forget.",
  "npc.malor.multi_6": "Well well, human. So you really have made it - you have smuggled the modified lamp into Gabel's bedroom! ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_7": "I never thought I would say this to a human, but I must confess I am impressed. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_8": "Perhaps I have underestimated you and your kind after all. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_9": "I guess I will take this as a lesson to keep in mind when I meet you on the battlefield. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_10": "But that's in the future. For now, I will confine myself to give you the permission to trade with my people whenever you want to. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_11": "Farewell, human!",
  "npc.malor.multi_12": "Well, listen. We are trying to acquire the ultimate weapon to defeat Gabel: Fa'hradin's lamp! ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_13": "At the moment it is still in the possession of that good old friend of mine, the Orc King, who kindly released me from it. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_14": "However, for some reason he is not as friendly as he used to be. You better watch out, human, because I don't think you will get the lamp without a fight. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_15": "Once you have found the lamp you must enter Ashta'daramai again. Sneak into Gabel's personal chambers and exchange his sleeping lamp with Fa'hradin's lamp! ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_16": "If you succeed, the war could be over one night later!",
  "npc.malor.multi_17": "So you would like to fight for us. Hmm. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_18": "You show true courage, human, but I will not accept your offer at this point of time.",
  "npc.malor.multi_19": "I guess this is the first time I entrust a human with a mission. And such an important mission, too. But well, we live in hard times, and I am a bit short of adequate staff. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_20": "Besides, Baa'leal told me you have distinguished yourself well in previous missions, so I think you might be the right person for the job. ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_21": "But think carefully, human, for this mission will bring you close to certain death. Are you prepared to embark on this mission?",
  "npc.malor.multi_22": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.malor.multi_23": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_1": "I hope that I am not asking too much of you with this task. I heard of a flower which is currently unique in Tibia and can survive at only one place. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_2": "This place is somewhere in the bleak mountains of Nargor. I would love to have a sample of its blossom, but the problem is that it seldom actually blooms. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_3": "I cannot afford to travel there each day just to check whether the time has already come, besides I have no idea where to start looking. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_4": "I would be deeply grateful if you could support me in this matter and collect a sample of the blooming Griffinclaw for me. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_5": "Have you understood everything I told you and will fullfil this task for me?",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_6": "I have one final task for you, |PLAYERNAME|. Many months ago, I was trying to free the war wolves which are imprisoned inside the orc fortress.",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_7": "Unfortunately, my intrusion was discovered and I had to run for my life. During my escape, I lost my favourite wolf tooth chain.",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_8": "It should still be somewhere in the fortress, if the orcs did not try to eat it. I really wish you could retrieve it for me.",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_9": "It has the letter 'C' carved into one of the teeth. Please look for it.",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_10": "Have you understood everything I told you and will fulfil this task for me?",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_11": "I'm glad that you are still with me, |PLAYERNAME|. Especially because my next task might require even more patience from your side than the ones before. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_12": "Demons... these unholy creatures should have never been able to walk the earth. They are a brood fueled only by hatred and malice. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_13": "Even if slain, their evil spirit is not fully killed. It needs a blessed stake to release their last bit of fiendishness and turn them into dust. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_14": "It does not work all the time, but if you succeed, their vicious spirit is finally defeated. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_15": "I want proof that you are on the right side, against Zathroth. Bring me 100 ounces of demon dust and I shall be convinced. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_16": "You will probably need to ask a priest for help to obtain a blessed stake. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_17": "Have you understood everything I told you and will fulfil this task for me?",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_18": "Listen, my next task for you is not exactly easy either. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_19": "In the mountains between Ankrahmun and Tiquanda are two hydra lairs. The nothern one has many waterfalls whereas the southern one has just tiny water trickles. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_20": "However, these trickles are said to contain water as pure and clean as nowhere else in Tibia. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_21": "If you could reach one of these trickles and retrieve a water sample for me, it would be a great help. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_22": "It is important that you take the water directly from the trickle, not from the pond - else it will not be as pure anymore. ...",
  "npc.ceiron.multi_23": "Have you understood everything I told you and will fulfil this task for me?",
  "npc.queen_eloise.multi_1": "Excellent! Now, let me explain. If you donate 1.000.000.000 gold pieces, you will be entitled to wear a unique outfit. ...",
  "npc.queen_eloise.multi_2": "You will be entitled to wear the {armor} for 500.000.000 gold pieces, {helmet} for an additional 250.000.000 and the {boots} for another 250.000.000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.queen_eloise.multi_3": "What will it be?",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_1": "These caves are incredibly beautiful, {crystals} in vibrant colours grow there like exotic flowers. There are more than a few captains who send down their men in order to quarry the precious crystals. ...",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_2": "But there are few volunteers. Often the crystal gatherers disappear and are never seen again. Other poor fellows then meet their former shipmates in the form of ghosts or skeletons. It's a {cursed} area, something evil is down there!",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_3": "As for myself I haven't been down there. But I heard some disturbing rumours. In these caves are wonderful crystal formations. Some more poetically inclined fellows call them the crystal gardens. ...",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_4": "At first glance it seems to be a beautiful - and precious - surrounding. But in truth, deep down in these caverns exists an old evil. Want to hear more?",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_5": "In my humble opinion a pirate should win a fortune by boarding ships not by crawling through caves and tunnels. But who am I to bring into question the captain's decision. All I know is that they sell the crystals at a high price. ...",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_6": "A certain amount of the crystals is ground to crystal dust with a special kind of mill. Don't ask me why. Some kind of magical component perhaps that they sell to mages and sorcerers.",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_7": "The evil I mentioned is a strange crystal, imbued with some kind of unholy energy. It is very hard to destroy, no weapon is able to shatter the thing. Maybe a jarring, very loud sound could destroy it. ...",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_8": "I heard of creatures, that are able to utter ear-splitting sounds. Don't remember the name, though. Would you go down there and try to destroy the crystal?",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_9": "As for myself I haven't been down there. But I heard some disturbing rumours. In these caves are wonderful crystal formations. Some more poetically inclined fellows call them the crystal gardens. ...",
  "npc.one_eyed_joe.multi_10": "At first glance it seems to be a beautiful - and precious - surrounding. But in truth, deep down in these caverns exists an old evil. Want to hear more?",
  "npc.curos.multi_1": "First we will test your strength and endurance. You'll have to face one of the most experienced Mooh'Tah masters. As you don't stand a chance to beat such an opponent, your test will be simply to survive. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_2": "Face him in a battle and survive for two minutes. If you do, we will be willing to assume that your are prepared for the life in these lands. Enter the ring of battle, close to my quarter. Return to me after you have passed this test.",
  "npc.curos.multi_3": "Finally, our enemy's vision is obscured. Now we can move in for some more daring raids until they replace their scrying device. You have proven yourself brave and useful so far. With that, you bought your allies some more days to live. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_4": "Here is a reward. It's a strange tome that we've found in the lizard ruins. Maybe it is of some value for you or your allies.",
  "npc.curos.multi_5": "We are aware that the lizards use magic to spy on us. In the Dragonblaze Mountains north of here, there is a tower which can only be entered through one of their underground fortresses. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_6": "In this tower, there must be some accessory used for magical scrying. Some pond, a crystal ball, or a mirror maybe - it has to be something shiny. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_7": "Usually we would send one of our youngsters on such a mission, but we are few and there is little new blood in our ranks. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_8": "We can't send a Mooh'Tah master on such a trivial assignment, neither can we use orcs for an infiltration mission. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_9": "This is your chance to show us your potential. Infiltrate this tower and destroy their scrying device. Once you have blinded our enemy, we might respect you somewhat more.",
  "npc.curos.multi_10": "So you still think you can be of any use for us? Words are cheap and easy. Admittedly, you've passed our first test but even some resilient beast might have accomplished that. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_11": "Your actions will tell if you are only yelping for attention like a puppy or if you have the teeth of a wolf. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_12": "A first tiny step was taken. You survived the test and ensured the survival of your allies for a while. Now it is time to make the next step. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_13": "So listen human: Our rule over the orcs is not unchallenged. Of course now and then someone shows up who thinks he can defeat us. Usually these fights end fast and bloody in the ring. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_14": "Right now, some coward from our midst, who is too afraid to face us in single combat, has gathered a group of followers, hoping more will follow and change sides. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_15": "With your help, his defeat will not only be deadly but also humiliating and so discourage others to follow his example. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_16": "You will seek out this rebel commander in his hideout and kill him. We will show them that not even a Mooh'Tah master is needed to get rid of such wannabe leaders but that a mere human can handle them. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_17": "Find him in the mountain north-west of here and kill him. If you find any loot, you can keep it.",
  "npc.curos.multi_18": "We have seen that you can fight and survive. Yet, it will also need cleverness and courage to survive in these lands. We might see later if you've got what it takes. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_19": "However, I stand to my word - our hordes will spare your insignificant piece of rock for now. Time will tell if you are worthy living next to us. ...",
  "npc.curos.multi_20": "Still, it will take years until we might consider you as an ally, but this is a start at least.",
  "npc.izsh.multi_1": "Fine, zo let'z prozeed. You uzed forged documentz to enter our zity, killed zeveral guardz who enjoyed a quite excluzive and expenzive training, deztroyed rare magical devizez in ze pozzezzion of ze emperor. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_2": "Ze good newz iz, your zree cheztz of platinum should be nearly enough to pay ze finez. Lucky you, ziz could have left you broke. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_3": "Zere are alzo zertain noble familiez complaining about ze murder of zeveral of zeir beloved onez. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_4": "I zink I can make a deal wiz ze noblez by zelling zem your property in ze zity. Your prezenze would ruin ze houze prizez zere anyway. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_5": "Of courze zat will not zuffize to compenzate zeir grief, zo I guezz you'll have to part wiz zat elite armor, too. Zadly, prizez for armor are on an all time low right now. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_6": "But luckily you ztill have zat mana cazket. Well, you had it. Now we have to zell it. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_7": "But not all iz lozt my blank-zkinned vizitor. According to my calculationz, zere iz ztill a bit left. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_8": "I zink we can zave you zome gold and zome treazurez, and you can keep one pieze of your elite armor at leazt. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_9": "You will find your rewardz in one of ze old zupply zellarz. Beware of ze ratz zough. ...",
  "npc.izsh.multi_10": "Ze rednezz of your faze and ze zound you make wiz your teez iz obviouzly a zign of gratitude of your zpeziez! I am flattered, but pleaze leave now az I have to attend to zome important buzinezz.",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_1": "Thank you my friend. The local representative of the explorers society has asked for our help ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_2": "You know their ways better than my people do and are probably best suited to represent us in this matter.",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_3": "Search for Lurik and talk to him about aprobable mission he might have for you.",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_4": "You encountered the restless ghost of my apprentice Tylaf in the old mines? We must find out what has happened to him. I enable you to talk to his spirit ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_5": "Talk to him and then report to me about your mission.",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_6": "Yes, I can feel it! The spirits are in touch with the obelisks. We will begin to channel a spell of ice on the caves. That will prevent the melting of the ice there ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_7": "If you would like to help us, you can turn in frostheart shards from now on. We use them to fuel our spell with the power of ice. ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_8": "Oh, and before I forget it - since you have done a lot to help us and spent such a long time in this everlasting winter, I have a special present for you. ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_9": "Take this outfit to keep your warm during your travels in this frozen realm!",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_10": "These are alarming news and we have to act immediately. Take this spirit charm of cold. Travel to the mines and find four special obelisks to mark them with the charm ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_11": "I can feel their resonance in the spirits world but we cant reach them with our magic yet. They have to get into contact with us in a spiritual way first ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_12": "This will help us to concentrate all our frost magic on this place. I am sure this will prevent to melt any significant number of demons from the ice ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_13": "Report about your mission when you are done. Then we can begin with the great ritual of summoning the children of Chyll ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_14": "I will also inform Lurik about the events. Now go, fast!",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_15": "There is no need to report about your mission. To be honest, Ive sent a divination spirit with you as well as a couple of destruction spirits that were unleashed when you approached the altar ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_16": "Forgive me my secrecy but you are not familiar with the spirits and you might have get frightened. The spirits are at work now, destroying the magic with that those evil creatures have polluted Helheim ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_17": "I cant thank you enough for what you have done for the spirits of my people. Still I have to ask: Would you do us another favour?",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_18": "There is indeed an important mission. For a long time, the spirits have been worried and have called us for help. It seems that some of our dead have not reached the happy hunting grounds of after life ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_19": "Everything we were able to find out leads to a place where none of our people is allowed to go. Just like we would never allow a stranger to go to that place ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_20": "But you, you are different. You are not one of our people, yet you have proven worthy to be one us. You are special, the child of two worlds ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_21": "We will grant you permission to travel to that isle of Helheim. Our legends say that this is the entrance to the dark world. The dark world is the place where the evil and lost souls roam in eternal torment ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_22": "There you find for sure the cause for the unrest of the spirits. Find someone in Svargrond who can give you a passage to Helheim and seek for the cause. Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_23": "We could indeed need some help. These are very cold times. The ice is growing and becoming thicker everywhere ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_24": "The problem is that the chakoyas may use the ice for a passage to the west and attack Svargrond ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_25": "We need you to get a pick and to destroy the ice at certain places to the east. You will quickly recognise those spots by their unstable look ...",
  "npc.hjaern.multi_26": "Use the pickaxe on at least three of these places and the chakoyas probably won't be able to pass the ice. Once you are done, return here and report about your mission.",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_1": "You found the thief! Excellent work, soldier! You are doing well - for a human, that is. Here - take this as a reward. ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_2": "Since you have proven to be a capable soldier, we have another mission for you. ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_3": "If you are interested go to Alesar and ask him about it.",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_4": "Well ... All right. You may only be a human, but you do seem to have the right spirit. ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_5": "Listen! Since our base of operations is set in this isolated spot we depend on supplies from outside. These supplies are crucial for us to win the war. ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_6": "Unfortunately, it has happened that some of our supplies have disappeared on their way to this fortress. At first we thought it was the Marid, but intelligence reports suggest a different explanation. ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_7": "We now believe that a human was behind the theft! ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_8": "His identity is still unknown but we have been told that the thief fled to the human settlement called Carlin. I want you to find him and report back to me. Nobody messes with the Efreet and lives to tell the tale! ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_9": "Now go! Travel to the northern city Carlin! Keep your eyes open and look around for something that might give you a clue!",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_10": "Each mission and operation is a crucial step towards our victory! ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_11": "Now that we speak of it ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_12": "Since you are no djinn, there is something you could help us with. Are you interested, human?",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_13": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.baa_leal.multi_14": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.navigator.multi_1": "I control EVERYTHING from this room, navigating the fate of this land for more than a century now. Can you see all these funnels? My voice travels through them and throughout everything down here! ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_2": "The stones on the beach? The trader up there? That was ME ALL THE TIME! I lured YOU into creating all this chaos up there and down here! ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_3": "You thought you could choose sides? Think again! I nearly led you into the destruction of two species! ME, THE NAVIGATOR! I CONTROL YOU, I OWN YOU! QJELL AFAR GOU JEY!",
  "npc.navigator.multi_4": "Of course you do. And they did, too. They obeyed me. They adored me. They followed me. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_5": "I learnt everything about their culture, their life, their goals and their problems. I found out about vile insect-like creatures inhabiting the surface of the island. And their waiting for the return of Qjell. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_6": "I practically rewrote their history. I WAS THE SECOND COMING. I WAS QJELL. I, THE NAVIGATOR. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_7": "And I navigated them out of their miserable lives. Away from their petty interests. I led them to a greater purpose - to form chaos out of order, to bring back the storm to the seas and to make THINGS MOVE. Do you want to hear the rest as well?",
  "npc.navigator.multi_8": "Hmpf. The armor was working. After some time I was surrounded by darkness and could only see as far as my shimmer glower would me allow to. But I didn't feel the cold - I could even breathe through that helmet. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_9": "I dived into the deep black. Across rugged mountains, vast fields of kelp, swarms of strange fish. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_10": "And then I laid my eyes on a creature I have never seen before. I now know that they call themselves Njey. You would call them the 'Creatures of the Deep' or 'Deeplings'. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_11": "I am now convinced that when they first saw me descending in that suit with the light of the shimmer glower encompassing me, they took me for their God King Qjell. And that's when it all started to make sense. Don't you agree?",
  "npc.navigator.multi_12": "I was once captain of a ship, the Skyflare. We were traders for King Tibianus and on our way home when we got into a storm. We fought hard to escape the cold grip of the sea. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_13": "I myself did what I could to navigate the Skyflare out of this mess. They depended on me. Me, the navigator. And I succeeded. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_14": "However, when the sea calmed down and the rain was finally gone, we recognised that our ship wouldn't move. It wasn't my fault. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_15": "There was a strong gale and we could already see this island on the horizon. There were seagulls all around the Skyflare to lead us to dry land. But the ship did not move a single inch. It was NOT my fault. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_16": "We dived under the bow and saw that it was stuck right on the tip of a sharp rock. The world below us was treacherous, we could see large underwater mountains and a labyrinthine system of caves and holes. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_17": "Some of my men panicked and hijacked the dinghies to reach the island, others tried to swim. I remained on the ship. It was not my FAULT. It was not. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_18": "When none of my men returned, I forced myself to make a decision. Either dying on this dead ship or plunging into the liquid black beneath. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_19": "In my desperation my thoughts fell onto a strange armor - a gift from a trader we dealt with just before the storm. Strange ornaments and fish-like elements decorated this armor. We thought it would fit just perfectly into the captain's cabin. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_20": "He said something like a 'blessed breath' and 'to subdue the drift'. We thought he wanted to sell us worthless decoration and make it look interesting. If I had only listened to what he said. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_21": "I figured that this thing would have something to do with diving or at least protect me from the icy water. I put it on, grabbed a shimmer glower from our storage to light my path and jumped in. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_22": "Do you want me to go on?",
  "npc.navigator.multi_23": "NAAAAARGH. If you promise to leave me alone and NOT TO TELL MY SECRET to anyone - you can have one. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_24": "NO! Not the one I'm wearing. I am BOUND to this device. This suit has granted me a longer life. However, once you have spent a certain time with this - there is no turning back if you know what I mean. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_25": "The armor will merge with your very body. Holding you captive, holding your life in its hands like a ransom. ...",
  "npc.navigator.multi_26": "Using Deepling craft and various components from down here, I created several spare helmets - just in case this one gets damaged. If you return that small golden anchor to me, you can have one. Will you?",
  "npc.rata_mari.multi_1": "You have come for the report? Great! I have been working hard on it during the last months. And nobody came to pick it up. I thought everybody had forgotten about me! ...",
  "npc.rata_mari.multi_2": "Do you have any idea how difficult it is to hold a pen when you have claws instead of hands? ...",
  "npc.rata_mari.multi_3": "But - you know - now I have worked so hard on this report I somehow don't want to part with it. At least not without some decent payment. ...",
  "npc.rata_mari.multi_4": "All right - listen - I know Fa'hradin would not approve of this, but I can't help it. I need some cheese! I need it now! ...",
  "npc.rata_mari.multi_5": "And I will not give the report to you until you get me some! Meep!",
  "npc.gnomargery.multi_1": "On the levels outside, we encountered the first serious resistance of our true enemy. As evidenced by the unnatural heat in an area with little volcanic activity, there is 'something' strange going on here. ...",
  "npc.gnomargery.multi_2": "Even the lava pools we have found here are not actually lava, but rock that was molten pretty much recently without any reasonable connection to some natural heat source. And for all we can tell, the heat is growing, slowly but steadily. ...",
  "npc.gnomargery.multi_3": "This is the first time ever that we can witness our enemy at work. Here we can learn a lot about its operations. ...",
  "npc.gnomargery.multi_4": "How they work, and possibly how to stop them. But therefore expeditions into the depths are necessary. The areas around us are highly dangerous, and a lethal threat to us and the Spike as a whole. ... ",
  "npc.gnomargery.multi_5": "Our first object is to divert the forces of the enemy and weaken them as good as we can while gathering as much information as possible about them and their movements. Only highly skilled adventurers stand a chance to help us down here. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_1": "Don't waste any more time. We need the spyreport of our man in Mal'ouquah as soon as possible! ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_2": "Also don't forget the password to contact our man: PIEDPIPER!",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_3": "You really have made it? You have the report? How come you did not get slaughtered? I must say I'm impressed. Your race will never cease to surprise me. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_4": "Well, let's see. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_5": "I think I need to talk to Gabel about this. I am sure he will know what to do. Perhaps you should have a word with him, too.",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_6": "Don't waste any more time. We need the spyreport of our man in Mal'ouquah as soon as possible! ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_7": "Also don't forget the password to contact our man: PIEDPIPER!",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_8": "I have heard some good things about you from Bo'ques. But I don't know. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_9": "Well, all right. I do have a job for you. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_10": "In order to stay informed about our enemy's doings, we have managed to plant a spy in Mal'ouquah. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_11": "He has kept the Efreet and Malor under surveillance for quite some time. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_12": "But unfortunately, I have lost contact with him months ago. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_13": "I do not fear for his safety because his cover is foolproof, but I cannot contact him either. This is where you come in. ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_14": "I need you to infiltrate Mal'ouqhah, contact our man there and get his latest spyreport. The password is {PIEDPIPER}. Remember it well! ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_15": "I do not have to add that this is a dangerous mission, do I? If you are discovered expect to be attacked! So goodluck, human!",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_16": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.fa_hradin.multi_17": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_1": "As I told you, fiendish ice creatures dragged my egg into the lower caves. ...",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_2": " Without enough heat the egg will die soon. Venture there and save my hatchling and the knowledge you seeek shall be yours!",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_3": "Grrr.",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_4": "So return to the upper tunnels where cultists and ice golems dwell. Somewhere in these tunnels you will find a small prison haunted by a ghost. South of this prison cell there is a tunnel that will lead you eastwards. ...",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_5": "Follow the tunnel until you reach a small cave. Step down and down until you see a blue energy field. It will lead you to my egg. It is sealed so that not everyone may enter the room. But you have the permission now.",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_6": "Wretched creatures of ice have stolen my egg that was close to hatching. ...",
  "npc.a_dragon_mother.multi_7": " Since I'm to huge to enter those lower Tunnels I have to ask you to take care of my {egg}. Will you do this?",
  "npc.the_dream_master.multi_1": "So I welcome you as the latest member of the order of the Nightmare Knights. You entered this place as a stranger, butyou will leave this place as a friend ...",
  "npc.the_dream_master.multi_2": "You can always ask me about your current rank and about the privileges the ranks grant to those who hold them.",
  "npc.the_dream_master.multi_3": "The Nightmare Knights are almost extinct now, and as far as I know I am the only teacher that is left. But you might beright and its time to accept new disciples ...",
  "npc.the_dream_master.multi_4": "After all you have passed the Dream Challenge to reach this place, which used to be the process of initiation in the past...",
  "npc.the_dream_master.multi_5": "So I ask you: do you wish to become a member of the ancient order of the Nightmare Knights, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.rock_steady.multi_1": "Have you got anything... what? You want what? A reward? HAHAHAHAAAA!! ...",
  "npc.rock_steady.multi_2": "No I'm just teasing you. I'm really happy about my collection now. ...",
  "npc.rock_steady.multi_3": "Well, I found some kind of weapon a long time ago. I believe it may be especially helpful underwater as it is from the deep folk. In any case it is of more use for you than it would be for me.",
  "npc.rock_steady.multi_4": "I collect everything that reflects light in strange ways. However, I am bored by my collection. And there wasn't anything new to add for years. ...",
  "npc.rock_steady.multi_5": "I like pearls for example - but I have already enough. I also like shells - but I can't even count how many I already own. ...",
  "npc.rock_steady.multi_6": "If you find anything of REAL VALUE - bring it to me. I will reward you well. You don't already have something for me by chance?",
  "npc.bron.multi_1": "Great! You see, I really would love to sew a nice shirt for him. I just need a few things for that, so please listen closely: ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_2": "He loves green and red, so I will need about 50 pieces of red cloth - like the material heroes make their capes of - and 50 pieces of the green cloth Djinns like. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_3": "Secondly, I need about 10 rolls of spider silk yarn. I think mermaids can yarn silk of large spiders to create a smooth thread. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_4": "The only remaining thing needed would be a bottle of warrior's sweat to spray it over the shirt... he just loves this smell. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_5": "Have you understood everything I told you and are willing to handle this task?",
  "npc.bron.multi_6": "I'm impressed... I am sure this was Ajax' idea. I would love to give him a present, but if I leave my hut to gather ingredients, hewill surely notice. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_7": "Would you maybe help me again, one last time, my friend? I assure you that your efforts will not be in vain.",
  "npc.bron.multi_8": "Really! That is such an incredibly nice offer! I already have a plan. You have to teach him that sometimes words are stronger than fists. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_9": "Maybe you can provoke him with something to get angry, like saying... 'MINE!' or something. But beware, I'm sure that he will try to hit you. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_10": "Don't do this if you feel weak or ill. He will probably want to make you leave by using violence, but just stay strong and refuse to give up. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_11": "If he should ask what else is necessary to make you leave, tell him to 'say please'. Afterwards, do leave and return to him one hour later. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_12": "This way he might learn that violence doesn't always help, but that a friendly word might just do the trick. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_13": "Have you understood everything I told you and are really willing to take this risk?",
  "npc.bron.multi_14": "This... person... makes me want to... say something bad... must... control myself. <sweats> I really don't know what to do anymore. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_15": "I wonder if Ajax has an idea. Could you ask him about Gelagos?",
  "npc.bron.multi_16": "Convincing Ajax that it is not always necessary to use brute force... this would be such an achievement. Definitely a hard task though. ...",
  "npc.bron.multi_17": "Listen, I simply have to ask, maybe a stranger can influence him better than I can. Would you help me with my brother?",
  "npc.alesar.multi_1": "So you have made it? You have really managed to steal a Tear of Daraman? ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_2": "Amazing how you humans are just impossible to get rid of. Incidentally, you have this character trait in common with many insects and with other vermin. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_3": "Nevermind. I hate to say it, but it you have done us a favour, human. That gemstone will serve us well. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_4": "Baa'leal, wants you to talk to Malor concerning some new mission. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_5": "Looks like you have managed to extended your life expectancy - for just a bit longer.",
  "npc.alesar.multi_6": "All right then, human. Have you ever heard of the {'Tears of Daraman'}? ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_7": "They are precious gemstones made of some unknown blue mineral and possess enormous magical power. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_8": "If you want to learn more about these gemstones don't forget to visit our library. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_9": "Anyway, one of them is enough to create thousands of our mighty djinn blades. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_10": "Unfortunately my last gemstone broke and therefore I'm not able to create new blades anymore. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_11": "To my knowledge there is only one place where you can find these gemstones - I know for a fact that the Marid have at least one of them. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_12": "Well... to cut a long story short, your mission is to sneak into Ashta'daramai and to steal it. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_13": "Needless to say, the Marid won't be too eager to part with it. Try not to get killed until you have delivered the stone to me.",
  "npc.alesar.multi_14": "So Baa'leal thinks you are up to do a mission for us? ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_15": "I think he is getting old, entrusting human scum such as you are with an important mission like that. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_16": "Personally, I don't understand why you haven't been slaughtered right at the gates. ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_17": "Anyway. Are you prepared to embark on a dangerous mission for us?",
  "npc.alesar.multi_18": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.alesar.multi_19": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.gnomewart.multi_1": "Ah, the test is a piece of mushroomcake! Just take the teleporter over there in the south and follow the hallway. ...",
  "npc.gnomewart.multi_2": "You'll need to run quite a bit. It is important that you don't give up! Just keep running and running and running and ... I guess you got the idea. ...",
  "npc.gnomewart.multi_3": "At the end of the hallway you'll find a teleporter. Step on it and you are done! I'm sure you'll do a true gnomerun! Afterwards talk to me.",
  "npc.eustacio.multi_1": "You are trustworthy enough to take my boat. My agent made sure it takes me to their island. Do you want to take it?",
  "npc.aneus.multi_1": "They used the same trick as against the Red Legion and the orcs ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_2": "... started to fight their non-orcish-allies. After a bloody long fight ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_3": "... the orcs went back to their cities. The city of Carlin was rescued. <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_4": "Since then, a woman has always been ruling over Carlin and this statue ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_5": "... was made to remind us of their great tactics against the orcs ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_6": "... and the Red Legion. So that was the story of Carlin and these Fields of Glory. I hope you liked it. *He smiles*",
  "npc.aneus.multi_7": "She tried to rescue the workers but it was too late. The orcs ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_8": "... started immediately to attack her troops, too. Her royal troops ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_9": "... went back to the city. A TRICK saved the city from DESTRUCTION.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_10": "It is said that the orcish shamans cursed the Red Legion. <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_11": "Nobody knows. But one third of the soldiers died by a disease on the way back. <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_12": "And the orcs wanted to take revenge, and after some days they stroke back! <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_13": "The orcs and many allied cyclopses and minotaurs from all ...<m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_14": "... over Tibia came to avenge their friends, and they killed nearly all ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_15": "... workers and soldiers in the castle. The HELP of the king's sister came too late.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_16": "Most of the Red Legion went to the island by night. The orcs ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_17": "... were not prepared and the Red Legion killed hundreds of orcs ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_18": "... with nearly no loss. After they were satisfied they WALKED BACK to the castle.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_19": "She ordered her loyal druids and hunters to disguise themselves ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_20": "... as orcs from the near ISLAND and to ATTACK the Red Legion by night over and over again.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_21": "The king's sister was pretty upset about the situation there but her brother ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_22": "... didn't want to do anything about this matter. So she made a PLAN to destroy the Red Legion for their CRUELTY forever.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_23": "All rebels were brought to the giant castle. Guarded by the Red Legion, ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_24": "... they had to work and live in even worser conditions. Also some FRIENDS of the king's sister were brought there.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_25": "The development of the city was fine. Also a giant castle was build ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_26": "... northeast of the city. But more and more workers started to REBEL because of the bad conditions.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_27": "The works on this new city began and the king sent his best ... <m>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_28": "... SOLDIERS to protect the workers from ORCS and to make them WORK HARDER.",
  "npc.aneus.multi_29": "Ok, sit down and listen. Back in the early days, one of the ancestors ... <press m for more>",
  "npc.aneus.multi_30": "... of our king Tibianus III wanted to build the best CITY in whole of Tibia.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_1": "Welcome to the Brotherhood! From now on you will walk the path of Bones. A life full of promises and power has just beenoffered to you ...",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_2": "Take it, if you are up to that challenge ... or perish in agony if you deserve this fate ...",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_3": "You can always ask me about your current rank and about the privileges the ranks grant to those who hold them.",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_4": "But know that your decision will be irrevocable. You will abandon the opportunity to join any order whose doctrine is incontrast to our own ...",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_5": "Do you still want to join the Brotherhood?",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_6": "The Brotherhood of Bones has suffered greatly in the past, but we did survive as we always will ...",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_7": "You have proven resourceful by beating the silly riddles the Nightmare Knights set up to test their candidates ...",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_8": "It's an amusing thought that after passing their test you might choose to join the ranks of their sworn enemies ...",
  "npc.the_bone_master.multi_9": "For the irony of this I ask you, |PLAYERNAME|: Do you want to join the Brotherhood of Bones?",
  "npc.gnomespector.multi_1": "Your examination is quite easy. Just step through the green crystal {apparatus} in the south! We will examine you with what we call g-rays. Where g stands for gnome of course ...",
  "npc.gnomespector.multi_2": "Afterwards walk up to Gnomedix for your ear examination.",
  "npc.zirella.multi_1": "Well, you know that old women like me like to talk a lot. If you see three dots at the end of a sentence, I have still something to say and you should not interrupt, like now ...",
  "npc.zirella.multi_2": "Patience is a virtue, young adventurer! So, the quest was to go into the forest south of here and to find a dead tree. Wait, let me continue! ...",
  "npc.zirella.multi_3": "'Use' a tree to break a dry branch from it. Afterwards, drag and drop the branch back to my cart and select 'Use with', then left-click on my cart. Thanks again for offering your help!",
  "npc.zirella.multi_4": "Thank you darling! My cart is right beside me. It's a little complicated: I need some firewood, but it's very difficult for my slightly advanced age. ...",
  "npc.zirella.multi_5": "Please go into the the forest southeast of here. You will find fine old rotten brown trees. Please RIGHT-CLICK in the lower right corner of that tree and choose 'USE'. That way, a branch should appear on the map. ...",
  "npc.zirella.multi_6": "Don't put it in your inventory like before, but instead DRAG it over the map by LEFT-CLICKING the loose branch, HOLDING the LEFT MOUSE BUTTON and moving it over the map. ...",
  "npc.zirella.multi_7": "When you are close to my cart, USE the branch WITH the cart: RIGHT-CLICK the branch on the floor and select 'USE WITH', Then LEFT-CLICK on the cart. Don't worry, you will see what I mean on the way. Thanks and {bye} for now!",
  "npc.corym_servant.multi_1": "Thank you very much! Our smiths are now able to craft heat-resistent weapons and armor. A little reward for you is this. ...",
  "npc.corym_servant.multi_2": "There is one last thing I would like to say to you, there are rumours that this dungeon can only be entered alive. This could mean that there's an unknown dungeon keeper guarding this place, so take care of you!",
  "npc.corym_servant.multi_3": "I see you are interested to change our sitation. The first thing I like you to do is to liberate the jailed coryms. There are three areas with locked doors. You have to find a way to get access. ...",
  "npc.corym_servant.multi_4": "For this reason I will give you access to the second floor. It was closed because it wasn't possible to continue working at these enourmous high temperatures. Furthermore we were instantly attacked by stonerefiners. So take care of you!",
  "npc.corym_servant.multi_5": "You have to know, that our work is very hard and the conditions we have are terrible. The wanted amount is abolutely unrealistic. Beyond that the food we get is never enough. ...",
  "npc.corym_servant.multi_6": "Our workers should give their best while starving. This is not possible. That's the point to {defy} the authority.",
  "npc.siflind.multi_1": "I am pleased to hear that. On the isle of Tyrsung foreign hunters have set up camp. They are hunting the animals there with no mercy. We will haveto find something that distracts them from hunting ...",
  "npc.siflind.multi_2": "Take this jug here and travel to the jungle of Tiquanda. There you will find a race of wood eating ants called termites. Use the jug on one of their hills to catch some of them ...",
  "npc.siflind.multi_3": "Then find someone in Svargrond that brings you to Tyrsung. There, release the termites on the bottom of a mast in the hull of the hunters' ship. If you are done, report to me about your mission.",
  "npc.charles.multi_1": "This passage is shorter and costs less gold - but on the other hand it is also a bit riskier. On this route there are frequent tempests and the severe winds may blow a passenger over board. ...",
  "npc.charles.multi_2": "Few ship captains would sail this route. But if you want to take the risk, I can bring you to Thais, Edron, Liberty Bay or Yalahar for less gold than usual. Interested?",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_1": "Crafted generations ago to rob a creature of its freedom for that it may earn it again truthfully. You will need them if you plan on returning the birds to their rightful home in the glade. ... ",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_2": "Are you in need of another one? ",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_3": "Indeed, you will. Take one of these cages, which have been crafted generations ago to rob a creature of its freedom for that it may earn it again truthfully. Return the birds back to their home in the glade. ...",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_4": "You will find {phials} for water near this sacred well which will take you safely to the glade. No seeds are left, they are in the hands of the intruders now. Have faith in yourself, guardian.",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_5": "My pride is great but not greater than reason. I am not too proud to ask for help as this is a dark hour. ... ",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_6": "This glade has been desecrated. We kept it secret for centuries, yet evil has found a way to sully and destroy what was our most sacred. ...",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_7": "There is only one way to reinvigorate its spirits, a guardian must venture down there and bring life back into the forest. ... ",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_8": "Stolen {seeds} need to be wrested from the {intruders} and planted where the soil still hungers. ... ",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_9": "The purest {water} from the purest well needs to be brought there and poured and {birds} that give life need to be brought back to the inner sanctum of the glade. ...",
  "npc.a_weakened_forest_fury.multi_10": "Will you be our guardian?",
  "npc.sven.multi_1": "Good, but to make barbarian mead we need some honey which is rare here. I'd hate to waste mead just to learn you're not worth it ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_2": "Therefore, you have to get your own honey. You'll probably need more than one try so better get some extra honeycombs. Then talk to me again about barbarian {mead}.",
  "npc.sven.multi_3": "That's the spirit! The barbarian test consists of a few tasks you will have to fulfill. All are rather simple - for a barbarian that is...",
  "npc.sven.multi_4": "Your first task is to drink some barbarian mead. But be warned, it's a strong brew that could even knock out a bear. You need to make at least ten sips of mead in a row without passing out to pass the test ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_5": "Do you think you can do this?",
  "npc.sven.multi_6": "As you have passed all three tests, I welcome you in our town as an honorary barbarian. You can now become a citizen. Don't forget to talk to the people here. Some of them might need some help ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_7": "We usually solve our problems on our own but some of the people might have a mission for you. Old Iskan, on the ice in the northern part of the town had some trouble with his dogs lately.",
  "npc.sven.multi_8": "Amazing. That was as clever and brave as a barbarian is supposed to be. But a barbarian also has to be strong and fearless. To prove that you will have to knock over a mammoth ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_9": "Did your face just turn into the color of fresh snow? However, you will find a lonely mammoth north west of the town in the wilderness. Knock it over to prove to be a true barbarian ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_10": "Return to me and talk about the {mammoth} pushing when you are done.",
  "npc.sven.multi_11": "An impressive start. Here, take your own mead horn to fill it at the mead bucket as often as you like ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_12": "But there is much left to be done. Your next test will be to hug a bear ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_13": "You will find one in a cave north of the town. If you are lucky, it's still sleeping. If not ... well that might hurt ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_14": "Unless you feel that you hugged the bear, the test is not passed. Once you are done, talk to me about the bear hugging.",
  "npc.sven.multi_15": "All of our juveniles have to take the barbarian test to become a true member of our community. Foreigners who manage to master the test are granted the title of an honorary barbarian and the respect of our people ...",
  "npc.sven.multi_16": "Are you willing to take the barbarian test?",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_1": "My experiments, my work - not at the moment, however. I'm on vacation. Trying to get away from it... it's all not right. Why... why am I doing this anyway.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_2": "NO! I should not talk like that, I just... I shouldn't. That's not even ME. I... I used to be MAD. A MAD SCIENTIST! THE BEST! THE... the... WORST! A SUPERLATIVE! Ah, nevermind.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_3": "Well I conduct experiments. Viscosity, consistency and overall elegance of {SLIME}. Fungus, I am currently working on a formula for the perfect {slime fungus}.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_4": "Not... right now, though. I am currently... on {vacation}. {Vacation}, yes. All my experiments went wrong. WRONG. Everything. I tried everything but still.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_5": "It's always the same, the {fungus} grows, I am EXCITED and... well... WHAAAAAM! It just EXPLODES! It spreads, covers everything.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_6": "At least I have my trusty {servants} helping me to clean up. They do ALL the work. Removing ALL the slime. At least they're working as intended. I designed them, you know.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_7": "However, sometimes people come and just... DESTROY them! Destroy my work!! Why? Do those people help me removing the slime instead? NO! Not at all.",
  "npc.sane_mage.multi_8": "All they do is ruining my experiments, my perfect testing conditions. It makes me just FURIOUS! And boy do I get FURIOUS, I tell you.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_1": "The definition of finer things is different for a dragon than for a human. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_2": "A young dragon appreciates diving into a lava pool, while an old dragon just can't stand to get rid of the {lava} afterwards and prefers bathing in boiling water.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_3": "Well, surely some of my kin might whine and complain as they always do. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_4": "You have no idea how backwards thinking some dragons can be. A few are even still idealising the times before the {mists}.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_5": "Being powerful creatures themselves, dragons had no need for inventions. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_6": "However, now that times have changed and the pressure increases, even my kin might slowly start to change in order to {adapt}.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_7": "Your books are an amazing thing. Draconic glyphs are so different. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_8": "They are not only more complicated but also more specific. A single word which always keeps the same meaning is astonishingly effective in its primitive way. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_9": "It helps you to conserve thoughts, stories and history and to share them with others - a {concept} I really appreciate. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_10": "Books are a wonderful {invention}. If you are ever tired of your heroic exploits, take the time to read one.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_11": "The world has changed so much; I'm beginning to feel really old. People have changed, the face of the world has changed, even the laws of nature are no longer the same. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_12": "I think it is the greatest advantage of you {humans} to be more flexible and adaptable.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_13": "There was a time before the gods cast the mists of healing over the world. At that time the dragons ruled and burnt the {world}. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_14": "In hindsight I'm not too proud of this. This was some kind of juvenile bullying.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_15": "The first awoken dragons were quite disoriented when leaving the {mists} and re-entering reality. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_16": "This led to certain vulnerabilities. However, the dragons overcame such shortcomings quickly and soon took their rightful place in the food chain, so to say.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_17": "To be honest, the first dragon hunters weren't {worthy}. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_18": "They used {weaknesses} to their advantage. It took some time before a dragon could be killed in a fair fight.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_19": "I really enjoy a good fight now and then. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_20": "A real pain, however, is the constant annoyance caused by tedious fights against adventurers with more healing pots than brain.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_21": "I dictated my memoirs to a human servant. I like the idea to share my thoughts and memories with humanity with the help of a {book}. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_22": "You are my greatest fans after all. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_23": "If it becomes popular, I might consider an orcish translation or even one in bonelord language. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_24": "By the way, it's a funny story how I learnt the bonelord language. However, I saved it for a possible part two of my memoirs.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_25": "When you are young, you are much more tolerant towards the burden of life. At a certain age even a {dragon} will start to think about if things will go on forever. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_26": "Eventually there comes a time when you decide all the {hassle} isn't worth it anymore and you decide to concentrate on the {finer} things life has to offer.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_27": "Even in {retirement} I sometimes succumb to the temptation of sweet battle. Fighting was so different back in the old {times}. You can read about it in my {memoirs}. There should be a copy lying here somewhere.",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_28": "Have a look at the chests over there. Feel free to take the things you find within. You know, gold, gems and the like. There's also a garment I'm storing here for a while. As it doesn't fit me I have no need for it. ...",
  "npc.the_first_dragon.multi_29": "But it might be a nice outfit for a little human. You also can take the porcelain mask and the feathers. There's a wizard named Muriel in Thais who reportedly embellishes outfits with stuff like this.",
  "npc.morgan.multi_1": "Hm, if you are that eager to work I have an idea how you could help me out. A distant relative of mine, the old sage Eremo lives on the isle Cormaya, near Edron. ...",
  "npc.morgan.multi_2": "He has not heard from me since ages. He might assume that I am dead. Since I don't want him to get into trouble for receiving a letter from a pirate I ask you to deliver it personally. ...",
  "npc.morgan.multi_3": "Of course it's a long journey but you asked for it. You will have to prove us your worth. Are you up to that?",
  "npc.percybald.multi_1": "Great! To clarify, donating 30,000 silver tokens and 25,000 gold tokens will entitle you to a unique outfit. ...",
  "npc.percybald.multi_2": "For 15,000 silver tokens and 12,500 gold tokens, you will receive the {armor}. For an additional 7,500 silver tokens and 6,250 gold tokens each, you can also receive the {shield} and {crown}. ...",
  "npc.percybald.multi_3": "What will you choose?",
  "npc.percybald.multi_4": "Hmpf. Why should I waste my time to help some amateur? I'm afraid I can only offer my assistance to actors that are as great as I am. ...",
  "npc.percybald.multi_5": "Though, your futile attempt to prove your worthiness could be amusing. Grab a copy of a script from the prop room at the theatre cellar. Then talk to me again about your test!",
  "npc.marina.multi_1": "<giggles> It's funny how easy it is to get humans to say what you want. Now, proving it will be even more fun! ...",
  "npc.marina.multi_2": "You want me to touch something gooey, so you have to touch something gooey for me too. <giggles> ...",
  "npc.marina.multi_3": "I love honey and I haven't eaten it in a while, so bring me 50 honeycombs and worship my beauty a little more, then we will see.",
  "npc.marina.multi_4": "This lovely, exotic Djinn is a true poet. And he is asking me for a date? Excellent. Now I can finaly dump this human pirate. He was growing to be boring more and more with each day ...",
  "npc.marina.multi_5": "As a little reward for your efforts I allow you to ride my sea turtles. Just look around at the shores and you will find them.",
  "npc.storkus.multi_1": "Ding, dong, the vampire is dead, eh? So I guess ye' can return to Henricus and tell him that ye' finished your job here. I'm quite sure he has some more challenging task up his sleeve. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_2": "One more thing before ye' leave: I already mentioned the master vampires. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_3": "They are quite hard to find. If ye' stumble across one of them and manage to kill him, he will surely drop some token that proves his death. Bring me these tokens. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_4": "If ye' kill enough of them, I might have a little surprise for ye'.",
  "npc.storkus.multi_5": "While ye' were keeping the lower ranks busy, I could get valuable information about some vampire lords. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_6": "One of them is hiding somewhere beneath the Green Claw Swamp. I expect ye' to find him and kill him. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_7": "But be warned: Without good preparation, ye' might get into trouble. I hope for ye' he will be sleeping in his coffin when ye' arrive. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_8": "Before ye' open his coffin and drag that beast out to destroy it, I advise ye' to place some garlic necklaces on the stone slabs next to his coffin. That will weaken him considerably. ...",
  "npc.storkus.multi_9": "Bring me his ring as proof for his death. And now hurry and good hunt to ye'.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_1": "I don't have any gems. If you bring me some, I can craft a sun catcher for you. Do you have gems?",
  "npc.taegen.multi_2": "Alright, I will craft a sun catcher for you.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_3": "I already crafted one sun catcher for you.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_4": "Please find this plant for me. But know that you'll only find it at night. It resembles a common fern but its leaves are of a lighter green.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_5": "Thank you, friend! Now I can visit Aurita in her underwater grotto!",
  "npc.taegen.multi_6": "That's very kind of you, my friend! Listen: I know there is a spell to transform her fishtail into legs. It is a temporary effect, so she could return to the ocean as soon as the spell ends. Unfortunately I don't know how to cast this spell. ...",
  "npc.taegen.multi_7": "But there is a fairy who once told me about it. Perhaps she will share her knowledge. You can find her in a small fairy village in the southwest of Feyrist.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_8": "Thank you again, mortal being. A sun catcher is similar to a dream catcher but other than the latter it can preserve sunlight rather than bad dreams. I can craft one out of enchanted branches of a fairy tree as well as several enchanted gems. ...",
  "npc.taegen.multi_9": "The branches are no problem, I will find some in the forest. But I don't have any gems. If you bring me some, I can craft a sun catcher for you. Do you have gems?",
  "npc.taegen.multi_10": "Have you found some raven herb?",
  "npc.taegen.multi_11": "Thank you! We are so happy. Now Aurita can take a walk on the beach. And I can visit her secret underwater grotto.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_12": "We are so happy. Now Aurita can take a walk on the beach. But I still can't visit her secret underwater grotto. To achieve this, we need something else: a very rare plant called raven herb. ...",
  "npc.taegen.multi_13": "If eaten it allows an air breathing creature to breathe underwater for a while. Please find this plant for me. But know that you'll only find it at night. It resembles a common fern but its leaves are of a lighter green.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_14": "There is a fairy who once told me about this spell. Perhaps she will share her knowledge. You can find her in a small fairy village in the southwest of Feyrist.",
  "npc.taegen.multi_15": "Yes, there is something. It's a bit embarassing, you must promise not to tell anyone else. I'm in love with Aurita. Well, that wouldn't be a reson to be ashamed, but she is a mermaid. ...",
  "npc.taegen.multi_16": "A faun on the other hand is inhabiting the forests, dancing with fairies and, well, nymphs. But I lost my heart to the lovely Aurita. I can't help it. We would love to spend some time together, but not just sitting on the beach. ...",
  "npc.taegen.multi_17": "I'd love to show her the deep forest I love so much. I have an idea but I can't do it alone. Would you help me?",
  "npc.jack.multi_1": "Ah, also a keen lover of arts I assume? You might have already caught a glimpse of that humble masterpiece over there in the corner - I sculpt sulky sculptures! ...",
  "npc.jack.multi_2": "Sculpting sculptures was my passion since childhood... ...and it was there at my first sandcastle when... ...and it formed... ...and it developed into... ...years of enduring sculpting... ...carved of something like... ...sulky... ...",
  "npc.jack.multi_3": "And that's what I like to do to this very day - hey, hey will you wake up? Were you even listening to me?",
  "npc.jack.multi_4": "I see. Well for starters, I think you're crazy. If I would have 'travelled' in some kind of - device? - that thing should be around here somewhere, or not? ...",
  "npc.jack.multi_5": "What? 'Dimensional fold?' Well, thanks for the information and please close the door behind you when you leave my house. Now.",
  "npc.jack.multi_6": "Oh hm, I've got a handkerchief here somewhere - ah, oh no it's already used, I'm sorry. So, you say that's a real person? Spectulus? I mean - what kind of weirdo thinks of a name like that anyway. ...",
  "npc.jack.multi_7": "And he does what? Hm. Here in Edron? I see. And I was - what? No way. Where? What! Why? And you say you are telling the truth?",
  "npc.jack.multi_8": "So... so this wasn't EVEN REAL? You brought all this ugly furniture here, you destroyed my sculpture... and on top of that you actually CONVINCED mother and my sister!? How can I possibly explain all that? ...",
  "npc.jack.multi_9": "I... I... Well, at least you told me the truth. I don't know if I can accept this as an excuse but it's a start. Now let me return to my work, I need to fix this statue and then the rest of this... mess.",
  "npc.cael.multi_1": "In the modern lizard culture thrones seem to be only a reminiscent of the past. Whereas in the past the rulers of the lizardmen used thrones and other insignia to show their status, in our days they are ruled by dragon kings. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_2": "Those kings seem to be massive dragons of immense power. Of course they do not actually 'use' thrones anymore, but claim them nonetheless as symbol for their position. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_3": "From what I can tell, the lizards are bound to those dragon kings by some kind of magic. I'm not sure what this magic does, but I guess it ensures their loyalty to some extent. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_4": "On an interesting side note - there were some hints in the tome that the dragon kings themselves are somehow bound to the dragon emperor through the same kind of magic. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_5": "It seems this kind of liege system was formed sometime after the arrival of the dragons in this land. It's definitely an interesting field of research and shows us how much we still have to learn and to discover. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_6": "Well, I've certainly learnt how the great old thrones look like. If you bring me some red cloth, I could probably try and reconstruct one for you.",
  "npc.cael.multi_7": "Dragons are of great symbolism for this land. Even before the dragons came here and took control over Zao, the lizards worshipped the dragons as strong mythical beasts. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_8": "When the future dragon kings came here - seemingly from a distant and foreign land - they probably took some advantage of this cult. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_9": "Another symbol - that of the snake - that must have been much more popular than the dragon, faded into unimportance over the years. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_10": "I think in the past, the lizardmen of this country might have worshipped a snake god or goddess just like their brethren in Tiquanda if we can believe the reports from this area. The dragons replaced the snake worship at some point of history. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_11": "The reference to heretics and their extermination suggests that there might have been a rebellion against the dragons, which in turn hints at some close link between lizards and dragons, maybe a forced one. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_12": "While reading this tome, I discovered a drawing of this beautiful statue. I was a skilled sculptor in the past, so I can't resist. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_13": "I'm probably not that good anymore, but if you're interested and find me a red lantern, I could make one of those for you.",
  "npc.cael.multi_14": "It seems that some parts of the tome are just copies from other sources and rather unrelated to each other. As far as I could piece them together, there was a mythical founder of the lizard civilisation. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_15": "His name was Zao and his deeds and exploits are immortalised in lizard folklore. Some of the earliest records in the tomes suggest a slightly different story though. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_16": "Many records talk about an early lizard dynasty, but I doubt that Zao was a single person born into that dynasty. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_17": "My guess is that several members of this dynasty are responsible for or connected to the feats that were attributed to the mythical 'Zao'. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_18": "The improbable lifespan of 'Zao' can thus be explained with the time the Zao dynasty reigned. On the other hand, we all know larger-than-life heroes did exist and some of them had an extremely long lifespan. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_19": "Most likely, he also had children which could explain the mentioning of a Zao family. I think even the lizardmen don't know for sure what happened in such distant past and so this might be one of those riddles that will never be solved. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_20": "It seems that the origin of the Zao dynasty was somewhere in the Dragonblaze Peaks, or rather under them. Legends tell of a large fortress, once erected up the highest peak, but now buried deep underground. Who knows, maybe you'll find answers there?",
  "npc.cael.multi_21": "I think the origin of the Draken sheds some new light on certain aspects of the lizard society. It is obvious from the books that the Draken appeared only after the dragon kings revealed themselves to the lizards. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_22": "It is specifically mentioned that the tide of the battle turned when they joined the army of the lizards. Parts of the tome were obviously erased and later overwritten. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_23": "In the parts of the original text that I was able to reconstruct with the help of some alchemy, there were some references to lizard spawns that were sighted in the Tiquanda area and linked to the snake god. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_24": "Admittedly, it is just a hypothesis that is based on a few hints in these tomes and my correspondence about serpent spawns with the sage Edowir... ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_25": "...However, considering everything that I could figure out about their origin, they seem to hatch from the same eggs like ordinary lizardmen. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_26": "It seems that some of those eggs are imbued with spiritual or magical power and as a result bear a serpent spawn. It appears that this changed when the dragon emperor became the ruler of this land. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_27": "Unlike serpent spawns, the Draken hatched from some of the eggs in the hatcheries. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_28": "I can only imagine what this might imply. As I said, it's only a theory, but I think a quite valid one and I'd treasure any additional information about that topic. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_29": "In the meantime, I've also talked to Esrik about some information that I found in the tome concerning weaponry and armory. Knowing this dwarf, he might have some interesting offers for you by now.",
  "npc.cael.multi_30": "You know, while all this talk about growing and preparing rice might sound boring, there are actually some bits of vital information hidden in all those lists. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_31": "It seems that not only the loss of the southern area hampered the rice harvest of the lizards. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_32": "Ever since the dragon kings established their reign, the harvest constantly got worse. And this is not all! It's reported that everything that is growing in this land experienced a fertility decrease. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_33": "Even the lizards themselves seem to suffer from a population decline. It's widely blamed to a plague that ravaged the land in the past, but that seems unlikely given the fact that also plants and various animals were affected. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_34": "Additionally, several plants changed in shape and became poisonous or toxic. Also, some new-born lizards seem to be affected by this. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_35": "According to the descriptions, I'd call them mentally unstable, but their people see them as 'blessed by the dragon emperor'. I assume there are strange forces at work in this land, and I have a bad feeling about it. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_36": "Anyway, you know what else was mentioned in this book? A path down to a hidden cave system below the Muggy Plains. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_37": "Apparently, at first this system was used to hide - or rather to get rid of - new-born lizards that carried the sign of corruption - before the lizards decided to view it as a blessing. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_38": "Who knows what happens down there now - maybe it's worth a look, maybe not. Maybe you won't even discover anything. In any case, be careful.",
  "npc.cael.multi_39": "Maybe you don't know that the great steppe was once a fertile ground. Well, to be precise - in the distant past it probably did not look any different from what it looks today. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_40": "But when the lizard civilisation was at its peak, they apparently developed advanced irrigation systems to water the steppe and used this area as major source for their supplies on rice and other food. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_41": "Back in those times, the lizard population was immense and their need of supplies tremendous. Therefore, they did not allow other races to co-exist and exterminated most of them almost completely. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_42": "Some relics of the settlements of the pre-lizard cultures can still be found. Most of them were probably converted by the victorious lizardmen into something that suited their purposes better. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_43": "All that talk about relics reminds me about something I've recently seen when getting some fresh air up in the mountains. Right next to the carpet pilot - may earth protect me from ever having to step on that thing - was an old lizard relic. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_44": "Incredible how far their realm might have stretched at the peak of their civilisation! Time left its marks on the relic and I suppose it looks rather dangerous, but I am convinced that it is safe. You should try it out sometime.",
  "npc.cael.multi_45": "Well, to be honest it doesn't say much about humans in this book. However, it seems that the humans on this continent used to live in the steppe. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_46": "In the great war against dragons and lizards, they didn't stand the slightest chance due to lack of equipment and well, let's face it, intelligence. The other races were superior in every way. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_47": "They were driven back into the mountains and survived by growing mushrooms, collecting herbs and probably hunting smaller animals. Today, the orcs pose a major threat to them, so I guess they need every help they can possibly get. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_48": "Anyway! The humans seem to make a so-called 'great hunt' now and then, and for that they play war instruments. If you're interested in drums or a didgeridoo and want to trade, let me know. I've recreated a few, they don't actually sound bad!",
  "npc.cael.multi_49": "Have you ever seen the towers of the large lizard city south-east of Zao? It's the last one south of the mountains and who knows how long they are able to hold it. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_50": "It's under constant and heavy siege by the steppe orcs and minotaurs. Sometimes they manage to crush the gates and storm the city. Watch out, you probably don't want to stumble right into the middle of a war. Or maybe you do? ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_51": "Anyway, I found another nice pattern in this book. It's for a lizard carrying device. I've given it to Pompan, just in case you're interested.",
  "npc.cael.multi_52": "I discovered an interesting recipe in this Tome of Knowledge. Maybe you've seen the large rice terraces in Muggy Plains - that is how the lizardmen apparently call that region. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_53": "The book is a lot of blabla about how they cultivate and harvest their rice, but there's something we could actually learn, and that is a certain way to prepare that rice. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_54": "If you ever come across a ripe rice plant, bring it to Swolt in the tavern and he might help you prepare it - grumpily.",
  "npc.cael.multi_55": "According to what I've read in that tome, the Draken seem to be a crossbreed between lizards and dragons, combining the dragons' strength with the lizards' swiftness. They seem to be the main figures in the dragons' internal quarrels. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_56": "They can't fly and are stuck with walking on two feet, but else they combine the best of two worlds - they are intelligent, powerful and both strong magic users and skilled weapon wielders. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_57": "Have you been to one of their settlements yet? They seem to have really beautifully adorned weapon racks. I've given a construction plan of such a rack to Esrik. Maybe he can recreate it.",
  "npc.cael.multi_58": "Did you know that most of the minotaurs you might have met by now do not originally come from Zao? The original minotaur race stood no chance against the united force of dragons and lizards. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_59": "Most of them were killed and captured, but a few of them were able to flee the continent. They found other minotaurs, mighty Mooh'Tah masters, and told them their story. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_60": "The Mooh'Tah masters actually found the continent Zao and started to look for their lost brothers, but it doesn't say whether they actually found any survivors. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_61": "In the tome, there was also a really nice pattern of a carrying device that might have been used by minotaurs. Or maybe by enemies of minotaurs. I've given it to Pompan. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_62": "Maybe he can find a way to use it... we dwarfs are not that skilled when it comes to fashion.",
  "npc.cael.multi_63": "Did you know that the lizardmen were among the first races roaming this continent? They were waging war against the orcs, minotaurs and humans on Zao and for a long time it seemed that the forces were even. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_64": "However, a while later, also a race of dragons arrived on this continent. Seeing the lizards as distant relatives, they decided to support their war, and together they drove all other races back into the steppe. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_65": "It turned out though that the dragonkin didn't really view the lizards as allies but as servants and demanded gold and slaves for their help. Part of the lizard population agreed and obeyed their new masters, the others stirred up a violent rebellion. ...",
  "npc.cael.multi_66": "It doesn't really say what happened afterwards, but in the book were also pictures of special symbols the lizards use for their flags and banners. I've given this to Pompan. Maybe he can find a way to use it.",
  "npc.umar.multi_1": "Oh. Ok. Welcome then. You may pass. ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_2": "And don't forget to kill some Efreets, now and then.",
  "npc.umar.multi_3": "If you want to enter our fortress you have to become one of us and fight the Efreet. ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_4": "So, are you willing to do so?",
  "npc.umar.multi_5": "How dare you lie to me?!? The caliph should choose his envoys more carefully. We will not accept his peace-offering ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_6": "...but we are always looking for support in our fight against the evil Efreets. Tell me if you would like to join our fight.",
  "npc.umar.multi_7": "I should go and tell Fa'hradin. ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_8": "I am impressed you know our address of welcome! I honour that. So tell me who sent you on a mission to our fortress?",
  "npc.umar.multi_9": "Whoa? You know the word! Amazing, |PLAYERNAME|! ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_10": "I should go and tell Fa'hradin. ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_11": "Well. Why are you here anyway, |PLAYERNAME|?",
  "npc.umar.multi_12": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_13": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.umar.multi_14": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.umar.multi_15": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.duncan.multi_1": "I am glad to hear this. Please listen. The pirates on Nargor are breeding tortoises. They think eating tortoises makes a hard man even harder. ...",
  "npc.duncan.multi_2": "However I am quite fond of tortoises and can't stand the thought of them being eaten. So I convinced Captain Striker that I can train them to help us. As a substitute for rafts and such ...",
  "npc.duncan.multi_3": "All I need is one tortoise egg from Nargor. This is the opportunity to save a tortoise from a gruesome fate! ...",
  "npc.duncan.multi_4": "I will ask Sebastian to bring you there. Travel to Nargor, find their tortoise eggs and bring me at least one of them.",
  "npc.duncan.multi_5": "Listen, the task is not that hard. Simply prove that you are with us and not with the pirates from Nargor by bringingme some of their belongings. ...",
  "npc.duncan.multi_6": "Bring me 100 of their eye patches, 100 of their peg legs and 100 of their hooks, in that order. ...",
  "npc.duncan.multi_7": "Have you understood everything I told you and are willing to handle this task?",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_1": "You are a noble soul! So listen: for many decades, over a century actually, the city of {Rathleton} had an Ambassador here in {Issavi}. ...",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_2": "{Kilmaresh} and {Oramond} maintain important commercial relations, and for this reason Rathleton has an envoy here. In the past, the relations were good but now ..",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_3": "I hate to admit it but I heavily suspect that the current {Ambassador} is a traitor and consorts with the forbidden cult of {Fafnar}. I have several hints and {Kallimae} saw it in one of her visions. ...",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_4": "But the vision of a Kilmareshian seer is no proof they will ever accept in Rathleton. And without proof we can't banish the {Ambassador}, this would cause major diplomatic fallout or even a war. I can't risk that. ...",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_5": "I need unequivocal evidence that the {Ambassador} conspires with the Fafnar cultists. Please go to his residence in the eastern part of the city and search for letters, journals ... anything that could prove him guilty.",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_6": "It seems that he destroyed every visible evidence of his treason. That's very unfortunate and I see only one remaining possibility: You need to see the {Ambassador}'s memories. ...",
  "npc.eshaya.multi_7": "But there is only one way to achieve this: You have to find a Ring of {Secret Thoughts}. Legend has it that a monstrous being called {Urmahlullu} has such a ring. If the myths are true you can find this creature in a subterranean tomb south of Issavi.",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.multi_1": "Normally we don't assign missions to civilians - and particularly to MALE civilians - but in this case I think we can make an exception. ...",
  "npc.bunny_bonecrusher.multi_2": "I need a courier to deliver a parcel to the watchtower in Femor Hills. You think you can handle that??",
  "npc.scrutinon.multi_1": "He travelled on the very ground to reach the hostile shores of Quirefang. He used something that turned the soil and carved a way to the island. ...",
  "npc.scrutinon.multi_2": "You will need to follow his trail if you want to reach it.",
  "npc.scrutinon.multi_3": "This island is cleft. Go there only prepared or you will meet your end. The surface of this forgotten rock is a barren wasteland full of hostile creatures. ...",
  "npc.scrutinon.multi_4": "Its visage is covered with holes and tunnels in which its leggy inhabitants are hiding. Its bowels filled with the strangest creatures, waiting to feast on whatever dares to disturb their hive. ...",
  "npc.scrutinon.multi_5": "And you will find no shelter in Quirefang's black depths, where the creatures of the deep are fulfilling a dark prophecy. ...",
  "npc.scrutinon.multi_6": "It is impossible to reach it by ship or boat. However, there was one before you. A {visitor} who found a way to enter the island.",
  "npc.the_beggar_king.multi_1": "Fine. But the first thing you have to know is that we are not the city's problem. We are just trying to survive. We usually seek shelter in the sewers.",
  "npc.the_beggar_king.multi_2": "There we are comparatively warm and safe. At least we were. But recently something has changed. There is {something} in the sewers. And it is hunting us.",
  "npc.razan.multi_1": "Alright, then listen to the following requirements. We are currently in dire need of ape fur since the Caliph has requested a new bathroom carpet. ...",
  "npc.razan.multi_2": "Thus, please bring me 100 pieces of ape fur. Secondly, it came to our ears that the explorer society has discovered a new undersea race of fishmen. ...",
  "npc.razan.multi_3": "Their fins are said to allow humans to walk on water! Please bring us 100 of these fish fin. ...",
  "npc.razan.multi_4": "Third, if the plan of walking on water should fail, we need enchanted chicken wings to prevent the testers from drowning. Please bring me two. ...",
  "npc.razan.multi_5": "Last but not least, just drop by with 100 pieces of blue cloth and I will happily show you how to make a turban. ...",
  "npc.razan.multi_6": "Did you understand everything I told you and are willing to handle this task?",
  "npc.bozo.multi_1": "You shaved the emperor, but lost the beard? What kind of fool are you? Well, at least he will have a nice surprise when he wakes up ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_2": "Still, as a small recognition of your accomplishments I'm willing to tell you how to get your own jester outfit. If you are interested in more fun and adventures, ask me for more missions.",
  "npc.bozo.multi_3": "What a foolish decision! You are indeed a worthy candidate! But let's talk about business ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_4": "Being a jester is not just about telling jokes. A good jester heavily relies on requisites ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_5": "Getting some requisites will be your first job. First of all we need a good supply of water squirt flowers ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_6": "I'm making them on my own in my spare time but I need the right material. South of Thais, next to the Whiteflower Temple, you will find the ideal flowers ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_7": "Take a kitchen knife, cut the thickest and healthiest flower and bring it here. Then talk to me about your mission.",
  "npc.bozo.multi_8": "So you want to make a total fool of yourself? Fine with me, but note that becoming a real fool means more than being just an ordinary fool ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_9": "You will have to master a whole series of challenging, lengthy and, above all, totally foolish quests ...",
  "npc.bozo.multi_10": "Are you sure you want to waste a part of your limited lifetime on a quest that makes a fool of yourself and which might award you with the prestigious title of a grand fool in a far away future?",
  "npc.wyda.multi_1": "The blood herb is very rare. This plant would be very useful for me, but I don't know any accessible places to find it.",
  "npc.wyda.multi_2": "To be honest, I'm drowning in blood herbs by now. But if it helps you, well yes.. I guess I could use another blood herb...",
  "npc.wyda.multi_3": "A quest? Well, if you're so keen on doing me a favour... Why don't you try to find a {blood herb}?",
  "npc.wyda.multi_4": "To be honest, I'm drowning in blood herbs by now.",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_1": "So you have mastered the crisis you invoked with your foolishness. I should crush you for your involvement right here and now. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_2": "But such an act would bring me down to your own barbaric level and only fuel the corruption that destroys the land that I own. Therefore I will not only spare your miserable life but show your the generosity of the dragon emperor. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_3": "I will reward you beyond your wildest dreams! ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_4": "I grant you three chests - filled to the lid with platinum coins, a house in the city in which you may reside, a set of the finest armor Zao has to offer, and a casket of never-ending mana. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_5": "Speak with magistrate Izsh in the ministry about your reward. And now leave before I change my mind!",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_6": "The amplified force of the snake god is tearing the land apart. It is using my crystals in a reverse way to drain the vital force from the land and its inhabitants to fuel its power. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_7": "I will withstand its influence as good as possible and slow this process. You will have to fight its worldly incarnation though. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_8": "It is still weak and disoriented. You might stand a chance - this is our only chance. I will send you to the point to where the vital force is channelled. I have no idea where that might be though. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_9": "You will probably have to fight some sort of vessel the snake god uses. Even if you defeat it, it is likely that it only weakens the snake. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_10": "You might have to fight several incarnations until the snake god is worn out enough. Then use the power of the snake's own sceptre against it. Use it on its corpse to claim your victory. ...",
  "npc.awarness_of_the_emperor.multi_11": "Be prepared for the fight of your life! Are you ready?",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_1": "We are still in need of more research concerning environmental as well as psychic ecto-magical influences. Besides more common ghosts we also need some of the harder to come by nightstalkers and - if you're really hardboiled - souleaters. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_2": "We will of course pay for every ghost you catch. You will receive more if you hunt for some of the tougher fellows - but don't overdue it. What do you say?",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_3": "Magnificent! Alright, we will at least need 5 caught ghosts. We will pay some more if you can catch 5 nightstalkers. Of course you will earn some more if you bring us 5 souleaters. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_4": "I heard they dwell somewhere in that new continent - Zao? Well anyway, if you feel you've got enough, just return with what you've got and we will see. Good luck! ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_5": "Keep in mind that the specimens are only of any worth to us if the exact amount of 5 per specimen is reached. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_6": "Furhtermore, to successfully bind Nightstalkers to the cage, you will need to have caught at least 5 Ghosts. To bind Souleaters, you will need at least 5 Ghosts and 5 Nightstalkers. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_7": "The higher the amount of spirit energy in the cage, the higher its effective capacity. Oh and always come back and tell me if you lose your spirit cage.",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_8": "Fascinating, let me see. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_9": "Amazing! I will transfer this to our spirit chamber right about - now! ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_10": "Alright, the device is holding it. The magical barrier should be able to contain nearly 20 times the current load. That's a complete success! Spectulus, are you seeing this? We did it! ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_11": "Well, you did! You really helped us pulling this off. Thank you Lord Stalks! ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_12": "I doubt we will have much time to hunt for new specimens ourselves in the near future. If you like, you can continue helping us by finding and capturing more and different ghosts. Just talk to me to receive a new task.",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_13": "Excellent. Now we need to concentrate on testing that thing. The spirit cage has been calibrated based on some tests we made - as well as your recent findings over at the graveyard. ...",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_14": "Using the device on the remains of a ghost right after its defeat should capture it inside this trap. We could then transfer it into our spirit chamber which is in fact a magical barrier. ..",
  "npc.sinclair.multi_15": "At first, however, we need you to find a specimen and bring it here for us to test the capacity of the device. Are you ready for this?",
  "npc.erayo.multi_1": "Thought so. Could use some help anyway. Listen, I need stuff. Someone gave me a strange assignment - sneak into Thais castle at night and shroud it with cloth without anyone noticing it. ...",
  "npc.erayo.multi_2": "I wonder why anyone would want to shroud a castle, but as long as long as the guy pays, no problem, I'll do the sneaking part. Need a lot of cloth though. ...",
  "npc.erayo.multi_3": "Gonna make it colourful. Bring me 50 pieces of {blue cloth}, 50 pieces of {green cloth}, 50 pieces of {red cloth}, 50 pieces of {brown cloth}, 50 pieces of {yellow cloth} and 50 pieces of {white cloth}. ...",
  "npc.erayo.multi_4": "Besides, gonna need 10 {spools of yarn}. Understood?",
  "npc.carlos.multi_1": "Well, that's how trading with NPCs like me works. I think you are ready now to cross the bridge to Rookgaard, just follow the path to the northwest. Good luck, |PLAYERNAME|! ...",
  "npc.carlos.multi_2": "And by the way: if you thought all of this was boring and you'd rather skip the tutorial with your next character, just say 'skip tutorial' to Santiago. ...",
  "npc.carlos.multi_3": "Then you'll miss out on those nice items and experience though. Hehehe! It's your choice. Well, take care for now!",
  "npc.carlos.multi_4": "Well, that's how trading with NPCs like me works. I think you are ready now to cross the bridge to Rookgaard, just follow the path to the northwest. Good luck, |PLAYERNAME|! ...",
  "npc.carlos.multi_5": "And by the way: if you thought all of this was boring and you'd rather skip the tutorial with your next character, just say 'skip tutorial' to Santiago. ...",
  "npc.carlos.multi_6": "Then you'll miss out on those nice items and experience though. Hehehe! It's your choice. Well, take care for now!",
  "npc.carlos.multi_7": "Well, that's how trading with NPCs like me works. I think you are ready now to cross the bridge to Rookgaard, just follow the path to the northwest. Good luck, |PLAYERNAME|! ...",
  "npc.carlos.multi_8": "And by the way: if you thought all of this was boring and you'd rather skip the tutorial with your next character, just say 'skip tutorial' to Santiago. ...",
  "npc.carlos.multi_9": "Then you'll miss out on those nice items and experience though. Hehehe! It's your choice. Well, take care for now!",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_1": "Marvellous! With this information combined we have all that's needed! ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_2": "So let me see. ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_3": "Hmm, interesting. And we shouldn't forget about the chant! Yes, excellent! ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_4": "So listen: To enter the veiled library, travel to the white raven monastery on the Isle of Kings and enter its main altar room. ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_5": "There, use an ordinary scythe on the right of the two monuments, while concentrating on this glyph here and chant the words: Chamek Athra Thull Zathroth ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_6": "Oh, and one other thing. For your efforts I want to reward you with one of my old outfits, back from my adventuring days. May it suit you well! ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_7": "Hurry now my friend. Time is of essence!",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_8": "About what of your mission s do you want to report? The {museum}, the darashian {desert}, the rumors about strange {fishmen}, the ancient {order}, the mysterious {asuri}, or the lost {isle}? ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_9": "Or shall me {check} how much information we acquired?",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_10": "There's a beautiful but very dangerous palace in the Tiquandan jungle. The young women who live there are actually demons and they are luring unsuspecting mortals in there. ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_11": "A lucky survivor told me about a portal at the very top of the palace that may lead to another asuri hideout.",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_12": "Our world has seen many noble knights and orders throughout the centuries. Most of them vanished a long time ago but only few under such mysterious circumstances as the Order of the Falcon. ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_13": "This noble alliance of honourable knights once resided in Edron to serve the king. Legend has it they vanished practically over night. Rumor has it their disappearance is connected to a forbidden book.",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_14": "Sightings of strange fishmen in Tiquanda are stirring up the region. You should be careful when investigating this. ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_15": "As far as I know a scholar in Edron already dealt with fish-like creatures before.",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_16": "This is ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_17": "An astonishing find to say the least! I'm certain it will help the efforts of accessing the library a lot!",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_18": "I gathered some lore on my own, but I desperately need more information that you might provide me. ...",
  "npc.dedoras.multi_19": "My leads are the {museum} in thais, something strange in the darashian {desert}, rumors about {fishmen}, an ancient {order}, the mysterious {asuri}, or a lost {isle}?",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_1": "Thank you, human being! I guess the thieving troll headed to the mountains east of here. As far as I know you can only reach these mountain tops by diving into a small cave. ...",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_2": "The connecting tunnels will lead you to a mountain where you may discover him. I heard a man named Jerom talking about this when he passed by this river. Perhaps he knows more about it.",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_3": "This is everything that remained of my cloak? That's terrible! However, I guess I can put the feathers together again. Yes, that should be enough feathers. ...",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_4": "Please give them to me so I can restore my cloak. But don't watch me! Swan maidens don't like to be observed. Nature's blessings, human being. I will tell Ikassis that you have been of great assistance.",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_5": "My sister Ikassis sent you? Blessed be her soul! Yes, it is true: I need help. Listen, I will tell you a secret but please don't break it. As you might already suspect I'm not really a swan but a fae. ...",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_6": "But other than many of my siblings I did not take over a swan's body. I'm a swan maiden and this is one of my two aspects. I can take the shape of a swan as well as that of a young maiden. ...",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_7": "But to do so I need a magical artefact: a cloak made of swan feathers. If I lose this cloak - or someone steals it from me - I'm stuck to the form of a swan and can't change shape anymore. And this is exactly what happened: ...",
  "npc.a_swan.multi_8": "A troll stalked me while I was bathing in the river and he stole my cloak. Now I am trapped in the form of a swan. Please, can you find the thief and bring back the cloak?",
  "npc.cledwyn.multi_1": "The following items can be enchanted: {pendulet}, {sleep shawl}, {blister ring}, {theurgic amulet}, {ring of souls}. ...",
  "npc.cledwyn.multi_2": "For sufficient silver tokens you can also enchant: {spiritthorn ring}, {alicorn ring}, {arcanomancer sigil}, {arboreal ring}, {turtle amulet}. Make you choice!",
  "npc.cledwyn.multi_3": "Why, certainly! I'm always up for some small talk. ...",
  "npc.cledwyn.multi_4": "The weather continues just fine here, don't you think? Just the day for a little walk around the town! ...",
  "npc.cledwyn.multi_5": "Actually, I haven't been around much yet, but I'm looking forward to exploring the city once I've finished trading {token}s.",
  "npc.todd.multi_1": "I'd really like to rebuild my reputation someday and maybe find a nice girl. If you come across scrolls of heroic deeds or addresses of lovely maidens... let me know! ...",
  "npc.todd.multi_2": "Oh no, it doesn't matter what name is on the scrolls. I'm, uhm... flexible! And money - yes, I can pay. My, erm... uncle died recently and left me a pretty sum. Yes.",
  "npc.eroth.multi_1": "Recently we found out that they are in the possession of a scrying crystal ball. They can hear all our discussions about tactics and upcoming attacks. ...",
  "npc.eroth.multi_2": "No wonder that they always have been so well prepared. Now you come into play, destroy the scrying crystal ball in Elvenbane. It should be on the top floor. ...",
  "npc.eroth.multi_3": "We don't really know how to destroy it but we suppose it may work if you reflect the invisible power of the ball. The beam should be adjusted to Ab'Dendriel. Take this mirror and give it a try. Good luck.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_1": "Have you heard about {Tiquanda's Revenge}? It is said that the jungle itself is alive and takes revenge for all the bad things people have done to it. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_2": "I myself believe that there is some truth in this clap-trap. Something 'real' which must have a hideout somewhere. Go find it and take revenge yourself! Ask me about the {special} task when you're done.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_3": "You can choose between the {Snapper}, {Hide}, {Deathbine}, the {Bloodtusk}, {Shardhead}, {Fleshcrawler}, {Ribstride}, {Bloodweb}, {Esmeralda}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_4": "{Thul}, {Flameborn}, {Sulphur Scuttler}, the {Old Widow}, {Hemming}, {Tormentor}, {Fazzrah}, {Tromphonyte}, {Bruise Payne}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_5": "the {Many}, the {Noxious Spawn}, {Stonecracker}, {Gorgo}, {Kerberos}, {Ethershreck}, {Zanakeph}, {Paiz the Pauperizer}, {Bretzecutioner} and {Leviathan}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_6": "You can choose between the {Snapper}, {Hide}, {Deathbine}, the {Bloodtusk}, {Shardhead}, {Fleshcrawler}, {Ribstride}, {Bloodweb}, {Esmeralda}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_7": "{Thul}, {Flameborn}, {Sulphur Scuttler}, the {Old Widow}, {Hemming}, {Tormentor}, {Fazzrah}, {Tromphonyte} and {Bruise Payne}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_8": "You can choose between the {Snapper}, {Hide}, {Deathbine}, the {Bloodtusk}, {Shardhead}, {Fleshcrawler}, {Ribstride}, {Bloodweb} and {Esmeralda}",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_9": "Spiffing! You gained 70 hunting points! From now on you can call yourself a 'Trophy hunter'. As a reward I have this special backpack for you and in addition, you can sell some more rare trophies to me. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_10": "Ask me for {special} tasks from time to time.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_11": "Good show! You gained 40 points for the 'Paw and Fur - Hunting Elite'. You have earned the right to join the ranks of those known as 'Big game hunter'. Congratulations! ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_12": "From now on I'll buy more trophies from you!",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_13": "You gained 20 points. It's time for a promotion. You advance to the rank of a 'Ranger'. Congratulations! ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_14": "Oh, I made a deal with Lorek. He ships Rangers from our society - and higher ranks of course - to Banuta, Chor or near the mountain pass to Darama. Just ask him for a passage.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_15": "You gained 10 points! Let me promote you to the first rank: 'Huntsman'. Congratulations! ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_16": "If you find any trophies - either monster heads or other parts of monsters that you don't need - feel free to ask me for a trade.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_17": "Alright, what would you like to hunt? Be aware you won't gain any paw and fur points as you already achieved the highest rank, but you'll get an experience reward and can face bosses. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_18": "You can try {hydras}, {serpent spawns}, {medusae}, {behemoths}, {sea serpents}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_19": "as well as {hellhounds}, {ghastly dragons}, {undead dragons}, {draken} and {destroyers} or maybe {demons}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_20": "Alright, what would you like to hunt? You can try {hydras}, {serpent spawns}, {medusae}, {behemoths}, {sea serpents}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_21": "as well as {hellhounds}, {ghastly dragons}, {undead dragons}, {draken} and {destroyers}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_22": "Alright, what would you like to hunt? {Underwater quara}, {giant spiders}, {werewolves}, {nightmares}, {hellspawns}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_23": "as well as {high class lizards}, {stampors}, {brimstone bugs}, {mutated bats}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_24": "You may not advance in your rank anymore until you've levelled up. But you can accept tasks without getting Paw & Fur points, just for an experience reward and the possibility to fight a boss from the range lower than level 130. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_25": "You can try {underwater quara}, {giant spiders}, {werewolves}, {nightmares}, {hellspawns}, {high class lizards}, {stampors}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_26": "as well as {brimstone bugs} and {mutated bats}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_27": "Alright, what would you like to hunt? {Ice golems}, {quara scouts}, {mutated rats}, {ancient scarabs}, {wyverns}, {lancer beetles}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_28": "or {wailing widows}, {killer caimans}, {bonebeasts}, {crystal spiders} or {mutated tigers}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_29": "You may not advance in your rank anymore until you've levelled up. But you can accept tasks without getting Paw & Fur points, just for an experience reward and the possibility to fight a boss from the range lower than level 80. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_30": "You can try {ice golems}, {quara scouts}, {mutated rats}, {ancient scarabs}, {wyverns}, {lancer beetles}, {wailing widows}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_31": "as well as {killer caimans}, {bonebeasts}, {crystal spiders} and {mutated tigers}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_32": "You may not advance in your rank anymore until you've levelled up. But you can accept tasks without getting Paw & Fur points, just for an experience reward and the possibility to fight a boss from the range lower than level 50. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_33": "You can try {crocodiles}, {badgers}, {tarantulas}, {carniphilas}, {stone golems}, {mammoths}, {gnarlhounds}, ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_34": "as well as {terramites}, {apes}, {thornback tortoises} and {gargoyles}.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_35": "Ah, okay. This time you'll just get an experience reward, no points for our society as you already gained enough points for your level range. Ask me for a {boss} and the choice is yours. ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_36": "Level up and new tasks and thus points will be available.",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_37": "Such brave deed deserves a special reward! Take this holy icon. It neutralises great evil and gives you access to areas which are protected by those forces. But remember ...",
  "npc.grizzly_adams.multi_38": "This is a one-time opportunity! You won't get the holy icon twice.",
  "npc.timothy.multi_1": "Oh, you are the contact person of the academy? Here are the notes that contain everything I have found out so far. ...",
  "npc.timothy.multi_2": "This city is absolutely fascinating, I tell you! If there hadn't been all this trouble and chaos in the past, this city would certainly be the greatest centre of knowledge in the world. ...",
  "npc.timothy.multi_3": "Oh, by the way, speaking about all the trouble here reminds me of Palimuth, a friend of mine. He is a native who was quite helpful in gathering all these information. ...",
  "npc.timothy.multi_4": "I'd like to pay him back for his kindness by sending him some experienced helper that assists him in his effort to restore some order in this city. Maybe you are interested in this job?",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.multi_1": "I didn't dare hope for it! The man told something about selling my babies to the orcs so they could train them as war wolves. ...",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.multi_2": "I guess he mentioned Ulderek's Rock. Please search for them and - be they alive or not - return and tell me what happened to them.",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.multi_3": "I'm heartbroken, traveler. Some months ago, I was taking care of my three newborn whelps. They just opened their eyes and started exploring the wilderness as a hunter came by. ...",
  "npc.ghostly_wolf.multi_4": "He shot me and took my three puppies with him. I have no idea where he brought them or whether they are still alive. This uncertainty harrows me and thus I'm unable to find peace. Will you help me?",
  "npc.gabel.multi_1": "So you've been there and faced Merikh the Slaughterer! Whether you killed him or not, I hope your presence at least scared him. He is so mighty that we can only hope to truly defeat him one day. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_2": "When you've recovered from your fight and would like to kill green djinns in our service again, just talk to me about that task.",
  "npc.gabel.multi_3": "You've done it, human! Daraman be praised! Take this for your efforts. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_4": "What's left to do now is seek out Merikh the Slaughterer, an especially cruel Efreet. He hides somewhere in Yalahar. I don't know if you can kill him, but you should at least try.",
  "npc.gabel.multi_5": "You've proven to be an experienced soldier, human. Though I still hope the war to be over soon, the Efreet are still threatening our tower. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_6": "Thus we need your help in killing the green ones. If you kill 500 green djinns or Efreet for us, I'll reward you with bonus experience and some extra gold pieces. Do you agree?",
  "npc.gabel.multi_7": "Daraman shall bless you and all humans! You have done us all a huge service! Soon, this awful war will be over! ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_8": "Know, that from now on you are considered one of us and are welcome to trade with Haroun and Nah'bob whenever you want to!",
  "npc.gabel.multi_9": "Farewell, stranger. May Uman open your minds and your hearts to Daraman's wisdom!",
  "npc.gabel.multi_10": "All right. Listen! Thanks to Rata'mari's report we now know what Malor is up to: he wants to do to me what I have done to him - he wants to imprison me in Fa'hradin's lamp! ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_11": "Of course, that won't happen. Now, we know his plans. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_12": "But I am aiming at something different. We have learnt one important thing: At this point of time, Malor does not have the lamp yet, which means it is still where he left it. We need that lamp! If we get it back we can imprison him again! ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_13": "From all we know the lamp is still in the Orc King's possession! Therefore I want to ask you to enter thewell guarded halls over at Ulderek's Rock and find the lamp. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_14": "Once you have acquired the lamp you must enter Mal'ouquah again. Sneak into Malor's personal chambersand exchange his sleeping lamp with Fa'hradin's lamp! ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_15": "If you succeed, the war could be over one night later! I and all djinn will be in your debt forever! May Daraman watch over you!",
  "npc.gabel.multi_16": "Sooo. Fa'hradin has told me about your extraordinary exploit, and I must say I am impressed. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_17": "Your fragile human form belies your courage and your fighting spirit. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_18": "I hardly dare to ask you because you have already done so much for us, but there is a task to be done, and I cannot think of anybody else who would be better suited to fulfill it than you. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_19": "Think carefully, human, for this mission will bring you into real danger. Are you prepared to do us that final favour?",
  "npc.gabel.multi_20": "So you would like to fight for us, would you. Hmm. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_21": "That is a noble resolution you have made there, human, but I'm afraid I cannot accept your generous offer at this point of time. ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_22": "Do not get me wrong, but I am not the kind of guy to send an inexperienced soldier into certain death! So you might ask around here for a more suitable mission.",
  "npc.gabel.multi_23": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.gabel.multi_24": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.berenice.multi_1": "Since you have already proved to be a valuable member of our society, I will happily entrust you with this mission, but there are a few things which you need to know, so listen carefully. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_2": "Calassa is an underwater settlement, so you are in severe danger of drowning unless you are well-prepared. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_3": "We have developed a new device called 'Helmet of the Deep' which will enable you to breathe even in the depths of the ocean. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_4": "I will instruct Captain Max to bring you to Calassa and to lend one of these helmets to you. These helmets are very valuable, so there is a deposit of 5000 gold pieces on it. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_5": "While in Calassa, do not take the helmet off under any circumstances. If you have any questions, don't hesitate to ask Captain Max. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_6": "Your mission there, apart from observing the Quara, is to retrieve a special logbook from one of the shipwrecks buried there. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_7": "One of our last expeditions there failed horribly and the ship sank, but we still do not know the exact reason. ...",
  "npc.berenice.multi_8": "If you could retrieve the logbook, we'd finally know what happened. Have you understood your task and are willing to take this risk?",
  "npc.elliott.multi_1": "A sacrificial site? Damn, sounds like some freakish cult or something. Just great. And this ancient structure you talked about that's not part of the sewers? You'd better see the local historian about that, man. ...",
  "npc.elliott.multi_2": "He can make more sense of what you found there. His name is Barazbaz. He should be in the magistrate building.",
  "npc.elliott.multi_3": "Wow, you already did it, that's fast. I'm used to a more laid-back attitude from most people. It's a shame to risk losing you to some collapsing tunnels, but a deal is a deal. ...",
  "npc.elliott.multi_4": "I hereby grant you the permission to enter the abandoned part of the sewers. Take care, man! ...",
  "npc.elliott.multi_5": "If you find something interesting, come back to talk about the {abandoned sewers}.",
  "npc.elliott.multi_6": "You want to enter the abandoned sewers? That's rather dangerous and not a good idea, man. That part of the sewers was not sealed off for nothing, you know? ...",
  "npc.elliott.multi_7": "But hey, it's your life, bro. So here's the deal. I'll let you into the abandoned sewers if you help me with our {mission}.",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_1": "Sanguine! Did you see those sparks! We definitely had some energy transfer! Well done! Now, for your reward. ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_2": "Err... I would awfully like to know more about the scroll ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_3": "Would you settle for a heartfelt handshake instead - oh, you wouldn't? Well, er, okay ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_4": "Give me a minute or two to retrieve it. Ask me for the {scroll} or the {mission}",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_5": "Now, let me see... yes... yes... very good. Let me add THIS ..... swill it... there. Sanguine! ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_6": "We're not finished yet. Take this tainted blood vial ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_7": "Dab some drops from it on to the four blood pagodas in the inner circle here. Then pull the lightning lever over there.",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_8": "Sanguine! I need two different blood samples - The first one from the necromancer's pure blood chamber. ... ",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_9": "I was barred from the premises. For my research! Shameful! I'm a martyr to the cause - oh, the second sample you said? ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_10": "The second sample you must retrieve from the sacrificial chamber in the ancient vampire crypts, first floor, far west. ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_11": "Take these two sterilised vials, one for each blood basin. Oh, I wish I could go myself! Come back when you have filled both vials.",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_12": "So someone sent you after a scroll, eh? A stroll for a scroll! <chuckles> Sounds like an old-fashioned necromancer thing. ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_13": "Well, this piece here is a rather fascinating thing - see those strange blood stains? - ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_14": "My predecessors have had it for quite a while without finding out more - I was hoping to investigate, but there's always so much to do! ...",
  "npc.tomruk_the_ruddy.multi_15": "Ah, so you want it, too? Well, do me a favour: fetch two samples and assist in my experiment, in exchange for the scroll piece. Yes?",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_1": "We gnomes need some special grindstones to cut and polish specific crystals. The thing is, they can only be found in a quite dangerous lava cave full of vile monsters. You'll reach it via the hot spot teleporter. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_2": "It will be your task to get one such grindstone and bring it back to me.",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_3": "We gnomes want you to gather a special collection of spores. All you have to do is use a puffball mushroom and use the spore gathering kit I gave you to gather the spores. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_4": "There is a catch though. You need to collect different spores in a specific sequence to fill your gathering kit. If you mix the spores in the wrong way, you ruin your collection and have to start over. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_5": "You have to gather them in this sequence: red, green, blue and yellow. You can see on your kit what is required next.",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_6": "I'm no expert on how those golems work, but it seems that when the crystals of the golems get out of harmony, they do as they please and even sometimes become violent. The violent ones are lost. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_7": "Don't bother with them, though you may decide to kill some to get rid of them. The others can be repaired, but to recall them to the workshops, the golems have to be put into a specific resonance. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_8": "Use the bell I gave you on the golems, so the gnomes can recall them to their workshops. Getting four of them should be enough for now. Report back when you are ready.",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_9": "You will have to find a lonely crystal a perfect match. I don't understand the specifics but the gnomes told me that even crystals need a mate to produce offspring. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_10": "Be that as it may, in this package you'll find a crystal. Take it out of the package and go to the crystal caves to find it a mate. Just look out for huge red crystals and try your luck. ...",
  "npc.gnomeral.multi_11": "They should look like one of those seen in your soul melody test. You will find them in the crystal grounds. {Report} back to me when you are done.",
  "npc.avar_tar.multi_1": "I'm tired of all these young unskilled wannabe heroes. Every Tibian can show his skills or actions by wearing a special outfit. To prove oneself worthy of the demon outfit, this is how it goes: ...",
  "npc.avar_tar.multi_2": "The base outfit will be granted for completing the annihilator quest, which isn't much of a challenge nowadays, in my opinion. Anyway ...",
  "npc.avar_tar.multi_3": "The shield however will only be granted to those adventurers who have finished the demon helmet quest. ...",
  "npc.avar_tar.multi_4": "Well, the helmet is for those who really are tenacious and have hunted down all 6666 demons and finished the demon oak as well. ...",
  "npc.avar_tar.multi_5": "Are you interested?",
  "npc.corym_slave.multi_1": "The repression has taken too long. With our new weapons the respective people will get their just punishment.",
  "npc.commander_stone.multi_1": "Take this little piggy here. It will one day become a great mushroom hunter for sure. For now it is depended on you and other pigs. ...",
  "npc.commander_stone.multi_2": "Well, other pigs like it is one, I mean. I was of course not comparing you with a pig! Go to the truffles area and follow the truffle pigs there. If they dig up some truffles, let the little pig eat the mushrooms. ...",
  "npc.commander_stone.multi_3": "You'll have to feed it three times. Then return it to me. ...",
  "npc.commander_stone.multi_4": "Keep in mind that the pig has to be returned to his mother after a while. If you don't do this, the gnomes will call it back via teleport crystals.",
  "npc.ocelus.multi_1": "Oh yes, I noticed that lovely mermaid. From afar of course. I would not dare to step into the eyes of such a lovely creature. ...",
  "npc.ocelus.multi_2": "... I guess I am quite shy. Oh my, if I were not blue, I would turn red now. If there would be someone to arrange a {date} with her.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_1": "You'll find our seven guards at the gates of each quarter. Just ask them for their report and they will tell you all you need to know.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_2": "I must warn you, the quarters are in a horrible state. I strongly advise you to stay on the main roads whenever possible while you get those reports. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_3": "I'm pleased to hear that. Rarely we meet outsiders that care about our problems. Most people come here looking for wealth and luxury. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_4": "However, I have to tell you that our ranking system is quite rigid. So, I'm not allowed to entrust you with important missions as long as you haven't proven yourself as reliable. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_5": "If you are willing to work for the city of Yalahar, you can ask me for a {mission} any time, be it night or day.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_6": "So the Yalahari that opposed us are dead or fled from the city. This should bring us more stability and perhaps a true chance to rebuild the city. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_7": "Still, I wonder from where they gained some of the Yalahari secrets. Did they find some source of knowledge? ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_8": "And if so, is this source still around so that we can use it for the benefit of our city? What really troubles me is that none of those false Yalahari had the personality of agreat leader. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_9": "Quite the opposite, they were opportunistic and not exactly bold. Perhaps they were led by some greater power which stayed behind the scenes. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_10": "I'm afraid we have not seen the last chapter of Yalahar's drama. But anyhow, I wish to thank you for putting your life at stake for our cause. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_11": "I allow you to enter the Yalaharian treasure room. I'm sure that you can put what you find inside to better use than them. Choose one chest, but think before takingone! ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_12": "Also, take this Yalaharian outfit. Depending on which side you chose previously, you can also acquire one specific addon. Thank you again for your help.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_13": "I cannot tell you how we acquired this information, but we have heard that a circle of Yalahari is planning some kind of ritual. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_14": "They plan to create a portal for some powerful demons and to unleash them in the city to 'purge' it once and for all. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_15": "I doubt those poor fools will be able to control such entities. I can't figure out how they came up with such an insane idea, but they have to be stopped. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_16": "The entrance to their inner sanctum has been opened for you. Please hurry and stop them before it's too late. Be prepared for a HARD battle! Better gather some friends to assist you.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_17": "Listen, I know you have worked for Azerus and his friends, but it is not too late to change your mind! I beg you to rethink your loyalties. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_18": "The fate of the whole city might depend on your decision! Think about your options carefully.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_19": "The constant unrest in the city is to a great extent caused by the lack of food. Weapons will only serve to suppress the poor. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_20": "The factory you were sent to was once used for the production of food. Somewhere in the factory you might find an old pattern crystal for the production of food. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_21": "If you use it on the controls instead of the weapon pattern, you will ensure that our people are supplied with the desperately needed food. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_22": "The quara are indeed a threat. Yet, they are numerous and reproduce quickly. Slaying some of them will only enrage them even more. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_23": "The quara have been there for many generations. They have never threatened anyone who stayed out of their watery realm. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_24": "It would be much more useful to find out what the quara are so upset about. Better avoid slaying their leaders as this will only further the animosities.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_25": "I thank you also in the name of these poor lost souls. I will send the charm to a priest who is able to release them. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_26": "Tell the Yalahari that the charm was destroyed by the energy it contained.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_27": "What a sick idea to misuse tortured souls to power some device! Though, this charm might be useful to free these poor souls. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_28": "Please capture the souls as you have been instructed and then bring the charm to me. I will see to it that the souls are freed to go to the afterlife in peace.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_29": "Warbeasts? Is this true? People are already starving. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_30": "How can we afford to feed an army of hungry beasts? They will not only strengthen the power of the Yalahari over the citizens, they also mean starvation and deathfor the poor. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_31": "Instead of breeding warbeasts, this druid should breed cattle to feed our people. Please I beg you, convince him to do that!",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_32": "You did quite well in gaining a new friend who will work together with us. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_33": "I'm sure he'll still try to gain some profit but that's still better than his former one-man rule during which he dictated his own laws.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_34": "Mr. West is a little paranoid. That's the reason for his immense private army of bodyguards. He could surely be helpful, especially as he rules over the former trade quarter. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_35": "If you were able to reach him without killing his henchmen, you could probably convince him that you mean no harm to him. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_36": "That would certainly cement our relationship without any needless bloodshed. Perhaps you could use the way through the sewers to avoid his men. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_37": "Mr. West is not a bad man. We should be able to work out some plans to reconstruct the city's safety as soon as he overcomes his paranoia towards us.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_38": "This quarter has been sealed off years ago. To send someone there poses a high risk to spread the plague. I assume these research notes you've mentioned must be very important. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_39": "After all those years it is more than strange that someone shows interest in these notes now. Considering what has happened to the alchemists, it is rather unlikely that they contain harmless information. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_40": "I fear these notes will be used to turn the plague into some kind of weapon. Someone with this plague at his disposal could subdue the whole city by blackmailing. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_41": "I beg you to destroy these notes. Just put them into some burning oven to get rid of them and report that you did not find the notes.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_42": "Now you know as much as we do about the things happening in Yalahar. It's up to you what you do with this information. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_43": "Now leave and talk to my superior Azerus in the city centre to get your next mission. I urge you, though, to talk to me whenever he sends you on a new mission. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_44": "I think it is important that you hear my opinion about them. Now hurry. I suppose Azerus is already waiting.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_45": "I did my best to impress my superiors with your accomplishments and it seems that it worked quite well. They want you for their own missions now. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_46": "Missions that are more important than the ones you've fulfilled for me. However, before you leave, there are still some things I need to tell you. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_47": "Listen, I can't explain you everything in detail right now and here. You never know who might be eavesdropping. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_48": "I left some notes in the small room there. Get them and read them. Talk to me again when you've read the notes.",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_49": "We are still present at each quarter's city wall, even though we can do little to stop the chaos from spreading. Still, our garrisons are necessary to maintain some sort of order in the city. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_50": "My superiors ask for a first hand report about the current situation in the single city quarters. I need someone to travel to our garrisons to get the reports from the guards. Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_51": "I hope your first mission will not scare you off. Even though, we cut off our sewer system from other parts of the city to prevent the worst, it still has deteriorated in the last decades. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_52": "Certain parts of the controls are rusty and the drains are stuffed with garbage. Get yourself a crowbar, loosen the controls and clean the pipes from the garbage. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_53": "We were able to locate the 4 worst spots in the sewers. I will mark them for you on your map so you have no trouble finding them. Report to me when you have finished your {mission}. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_54": "You probably heard that we have numerous problems in different quarters of our city. Our forces are limited, so we really could need some help from outsiders. ...",
  "npc.palimuth.multi_55": "Would you like to assist us in re-establishing order in our city?",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_1": "So listen: The lairs are secluded and you can only reach them by using a magical gem teleporter. You will find a teleporter carved out of a giant emerald in the dragon lairs deep beneath the Darama desert, which will lead you to Tazhadur's lair. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_2": "A ruby teleporter located in the western Dragonblaze Peaks allows you to enter the lair of Kalyassa. A teleporter carved out of sapphire is on the island Okolnir and leads you to Gelidrazah's lair. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_3": "And finally an amethyst teleporter in undead-infested caverns underneath Edron allows you to enter the lair of Zorvorax.",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_4": " Fine! I'll tell you where to find our ancestors. You now may ask yourself why I should want you to go there and fight them. It's quite simple: I am a straight descendant of Kalyassa herself. She was not really a caring mother. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_5": "No, she called herself an empress and behaved exactly like that. She was domineering, farouche and conceited and this finally culminated in a serious quarrel between us. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_6": "I sought support by my aunt and my uncles but they were not a bit better than my mother was! So, feel free to go to their lairs and challenge them. I doubt you will succeed but then again that's not my problem. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_7": "So, you want to know about their secret lairs?",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_8": "Each kind of dragon has its own incitement, an important aspect that impels them and occupies their mind. For the common dragons this is the lust for power, for the dragon lords the greed for treasures. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_9": "The frost dragons' incitement is the thirst for knowledge und for the undead dragons it's the desire for life, as they regret their ancestor's mistake. ...",
  "npc.tamoril.multi_10": "These incitements are also a kind of trial that has to be undergone if one wants to {find} the First Dragon's four descendants.",
  "npc.shauna.multi_1": "My last prisoner? Hmm. ...",
  "npc.shauna.multi_2": "I think he was some guy from Darama. Can't remember his name. ...",
  "npc.shauna.multi_3": "He was here just for one night, because he got drunk and annoyed our citizens. ...",
  "npc.shauna.multi_4": "Obviously he wasn't pleased with this place, because he headed for Thais the next day. ...",
  "npc.shauna.multi_5": "Something tells me that he won't stay out of trouble for too long.",
  "npc.shauna.multi_6": "Oh, there's a waterpipe in one of my cells? ...",
  "npc.shauna.multi_7": "I guess my last {prisoner} forgot it there.",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_1": "You will have to leave the plant through the eastern door on the lowest level. I have arranged for it to be 'accidentally' open. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_2": "As in the past, our enemy still uses a series of machines to open the way to the next section of his lair. You have to turn them all on to proceed. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_3": "They will only work for a certain amount of time though, so you will have to hurry or some of the machines will turn inactive again.",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_4": "While it's buried, it only uses his tentacles to attack. If one is destroyed it will simply use another set of tentacles and its supply seems endless. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_5": "If you manage though to kill all the tentacles it is using within a few heartbeats, it will become confused by its momentary helplessness and will probably attack with its main body. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_6": "That is when you have a chance to destroy it. Pass through its chamber and look for another of my tubes to contact me. Please hurry! End of communication.",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_7": "It's a fearsome subterranean beast like nothing I've ever encountered. It is dangerous and almost unbeatable because its main body is hidden beneath the ground ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_8": "And it has an endless supply of tentacles. But not all is lost, as I have devised a {plan} to battle the beast.",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_9": "His allies are an enigma even to me. It seems they belong to some unknown race that lives deep under the earth. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_10": "They seem to have supplied him with resources and workforce and a powerful {guardian} to prevent anyone from entering the passages to his lair.",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_11": "He is an old enemy of the city and I've battled him often in the past. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe.multi_12": "Now he has returned for vengeance, he reclaimed an old abandoned underground {laboratory} and he has acquired new powerful {allies}.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_1": "That's very kind of you, my friend! Listen: I know there is a spell to transform my fishtail into legs. It is a temporary effect, so I could return to the ocean as soon as the spell ends. Unfortunately I don't know how to cast this spell. ...",
  "npc.aurita.multi_2": "But there is a fairy who once told me about it. Perhaps she will share her knowledge. You can find her in a small fairy village in the southwest of Feyrist.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_3": "I already gave you the empty starlight vial.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_4": "Thank you, friend! Please take the starlight vial. It is made of a very rare kind of enchanted glass and magical metals, so it is able to preserve starlight. ...",
  "npc.aurita.multi_5": "A long time ago a pixie knight of Maelyrra carried it with her. But when she was flying above the waves she accidentally dropped it and it sunk. I found it but now you may take it and use it to help Feyrist.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_6": "Thank you again, friend! Taegen and I we're so happy now.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_7": "The spell works! I already took a walk on the beach last night in the moonlight. Please talk to Taegen now, he may have another request.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_8": "There is a fairy who once told me about this spell. Perhaps she will share her knowledge. You can find her in a small fairy village in the southwest of Feyrist.",
  "npc.aurita.multi_9": "Yes, there is something. I'm in love with Taegen, but he is a faun. As such he's inhabiting the forests, dancing with fairies. And I, being a mermaid, am living in the ocean, swimming with the fish between coral reefs. ...",
  "npc.aurita.multi_10": "But I lost my heart to Taegen, I can't help it. We would love to spend some time together, but not just sitting on the beach. ...",
  "npc.aurita.multi_11": "I'd love to show him my homestead beneath the waves. I have an idea but I can't do it alone. Would you help me?",
  "npc.nokmir.multi_1": "He said he still had it after work. On that evening, {Grombur}, {Rerun} and me opened a cask of beer in one of the mine tunnels. We had a fun evening there. ...",
  "npc.nokmir.multi_2": "On the next day, the guards brought me to emperor {Rehal}, and Rerun was there, too. He said I had stolen his ring. I'd never steal, you have to believe me.",
  "npc.vescu.multi_1": "You're a true buddy. I promise I will t-try to avoid killing you even if someone asks me to. <hicks> ...",
  "npc.vescu.multi_2": "Listen, I have this old formula from my grandma. <hicks> It says... 30 {bonelord eyes}... 10 {red dragon scales}. ...",
  "npc.vescu.multi_3": "Then 30 {lizard scales}... 20 {fish fins} - ew, this sounds disgusting, I wonder if this is really a potion or rather a cleaning agent. ...",
  "npc.vescu.multi_4": "Add 20 ounces of {vampire dust}, 10 ounces of {demon dust} and mix well with one flask of {warrior's sweat}. <hicks> ...",
  "npc.vescu.multi_5": "Okayyy, this is a lot... we'll take this step by step. <hicks> Will you help me gathering 30 {bonelord eyes}?",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_1": "The book! You have it! Let me see! <browses the book> ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_2": "Dragon Egg Omelette, Dwarven beer sauce... it's all there. This is great! Here is your well-deserved reward. ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_3": "Incidentally, I have talked to Fa'hradin about you during dinner. I think he might have some work for you. Why don't you talk to him about it?",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_4": "Fine! Even though I know so many recipes, I'm looking for the description of some dwarven meals. ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_5": "So, if you could bring me a cookbook of the dwarven kitchen, I'll reward you well.",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_6": "I'm preparing the food for all djinns in Ashta'daramai. ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_7": "Therefore, I'm what is commonly called a cook, although I do not like that word too much. It is vulgar. I prefer to call myself 'chef'.",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_8": "My collection of recipes is almost complete. There are only but a few that are missing. ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_9": "Hmmm... now that we talk about it. There is something you could help me with. Are you interested?",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_10": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_11": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_12": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.bo_ques.multi_13": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.irmana.multi_1": "A wolf whelp fur? Well, some months ago a hunter came here - a rather scruffy, smelly guy. I would have thrown him out instantly, but he had to offer some fine pelts. One of them was the fur of a very young wolf. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_2": "I was not delighted that he obviously killed such a young animal. When I confronted him, he said he wanted to raise it as a companion but it unfortunately died. A sad story. In the end, I bought some of his pelts, among them the whelp fur. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_3": "You can have it if this is important for you. I would sell it for 1000 gold. Are you interested?",
  "npc.irmana.multi_4": "This accessory requires a small fee of 150000 gold pieces. Of course, we do not want to put you at any risk to be attacked while carrying this huge amount of money. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_5": "This is why we have established our brand-new instalment sale. You can choose to either pay the price at once, or if you want to be safe, by instalments of 10000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_6": "I also have to inform you that once you started paying for one of the accessories, you have to finish the payment first before you can start paying for the other one, of course. Are you interested in purchasing this accessory?",
  "npc.irmana.multi_7": "This accessory requires a small fee of 150000 gold pieces. Of course, we do not want to put you at any risk to be attacked while carrying this huge amount of money. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_8": "This is why we have established our brand-new instalment sale. You can choose to either pay the price at once, or if you want to be safe, by instalments of 10000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_9": "I also have to inform you that once you started paying for one of the accessories, you have to finish the payment first before you can start paying for the other one, of course. Are you interested in purchasing this accessory?",
  "npc.irmana.multi_10": "This accessory requires a small fee of 150000 gold pieces. Of course, we do not want to put you at any risk to be attacked while carrying this huge amount of money. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_11": "This is why we have established our brand-new instalment sale. You can choose to either pay the price at once, or if you want to be safe, by instalments of 10000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_12": "I also have to inform you that once you started paying for one of the accessories, you have to finish the payment first before you can start paying for the other one, of course. Are you interested in purchasing this accessory?",
  "npc.irmana.multi_13": "The accessory requires a small fee of 150000 gold pieces. Of course, we do not want to put you at any risk to be attacked while carrying this huge amount of money. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_14": "This is why we have established our brand-new instalment sale. You can choose to either pay the price at once, or if you want to be safe, by instalments of 10000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.irmana.multi_15": "I also have to inform you that once you started paying for one of the accessories, you have to finish the payment first before you can start paying for the other one, of course. Are you interested in purchasing this accessory?",
  "npc.ajax.multi_1": "Good! Me make shiny weapon. If you help me, I make one for you too. Like axe I wear. I need stuff. Listen. ...",
  "npc.ajax.multi_2": "Me need 100 iron ore. Then need crude iron. Then after that 50 behemoth fangs. And 50 lizard leather. You understand?",
  "npc.ajax.multi_3": "Help me yes or no?",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_1": "Once, this tower has been my prison but after the death of Winfred it has become my refuge from the rest of the world. ...",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_2": "I welcome the loneliness here because it mirrors the state of my heart.",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_3": "He wasn't a bad man. He was only misguided by false friends who told him what society expected of him ...",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_4": "By trying to uphold a respectable image in society, he ruined not only my life but also his own.",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_5": "He was my one and only true love. He was a mere commoner and so my {father} forbid me to see him ...",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_6": "We met anyway, we had plans to flee to {Port Hope} and to start a new life there ...",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_7": "A {druid}, in service of my father, had spied on us. So they brought me here and locked me into this {tower}. The druid cast a spell on the plants at the entrance which kept everyone from entering the tower ...",
  "npc.caramellia.multi_8": "I could see Winfred from the window but he could not come to me. One day he disappeared. I knew immediately that something horrible had happened to him.",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_1": "You will have to leave the plant through the eastern door on the lowest level. I have arranged for it to be 'accidentally' open. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_2": "As in the past, our enemy still uses a series of machines to open the way to the next section of his lair. You have to turn them all on to proceed. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_3": "They will only work for a certain amount of time though, so you will have to hurry or some of the machines will turn inactive again.",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_4": "While it's buried, it only uses his tentacles to attack. If one is destroyed it will simply use another set of tentacles and its supply seems endless. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_5": "If you manage though to kill all the tentacles it is using within a few heartbeats, it will become confused by its momentary helplessness and will probably attack with its main body. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_6": "That is when you have a chance to destroy it. Pass through its chamber and look for another of my tubes to contact me. Please hurry! End of communication.",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_7": "It's a fearsome subterranean beast like nothing I've ever encountered. It is dangerous and almost unbeatable because its main body is hidden beneath the ground ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_8": "And it has an endless supply of tentacles. But not all is lost, as I have devised a {plan} to battle the beast.",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_9": "His allies are an enigma even to me. It seems they belong to some unknown race that lives deep under the earth. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_10": "They seem to have supplied him with resources and workforce and a powerful {guardian} to prevent anyone from entering the passages to his lair.",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_11": "He is an old enemy of the city and I've battled him often in the past. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe2.multi_12": "Now he has returned for vengeance, he reclaimed an old abandoned underground {laboratory} and he has acquired new powerful {allies}.",
  "npc.chartan.multi_1": "You did it! Zere waz zome kind of zparkle and I zink it iz working again - oh pleaze feel free to try it, I uhm, I will wait here and be ready juzt in caze zomezing uhm happenz to you. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_2": "And if you head to Zalamon, be zure to inform him about our zituation. Food rationz are running low and we are ztill not well equipped. We need to eztablish a working zupply line. ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_3": "Alright. Well, az you might not be aware of it yet - we are on top of an old temple complex. It haz been abandoned and it haz crumbled over time. ...",
  "npc.chartan.multi_4": "Ze teleporter over zere uzed to work juzt fine to get uz back to ze zouz. But it haz ztopped operating for quite zome time. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_5": "My men believe it iz a dizturbanze cauzed by ze corruption zat zpreadz everywhere. Zey are too zcared to go down zere. And zat'z where you come in. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_6": "Zere were meanz to activate teleporterz zomewhere in ze complex. But zinze you cannot reach all ze roomz, I guezz you will have to improvize. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_7": "Here iz ze key to ze entranze to ze complex. Figure zomezing out, reztore ze teleporter zo we can get back to ze plainz in ze zouz. ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_8": "I zee. Zalamon zent word of ze arrival of a zoftzkin quite zome time ago. Zat muzt be you zen. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_9": "Well, I exzpected zomeone more - imprezzive. However, we will zee how far you can get. You've got newz from ze zouz? ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_10": "Hm, I underztand. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_11": "Oh you did. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_12": "I zee. Interezting. ... ",
  "npc.chartan.multi_13": "You being here meanz we have eztablished connectionz to ze zouz. Finally. And you are going to help uz. Well, zere iz zertainly a lot for you to do. Zo better get ztarted. ",
  "npc.chrak.multi_1": "You have done ze impozzible and beaten ze champion. Your mazter will be pleazed. Hereby I cleanze ze poizon from your body. You are now allowed to leave. ...",
  "npc.chrak.multi_2": "For now ze mazter will zee zat you and your alliez are zpared of ze wraz of ze dragon emperor az you are unimportant for hiz goalz. ...",
  "npc.chrak.multi_3": "You may crawl back to your alliez and warn zem of ze gloriouz might of ze dragon emperor and hiz minionz.",
  "npc.chrak.multi_4": "Ze tournament iz ze ultimate challenge of might and prowrezz. Ze rulez may have changed over ze centuriez but ze ezzence remained ze zame. ...",
  "npc.chrak.multi_5": "If you know ze rulez, you might enter ze arena for ze {battle}.",
  "npc.chrak.multi_6": "Zo you want to enter ze arena, you know ze rulez and zat zere will be no ozer option zan deaz or victory?",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.multi_1": "Please. Wait. I. Can. Not. Han-Han-Han*chhhhhrrrchrk*Handle. *chhhhrchrk* This. Is. Enough. Material. *chrrrchhrk* ...",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.multi_2": "I. Have-ve-ve-veee*chrrrck*. Also. Cleaned. Your. Clothes. Master. It. Is. No-No-No*chhrrrrk*Now. Free. Of. Sample. Stains.",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.multi_3": "Yo-Yo-Your*chhhrk*. Cap. Is. Slimed. I. Can. Clean. It. *chhhhrrrkchrk* ...",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.multi_4": "Here. You. Are. *chhhrrrrkchrk*",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.multi_5": "Yo-Yo-Your*chhhrk*. Cap. Is. Slimed. I. Can. Clean. It. *chhhhrrrkchrk* ...",
  "npc.broken_servant_sentry.multi_6": "Here. You. Are. chhhrrrrkchrk",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.multi_1": "Splendid! My son Rehon set off on an expedition to the deeper mines. He and a group of dwarfs were to search for new veins of crystal. Unfortunately they have been missing for 2 weeks now. ...",
  "npc.emperor_rehal.multi_2": "Find my son and if he's alive bring him back. You will find a reactivated ore wagon tunnel at the entrance of the great citadel which leades to the deeper mines. If you encounter problems within the tunnel go ask Xorlosh, he can help you.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_1": "Hm, no sign of any notes you say? That's odd - odd and a bit suspicious. I doubt you have tried hard enough. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_2": "There are only a few chances to impress us. For those who please us great rewards are in store. If you fail though, you might lose more than you can imagine.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_3": "For your noble deeds, we would like to invite you to a special celebration ceremony. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_4": "Only the most prominent Yalahari are allowed to join the festivities. I assume you can imagine what honour it is that you'vebeen invited to join us. Meet us in the inner city's centre. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_5": "As our most trusted ally, you may pass all doors to reach the festivity hall. There you will receive your reward for the achievements you have gained so far. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_6": "I'm convinced your reward will be beyond your wildest dreams. And that is just the beginning!",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_7": "I'm impressed by your support for our cause. Still, I'm aware that this scheming Palimuth tried to influence you. Think about who are your real friends and who can assist you in your career. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_8": "Come back if you have decided to which side you want to belong.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_9": "In the past, we had many magical factories providing the citizens with everything they needed. Now that most of these factories are shut down, we have trouble getting enough supplies. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_10": "We need you to enter one of the lesser damaged factories. Go to the factory district and look for a pattern crystal used for weapon production. Use it on the factory controller. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_11": "It will ensure that the factory will provide us with a suitable amount of weapons which we dearly need to reclaim and secure the most dangerous parts of the city. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_12": "I will inform the guards that you are allowed to pass the centre gate to the factory quarter now. Just use the gate mechanism to pass.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_13": "Recently, our fishermen have been attacked by a maritime race called the quara. They live in the sunken quarter and are a significant threat to our people. I ask you to enter the sunken quarter and slay all their leaders. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_14": "We believe that there are three leaders in this area. Your task is simple enough, so you better don't fail! ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_15": "I will inform the guards that you are allowed to pass the centre gate to the sunken quarter now. Just use the gate mechanism to pass.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_16": "Ah, what an unexpected sight. I can almost feel the energy of the charm. It will help to recover some of the past wealth. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_17": "You did quite an impressive job. I'm considering to introduce you to my ma.. to my direct superior one day. But there are still other missions to fulfil.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_18": "Destroyed you say? That's impossible! I'm not sure if I can trust you in this matter? One might assume, you fled from the ghosts in terror and left the charm there. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_19": "You will have to work twice as hard on your next missions to restore the trust you have lost.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_20": "The old cemetery of the city has been abandoned decades ago when the activity of the various undead there became unbearable. The reason for their appearance was never found out or researched. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_21": "However, those undead could be useful, at least some of them. Particular ghosts consist of a substance that is very similar to the energy source that powered some of our devices. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_22": "Since we lack most of the original sources, some substitute might come in handy. Take this ghost charm and place it on the strange carving in the cemetery. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_23": "Use it to attract ghosts and slay them. Then use the residues of the ghosts on the charm to capture the essence. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_24": "Once it is filled, ghosts will not be attracted any longer. Then return the charm to me. I will inform the guards that you are allowed to pass the centre gate to the cemetery quarter now. Just use the gate mechanism to pass.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_25": "So have you won us a new ally? Excellent. I knew you would not dare to ruin this mission. Soon we might be able to strengthen our defences and even relocate some of our guards. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_26": "Perhaps some day soon, you lead your own unit of men. However, there are more missions that need to be accomplished. Let's talk about them.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_27": "This druid dares to affront us? We will look into this when we have enough time. But there are other things that needs to be settled. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_28": "Although, we probably should not do so after your last failure, we are willing to grant you another mission.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_29": "As you probably noticed, once our city had a park and a zoo around a grand arena. It was a favourite pastime of our citizens to visit this quarter in their spare time. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_30": "Nowadays, the quarter is lost. The animals are on the loose, and an attempt to revitalise the city with new arena games resulted in a revolt of the foreign gladiators. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_31": "Now all kinds of beasts roam the park, and gladiators challenge them and visitors to test their skills. One of the residents is an ancient druid that rather cares foranimals than for people. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_32": "It is said that he is able to use magic to breed animals with changed abilities and appearances. Such skills are of course quite useful for us. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_33": "We lack the manpower to retake all quarters, or just to defend ourselves adequately. If he bred us some guards and warbeasts, we could strengthen our positionconsiderably. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_34": "Travel to the arena quarter and gain his assistance for us. I will inform the guards that you are allowed to pass the centre gate to the arena quarter now. Just use thegate mechanism to pass.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_35": "I hope you gave this criminal a real scare! I'm sure he'll remember what he has to expect if he arouses our anger again. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_36": "You have proven yourself as quite valuable with this mission! That was just the first step on your rise through the ranks of our helpers. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_37": "Just ask me for more missions and we will see what you are capable of!",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_38": "So he has been too uncooperative for you? Well, you weren't the first we have sent and you won't be the last. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_39": "However, if you cannot even serve us as a bully, we might have to rethink if you are the right person for us. That was a bad job and we don't tolerate many of them.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_40": "We surely cannot allow some underworld kingpin to rule a significant part of the city. Although, I have to admit that his firm grip on the former trade quarter might be useful....",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_41": "I expect you to fight your way through his minions and to show him that we are determined and powerful enough to retake the quarter, if necessary by force. Talk to himafter killing some of his henchmen. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_42": "I'm sure he'll understand that he will succumb to a greater power. That's how his little empire has worked after all. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_43": "Also, I will inform the guards that you are allowed to pass the centre gate to the trade quarter now. Just use the gate mechanism to pass.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_44": "The former alchemist quarter was struck by even more disasters than the rest of the city. Fires, explosions, poisonous fumes - all sorts of catastrophes. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_45": "The worst plague, however, are unknown diseases that have spread in this quarter and eradicated any human population. We must stop it before other quarters areafflicted. We already identified certain carriers responsible for spreading the plague. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_46": "It will be your task to eliminate them. This spell will protect you from becoming infected yourself. Enter the alchemist quarter and kill the three plague carriers, and atbest anything else you might find there. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_47": "Even more important, retrieve the last research notes that the local alchemists made before the plague killed them. They might be the key for a cure or something else. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_48": "At least we have to make sure that these scientists did not die in vain, and honour their researches. So please bring us these research notes. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_49": "Also, I will inform the guards that you are allowed to pass the centre gate to the alchemist quarter. Just use the gate mechanism to pass.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_50": "I'm mildly impressed by your previous deeds in our service. So I'm willing to grant you some more important {missions}. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_51": "If you please us, a life of luxury as an important person in our city is ensured. If you fail, you will be replaced by someone more capable than you. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_52": "So if you are up for a challenge, ask me for a {mission}.",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_53": "With all the coming and going of strangers here, it would be quite tedious to explain everything again and again. So we have written a manifesto. ...",
  "npc.yalahari.multi_54": "Grab a copy from the room behind me. Let's talk about your further career in our ranks once you've read it.",
  "npc.gnomally.multi_1": "For two minor tokens, you can buy one gnomish {supply} package! For eight tokens, you can buy a {muck} remover! For ten tokens, you can buy a {mission} crystal. For fifteen tokens, you can buy a crystal {lamp} or a mushroom {backpack}. ...",
  "npc.gnomally.multi_2": "For seventy tokens, I can offer you a voucher for an {addition to the soil guardian outfit}, or a voucher for an {addition to the crystal warlord armor outfit}.",
  "npc.gnomally.multi_3": "For ten major tokens, I can offer you a {gill gugel}, a {gill coat}, {gill legs}, a {spellbook} of vigilance, a {prismatic helmet}, a {prismatic armor}, {prismatic legs}, {prismatic boots} or a {prismatic shield} ...",
  "npc.gnomally.multi_4": "For twenty major tokens, I can offer you a {basic soil guardian outfit}, a {basic crystal warlord outfit}, an {iron loadstone} or a {glow wine}.",
  "npc.gnomally.multi_5": "You can buy different equipment for minor or for major tokens. So, which is the equipment you are interested in, the one for {minor} or {major} tokens? ...",
  "npc.gnomally.multi_6": "By the way, if you want to have a look on the prismatic and gill items first, just head over to the depot and check the market.",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_1": "Since you are seasoned adventurers I'll skip the basics and jump right to the important part! This cave system is overrun by the minions of ... ah well, the greatest shame of gnomekind. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_2": "That traitorous gnome, known as Gnomevil, who was my pupil before his changeover to the dark side of gnomedom, has abandoned all gnomish ethics and joined forces with our enemies. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_3": "It's hard to tell what led to his downfall. In the end he seems to have forgotten the principle that with small stature comes great responsibility. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_4": "He became tainted and corrupted by evil, obviously enough to grow in size, which is always an indicator for evil of course. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_5": "Now he commands his armies in the name of those below and hides in his lair protected by layers of thick crystal that only he can form and change due to his corrupted powers! ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_6": "There is one thing though that could cause his downfall! His corruption has spread to his minions and in his lair there are some infected weepers that are full of parasites. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_7": "These parasites will spread a fluid that will weaken the integrity of the crystals in front of Gnomevils lair when they die. The entrance is marked with crystal columns, so you can't miss it. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_8": "You have to kill enough of the parasites DIRECTLY in front of the crystals. Eventually the columns will collapse and allow you entrance to Gnomevils lair. ...",
  "npc.gnomole.multi_9": "Take care though, due to Gnomevils power the crystals will grow back quite fast. Better manage the parasites in quick succession or everything will be for naught. ..., Enter his lair and bring an end to his despicable reign!",
  "npc.undal.multi_1": "You have to empower eight ward stones. Once charged with arcane energy, they will strengthen the Nightmare Beast's prison and at the same time weaken this terrible creature. We know about the specific location of six of those stones. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_2": "You can find them in the mountains of the island Okolnir, in a water elemental cave beneath Folda, in the depths of Calassa, in the forests of Feyrist and on the islands Meriana and Cormaya. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_3": "The location of the other two ward stones is a bit more obscure, however. We are not completely sure where they are. You should make inquiries at an abandoned house in the Plains of Havoc. You may find it east of an outlaw camp. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_4": "The other stone seems to be somewhere in Tiquanda. Search for a small stone building south-west of Banuta. Take this talisman to empower the ward stones. It will work with the six stones at the known locations. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_5": "However, the empowering of the two hidden stones could be a bit more complicated. But you have to find out on yourself what to do with those stones.",
  "npc.undal.multi_6": "You empowered all eight ward stones. Well done! You may now enter the Dream Labyrinth via the portal here in the Court. Beneath it you will find the Nightmare Beast's lair. But the labyrinth is protected by seven so called Dream Doors. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_7": "You have to find the Seven {Keys} to unlock the Seven Dream Doors down there. Only then you will be able to enter the Nightmare Beast's lair.",
  "npc.undal.multi_8": "You will have to re-empower several wardstones all over the world, to weaken the beast of nightmares. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_9": "The next step would be to enter a place known as dream scar and participate in battles, to gain access to the lower areas. ...",
  "npc.undal.multi_10": "There the nightmare beast can be challenged and defeated.",
  "npc.undal.multi_11": "So do you want to learn the story behind of this or rather talk about the {task} at hand?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_1": "I'm impressed with your dedication and courage. I can't show you the exact location of cyclopolis on the map though. It is somewhere north of Edron city. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_2": "Exit the city and go through a mountain passage leading to the west, then keep on heading north. The entrance is marked by large, obelisk-like stones arranged in a circle. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_3": "You can kill normal cyclopes as well as drones and smiths to reach your goal. Good hunting!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_4": "Great! You can find rotworms south of the city, for example. Take a rope and shovel and look for loose stone piles to dig open. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_5": "You can kill normal rotworms as well as their larger brothers, the carrion worms, to fulfil your task. Be careful and good luck!",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_6": "Very well, maybe you know that the orcs here in Edron learnt to raise giant spiders. It is going to become a serious threat. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_7": "The mission is simple: go to the orcs and destroy all spider eggs that are hatched by the giant spider they have managed to catch. The orcs are located in the south of the western part of the island.",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_8": "We've successfully driven the minotaurs off this island, but the underground city of the cyclopes - Cyclopolis - is still standing. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_9": "We're always looking for adventurers who'd help us decimate the number of cyclopes. Will you assist the city of Edron by killing 500 of them?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_10": "It's not only the trolls invading from the west coast. <sighs> Goblins also have a lair there where they constantly prepare for their next attack. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_11": "If you could kill 150 goblins for us, that'd be a good start. Would you be willing to help us in this matter?",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_12": "The trolls living west of our city have become quite a nuisance lately. Not that they are really dangerous to us, but still, we must show them that there's a line they shouldn't cross. ...",
  "npc.daniel_steelsoul.multi_13": "I want you to kill 100 of them. If you succeed, I'll provide you some pretty coins and experience. Are you willing to take on this task?",
  "npc.tim_the_guard.multi_1": "It's not a drama!! I think there is just no god who's responsible for toothbrush safety, that's all ...",
  "npc.tim_the_guard.multi_2": "And even IF through some miracle the stupid toothbrush had jumped out of the toilet into my hand, I honestly doubt I would ever use it again.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_1": "That's great! I have stolen something from Dermot.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_2": "You can buy it for 200 gold. Do you want to buy it?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_3": "Well, it's the least you can do for those who live in dire poverty.",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_4": "A single cookie is a bit less than I'd expected, but better than ... WHA ... WHAT??",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_5": "MY BEARD! MY PRECIOUS BEARD! IT WILL TAKE AGES TO CLEAR IT OF THIS CONFETTI!",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_6": "When I was wandering around in Tibia, I lost my favourite staff somewhere in the northern ruins in Edron. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_7": "Uh, don't ask me what I was doing there... sort of a pilgrimage. Well anyway, if you could bring that staff back to me, I promise I'll give you my current one. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_8": "What do you say?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_9": "I can mix a secret potion which increases facial hair growth enormously. I call it 'Instabeard'. However, I fear it works only for men. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_10": "Even if it worked on girls, I'd rather not be responsible for you ruining your pretty face. I have an idea though. If you help me brew one of these potions, I will sell something nice to you. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_11": "I still have a pretty gypsy dress and a pearl necklace somewhere, which you could wear instead of this ragged skirt. For the small fee of 20000 gold pieces, it'd be yours. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_12": "You only have to bring me 100 pieces of ape fur, so I can brew the potion. Do we have a deal?",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_13": "I can mix a secret potion which will increase your facial hair growth enormously. I call it 'Instabeard'. However, it requires certain ingredients. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_14": "For the small fee of 20000 gold pieces I will help you mix this potion. Just bring me 100 pieces of ape fur, which are necessary to create this potion. ...",
  "npc.simon_the_beggar.multi_15": "Do we have a deal?",
  "npc.hugo.multi_1": "Good! Listen, I need the following material - first, 20 pieces of brown cloth, like the worn and ragged ghoul clothing. ...",
  "npc.hugo.multi_2": "Secondly, 50 pieces of minotaur leather. Third, I need bat wings, maybe 10. And 30 heaven blossoms, the flowers elves cultivate. ...",
  "npc.hugo.multi_3": "Have you noted down everything and will help me gather the material?",
  "npc.hugo.multi_4": "I think I'm having an innovative vision! I feel that people are getting tired of attempting to look wealthy and of displaying their treasures. ...",
  "npc.hugo.multi_5": "A really new and innovative look would be - the 'poor man's look'! I can already see it in front of me... yes... a little ragged... but not too shabby! ...",
  "npc.hugo.multi_6": "I need material right now! Argh - the vision starts to fade... please hurry, can you bring me some stuff?",
  "npc.gnomission.multi_1": "You can trade special spoils of war to get a permission to use the war teleporters to the area of the corresponding boss without need of mission crystals. ...",
  "npc.gnomission.multi_2": "Which one would you like to trade: the deathstrike's {snippet}, gnomevil's {hat} or the abyssador {lash}?",
  "npc.gnomission.multi_3": "There are three warzones. In each warzone you will find fearsome foes. At the end you'll find their mean master. The masters is well protected though. ...",
  "npc.gnomission.multi_4": "Make sure to talk to our gnomish agent in there for specifics of its' protection. ...",
  "npc.gnomission.multi_5": "Oh, and to be able to enter the second warzone you have to best the first. To enter the third you have to best the second. ...",
  "npc.gnomission.multi_6": "And you can enter each one only once every twenty hours. Your normal teleport crystals won't work on these teleporters. You will have to get {mission} crystals from Gnomally.",
  "npc.albinius.multi_1": "The {Shapers} were an advanced civilisation, well versed in art, construction, language and exploration of our world in their time. ...",
  "npc.albinius.multi_2": "The foundations of this {temple} are testament to their genius and advanced understanding of complex problems. They were master craftsmen and excelled in magic.",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_1": "It is hard to explain. Of course, it's not a real song as you would understand it. I don't hear it with my ears, but rather, I feel it deep inside of me. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_2": "Calling it a song or melody is the best I can do to describe it to those who don't share this kind of perception. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_3": "It also helps me to express and understand something for which our language has no appropriate expression. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_4": "You know, we are so dependent on words that we can't think about concepts when we don't have words for them. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_5": "I sometimes think words have become just as much of a hindrance as a help. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_6": "Perhaps we would fare better if only we forgot words and dealt purely in feelings. Then perhaps all of us could hear the wonderful melody of nature.",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_7": "How can I explain my connection to the elements so that you can understand it? Hmmm, it is like a faint melody, a song, that is always there. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_8": "I hear that melody shifting in time with the shifts in the elements. With so many years of listening, I have learned to interpret these shifts and so come to a deeper understanding of the elements. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_9": "It was a natural step for me to become responsible for researching elemental lore. I try to learn as much as I can and share it with my fellow druids. ...",
  "npc.cerdras.multi_10": "Unfortunately, much of my understanding is instinctive, and our language just doesn't contain the right words for me to express the things I feel adequately.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_1": "Alright very good. Now the only thing you need to do is taking these traps and moving out to the area I have marked on your map where you need to place them. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_2": "Once you did that go to the large high seat near the camp and watch for the travelling merchants. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_3": "Once all of them are trapped in the nets, you can go down and gather anything of value you can find. But only take what we... you really need - around 100 gold should be enough for any man to take. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_4": "We have manners after all, haven't we. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_5": "My men will take their share of course and... help you relieve the merchants of any valuables. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_6": "You're done if you get at least... let's say 5 of these fools. Return to me and you will be rewarded. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_7": "Off you go and - good hunt, heh.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_8": "Right, now before the merchants enter the woods, you will install several traps - nothing too dangerous, just nets and ropes. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_9": "When they enter said area which is located close to our hidden camp, they will be trapped and you can... lighten their heavy burden of valuable goods. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_10": "There is but a tiny little catch - we cannot help you laying these traps. You know, some of the guys became sick recently, we talk about several broken legs here, one almost lost his arm ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_11": "So... it's entirely up to you, will you do this or not?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_12": "Mmmmh, I have to say - good workmanship. No doubt. Yes, the person who made that tool you used to fix all this was a pure professional. Something I can't say about your work, though. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_13": "The walls look as if they will come off in a matter of hours. Oh well, you can always come back and repair this mess, ask me for a task if you want to. Yeah, yeah and here's your reward for today.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_14": "Fine, now hurry into the woods and find some rabbits. Find them and kill them that is. Use a sharp, thin knife to get the rabbit foot and be careful not to destroy it - no one would buy it in a bad condition after all. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_15": "Once you gathered some rabbit feet, put one of our - handcrafted by the guys - ribbons on each of them. That will make two lucky charms per rabbit. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_16": "We will need at least seven. And seven is a lucky number, don't you think? Heh. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_17": "If you need some more ribbons just come back to me and ask.",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_18": "Oh |PLAYERNAME| my good friend, good to see you! Today you will help us with a very important task. Very important indeed. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_19": "You know, a large group of merchants is travelling from Thais to Venore and they are crossing the forest to shorten their way - can you believe it? ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_20": "They will enter the forest near our camp which is where you come in - uhm I mean you do want to help us with this, right?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_21": "Of course, of course, there is indeed something you can help us with. Remember that we also have some tasks for you. So, are you ready for another quest to help the men of the forest?",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_22": "There is a problem with one of our deer stands. Right. Well, there are two problems, our deer stands - and some of the walls of the buildings in the camp are broken. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_23": "You know, the guys built all of that themselves. Sure, at first it didn't quite work out as we planned and in the end we had to tear down half the forest - but - it was worth it. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_24": "Still, most of the camp is kind of... broken now. And someone with a good hammer and a steady hand needs to fix that. Or I am afraid we will have to freeze... during the cold evenings... well you know, hard times. ...",
  "npc.rottin_wood.multi_25": "So what do you say, in for this one?",
  "npc.yaman.multi_1": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.yaman.multi_2": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.frafnar.multi_1": "Great! That's my breakthrough. Now she can't refuse to go out with me. I grant you access to the western part of the mine.",
  "npc.frafnar.multi_2": "So did you tell her that the cake came from me?",
  "npc.ariella.multi_1": "The sailors always tell tales about the famous beer of Carlin. You must know, alcohol is forbidden in that city. ...",
  "npc.ariella.multi_2": "The beer is served in a secret whisper bar anyway. Bring me a sample of the whisper beer, NOT the usual beer but whisper beer. I hope you are listening.",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_1": "So you have made it? You have really managed to steal a Tear of Daraman? ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_2": "Amazing how you humans are just impossible to get rid of. Incidentally, you have this character trait in common with many insects and with other vermin. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_3": "Nevermind. I hate to say it, but it you have done us a favour, human. That gemstone will serve us well. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_4": "Baa'leal, wants you to talk to Malor concerning some new mission. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_5": "Looks like you have managed to extended your life expectancy - for just a bit longer.",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_6": "All right then, human. Have you ever heard of the {'Tears of Daraman'}? ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_7": "They are precious gemstones made of some unknown blue mineral and possess enormous magical power. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_8": "If you want to learn more about these gemstones don't forget to visit our library. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_9": "Anyway, one of them is enough to create thousands of our mighty djinn blades. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_10": "Unfortunately my last gemstone broke and therefore I'm not able to create new blades anymore. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_11": "To my knowledge there is only one place where you can find these gemstones - I know for a fact that the Marid have at least one of them. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_12": "Well... to cut a long story short, your mission is to sneak into Ashta'daramai and to steal it. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_13": "Needless to say, the Marid won't be too eager to part with it. Try not to get killed until you have delivered the stone to me.",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_14": "So Baa'leal thinks you are up to do a mission for us? ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_15": "I think he is getting old, entrusting human scum such as you are with an important mission like that. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_16": "Personally, I don't understand why you haven't been slaughtered right at the gates. ...",
  "npc.alesar_functions.multi_17": "Anyway. Are you prepared to embark on a dangerous mission for us?",
  "npc.arito.multi_1": "Thank you thousand times! Well, I think I start telling you what I think they are after...",
  "npc.arito.multi_2": "You have to know, I was one of them before I opened that shop here. Sure they fear about their hideout being revealed by me. Please go to the north, there is a small cave in the mountains with a rock in the middle. ...",
  "npc.arito.multi_3": "If you stand in front of it, place a scimitar - which is the weapon of the nomads - left of you and make a sacrifice to the earth by pouring some water on the floor to your right. ...",
  "npc.arito.multi_4": "The entrance to their hideout will be revealed in front of you. I don't know who is in charge there right now but please tell him that I won't spoil their secret...",
  "npc.arito.multi_5": "... well, I just told you but anyway .... I won't tell it to anybody else. Now hurry up before they get here!!",
  "npc.arito.multi_6": "What?? My name on a deathlist which you retrieved from a nomad?? Show me!! ...",
  "npc.arito.multi_7": "Oh my god! They found me! You must help me! Please !!!! Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_1": "I can't explain that stuff, even the gnomes don't know what grows in those caves. All we know is that this stuff brought about all the diremaws we are now facing. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_2": "This vermin is somehow attracted to this sponge, my guess is they use it as a nourishment, too. We need to get rid of the stuff regularly to reduce their numbers to a manageable level. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_3": "We hauled our explosives down there - and I mean ALL our explosives. Dangerous? Indeed, so we positioned someone down there to actually watch this depot. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_4": "We built an iron fence around it and added a mechanism to quickly get barrel if need be. Then an... accident happened to our guard down there and ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_5": "Well, to make a long story short, the barrels are unguarded right now and the diremaws are now too numerous and we are in desperate need of volunteers. ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_6": "We need someone to take those barrels to the source of the ever growing sponge and burn it down. All of it. There should be at least five locations. Are you up for that? ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_7": "I can't explain that stuff, even the gnomes don't know what grows in those caves. All we know is that this stuff brought about all the diremaws we are now facing. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_8": "This vermin is somehow attracted to this sponge, my guess is they use it as a nourishment, too. We need to get rid of the stuff regularly to reduce their numbers to a manageable level. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_9": "We hauled our explosives down there - and I mean ALL our explosives. Dangerous? Indeed, so we positioned someone down there to actually watch this depot. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_10": "We built an iron fence around it and added a mechanism to quickly get barrel if need be. Then an... accident happened to our guard down there and ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_11": "Well, to make a long story short, the barrels are unguarded right now and the diremaws are now too numerous and we are in desperate need of volunteers. ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_12": "We need someone to take those barrels to the source of the ever growing sponge and burn it down. All of it. There should be at least five locations. Are you up for that? ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_13": "The gnomes say that these creatures seem to thrive on mushroom sponges. But not only that, apparently they also lay eggs in their own cadavers to breed even faster. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_14": "Yes, disgusting. I guess it provides everything their offspring needs... well, we probably shouldn't go into that much further. Instead we should focus on preventing that from happening. ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_15": "If I understood that correctly, the gnomes 'grew' a device to completely neutralise diremaw corpses. Acting as a very effective counter measure. ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_16": "A lot of corpses are lying around wherever these creatures are being hunted. Now all we need are, you guessed it, volunteers to clean up as many of those remains as possible ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_17": "Are you willing to help? ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_18": "The gnomes say that these creatures seem to thrive on mushroom sponges. But not only that, apparently they also lay eggs in their own cadavers to breed even faster. ...",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_19": "Yes, disgusting. I guess it provides everything their offspring needs... well, we probably shouldn't go into that much further. Instead we should focus on preventing that from happening. ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_20": "If I understood that correctly, the gnomes 'grew' a device to completely neutralise diremaw corpses. Acting as a very effective counter measure. ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_21": "A lot of corpses are lying around wherever these creatures are being hunted. Now all we need are, you guessed it, volunteers to clean up as many of those remains as possible ... ",
  "npc.lardoc_bashsmite.multi_22": "Are you willing to help? ",
  "npc.vanys.multi_1": "You have to empower eight ward stones. Once charged with arcane energy, they will strengthen the Nightmare Beast's prison and at the same time weaken this terrible creature. We know about the specific location of six of those stones. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_2": "You can find them in the mountains of the island Okolnir, in a water elemental cave beneath Folda, in the depths of Calassa, in the forests of Feyrist and on the islands Meriana and Cormaya. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_3": "The location of the other two ward stones is a bit more obscure, however. We are not completely sure where they are. You should make inquiries at an abandoned house in the Plains of Havoc. You may find it east of an outlaw camp. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_4": "The other stone seems to be somewhere in Tiquanda. Search for a small stone building south-west of Banuta. Take this talisman to empower the ward stones. It will work with the six stones at the known locations. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_5": "However, the empowering of the two hidden stones could be a bit more complicated. But you have to find out on yourself what to do with those stones.",
  "npc.vanys.multi_6": "You empowered all eight ward stones. Well done! You may now enter the Dream Labyrinth via the portal here in the Court. Beneath it you will find the Nightmare Beast's lair. But the labyrinth is protected by seven so called Dream Doors. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_7": "You have to find the Seven {Keys} to unlock the Seven Dream Doors down there. Only then you will be able to enter the Nightmare Beast's lair.",
  "npc.vanys.multi_8": "You will have to re-empower several wardstones all over the world, to weaken the beast of nightmares. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_9": "The next step would be to enter a place known as dream scar and participate in battles, to gain access to the lower areas. ...",
  "npc.vanys.multi_10": "There the nightmare beast can be challenged and defeated.",
  "npc.vanys.multi_11": "So do you want to learn the story behind of this or rather talk about the {task} at hand?",
  "npc.emma.multi_1": "I have bad news: a mad dwarf threatens to destroy our beloved city. He claims to have invented some device that enables him to destroy the whole city ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_2": "He has a laboratory somewhere in Kazordoon, probably somewhere near the technomancer hall. Find him and kill him! Bring me his beard as a proof!",
  "npc.emma.multi_3": "As you might know, once the old aristocracy of our city shared blood-ties with the noblemen of Thais. There are many unresolved claims for titles and family heirlooms and Thais does little to help in this matter ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_4": "Therefore, we will take matters into our own hands. There is a grave in the crypts on the Isle of the Kings in which we assume a book containing ancient family histories and family trees ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_5": "We need this book! We will not ask how you acquired it.",
  "npc.emma.multi_6": "Ruins of some ancient cathedral are found south west of Venore. It was a project that the Thaians never finished. However, our scouts reported some suspicious activities there ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_7": "There is a continual coming and going which hints on something big hiding there. We ask you to enter the ruins of the cathedral and to find out what all these people are doing there ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_8": "You might find several hints there, but I am sure you will know exactly when you have found what we are looking for.",
  "npc.emma.multi_9": "Venore has plans for a new kind of ship. It will be faster and more resilient than any other known ship. It will surely improve their dominance over the sea trade. Unless we get those plans for ourselves ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_10": "And this is where you come into play. Find the ship plans in the Venorean shipyard or perhaps at the harbour and bring them here immediately.",
  "npc.emma.multi_11": "The scheming Venoreans are a constant thorn in our side. They supply our enemies with all kind of equipment to boost the threat they pose to our freedom. It will be your task to hinder future weapon deliveries significantly ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_12": "The druids have supplied us with some exotic bugs. They are called rust bugs and they did not receive this name for their colour ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_13": "Take this box of rust bugs and use them on the keyhole of the smithy in the Ironhouse. These 'pets' will ruin all metal there and it will take them a while to get rid of them.",
  "npc.emma.multi_14": "The druids have asked the brigade for a favour. Given that we heavily rely on their resources and they are important supporters of our cities, we can't deny them the request ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_15": "A wandering druid has recently visited the Green Claw Swamp, located north west of that corrupted hell hole Venore. While gathering herbs, he noticed some malignant presence in the said area ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_16": "Searching for the source of evil there, he detected some old ruin. Suddenly, he was attacked by bonelords and their undead minions. He barely managed to escape alive ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_17": "The evidence he found let him conclude that the bonelords in the ruins were raising so-called death trees.These trees are full of negative energy and slowly but steadily corrupt their surrounding ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_18": "After the druid's return to Carlin, divination confirmed his upsetting assumptions about the existence of these trees ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_19": "Over the years, hundreds have fallen victim to the swamp, conserved by mud and water for eternity. With the help of the death trees, the bonelords strive for an army of undeads. This cannot be tolerated ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_20": "Travel to Green Claw Swamp and rip out the heart out of the master tree. Without it, the unnatural trees will wither soon. Bring me the heart as proof.",
  "npc.emma.multi_21": "Our relations with Thais can be called strained at best. Therefore, it's not really astounding that the Thaian financed Edron's academy but refuse to share some knowledge with our druids ..",
  "npc.emma.multi_22": "But we won't accept this so easily. With the help of divination, we learnt that the knowledge our druids are looking for is found in a certain book ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_23": "It will be your task to enter the academy and to steal this book for us.",
  "npc.emma.multi_24": "Excellent. The queen was not amused about this threat. It's a good thing that you have saved the city ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_25": "Unfortunately, as we are secret agents we can't parade for you or something like that, but let me express our gratitude for everything you have done for our city ...",
  "npc.emma.multi_26": "Take this token of gratitude. You will know when to use it!",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_1": "Impressive!! Let me take a look.......Ahh, ",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_2": "an ETERNAL FLAME! Now you need to find a knight, a druid, and a paladin who also completed this first task. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_3": "MOTHER SOIL! Now you need to find a knight, a paladin, and a sorcerer who also completed this first task. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_4": "a FLAWLESS ICE CRYSTAL! Now you need to find a knight, a druid, and a sorcerer who also completed this first task. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_5": "PURE ENERGY! Now you need to find a druid, a paladin, and a sorcerer who also completed this first task. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_6": "Go down in the cellar again. I prepared a room under the academy where it should be safe. Your task is to charge the machines with the elemental substances and summon the LORD OF THE ELEMENTS. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_7": "When you use an obsidian knife on it's corpse you hopefully get some of the precious neutral matter. It's the only way to revive my dear friend Alverus!!",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_8": "Okay, listen closely: First of all, you need to gather 20 enchanted amethysts in order to go to the energy sphere. Deep under the academy, one floor below the elemental shrines, there is a machine. Put the gems in there and activate it. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_9": "Once you got there, find a way to gather elemental energy in any form. You will face energy elementals, that's for sure, but I don't know how the energy is stored. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_10": "Anyway, there should be a way to use that energy and strengthen one of the elementals. If my calculations are right, you will create an Energy Overlord who hopefully will consist of some sort of 'concentrated' energy. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_11": "THAT'S what we need!! Are you in on it?",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_12": "Okay, listen closely: First of all, you need to gather 20 enchanted sapphires in order to go to the ice sphere. Deep under the academy, one floor below the elemental shrines, there is a machine. Put the gems in there and activate it. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_13": "Once you got there, find a way to gather elemental ice in any form. You will face ice elementals, that's for sure, but I don't know how the ice is stored. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_14": "Anyway, there should be a way to use that elemental ice and strengthen one of the elementals. If my calculations are right, you will create an Ice Overlord who hopefully will consist of some sort of 'concentrated' ice or something similar. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_15": "THAT'S what we need!! Are you in on it?",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_16": "Okay, listen closely: First of all, you need to gather 20 enchanted emeralds in order to go to the earth sphere. Deep under the academy, one floor below the elemental shrines, there is a machine. Put the gems in there and activate it. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_17": "Once you got there, find a way to gather elemental earth in any form. You will face earth elementals, that's for sure, but I don't know how the earth is stored. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_18": "Anyway, there should be a way to use that elemental earth and strengthen one of the elementals. If my calculations are right, you will create an Earth Overlord who hopefully will consist of some sort of 'concentrated' earth or something similar. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_19": "THAT'S what we need!! Are you in on it?",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_20": "Okay, listen closely: First of all, you need to gather 20 enchanted rubies in order to go to the fire sphere. Deep under the academy, one floor below the elemental shrines, there is a machine. Put the gems in there and activate it. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_21": "Once you got there, find a way to gather elemental fire in any form. You will face fire elementals, that's for sure, but I don't know how the fire is stored. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_22": "Anyway, there should be a way to use that elemental fire and strengthen one of the elementals. If my calculations are right, you will create a Fire Overlord who hopefully will consist of some sort of 'concentrated' fire or something similar. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_23": "THAT'S what we need!! Are you in on it?",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_24": "There are four spheres we know of: ice, fire, earth and energy. ....<mumbles> Hmmm, should I ask or not?....The heck with it! Now that you know about the spheres ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_25": "I found a way to visit them. It's VERY dangerous and there is a decent chance that you won't come back BUT if you succeed you'll write history!!! Ask me about that {mission} if you're interested.",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_26": "The creation of the elemental shrines is a really complex matter. They are actually nodes, locations where the matching elemental sphere is very close. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_27": "The shrine itself is like a portal between our world and the elemental {sphere} and enables us to use the elemental energy emerging from it.",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_28": "It happened while he carried out an experiment concerning the creation of the elemental {shrines}. I still get goose bumps just by thinking of it. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_29": "You need to know about the process of creating an elemental shrine to understand it completely, but I don't want to go into detail now. ...",
  "npc.arkulius.multi_30": "Anyway, his spell had a different outcome than he had planned. He accidentally created an Ice Overlord, pure living elemental ice, who froze him in a blink of an eye.",
  "npc.tamerin.multi_1": "Why should I do something for another human being? I have been on my own for all those years. Hmm, but actually there is something I could need some assistance with. ... ",
  "npc.tamerin.multi_2": "If you help me to solve my problems, I will help you with your mission. Do you accept?",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_1": "You have to travel to the isle of the kings. There, hidden beneath the isle of the kings is the shamefully hidden grave of king Zelos. It is him, they are trying to raise. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_2": "With some luck you will arrive before the ritual's completion. But be warned. At least four risen lich-knights will be present, to raise 'their king'. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_3": "Hopefully the ritual will bind some of their powers but they will still be formidable foes. You will have to act quick because with each moment you take to defeat the knights ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_4": "The ritual will progress and the king will become stronger up to a point where you might be unable to defeat him. Due to the efforts and sacrifices of the death cultists, the king will be active at some capacity and you will have to confront him. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_5": "Remember, the further the ritual progresses when you face him, he will become considerably more powerful. So time is of the essence. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_6": "All I can do right now is to wish you good luck and may the gods bless you.",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_7": "It became obvious that their goal is to raise an ancient and fallen king, to lead their lich-knights and raise even more of them. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_8": " With each lich-knight being able to raise and control lesser undead, this would lead to a chain-reaction. If they succeed, we might face an undead {threat} not seen since the corpse wars.",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_9": "While you travel and fight the threat where it arises, we will put all our resources into researching the ultimate plans of the legion. Perhaps I can tell you more when you {report} back. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_10": "Don't forget that you'll need very potent holy water for your task. If you need some, just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_11": "While you travel and fight the threat where it arises, we will put all our resources into researching the ultimate plans of the legion. Perhaps I can tell you more when you {report} back. ...",
  "npc.jack_springer.multi_12": "Don't forget that you'll need very potent holy water for your task. If you need some, just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.elvith.multi_1": "The last issue I had was bought by Randor Swiftfinger. He was banished through the hellgate and probably took the book with him ...",
  "npc.elvith.multi_2": "I would not recommend seeking him or the book there, but of course it is possible.",
  "npc.jacob.multi_1": "A sacrificial site? Damn, sounds like some freakish cult or something. Just great. And this ancient structure you talked about that's not part of the sewers? You'd better see the local historian about that, man. ...",
  "npc.jacob.multi_2": "He can make more sense of what you found there. His name is Barazbaz. He should be in the magistrate building.",
  "npc.jacob.multi_3": "Wow, you already did it, that's fast. I'm used to a more laid-back attitude from most people. It's a shame to risk losing you to some collapsing tunnels, but a deal is a deal. ...",
  "npc.jacob.multi_4": "I hereby grant you the permission to enter the abandoned part of the sewers. Take care, man! ...",
  "npc.jacob.multi_5": "If you find something interesting, come back to talk about the {abandoned sewers}.",
  "npc.jacob.multi_6": "You want to enter the abandoned sewers? That's rather dangerous and not a good idea, man. That part of the sewers was not sealed off for nothing, you know? ...",
  "npc.jacob.multi_7": "But hey, it's your life, bro. So here's the deal. I'll let you into the abandoned sewers if you help me with our {mission}.",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_1": "Even though we are spirits, we can't create anything out of thin air. You will have to donate some precious metal which we can drain for energy and substance. ...",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_2": "The equivalent of 5000 gold will do. Are you willing to make such a donation?",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_3": "Even though we are spirits, we can't create anything out of thin air. You will have to donate some precious metal which we can drain for energy and substance. ...",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_4": "The equivalent of 5000 gold will do. Are you willing to make such a donation?",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_5": "Even though we are spirits, we can't create anything out of thin air. You will have to donate some precious metal which we can drain for energy and substance. ...",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_6": "The equivalent of 5000 gold will do. Are you willing to make such a donation?",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_7": "Although we are willing to hand this item to you, there is something you have to understand: There is no such thing as 'the' sceptre. ...",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_8": "Those sceptres are created for special purposes each time anew. Therefore you will have to create one on your own. It will be your {mission} to find us three keepers and to get the three parts of the holy sceptre. ...",
  "npc.ghost_of_a_priest.multi_9": "Then go to the holy altar and create a new one.",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_1": "Thank you! He told me the other researchers in his team discovered a bridge leading to a cave with a dragon sculpture somewhere in a muggy, grassy area. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_2": "The cave is said to lead to a temple complex underground which is ued as a gathering place for a race called 'draken'. He left right away and tried to enter Zao on his own. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_3": "I was even more worried when he explained the route he chose. he wanted to head straight through a giant steppe and through a massive mountainous ridge to reach the grassy plains of lower Zao. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_4": "If you're interested: I know that the Shapers where active in all corners of Tibia. If you happen to find Shaper ruins there, you may even be able to gather some of their lost knowledge. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_5": "I may have been a bit stubborn and angry the day he left, I even refused to say farewell. And now I worry if he is safe. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_6": "I can not do much to help you but I can open a portal to get you quite close to his last known location in Zao. What do you say, will you help me find my father?",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_7": "What? You're telling me you found father? How is he? What did papa say? A chalice? As a disguise? The whole time? ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_8": "Well, I am not as much surprised as I am happy to hear that he's alright. You know, after the incident with the duck and the umbrella—it doesn't get to me that easily anymore. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_9": "Thank you very much for doing all this for me; I will be forever grateful. I have nothing to repay you with, but you are already blessed to have been able to lay eyes on the sacred Shaper ruins.",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_10": "Papa- my father has recently started an adventure on his own. His name is Silus; he is a member of the Edron academy. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_11": "Ever since he joined what he called a 'special research division', he went on and on about Zao and how venturing there would help him get ahead. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_12": "You must know he lives for science, especially concerning faraway lands and cultures. He talked about the importance of practical field studies but, frankly, he isn't particularly cut out for that. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_13": "I know he has to focus to get his research done right now, and I simply cannot leave my duties in the temple. You seem like a person who travels a lot; would you be willing to help me?",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_14": "The astral Shapers had many ways to shape and refine weapons and equipment. They built shrines dedicated to this world's energies, focussing it and utilising it like a tool to enhance objects. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_15": "They called this process imbuing and perfected it throughout time. Remains of these shrines are scattered all over Tibia. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_16": "If you truly want to master this art, you will need to visit the various ancient sites related to the original Shaper imbuements. There is one for each element and we know of at least one other besides these. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_17": "The discovery of the foundations of this very temple we are standing in, was the key to access their legacy. It is now the center of all our efforts in getting closer to the astral predecessors. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_18": "They found ways to connect various sites with a system of gates, all concentrating energy to allow travel to far away places. The more we learn, the more we can restore of these ancient gateways. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_19": "We see the gates as an invitation, use them to your advantage and follow the ways of the Shapers. Access to one of these ancient shrines is the only way to learn additional imbuements. ...",
  "npc.ivalisse.multi_20": "But beware, as far as we know, some of them have been claimed by other ancient beings and there is now way for us to prepare you what lies beyond any of those gates.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_1": "I knew it! I knew I had made a copy! Oh, I am so clever! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_2": "Now, watch this. <mumbles darkly> THERE. THE COMPLETE INCANTATION SCROLL. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_3": "You have done well. Only one thing remains, and you shall be rich beyond your dreams. Ready for the really final task?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_4": "Hahah, eager for it, I like that! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_5": "One piece stayed in the hands of a beautiful priestess. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_6": "As they never throw anything away that looks like an incantation - you get my drift. Find out where they still keep it! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_7": "Oh, one more thing! They only talk to you when you look like a fellow summoner. It's dangerous to go without a cape. Use this.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_8": "Good! As you can imagine, I had a scroll piece, too. I hid it in my old quarters, northwest of the library. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_9": "The door is magically sealed. Use this copper key with it to get inside. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_10": "Beneath one of the chests is a secret stash, under a loose stone tile. The scroll piece should be inside. Off you go.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_11": "Hah, developed a taste for it, have you? I believe the next scroll piece was hidden somewhere, my old friend being of a somewhat distrustful nature. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_12": "The scent may not be lost, though - ask a shadow pupil if he can help - but be careful. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_13": "Those shadow pupils are - strange. Try to find one who will answer and not kill you!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_14": "Oh, praise the Dark Lord! It is my scroll piece! Give it here! You can have this instead. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_15": "Ahh, that feels GOOD. Now, only two pieces left to hunt down! On to the {next} scroll piece, yes?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_16": "Well, it is a rather long story. The short version: I had friends - no need to snigger. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_17": "We were five highly brilliant dark summoners. We joined our forces to find the scroll of Youth and Life Eternal. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_18": "But when we finally found it after years of toiling and danger, we quarreled over who could have it. The scroll tore. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_19": "We each retained one piece of the scroll. Well, that was a long time ago. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_20": "But I think I have a clue where we can find the first piece of the scroll. Would you go looking?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_21": "<reverential> The final altar that remains to be hallowed... the Shadowthrone. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_22": "Only a candle made of human tallow placed before each shadow statue in the right order, will awaken it. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_23": "I say, are you sick? Human tallow candles are a perfectly good tool - don't look at me like that! Be professional about this, will you? ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_24": "I have some candles hidden deep down in the lich caves, east of here. Here's the key that opens the trapdoor to the cache. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_25": "And take this parchment. Identify the right candles with it, take three with you and place one in front of the three shadowthrone statues, starting counterclockwise. Now go!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_26": "Yes, I said blood. Important ingredient in necromantic rituals, usually. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_27": "You need to spill some vials of blood tincture for this task. Probably means killing blood priests to get those vials. Ready to do this?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_28": "I expected no less. Next is the Bonemarrow Altar, where the Dark Lord feasts upon the hallowed bones of...err. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_29": "Ahem. Just take a yellowed bone or big bone, and hallow it - you don't know how? ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_30": "Huh. To HALLOW a yellowed bone, use it with one of the hallowed bonepiles in the Gardens Of Night. There are always bones around there - or were, in my days. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_31": "Then, place the hallowed bone on the firebasin of the Bonemarrow Altar so the Dark Lord can consume it and grants us his power. Return to me after that.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_32": "Good! Let's not waste time. The first altar you must hallow is the Dragonsoul Altar, at the eastern side of the room. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_33": "To hallow it, dig out three dragon tears and place them on the altar to appease the dark powers. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_34": "What? Oh, you'll find some dragon tears near dragon skulls... where? ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_35": "In the Dragonbone Cemetery, OBVIOUSLY! Must I explain EVERYTHING to you? Now go!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_36": "Then let's go. Take my skull and the incantation scroll to the working station in the fiveserrated room ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_37": "Where the lava flows and the southern legs of the room meet. Place the Skull on the sacrificial stone and use the scroll ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_38": "AND I shall be made whole, and YOU shall be RICH!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_39": "I am so excited! Finally, we - wait. What is this? That... is not the complete scroll piece. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_40": "I don't care what you say! This is a disaster! We need a complete scr - wait. I have an idea. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_41": "There must be a copy or something in my old library. something to use with the scroll, to find the missing words. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_42": "There must be. Go look there. Next to the fiveserrated room, a small library. Go go go!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_43": "That's the spirit! Speaking of which, you will have to look for a White Shade ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_44": "That's a ghost, in case you don't know. Goes by name of... Zarifan, if I recall correctly. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_45": "His grave is somewhere to the south, somewhere deeper. And he only reacts to magic words. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_46": "Err... it's embarrassing... the magic words are <mumble> <mumble> <ahem> ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_47": "'Friendship lives forever.' Silly, really. Untrue, as well. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_48": "Anyway, say those three words - don't make me repeat them - and the old softie will tell you where the scroll is. Pathetic.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_49": "Ahhh, capital, capital. Good girl for keeping it for me. I'll take back my cape now, thank you. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_50": "Now - the final part of the scroll! Ready to go retrieve it?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_51": "Hahah, eager for it, I like that! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_52": "One piece stayed in the hands of a beautiful priestess. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_53": "As they never throw anything away that looks like an incantation - you get my drift. Find out where they still keep it! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_54": "Oh, one more thing! They only talk to you when you look like a fellow summoner. It's dangerous to go without a cape. Use this.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_55": "Oh, praise the Dark Lord! It is my scroll piece! Give it here! You can have this instead. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_56": "Ahh, that feels GOOD. Now, only two pieces left to hunt down! On to the {next} scroll piece, yes?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_57": "Good! As you can imagine, I had a scroll piece, too. I hid it in my old quarters, northwest of the library. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_58": "The door is magically sealed. Use this copper key with it to get inside. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_59": "Beneath one of the chests is a secret stash, under a loose stone tile. The scroll piece should be inside. Off you go.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_60": "Hah, developed a taste for it, have you? I believe the next scroll piece was hidden somewhere, my old friend being of a somewhat distrustful nature. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_61": "The scent may not be lost, though - ask a shadow pupil if he can help - but be careful. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_62": "Those shadow pupils are - strange. Try to find one who will answer and not kill you!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_63": "Superb! You won't regret this. I will reward you beyond your wildest dreams! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_64": "I know that one of my former friends joined the blood priests later on. He made it quite high before he was ritually killed. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_65": "Go find a blood priest you can talk to. Ask him, but subtly. And never tell anyone what the scroll does!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_66": "Excellent. To bind the earthly powers, we, I mean you, must worship at the Fireglass Altar. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_67": "This means scattering sacred ashes from the Ember Chamber on the sacrificial stones of the Fireglass Altar. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_68": "To gather the sacred ashes, you have to use magic chalk with the Shadow Fire in the Ember Chamber. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_69": "Gather the resulting ashes from the Shadow Hearth, and scatter them on the Fireglass Altar's sacrificial stones. Then return here.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_70": "Ah, I knew you were a sturdy fellow! Necromancer material if ever I saw one! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_71": "Well then, the next task is to anoint the Bloodgong Altar. This will animate the dark flows we need for the ritual. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_72": "You need to spill a vial of blood tincture on each of the four sacrifical stones of the altar in order to anoint them. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_73": "Then, toll the Bloodgong north of the sacrificial stones to set the dark flows going. Return to me after that.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_74": "Ah... interesting. A snake? Not bad, not bad at all. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_75": "Right. Now, we need to waken the old powers through ritual. Let me know when you are ready for this {mission}.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_76": "Very sensible of you. I will pay you handsomely for your help. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_77": "All you have to do is fetch diverse fresh body parts and then prepare the resurrection ritual. Nothing out of the ordinary. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_78": "First, I need two arms. Ghouls usually carry some as a snack. Two ghoul snacks should not be hard to get! Return when you have them.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_79": "It failed! IT FAILED! WHY? What have you done! This must be your fault! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_80": "You... did... that was a recipe for chicken soup! No wonder the scroll failed! Now... all is lost ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_81": "<sobs drily> I never want to see you again! You and your dirty gravedigger hands! Take this, you ungrateful, useless, imbecile... human! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_82": "Now... get out! And never, ever, dare come back! You ruined EVERYTHING!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_83": "That's the spirit! Speaking of which, you will have to look for a White Shade ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_84": "That's a ghost, in case you don't know. Goes by name of... Zarifan, if I recall correctly. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_85": "His grave is somewhere to the south, somewhere deeper. And he only reacts to magic words. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_86": "Err... it's embarrassing... the magic words are <mumble> <mumble> <ahem> ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_87": "'Friendship lives forever.' Silly, really. Untrue, as well. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_88": "Anyway, say those three words - don't make me repeat them - and the old softie will tell you where the scroll is. Pathetic.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_89": "Hahah, eager for it, I like that! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_90": "One piece stayed in the hands of a beautiful priestess. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_91": "As they never throw anything away that looks like an incantation - you get my drift. Find out where they still keep it! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_92": "Oh, one more thing! They only talk to you when you look like a fellow summoner. It's dangerous to go without a cape. Use this.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_93": "Good! As you can imagine, I had a scroll piece, too. I hid it in my old quarters, northwest of the library. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_94": "The door is magically sealed. Use this copper key with it to get inside. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_95": "Beneath one of the chests is a secret stash, under a loose stone tile. The scroll piece should be inside. Off you go.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_96": "Hah, developed a taste for it, have you? I believe the next scroll piece was hidden somewhere, my old friend being of a somewhat distrustful nature. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_97": "The scent may not be lost, though - ask a shadow pupil if he can help - but be careful. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_98": "Those shadow pupils are - strange. Try to find one who will answer and not kill you!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_99": "Yes! YES! I have felt that! The altars are alive again! Well done! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_100": "We are close now. Only one important thing remains: the incantation itself. We need the {scroll} for that.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_101": "Ah, finally. Exceptional! Don't you feel the earth awakening to our call? No? Oh. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_102": "Anyway, you succeeded in hallowing the Fireglass Altar! Only one altar remains to be hallowed! Shall we {proceed}?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_103": "Ah, it is invigorating to fell the dark flows, rushing through Drefia, once again! Capital. This has earned you a reward. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_104": "Now, the next mission awaits, {yes}?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_105": "Yes, I said blood. Important ingredient in necromantic rituals, usually. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_106": "You need to spill some vials of blood tincture for this task. Probably means killing blood priests to get those vials. Ready to do this?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_107": "Ah, welcome, welcome! I felt that one! The Dark Lord is pleased with the gift you brought, so now we can proceed with everything as planned. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_108": "If it had gone wrong though, he would have had your guts for gart... er... well, here you are, so - ready to get some {blood} flowing?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_109": "Are you still here? Come on, let's not laze about, go to the Gardens of Night - where? ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_110": "East of the Necromancer Halls, you can't miss it, just look for a lot of dark and white sand, dried trees, and priestesses! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_111": "Or got a {problem} with finding bones? Hah!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_112": "I expected no less. Next is the Bonemarrow Altar, where the Dark Lord feasts upon the hallowed bones of...err. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_113": "Ahem. Just take a yellowed bone or big bone, and hallow it - you don't know how? ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_114": "Huh. To HALLOW a yellowed bone, use it with one of the hallowed bonepiles in the Gardens Of Night. There are always bones around there - or were, in my days. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_115": "Then, place the hallowed bone on the firebasin of the Bonemarrow Altar so the Dark Lord can consume it and grants us his power. Return to me after that.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_116": "Good. As you may have gathered, the body parts you brought need to be assembled to form a whole body. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_117": "This will happen through a necromantic ritual that we - or rather, you - now have to prepare. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_118": "In a first step, it will involve retrieving specific artefacts of dark magic and hallowing the altars of the dark powers with them. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_119": "After that, you will have to speak an ancient incantation to animate the body and fuse my soul within. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_120": "But first things first. Are you ready to {undertake} the hallowing of the five altars?",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_121": "Now that you have shown you've got the brains, I need you to show initiative. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_122": "I will need something that can be adequately used as intestines. Something alive. Stuff it into this storage flask and return it to me!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_123": "I will need brains - don't laugh! Ahem. I will need a stimulated brain, to be precise. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_124": "Use two half-eaten brains with the Brain Heater Machine in the Necromancer halls and bring me the fused, stimulated brain. Now go!",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_125": "Yes? You have it? You what? Not in the amphoras? You picked it off someone else?!? ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_126": "Well, the important thing is that you have it. Let's see if it's still in good shape. {Give} it to me.",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_127": "I need my heart back. I know where they have hidden it. Too afraid to destroy my beating heart, hah! ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_128": "It is in a dusty amphora in a sealed mass grave in the downmost cellar of my ancient home. The ruins lie to the north at the beach. ...",
  "npc.omrabas.multi_129": "Crash the amphoras to find my heart, and bring it to me.",
  "npc.the_librarian.multi_1": "To extract memories from the ring, you have to enter a trance-like state with the help of a hallucinogen. Like this you can see all memories that are stored in the ring. Ask Faloriel for a respective potion. ...",
  "npc.the_librarian.multi_2": "Drink it while wearing the ring in the Temple of Bastesh and say: 'Sa Katesa Tarsani na'. If the legends are true you will be able to take memories with you in the form of memory shards.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_1": "Oh, my! That sounds like a real mess. For now this dragon empire seems otherwise engaged, but we will be on guard thanks to you my friend. We will continue to fortify the base. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_2": "This leaves not much to do for you down here. I recommend you continue to explore this strange new land. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_3": "I'm pretty sure there are several opportunities at hand for an adventurer like you. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_4": "Perhaps you can help the primitives you encountered. Who knows, maybe even those minotaurs give you a chance to fortify this fragile peace between us. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_5": "Even some of the people here in the base might offer you some tasks sooner or later. If you prefer, you can also do some exploring, hunting and good ol' plundering on your own of course. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_6": "This new land is yours to be taken, so to say. Go out and make your fortune! With Farmine you have always a safe haven to return to. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_7": "Oh and one last thing: We convinced a carpet pilot to join us here. You'll find him on top of our lift in the mountains. I think he can offer you fast access to some cities back home.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_8": "Ooook. Now that we managed to keep those orcs and minotaurs at bay at least for a while, we learn that the real meanies over here are some lizardmen. Just great, isn't it?. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_9": "So you might already guess your next mission: Find a way to hold those lizards off. Find them, contact them, talk to them, scare them, bribe them, whatever. Just keep that snakes away if anyhow possible. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_10": "If the orcs are right, they are somewhere in or behind those mountains in the north. I doubt you can reason with them in any way, but you'll have to try for the sake of Farmine.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_11": "Our new friends, those primitive humans sent us a warning. According to them, the 'green men' of the plains plan an attack on the mountains. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_12": "Considering their expected number, there is no chance for us to beat them off. We might be able to hold our ground for a while, but without access to the surface and under constant attacks, we might have to abandon the base. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_13": "Now, I'm aware that you cannot stop an entire army by yourself, but desperate situations call for desperate measures. I ask you to find the leaders of the orcs and - well do something. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_14": "Scare them, bribe them, give them another target or whatever. As futile as it may sound: Try to talk to their leaders in some way and make them stop their attack plans. This is our only hope.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_15": "Things are getting more and more complicated. You need to convince our friends that some intervention for their part is needed. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_16": "We've come a long way with our own resources, but now our resources are short and we need the others to step in. I want you to negotiate some more support from our partners. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_17": "You'll need all your diplomacy and influence. If you blow the negotiations, look for a guy called Black Bert in Thais. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_18": "He has access to all kind of odd items, and he might have just the right bribe to convince someone to continue negotiations. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_19": "It will not be as easy as it might sound. So watch your words and your manners and keep in mind whom you are talking to. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_20": "Different strategies might be necessary for different people. You may try to FLATTER, THREATEN, IMPRESS, BLUFF, PLEA or to REASON with them. You probably need some luck as well. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_21": "And now listen: We need more workers for the mines. The technomancers told us that a guy named Telas, who lives in Edron, copied the worker golem technology from Yalahar. Convince him to send us some of these golems. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_22": "Further, we have more ore and end products than we can use right now. So we need someone to buy all the surplus. Convince Leeland Slim in Venore that the local traders step in as resellers. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_23": "Another issue at hand is our lack of drilling worms. That should not be a big problem though. Just talk to the worm tamer in Kazordoon. If he does not get mad about you, there should be no problem to get his support. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_24": "Also, now that our monetary resources are used up and not much cash is coming in, we need additional help to finance this venture. Thais has promised money in advance, but we haven't seen any of this support, yet. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_25": "Convince the Thaian king to send us the promised money right now. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_26": "Another problem we need to solve is the exploration of our surroundings. We need to know friends and enemies, and find out about the plants and beasts in the vicinity and learn what is edible and what is dangerous. ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_27": "This is all stuff the Explorer Society is interested in. It should be easy to convince their representative in Port Hope. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_28": "At last, with the growing numbers of adventurers here, not only the security of the base is growing but also the demand for certain supplies. I'd like the Edron academy to open up a shop in the base. We need to keep you adventurers happy, don't we? ... ",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_29": "Well, I hope you understand the importance of this mission and got what it takes to fulfil it. So hurry up and get us the needed support.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_30": "It seems things went from bad to worse! First we had some problems with the mine shafts we were building, and now that we found some precious veins in one of the new mines, and it happens to be the holiday resort of some hostile stone creatures! ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_31": "Nothing we dwarfs couldn't handle alone, but I rather thought this could be something interesting for an adventurer like you. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_32": "So I reserved you the privilege to slay the leader! Use the mining lift to reach mine A07. The more stone creatures you kill, the better. Your mission, however, is to slay their leader, most likely some special stone beast.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_33": "Primitive humans you say? These are most startling news, that's for sure. Well, I guess I'll send some victuals we can spare as a sign of our good will. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_34": "However, our miners encountered another problem in the meantime. I'm afraid this will be your next {mission}",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_35": "Our guards reported some nightly visitors. They chased them through the mountains but lost them when the fugitives climbed up some vines. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_36": "It could easily be some trap and I'm somewhat reluctant to send you there, but we can't allow some invisible aggressor to spy on us and maybe to prepare an attack. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_37": "Find these vines in this mountain, climb up there and find out who is spying on us! If they mean harm, get rid of them if possible. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_38": "If they are too powerful, just retreat and we will have to re-evaluate the situation. If they are harmless, all the better.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_39": "Things are running fine so far. Actually so fine that we are short of supplies and men. I'd send a letter home but I guess sending you to get some assistance gives the whole affair a bit more urgency. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_40": "So please travel back to Kazordoon. In the western mines outside of The Big Old One, you'll find Melfar of the imperial mining guild. Ask him to send some more miners and wood. When you return, I might have some more interesting missions for you.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_41": "Listen, I can handle the organisation down here and my boys will handle the construction of the base fine enough. Actually, all you do down here is to stand in the workers' way. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_42": "But there might be something for you to do outside the base. We need to learn more about the land up there. Take the lift and do some exploring. Find a passage leading out of the mountains. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_43": "Do not explore any further though. You never know whom you might be messing with.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_44": "<grumbles> Well, we have found this place here full of promising resources and plan to create a new mining outpost. Of course this takes a lot of effort and organisation. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_45": "For some of the tasks at hand we need help, even from outsiders like you. So if you are interested in some missions, let me know.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_46": "After centuries the resources beneath and around the Big Old One became alarmingly short. Some decades ago, the imperial mining guild financed a project to search and establish new mines far away from Kazordoon. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_47": "After several tries with mixed success, the project of the technomancers proved the most successful. Their steamships studied and mapped the great underwater rivers deep beneath the earth. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_48": "With the help of certain apparatuses, they tracked deposits of ore and compiled ship routes to reach them. These mining bases had some obvious advantages and disadvantages. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_49": "The suitable spots had no connection to the surface. On the one hand, this meant that the new mines were safe from most kinds of beasts. On the other hand, it meant that all food and material had to be brought there by ship. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_50": "Special, heavy ships were built to carry ore and supplies back and forth. The only limitation for such bases had been the range of the steamships. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_51": "Recently, the technomancers with the help of the temples of fire and earth made some crucial discoveries that allowed the ships to extend their cruising range almost limitlessly. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_52": "The survey ships of the technomancers were once again sent out to find new, promising resources. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_53": "Sadly some of the ships never returned and others only found minor deposits of ore, not worth the effort. But one of the ships made some groundbreaking discovery - a cave that had a connection to the surface. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_54": "As far as the explorers could tell, the area had been unknown to dwarfhood and mankind so far. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_55": "What was more, the said cave system had an abundance of rare ores. The imperial mining guild agreed to fund a new project and to name it 'project far far away'. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_56": "Don't look at me, I'm not the one who came up with that name! Those technomancers are such an imaginative bunch. But where have we been? Oh, yes, the new project! ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_57": "Well, some ships were sent to establish a first base. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_58": "It became painfully obvious that the number of workers needed there could not easily be supplied by the ships alone. Also such a base would require an amount of money, expertise and manpower that the guild could not provide. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_59": "We would need help and additional resources. That's were you come into play. If you are interested, let's talk about possible missions.",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_60": "Well, it's a long story but you really should listen to understand what is going on here. You can also hear a short version of the story, but then don't blame me if you mess something up due to your undwarfish impatience. ...",
  "npc.ongulf.multi_61": "So what would you like to hear, the {long} story or the {short} version?",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_1": "You well did! Great hunt is under best signs now. We prepare weapons and paint faces and then go! ...",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_2": "No no, you no need to help us. But can prepare afterparty! Little men sent us stuff some time ago. Was strange water in there. Brown and stinky! But when we tried all tribe became veeeeeeery happy. ...",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_3": "Now brown water is gone and we sad! Can you bring POT of brown water for party after great hunt? Just bring to me and me trade for shiny treasure.",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_4": "You brought back skull of first leader. Hero of tribe! But we more missions to do. ...",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_5": "Me and Ulala talk about land outside. We wanting to see more of land! Land over big water! But us no can leave tribe. No can cross water. Only way is skull of first leader. ...",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_6": "What holy skull sees, tribe sees. That we believe. Can you bring holy skull over big water and show places?",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_7": "Big problem we have! Skull of first leader gone. He ancestor of whole tribe but died long ago in war. We have keep his skull on our sacred place. ...",
  "npc.lazaran.multi_8": "Then one night, green men came with wolves... and one of wolves took skull and ran off chewing on it! We need back - many wisdom and power is in skull. Maybe they took to north fortress. But can be hard getting in. You try get our holy skull back?",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_1": "You will have to leave the plant through the eastern door on the lowest level. I have arranged for it to be 'accidentally' open. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_2": "As in the past, our enemy still uses a series of machines to open the way to the next section of his lair. You have to turn them all on to proceed. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_3": "They will only work for a certain amount of time though, so you will have to hurry or some of the machines will turn inactive again.",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_4": "While it's buried, it only uses his tentacles to attack. If one is destroyed it will simply use another set of tentacles and its supply seems endless. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_5": "If you manage though to kill all the tentacles it is using within a few heartbeats, it will become confused by its momentary helplessness and will probably attack with its main body. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_6": "That is when you have a chance to destroy it. Pass through its chamber and look for another of my tubes to contact me. Please hurry! End of communication.",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_7": "It's a fearsome subterranean beast like nothing I've ever encountered. It is dangerous and almost unbeatable because its main body is hidden beneath the ground ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_8": "And it has an endless supply of tentacles. But not all is lost, as I have devised a {plan} to battle the beast.",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_9": "His allies are an enigma even to me. It seems they belong to some unknown race that lives deep under the earth. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_10": "They seem to have supplied him with resources and workforce and a powerful {guardian} to prevent anyone from entering the passages to his lair.",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_11": "He is an old enemy of the city and I've battled him often in the past. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe1.multi_12": "Now he has returned for vengeance, he reclaimed an old abandoned underground {laboratory} and he has acquired new powerful {allies}.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_1": "So you went into the leaders' hideout? I hope you were successful and got what you were looking for! Thank you, my friend. Pirates still keep coming here, unfortunately. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_2": "Do you, by chance, would like to kill pirates again for us?",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_3": "This was probably the last time you will be able to enter that hideout. Well done, my friend, our thanks are with you. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_4": "You are most welcome to keep on killing pirates for us though for some bucks and experience. If you want to do so, just ask me about a {task} anytime.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_5": "Hey, great. You've done well! As a small reward I give you some coins from our treasure box. Also, let me tell you an interesting piece of information. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_6": "One of our spies told us about a secret hideout somewhere on Nargor. Supposedly, one of the four pirate leaders can be found there sometimes. If you dare go there, you might be able to face him or her in one on one combat. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_7": "Beware though - prepare yourself well and only flee if you must. This might be your only chance to get into there, so be careful and don't die!",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_8": "The pirates on Nargor are becoming more and more of a threat to us each day. I wish someone could get rid of them once and for all, but unfortunately they just keep coming! ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_9": "Only a dead pirate is a good pirate. I think killing a large number of them would definitely help us to make Sabrehaven a safer place. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_10": "It doesn't matter how long it takes, but... would you be willing to kill 3000 pirates for us?",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_11": "Incredible! You did what no other did even dare to think about! You are indeed a true hero to our cause ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_12": "Sadly I have no ship that lacks a captain, else you would of course be our first choice. I am still true to my word asbest as I am able. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_13": "So take this as your very own ship. Oh, and remind me about the pirate outfit sometime.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_14": "Well done, my friend. That will help us a lot. Of course there are other things to be done though. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_15": "I learned that Klaus, the owner of the tavern, wants me dead. He is offering any of those pirates a mission to kill me....",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_16": "If we could convince him that you fulfilled that mission, the pirates will have the party of their lives. This would beour chance for a sneak attack to damage their boats and steal their plunder! ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_17": "Obtain this mission from him and learn what he needs as a proof. Then return to me and report to me about yourmission so we can formulate an appropriate plan.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_18": "If you manage to accomplish this vital mission you will prove yourself to be a worthy member of our community. Imight even grant you your own ship and pirate clothing! ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_19": "So listen to the first step of my plan. I want you to infiltrate their base. Try to enter their tavern, which meansthat you have to get past the guard. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_20": "You will probably have to deceive him somehow, so that he thinks you are one of them. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_21": "In the tavern, the pirates feel safe and plan their next strikes. Study ALL of their maps and plans lying around ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_22": "Afterwards, return here and report to me about your mission.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_23": "The mission on which I will send you is vital to our cause. It is a sabotage mission. Nargor is guarded by several heavy catapults. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_24": "I need you to sabotage the most dangerous of those catapults which can be found right in their harbour, aiming at ships passing by the entrance. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_25": "Get a fire bug - you can buy them in Liberty Bay - and set this catapult on fire. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_26": "Make sure to use the bug on the left part of the catapult where its lever is. That is where it's most vulnerable. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_27": "If you see a short explosion, you will know that it worked. I will tell Sebastian to bring you to Nargor, but beware. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_28": "Of course, he can't drop you off directly in the pirate's base. However, we have discovered a secret way into the Howling Grotto. ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_29": "Try to make your way through the caves of Nargor to reach their harbour. This is where you will find the catapult in question.",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_30": "Indeed, I could use some help. The evil pirates of Nargor have convinced an alchemist from Edron to supply them with a substance called Fafnar's Fire ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_31": "It can burn even on water and is a threat to us all. I need you to travel to Edron and pretend to the alchemist Sandra that you are the one whom the other pirates sent to get the fire ...",
  "npc.raymond_striker.multi_32": "When she asks for a payment, tell her 'Your continued existence is payment enough'. That should enrage any member of the Edron academy enough to refuse any further deals with the pirates.",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_1": "That's wonderful! Now you will be able to repair the magical barrier. You have to strengthen the arcane sources that power this mystic shield. There are three different arcane sources: the moon sculptures, the dream bird trees and the sun mosaics. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_2": "There are five of each of them and you have to find them all to repair the barrier. Spread the gathered moon rays on the moon sculptures. Pour out the starlight over the dream bird trees and let the sunlight shine on the mosaics. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_3": "If you charge all fifteen arcane sources with the respective light, Feyrist's protection will be ensured again.",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_4": "Very good, mortal being! Now you have to catch the respective light and store it in the corresponding vessel. You can gather moon rays by night but this will only work on one special sacred glade on Feyrist. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_5": "You can find this glade in the deep forest, east of our village. The starlight must also be gathered by night. There is a rock plateau high in the mountains at the border to Roshamuul where you can catch the starlight in the vial. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_6": "You will recognise the place by the elemental energy shrine there. You have to gather the sunlight by day, of course. There is a beach in the north of Feyrist, shaped like a snake's head. There you may gather Suon's light with the sun catcher.",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_7": "You have to find three vessels that are able to hold three different types of light: starlight, sunlight and moon rays. You have already found the moon mirror but we also need the starlight vial and the sun catcher. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_8": "Ask the mermaid Aurita for the starlight vial and the faun Taegen for the sun catcher.",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_9": "Some of our siblings are tainted by the destructive energies that threaten Feyrist. They are darker now, more aggressive, twisted ... I'm sure you already met them. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_10": "They are living in tunnels and caves but at night they surface, even attacking their own siblings. They kidnapped some fairies, holding them prisoner in their mouldy dens. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_11": "And as if this wasn't enough they stole an ancient and precious artefact, the moon mirror. Please seek out the tainted fae, retrieve the artefact and free the captured fairies. ...",
  "npc.maelyrra.multi_12": "You may discover the entrance to the tainted caves somewhere in the deep forest. The tainted fae like to hide their treasures in hollow logs or trumps, so have a closer look at them.",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_1": "Fine. I guezz poizzoning zzome of hizz plantzz will be enough to lure him out of hizz conzzealment. Zzizz plant poizzon here should allow you to do zzome zzignificant damage, take it. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_2": "You can find him eazzt of zze corrupted gardenzz. Zzere uzzed to be a zzmall domizzile zzere but it hazz probably been conzzumed by zze corruption zzo beware. And now - go. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_3": "Alright. Let uzz create a crate. Hm. Let me zzee. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_4": "Good. Zzat will do. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_5": "Zze maintenanzze tunnelzz are in zze eazzt of zze plainzz, near ze coazt. Here, I will mark zzem on your map. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_6": "Uzze zze dizzguizze wizzely, try to hide in zze dark and avoid being zzeen at all cozzt. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_7": "Onzze you have reached zze norzz, you can find zze rezzizztanzze hideout at zze ozzer zzpot I marked on your map. Now hurry. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_8": "Very good, I am confident zzizz will zzuffizze. Now I can build and mark a {crate} large enough for you to fit in - while zztill being able to breazze of courzze - and I will mark it in our tongue zzo it will look lezz zzuzzpizziouzz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_9": "Wizz zzeir eyezz towardzz zze gate, your chanzzezz to zzlip zzrough have never been better. I will keep zze zzpare materialzz here wizz me, we can alwayzz build a new one if you need to. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_10": "Your determination izz highly appreciated. To zzneak pazzt zze eyezz of zze enemy, you will have to uzze a diverzzion. Zzere are zzeveral old tunnelzz beneazz zze zzoil of Zzao. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_11": "One of zzem izz uzzed azz a maintenanzze connection by enemy lizardzz. To enter it, you will have to uzze a dizzguizze. Zzomezzing like a crate perhapzz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_12": "Mh, if you can find zzome nailzz - 3 should be enough - and 1 piezze of wood, I should be able to create an appropriate cazzing. Return to me if you found zze itemzz and we will talk about zze next zztep. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_13": "You continue to imprezz, zzoftzzkin. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_14": "A contact of zze rezzizztanzze izz located furzzer in zze norzz of Zao. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_15": "Zze emperor will drag hizz forzzezz to zze great gate now to bolzzter hizz defenzze. Zzinzze we attacked zze gate directly, he will not expect uzz taking a completely different route to reach zze norzzern territoriezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_16": "I azzume you are already geared up and ready to conquer zze norzz? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_17": "You did well on your quezzt zzo far. I hope you will reach zze great gate in time. If we are lucky, it will zztill be open. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_18": "If not, it will already be overrun by enemy zzoldierzz. Direct confrontation will be inevitable in zzat cazze, palezzkin. Now clear your mind and approach zze portal.",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_19": "Zzen zzizz izz zze way which will lead you to zze great gate. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_20": "By zze way, before I forget it - zzinzze you are zzkilled in zzolving riddlezz, maybe you can make uzze of zzizz old tome I've found? It containzz ancient knowledge and truly izz a tezztament of our culture, treat it wizz care. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_21": "I may alzzo have anozzer mizzion for you if you are interezzted.",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_22": "Interezzting. It'zz a riddle, zzoftzzkin. Zzuch gamezz are very popular in our culture. I believe zze leverzz will alter zze arrangement. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_23": "Not too far from zze lever, zzere muzzt be a hint of zzome zzort. An image of how zze zzymbolzz muzzt be arranged. Zzurely zze mechanizzm will trigger a zzecret pazzage, maybe a moving wall or a portal. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_24": "Zzizz should be our pazz to zze great gate. Head to zze zztorage onzze again. Zzere should be zzome extra greazzy oil which should work wizz zzuch a large mechanizzm. Zze leverzz should zzen be movable again. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_25": "Perhapzz you can find a way to enter zze norzz of zze valley and find a pazzage to zze great gate itzzelf. Zzearch any templezz or zzettlementzz you come accrozz for hidden pazzagezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_26": "I wish for a zzafe return wizz good newzz. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_27": "Good. Zze fieldzz should be not far from Xiachai in zze eazzt. Go to zze top terrazze and mix zze poizzon wizz zze water. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_28": "{Poizzon} izz often uzzed by cowardzz, yet it grantzz great power to zze opprezzed. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_29": "Not far to zze eazzt of zze village, you'll find rizze fieldzz. Zzey uzze zzem to rezztore zzeir food suppliezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_30": "In zze zztorage accrozz zzizz room, you'll find a zzpecial poizzon which will zzignificantly weaken zzem if uzzed on zze water and zzoil zze rizze growzz in. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_31": "Are you fully prepared for zzizz?",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_32": "I'll mark zze entranzze to Chaochai on your map. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_33": "Conzzentrate on one location at a time. Zze one who chazzezz after two harezz, won't catch even one. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_34": "Aaah, zzezze look zzertainly interezzting. Zzezze manuzzcriptzz show uzz zzeveral locationzz of zze enemy troopzz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_35": "I'm imprezzed, zzoftzzkin. Maybe you can be of zzome more help. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_36": "Zzen indeed, I have a tazzk for you. Lizzten carefully and you might even learn zzomezzing. A wizze being hearzz one zzing and underzztandzz ten. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_37": "Zze mountainzz to zze norzz are overrun by corrupted lizzardzz. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_38": "Beyond zzem, you'll find a lush valley, zze Muggy Plainzz. Find out about zzeir planzz, zzeir tacticzz. Zze lizzardzz' art of war izz characterizzed by dizzguizze and zzecrezzy. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_39": "A traveller told me about a barricaded zzettlement zzey ezztablished. It'zz a weak and in all zzeir arroganzze, poorly guarded outpozzt beyond zze mountainzz. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_40": "If you can find any documentzz about zzeir zztrategiezz, zze rezzizztanzze will be very grateful. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_41": "Are you interezzted, palezzkin?",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_42": "Mh, zze zzymbolzz of zze chamber you dezzcribe are very common in our culture, palezzkin. You should have come accrozz zzem in many a plazze already. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_43": "Zze zzymbolzz zzeem to be arranged in zzome way you zzay? Were zzere any notizzeable devizzezz? Zzwitchezz or leverzz? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_44": "Now we need to get clozzer to zze emperor himzzelf. A hive of beezz would defend zzeir queen wizz zzeir lives in cazze an enemy gained entranzze. Zzizz makezz a formidable defenzze line, nearly inviolable. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_45": "But a zztranger directly in zze midzzt of zze hive will be acczzepted - after all it izz not pozzible to overcome zzuch a formidable defenzze which izz nearly inviolable, or izz it? Ha. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_46": "Now zzat you overcame zzeir linezz of defenzze at zze great gate, you only need to find a way to enter zzeir home. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_47": "Head zztraight to zze entranzze of zze zzity. If you can convinzze zze guardzz to let you enter zze zzity, you should be able to reach our contact zzere wizz eazze. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_48": "We have alzzo forged zome paperzz for you and zzent zzem to zze zzity. Your victory in zze arena iz well known in our land. Wizz zze help of zzezze paperzz you will pretend zzat zzome of zze higher officialzz want to talk to you about your battle. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_49": "Zzizz way you will be able to enter zze zzity of zze dragon emperor and meet our contact zzere in zze imperial offizze. He will give you zze next inzztructionzz. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_50": "At zze dawn of time, zze children of zze Great Zznake were numerouzz. Zzey daringly colonizzed many partzz of zze world. But all bravery did not help againzzt zze sheer number of enemiezz zzey encountered. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_51": "And while zze entitiezz zze unbelieverzz call godzz battled for power out of vanity, zze fazze of zze world changed violently. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_52": "Many zzentrezz of our magnifizzent zzivilizzation were dezztroyed and only two realmzz zzat we know of remained intact but lozzt contact to each ozzer. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_53": "In vizzionzz, zze Great Zznake revealed to Zalamon zze exzzizztenzze of ozzer lizzard people in a vazzt jungle in a far away land. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_54": "Zzough zze lizardzz of zze land failed zze Great Zznake and lozzt itzz favour, zzey are zztill in pozzezzion of ancient reliczz of immenzze power, onzze imbued by zze Great Zznake himzzelf. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_55": "I had vizzionzz of an - item. Yezz. It may be uzzeful for uzz - I mean you, ezzpecially you. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_56": "We need a zzeptre of power zzat can be found in zze underground of an ancient temple. It hazz been overrun by zzavage apezz and you will have to fight zzem and zze ancient guardianzz of zze temple azz well. Get uzz zzat zzeptre wherever it might be. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_57": "It wazz revealed zzat it hazz been zzplit into 3 partzz for reazzonzz zzat are of no importanzze anymore. Zzizz powerful devizze could help uzz in our battle againzzt zze emperor. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_58": "A shaft, a cuzzp, and an emerald form a zzeptre of zzuch power zzat zze partzz were hidden and are now guarded by vile creaturezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_59": "Find it. Retrieve it. And bring it back to me. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_60": "You ezztablished zze connection to zze hideout, good. But zzizz izz no time to rezzt. Your new tazzk will be quite different. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_61": "Zze gardenzz are plagued by a creature. Zze former keeper of zzizz garden became an abomination of madnezz zzat needzz to be zztopped. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_62": "He hidezz deep underground and it will be dangerouzz to challenge him in hizz lair but I am willing to rizzk it. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_63": "Find him, dezztroy him, bring me hizz - I uhm, mean it izz utterly nezzezzary for you to deliver me a proof of hizz deazz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_64": "Now go - what are you waiting for, zzoftzzkin? Ready to finish what needzz to be finished? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_65": "Zze attackzz have weakened our enemy zzignificantly. Yet, your quezzt continuezz. Bezzidezz zzome tazzkzz you could take, zze zzreat of zze emperor izz zztill hanging over our headzz like a rain cloud. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_66": "Zzo, are you indeed willing to continue zze fight for our cauzze? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_67": "Too clozze, far too clozze. I felt a huge impact not long after you left. Zze war machinery of zze emperor muzzt finally have been zztarted. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_68": "I focuzzed and could only hope zzat I would reach you before everyzzing wazz too late. If I hadn't been able to tranzzport you here, our cauzze would have been lozzt. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_69": "I'm afraid we cannot continue zzizz fight here today. Zze rezzizztanzze izz zztill fragile. I'm afraid, zzere izz zztill much left to do. We'll have to prepare for war. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_70": "You've helped uzz a great deal during zzezze dark hourzz, I've got zzomezzing for you my friend. Pleazze, take zzizz zzerpent crezzt azz a zzign of my deep rezzpect. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_71": "Rezzt for now, you will need it - you have earned it.",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_72": "If I'm correct, zze portal in zze chamber beyond zze mechanizzm will lead you to zze great gate. It izz perfectly pozzible, however, zzat you will not be tranzzported directly into zze area. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_73": "You will razzer be brought to a plazze clozze by your goal. Where exzzactly, I cannot zzay. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_74": "Take all your courage and walk zze pazz zzrough zze portal. At leazzt TRY it - after all, I didn't make you my pupil for nozzing, Kohei. Are you prepared?",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_75": "You have zzolved zze riddle? Imprezzive, palezzkin. Zze humming you hear in zze chamber mozzt zzertainly comezz from a magic portal zzomewhere in zze temple. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_76": "Have you zzearched zze ozzer chamberzz for any magical devizzezz or portalzz?",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_77": "Wizz zze enemy'zz forzzezz weakened like zzizz, we will be able to zzneak pazzt zze defenzze and furzzer inzzpect zze norzz. You should travel to zze mountain range furzzer eazzt of zze village. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_78": "Zze old route to zze gate hazz been taken by darknezz. You'll have to find ozzer wayzz. Are you up to zzizz, palezzkin? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_79": "You accomplished an important tazzk in breaking zze defenzze of zze emperor. Not everyzzing might be lozzt yet. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_80": "I've got anozzer mizzion for you which will be even more dangerouzz zzan zze lazzt one. Return to me when you're ready. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_81": "Your lazzt excurzzion revealed a terrifying truzz. Zze enemy'zz forzzezz are overwhelming, zzeir zztrengzz probably unrivaled. We cannot attack an army of zzizz zzize unlezz - unlezz we zzin out zzeir rankzz a little. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_82": "A zzingle individual can be azz zztrong azz an army if he zztrikezz zze army azz a whole. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_83": "Are you ready for your nexzzt tazzk? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_84": "Zzizz izz mozzt unfortunate. Zzo many warriorzz? Large amountzz of food? And how many weaponzz did you zzay? I zzee, hmm. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_85": "Direct confrontation izz futile. We'll have to find ozzer wayzz to approach zze emperor and hizz army. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_86": "Large partzz of zze empire are tainted. I zzee now zzat zzere izz almozzt nozzing left of our onzze zzo zztrong zzivilizzation. But I zztill don't know which danger our enemy really pozzezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_87": "Zzere uzzed to be a remote and quiet zzettlement in zze middle of zze valley. If it hazz not been dezztroyed by zze corruption, I'm zzure zze army of zze emperor will have confizzcated it to gazzer rezzourzzezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_88": "If you can get inzzide zze village, find out anyzzing you can about zzeir zzituation. Zze clever hawk hidezz itzz clawzz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_89": "I'm mozzt interezzted in zzeir weaponzz, food and zze zztrengzz of zzeir forzzezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_90": "Are you prepared for zzizz mizzion? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_91": "Zzo you found zze temple... lozzt you zzay. It wazz our lazzt remaining bazztion of hope for help from wizzin zze plainzz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_92": "Zzat meanzz zze plainzz are now in zze handzz of zze emperor and hizz army. I'm afraid zzat even zze great gate izz zzealed and zze landzz beyond it tainted azz well. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_93": "Dark timezz, and I fear we know nozzing about our enemy yet. ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_94": "Zzurely you have zzeen zze black pondzz and puddlezz all over zze mountain pazz, palezzkin. It izz zze corruption zzat pervadezz zze landzz. It would be wizze not to drink or tazzte from zzem. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_95": "It zzoakzz zze land, itzz people and even zze air itzzelf. But zzere are zztill zzpotzz not tainted by zze darknezz. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_96": "A temple, norzzwezzt of zze barricaded outpozzt wizztood zze evil influenzze. However, I lozzt contact to itzz inhabitantzz when zze lizzardzz tightened zzeir grip. ... ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_97": "No one made it zzrough zze mountainzz for quite zzome time now - exzzept you. Maybe you can find out what happened zzere? ",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_98": "Zzo you are offering your help to a lizzard? Hmm, unuzzual. I don't know if I can fully truzzt you yet. ...",
  "npc.zalamon.multi_99": "You'll have to work to earn my truzzt. Are you zzure you want to offer me your help?",
  "npc.gnomad.multi_1": "You will encounter quite a lot of beasties in the area ahead of us. The end of the cave-system is where the trouble begins though. The monsters here all serve some massive creature only known as Deathstrike. ...",
  "npc.gnomad.multi_2": "The creature is hidden in a well protected chamber. The good news is, we've managed to erect a crystal structure close to the cave that is able to breach its defence and teleport someone into the chamber. ...",
  "npc.gnomad.multi_3": "The bad new is that the crystals need a specific charge before they can work. As soon as the crystals begin to charge up, Deathstrikes' minions will frenzy and spawn in waves to crush all opposition. ...",
  "npc.gnomad.multi_4": "You will have to kill them quite fast, to not be overwhelmed by their numbers! Our own tries to breach the defence has proven that you'll have to endure six waves until the teleporter to Deathtstrikes' cave opens for a short 30 seconds. ...",
  "npc.gnomad.multi_5": "Use the GREEN command crystal in the cave to begin the charging of the teleport! Good luck.",
  "npc.zlak.multi_1": "Your eagernezz for killing and bloodshed iz frightening, but your next mizzion will zuit your tazte. Wiz ze zity in chaoz and defenzez diverted, ze ztage iz zet for our final ztrike. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_2": "A large number of rebelz have arrived undercover in ze zity. Zey will attack ze palaze and zome loyal palaze guardz will let zem in. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_3": "Meanwhile, you will take ze old ezcape tunnel zat leadz from ze abandoned bazement in ze norz of ze miniztry to a lift zat endz zomewhere in ze palaze. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_4": "When everyzing workz according to ze plan, you will meet Zalamon zomewhere in the underground part of ze palaze.",
  "npc.zlak.multi_5": "Word of your deedz iz already zpreading like a wildfire. Zalamon'z plan to unleash zome murderouz beaztz in ze zity workz almozt too well. You are already becoming zome kind of legend with which motherz frighten zeir unruly hatchlingz. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_6": "Your next {mizzion} will be a ztrike into ze heart of ze empire.",
  "npc.zlak.multi_7": "Chaoz and panic are already zpreading. Your barbaric brutality iz frightening effectively. I could acquire a key zat we need to get you into ze palaze itzelf. But zere are ztill too many guardz and elite zquadz even for you to fight. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_8": "I need you to enter ze zity and zlay at leazt zix noblez. Ze otherz will feel zreatened and call guardz to zemzelvez, and ze dragon kingz will accuze each ozer to be rezponzible for zlaying zeir pet noblez. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_9": "Zat should enable uz to give you at leazt a chanze to attack ze palaze.",
  "npc.zlak.multi_10": "Ze rumour mill iz quite fazt. Ezpecially when zomeone unuzual az you enterz ze zity. Zoon zey will learn zat you have no reazon to be here and our raze will be buzted. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_11": "Zo we have to ztrike fazt and quickly. You will have to eliminate zome high ranking key officialz. I zink killing four of zem should be enough. ...",
  "npc.zlak.multi_12": "Ziz will dizrupt ze order in ze zity zignificantly zinze zo much dependz on bureaucracy and ze chain of command. Only chaoz and dizorganization will enable me to help you with ze next ztep in ze plan.",
  "npc.ezebeth.multi_1": "We provide addons to people dedicated to our city. So the first addon is granted to someone who has voted for each of the available shortcuts and each dungeon at least once. ...",
  "npc.ezebeth.multi_2": "The second addon is granted to someone who has voted for each bossfight at least once.",
  "npc.karith.multi_1": "The evergreen flower pots are an amusing item that might find some customers here. Do you want a passage to Carlin for 185 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_2": "An unremarkable town compared to the wonders of Yalahar. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_3": "Do you want a passage to Liberty Bay for 275 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_4": "Which sane captain would sail his ship to a pirate town? Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_5": "Astonishing enough the royal satin seems to suit the exquisite taste of the Yalahari. Do you want a passage to Thais for 200 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_6": "Thais must be a hell hole if only half of the stories we hear about it are true. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_7": "Ivory is highly prized by the artisans of the Yalahari. Do you want a passage to Port Hope for 260 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_8": "Another pointless human settlement. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_9": "The Yalahari seem to be obsessed with conserving their dead, so I guess the embalming fluid will be a great success in Yalahar. Do you want a passage to Ankrahmun for 230 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_10": "A city full of mad death worshippers, no thanks. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_11": "Another port full of smelly humans, fittingly located in a swamp. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_12": "Of course it is merely superstition that the darashian sand wasp honey brings back youth and vitality, but as long people pay a decent price, I couldn't care less. Do you want a passage to Darashia for 210 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_13": "From all what I have heard, it is an unremarkable pile of huts in the desert. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_14": "Do you want a passage to Ab'Dendriel for 160 gold?",
  "npc.karith.multi_15": "I've never been there. I doubt the elves there came up with something noteworthy. Or did you find something interesting there?",
  "npc.karith.multi_16": "For the sake of profit, we established ship routes to {Ab'Dendriel}, {Darashia}, {Venore}, {Ankrahmun}, {Port Hope}, {Thais}, {Liberty Bay} and {Carlin}.",
  "npc.karith.multi_17": "I see no reason to establish ship routes to other cities. There is nothing that would be worth the effort. ...",
  "npc.karith.multi_18": "But since you won't stop bugging me, let's make a deal: If you can prove that at least five of your so-called 'cities' are not worthless, I might reconsider my position. ...",
  "npc.karith.multi_19": "Bring me something SPECIAL! The local bar tenders usually know what's interesting about their city.",
  "npc.sholley.multi_1": "A transporter dead? This is more then alarming. It seems Harsin is up to something and whatever it is, it's nothing good at all. But not all is lost. A local medium, Barnabas, has truly the gift to speak to the dead. ...",
  "npc.sholley.multi_2": "I'll mark his home on your map. He should be able to get the information you need to locate Harsin.",
  "npc.sholley.multi_3": "So you have proven yourself a true friend of our city. It's hard to believe but I think your words only give substance to suspicions my heart had harboured since quite a while. ...",
  "npc.sholley.multi_4": "So Harsin is probably not the person he appeared to be. Actually I haven't heard from him for quite a while. He was resident in the local bed and breakfast hotel. You should be able to find him there or at least to learn about his whereabouts.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_1": "Great, you are here. We need your service in a mission of utmost urgency ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_2": "A mad dwarven technomancer that listens to the name of Blowbeard sent us a blackmailing letter. He demands to deliver all of Thais's gold to him. Else he will destroy the city with an artificial earthquake caused by one of his machines! ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_3": "We need you to find his base in Kazordoon and to kill him before he can use his infernal machine. Bring us his beard as proof of your success.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_4": "The women of Carlin have the northern city Svargrond in the firm grip of her manicured hands. At the moment, there is little we can do about it but there is one thing that plays into our hands ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_5": "The barbarians have surely at least heard about the fact that alcohol is outlawed in Carlin ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_6": "If some amazonian warrior would smash a beer or ale cask in front of some witnesses, the relationship would surely suffer a bit. So go and disguise yourself as an amazon. Then use a crowbar to destroy a cask.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_7": "It's bad enough that Carlin got a solid foothold in the far North but now the Venoreans also try to move in. They try to gain influence on the barbarian raiders by bribing their leaders or making them great promises ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_8": "We want you to cause some bad blood in this relationship. Travel to their most southern camp, enter the ice tower of their leaders and kill some of them ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_9": "Here is a signet ring that the Venorean emissaries use to wear. 'Lose' the ring in the north-western corner of the highest level of the tower. They will surely find it there.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_10": "Just recently we were able to secretly help our elven friends to exposure an agitator sent by Carlin to poison our connections with them. The elves' reaction wasswift and without compromise ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_11": "They banished the delinquent in a place they call 'Hellgate'. Unfortunately, we learnt later that the convict was sent there with several of his belongings and it is very likely that he took vital papers with him ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_12": "These papers can tell us much about Carlin's plans in the North. We need you to enter 'Hellgate' and to retrieve the papers for us ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_13": "We don't care how you get them. Do whatever you think is necessary.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_14": "One of our agents is missing. He was investigating the cause for the slow growth of our colony Port Hope ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_15": "You will continue these investigations at the point where the information that the lost agent has sent us ends. Some of the traders in Port Hope must have connections to persons who are interested in sabotaging our efforts in Tiquanda ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_16": "Search their personal belongings to find some sort of evidence that we could need!",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_17": "Your next mission concerns an internal matter for our agency. Some decades ago, one of our most talented field agents vanished in the Green Claw Swamp ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_18": "Nowadays, that more and more adventurers are swarming this area, there is an increasing number of reports on some sinister goings-on and mysterious ruins in the middle of the swamp ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_19": "We got some credible clues that there might be a connection between the ruins and the disappearance of our agent ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_20": "As he is already missing since decades it is unlikely that he is still alive. Nevertheless, we want you to find out something about the whereabouts of our agent in the ruins in the Green Claw Swamp, north west of Venore ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_21": "He used to write diaries, maybe you can find one of those, or some other hints, or even his remains. You have to understand that he was a member of a prestigious Thaian family. Very influential people are interested in his whereabouts ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_22": "The Green Claw Swamp is treacherous and dangerous. You will have a hard time to find any clues ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_23": "As a small incentive I think its worthy to mention that he was wearing a quite impressive armor. You may keep it for yourself if you stumble across it.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_24": "Your first task is to deliver a warning. Illegally, the Venoreans are crafting more ships than the Thaian authorities have allowed them ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_25": "Our sources have told us that those ships often end up in the hands of pirates or smugglers ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_26": "An official note would strain the relationship between Thais and Venore too much as this would mean that we had to admit officially that we know about those activities ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_27": "Still, we can't allow them to continue like this. It will be your task to let them know that we do not tolerate such behaviour. Get a fire bug from Liberty Bay and set their shipyard on fire ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_28": "Use the fire bug on some flammable material there to start the fire. It might take a while to find some wood that's dry enough for the fire to spread. Just keep trying ... ",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_29": "If you get captured or killed during your mission, we will deny any contact with you.",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_30": "Our bureau is an old and traditional branch of the Thaian government. It takes more than lip service to join our ranks ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_31": "Absolute loyalty to the crown and the Thaian cause as well as courage face-to-face with the enemy is the least we expect from our members ...",
  "npc.chester_kahs.multi_32": "You will swear allegiance to Thais alone and abandon the service of any other city. So is it really your wish to become one of our field agents?",
  "npc.corym_butler.multi_1": "We have to dig up valuable resources, but don't get enough to eat. The situation is terrible.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_1": "Our members travel to far away places and cross dangerous areas, many fall prey to enemies or the land ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_2": "Sometimes the personal explorer brooches can be recovered. That way we learn about the fate of our members ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_3": "We offer a reward for each brooch returned to us. Have you found an explorer brooch?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_4": "Ratha was a great explorer and even greater ladies' man. Sadly he never returned from a visit to the amazons. Probably he is dead ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_5": "The society offers a substantial reward for the retrieval of Ratha or his remains. Do you have any news about Ratha?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_6": "Good, just take this spectral essence and use it on the strange carving in this building as well as on the corresponding tile in our base at Northport ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_7": "As soon as you have charged the portal tiles that way, report about the spectral portals.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_8": "That is quite courageous. We know, it's much we are asking for. The queen of the banshees lives in the so called Ghostlands, south west of Carlin. It is rumoured that her lair is located in the deepest dungeons beneath that cursed place ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_9": "Any violence will probably be futile, you will have to negotiate with her. Try to get a spectral dress from her. Good luck.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_10": "Fine. The society is looking for new means to travel. Some of our most brilliant minds have some theories about astral travel that they want to research further ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_11": "Therefore we need you to collect some ectoplasm from the corpse of a ghost. We will supply you with a collector that you can use on the body of a slain ghost ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_12": "Do you think you are ready for that mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_13": "You are a brave soul. As far as we can tell, the orcs maintain some sort of training facility in some hill in the north-east of their city ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_14": "There you should find lots of their war wolves and hopefully also some of the orcish powder. Good luck!",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_15": "Excellent! So travel to the city of Darashia and then head north-east for the pyramid ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_16": "If any documents are left, you probably find them in the catacombs beneath. Good luck!",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_17": "You have indeed the spirit of an adventurer! In the south-east of Tiquanda is a small settlement of the lizard people ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_18": "Beneath the newly constructed temple there, the lizards hide the said urn. Our attempts to acquire this item were without success ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_19": "Perhaps you are more successful.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_20": "This preparation kit will allow you to collect a purple butterfly you have killed ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_21": "Just use it on the fresh corpse of a purple butterfly, return the prepared butterfly to me and give me a report of your butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_22": "So listen please: Take this ice pick and use it on a block of ice in the caves beneath Folda. Get some ice and bring it here as fast as you can ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_23": "Should the ice melt away, report on your ice delivery mission anyway. I will then tell you if the time is right to start another mission.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_24": "Excellent, you brought just the tool we need! Of course it was only a simple task. However ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_25": "I officially welcome you to the explorer society. From now on you can ask for missions to improve your rank.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_26": "Fine, though it takes more then a mere lip service to join our ranks. To prove your dedication to the cause you will have to acquire an item for us ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_27": "The mission should be simple to fulfil. For our excavations we have ordered a sturdy pickaxe in Kazordoon. You would have to seek out this trader Uzgod and get the pickaxe for us ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_28": "Simple enough? Are you interested in this task?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_29": "We would like to study some ancient runes that were used by the lizard race. We suspect some relation of the lizards to the founders of Ankrahmun ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_30": "Somewhere under the ape infested city of Banuta, one can find dungeons that were once inhabited by lizards...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_31": "Look there for an atypical structure that would rather fit to Ankrahmun and its Ankrahmun Tombs. Copy the runes you will find on this structure...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_32": "Are you up to that challenge?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_33": "We acquired some knowledge about special magic stones. Some lost civilisations used it to store knowledge and lore, just like we use books ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_34": "The wisdom in such stones must be immense, but so are the dangers faced by every person who tries to obtain one...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_35": "As far as we know the ruins found in the north-west of Edron were once inhabited by beings who used such stones. Do you have the heart to go there and to get us such a stone?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_36": "Some high ranking members would like to study elven poetry. They want the rare book 'Songs of the Forest' ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_37": "For sure someone in Ab'Dendriel will own a copy. So you would just have to ask around there. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_38": "It is commonly known that orcs of Uldereks Rock use some sort of powder to increase the fierceness of their war wolves and berserkers ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_39": "What we do not know are the ingredients of this powder and its effect on humans ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_40": "So we would like you to get a sample of the aforesaid powder. Do you want to accept this mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_41": "We want to learn more about the ancient race of bonelords. We believe the black pyramid north east of Darashia was originally built by them ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_42": "We ask you to explore the ruins of the black pyramid and look for any signs that prove our theory. You might probably find some document with the numeric bonelord language ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_43": "That would be sufficient proof. Would you like to accept this mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_44": "This preparation kit will allow you to collect a red butterfly you have killed ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_45": "Just use it on the fresh corpse of a red butterfly, return the prepared butterfly to me and give me a report of your butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_46": "This preparation kit will allow you to collect a blue butterfly you have killed ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_47": "Just use it on the fresh corpse of a blue butterfly, return the prepared butterfly to me and give me a report of your butterfly hunt.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_48": "Our finest minds came up with the theory that deep beneath the ice island of Folda ice can be found that is ancient. To prove this theory we would need a sample of the aforesaid ice ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_49": "Of course the ice melts away quickly so you would need to hurry to bring it here ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_50": "Would you like to accept this mission?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_51": "Both carvings are now charged and harmonised. In theory you should be able to travel in zero time from one base to the other ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_52": "However, you will need to have an orichalcum pearl in your possession to use it as power source. It will be destroyed during the process. I will give you 6 of such pearls and you can buy new ones in our bases ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_53": "In addition, you need to be a premium explorer to use the astral travel. ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_54": "And remember: it's a small teleport for you, but a big teleport for all Tibians! Here is a small present for your efforts!",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_55": "With the objects you've provided our researchers will make steady progress. Still we are missing some test results from fellow explorers ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_56": "Please travel to our base in Port Hope and ask them to mail us their latest research reports. Then return here and ask about new missions.",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_57": "The research on ectoplasm makes good progress. Now we need some spectral article. Our scientists think a spectral dress would be a perfect object for their studies ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_58": "The bad news is that the only source to got such a dress is the queen of the banshees. Do you dare to seek her out?",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_59": "Those stories are just amazing! Men with faces on their stomach instead of heads you say? And hens that lay golden eggs? Whereas, most amazing is this fountain of youth you've mentioned! ...",
  "npc.mortimer.multi_60": "I'll immediately send some of our most dedicated explorers to check those things out!",
  "npc.marlene.multi_1": "Well, I heard about evil beings living in a dungeon below us. So once I tried to find them and went down the hole far to the southwest. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_2": "I'm pretty curious, you know. *smiles* So I took the coat of invisibility from my husband and went down there. At first I only found some spiders, snakes, and wolves. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_3": "But after some time I found a ladder to a deeper level of the dungeon but I didn't dare to go down there because I heard many voices. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_4": "The voices were very strange and I ran back to my house because they were very loud and very angry. I hope they will never get the idea to attack the surface beings. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_5": "I heard they are almighty and have incredible powers! I already packed our stuff for an emergency escape. You never know. Maybe they plan to conquer the whole world. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_6": "I bet that they look very ugly. Most mighty monsters look very ugly. Hmm, you seem to be very strong. Maybe you can go deeper and explore the area. But be careful, please. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_7": "I heard that they can kill humans with only one hit! And that they have magic abilities twenty times stronger than the mightiest sorcerer in our world.",
  "npc.marlene.multi_8": "A very nice person. He has a great story to tell with big fights and much magic. Just ask him for his story. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_9": "I heard that he came from far, far away. He must have seen soooo many countries, cities, different races. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_10": "He must have collected so much wisdom. *sigh* I wish I could also travel around the world. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_11": "I would try to visit as many cities and meet as many beings as possible. Who knows what strange races I will meet? ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_12": "Maybe I can also find a lovely new dress for me. I have been looking for one for months now but never found a good one. Maybe... *keeps on babbling*",
  "npc.marlene.multi_13": "Only some days ago I was at the docks late in the night and was looking for my husband's ship when suddenly a known noise appeared near the docks. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_14": "I know this noise very well because it is the noise of a ship sailing very fast. I searched the horizon in hope to see my husbands ship. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_15": "But instead of a ship I saw a huge shape far away. It was like a big snake swimming in the sea. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_16": "I couldn't see it clearly because of the fog but I think I saw two lava-red eyes glowing in the nightly fog. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_17": "I ran into the house and hoped that my husband would arrive safely from fishing. And after one hour he finally arrived. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_18": "I told him about what I saw but he didn't believe me because he never saw anything like that in all the years before. But you believe me right? Go and convince yourself. ...",
  "npc.marlene.multi_19": "Just go to the docks at exactly midnight and be very quiet. Look at the horizon and maybe you will hear and see it, too!",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_1": "We need to find a way to drive off the exiles from these caves. Countless makeshift homes are popping up at every corner. Destroy them and get the Lost out of hiding to eliminate them. ... ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_2": "If you can capture a few of them, you'll receive a bonus. Just bring 'em to the border of our outpost and we will take care of the rest. ... ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_3": "Are you ready for that? ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_4": "We need to find a way to drive off the exiles from these caves. Countless makeshift homes are popping up at every corner. Destroy them and get the Lost out of hiding to eliminate them. ... ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_5": "If you can capture a few of them, you'll receive a bonus. Just bring 'em to the border of our outpost and we will take care of the rest. ... ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_6": "Are you ready for that? ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_7": "Vermin. Everywhere. We get a lot of strange four-legged crawlers and worms down here lately. It's getting out of hand and... well, I need a real killer for this. ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_8": "Prepared to get rid of some seriously foul creepers for us?",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_9": "Vermin. Everywhere. We get a lot of strange four-legged crawlers and worms down here lately. It's getting out of hand and... well, I need a real killer for this. ",
  "npc.klom_stonecutter.multi_10": "Prepared to get rid of some seriously foul creepers for us?",
  "npc.tigo.multi_1": "The trial consists of three steps. The trial of tar, where you will suffer unbearable heat and embrace the stigma of misfortune. ...",
  "npc.tigo.multi_2": "The trial of sulphur, where you will bathe in burning sulphur and embrace the stigma of vanity. Then, there is the trial of purification. The truest of us will be purified to face judgement from the {Penitent}.",
  "npc.tigo.multi_3": "To purge your soul, your body will have to be near absolute zero, the point where life becomes impossible. ...",
  "npc.tigo.multi_4": "Something about you is different.  I know that you will find a way to return even if you should die during the purification. And if you do... Leiden will become aware of you and retreat. ...",
  "npc.tigo.multi_5": "If he does, follow him into his own chambers. Barkless are neither allowed to go near the throne room, aside from being judged, nor can we actually enter it.",
  "npc.tigo.multi_6": "He should be easy to defeat with his back to the wall, find him - and delvier us from whatever became of the Penitent.",
  "npc.miraia.multi_1": "Alright, then listen to the following requirements. We are currently in dire need of ape fur since the Caliph has requested a new bathroom carpet. ...",
  "npc.miraia.multi_2": "Thus, please bring me 100 pieces of ape fur. Secondly, it came to our ears that the explorer society has discovered a new undersea race of fishmen. ...",
  "npc.miraia.multi_3": "Their fins are said to allow humans to walk on water! Please bring us 100 of these fish fin. ...",
  "npc.miraia.multi_4": "Third, if the plan of walking on water should fail, we need enchanted chicken wings to prevent the testers from drowning. Please bring me two. ...",
  "npc.miraia.multi_5": "Last but not least, just drop by with 100 pieces of blue cloth and I will happily show you how to make a turban. ...",
  "npc.miraia.multi_6": "Did you understand everything I told you and are willing to handle this task?",
  "npc.maritima.multi_1": "The quara in this area are a strange race that seeks for inner perfection rather than physical one. ...",
  "npc.maritima.multi_2": "Considering that they are quara, they are rather peaceful as long no one enters their territory. ...",
  "npc.maritima.multi_3": "However, recently the quara got mad because their area is flooded with toxic sewage from the city. If you could inform someone about it, they might stop the sewage and the quara could return to their own business.",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.multi_1": "That's very kind of you, my friend! Listen: I know there is a spell to transform my fishtail into legs. It is a temporary effect, so I could return to the ocean as soon as the spell ends. Unfortunately I don't know how to cast this spell. ...",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.multi_2": "But there is a fairy who once told me about it. Perhaps she will share her knowledge. You can find her in a small fairy village in the southwest of Feyrist.",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.multi_3": "Each of those notes will grant her a walk on the beach with Taegen.",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.multi_4": "So, you are searching for a way to transform Aurita's fishtail into legs temporarily. As you might already have figured out you need some magic for this purpose. There is a place on Feyrist where you can find the arcane energies you need. ...",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.multi_5": "Northeast from here you'll discover a big lake with a small island. Take a swim there and you will find a magical fountain. If you play the panpipes while standing near this fountain, you will create some magical music notes. ...",
  "npc.dancing_fairy.multi_6": "Collect them and give them to Aurita. Each of those notes will grant her a walk on the beach with Taegen.",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_1": "Yes, well for instance I tried for some time to figure out how to enter the fiery portal in this complex. Most of the draken never come up here. They rather hide somewhere down there, planning and plotting. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_2": " I already know how to enter it, you need to step in and yell 'zzubaran'. Unfortunately they never took me with them. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_3": " I heard them say it once, when a seemingly drunk guard yelled it in front of a wall mounted torch, hitting his head against it afterwards. He spilt all my contents on the floor, hmpf.",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_4": "Ah did I say that? Nevermind, I'm not really thirsty. It's part of this illusion. Somehow, I've been in hiding for so long, I started to... become... a vessel. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_5": "I don't know, I have that constant urge to drink but in this form I would not need to, there is no mouth, no stomach, no flesh and no actual need to eat, drink or sleep. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_6": "I basically communicate by making the metal of this goblet vibrate and using its form as a body of sound. Like a real voice, don't you think?? Yes, alright I know it's creepy. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_7": "I am still in the middle of my research and do not want to go home, so please tell my daughter to not worry about my - this will be a breakthrough! I already {learned} a lot!",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_8": "Oh yes, so since I wanted to study the Draken up close, I came up with an idea. Based on my research, and some slight bruises and a scar, the perfect hiding place is often right in the middle of subjects. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_9": "If I could enter their lair unseen and establish a forward camp, I would be able to study the draken in peace - or so I thought. Turns out the whole place was empty. I set up my camp and waited. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_10": "Then something happened, lizardfolk started to appear, searching the place. I had to retreat from my hiding place and advance through a safer position. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_11": "I needed to get close and blend in. So I came up with the ultimate disguise: a chalice. I could establish foothold right in their midst, would never be identified as an intruder and could even analyse their drinks! ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_12": "I quickly dug a tunnel to get into what I assume is a throne room and waited for them to pick me up an carry me around! ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_13": "They also 'used' me a bit, you don't want to go into any details here. I am really {thirsty}.",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_14": "No water then? Ah drat - er, don't worry, no problem. So, from the day I received news of the discovery of Zao, I wanted to study its inhabitants, wildlife, plants and geography. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_15": "The academy instated the 'Edron-Zaoan Exploration Division' shortly after. I was a founding member and head of the 'Draken' research branch. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_16": "Since my valued and practical oriented colleague and mentor Spectulus did not join us, there is only one member of the academy exploration division to actually venture out to see the place - me. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_17": "You must know, most things in the academy happen 'inside', behind closed doors. But some of us simply refuse to let theory reign over practical experience in science. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_18": "Well, basically Spectulus is the only one likeminded so far. In fact, he incited me to work in the field in first place. So here I am! {Disguised} as a chalice.",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_19": "Well, besides being a renowned sorcerer and scholar at the magic academy in Edron, I am also the proud father of a beautiful daughter, Ivalisse. My little endeavour here must have troubled the poor thing all the time since I left. ...",
  "npc.a_strange_chalice.multi_20": "Tell her I love her and that I will take care. I have to press on! My research is most valuable to the 'Edron-Zaoan Exploration Division'. You don't happen to have some water, do you? Ah nevermind. It's a long {story}.",
  "npc.jerom.multi_1": "I'm not sure but I suppose that an evil troll lives in the mountains here! I saw him rummaging in the ruins of my house. ...",
  "npc.jerom.multi_2": "I took a closer look and found my family casket ripped open. It contained a precious necklace. If I had it back, I could sell it and start over! ...",
  "npc.jerom.multi_3": "Could you look for this mean beast, find out why he did and either get me some money ormy necklace to rebuild my business?",
  "npc.melfar.multi_1": "So take this beaver bait. It will work best on dwarf trees. I'll mark the three trees on your map. Here .. here .. and here! So now mark those trees with the beaver bait. ...",
  "npc.melfar.multi_2": "If you're unlucky enough to meet one of the giant beavers, try to stay calm. Don't do any hectic moves, don't yell, don't draw any weapon, and if you should carry anything wooden on you, throw it away as far as you can.",
  "npc.melfar.multi_3": "Just great, another disturbance. Just what I need.",
  "npc.melfar.multi_4": "Ha! Men and wood you say? Well, I might be able to relocate some of our miners to the base. Acquiring wood is an entirely different matter though. ... ",
  "npc.melfar.multi_5": "I can't spare any men for woodcutting right now but I have an unusual idea that might help. ... ",
  "npc.melfar.multi_6": "As you might know, this area is troubled by giant beavers. Once a year, the miners decide to have some fun, so they lure the beavers and jump on them to have some sort of rodeo. ... ",
  "npc.melfar.multi_7": "However, I happen to have some beaver bait left from the last year's competition. ... ",
  "npc.melfar.multi_8": "If you place it on trees on some strategic locations, we could let the beavers do the work and later on, I'll send men to get the fallen trees. ... ",
  "npc.melfar.multi_9": "Does this sound like something you can handle? ",
  "npc.mother_of_jack.multi_1": "Oh my... he did what? Why was he there? Edron Academy? ...",
  "npc.mother_of_jack.multi_2": "I see... this cannot be. Spectrofuss? Who? Jack! When? How? But why did he do that? Jack!! JACK!! When I find him he owes me an EXPLANATION. Thanks for telling me what he is actually doing in his FREE TIME. ...",
  "npc.mother_of_jack.multi_3": "JAAAAACK!",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_1": "So listen, please. Plague was not ordinary plague. That's why Hairycles could not heal at first. It is new curse of evil lizard people ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_2": "I think curse on little one was only a try. We have to be prepared for big strike ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_3": "Me need papers of lizard magician! For sure you find it in his hut in their dwelling. It's south east of jungle. Go look there please! Are you willing to go?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_4": "So listen, little ape was struck by plague. Hairycles not does know what plague it is. That is strange. Hairycles should know. But Hairycles learnt lots and lots ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_5": "Me sure to make cure so strong to drive away all plague. But to create great cure me need powerful components ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_6": "Me need whisper moss. Whisper moss growing south of human settlement is. Problem is, evil little dworcs harvest all whisper moss immediately ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_7": "Me know they hoard some in their underground lair. My people raided dworcs often before humans came. So we know the moss is hidden in east of upper level of dworc lair ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_8": "You go there and take good moss from evil dworcs. Talk with me about mission when having moss.",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_9": "So listen, little ape was struck by plague. Hairycles not does know what plague it is. That is strange. Hairycles should know. But Hairycles learnt lots and lots ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_10": "Me sure to make cure so strong to drive away all plague. But to create great cure me need powerful components ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_11": "Me need whisper moss. Whisper moss growing south of human settlement is. Problem is, evil little dworcs harvest all whisper moss immediately ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_12": "Me know they hoard some in their underground lair. My people raided dworcs often before humans came. So we know the moss is hidden in east of upper level of dworc lair ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_13": "You go there and take good moss from evil dworcs. Talk with me about mission when having moss.",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_14": "Finally my people are safe! You have done incredible good for ape people and one day even me brethren will recognise that. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_15": "I wish I could speak for all when me call you true friend but my people need time to get accustomed to change. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_16": "Let us hope one day whole Banuta will greet you as a friend. Perhaps you want to check me offers for special friends... or shamanic powers.",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_17": "You have proven yourself a friend, me will grant you permission to enter the deepest catacombs under Banuta which we have sealed in the past. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_18": "Me still can sense the evil presence there. We did not dare to go deeper and fight creatures of evil there. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_19": "You may go there, fight the evil and find the monument of the serpent god and destroy it with hammer me give to you. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_20": "Only then my people will be safe. Please tell Hairycles, will you go there?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_21": "Now that the false cult was stopped, we need to strengthen the spirit of my people. We need a symbol of our faith that ape people can see and touch. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_22": "Since you have proven a friend of the ape people I will grant you permission to enter the forbidden land. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_23": "To enter the forbidden land in the north-east of the jungle, look for a cave in the mountains east of it. There you will find the blind prophet. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_24": "Tell him Hairycles you sent and he will grant you entrance. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_25": "Forbidden land is home of Bong. Holy giant ape big as mountain. Don't annoy him in any way but look for a hair of holy ape. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_26": "You might find at places he has been, should be easy to see them since Bong is big. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_27": "Return a hair of the holy ape to me. Will you do this for Hairycles?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_28": "Mighty life charm is protecting us now! But my people are still in danger. Danger from within. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_29": "Some of my people try to mimic lizards to become strong. Like lizards did before, this cult drinks strange fluid that lizards left when fled. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_30": "Under the city still the underground temple of lizards is. There you find casks with red fluid. Take crowbar and destroy three of them to stop this madness. Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_31": "Last ingredient for charm of life is thing to lure magic. Only thing me know like that is mushroom called witches' cap. Me was told it be found in isle called Fibula, where humans live. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_32": "Hidden under Fibula is a secret dungeon. There you will find witches' cap. Are you willing to go there for good ape people?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_33": "So much there is to do for Hairycles to prepare charm that will protect all ape people. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_34": "You can help more. To create charm of life me need mighty token of life! Best is egg of a regenerating beast as a hydra is. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_35": "Bring me egg of hydra please. You may find it in lair of Hydra at little lake south east of our lovely city Banuta! You think you can do?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_36": "Ah yes that scroll. Sadly me not could read it yet. But the holy banana me insight gave! In dreams Hairycles saw where to find solution. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_37": "Me saw a stone with lizard signs and other signs at once. If you read signs and tell Hairycles, me will know how to read signs. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_38": "You go east to big desert. In desert there city. East of city under sand hidden tomb is. You will have to dig until you find it, so take shovel. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_39": "Go down in tomb until come to big level and then go down another. There you find a stone with signs between two huge red stones. ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_40": "Read it and return to me. Are you up to that challenge?",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_41": "Whisper moss strong is, but me need liquid that humans have to make it work ...",
  "npc.hairycles.multi_42": "Our raiders brought it from human settlement, it's called cough syrup. Go ask healer there for it.",
  "npc.muhad.multi_1": "I appreciate your will to help the sons of the desert. Recently a bunch of thieves have stolen something very valuable from us. It is a secret the true sons kept for aeons and I am not allowed to tell you about it. ...",
  "npc.muhad.multi_2": "All we know about the thieves is that they have their hideout somewhere in {Ankrahmun}. We managed to catch one of them and he told us that there is a pillar in {Ankrahmun} with a hidden mechanism. ...",
  "npc.muhad.multi_3": "If you press the eye of the hawk symbol a secret passage will appear that leads to their hideout. Once inside you have to look for a small casket. ...",
  "npc.muhad.multi_4": "Try to sneak in undetectedly and bring back our treasure as soon as you obtain it. May Daraman hold his protective hand over you on your mission. I wish you good luck. ...",
  "npc.muhad.multi_5": "One last thing before you leave. Take the path behind me and you will get out of our hideout unharmed.",
  "npc.muhad.multi_6": "Ahh, I know that some of my people fear that Arito tells the old secrets of our race and want to see him dead but I don't bear him a grudge. I will have to have a serious word with my people. ...",
  "npc.muhad.multi_7": "Tell him that he can consider himself as acquitted. He is not the reason for our attacks towards {Ankrahmun}.",
  "npc.muhad.multi_8": "I don't know how something like this ever could be possible. He met a girl from {Ankrahmun} and she must have twisted his head. Arito started to tell stories about the Pharaoh and about {Ankrahmun}. ...",
  "npc.muhad.multi_9": "In the wink of an eye he left us and was never seen again. I think he feared revenge for leaving us - which partially is not without reason. Why are you asking me about him? Did he send you to me?",
  "npc.torkada.multi_1": "So hereby receive the blessings of the gods, provided by me as the voice of the inquisition! ...",
  "npc.torkada.multi_2": "Go now and search the ancient temple in the north-west part of the drefian ruins. Slay the evil that lurks there and cleanse the foul place from its taint!",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_1": "Well then - welcome to Mal'ouquah. ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_2": "Go now to general Baa'leal and don't forget to greet him correctly! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_3": "And don't touch anything!",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_4": "Of cour... Huh!? No!? I can't believe it! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_5": "You... you got some nerves... Hmm. ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_6": "Maybe we have some use for someone like you. Would you be interested in working for us. Helping to fight the Marid?",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_7": "Only the mighty Efreet, the true djinn of Tibia, may enter Mal'ouquah! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_8": "All Marid and little worms like yourself should leave now or something bad may happen. Am I right?",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_9": "Only the mighty Efreet, the true djinn of Tibia, may enter Mal'ouquah! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_10": "All Marid and little worms like yourself should leave now or something bad may happen. Am I right?",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_11": "And he is sending a worm like you to us!?! The mighty Efreet!! Tell him that we won't be part in his 'great' plans and now LEAVE!! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_12": "...or do you want to join us and fight those stinking Marid who claim themselves to be noble and righteous?!? Just let me know.",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_13": "You have the smell of the Marid on you. Tell me who sent you?",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_14": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_15": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_16": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.ubaid.multi_17": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.padreia.multi_1": "I knew I could count on you. Take this highly intensified vermin poison. In my vision, I saw some kind of 'pool' where these slimes came from. ...",
  "npc.padreia.multi_2": "Pour the poison in the water to stop the demise of Carlin. Tell me about your mission after you fulfilled your task.",
  "npc.padreia.multi_3": ", thank god you came to me. Last night, I had a vision about an upcoming plague here in Carlin. ...",
  "npc.padreia.multi_4": "It will originate from slimes that will swarm out of the sewers and infect every citizen with a deadly disease. Are you willing to help me save Carlin?",
  "npc.dorian.multi_1": "Once again you've finished your job, and I'll keep my promise. From now on, you can trade with old Black Bert somewhere upstairs to get access to certain items that mightbe of value to someone like you. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_2": "If you like, you can also enter the room to the left and pick one item of your choice.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_3": "Excellent, that little letter will do the trick for sure ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_4": "I think you're really capable and if you finish another mission, I'll allow you full access to our black market of lost and found items. Just ask me to learn more about that mission.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_5": "Ah, the key to untold riches. Don't worry, we'll make sure that no one will connect you to the disappearance of certain royal possessions. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_6": "You're too valuable to us. Speaking about your value, I might have some other mission for you.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_7": "Excellent. You'll learn this trade from scratch. Our operations cover many fields of work. Some aren't even illegal. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_8": "Well, as long as you don't get caught at least. Ask me for a mission whenever you're ready.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_9": "Competition might be an interesting challenge but our guild isn't really keen on competition. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_10": "Unfortunately, we are lacking some good fighters, which is quite a disadvantage against certain other organisations. However, I think you're a really good fighter ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_11": "Travel to the Plains of Havoc and find the base of our competitors under the ruins of the dark cathedral ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_12": "On the lowest level, you'll find a wall with two trophies. Place a message of our guild on the wall, right between the trophies. On your way, get rid of as many of our competitors as you can.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_13": "We'd like to ease our lives somewhat. Therefore, we would appreciate the cooperation with one of the Venore city guards. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_14": "Find some dirt about one of them. It's unimportant what it is. As soon as we have a foothold, we'll convince him to cooperate. Bring me whatever you may find.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_15": "Your next job will be kidnapping. You'll get us the only creature that this scrupulous trader Theodore Loveless in Liberty Bay holds dear. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_16": "His little goldfish! To get that fish, you'll have to get in his room somehow. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_17": "As you might know I sell lock picks, but I fear unless you're extremely lucky, you won't crack this expensive masterpiece of a lock. However, get us that fish, regardless how.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_18": "Your next mission will lead you to Tiquanda. There is a hidden smugglers cave, north of town. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_19": "These smugglers think they don't have to pay us respect and try to withhold our share of the profit. Recently, they got hold of a certain valuable goblet. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_20": "Find them and get us this goblet as rightful payment. If you have to bash some noses during your mission, even better.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_21": "Your next mission is somewhat bigger and I'm sure much fun for you. Some new-rich merchant is being a bit more greedy than it's good for him. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_22": "The good thing is he's as stupid as greedy, so we have a little but cunning plan. We arranged the boring correspondence in advance, so you'll come in when the fun starts. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_23": "You'll disguise yourself as the dwarven ambassador and sell that fool the old dwarven bridge, south of Kazordoon. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_24": "Well, actually it is a bit more complicated than that. Firstly, you'll have to get forged documents. Ask around in the criminal camp to find a forger. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_25": "Secondly, you'll need a disguise. Percybald in Carlin is an eccentric actor that might help you with that. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_26": "As soon as you got both things, travel to Venore and find the merchant Nurik. Trade the false documents for the famous painting of Mina Losa and bring it to me.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_27": "Our beloved king will hold a great festivity at the end of the month. Unfortunately he forgot to invite one of our guild's representatives. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_28": "Of course it would be rude to point out this mistake to the king. It will be your job to get us an invitation to the ball. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_29": "Moreover, It will be a great chance to check the castle for, well, opportunities. I'm sure you understand. However, it's up to that pest Oswald to give out invitations, so he's the man you're looking for.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_30": "A client of our guild would like to get a certain vase. Unfortunately, it's not for sale. Well, by the original owner, that is. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_31": "We, on the other hand, would gladly sell him the vase. Therefore, it would come in handy if we get this vase in our hands. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_32": "Luckily, the walls of the owner's house are covered with vines, that will make a burglary quite easy. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_33": "You'll still need some lock picks to get the chest open in which the vase is stored. Must be your lucky day, as I'm selling lock picks for a fair price. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_34": "You might need some of them to get that chest open. The soon to be ex-owner of that vase is Sarina, the proprietor of Carlin's general store.",
  "npc.dorian.multi_35": "Your first job is quite easy. The Thaian officials are unwilling to share the wealth they've accumulated in their new town Port Hope. ...",
  "npc.dorian.multi_36": "They insist that most resources belong to the crown. This is quite sad, especially ivory is in high demand. Collect 10 elephant tusks and bring them to me.",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_1": "We need you to recharge our ghost pacifiers. They are placed at several strategic points in the caves around us and should be easy to find. Your mission would be to charge seven of them.",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_2": "If you are interested, I can give you some more {information} about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_3": "On these levels we found evidence of some monumental battle that has taken place here centuries ago. We also found some grave sites, but oddly enough no clues of any form of settlement. ...",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_4": "Some evidence we have found suggests that at least one of the battles here was fought for many, many years. People came here, lived here, fought here and died here. ...",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_5": "The battles continued until someone or something literally ploughed through the battlefields, turning everything upside down. All this killing and death soaked the area with negative energy. ...",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_6": "Necromantic forces are running wild all over the place and we are hard-pressed to drive all these undead, spirits and ghosts, away from the Spike. ...",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_7": "Unless we can secure that area somehow, the Spike operation is threatened to become crippled by the constant attacks of the undead. ...",
  "npc.gnomilly.multi_8": "The whole growing downwards could come to a halt, leaving us exposed to even more attacks, counter attacks, and giving the enemy time to prepare their defences. There's a lot to do for aspiring adventurers.",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_1": "So let us begin. Please concentrate with me. Concentrate! ...",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_2": "Concentrate! ...",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_3": "Concentrate! ...",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_4": "Concentrate! ...",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_5": "Concentrate! ...",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_6": "Do you feel something?",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_7": "I am afraid my supplies of peppermoon bell powder have gone flat again. Please provide me with the pollen of this flower. ...",
  "npc.barnabas_dee.multi_8": "It only blooms underground in a cavern to the northwest. I will need 15 units of pollen. Bring them to me and we shall conduct a seance.",
  "npc.muriel.multi_1": "Great! Here is the container for the bone. Once, I used it to collect ectoplasma of ghosts, but it will work here as well. ...",
  "npc.muriel.multi_2": "If you lose it, you can buy a new one from the explorer's society in North Port or Port Hope. Ask me about the mission when you come back.",
  "npc.muriel.multi_3": "I am so glad you are still alive. Benjamin found the container with the bone sample inside. Fortunately, I inscribe everything with my name, so he knew it was mine. ...",
  "npc.muriel.multi_4": "I thought you have been haunted and killed by the undead. I'm glad that this is not the case. Thank you for your help.",
  "npc.muriel.multi_5": "The rotworms dug deep into the soil north of Thais. Rumours say that you can access a place of endless moaning from there. ...",
  "npc.muriel.multi_6": "No one knows how old that common grave is but the people who died there are cursed and never come to rest. A bone from that pit would be perfect for my studies.",
  "npc.muriel.multi_7": "Indeed, there is something you can do for me. You must know I am researching for a new spell against the undead. ...",
  "npc.muriel.multi_8": "To achieve that I need a desecrated bone. There is a cursed bone pit somewhere in the dungeons north of Thais where the dead never rest. ...",
  "npc.muriel.multi_9": "Find that pit, dig for a well-preserved human skeleton and conserve a sample in a special container which you receive from me. Are you going to help me?",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_1": " Ah yeeeeees, ",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_2": ". I will remember you. Now, lessons are every day in the morning and once a week in the evening... ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_3": "Oh, you're not here for this, are you? So about the ghoooosts, yes. You seeeee, there are 3 secret passages here. ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_4": "Thiiiiis is no ordinary house... it is a nexus, a gateway to a once hidden cathedral. Sheltering a small and peaceful society of scholars and monks. Secluded from every distraction. ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_5": "I was one of them and ordered to hold contact to the outside woooorld. But then, something... happened. ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_6": "Outsiders managed to sneak in, infiltrate and influence the society... for the worse. Who knows for what ends. They chaaaaanged... ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_7": "Shortly after, contact was lost... the nexus broken and sealed, ghosts appeared... eeeeeeeverywhere. ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_8": "Find the three passages... one is right here in the cellars, one in the jungles of Tiquanda and one in the deserts of Darama. ...",
  "npc.stricken_soul.multi_9": "Restore their connection and open this nexus to access the buried cathedral and find the cause to this... eliminate all remainders there if you must, ",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_1": "My friend, it seems you have already learnt a lot about the art of trading. I think you are more than worthy to become a recognised trader. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_2": "There is just one little favour that I would ask from you... something personal, actually, forgive my boldness. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_3": "I have always dreamed to have a small pet, one that I could take with me and which wouldn't cause problems. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_4": "Could you - just maybe - bring me a small goldfish in a bowl? I know that you would be able to get one, wouldn't you?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_5": "Fine! There's one more skill that I need to test and which is cruicial for a successful trader. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_6": "Of course you must be able to haggle, else you won't survive long in this business. To make things as hard as possible for you, I have the perfect trade partner for you. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_7": "Dwarves are said to be the most stubborn of all traders. Travel to {Kazordoon} and try to get the smith {Uzgod} to sell a {crimson sword} to you. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_8": "Of course, it has to be cheap. Don't come back with anything more expensive than 400 gold. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_9": "And the quality must not suffer, of course! Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_10": "Dwarves are said to be the most stubborn of all traders. Travel to Kazordoon and try to get the smith Uzgod to sell a crimson sword to you. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_11": "Well, that's good to hear. From you as my trader and deliveryman, I expect more than bringing stinky cheese. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_12": "I wonder if you are able to deliver goods so fragile they almost break when looked at. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_13": "I have ordered a special elven vase from Briasol in Ab'Dendriel. Get it from him and don't even touch it, just bring it to me while I'm in Ankrahmun. Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_14": "Well, that's good to hear. From you as my trader and deliveryman, I expect more than carrying heavy packages. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_15": "You also need to be fast and deliver wares in time. I have ordered a very special cheese wheel made from Darashian milk. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_16": "Unfortunately, the high temperature in the desert makes it rot really fast, so it must not stay in the sun for too long. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_17": "I'm also afraid that you might not be able to use ships because of the smell of the cheese. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_18": "Please get the cheese from Miraia and bring it to me while I'm in Port Hope. Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_19": "Alright, that's good to hear. From you as my trader and deliveryman, I expect more than finding rare items. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_20": "You also need to be able to transport heavy wares, weaklings won't get far here. I have ordered a special package from Edron. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_21": "Pick it up from Willard and bring it back to me while I'm in Liberty Bay. Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_22": "Very good! I need talented people who are able to handle my wares with care, find good offers and the like, so I'm going to test you. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_23": "First, I'd like to see if you can dig up rare wares. Something like a ... mastermind shield! ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_24": "Haha, just kidding, fooled you there, didn't I? Always control your nerves, that's quite important during bargaining. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_25": "Okay, all I want from you is one of these rare deer trophies. I have a customer here in Svargrond who ordered one, so I'd like you to deliver it tome while I'm in Svargrond. ...",
  "npc.rashid_custom.multi_26": "Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_1": "I am glad to hear that. In the spirit of our own foreign legion we suggested the gnomes might hire heroes like you to build some kind of troop. They gave me that strange crystal to allow people passage to their realm. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_2": "I hereby grant you permission to use the basic gnomish teleporters. I also give you four gnomish teleport crystals. One will be used up each time you use the teleporter. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_3": "You can stock up your supply by buying more from me. Just ask me for a {trade}. Gnomette in the teleport chamber of the gnome outpost will sell them too. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_4": "The teleporter here will transport you to one of the bigger gnomish outposts. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_5": "There you will meet Gnomerik, the recruitment officer of the Gnomes. If you are lost, Gnomette in the teleport chamber might be able to help you with directions. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_6": "Good luck to you and don't embarrass your race down there! Keep in mind that you are a representative of the big people.",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_7": "The gnomes are locked in a war with an enemy that thins out their resources but foremost their manpower. We have suggested that people like you could be just the specialists they are looking for. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_8": "If you are interested to {join} the gnomish cause I can arrange a meeting with their recruiter.",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_9": "The gnomes preferred to keep our alliance and their whole {existence} a secret. They are a bit distrustful of others. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_10": "They are quite self-sufficient and the fact that they are actually accepting some help is more than alarming. The gnomes are in real trouble and I am kind of an ambassador to find some people willing to {help}.",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_11": "I am glad to hear that. In the spirit of our own foreign legion we suggested the gnomes might hire heroes like you to build some kind of troop. They gave me that strange crystal to allow people passage to their realm. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_12": "I hereby grant you permission to use the basic gnomish teleporters. I also give you four gnomish teleport crystals. One will be used up each time you use the teleporter. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_13": "You can stock up your supply by buying more from me. Just ask me for a {trade}. Gnomette in the teleport chamber of the gnome outpost will sell them too. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_14": "The teleporter here will transport you to one of the bigger gnomish outposts. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_15": "There you will meet Gnomerik, the recruitment officer of the Gnomes. If you are lost, Gnomette in the teleport chamber might be able to help you with directions. ...",
  "npc.xelvar.multi_16": "Good luck to you and don't embarrass your race down there! Keep in mind that you are a representative of the big people.",
  "npc.mirabell.multi_1": "Here they are. Wait! Two things you should know: Firstly, they won't last long in the sun so you better get them to their destination as quickly as possible ...",
  "npc.mirabell.multi_2": "Secondly, since my pies are that delicious it is forbidden to leave the town with them. We can't afford to attract more tourists to Edron.",
  "npc.jorge.multi_1": "In this category I can offer you a Norseman doll, an abacus, a key of numerous locks, a friendship amulet, a mexcalibur sword, an orc shredder, a frozen heart, a phoenix statue, a dragon eye and a noble sword. Or: ...",
  "npc.jorge.multi_2": "A hand puppet, a music box, an encyclopedia, a Durin doll, a medusa skull, a newspaper, a bag of spices or an Exhiti imortus. ...",
  "npc.jorge.multi_3": "A mathmaster shield, a draken doll, an emblem, a crimson doll, an old radio, a bookworm doll, a golden falcon and an assassin doll. ...",
  "npc.jorge.multi_4": "A dragon goblet, a pigeon trophy, a loremaster doll and a jade amulet. ...",
  "npc.jorge.multi_5": "All listed souvenirs are at 20 silver raid tokens each. Which one of them do you want?",
  "npc.myra.multi_1": "Okay, great! You see, I need a few magical ingredients which I've run out of. First of all, please bring me 70 bat wings. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_2": "Then, I urgently need a lot of red cloth. I think 20 pieces should suffice. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_3": "Oh, and also, I could use a whole load of ape fur. Please bring me 40 pieces. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_4": "After that, um, let me think... I'd like to have some holy orchids. Or no, many holy orchids, to be safe. Like 35. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_5": "Then, 10 spools of spider silk yarn, 60 lizard scales and 40 red dragon scales. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_6": "I know I'm forgetting something.. wait... ah yes, 15 ounces of magic sulphur and 30 ounces of vampire dust. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_7": "That's it already! Easy task, isn't it? I'm sure you could get all of that within a short time. ...",
  "npc.myra.multi_8": "Did you understand everything I told you and are willing to handle this task?",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_1": "Good. Registered as... ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_2": "... with... about ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_3": " of righteously earned inquisition gold added. There. Thanks for your help! ..",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_4": "Good. Ask me any time in case you want to know your current {record}. If you have time, Remember you can also {trade} your earnings into some of these... probably far more valuable, ahem... cluster... things, yes.",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_5": "Of course, let's see. Hm, your recent endeavours would earn you ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_6": " of righteous inquisition gold. You have earned ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_7": " of gold in total. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_8": "Do you want me to add this amount to my books? This will reset your current records, too, however - so?",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_9": "Alright, so you mixed and delivered ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_10": " mortar and ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_11": "You killed ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_12": " frazzlemaws and ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_13": "You also hunted ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_14": " silencers. That would equal ",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_15": " of inquisition gold - BUT we are currently short of this valuable metal so... do you want me to add this amount to my {books} for now or {trade} it for something else.",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_16": "We scouted some caves beneath the island which hold plenty of chalk to mix some good mortar. The entrances are not very far from here in fact. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_17": "However, the entrances are somewhat... twisted. The entrance we had mapped to a certain cave one day, would lead to a completely different cave on the next. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_18": "And even when emerging from one of the caves you never know where you are since its exits are just as deceptive. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_19": "Once you gathered some chalk, you should also find gravel on the island. If you have a pick and a bucket, you should be able to collect enough fine gravel to mix some mortar. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_20": "Do not forget to bring some buckets, if you are in short supply, brother Maun will hand some out to you - for a fee of course.",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_21": "Our brother Mortis is constantly working on keeping the bridge intact. We tried some simple wood planks first but it didn't work out that... well. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_22": "What we need is enough {mortar} to actually build a durable traverse. And we will need even more mortar to maintain it as it constantly gets attacked by vile critters.",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_23": "First, you will help us rebuilding this wretched {bridge} we cannot cross. We need mortar and there are several types of monsters who try to keep us away from it. ...",
  "npc.sandomo.multi_24": "Then there is this enormous wall in the distance. Once we crossed the bridge, we will have to breach this monument. As I see it, you are working for the Inquisition now, I will hear no objection. You may even earn our gratitude.",
  "npc.briasol.multi_1": "Rashid sent you, I suppose. Before I sell you that vase, one word of advice. ...",
  "npc.briasol.multi_2": "Make room in your backpack so that I can place the vase carefully inside it. If it falls to the floor, it will most likely shatter or break if you try to pick it up again. ...",
  "npc.briasol.multi_3": "This vase it not meant to be touched by human hands, so just keep your hands off it. Are you ready to buy that vase for 1000 gold?",
  "npc.santiago.multi_1": "Here, take this fish which I've caught myself. Find it in your inventory, then 'Use' it to eat it. This will slowly refill your health. ...",
  "npc.santiago.multi_2": "By the way: If your hitpoints are below 150, you will regenerate back to 150 hitpoints after few seconds as long as you are not hungry, outside a protection zone and do not have a battle sign. {Easy}, yes?",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_1": "I am glad to hear that. So please listen: Due to circumstances too complicated to explain now, I met Captain Ray Striker. He is ... a freedom fighter and would not find my father's acceptance, but we fell in love ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_2": "Even though he had to hide for a while, we have stayed in contact for a long time now. And our love grew even further against all odds ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_3": "However, recently we lost contact. I don't know what has happened to him and fear the worst ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_4": "We always have been aware that something terrible might happen to him due to his lifestyle. But perhaps there is a harmless explanation for the absence of messages <holds her tears back>. I have arranged a passage for you to Ray's hiding place ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_5": "Contact Captain Waverider, the old fisherman, and tell him the secret word 'peg leg'. He will make sure that you arrive safely ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_6": "Please look for Ray and find out what happened to him and why he was not able to answer. Return to me as soon as you have found something out. I wish you a good journey.",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_7": "Ahh, now I understand... One of my suitors - a real chicken-heart - just brought back my ring. I was really surprised. Suddenly he shows brave attitude. But... It seems you lost it and he tries to take advantage. ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_8": "Thanks a lot anyways and take this gold as a reward. By the way, I would need some help in another matter. It is only a small errand. Are you interested?",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_9": "My ring was stolen by a parrot, directly from my dressing table near the window. It flew to the nearby mountains and I fear my ring will be lost forever. Whoever returns it to me will be rewarded generously. ...",
  "npc.eleonore.multi_10": "I guess that evil parrot hid the ring somewhere on a high tree or a rock so that you might need a rake to get it.",
  "npc.julius.multi_1": "Here is the map. When you are standing near a remarkable spot, use it to mark that spot on the map. Don't forget, come back with at least five marks! ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_2": "Also, they say there is a castle on this island. That mark HAS to be included, it's far too important to leave it out. Good luck!",
  "npc.julius.multi_3": "Great, now here's my plan. As I said, my strength lies not on the battlefield, but it's theory and knowledge. While you were distributing cookies I developed a spell. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_4": "This spell is designed to reveal the identity of the master vampire and force him to show his true face. It is even likely that it instantly defeats him. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_5": "I want you to go to the five vampires you detected and try out the magic formula on them. One of them - the oldest and most powerful - will react to it, I'm sure of it. The words are: '{Alori Mort}'. Please repeat them.",
  "npc.julius.multi_6": "As I already told you, anyone in this city could really be a vampire, even the most unsuspicious citizen. I want you to find that brood. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_7": "You can possibly identify the vampires by using a trick with hidden garlic, but better put it into something unsuspicious, like... cookies maybe! ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_8": "Just bake a few by using holy water on flour, then use that holy water dough on garlic, use the garlic dough on a baking tray and finally place the tray on an oven. Then just play little girl scout and distribute some cookies to the citizens. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_9": "Watch their reaction! If it's suspicious, write down the name and let me know. Then we'll work something out against them. Agreed?",
  "npc.julius.multi_10": "You know, I came to think that the spell didn't work because there is another, greater power behind all of this. I fear that if we don't find the source of the vampire threat we can't defeat them. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_11": "I heard that there is an island not far from here. Unholy and fearsome things are said to happen there, and maybe that means vampires are not far away. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_12": "I want you to try and convince someone with a boat to bring you to this island, Vengoth. I'll give you an empty map. Please map the area for me and pay special attention to unusual spots. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_13": "Mark them on my map and come back once you have found at least five remarkable places on Vengoth. Can you do that for me?",
  "npc.julius.multi_14": "Listen, I thought of something. If we could somehow figure out who among those five is their leader and manage to defeat him,the others might give up too. ...",
  "npc.julius.multi_15": "Without their leader they will at least be much weaker. Before I explain my plan, do you think you could do that?",
  "npc.sam.multi_1": "Thank you very much! This brings back good old memories! Please, as a reward, travel to Kazordoon and ask my old friend Kroox to provide you a special dwarven armor. ...",
  "npc.sam.multi_2": "I will mail him about you immediately. Just tell him, his old buddy Sam is sending you.",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_1": "Ah, the Lady of Darkstone. You have done well to remember her name. ...",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_2": "Now, the shadows say the thing you seek lies next to Akab, the Quarrelsome. ...",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_3": "No coal is burned in his honour. Find his resting place and dig near it. Now go.",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_4": "Then into the vampire crypts, deep down, you must go. ...",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_5": "There... three graves where the shadows swirl, unseen. The first one: name the colour of the silent gong. Then ...",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_6": "The second: the name that is silent now in the halls of Darkstone ...",
  "npc.oblivion.multi_7": "The third: the lost beauty of Dunesea. It must be remembered, the shadows command it. Go now.",
  "npc.lurik.multi_1": "Now we're talking! Maybe you've already heard of the island Okolnir south of Hrodmir. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_2": "Okolnir is the home of a new and fierce dragon race, the so-called frost dragons. However, we have no idea where they originate from. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_3": "Rumours say that dragon lords, that roamed on this isle, were somehow turned into frost dragons when the great frost covered Okolnir. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_4": "Travel to Okolnir and try to find a proof for the existence of dragon lords there in the old times. I think old Buddel might be able to bring you there.",
  "npc.lurik.multi_5": "The information was quite useful. What worries me most are not the raiders but those that have driven them from the old mines...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_6": "We need to investigate the mines. Most entrances collapsed due to the lack of maintenance but there should be some possibilities to get in ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_7": "In case you find a door, Ill tell you the old trick of the Carlin mining company to open it <whisper> <whisper>. Find some hint or someone who is willing to talk about what is going on there.",
  "npc.lurik.multi_8": "You are the one who became an honorary barbarian! The one who made friends with the grim local musher and helped the shamans of Nibelor! The one they call old bearhugg ... erm ... I mean indeed I might have a mission for someone like you ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_9": "We are trying to find out what is happening in the raider camps. Through our connection to the shamans we could get a covered contact in their majorcamp far to the south. We equipped our contact with a memory crystal so he could report all he knew ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_10": "We need you to recover this crystal. Travel to the southern camp of the raiders and find our contact man there. Get the memory crystal and bring ithere. The society and the shamans will then decide our next steps. Do you think you can do this?",
  "npc.lurik.multi_11": "Ah! You did it! I can't wait to hear the sound... but I will do that in a silent moment. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_12": "You helped as much in our research here. As a reward, you may use our astral portal in the upper room from now on. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_13": "For just one orichalcum pearl, you can travel between Liberty Bay and Svargrond. Thank you again!",
  "npc.lurik.multi_14": "Ah, yes, the mission. Let me tell you about something called ice music. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_15": "There is a cave on Hrodmir, north of the southernmost barbarian camp Krimhorn. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_16": "In this cave, there are a waterfall and a lot of stalagmites. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_17": "When the wind blows into this cave and hits the stalagmites, it is supposed to create a sound similar to a soft song. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_18": "Please take this resonance crystal and use it on the stalagmites in the cave to record the sound of the wind.",
  "npc.lurik.multi_19": "A frozen dragon lord? This is just the information we needed! And you even brought a scale from it! Take these 5000 gold pieces as a reward. ...",
  "npc.lurik.multi_20": "As you did such a great job, I might have another mission for you later.",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_1": "Didn't exzpect anyzing lezz from you. Alright, zankz to your effortz to build an effective reziztanze, our comradez zalvaged ziz potion and ze formula you need to utter to breach hiz zubconzciouznezz. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_2": "Drink it and when you are cloze to ze dragon zpeak: Z...z.. well, juzt take ze sheet wiz ze word and read it yourzelf. A lot of rebelz have died to retrieve ziz information, uze it wizely. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_3": "Now go and try to find a way to reach ze emperor and to free ze land from it'z opprezzor. Onze you have found a way, return to me and I will explain what to do wiz ze cryztalz. May ze Great Znake guide you!",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_4": "You freed ze dragon! And you pozzezz ze key to enter ze inner realmz of ze emperor, well done. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_5": "Now you are ready to reach ze inner zanctum of ze emperor. Zalamon'z revelationz showed him zat zere are four cryztalz channelling ze will of ze emperor into ze land. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_6": "Wiz ze relic you gained from Zalamon we were able to create powerful replicaz of ze zeptre. Take ziz wiz you. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_7": "You will have to realign ze cryztalz one after ze ozer. Ztart wiz ze one in ze norz-wezt and work your way clockwize zrough ze room. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_8": "Uzing ze zeptre will forze a part of ze emperor'z willpower out of ze cryztal. You will have to kill zoze manifeztationz. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_9": "Zen uze your zeptre on ze remainz to deztroy ze emperor'z influenze over ze cryztal. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_10": "I recommend not to go alone becauze it will be very dangerouz - but ALL of you will have to uze zeir zeptre replicaz on ze emperor'z remainz to prozeed! ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_11": "You will need it. Now go to the north of Sleeping Dragon room, {dont need talk} with he! Good luck.",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_12": "Ze dragon emperor controlz ze whole empire wiz hiz willpower. But even he iz not powerful enough to uze ziz control continuouzly wizout zome form of aid. ... ",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_13": "Wiz ze ancient zeptre zat you acquired for uz earlier, I can charge ozer zeptrez wiz azpectz of power of ze Great Znake. If you manage to touch one of ze tranzmitter cryztalz wiz ze zeptre, itz godly power will realign ze cryztal. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_14": "Not only will ze cryztal ztop zending ze orderz of ze emperor into ze mindz of my opprezzed people, it will alzo zend a mezzage of freedom and zelf-rezpect inztead. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_15": "Dizabling ze cryztalz will probably alert ze emperor. It will likely be too late for him to intervene in perzon but a creature of hiz power might have ozer wayz to intervene. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_16": "But zere iz more. To reach ze emperor, you will need accezz to hiz inner realmz. Ze zecret to enter iz guarded by a dragon. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_17": "But ziz iz not ze catch - ze catch iz, zat ze key iz buried in hiz vazt mind. Ze emperor haz bound ze dragon to himzelf, forzing him into an eternal zlumber. ...",
  "npc.zizzle.multi_18": "A zignificant part of ze emperor'z power iz uzed to reztrain ze dragon. Ze only way to free him will be to enter hiz dreamz. Are you prepared for ziz?",
  "npc.myzzi.multi_1": "I know only little and I forget so much. So many things going around my mind! ...",
  "npc.myzzi.multi_2": "However, I can grant you access to the {Courts} of Summer and Winter if you promise to help! There you can meet with Undal or Vanys, the servants of Lord Cadion and Lady Alivar. They will be able to tell you more about the issue.",
  "npc.lugri.multi_1": "You do? I mean - wise decision. Let me explain. By now, Tibia has been overrun by numerous followers of different cults and beliefs. The true Necromancers died or left Tibia long ago, shortly after their battle was lost. ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_2": "What is left are mainly pseudo-dark pretenders, the old wisdom and power being far beyond their grasp. They think they have the right to tap that dark power, but they don't. ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_3": "I want you to eliminate them. As many as you can. All of the upstart necromancer orders, and those priestesses. And as I said, don't expect a reward - this is what has to be done to cleanse Tibia of its false dark prophets.",
  "npc.lugri.multi_4": "Hrm. So you had the guts to enter that room. Well, it's all fake magic anyway and no real threat. ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_5": "What are you looking at me for? Waiting for something? I told you that there was no reward. Despite being allowed to stand before me without being squashed like a bug. Get out of my sight!",
  "npc.lugri.multi_6": "You've slain a mere ",
  "npc.lugri.multi_7": " necromancers and priestesses. Still, you've shown some dedication. Maybe that means you can kill one of those so-called 'leaders' too. ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_8": "Deep under Drefia, a necromancer called Necropharus is hiding in the Halls of Sacrifice. I'll place a spell on you with which you will be able to pass his weak protective gate. ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_9": "Know that this will be your only chance to enter his room. If you leave it or die, you won't be able to return. We'll see if you really dare enter those halls.",
  "npc.lugri.multi_10": "What? Who are you to imply I need help from a worm like you? ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_11": "I don't need help. But if you desperately wish to do something to earn the favour of Zathroth, feel free. Don't expect any reward though. ...",
  "npc.lugri.multi_12": "Do you want to help and serve Zathroth out of your own free will, without demanding payment or recognition?",
  "npc.uncle.multi_1": "Some dwarven criminal called Blowbeard dares to blackmail our city. He threatens to destroy the whole city and demands an insane amount of gold ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_2": "Of course we are not willing to give him a single gold coin. It will be your job to get rid of this problem. Go and kill this infamous dwarf ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_3": "His laboratory is near the technomancer hall. Bring me his beard as proof of his demise.",
  "npc.uncle.multi_4": "We try to establish new trade agreements with various potential customers. Sometimes we have to offer some presents in advance to ensure that trade is prospering and flourishing. It will be your task to deliver one of those little presents ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_5": "The northern barbarians are extremely hostile to us. The ones living in Svargrond are poisoned by the lies of agitators from Carlin. The barbarians that are also known as raiders are another story though ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_6": "Of course they are extremely wild and hostile but we believe that we will sooner or later profit from it when we are able to improve our relations. Please deliver this chest of weapons to the barbarians as a sign of our good will ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_7": "Unfortunately, most of them will attack you on sight. It will probably take some time until you find somebody that is willing to talk to you and to accept the weapons.",
  "npc.uncle.multi_8": "As you know, our lovely city is a bastion of civilisation surrounded by numerous hazards. The nearby Plains of Havoc and the hostile elven town Shadowthorn are only a few of the obstacles we have to overcome on an almost daily basis ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_9": "Against all odds, we managed to gain some modest profit by exploiting these circumstances in one way or the other. Recently though, one of our neighbours went too far...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_10": "In some ruin in the midst of the Green Claw Swamp, a dark knight had fancied himself as the lord of the swamp for quite a while ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_11": "For some years, we had some sort of gentleman's agreement. In exchange for some supplies and luxuries, the deranged knight used his ominous influence over the local bonelord species to supply us with ... certain goods ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_12": "However, lately the black knight has proven himself to be no gentleman at all. In a fit of unprovoked rage, he slew our emissary and almost all of his henchmen ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_13": "Even though we can live with this loss, it becomes obvious that the knight's madness gets worse which makes him unbearable as a neighbour. Find him in his hideout in the Green Claw Swamp and get rid of him.",
  "npc.uncle.multi_14": "The oppression of Carlin's men by their lunatic women is unbearable to some of our authorities. We see it as our honourable duty to support the male resistance in Carlin ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_15": "The poor guys have some speakeasy in the sewers. Bring them this barrel of beer with our kind regards to strengthen their resistance.",
  "npc.uncle.multi_16": "Our Thaian allies are sometimes a bit forgetful. For this reason we are not always informed timely about certain activities. We won't insult our great king by pointing out this flaw ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_17": "Still, we are in dire need of these information so we are forced to take action on our own. Travel to the Thaian castle and 'find' the documents we need. They have the file name AH-X17L89. ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_18": "Now go to Thaian castle and get the File.",
  "npc.uncle.multi_19": "Well, well, well! As you might know, we are entrusted by the Venorean tradesmen to ensure the safety of their ventures ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_20": "This task often puts our representatives in rather dangerous and challenging situations. On the other hand, you can expect a generous compensation for your efforts on our behalf...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_21": "Just keep in mind though that we expect quick action and that we are rather intolerant to needless questions and moral doubts ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_22": "If you join our ranks, you cannot join the service of another city! So do I understand you correctly, you want to join our small business?",
  "npc.uncle.multi_23": "You have proven yourself as very efficient. The future may hold great things for you in store ...",
  "npc.uncle.multi_24": "Take this token of gratitude. I hope you can use well what you will find inside!",
  "npc.gareth.multi_1": "Hmm, interesting. Several years ago I have read some books dealing with strange locking mechanisms. I think what you have found here is a bone lever of category 3. ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_2": "Normally this is not used because it is not secure. The production failed and the lever can always be activated as follows: back, back, up, right, left. Just have a try, it should work.",
  "npc.gareth.multi_3": "Well, the situation is this: We have explored a portal, I would say a very aggressive, capriciously and dangerous one. Through this gate monsters entered the construction site and attacked our workers. ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_4": "With enormous effort they could have been dispersed. When my fellows tried to fill up the portal, it appeared again and again. So the only thing they could do was to stop working for the moment. Are you eventually interested in further investigations?",
  "npc.gareth.multi_5": "You have found an inscription I would like to translate for you. The tibianus cipher was used: ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_6": "Those who are accorded the honour to visit this exclusive place will smash their blindness and face the truth. ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_7": "Astonishingly, Dedoras from Cormaya has recently asked me for these kinds of inscriptions. For sure he is able to bring light into the darkness. You should visit him. ",
  "npc.gareth.multi_8": "You're back, nice. Angelo's team hasn't found an artefact yet? I thought the progress would be faster. Anyway thanks for you efforts. ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_9": "I have no work for you right now. If you like to, you can have a look at the last floor. I open the door for you.",
  "npc.gareth.multi_10": "Nice! I'm really happy to have the picture back. First of all I have to check if everything's fine. Then I'll put it back on its place. For now, I'd like you to find out if some rumours about fake pictures in the MOTA are true. ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_11": "Some say one of the small pictures in the entrance hall here is fake. For this reason you have to go to my friend {Angelo} and ask him to get a {magnifier} for the investigation.",
  "npc.gareth.multi_12": "Then do your job here in the museum and come back.",
  "npc.gareth.multi_13": "This is a very wise decision. You won't regret it. Congratulations! As your first task I like you to investigate the crime scene of a theft wich occurred last night. ...",
  "npc.gareth.multi_14": "A very varuable artefact has been stolen. I open the door for you. You can find the room on the same floor as we are right now.",
  "npc.xorlosh.multi_1": "There should be a book in our library about tunnelling. I don't have that much time to talk to you about that. ...",
  "npc.xorlosh.multi_2": "If you want to have some information, you'll just have to find that book. If you need some equipment, go ask Harog. You'll find the library in the north eastern wing of Beregar city.",
  "npc.zarifan.multi_1": "Yes... YES... friendship... lives... FOREVER. ...",
  "npc.zarifan.multi_2": "What you seek.... is buried. Beneath the sand. No graves. ...",
  "npc.zarifan.multi_3": "Between a triangle of big stones you must dig... in the eastern caves. ...",
  "npc.zarifan.multi_4": "And say hello... to... my old friend... Omrabas.",
  "npc.thanita.multi_1": "Oh great! Supplies from Carlin! Let me see ...<she digs into the parcel>...ahh, nothing meaningful at all, like always. Well, before I give you the password for the delivery, you have to help me! ...",
  "npc.thanita.multi_2": "I have massive problems with the goblin tribe that lives here. You look strong enough to face their leader but you need to be smart to lure him out. ...",
  "npc.thanita.multi_3": "I heard they don't like fire very much, maybe that's worth a try. Their beds are mostly made of straw which is known as easily inflammable. ...",
  "npc.thanita.multi_4": "The entrance to their cave is at the pond south east of here.",
  "npc.theodore_loveless.multi_1": "Ah what a fine blend. I really ...",
  "npc.theodore_loveless.multi_2": "OUCH! What have you done you fool? How dare you???",
  "npc.melchior.multi_1": "The djinns have an ancient code of honour. This code includes a special concept of hospitality. Anybody who utters the word of greeting must not be attacked even if he is an enemy. Well, at least that is what the code says. ...",
  "npc.melchior.multi_2": "I have found out, though, that this does not work at all times. There is no point to say the word of greeting to an enraged djinn. ...",
  "npc.melchior.multi_3": "I can tell you the word of greeting if you're interested. It is {DJANNI'HAH}. Remember this word well, stranger. It might save your life one day. ...",
  "npc.melchior.multi_4": "And keep in mind that you must choose sides in this conflict. You can only follow the Efreet or the Marid - once you have made your choice there is no way back. I know from experience that djinn do not tolerate double-crossing.",
  "npc.gnomaticus.multi_1": "To the left you see our shooting range. Grab a cannon and shoot at the targets. You need five hits to succeed. ...",
  "npc.gnomaticus.multi_2": "Shoot at the villain targets that will pop up. DON'T shoot innocent civilians since this will reset your score and you have to start all over. Report to me afterwards.",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_1": "To actually 'find' a suitable location to deploy the probing device for my measurements, you should use my mono detector. The device detects singular chemical structures of any material or fabric I feed it with and signals it! ...",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_2": "If you have lost your detector or your probing device, I can hand out another - it will take some time, however. Do you need a new one?",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_3": "Very good, these readings do tell me a lot - the coloured glooth may be instable but it has some... 'interesting' effects on its surroundings. Oh - no worries, you will be perfectly safe. I will also take back my detector now, thanks. ..",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_4": "Feel free to help me deploy more probes whenever you like.",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_5": "Because of my {experiments} with the {glooth}, some things in the new sewers of Rathleton aren't exactly 'in order' anymore - if you follow me. A sort of mushroom has formed down there and some... 'things' now nest in the lower drainage areas. ...",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_6": "Could you please just go down there and check if this is caused by... my... version of the {glooth}? You know, just some experiments I did to alter the basic elemental structure of the {glooth}, nothing personal. ...",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_7": "If you'd just take this very tiny probing device I designed to analyse the {coloured glooth} and, you know, go down there and place it - oh, and I'll also give you this really tiny {detector}, modified to find a spot where to place the {probe} - so?",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_8": "Good! Quite good! You know, there are actually several things I want you to address. ...",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_9": "First, there is the problem with {communication}, second I need someone to {probe} part of the sewers and last - {combinatorics}!",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_10": "Yes, well I am working on something very time-consuming at the moment. You see, a lot of us don't have time to go out much, to converse even just to meet and talk about recent discoveries. ...",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_11": "So I thought about a device to help communication in this wonderful city. I already had a helper, he was easily... 'stressed' and quit. Didn't have time to find a new one. ...",
  "npc.doubleday.multi_12": "So, if you'd like to help - there is a lot to do for me to bring my plans to fruition - and if you help me, you will earn my {votes} for the {magistrate} in turn! Are you in?",
  "npc.habdel.multi_1": "Listen, um... I know that Ishina has been wanting a comb for a long time... not just any comb, but a mermaid's comb. She said it prevents split ends... or something. ...",
  "npc.habdel.multi_2": "Do you think you could get one for me so I can give it to her? I really would appreciate it.",
  "npc.budrik.multi_1": "By all that is holy! You are a truly great warrior! With much patience! I have just found out the location the hideout of The Horned Fox! I have marked the spot on your map so you can find it. Go there and slay him!! ...",
  "npc.budrik.multi_2": "BUT, you will have only this ONE chance to catch him! Good luck!",
  "npc.budrik.multi_3": "I am so angry I could spit grit! That damn {Horned Fox} and his attacks! Let's show those bull-heads that they have messed with the wrong people....",
  "npc.budrik.multi_4": "I want you to kill 5000 minotaurs - no matter where - for me and all the dwarfs of Kazordoon! Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.budrik.multi_5": "Funny that you are asking me for a mission! There is indeed something you can do for me. Ever heard about The Horned Fox? Anyway, yesterday his gang has stolen my mining helmet during a raid. ...",
  "npc.budrik.multi_6": "It belonged to my father and before that to my grandfather. That helmet is at least 600 years old! I need it back. Are you willing to help me?",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_1": "Ah, thank you. Now look at that texture and fine colour, simply marvellous. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_2": "I hope the sun in the steppe did not exhaust you too much? Shellshock. A dangerous foe in the world of field science and exploration. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_3": "Here, I always wore this comfortable hat when travelling, take it. It may be of use for you on further reconnaissances in Zao. Again you have my thanks, friend.",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_4": "Why yes, there is indeed some minor issue I could need your help with. I was always a friend of nature and it was not recently I discovered the joys of plants, growths, of all the flora around us. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_5": "Botany my friend. The study of plants is of great importance for our future. Many of the potions we often depend on are made of plants you know. Plants can help us tending our wounds, cure us from illness or injury. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_6": "I am currently writing an excessive compilation of all the knowledge I have gathered during my time here in Farmine and soon hope to publish it as 'Rabaz' Unabridged Almanach Of Botany'. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_7": "However, to actually complete my botanical epitome concerning Zao, I would need someone to enter these dangerous lands. Someone able to get closer to the specimens than I can. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_8": "And this is where you come in. There are two extremely rare species I need samples from. Typically not easy to come by but it should not be necessary to venture too far into Zao to find them. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_9": "Explore the anterior outskirts of Zao, use my almanach and find the two specimens with missing samples on their pages. The almanach can be found in a chest in my storage, next to my shop. It's the door over there. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_10": "If you lose it I will have to write a new one and put it in there again - which will undoubtedly take me a while. So keep an eye on it on your travels. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_11": "Once you find what I need, best use a knife to carefully cut and gather a leaf or a scrap of their integument and press it directly under their appropriate entry into my botanical almanach. ...",
  "npc.rabaz.multi_12": "Simply return to me after you have done that and we will discuss your reward. What do you say, are you in?",
  "npc.sandra.multi_1": "The Edron academy has introduced a bonus system. Each time you deposit 100 vials without claiming the money for it, you will receive a lottery ticket. ...",
  "npc.sandra.multi_2": "Some of these lottery tickets will grant you a special potion belt accessory, if you bring the ticket to me. ...",
  "npc.sandra.multi_3": "If you join the bonus system now, I will ask you each time you are bringing back 100 or more vials to me whether you claim your deposit or rather want a lottery ticket. ...",
  "npc.sandra.multi_4": "Of course, you can leave or join the bonus system at any time by just asking me for the 'bonus'. ...",
  "npc.sandra.multi_5": "Would you like to join the bonus system now?",
  "npc.gnomelvis.multi_1": "Congratulations on finding your soul melody. And a pretty one as far as I can tell. Now you are a true recruit of the Bigfoot company! Commander Stone might have some tasks for you to do! ...",
  "npc.gnomelvis.multi_2": "Look for him in the central chamber. I marked your map where you will find him.",
  "npc.gnomelvis.multi_3": "Ah well. Everyone has a very personal melody in his soul. Only if you know your soul melody then you know yourself. And only if you know yourself will you be admitted to the Bigfoot company. ...",
  "npc.gnomelvis.multi_4": "So what you have to do is to find your soul melody. Do you see the huge crystals in this room? Those are harmonic crystals. Use them to deduce your soul melody. Simply use them to create a sound sequence. ...",
  "npc.gnomelvis.multi_5": "Every soul melody consists of seven sound sequences. You will have to figure out your correct soul melody by trial and error. If you hit a wrong note, you will have to start over.",
  "npc.angus.multi_1": "Our members travel to far away places and cross dangerous areas, many fall prey to enemies or the land ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_2": "Sometimes the personal explorer brooches can be recovered. That way we learn about the fate of our members ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_3": "We offer a reward for each brooch returned to us. Have you found an explorer brooch?",
  "npc.angus.multi_4": "Ratha was a great explorer and even greater ladies' man. Sadly he never returned from a visit to the amazons. Probably he is dead ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_5": "The society offers a substantial reward for the retrieval of Ratha or his remains. Do you have any news about Ratha?",
  "npc.angus.multi_6": "That is quite courageous. We know, it's much we are asking for. The queen of the banshees lives in the so called Ghostlands, south west of Carlin. It is rumoured that her lair is located in the deepest dungeons beneath that cursed place ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_7": "Any violence will probably be futile, you will have to negotiate with her. Try to get a spectral dress from her. Good luck.",
  "npc.angus.multi_8": "Fine. The society is looking for new means to travel. Some of our most brilliant minds have some theories about astral travel that they want to research further ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_9": "Therefore we need you to collect some ectoplasm from the corpse of a ghost. We will supply you with a collector that you can use on the body of a slain ghost ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_10": "Do you think you are ready for that mission?",
  "npc.angus.multi_11": "Fine, though it takes more then a mere lip service to join our ranks. To prove your dedication to the cause you will have to acquire an item for us ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_12": "The mission should be simple to fulfil. For our excavations we have ordered a sturdy pickaxe in Kazordoon. You would have to seek out this trader Uzgod and get the pickaxe for us ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_13": "Simple enough? Are you interested in this task?",
  "npc.angus.multi_14": "We would like to study some ancient runes that were used by the lizard race. We suspect some relation of the lizards to the founders of Ankrahmun ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_15": "Somewhere under the ape infested city of Banuta, one can find dungeons that were once inhabited by lizards...",
  "npc.angus.multi_16": "Look there for an atypical structure that would rather fit to Ankrahmun and its Ankrahmun Tombs. Copy the runes you will find on this structure...",
  "npc.angus.multi_17": "Are you up to that challenge?",
  "npc.angus.multi_18": "We acquired some knowledge about special magic stones. Some lost civilisations used it to store knowledge and lore, just like we use books ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_19": "The wisdom in such stones must be immense, but so are the dangers faced by every person who tries to obtain one...",
  "npc.angus.multi_20": "As far as we know the ruins found in the north-west of Edron were once inhabited by beings who used such stones. Do you have the heart to go there and to get us such a stone?",
  "npc.angus.multi_21": "Some high ranking members would like to study elven poetry. They want the rare book 'Songs of the Forest' ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_22": "For sure someone in Ab'Dendriel will own a copy. So you would just have to ask around there. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.angus.multi_23": "We want to learn more about the ancient race of bonelords. We believe the black pyramid north east of Darashia was originally built by them ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_24": "We ask you to explore the ruins of the black pyramid and look for any signs that prove our theory. You might probably find some document with the numeric bonelord language ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_25": "That would be sufficient proof. Would you like to accept this mission?",
  "npc.angus.multi_26": "Both carvings are now charged and harmonised. In theory you should be able to travel in zero time from one base to the other ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_27": "However, you will need to have an orichalcum pearl in your possession to use it as power source. It will be destroyed during the process. I will give you 6 of such pearls and you can buy new ones in our bases ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_28": "In addition, you need to be a premium explorer to use the astral travel. ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_29": "And remember: it's a small teleport for you, but a big teleport for all Tibians! Here is a small present for your efforts!",
  "npc.angus.multi_30": "Those stories are just amazing! Men with faces on their stomach instead of heads you say? And hens that lay golden eggs? Whereas, most amazing is this fountain of youth you've mentioned! ...",
  "npc.angus.multi_31": "I'll immediately send some of our most dedicated explorers to check those things out!",
  "npc.huntsman.multi_1": "To be honest, I don't care too much about that spiritual balance thing. Better talk to {Benevola} about such things. ...",
  "npc.huntsman.multi_2": "As a matter of fact though, if too many animals are killed, things might rapidly change for the worse. ...",
  "npc.huntsman.multi_3": "So it's only practical thinking to keep the balance in mind as long as I can afford it.",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_1": "Every month around the 13th, the single Tibian moon will by fully visible to us. That's when the curse hits us hardest. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_2": "The two days around the 13th, the 12th and the 14th, are considered 'Harvest Moon', those are the best to gather {nightshade}. However, only after it has reached its apex on the 13th, the curse strengthens. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_3": "We do not know what happens down there in those tunnels around that time but there is a presence there, we all feel - yet cannot quite fathom. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_4": "At full moon, humans transform into wild beasts: wolves, boars, bears and others. Some call it the {curse} of the Full Moon, others think it is a kind of sickness. .",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_5": "During this time, we try to not leave the house, we shut the windows and hope it will pass. The curse will weaken a bit after that but it returns. Every month.",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_6": "We are not sure what they are doing down there. We're glad if they stay in the caverns and leave us alone. Only at full moon do they come up and threaten the island's surface and village. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_7": "I, however, have a {hunch} as to why they dwell so deep under the earth.",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_8": "It transforms peaceful villagers into savage beasts. We're not sure how this curse found the way into our small village. But one day it began. At first it befell just a few people. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_9": "In a full moon night they changed into bears and wolves, and tore apart their unsuspecting relatives while they were asleep. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_10": "Those merely wounded, first thought they were lucky. But then we realised they were changing, too. Later, others assumed the forms of badgers and boars also. ...",
  "npc.maeryn.multi_11": "But that does not mean they were any less wild or dangerous than the others.",
  "npc.jondrin.multi_1": "A necrometer? Have you any idea how rare and expensive a necrometer is? There is no way I could justify giving a necrometer to an inexperienced adventurer. Hm, although ... if you weren't inexperienced that would be a different matter. ...",
  "npc.jondrin.multi_2": "Did you do any measuring task for Doubleday lately?",
  "npc.haroun.multi_1": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.haroun.multi_2": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.marvin.multi_1": "So far you earned x votes. Each single vote can be spent on a different topic or you're also able to cast all your votes on one voting. ...",
  "npc.marvin.multi_2": "Well in the topic b you have the possibility to vote for the funding of the {archives}, import of bug {milk} or street {repairs}.",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.multi_1": "Ya gotta learn a lot! The correct command would be STARBOARD side. ...",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.multi_2": "After you told me about the direction, put a bait on the crane again and go up to the lookout! That would be all sailor, let's go hunt down the sea serpent!!",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.multi_3": "A'right, first of all you need a bait which isn't for free, though. I sell them for 50 gold each. Use the bait on the crane over there when you see something in the telescope. ...",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.multi_4": "Then go up to the lookout and check the telescope for a sight of the sea serpent. ...",
  "npc.captain_haba_open_sea.multi_5": "If you see it in front of ya, get down at once. And what d'ya gonna say to me?",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_1": "I have four sons which are very dear to me. Though they were born on the same day and even in the same hour, they took quite different paths in life. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_2": "Each of them chose a different vocation, one will become a knight, one a sorcerer, one a druid, and the other a paladin. In a few weeks they will reach adulthood and I am holding a birthday party for them. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_3": "It should become a day to remember and so I want to give them something special as a present. I searched the land for the finest craftsmen so they could create suitable presents for my sons. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_4": "But something of fine craftsmanship will just not cut it. So I asked them what they would need to create something special. They all came up with lists of rare and expensive items necessary for the task ahead. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_5": "I spent a small fortune to buy most of the materials but in the end the key components are that rare that they cannot be simply bought somewhere. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_6": "As far as I understood it, the places where you can get these items are quite dangerous and so it would take some adventurer to get them. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_7": "That would be your mission if you are interested. Uhm, so are you interested?",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_8": "I'm so glad I finally have all the parts for the presents. Your reward is my eternal gratitude. Well, that and some gold of course. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_9": "Take this sachet over there, I wrapped the coins into this old cape I had still lying around here from a barter with a stranger, it is of no use for me anyway. Farewell and thank you once again.",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_10": "I met this troll when he was hanging around near the town. He carried something I would consider rather uncharacteristic for a troll: a stunningly beautiful cloak entirely made of white feathers. I was curious and asked him if he would sell it. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_11": "He seemed to be more interested in some of my coins and a piece of meat than in this unusual garment. Therefore, we made a trade: He got some meat and coins and I got the cloak. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_12": "I had a clue that it was a magical item but nobody in Edron knew something about it. As I have a very lettered friend in Darashia I took a magical carpet flight to visit him and ask him about the cloak. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_13": "But then something very annoying happened: During the flight the wind blew so strongly that it tattered the cloak. Feather after feather was blown off the carpet but I didn't realise it. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_14": "When I reached Darashia there was no cloak just a handful of feathers. *sighs* I'm not sure whether it makes sense to search for these feathers. There was a small wind gust when we were still above Edron. ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_15": "But the actual storm began when we were in the air above the Darama. The feathers are now scattered all over the desert I guess. Rather futile to look out for them but if you really want to try: ...",
  "npc.tereban_functions.multi_16": "The magic carpet made a beeline from Edron to Darashia. You should search along this line on the ground. Good luck!",
  "npc.rashid.multi_1": "My friend, it seems you have already learnt a lot about the art of trading. I think you are more than worthy to become a recognised trader. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_2": "There is just one little favour that I would ask from you... something personal, actually, forgive my boldness. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_3": "I have always dreamed to have a small pet, one that I could take with me and which wouldn't cause problems. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_4": "Could you - just maybe - bring me a small goldfish in a bowl? I know that you would be able to get one, wouldn't you?",
  "npc.rashid.multi_5": "Fine! There's one more skill that I need to test and which is cruicial for a successful trader. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_6": "Of course you must be able to haggle, else you won't survive long in this business. To make things as hard as possible for you, I have the perfect trade partner for you. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_7": "Dwarves are said to be the most stubborn of all traders. Travel to {Kazordoon} and try to get the smith {Uzgod} to sell a {crimson sword} to you. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_8": "Of course, it has to be cheap. Don't come back with anything more expensive than 400 gold. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_9": "And the quality must not suffer, of course! Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid.multi_10": "Well, that's good to hear. From you as my trader and deliveryman, I expect more than bringing stinky cheese. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_11": "I wonder if you are able to deliver goods so fragile they almost break when looked at. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_12": "I have ordered a special elven vase from Briasol in Ab'Dendriel. Get it from him and don't even touch it, just bring it to me while I'm in Ankrahmun. Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid.multi_13": "Well, that's good to hear. From you as my trader and deliveryman, I expect more than carrying heavy packages. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_14": "You also need to be fast and deliver wares in time. I have ordered a very special cheese wheel made from Darashian milk. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_15": "Unfortunately, the high temperature in the desert makes it rot really fast, so it must not stay in the sun for too long. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_16": "I'm also afraid that you might not be able to use ships because of the smell of the cheese. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_17": "Please get the cheese from Miraia and bring it to me while I'm in Port Hope. Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid.multi_18": "Alright, that's good to hear. From you as my trader and deliveryman, I expect more than finding rare items. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_19": "You also need to be able to transport heavy wares, weaklings won't get far here. I have ordered a special package from Edron. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_20": "Pick it up from Willard and bring it back to me while I'm in Liberty Bay. Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.rashid.multi_21": "Very good! I need talented people who are able to handle my wares with care, find good offers and the like, so I'm going to test you. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_22": "First, I'd like to see if you can dig up rare wares. Something like a ... mastermind shield! ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_23": "Haha, just kidding, fooled you there, didn't I? Always control your nerves, that's quite important during bargaining. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_24": "Okay, all I want from you is one of these rare deer trophies. I have a customer here in Svargrond who ordered one, so I'd like you to deliver it tome while I'm in Svargrond. ...",
  "npc.rashid.multi_25": "Everything clear and understood?",
  "npc.kroox.multi_1": "Oh, so its you, he wrote me about? Sadly I have no dwarven armor in stock. But I give you the permission to retrive one from the mines. ...",
  "npc.kroox.multi_2": "The problem is, some giant spiders made the tunnels where the storage is their new home. Good luck.",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.multi_1": "Thank you. Luckily the damage my ship has taken looks more severe than it is, so I will only need a few wooden boards. ...",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.multi_2": "I saw some lousy trolls running away with some parts of the ship. It might be a good idea to follow them and check if they have some more wood. ...",
  "npc.jack_fate_goroma.multi_3": "We will need 30 pieces of wood, no more, no less. Did you understand everything?",
  "npc.partos.multi_1": "Yes, I've lived in Ankrahmun for quite some time. Ahh, good old times! ...",
  "npc.partos.multi_2": "Unfortunately I had to relocate. <sigh> ...",
  "npc.partos.multi_3": "Business reasons - you know.",
  "npc.partos.multi_4": "What!? I bet, Baa'leal sent you! ...",
  "npc.partos.multi_5": "I won't tell you anything! Shove off!",
  "npc.kazzan.multi_1": "Very good. I hope you are able to convince one of the fractions to stand on our side. If you haven't done yet, you should first go and look for old Melchior in Ankrahmun. ...",
  "npc.kazzan.multi_2": "He knows many things about the djinn race and he may have some hints for you.",
  "npc.kazzan.multi_3": "Alright. The problem is that I want to know at least one of them on my side. You never know. I don't mind if it's the evil Efreet or the Marid. ...",
  "npc.kazzan.multi_4": "Your mission will be to visit one kind of the djinns and bring them a peace-offering. Are you interested in that mission?",
  "npc.nurik.multi_1": "Excellent! Here is the painting you requested. It's quite precious to my father, but imagine his joy when I tell him about my clever deal! ...",
  "npc.nurik.multi_2": "Now leave me alone please. I have to prepare for my departure. Now my family will not call me a squandering fool anymore!",
  "npc.nurik.multi_3": "That's just incredible! I've dreamed about acquiring the dwarven bridge since I was a child! Now my dream will finally become true. ...",
  "npc.nurik.multi_4": "And you are sure you want to sell it? I mean really, really sure?",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_1": "Very good. We prepared a lot of maps as the complete mapping of this system will probably take a lot of research. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_2": "Take one from the stack here next to me and map as many structures as possible. However, we need at least three locations to make any sense of this ancient layout at all. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_3": "If you manage to map one of each structure around these parts - I assume there must be at least two times as many around here - I will hand you a bonus!",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_4": "While exploring these caves to find places to collect spores and grow mushrooms, we found several strange structures. I am convinced that this system was once home to intelligent beings. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_5": "However, the creatures from below are now disturbing our research as well as some particularly pesky dwarves who just would not leave us alone. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_6": "As we have our hands full with a lot of things right now, we could need someone to chart the unknown parts of this underground labyrinth ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_7": "I am especially interested in the scattered dark structures around these parts. Would you do that?",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_8": "While exploring these caves to find places to collect spores and grow mushrooms, we found several strange structures. I am convinced that this system was once home to intelligent beings. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_9": "However, the creatures from below are now disturbing our research as well as some particularly pesky dwarves who just would not leave us alone. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_10": "As we have our hands full with a lot of things right now, we could need someone to chart the unknown parts of this underground labyrinth ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_11": "I am especially interested in the scattered dark structures around these parts. Would you do that?",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_12": "Excellent, just follow the path to east until you reach a dead end, there is a hole that leads to a small cave underneath which will bring you right to the old trail. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_13": "Help whoever you can and return them to the save cave exit - oh, and while you're at it... some of them will have pack animals. If you can rescue those as well, I'll hand you a bonus. Good luck!",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_14": "AMAZING! Not only did you salve all our friends - you also rescued the animals! Here is your reward and bonus! ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_15": "The other are already telling stories about you. Please return to me later if you want to help out some more!",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_16": "I am constantly waiting for ordnance to arrive. A lot of gnomes intend to travel out here to help us but the main access path to our base is not safe anymore. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_17": "Tragically we lost several gnomes after an outbreak of what I can only describe as a force from below. We were completely surprised by their onslaught and retreated to this outpost. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_18": "All our reinforcements arrive at the crystal teleporter to the east of the cave system. We need someone to navigate the new arrivals through the hazards of the dangerous caves. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_19": "Hideous creatures and hot lava makes travelling extremely dangerous. And on top of that there is also the constant danger from falling rocks in the area. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_20": "Are you willing to help?",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_21": "I am constantly waiting for ordnance to arrive. A lot of gnomes intend to travel out here to help us but the main access path to our base is not safe anymore. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_22": "Tragically we lost several gnomes after an outbreak of what I can only describe as a force from below. We were completely surprised by their onslaught and retreated to this outpost. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_23": "All our reinforcements arrive at the crystal teleporter to the east of the cave system. We need someone to navigate the new arrivals through the hazards of the dangerous caves. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_24": "Hideous creatures and hot lava makes travelling extremely dangerous. And on top of that there is also the constant danger from falling rocks in the area. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_25": "Are you willing to help?",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_26": "How fortunate! There are some trignometres lying around next to that device behind me. Take one and hold it next to high temperature heat sources. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_27": "If you gathered enough data, you will actually smell it from the device. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_28": "Return to me with the results afterwards. Best of luck, we count on you!",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_29": "Excellent, you returned with more data! Let me see... hmm. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_30": "Well, we need more data on this but first I will have to show this to our grand horticulturist. Thank you for getting this for us!",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_31": "The heat down here is not the only problem we have but one of our greatest concerns. Not only is it almost unbearable for us, it also seems to be rising. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_32": "We need to find out if this is true and what that means for this place - and for us gnomes. You can help us do this by grabbing one of our trignometres and collecting as much as data from the heat in this area as possible. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_33": "We'd need at least 5 measurements. Are you willing to do this?",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_34": "The heat down here is not the only problem we have but one of our greatest concerns. Not only is it almost unbearable for us, it also seems to be rising. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_35": "We need to find out if this is true and what that means for this place - and for us gnomes. You can help us do this by grabbing one of our trignometres and collecting as much as data from the heat in this area as possible. ...",
  "npc.gnomus.multi_36": "We'd need at least 5 measurements. Are you willing to do this?",
  "npc.zumtah.multi_1": "Oh, excuse me of course, you... wanted to go. Like all... the others. I am sorry, so sorry. You... you can leave. Yes. You can go. You are free. I shall stay here and help every poor soul which ever gets thrown in here from this day onward. ...",
  "npc.zumtah.multi_2": "Yes, I will redeem myself. Maybe in another 278 years. ...",
  "npc.zumtah.multi_3": "If you want to go, just ask for an {exit} and I will transform you into a creature small enough to fit through that hole over there.",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.multi_1": "There are three questions. First: What is the name of the princess who fell in love with a Thaian nobleman during the regency of pharaoh Uthemath? Second: Who is the author of the book ,The Language of the Wolves'? ...",
  "npc.gelidrazahs_thirst.multi_2": "Third: Which ancient Tibian race reportedly travelled the sky in cloud ships? Can you answer these questions?",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_1": "Well, he does not really like it if someone tells his story ... but I do! A long, long time ago Santa was nothing but a greedy little dwarf. A real miser, I tell ya ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_2": "He was greedy even by dwarven standards. He would never share anything or give away the cheapest thing in his possession ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_3": "One day a woman came to his house and asked him for a cup of water ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_4": "Of course he refused. He even mocked her for being so naive. But what he did not know was that this woman was some kind of mighty faery or perhaps a goddess in disguise ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_5": "Be it as it may, the woman cursed old Santa, forcing him to share his fortune with everyone he met ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_6": "Santa was horrified. Of course, he could not bear the thought of sharing anything at all. So he went into hiding ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_7": "He hid in the most remote places in the world, but time and again someone found him out, and the curse made him share his wealth ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_8": "And know something? Old Santa actually came to like it! He saw the joy his presents brought, and this opened his old stony heart ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_9": "And he learned that this way his fortune gave him more joy and pleasure than it ever did when he locked it away. ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_10": "Over the years he turned it into a game. He hid somewhere to reward those who found him ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_11": "But once every year, on a very special day which happens to be his curse's anniversary, he goes out and brings presents to the people, and especially to the children ...",
  "npc.ruprecht.multi_12": "Well, that is his story ... Nah, that's not a tear in my eye. It's just the wind, you know.",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_1": "With your help and efforts we finally cornered what we think is one of 'those below'! For all you have done and endured you are granted the privilege to be one of the first to fight the true enemy. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_2": "For all we know your successes have brought some unrest to our enemies and they sent one of their observers to punish their slaves and force them to more fierce attacks. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_3": "This is our chance to deal the enemy the first blow in this conflict. With reinforcements from Gnomehome we are attacking the troops of the enemy and binding a great deal of their forces in battle. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_4": "Now it is up to you to fight your way to the heart of the enemy's defences and kill the observer. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_5": "Our first tries were met with no success though. The observer has brought with him one of his creatures or lieutenants, the lost call the thing Versperoth. I am not sure if it is a name or a race. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_6": "However Versperoth itself is protected by hoards of minions. Sometimes this thing will withdraw into the ground and let all hell loose in form of its' slaves. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_7": "You'd better be finished with them before Versperoth re-emerges. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_8": "Only when you manage to kill Versperoth, will you be able to enter the portal behind him and face the true evil of the observer. ...",
  "npc.gnomercy.multi_9": "Use the GREEN command crystal in the cave to begin the charging of the teleport! Good luck.",
  "npc.oldrak.multi_1": "You chopped down the demon oak?!? Unbelievable!! Let's hope it doesn't come back. As long as evil is still existent in the soil of the plains, it won't be over. Still, the demons suffered a setback, that's for sure. ...",
  "npc.oldrak.multi_2": "For your brave action, I tell you a secret which has been kept for many many years. There is an old house south of the location where you found the demon oak. There should be a grave with the name 'Yesim Adeit' somewhere close by. ...",
  "npc.oldrak.multi_3": "It belongs to a Daramian nobleman named 'Teme Saiyid'. I knew him well and he told me -almost augured- that someone will come who is worthy to obtain his treasure. I'm sure this 'someone' is you. Good luck in finding it!",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_1": "I heard there is a problem with a wolf mother and her whelps. However, I don't know more about it. One of my sisters, Ikassis, has taken over the body of a snake. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_2": "She knows more about the wolf. Seek her out in the north-west of Edron, near a circle of standing stones.",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_3": "Your decision honours you. However, if you consider killing the poachers in question I ask you to halt. We, the fae, are rather peaceful beings and abhor bloodshed. Therefore, we must find another way to solve this problem. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_4": "I already have an idea: Some birds told me that poachers are a superstitious lot. Perhaps we can get them with their own misbelief. I know that the poachers have a kind of camp north of the Green Claw Swamps. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_5": "Please search it out and examine it closely. Perhaps you will find something you can use against them in order to stop them from hunting white deer.",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_6": "I indeed have some troubles since I'm travelling this part of the world. When I took over the body of a white deer I wasn't aware that such an animal is a sought after quarry for hunters and poachers. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_7": "Now I'm living in the constant danger of being caught and killed. Of course, I could just take over another animal but this deer has really grown on me. I'd like to help this beautiful stag but I need your assistance. Are you willing to help me?",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_8": "I'm very happy that you could help fae and animals alike. You earned our trust and may now visit our secret realm. I marked you with an arcane fae seal. Hereby you will be able to use the elemental shrines strewn about Tibia. ...",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_9": "There are fire, ice, energy and earth shrines. If you don't know their locations you can also reach them by most temples in this world. The elemental shrines will transport you to Feyrist now that you bear the magical seal.",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_10": "You succeeded! It seems the poachers have read your little faked story about killing white deer and the ensuing doom. They stopped chasing me. Thank you! ...",
  "npc.alkestios.multi_11": "You proved yourself trustworthy - at least as far as I am concerned. But as I told you I'm actually not a real animal. If you want to enter our hidden island, you must prove that you are also willing to help real animals. Would you do that?",
  "npc.henricus.multi_1": "Even though they claim differently, this city is in the firm grip of Zathroth and his evil minions. Their whole twisted religion is a mockery of the teachings of our gods ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_2": "As soon as we have gathered the strength, we should crush this city once and for all.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_3": "Edron illustrates perfectly why the inquisition is needed and why we need more funds and manpower. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_4": "Our agents were on their way to investigate certain occurrences there when some faithless knights fled to some unholy ruins. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_5": "We were unable to wipe them out and the local order of knighthood was of little help. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_6": "It's almost sure that something dangerous is going on there, so we have to continue our efforts.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_7": "Fafnar is mostly worshipped by the peasants and farmers in rural areas. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_8": "The inquisition has a close eye on these activities. Simply people tend to mix local superstitions with the teachings of the gods. This again may lead to heretical subcults.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_9": "The church of Uman oversees the education of the masses as well as the doings of the sorcerer and druid guilds. It decides which lines of research are in accordance with the will of Uman and which are not. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_10": "Concerned, the inquisition watches the attempts of these guilds to become more and more independent and to make own decisions. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_11": "Unfortunately, the sorcerer guild has become dangerously influential and so the hands of our priests are tied due to political matters ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_12": "The druids lately claim that they are serving Crunor's will and not Uman's. Such heresy could only become possible with the independence of Carlin from the Thaian kingdom. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_13": "The spiritual centre of the druids switched to Carlin where they have much influence and cannot be supervised by the inquisition.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_14": "In the past, the order of Banor was the only order of knighthood in existence. In the course of time, the order concentrated more and more on spiritual matters rather than on worldly ones. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_15": "Nowadays, the order of Banor sanctions new orders and offers spiritual guidance to the fighters of good.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_16": "The Thaian kings are crowned by a representative of the churches. This means they reign in the name of the gods of good and are part of the godly plan for humanity. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_17": "As nominal head of the church of Banor, the kings aren't only worldly but also spiritual authorities. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_18": "The kings fund the inquisition and sometimes provide manpower in matters of utmost importance. The inquisition, in return, protects the realm from heretics and individuals that aim to undermine the holy reign of the kings.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_19": "The dark powers are always present. If a human shows only the slightest weakness, they try to corrupt him and to lure him into their service. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_20": "We must be constantly aware of evil that comes in many disguises.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_21": "Incredible! You're a true defender of faith! I grant you the title of a High Inquisitor for your noble deeds. From now on you can obtain the blessing of the inquisition which makes the pilgrimage of ashes obsolete ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_22": "The blessing of the inquisition will bestow upon you all available blessings for the price of 110000 gold. Also, don't forget to ask me about your {outfit} to receive the final addon as demon hunter.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_23": "Indeed, this is exactly what my other sources told me. Of course I knew the outcome of this investigation in advance. This was just a test. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_24": "Well, now that you've proven yourself as useful, you can ask me for another mission. Let's see if you can handle some field duty, too.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_25": "So the beast is finally dead! Thank the gods. At least some things work out in our favour ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_26": "Our other operatives were not that lucky, though. But you will learn more about that in your next {mission}.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_27": "We've got information about something very dangerous going on on the isle of Edron. The demons are preparing something there ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_28": "Something that is a threat to all of us. Our investigators were able to acquire vital information before some of them were slain by a demon named Ungreez. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_29": "It'll be your task to take revenge and to kill that demon. You'll find him in the depths of Edron. Good luck.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_30": "You're indeed a dedicated protector of the true believers. Don't stop now. Kill as many of these creatures as you can. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_31": "I also have a reward for your great efforts. Talk to me about your {demon hunter outfit} anytime from now on. Afterwards, let's talk about the next mission that's awaiting you.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_32": "You've handled heretics, witches, vampires and ghosts. Now be prepared to face the most evil creatures we are fighting - demons. Your new task is extremely simple, though far from easy. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_33": "Go and slay demonic creatures wherever you find them. Bring me 20 of their essences as a proof of your accomplishments.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_34": "We've got a report about an abandoned and haunted house in Liberty Bay. I want you to examine this house. It's the only ruin in Liberty Bay so you should have no trouble finding it. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_35": "There's an evil being somewhere. I assume that it will be easier to find the right spot at night. Use this vial of holy water on that spot to drive out the evil being.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_36": "I think it's time to truly test your abilities. One of our allies has requested assistance. I think you are just the right person to help him ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_37": "Storkus is an old and grumpy dwarf who works as a vampire hunter since many, many decades. He's quite successful but even hehas his limits. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_38": "So occasionally, we send him help. In return he trains and tests our recruits. It's an advantageous agreement for both sides ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_39": "You'll find him in his cave at the mountain outside of Kazordoon. He'll tell you about your next mission.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_40": "Listen, we have information about a heretic coven that hides in a mountain called the Big Old One. The witches reach this cursed place on flying brooms and think they are safe there. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_41": "I've arranged a flying carpet that will bring you to their hideout. Travel to Femor Hills and tell the carpet pilot the codeword 'eclipse' ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_42": "He'll bring you to your destination. At their meeting place, you'll find a cauldron in which they cook some forbidden brew ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_43": "Use this vial of holy water to destroy the brew. Also steal their grimoire and bring it to me.",
  "npc.henricus.multi_44": "Let's see if you are worthy. Take an inquisitor's field guide from the box in the back room. ...",
  "npc.henricus.multi_45": "Follow the instructions in the guide to talk to the Thaian guards that protect the walls and gates of the city and test their loyalty. Then report to me about your {mission}.",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.multi_1": "Yesss! So this time he will get it for a change! And he lived there...? He helped whom? Ha! He won't get away this time! What did he do there? I see... interesting! ...",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.multi_2": "Wait till mother hears that! Oh he will be in for a surprise, I can tell you that. Ma!! Maaaaa!!",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.multi_3": "I knew it! He likes taking extended walks outside, leaving all the cleaning to me - especially when he is working on this sculpture, this... 'thing' he tries to create. ...",
  "npc.sister_of_jack.multi_4": "What did he do? Since you look like a guy from the city, I bet he went to Edron in secrecy or something like that, didn't he? And you are here because of that?",
  "npc.iskan.multi_1": "That's surprising. Take a piece of meat. If you find the boy, feed it to him. That will give him enough strength and incentive to return to his pack ...",
  "npc.iskan.multi_2": "Talk to him by calling his name 'Sniffler' and tell him you got meat for him. After he has eaten the meat, return here to talk to me about your mission.",
  "npc.iskan.multi_3": "Well, one of the boys has run away. I think he got the scent of some beast. He's young and inexperienced so I can't blame the cub ...",
  "npc.iskan.multi_4": "I would like you to see after him. He should be somewhere north west of the town. He is probably marking his territory so you should be able to find his trace. Are you willing to do that?",
  "npc.the_orc_king.multi_1": "I can sense your evil intentions to imprison a djinn! You are longing for the lamp, which I still possess. ...",
  "npc.the_orc_king.multi_2": "Who do you want to trap in this cursed lamp?",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_1": "Time to have a sweet drink! Let's pour the bug milk into my cauldron and heat it over fire until it's boiling... <starts slicing mangoes in the meantime> there! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_2": "Now we're breaking all of the eggs into there - 1, 2, 10, 20, 40 <ticktickcrack> crumble the honeycombs and toss the sliced mangoes into the hot mix. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_3": "Now we just have to let it simmer and stir using a blessed wooden stake <stirs so vigorously that you can barely see his arms anymore> for thirty minutes. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_4": "By now, the power of the blessed wooden stake will have been transferred into our elixir, so let's put out the fire and let it cool down. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_5": "<carefully pours the cooled elixir into a small bottle or glass> There! Its inventor said it had amazing effects on the ring you're wearing, as long as the ring is based on time, not on charges. Enjoy! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_6": "And by the way... since those were all the recipes from this year and you cooked them so nicely, you may take the cookbook containing them from upstairs, if you like!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_7": "Very nice! I'm ready for action! <quickly grabs all the candies, candy canes and gingerbread men and crushes them with amazing speed> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_8": "After having crushed all those sweets, we need to melt the chocolate into a thick liquid... <creates a magical flame by snapping his fingers and melts the chocolate so fast over the sweets that it's amazing he didn't spill it everywhere> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_9": "... and form little balls together with the sweets! <shapes candy balls about the size of rice balls faster and more perfectly than any mortal ever could> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_10": "Now, carefully, we add the demonic blood... <and time seems to stand still as seemingly for the first time ever he does something slowly, pouring a single drop of concentrated demonic blood onto each ball> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_11": "Here you go, but beware possible side effects! You never know for sure what will happen and so far all of those I tried had awesome effects, so of course I don't hope for nasty surprises! Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_12": "Awesome! Let's go! Let's start with preparing the sandcrawlers <starts boiling water on a stove and tosses the sandcrawler shells in there> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_13": "I understand your scepticism, but believe me, all will be well! As you can see, they change colour from dark to light red, and that's when they also start turning soft. <stirs with one hand while he slices carrots and peppers with the other hand> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_14": "Now add whole potatoes and let everything cook at high temperature until the potatoes are so soft they're basically falling apart. <mashes really fast, creating something of a dark brownish colour that doesn't really look tasty> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_15": "Yes yes, I know, don't give me that look! You'll be surprised! Now just add the chopped carrots and chili for a healthy portion of vitamins and spices, keep stiring and mashing and let it simmer for about an hour. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_16": "You're wondering why I chose a simple recipe like that for my famous menu? You'll know when you taste it! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_17": "Heeeeeere you are - just a few spoons of this great stew make you so full that the bowl I give you will last for a long time until it's finally depleted. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_18": "Yum! Just the thought of it makes me drool. <tosses the shrimps into a bowl and soaks them in coconut milk as he goes on chopping all mushrooms in the blink of an eye> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_19": "I see you brought real Zaoan rice balls! That saves us a lot of time as we don't have to cook the rice anymore. Now we just flatten them out nice and medium thick on this baking tray. <squeezes and smoothes the rice piles with his fingers> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_20": "In the meantime, our shrimps have absorbed some of the coconut milk and we can now add them on top of the rice. <spreads them evenly across the rice and pours the coconut milk from the bowl over the rice> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_21": "Now we just need to add the mushrooms <tosses them all over the tray>, pour the rest of the coconut milk over it and put it into the oven! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_22": "... dum di dum ... <waits> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_23": "Aaaaaaand there you go! Sweet coconut goodness! And psst - the shrimps add some submarine flavour to this dish. You should definitely eat it while walking underwater and wearing a helmet of the deep. Just in case. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_24": "So, now for our final dish - a grand dessert from the amazon girls at Carlin! <grates carrots during his explanations> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_25": "It's easy as it can be - mix a normal cake dough with milk, flour and eggs, then add some cookie crumbs for the crunchy effect later on. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_26": "Stir in the grated carrots and tiny peanut pieces and bake it for about thirty minutes! Now we'll make a great topping with sugar and lemon juice, pour it over the cake and decorate it. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_27": "And voilà, we're done! The girls of Carlin swear that it sharpens their eyesight, at least for a while. I'm sure it will somehow aid you in your battles. Enjoy! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_28": "Oh, which reminds me - my little apprentice, we are finished with our cooking course. I think you did great and if it was my decision, you could open your own tavern. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_29": "But anyway, it's up to you what you make of your newly discovered skills! In case you forget my recipes, please feel free to take a copy of the cookbook upstairs. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_30": "You can drop by and practice cooking those dishes, at least during the time that I'm at home. I promise that I will cook each dish once with you, but then I have to take care of my other apprentices. Cheers to you!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_31": "Great! After all this meat, we shouldn't neglect to prepare some fish. <carefully removes heads, tails and bones from the fishes and peels shrimps at incredible speed> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_32": "This easy dish from Svargrond is what you'd call fast food, but its outstanding taste justifies to put it in my book about {Hot Cuisine}. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_33": "Simply cut the rolls in half, shortly fry one slice of each fish type, put in the shrimps and spice up with grinded fern, which, by the way, tastes slightly like dill. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_34": "Nicely decorate it on a plate, and voilà, we're done already! Can't tell you much about the effects, but fishermen in Svargrond seem to love it. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_35": "Here we go! <pounds with his bare hands on the steak> This will break through the meat fibres, making our steak more tender for this fine Daramanian dish. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_36": "It's easy to prepare, just chop and sweat the onions and add small pieces of pumpkin, beetroot, plums and peppers. Put the steak into the pan too to let it absorb some of the sweet and fruity flavour. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_37": "Finally, remove the fruits and onions from the pan and fry the steak from both sides until it's crisp and crusty. Put on a plate and decorate with the fruit mix. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_38": "The people of Darashia say that it has magical abilities and will help you if you feel totally drained. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_39": "Okay! So after all of these heavy dishes, we're going to create a fast little snack. <starts preparing the peppers as he speaks> ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_40": "First of all, remove the top of the jalapeño peppers and clean their inside, so that you have space for the filling. Now for the filling, we grate the cheese and mix it with the mead and the eggs, until it has a nice consistency. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_41": "We add the grinded herbs and blend it well. Push a spoonful in each jalapeño pepper until they are nicely stuffed. Now, we shortly fry the jalapeño peppers in a pan to heat them up. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_42": "The filling will melt nicely, just be careful that it doesn't drip out! And voilà, we're done! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_43": "This famous dish from Ankrahmun is quite hot and spicy, so only eat one at a time. It's also possible that you get the urge to run really fast afterwards. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_44": "So let's start! <rubs hands together and chops the vegetables> This is a dish especially famous in the area around Ab'Dendriel! Chop the onions into little cubes and sweat them in a pan until they are glassy. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_45": "Add garlic and mushrooms and fry gently until the mushrooms have shrunk up. Now, we add the peeled tomatoes and corn and have it all nicely cook together. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_46": "Put in carrot pieces and cucumber at the very end, so they will stay crisp! Finally put the cheese over it like a little blanket have it melt on the oven until it's slightly brownish. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_47": "And voilà, we're done! This dish will help you in your battles and supply you with enough power to hit really hard! Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_48": "Great! Let's get it done! <mixes and shakes faster than any human could> An easy one again, but you'll get right into holiday mood, like the Meriana beach dwellers I got that recipe from. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_49": "Melt the chocolate in a hot-water bath and add the grinded herbs - did you know, those herbs have a flavour like cinnamon and vanilla, yummy! Keep at gentle heat and add the milk. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_50": "Mash the banana and stir it really well into the chocolate-milk mixture. Gosh, do you smell that? Pure goodness! Now finally, we take just a bit of the creamcake and fold it in. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_51": "Voilà, we're done! To be honest, I don't know what this drink does, but at least it makes me really happy. Drink together with a loved one and enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_52": "This is a recipe right from the jungles of Tiquanda! <grinds and chops during his talk> Grind the stone herb and mix it with the coconut milk, then bathe the chicken in it for a while. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_53": "In the meantime, peel the oranges and mangos, chop them into pieces and add them to the mix. Take the chicken out of its bath and fry it, preferably over open fire. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_54": "Take the fruits out of the spicy coconut milk and heat them on an oven. Once the chicken is fried, add the fruits and spray some squeezed lemon over it. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_55": "Voilà, we're done! They say that this dish has magical abilities and can awaken secret powers in you during your battles. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_56": "Let's get started! <starts grinding and chopping at amazing speed> The trick with this one is the crunchy crust around the wings. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_57": "First, we grate the dry brown bread into very small crumbs and mix that with the two eggs. Add grinded peppers for the spicy taste and the powder herb for a hint of curry flavour. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_58": "Carefully separate the bat wings, clean them of any possible hairs and coat them in our mixture. Roast them in a pan together with sliced mushrooms and serve. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_59": "Voilà, we're done! This recipe is from the area around Thais and should help you protect yourself in your battles. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_60": "Okay, here we go! <cuts the ingredients so fast that his hands seem almost blurry> This one is easy, just chop the hydra tongues, tomatoes and cucumber into tiny pieces. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_61": "Now for the sauce - our base is wine, in which we mix the raw eggs until it got a nice smooth consistency. Add grinded troll green, whose flavour is quite similar to basil and shake the sauce in a mug. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_62": "Pour it over the salad, and voilà, we're done! This is a Venorean recipe and very tasty. I recommend eating it when you're suffering from some kind of dangerous condition. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_63": "Aah, so let's see! <prepares the food quickly while he explains it to you> We cook the meat in a large pot together with the chopped onion until it's separated from the bones. Now we also have a fine meat broth! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_64": "Cut the potatoes into small pieces and add them to the pot. Add some flour to thicken the stew. Finally, spice it up with some garlic and add beer for the typical dwarvish taste! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_65": "And voilà, we're done. I developed this recipe while talking to Maryza in the Jolly Axeman. She said to eat it when one's health is low. Enjoy!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_66": "Did you dare eat all of your Demonic Candy Balls...? Hehehe! Well, I almost forgot one of the most essential parts for a perfect dinner. A drink! I have one for you, almost a designer drink you could say. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_67": "Its inventor seems to have done some scientific research in order to achieve his desired effect, which is - charging magical rings. You have to drink it while you're wearing one for a miraculous effect! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_68": "Bring me the following ingredients and we'll get started: Fourty eggs, twenty mangos, ten honeycombs, one bottle of bug milk and one blessed wooden stake. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_69": "Oh yes, I understand your worries about the eggs, but just make sure they're fresh and all should be fine for our {Sweet Mangonaise Elixir}!",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_70": "Weren't you surprised by the great taste of our main dish? In case you still have some space left in your tummy, we're in for a sweet and fun dessert - but beware unwanted side effects! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_71": "It was introduced to me by a fearless knight who invented this recipe rather by accident when a bottle of demonic blood broke in his backpack and spilled its contents over his bag of candy balls. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_72": "Curiously, he tried one and red steam came out of his ears - but it tasted so great that he instantly popped another one in his mouth, and then another, and another. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_73": "Each one seemed to cause a different effect and he was never really sure what the next one would do. Seems safer to be careful with them and not to eat them in dangerous situations! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_74": "In any case, bring me the following ingredients and we'll make some {Demonic Candy Balls}, if you like: Three candies, three candy canes, two bars of chocolate, fifteen gingerbread men and one concentrated demonic blood.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_75": "After this wonderful and tasty starter we're all set for a special dish I learnt from a brave adventurer who almost starved when he got lost in the mountains between Ankrahmun and Port Hope, or so he told me. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_76": "Luckily, he was saved by nomads - can you imagine? - and they fed him a special local dish that's very cheap and easy to prepare, yet rich in vitamins and spending energy for hours. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_77": "Now don't be shocked, but - they do put sandcrawlers in there. When I tried to prepare that dish at first, I was repelled by its awful appearance, but since it smelled so good I did take a sip and was pleasantly surprised of the great taste. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_78": "According to the adventurer, this meal works well with any kind of vegetables or any kind of edible creepy-crawlers, depending on what the nomads get their hands on, but we'll stick to the original for now! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_79": "Bring me the following ingredients - if you dare - and I'll show you the secret of {Blackjack}: Five sandcrawler shells, two vials of water, twenty carrots, ten potatoes and three jalapeño peppers.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_80": "Yes, you heard that right! Even though I was laying sick on my divan for weeks, I have some new dishes for you. Ehem. Of course I couldn't have done it without my little helpers travelling around the world and discovering recipes. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_81": "So... <rubs hands together> ... each good menu needs an amazing starter to awaken and stimulate all the little taste buds on your tongue. We're going to cook a nice portion of {Coconut Shrimp Bake}! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_82": "This is an exotic rice dish with hints of mushrooms and shrimps, topped with sweet coconut goodness - brought to me by a beautiful druid lady a few days ago. My mouth starts watering already! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_83": "... because of the dish, I mean, of course. Ehem. Bring me the following ingredients and we'll get started: Five vials of coconut milk, five brown mushrooms, five red mushrooms, ten rice balls and ten shrimps.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_84": "The last dish we are going to prepare together is called {Carrot Cake}. Yes, it's a real cake, we need a tasty desert to complete our cooking course. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_85": "Bring me the following ingredients and I'll lead you through it: five carrots, one vial of milk, one lemon, ten ounces of flour, two eggs, ten cookies and two peanuts.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_86": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Northern Fishburger}. I hope you like fish, not everyone does. This one is a specialty I picked up in Svargrond. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_87": "Bring me the following ingredients and I'll show you how it's done: one northern pike, one rainbow trout, one green perch, five shrimps, two rolls and one fern.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_88": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Blessed Steak}. <giggles> I'm sorry, I couldn't resist the pun with this one. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_89": "Don't worry, there's no temple trip awaiting you. Just bring me the following: one piece of ham, five plums, one onion, two beetroots, one pumpkin and two jalapeño peppers.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_90": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Filled Jalapeño Peppers}. It's a great snack and quite spicy, for those who like it hot. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_91": "Bring me the following ingredients and I'll show you how it's done: Ten jalapeño peppers, two pieces of cheese, one troll green, one shadow herb, one vial of mead and two eggs.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_92": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Veggie Casserole}. This one is going to be your masterpiece so far, I'm telling you. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_93": "It's also quite healthy! - Well, that's what I keep telling me when I eat the third serving, hehehe. Bring me the following ingredients and I'll show you how it's done. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_94": "Two carrots, two tomatoes, two corncobs, two cucumbers, one onion, one bulb of garlic, one piece of cheese, twenty white mushrooms and five brown mushrooms.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_95": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Banana Chocolate Shake}. After all those spicy dishes you should treat your guests with a sweet surprise. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_96": "Bring me the following ingredients and we'll make one hell of a drink: one bar of chocolate, one cream cake, two bananas, two vials of milk, one sling herb and one star herb.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_97": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Tropical Fried Terrorbird}. You might have guessed it, we're not going to use a terrorbird. But! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_98": "The dish is quite fried and tropical. Bring me the following ingredients and we're going to prepare it: One fresh dead chicken, two lemons, two oranges, two mangos, one stone herb and two vials of coconut milk.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_99": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Roasted Dragon Wings}. Oh, don't give me that look! Of course you don't have to bring a whole dragon up here. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_100": "The 'dragon' part derives from the fiery afterburn of this meal, but the wings we use are much smaller, though similar in shape. Bring me the following ingredients and I'll show you how it's done. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_101": "One fresh dead bat, three jalapeño peppers, five brown breads, two eggs, one powder herb and five red mushrooms.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_102": "The next dish we are going to prepare together is called {Hydra Tongue Salad}. The common hydra tongue is a pest plant with an surprisingly aromatic taste. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_103": "We'll add some other vegetables and spices for the delicate and distinctive taste. Bring me the following ingredients and I'll show you how it's done. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_104": "Two hydra tongue plants, two tomatoes, one cucumber, two eggs, one troll green and one vial of wine.",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_105": "The first dish we are going to prepare together is called {Rotworm Stew}. Now, don't be scared off. Of course we won't eat those nasty and dirty earth-crawlers! ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_106": "The name is just for the effect it has on people. <winks> Bring me the following ingredients and I'll show you how it's done. ...",
  "npc.jean_pierre.multi_107": "Two pieces of meat, two vials of beer, twenty potatoes, one onion, one bulb of garlic and five ounces of flour. Make sure that the ingredients are fresh and smell good.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_1": "I put these crystals onto the top of compass. As you can see, the compass is now pulsating in a warm, violet colour. ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_2": "Now this compass is ready for usage. It can transfer the bound energy to other inanimate objects to open certain gates or chests.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_3": "Nice! To do so, take this golden axe and mine the prominent crystals in the cave. Besides, I need a poison gland of quite rare spiders, they are called lucifuga araneae. ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_4": "These are quite shy, but I have a {bait} for you to lure them. But take care not to face too many of them at once. And hurry, the effect won't last forever!",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_5": "Alright, I put the glasses into the right pattern and can repair the compass. ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_6": "There we are! The next step is the charging of the compass. For this you have to dig three different crystals down there: 5 blue, 3 green and one violet crystal. Are you ready to do that?",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_7": "Only in the cave down there you will find the materials you need to repair the {compass}. Now you know why the entrance is sealed. There's the seal, but I have a deal for you: ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_8": "I can repair the compass for you if you deliver what I need. Besides the broken compass you have to bring me the following materials: 50 blue glas plates, 15 green glas plates and 5 violet glas plates. ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_9": "They all can be found in this closed cave in front of you. I should have destroyed this seal key but things have changed. The entrance is opened now, go down and do what has to be done.",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_10": "Well, a while ago powerful magic devices were used all around Tibia. These are chargeable compasses. There was but one problem: they offered the possibility to make people rich in a quite easy way. ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_11": "Therefore, these instruments were very coveted. People tried to get their hands on them at all costs. And so it happened what everybody feared - bloody battles forged ahead. ...",
  "npc.andrew_lyze.multi_12": "To put an end to these cruel escalations, eventually all of the devices were collected and destroyed. The remains were buried {deep} in the earth.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_1": "Well, if you really want to delve into this - I could use some help. So you have found my machine on that island? And you found the notes with the coordinates? Then you can find the entrance! ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_2": "Just look for a large staircase with sprawling steps. There is an unpassable stream there that will prevent you from venturing further on. But fear not, you can indeed travel down there - with these small enhancements I created. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_3": "I will put this under your footgear. Here you go. And this in your nose. There. And there will be no further problems for you down there. Except- ah, well you'll find out yourself soon enough, won't you?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_4": "Mh? Ah, yes yes. 'Njey' is the native-language term for a very old race of undersea creatures which ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_5": "...hm, wait - only a select few of my colleagues even bothered studying their culture. They are a mere fantasy to the common man - is there anything of importance you want to tell me?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_6": "There are rumours of aggressive fishmen in northern Tiquanda. We have to find out if this is even remotely connected to the Njey. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_7": "What's puzzling me is that they were sighted above ground and then retreated into a temple ruin. If we find that ruin, we could find out if there's a relation. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_8": "Are you willing to help me?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_9": "Well, if you really want to delve into this - I could use some help. So you have found my {machine} on that island? And you found the notes with the coordinates? Then you can find the entrance! ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_10": "Just look for a large staircase with sprawling steps. There is an unpassable stream there that will prevent you from venturing further on. But fear not, you can indeed travel down there - with these small {enhancements} I created. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_11": "At first, take this gold for the passage by ship and return to the Gray Island from where I started my expedition many years ago. From there you should find a way to reach the Gray Beach of Quirefang as no ordinary ship can land there. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_12": "I will put this under your footgear. Here you go. And this in your nose. There. And there will be no further problems for you down there. Except- ah, well youll find out yourself soon enough, wont you?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_13": "You do? Well, the end of this story was that I had to leave the place. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_14": "I couldnt explore what lies below the stairs as there was an unpredictable stream. Diving into these waters would have been an uncontrollable risk, even with the means to survive without any air. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_15": "So I used the portable teleporting device I installed into my machine in case of an emergency and went home. I could only take the most important research documents with me and had to leave most of my equipment in the cave. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_16": "Of course I also left my final notes with the coordinates there. And for the life of me I cannot remember where I dug that stupid hole. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_17": "When I arrived at home I immediately started looking for a way to manoeuvre in these chaotic conditions once I rediscovered the lost entrance. I never remembered it, but it seems you found it as you indeed have my original notes. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_18": "Oh and just in case you want to complete what I have started - feel free to do so. Up to it?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_19": "Ah, the machine you found at that island. Well, I built this thing to venture far beneath the very soil we walk on. I suspected something there. Something deep down below. Something evil. Even more so than the dreaded bugs which are crawling my study. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_20": "Drilling hole after hole only to get stuck in another hard, unbreakable sediment again and again, I was about to quit this pointless enterprise. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_21": "However, the very last day I lingered on that island, I finally fell into a large hollow right under the beach. My drill was shattered and the machine was not mobile anymore. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_22": "I am well aware that this may sound laughable now - at this part all of my colleagues burst into laughter anyway - but suddenly there were stairs. Incredibly large stairs that led to the underworld. A world deep under the sea - can you believe this?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_23": "Well you know Jack - after all you talked to him in person. He will get over it. As for the real Jack, my former intern... I am glad that nothing serious happened to him. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_24": "According to his letter, he did just fine so many years ago. He somehow managed to make a name of himself when he cast some magic we enhanced through our research - of course no one back then had ever seen such spells. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_25": "Oh and he sends his regards to... how did he put it - 'whoever is currently helping me getting out of whatever mess I am currently in'. I... don't really know how this was meant but I guess this is directed at... you!",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_26": "Success!! Now it will be far easier to convince him of his true self! Excellent work. Now the only thing left to do is to separate him from whatever still binds him to that place. Did he develop any habits perhaps? ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_27": "A hobby or something! Yes, ask him about his hobbies! Convince him somehow that anything he is doing there does not match his true self - he didn't have any hobbies except a healthy interest in science - you MUST convince him, no matter what! ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_28": "Or everything we achieved would be in vain. We can still save Jack! Now go and do what you must do.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_29": "Alright listen. As long as his social environment accepts him as the person he is now, he will never come free from the shackles that bind him to this alternate self. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_30": "Oh, he has a sister you say? And his mother is living with them? ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_31": "Hm... that's strange, I don't even recall his family. Never knew he had a mother and a sister. Tell them the truth about him - maybe they will understand and even help him getting this over with. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_32": "But be careful, the {dimensional} shift could mean that they will not even know what you're talking about since they are more closely linked to him than anyone else.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_33": "A trigger is needed to make him recall what happened. First thing should be to change his environment to be more... familiar. As soon as he will have the things he used to have around him, his memories will come back. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_34": "I know that he used to have a very comfy red cushioned chair and an old globe which sat near the middle of the room. He also used a smaller telescope and he had that extremely large amphora in a corner. And... there was one other thing. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_35": "A rocking horse. He just loved it! Find these items, buy them if you need to and place them where {Jack} lives. Ask him about the furniture and don't forget to tell me about his reaction!",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_36": "Thank you. So here we are - now how to get {Jack} back to our {dimension}? Well, the answer to that is easy. It is simply not possible. All my tests concerning the reversal of the process failed. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_37": "But {Jack} is not yet lost to us - if we can get him back to his former self! You have to tell him about his former life, convince him, change his environment. But at first you will need to talk to him and find out who exactly we are dealing with now. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_38": "I will mark his current location on your map, just ask him about me and see what happens - good luck.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_39": "You know, in some way you remind me of {Jack}. Well, I am glad you are up to this task - we just have to get him back. I owe that to him and I owe it to science. Alright, now let me explain that whole {dimensional} problem. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_40": "The bad news is, using the device at that state was not a good idea. We effectively caused a magical distortion in the fabric of time, space and thus folded infinity - just a little. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_41": "The good news is that {Jack} is still on our world, and not even inconveniently far away. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_42": "Unfortunately in the current state of time, he was never interested in attending Edron Academy, he never looked for a job to finance his studies and of course has never been one of my interns. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_43": "Since he was in the magic sphere during the launch, the time fold only affected his own {dimensional} anchoring. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_44": "The number of parallel {dimensions} is endless and the fold made him slip into one completely different course of time where he never was the person I once knew. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_45": "Now you know it all. Still want to help?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_46": "Very well, hmmm, but this one might get a bit - unpleasant. What? No no, not for you. Probably only for the person I want you to help me with. You know, I once had an {intern}. His name was {Jack}. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_47": "He was as eager as you to help me - quite a nice person, really. At the time he was still around I was working on a device to transport its user to any specified point in time - be it back or to the future if you know what I mean. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_48": "He was helping me quite a lot, no matter which task I applied to him. And one day we finally did it, our tempus machina was up and running. He was certainly all man of action when he actually stepped into the machine for our first run. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_49": "The device was designed for one person with enough room for some provisions and one or two books for reading if one would land in some drab solitude. You never know, you know? So we fired it up and yes, it actually worked! ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_50": "He completely disappeared right before my eyes! Eureka! Well ahem, there was but one tiny little problem. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_51": "As all magical calibration was done from my lab I never thought about adding some sort of control to its interior. In other words {Jack} has travelled in time, without any means to come back. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_52": "Sleepless days of intensive research, however, brought me to the conclusion that he was not actually travelling to the future, but to another {dimension}, {parallel} to ours. There is still a chance to rescue him - and you can help me. What do you say?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_53": "I recently teamed up with a fellow scientist and friend Sinclair, who is also more of an explorer than me, to combine our discoveries in the field of complex phenomena not that easily to describe just by today's state of magic. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_54": "Of course I am talking about ghosts. I know, I know. Hard to believe in those times of highly advanced magic we live in. Yet there are some things, we fail to explain. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_55": "And that is exactly where we come in! Oh, and you of course. We will not only explain them - we will ''remove'' them. Just tell me whenever you are ready to help us with our research.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_56": "Alright. Let's see - yes. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_57": "Three: You can explain at least three of the following terms, infestations, collective apparitions, ectoplasmic segregations, ecto-magical field phenomena, neuro-speculative sub-conscious awareness of spirits, ghosts and/or ghasts.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_58": "Ah yes, slowly, carefully, careful ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_59": "...and how shiny it is, almost there ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_60": "...now wh- no, NO, NOOO! It just ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_61": "...slipped. And cracked. Don't look at me like that ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_62": "...I need some time to get over this. What? Oh, yes you can take the remains if you like. Just get it out of my sight.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_63": "A debacle, catastrophe, disaster - I need time to fully understand what chance just slipped through our hands here... hm? Oh yes, yes through my hands, my hands of course. Now would you please leave me alone?!",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_64": "Alright, now listen. West of Edron, near the ocean, you'll find the Lost Mines. Go down there to recover one of its rare crystals. But beware, people say the mine workers who died there years ago in an horrible accident are still digging. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_65": "I will mark the location of the mines on your map. Be careful when entering these muddy depths and don't forget that you will need a pick to gather the crystals.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_66": "That's the spirit! As time is of the essence, we should start right now. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_67": "A beggar here in Edron brags about how smart he is and that he knows about a man who lost his sanity because of an experiment, but he won't tell anyone any details. Maybe he knows more.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_68": "Oh you are back already. Hm... I doubt it worked, did it? It DID? Oh well... good job. Really! Now... the thing is - the actual {Jack} wrote. No, no wait. Calm down first. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_69": "You remember me explaining the fold in time, causing a tiny disturbance in infinity? Well, as I already told you, {Jack} was indeed not transported to the future... but to the past. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_70": "I received some kind of letter this morning that has been stored for me by the Academy for about 70 years now. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_71": "It said it should be opened at a specific day 20 years ago to prevent this whole incident but I wasn't even at the Academy by that time. Someone just found the letter earlier today and brought it to my attention. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_72": "So our {Jack} here was in fact... a completely different person. Now, now... don't get upset, there was no chance for me to warn you earlier! ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_73": "And it wasn't all that bad, was it? Heh... I mean... everyone needs a change in life now and then! And he can still come here if he likes to! ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_74": "Or wait - erm... better not tell him where exactly I live, I have some kind of presentiment concerning that whole affair... yes, we should just leave everything as it is now, indeed we should. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_75": "Anyway you did a great job and I thank you for... putting your hands into my fire Player... once again.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_76": "Did you find a rare crystal? Show me... Amazing, absolutely amazing. This crystal alone is worth a small fortune. Ahem, of course I'm glad you brought it to me for further research instead of bringing it to a merchant. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_77": "Please return here if you want to continue helping me with another mission.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_78": "Alright, now that we have enough results, the analysing can start. While I do this, I will need you to test the magically enhanced cage Sinclair developed to contain spirits effectively. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_79": "Take the spirit cage from him and use it on the essence of a common ghost. Its essence will then be sucked into the cage and we can study him right here in the safety of the academy walls.",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_80": "I fine-tuned another set of devices. You are the lucky candidate to first lay eyes on some revolutionary new concepts. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_81": "Are you ready to help science once again?",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_82": "Alright. Let's go. At first we need to find out more about ghosts in general. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_83": "I still need more information and values to properly calibrate the magical orientation of orange and turquoise sparkle attractors which we will need to actually contain ghost-emissions. ...",
  "npc.spectulus.multi_84": "So are you in?",
  "npc.corym_footman.multi_1": "What we get to eat is really ridiculous. Particularly in view of the fact that we should dig up an insane amount of ores.",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_1": "You will have to leave the plant through the eastern door on the lowest level. I have arranged for it to be 'accidentally' open. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_2": "As in the past, our enemy still uses a series of machines to open the way to the next section of his lair. You have to turn them all on to proceed. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_3": "They will only work for a certain amount of time though, so you will have to hurry or some of the machines will turn inactive again.",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_4": "While it's buried, it only uses his tentacles to attack. If one is destroyed it will simply use another set of tentacles and its supply seems endless. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_5": "If you manage though to kill all the tentacles it is using within a few heartbeats, it will become confused by its momentary helplessness and will probably attack with its main body. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_6": "That is when you have a chance to destroy it. Pass through its chamber and look for another of my tubes to contact me. Please hurry! End of communication.",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_7": "It's a fearsome subterranean beast like nothing I've ever encountered. It is dangerous and almost unbeatable because its main body is hidden beneath the ground ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_8": "And it has an endless supply of tentacles. But not all is lost, as I have devised a {plan} to battle the beast.",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_9": "His allies are an enigma even to me. It seems they belong to some unknown race that lives deep under the earth. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_10": "They seem to have supplied him with resources and workforce and a powerful {guardian} to prevent anyone from entering the passages to his lair.",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_11": "He is an old enemy of the city and I've battled him often in the past. ...",
  "npc.strange_pipe3.multi_12": "Now he has returned for vengeance, he reclaimed an old abandoned underground {laboratory} and he has acquired new powerful {allies}.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_1": "SAETHELON TORILUN GARNUM. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_2": "SLEEP. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_3": "GAIN. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_4": "RISE. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_5": "The transfer was successful. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_6": "You are now prepared to enter the realm of the evildoer. I am grateful for your help, wayfarer. Should you seek my council, use this charm I cede to you. For my spirit will guide you wherever you are. May you enjoy a sheltered future, you shall prevail.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_7": "Aaaah... free at last. Hmmm. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_8": "I assume you need to get through the gate to reach the evildoer. I can help you if you trust me, wayfarer. I will share a part of my mind with you which should enable you to step through the gate. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_9": "This procedure may be exhausting. Are you prepared to receive my key?",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_10": "With your eyes covered and avoiding direct sight of the rays, you put the mirror into the stand. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_11": "Instinctively you run to a larger emerald bluff near the raise to find cover. Mere seconds after you claimed the sturdy shelter, a deep dark humming starts to swirl through the air. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_12": "Seconds pass as the hum gets louder. The noise is maddening, drowning all other sounds around you. As you cover your ears in pain, the humming explodes into a deafening growl. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_13": "You raise your head above the edge of the emerald to catch a glimpse of what's happening. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_14": "The hand seems to have grown into a fist. In the distance you can now see a blurry scheme of a creature too large for your eyes to get a sharper view of its head. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_15": "Blending the rays, the mirror directs pure white light directly towards the part where you assume the face of the creature. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_16": "The growl transforms into a scream, everything around you seems to compress. As you press yourself tightly against the bluff, everything falls silent and in a split second, the dark being dissolves into bursts of blackness. You wake.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_17": "You lunge out and throw the model far into the water. As nothing happens, you turn your back to the ocean. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_18": "The very moment you walk down the dune to head back south, rays of light burst over your head in a shock wave that makes you tumble down the rest of the hill. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_19": "As your eyes adjust to the sudden reduction of brightness, you see the giant wings of the gate before you move to the side. You can also make out something shiny on the ground.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_20": "You pick the mirror from the ground.",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_21": "Dragon dreams are golden. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_22": "A broad darkness surrounds you as if a heavy curtain is closing before your eyes. After what seems like minutes of floating through emptiness, you get the feeling as if a hole opens in the dark before you. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_23": "The hole grows larger, you cannot close your eyes. An unimaginable black. Deeper and darker than any nothingness you could possibly imagine drags you into it. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_24": "You feel as if you cannot breathe anymore. The very second you let loose of your consciousness, you sense all heaviness around you lifted. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_25": "You dive into an ocean of emerald light. Feeling like born anew the colour around you is almost overwhelming. Countless objects of all shapes and sizes are dashing past you. Racing against each other, millions are clashing in the distance. ..",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_26": "The loudness of the gargantuan spectacle around you bursts your hearing, yet you absorb all the sounds around you. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_27": "As several large obstacles move aside directly in front of you, an intense bright centre leaps into your view. Though you cannot perceive how fast you are, your pace seems too slow. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_28": "Ever decelerating, you ultimately approach a middle in this chaos of tones of green. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_29": "As you come closer to it, yellowish shades of orange embrace you, softer shapes emerge and you almost forget the mayhem before. In warm comfort you see what lies in the heart of it all. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_30": "A majestic dragon in his sleep is surrounded by what seems the warmth and energy of a thousand suns. The tranquillity of its sight makes you smile gently. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_31": "You feel a perfect mixture of joy, compassion and sudden peacefulness. Bright xanthous impressions of topaz, orange and white welcome you at the final halt of your journey. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_32": "Dragon dreams are golden. ...",
  "npc.a_sleeping_dragon.multi_33": "You find yourself inside the dragon's dream. You can {look} around or {go} into a specific direction. You can also {take} or {use} an object. Enter {help} to display this information at any time.",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.multi_1": "Excellent! Now, let me explain. If you donate 1.000.000.000 gold pieces, you will be entitled to wear a unique outfit. ...",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.multi_2": "You will be entitled to wear the {armor} for 500.000.000 gold pieces, {helmet} for an additional 250.000.000 and the {boots} for another 250.000.000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.emperor_kruzak.multi_3": "What will it be?",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_1": "You have failed the test with ",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_2": " of 112 possible points. You probably were just too nervous. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_3": "I suggest you relax a bit with a fresh mushroom beer and we'll start over after that. Gnominus sells some beer. You should find him somewhere in the central chamber.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_4": "On a military campaign what piece of equipment would you need most? ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_5": "Is it {A}) some tasty mushroom beer to keep the morale high. {B}) A large backpack to carry all the loot. {C}) A mighty weapon to vanquish the foes. {D}) Mushroom earplugs to be spared of the cries of agony of your opponents?",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_6": "If your mushroom patch is infested with cave worms, would you {A}) place some green light crystals to drive them away. {B}) place some disharmonic crystals to drive them away. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_7": "{C}) burn everything down. {D}) switch your diet to cave worms.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_8": "What is a pollyfluxed quantumresonator? {A}) Something funny. {B}) Something important. {C}) Something to be destroyed. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_9": "{D}) Sadly I am not a gnome and lack the intelligence and education to know about even the simplest of gnomish inventions.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_10": "How many bigfoot does it take to change a light crystal? {A}) Only one since it's a piece of mushroom cake. {B}) Light crystals are delicate products of gnomish science and should only be handled by certified gnomish experts. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_11": "{C}) Three. One to hold the crystal and two to turn him around. {D}) Five. A light crystal turner, a light crystal picker, a light crystal exchanger, a light crystal changing manager and finally a light crystal changing manager assistant.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_12": "Now imagine you were given the order to guard a valuable and unique mushroom. You guard it for days and no one shows up to release you and you grow hungry. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_13": "Would you {A}) eat your boots. {B}) eat the mushroom. {C}) eat a bit of the mushroom. {D}) stick to your duty and continue starving.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_14": "Imagine you were participating in a gnome-throwing competition. Would you {A}) do some physical calculations in advance to increase your chances of winning. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_15": "{B}) throw the gnome as safely as you can to ensure his safety. {C}) Sabotage the throwing gnomes of your competitors. {D}) Never participate in such an abominable competition.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_16": "Now let us assume you see a gnome in danger. Would you {A}) not care because you must be imagining things. {B}) Save the gnome despite all odds and risk to your own life. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_17": "{C}) Inspire the gnome by singing the gnomish national anthem. {D}) Hide and loot his corpse if he dies.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_18": "Imagine you wake up one morning and discover you have forgotten how to knot your shoelaces. Would you {A}) admit defeat and go to bed once more. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_19": "{B}) look for a gnome that can remind you how to do it. {C}) Despite the risk of injuring yourself, try to figure it out on your own. {D}) Use some pottery instead of shoes.",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_20": "Imagine, during your travels you come upon a rare and unknown mushroom. Would you {A}) note down its specifics and location and look for a gnome to take care of it. ...",
  "npc.gnomerik.multi_21": "Or would you {B}) smash it to an unrecognisable pulp. Or would you {C}) pluck it to take it with you for further examination. Or would you {D}) try to become friends with the mushroom by singing questionable bar-room songs?",
  "npc.willard.multi_1": "Oooh, damn, I completely forgot about that. I was supposed to pick it up from the Outlaw Camp. ...",
  "npc.willard.multi_2": "I can't leave my shop here right now, please go and talk to Snake Eye about that package... I promise he won't make any trouble. ...",
  "npc.willard.multi_3": "Don't tell Rashid! I really don't want him to know that I forgot his order. Okay?",
  "npc.nah_bob.multi_1": "Hahahaha! ...",
  "npc.nah_bob.multi_2": "|PLAYERNAME|, that almost sounded like the word of greeting. Humans - cute they are!",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_1": "With all their powers and vast magic knowledge they are still more pawns than anything else. Given their resources, ascension might seem within reach. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_2": "The absence of any ascendant demon might prove that they are no true beings at all and literally damned to be stuck in their accursed forms.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_3": "The elves are like lost children. Their potential might be great, but they lack focus and dedication to truly improve. If their myths are true, some of the more early elves might have accomplished ascension. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_4": "Yet even if hints strongly suggest those stories are true, the sheer inaction of those assumedly ascended beings is disturbing. Perhaps what those legendary elves achieved was something completely different.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_5": "The dwarves are leftovers from a time long gone by. They have outlived their usefulness to the gods and seem to have come to terms with that. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_6": "They are as unchanging as rock and no greatness awaits them any more. They missed their chance, if they ever had any.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_7": "Although already powerful in his own right, it is obvious that his ultimate goal seems to be the ascension to godly powers. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_8": "His whole existence seems to be centred on becoming a name that strikes fear into the heart of men and to become a persistent figure in the minds of humanity. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_9": "This gives him a hold in reality and a kind of mould to fill with his power and conscience. It's also obvious that this kind of belief of the people alone won't be enough to empower him sufficiently. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_10": "Therefore he has to tap into other, probably even more sinister power sources. I can't tell what these sources are, but my scrying revealed that he has reached massive amounts of power. He has probably been infusing himself since years. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_11": "By now he is apparently reaching the end circle of his ascension and could make his final move any day.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_12": "Ascension is a fascinating topic that dates back to efforts and philosophies of some of the most ancient, and mostly extinct, races which fought in the godwars. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_13": "Probably born out of desperation, they extensively researched ways to acquire godhood themselves. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_14": "Some of them at least even met with moderate success. But the process is complicated at best, and may vary from race to race or even from one individual to another. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_15": "The theories differ vastly and waxed and waned in popularity over the centuries if not aeons. Even today and in human society there are a number of obscure ascension cults. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_16": "Some of them claim that humans are most suitable for ascension because they already own a bit of divinity through Banor's godly spark.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_17": "It is a place, so to say, not completely of this world. It is separate of, yet strongly connected to, our own world. I would imagine it is quite limited in size and its laws of physics and magic should be roughly the same as ours. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_18": "Being home to a host of demons for a while, I expect it to be a hostile and dangerous environment.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_19": "For a long time, I thought the godbreaker to be some apocryphal myth. But apparently others had learned about the godbreaker in the aeons past and lusted for its power. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_20": "They had gathered hint after hint - until, ultimately, they were squashed by the Seven or their minions; which only made the leads that hinted at them all the more probable. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_21": "What Zathroth hoped to accomplish with the creation of such a weapon can only be subject to speculation. Assumedly he already had slain Tibiasula, so the godbreaker might have been even more powerful, more absolute. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_22": "However, it has to be assumed that in the end the sheer power of his creation scared Zathroth, who had to fear the weapon could one day be used against him. So he disassembled it. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_23": "He kept the parts hidden and guarded, and if the resources can be trusted and my interpretation is right, moved them again and again, never satisfied with a hiding place. In the end he entrusted the parts to the {Ruthless Seven}. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_24": "Knowing that they would never, ever allow one of their own to come in possession of all parts. Since then, the parts have been hidden in a {demi-plane} shared by the Seven.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_25": "Well, I need 30 {demonic essences} to exchange for a passage so you can access.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_26": "My studies indicate that without all doubt Ferumbras the fiendish is in the process of accumulating nearly godlike powers. We have to stop him.",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_27": "Therefore I need you to enter a hellish dimension and acquire the parts of a weapon, the {godbreaker}, powerful enough to stop him once and for all. Are you willing to help me in this dire mission?",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_28": "He obviously had taken an interest to the topic of ascension, and I came into possession of some of his early writings. ...You have to know I'm a scholar of some renown. In the course of my latest studies about ascension, I stumbled upon disturbing facts about the person of the all too well known Ferumbras, the fiendish. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_29": "This, combined with investigation and divination, bit by bit led to the conclusion that all that Ferumbras has done in the past may be part of a cunning plan. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_30": "Considering his writings and the books he based them upon, it became clear that Ferumbras is planning his ascension to godlike status. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_31": "All of his attacks and defeats only served one purpose: to become an integral part of the people's knowledge, fears and beliefs. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_32": "He actually used this as an energy source, and combined it with some sources of power which might not all be of our own world. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_33": "He uses this energy to increasingly empower himself and will eventually be prepared to take the final step to transform himself into a godlike being. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_34": "With the knowledge what to look for, I acquired expensive but powerful artefacts to scry the world for the expected power signature - and indeed I made contact. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_35": "To my horror I had to recognise that Ferumbras had already made significant progress, and his final bid for ascension is imminent! ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_36": "His power levels are already too high for there to be any hope of stopping him with conventional means. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_37": "But not all is lost yet. During my studies about godhood, I learned that the dark Zathroth himself had created a weapon so powerful that it could actually slay a god. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_38": "Yet even he deemed this so-called '{godbreaker}' too dangerous, and split it into seven parts. These were at some point entrusted to his powerful minions, known as the Ruthless Seven. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_39": "Ancient, forbidden texts hinted at a hellish place where the seven built deadly dungeons, and placed some of their most fearsome and terrible minions as guards, before they sealed the place off. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_40": "I'm confident that I can prepare a matching ritual that will breach their protection and allow someone to enter their realm; but I'm in no way suited to handle the horrors to be encountered there. ...",
  "npc.mazarius.multi_41": "Therefore I have to ask you, if you are willing to retrieve the parts of the godbreaker, and face the threat of the ascending Ferumbras?",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_1": "Well then. Here, take the book, I added the story. Oh, just a piece of advice: Not to inflame prejudice but poachers are of rather simple disposition. I doubt they are ardent readers. ...",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_2": "So if you want to make sure they read this anytime soon, perhaps don't hide the book in a shelf or chest. Make sure to place it somewhere where they will find it easily, like very obviously on a table or something.",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_3": "Of course you do! Go hunt down the thieves and bring back the stuff they have stolen from me. ...",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_4": " I saw them running out of town and then to the north. Maybe they hide at the oasis.",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_5": "What are you talking about?? I was robbed!!!! Someone catch those filthy thieves!!!!! GUARDS! ...",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_6": "<nothing happens>....<SIGH> Like usual, they hide at the slightest sign of trouble! YOU! Want to earn some quick money?",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_7": "You need some forged documents? But I will only forge something for a friend. ...",
  "npc.ahmet.multi_8": "The nomads at the northern oasis killed someone dear to me. Go and kill at least one of them, then we talk about your document.",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.multi_1": "Hm. I see. Well, I will be frank. Every blood sacrifice has its price. Blood money will please the blood god... just as well. ...",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.multi_2": "The sum would be five million gold pieces and I... my master will be pleased. Are you prepared for a sacrifice such as this?",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.multi_3": "To enter the realm of the sanguine master and destroy its spawn, a sufficient sacrifice is imperative. ...",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.multi_4": "Find and slay the keeper of blooded tears and bring the nectar of his eyes before the blood god. Present your gift on the sacrificial altar. ...",
  "npc.bloodshade_sacrifice.multi_5": "After - and under no circumstances before - you have completed this procedure, you can enter the sacred fluid. You can, of course also take a slightly faster... {detour}.",
  "npc.corym_worker_02.multi_1": "We need weapons to overcome our situation.",
  "npc.noozer.multi_1": "Yes, yes. Or wait - why do you want to.. ah what does it matter. So you want to get through these {caves}, fine. But be warned! ...",
  "npc.noozer.multi_2": "...wait a second, I lost it. What was I going to say again? Ah yes - DANGEROUS! These. Caves. Are. Dangerous. No way you get out alive. Ever. Again. ...",
  "npc.noozer.multi_3": "Also you should not disturb those... people down there. Yeah. They... hm, wait, they - who are they again? Hey! Who are you? Are you talking to me?! Ah, ah... oh yes, I remember. ...",
  "npc.noozer.multi_4": "Wait - I am the guardian here, yes! The keeper of... something... or another, yes, I... guard this place. With my life. Don't I? Of course! ...",
  "npc.noozer.multi_5": "Is, er... this the moment where I should try to... stop you? Yes? No? Ah, you know what - you go down there, those guys are angry as dung anyway. Try your luck, return to me when you're done. If you still can. Or not.",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_1": "Our mission for you is to use a magnet on three different monoliths in the cave system here. After the magnet evaporates on the last charge, enter the magnetic extractor here to deliver your charge.",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_2": "If you are interested, I can give you some more {information} about it. Are you willing to accept this mission?",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_3": "The levels around us are... well, they are strange. We are still not entirely sure how they were created. It seems obvious that they are artificial, but they seem not to be burrowed or the like. ... ",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_4": "We found strange stone formations that were not found on other layers around the Spike, but there is no clue at all if they are as natural as they look. It seems someone used some geomantic force to move the earth. ...",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_5": "For what reason this has been done we can't tell as we found no clues of colonisation. ...",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_6": "There are theories that the caves are some kind of burrow of some extinct creature or even creatures that are still around us, but exist as some form of invisible energy; but those theories are far-fetched and not supported by any discoveries. ...",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_7": "Be that as it may, whatever those caves were meant for, these days they are crawling with creatures of different kinds and all are hostile towards us. The competition for food is great down here, and everything is seen as prey by the cave dwellers. ...",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_8": "Some would like to feast on the crystal of the Spike, others would prefer a diet of gnomes. What they have in common is that they are a threat. If we can't keep them under control their constant attacks and raids on the Spike will wear us down. ...",
  "npc.gnombold.multi_9": "That's where adventurers fit in to save the day. ",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_1": "By Uman! That's one of the rare almanacs of Origus! I had no idea that you are a scholar yourself! And a generous one on top of it! ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_2": "This book must be worth some thousand crystal coins on the free market. Look at the signature here, it's Origus' very own! ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_3": "Of course we should talk again about your request. What do you say makes Farmine important?",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_4": "There is indeed something that needs our attention. In the far north, a new city named Yalahar was discovered. It seems to be incredibly huge. ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_5": "According to travelers, it's a city of glory and wonders. We need to learn as much as we can about this city and its inhabitants. ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_6": "Gladly the explorer's society already sent a representative there. Still, we need someone to bring us the information he was able to gather until now. ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_7": "Please look for the explorer's society's captain Maximilian in Liberty Bay. Ask him for a passage to Yalahar. There visit Timothy of the explorer's society and get his research notes. ...",
  "npc.wyrdin.multi_8": "It might be a good idea to explore the city a bit on your own before you deliver the notes here, but please make sure you don't lose them.",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_1": "You have indeed. The shrines have sung back to you. Well done, brother. Not many men take such an interest in our art. ...",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_2": "I will take the flute back. Our bargain stands. You may take the scroll.",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_3": "I would have to sing to the Dark Shrines, but I cannot. ...",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_4": "I... cannot bear Urgith's breed. Everywhere, I hear them - scrabbling, squeaking ...",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_5": "Take this bone flute and play it in front of the five Dark Shrines so that they answer with song in return. You will find them in the Gardens of Night. ...",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_6": "If you have done that, you may have the scroll piece. Now go.",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_7": "The scroll piece there? The symbols look promising, but it is incomplete. ...",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_8": "It is of little use to us. But it seems to be of interest to you ...",
  "npc.elyen_ravenlock.multi_9": "In exchange for the scroll piece, you must assist me with something. {Agreed}?",
  "npc.a_restless_soul.multi_1": "I was captured and tortured to death by the cultists here. They worship a being that they call Ghazbaran ...",
  "npc.a_restless_soul.multi_2": "In his name they have claimed the mines and started to melt the ice to free an army of vile demons that have been frozen here for ages ...",
  "npc.a_restless_soul.multi_3": "Their plan is to create a new demon army for their master to conquer the world. Hjaern and the other shamans must learn about it! Hurry before its too late.",
  "npc.lynda.multi_1": "Thank you, I promise that your efforts won't be in vain! Listen closely now: First, I need a sample of five druid rods and five sorcerer wands. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_2": "I need a snakebite rod, a moonlight rod, a necrotic rod, a terra rod and a hailstorm rod. Then, I need a wand of vortex, a wand of dragonbreath ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_3": "... a wand of decay, a wand of cosmic energy and a wand of inferno. Please bring them all at once so that their energy will be balanced. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_4": "Secondly, I need 10 ounces of magic sulphur. It can absorb the elemental energy of all the wands and rods and bind it to something else. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_5": "Next, I will need a soul stone. These can be used as a vessel for energy, evil as well as good. They are rarely used nowaday though. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_6": "Lastly, I need a lot of holy energy. I can extract it from ankhs, but only a small amount each time. I will need about 20 ankhs. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_7": "Did you understand everything I told you and will help me with my blessing?",
  "npc.lynda.multi_8": "Angelina had been imprisoned? My, these are horrible news, but I am so glad to hear that she is safe now. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_9": "I will happily carry out her wish and reward you, but I fear I need some important ingredients for my blessing spell first. ...",
  "npc.lynda.multi_10": "Will you gather them for me?",
  "npc.yana.multi_1": "You have chosen ",
  "npc.yana.multi_2": ". {Basic}, {intricate} or {powerful}?",
  "npc.ikassis.multi_1": "Nature's blessings! You may find the desperate wolf mother in the south of Cormaya. You will know the place because there is a big stone that looks like a grumpy face. ...",
  "npc.ikassis.multi_2": "At night it will weep bloody tears and only at night you will meet the ghost there. Take this talisman so you may be able to talk with animals and even plants and stones. Just don't expect that all of them will answer you.",
  "npc.ikassis.multi_3": "One of my sisters, in the disguise of a nightingale, told me that Alkestios would send you. There is a problem which is not concerning me but a wolf mother on the small island Cormaya. ...",
  "npc.ikassis.multi_4": "As we, the fae, consider ourselves guardians and protectors of plants and animals, it is important for me to help this wolf. Unfortunately, I can't do it myself because at the moment I'm bound to this vessel, this snake. ...",
  "npc.ikassis.multi_5": "Thus I can't cross the ocean to reach Cormaya. Will you help me?",
  "npc.bloodshade_rotten.multi_1": "First you must fight the two pairs of evil twins that lurk in the realm beyond here. ...",
  "npc.bloodshade_rotten.multi_2": "Only when you are victorious over all four of them, your path to the source of vileness, the path to Bakragore will be opened. ...",
  "npc.bloodshade_rotten.multi_3": "And even this victory will only be the beginning.",
  "npc.ishina.multi_1": "Listen, um... I have been wanting a comb for a long time... not just any comb, but a mermaid's comb. Having a mermaid's comb means never having split ends again! ...",
  "npc.ishina.multi_2": "You know what that means to a girl! Could you please bring me such a comb? I really would appreciate it.",
  "npc.elane.multi_1": "Alright, I will give you a chance. Pay close attention to what I'm going to tell you now. ...",
  "npc.elane.multi_2": "Recently, one of our members moved to Liberty Bay out of nowhere, talking about some strange cult. That is not the problem, but he took my favourite crossbow with him. ...",
  "npc.elane.multi_3": "Please find my crossbow. It has my name engraved on it and is very special to me. ...",
  "npc.elane.multi_4": "Secondly, we need a lot of leather for new quivers. 100 pieces of lizard leather and 100 pieces of red dragon leather should suffice. ...",
  "npc.elane.multi_5": "Third, since we are giving out tiaras, we are always in need of enchanted chicken wings. Please bring me 5, that would help us tremendously. ...",
  "npc.elane.multi_6": "Lastly, for our arrow heads we need a lot of steel. Best would be one piece of royal steel, one piece of draconian steel and one piece of hell steel. ...",
  "npc.elane.multi_7": "Did you understand everything I told you and are willing to handle this task?",
  "npc.king_tibianus.multi_1": "Excellent! Now, let me explain. If you donate 1.000.000.000 gold pieces, you will be entitled to wear a unique outfit. ...",
  "npc.king_tibianus.multi_2": "You will be entitled to wear the {armor} for 500.000.000 gold pieces, {helmet} for an additional 250.000.000 and the {boots} for another 250.000.000 gold pieces. ...",
  "npc.king_tibianus.multi_3": "What will it be?",
  "npc.ulala.multi_1": "Uzroth very easy to anger. You been great help so far but me think that need to pray to Uzroth meself. Only me understand what he wants at time and he is veeeeeery moody. Cannot risk to make angry! ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_2": "So me will do when you gone. But me thank you very much. Go speak Lazaran and tell the gods are pleased now.",
  "npc.ulala.multi_3": "We need make sure Fasuon is on our side. There is laaaaaaaarge crystal on top of mountain. Don't know where come from, was there before us. Problem is - way is infested with creatures! ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_4": "Creatures from the other side of mountain. Bony! Scary! We too weak to go through there, can just run and hope to survive.. but you do better! ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_5": "Please find great crystal of Fasuon and pray there for his support!",
  "npc.ulala.multi_6": "You born dancer! Krunus is pleased and support the great hunt. But he easy to please! Pandor much harder. We weak, so he sad about us. ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_7": "Maybe we can please with sacrifice of body parts of our enemies. But you need help us get it! We much too weak. ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_8": "If you bring us 5 teeth of green men, 5 skin of horned ones and 5 skin of snakemen that already be good. Please help tribe make Pandor happy!",
  "npc.ulala.multi_9": "The great hunt! About to begin, but gods are not in favour of us yet. We need all help we get. We please Krunus with special nature dance. ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_10": "You seen Krunus altar south in camp, on mountain top? This is where dance is. If you do right steps Krunus will give you sign. If wrong, he not pleased. ...",
  "npc.ulala.multi_11": "Do Krunus dance for us! Step and dance and turn around! You will know when you do good. Make {Krunus} happy and support our great hunt!",
  "npc.tarun.multi_1": "So, he is dead as I feared. I warned him not to go with this woman, but he gave in to temptation. My heart darkens and moans. But you have my sincere thanks. ...",
  "npc.tarun.multi_2": "Without your help I would have stayed in the dark about his fate. Please, take this as a little recompense.",
  "npc.tarun.multi_3": "My brother is missing. I fear, he went to this evil palace north of here. A place of great beauty, certainly filled with riches and luxury. But in truth it is a threshold to hell and demonesses are after his blood. ...",
  "npc.tarun.multi_4": "He is my brother, and I am deeply ashamed to admit but I don't dare to go there. Perhaps your heart is more courageous than mine. Would you go to see this place and search for my brother?",
  "npc.gerimor.multi_1": "You have done our world a great favour and reason enough to be proud of yourself. ...",
  "npc.gerimor.multi_2": "Although we could not rout out each and every cult and they will soon find another source to fuel their evil, we have dealt the enemy a vital blow that will take time and resources to recouperate from. ...",
  "npc.gerimor.multi_3": "You have undoubtedly bought your world some valuable time and weakened the enemy. Take my thanks in behalf of the world and keep up your heroic work. For your reward you must have two free slots. Are you ready to receive it?",
  "npc.gerimor.multi_4": "Your actions have weakened the worldly anchors of the enemy and unveiled the source they use to strengthen their cults. ...",
  "npc.gerimor.multi_5": "Our circle has used this opportunity to breach their protective shroud and aim a teleporter to this source. I would like to ask you to use it, to travel to this source and destroy it. ...",
  "npc.gerimor.multi_6": "But be warned, you will need a group twice as great compared to those with which you defeated the cults. Go now, with my blessings.",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_1": "A thousand thanks in advance. I need no less than 7 ingredients for the cure. You can ask me about each specifically ...",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_2": "I need a part of the sun adorer cactus, a vial of geyser water, sulphur of a lava hole, a frostbite herb, a blossom of a purple kiss, a hydra tongue and spores of a giant glimmercap mushroom ...",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_3": "Turn them in individually by talking about them to me. As soon as I obtained them all, talk to me about the medicine. First time bring a Part of the Sun Adorer {Cactus}.",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_4": "You will need a specially prepared waterskin to collect the water. You can buy one from me ...",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_5": "Use it on a geyser that is NOT active. The water of active geysers is far too hot. You can find inactive geysers on Okolnir. Do you have some geyser water with you?",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_6": "Thank you. Now I have all necessary ingredients. As a reward I grant you the use of our dog sled, which is located to the east of here. ...",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_7": "The dogs can be a bit moody, but if you always carry some ham with you there shouldnt be any problems. Oh, and Hjaern might have a mission for you. So maybe you go and talk to him.",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_8": "I am in dire need of help. A plague has befallen my dogs. I even called a druid of Carlin for help but all he could do was to recommend some strong medicine ...",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_9": "The thing is the ingredients of the medicine are extremely rare and some only exist in far away and distant lands. If you could help me collecting the ingredients, I would be eternally grateful ...",
  "npc.nilsor.multi_10": "Are you willing to help me?",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_1": "Alright, I guess you need a stake first. Maybe Gamon can help you, the leg of a chair or something could just do. Try asking him for a stake, and if you have one, bring it back to me.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_2": "I guess you couldn't convince Gamon to give you a stake, eh?",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_3": "Yes, I was informed what to do. Are you prepared to receive my line of the prayer?",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_4": "So receive my prayer: 'Light shall be near - and darkness afar'. Now, bring your stake to Tibra in the Carlin church for the next line of the prayer. I will inform her what to do.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_5": "I will wait for you.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_6": "You should visit Tibra in the Carlin church now.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_7": "You already received my line of the prayer.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_8": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_9": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_10": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_11": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_12": "No problem.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_13": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_14": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_15": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_16": "No problem.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_17": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_18": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_19": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_20": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_21": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_22": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_23": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_24": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_25": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_26": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_27": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_28": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_29": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.ninev.stdmod_30": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_1": "Well, I sell freshly caught fish. You like some? Of course, you can buy more than one at once. *grin* Just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_2": "Well, I sell freshly caught fish. You like some? Of course, you can buy more than one at once. *grin* Just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_3": "Well, I sell freshly caught fish. You like some? Of course, you can buy more than one at once. *grin* Just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_4": "My name is Bruno.",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_5": "My job is to catch fish and to sell them here.",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_6": "Ah yes, my lovely wife. God forgive her, but she can't stop talking. So my work is a great rest for my poor ears. *laughs loudly*",
  "npc.bruno.stdmod_7": "I like this old salt. I learned much from him. Whatever. You like some fish? *grin*",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_3": "Ah, you may not have heard of me. I am Captain Gulliver, the first Oramondian for a hundred years to have sailed through the mist to your strange lands.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_4": "I am the captain of the 'Sea Goddess', the splendid and beautiful ship you see over there.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_5": "I am the captain of the 'Sea Goddess', the splendid and beautiful ship you see over there.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_6": "The 'Sea Goddess' is the most beautiful in Oramond, a whole new model of ship, elegant, sure and swift. There's no weather she can't take!",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_7": "Ah, your lands are quite a sight! I have only visited Thais so far, but I think of navigating to more cities, when the time - and public demand - comes.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_8": "I will gladly take on board everything you wish to transport. No pets, though.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_9": "<bows> I would be delighted to have you on board.",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_10": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_11": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_12": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_13": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_14": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_15": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_16": "You would like to book a passage for {Thais} or {Krailos}?",
  "npc.captain_gulliver.stdmod_17": "This is the only safe landing place on Oramond. The cliffs surrounding the isle are too dangerous, you see.",
  "npc.archery.stdmod_1": "I am the owner of this saloon. I call it Archery's Hut. I am also {selling} ammunitions.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_1": "Time doesn't matter to me.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_2": "I'm Hyacinth.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_3": "I'm a {druid} and healer, a follower of {Crunor}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_4": "May Crunor bless you and protect you on your journeys!",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_5": "There are only two other druids on Rookgaard, {Lily} and {Cipfried}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_6": "Storage for worldly wealth.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_7": "Who knows what it will be? Only time will show.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_8": "Thank the gods, I'm fine.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_9": "What help do you seek? I sell health potions, ask me for a {trade} if you need one.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_10": "I can't teach you magic. On the {mainland} you will learn spells early enough.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_11": "I'm one of the few magic users on this isle. I can sense a follower of the dark path of magic hiding somewhere in the depths of the dungeons.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_12": "It is shaped by the will of the gods, so we don't have to question it.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_13": "I used to be there with my old friend Cipfried to heal adventurers. After all these years, I prefer solitude now.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_14": "Teaching you about the gods would require too much time. But you can always read the books in the {library}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_15": "The library is in the {academy}, north of the {temple}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_16": "A place to learn about {Tibia}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_17": "Are you hungry? I'm sorry, I have no food here.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_18": "Yes, I sell small health potions. Ask me for a trade if you need one.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_19": "I don't care about kings, queens, and the like.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_20": "I rarely visit the town. It's much better here.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_21": "There's a huge world waiting for you.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_22": "Most of the so-called monsters of this isle are only creatures of the gods. There are some beasts that are truly monstrous on the {mainland}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_23": "Are you hungry? I'm sorry, I have no food here.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_24": "The dungeons are dangerous for inexperienced adventurers.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_25": "Just ask me for a {trade} to check out my offers. I have only small health potions for sale, though.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_26": "You'll have to buy that from the merchants in town. I'm just a simple druid and healer.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_27": "I'll pay you 5 gold for every empty vial and potion flask. Just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_28": "A greedy and annoying person just like most people are.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_29": "Now she has completely gotten out of her mind.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_30": "He was a promising young druid when something happened to his mind. It's a sad story.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_31": "He does a good job out there.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_32": "I know her since she was little.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_33": "One of these greedy merchants.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_34": "I saw her stranding with her raft.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_35": "He's a farmer and behaves a little better than his cousin.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_36": "An unpleasant person.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_37": "His healing powers equal mine.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_38": "I think she's under bad influence.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_39": "That's my name.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_40": "She's actually quite nice.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_41": "She's a druid. Since she started selling health potions, people visit me only rarely. Which is a good thing, but of course I'll help if I'm needed.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_42": "The oracle will lead you to your {destiny} once you are level 8.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_43": "I think that guy is new. He's a {bank} clerk.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_44": "He has some inner devils that torture him.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_45": "Tom is the local tanner. That means he always needs fresh corpses or leather.",
  "npc.hyacinth.stdmod_46": "A man of the sword.",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a passage to Thais for |TRAVELCOST|?",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_2": "By direct edict of the honorable Henricus himself... well, you know.",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_3": "I can bring you back to {Thais} if you are weary or you can stay and fight. What shall it be?",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_4": "My name is Chelop and I am a captain of this {inquisition} ship.",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_5": "Can't you see? I'm captain of the Pesadilla, the proud {inquisition} ship which anchors here.",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_6": "By edict of the honorable Henricus himself, we are ordered to give passage to all recruits of the Roshamuul mission for a small fee.",
  "npc.captain_chelop.stdmod_7": "This is the island you are currently on, just in case you forgot.",
  "npc.nina.stdmod_1": "The lizards here are the chosen ones of their kind. We believe them to be the strongest warriors in these lands.So I lead my people here to learn their ways. We are mere assassins but they are using foreign techniques and seem to be far more efficient",
  "npc.nina.stdmod_2": "We of the Grey Shadow clan are studying the ways of the Chosen. Our training is hard, encounters with the lizards often deadly. Every one of us fights on his own. Each one more deadly than the other. Under my lead we wil rise renewed, as the Shadow Nina.",
  "npc.nina.stdmod_3": "I am Nina, leader of the Grey Shadow clan. Me and my followers, the Shadow Nina, are exploring the largely uncharted parts of the continent Zao.",
  "npc.cornell.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.cornell.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.cornell.stdmod_3": "I can travel you to {Grimvale} or {Edron}.",
  "npc.captain_cookie.stdmod_1": "I can bring you to our base in Liberty Bay for |TRAVELCOST|. Is that what you want?",
  "npc.captain_cookie.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.captain_cookie.stdmod_3": "I can take you to {Liberty Bay}.",
  "npc.captain_cookie.stdmod_4": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.captain_cookie.stdmod_5": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.captain_cookie.stdmod_6": "I travelled here, hoping to find the cockaigne. Imagine my disappointment when I discovered I was wrong.",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_1": "I'm sorry but I don't sail there.",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_2": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_3": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_4": "My boat is ready to bring you to {Venore}, {Port Hope}, {Liberty Bay}, {Yalahar}, {Gray Island}, {Ankrahmun}, {Krailos} or {Issavi}. Or to {Travora} - a place between the worlds.",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_5": "I am the captain of this ship.",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_6": "Where do you want to go - {Krailos}, {Venore}, {Port Hope}, {Liberty Bay}, {Ankrahmun}, {Yalahar} or {Gray Island}?",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_7": "That's where we are.",
  "npc.petros.stdmod_8": "It's Petros.",
  "npc.tonar.stdmod_1": "You are not ready yet.",
  "npc.tonar.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_1": "Never heard about a place like this.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_2": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_3": "I am known as Uzon Ibn Kalith.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_4": "I am a licensed Darashian carpet pilot. I can bring you to {Darashia}, {Kazordoon}, {Svargrond} or {Edron}.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_5": "The caliph welcomes travellers to his land.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_6": "The caliph welcomes travellers to his land.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_7": "Oh, there is so much to tell about Daraman. You better travel to Darama to learn about his teachings.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_8": "I would never transport this one.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_9": "So you heard about haunted Drefia? Many adventures travel there to test their skills against the undead: vampires, mummies, and ghosts.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_10": "Some people claim it is hidden somewhere under the endless sands of the devourer desert in Darama.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_11": "Thais is noisy and overcrowded. That's why I like Darashia more.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_12": "I have seen almost every place on the continent.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_13": "I could retell the tales of my travels for hours. Sadly another flight is scheduled soon.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_14": "Just another Thais but with women to lead them.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_15": "You can buy flying carpets only in Darashia.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_16": "I transport travellers to the continent of Darama for a small fee. So many want to see the wonders of the desert and learn the secrets of Darama.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_17": "I heard too many news to recall them all.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_18": "I heard too many news to recall them all.",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_19": "I can fly you to {Darashia} on Darama, {Kazordoon}, {Svargrond}, {Issavi}, {Farmine} or {Edron} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_20": "I can fly you to {Darashia} on Darama, {Kazordoon}, {Svargrond} or {Edron} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_21": "I can fly you to {Darashia} on Darama, {Kazordoon}, {Svargrond} or {Edron} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_22": "I can fly you to {Darashia} on Darama, {Kazordoon}, {Svargrond} or {Edron} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.uzon.stdmod_23": "It's 3:42 pm right now. The next flight is scheduled soon.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_1": "Just ask me for a {trade} to see what I buy from you.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_2": "Just ask me for a {trade} to see my offers.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_3": "If you need general {equipment}, just ask me for a {trade}. I can also provide you with some general {hints} about the game.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_4": "As an adventurer, you should always have at least a {backpack}, a {rope}, a {shovel}, a {weapon}, an {armor} and a {shield}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_5": "I'm fine. I'm so glad to have you here as my customer.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_6": "I'm a merchant. Just ask me for a {trade} to see my offers.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_7": "My name is Al Dee, but you can call me Al. Can I interest you in a {trade}?",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_8": "It's about |TIME|. I'm so sorry, I have no watches to sell. Do you want to buy something else?",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_9": "If you want to challenge monsters in the {dungeons}, you need some {weapons} and {armor} from the local {merchants}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_10": "If you want to explore the dungeons such as the {sewers}, you have to {equip} yourself with the vital stuff I am selling. It's {vital} in the deepest sense of the word.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_11": "Oh, our sewer system is very primitive - it's so primitive that it's overrun by {rats}. But the stuff I sell is safe from them. Just ask me for a {trade} to see it!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_12": "The king encouraged salesmen to travel here, but only I dared to take the risk, and a risk it was!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_13": "Bugs plague this isle, but my wares are bug-free, totally bug-free.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_14": "One day I will return to the continent as a rich, a very rich man!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_15": "Thais is a crowded town.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_16": "Have you ever wondered what that 'main' is people are talking about? Well, once you've reached level 8, you should talk to the {oracle}. You can choose a {profession} afterwards and explore much more of Tibia.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_17": "Oh, I'm sorry, but I don't deal with weapons. That's {Obi's} or {Lee'Delle's} business. I could offer you a {pick} in exchange for a {small axe} if you should happen to own one.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_18": "Armor and shields can be bought at {Dixi's} or at {Lee'Delle's}. Dixi runs that shop near {Obi's}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_19": "Armor and shields can be bought at {Dixi's} or at {Lee'Delle's}. Dixi runs that shop near {Obi's}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_20": "I you want to find someone who may want to buy your cookies, you should meet Lily.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_21": "Blueberries grow on bushes. They're quite common in Tibia. Just pick them from a bush if you need a snack!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_22": "Sorry, I don't sell potions. You should visit {Lily} for that.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_23": "Hmm, the best address to look for food might be {Willie} or {Billy}. {Norma} also has some snacks for sale.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_24": "A bank is quite useful. You can deposit your money safely there. This way you don't have to carry it around with you all the time. You could also invest your money in my {wares}!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_25": "The big building in the centre of Rookgaard. They have a library, a training centre, a {bank} and the room of the {oracle}. {Seymour} is the teacher there.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_26": "The monk {Cipfried} takes care of our temple. He can heal you if you're badly injured or poisoned.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_27": "As a premium adventurer you have many advantages. You really should check them out!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_28": "If you tell me the name of a citizen, I'll tell you what I know about him or her.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_29": "To view the offers of a merchant, simply talk to him or her and ask for a {trade}. They will gladly show you their offers and also the things they buy from you.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_30": "You will learn everything you need to know about professions once you've reached the {Island of Destiny}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_31": "The Island of Destiny can be reached via the {oracle} once you are level 8. This trip will help you choose your {profession}!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_32": "No thank you. I can already overstock the market with torches.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_33": "I sell fishing rods and worms if you want to fish. Simply ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_34": "Yes, I am selling that. Simply ask me for a {trade} to view all my offers.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_35": "He is just an old monk. However, he can heal you if you are badly injured or poisoned.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_36": "Poor old woman, her son {Tom} never visits her.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_37": "He dedicated his life to welcome newcomers to this island.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_38": "No idea who that is.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_39": "Yep, that's me. Smart of you to notice that!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_40": "He's the local {bank} clerk.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_41": "He mostly stays by himself. He's a hermit outside of town - good luck finding him.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_42": "She's {Obi's} granddaughter and deals with {armors} and {shields}. Her shop is south west of town, close to the {temple}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_43": "He sells {weapons}. His shop is south west of town, close to the {temple}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_44": "If you are a {premium} adventurer, you should check out {Lee'Delle's} shop. She lives in the western part of town, just across the bridge.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_45": "He's the local tanner. You could try selling fresh corpses or leather to him.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_46": "She's currently recovering from her travels in the {academy}. It's always nice to chat with her!",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_47": "You can find the oracle on the top floor of the {academy}, just above {Seymour}. Go there when you are level 8.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_48": "Seymour is a teacher running the {academy}. He has many important {information} about Tibia.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_49": "She sells health {potions} and antidote potions. Also, she buys {blueberries} and {cookies} in case you find any.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_50": "This is a local farmer. If you need fresh {food} to regain your health, it's a good place to go. However, many monsters also carry food such as meat or cheese. Or you could simply pick {blueberries}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_51": "This is a local farmer. If you need fresh {food} to regain your health, it's a good place to go. He's only trading with {premium} adventurers though.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_52": "She used to sell equipment, but I think she has opened a small bar now. Talks about changing her name to 'Mary' and such, strange girl.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_53": "Some call him a hero. He protects the town from {monsters}.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_54": "Picks are hard to come by. I trade them only in exchange for high quality small axes. Would you like to make that deal?",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_55": "Splendid! Here, take your pick.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_56": "Sorry, I am looking for a SMALL axe.",
  "npc.al_dee.stdmod_57": "Well, then don't.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_1": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_2": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_3": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_4": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_5": "No problem.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_6": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_7": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_8": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_9": "No problem.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_10": "I think you have forgotten to bring your stake, kid.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_11": "Yes, I was informed what to do. Are you prepared to receive my line of the prayer?",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_12": "So receive my prayer: 'Unclean spirits shall be repelled'. Now, bring your stake to Amanda in Edron for the next line of the prayer. I will inform her what to do.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_13": "I will wait for you.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_14": "You should visit Amanda in Edron now, kid.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_15": "You already received my line of the prayer.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_16": "A blessed stake? That's a strange request. Maybe Quentin knows more, he is one of the oldest monks after all.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_17": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_18": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_19": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_20": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_21": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_22": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_23": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_24": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_25": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_26": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_27": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_28": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_29": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.isimov.stdmod_30": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_1": "I'm sorry but I don't sail there.",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_2": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_3": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_4": "We would like to welcome you on board.",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_5": "Where do you want to go? To {Nostalgia}, {Horror Village}",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_6": "Where do you want to go? To {Nostalgia}, {Horror Village}",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_7": "Where do you want to go? To {Nostalgia}, {Horror Village}",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_8": "This is Nostalgia. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.kendra_thais.stdmod_9": "This is Horror Village. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_1": "Never heard about a place like this.",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_2": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_3": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_4": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_5": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_6": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_7": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, {Edron}, {Issavi}, {Svargrond}, {Kazordoon}, {Zao} or to {Femor Hills} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_8": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_9": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_10": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.ziyad.stdmod_11": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Svargrond}, to {Kazordoon}, to {Zao}, to the {Femor Hills}, to {Edron} or to {Issavi} if you like. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_1": "Here in the whiteflower temple you may receive the blessing of spiritual shielding. But we must ask of you to sacrifice |BLESSCOST| gold. Are you still interested?",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_2": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_3": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_4": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_5": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_6": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_7": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_8": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_9": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_10": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_11": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_12": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_13": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.norf.stdmod_14": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_1": "The Spark of the Phoenix is given by me and by the great pyromancer in the nearby fire temple. Do you wish to receive my part of the Spark of the Phoenix?",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_2": "So receive the blessing of the life-giving earth, pilgrim.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_3": "Ok. If you don't want it...",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_4": "The gods are treacherous and vain. They want to use us like they did in the past. Only the elements can be trusted, because all they want is for nature to run its set course.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_5": "I am the great geomancer of dwarvenkind.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_6": "We investigate the will of the earth. It is our duty to make sure things to work in their natural way.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_7": "Life is born by earth and fed by earth.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_8": "I am Kawill Marbleeye, Son of Earth, from the Molten Rock.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_9": "There's nothing I need, better ask others.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_10": "Nice world in general. It's a shame there is so much water ruining the general impression.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_11": "Time is not of importance.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_12": "May the earth swallow them all!",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_13": "Ah, a weapon to be feared by man, beast and god alike, jawoll. He who wields it will be both blessed and cursed at the same time.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_14": "The day will come when he finally bites the dust.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_15": "By using the powers of fire and earth we forced the river that once wound its way through the big old one in other directions, and created our home.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_16": "Bezil and Nezil have pawn and equpiment shop with an amazing stock.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_17": "Bezil and Nezil have pawn and equpiment shop with an amazing stock.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_18": "The first knight of dwarvenkind is a fine woman.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_19": "I fear the sorcerers focus on the destructive forces of fire. They forget about the protection earth could provide.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_20": "He is a jolly fellow and one of the oldest dwarves alive.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_21": "He is a fine smith and his armour may save your neck one day.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_22": "She is a fine cook, jawoll.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_23": "Uzgod is a blacksmith and understands the ways of his element well.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_24": "The emperor has rarely visited the temple district in the last years. He should care more about spirituality then about politics. Jawoll.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_25": "The emperor has rarely visited the temple district in the last years. He should care more about spirituality then about politics. Jawoll.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_26": "The celestial paladin, the protector of our race. The only divine being we care for and the only one who still cares for dwarfs.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_27": "Where earth is giving, fire is taking. That is the way of the elements.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_28": "The lifegiving earth protects us, feeds us and takes us home after death.",
  "npc.kawill.stdmod_29": "The mountain we live in is called the big old one. It's the mountain of mountains, and it isand like a friend and protector to our race.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_1": "Hmm, |PLAYERNAME|. I really don't know if you should go into the wilderness without a shield. You should earn some money by hunting rats under the village first until you can afford at least a wooden shield.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_2": "Dallheim, at your service.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_3": "I'm the guard of this bridge. I defend Rookgaard against the beasts of the {wilderness} and the {dungeons}, and even of the stinking {sewers}.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_4": "My duty is eternal. Time is of no importance.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_5": "Before you fight monsters, deposit your money there. If you die, you won't lose it if it's save in the bank.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_6": "Fine.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_7": "I have to stay here, sorry. But I can heal you if you are wounded. I have also valuable information about {monsters}.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_8": "I'm an expert concerning the wildlife and {monsters} on this island.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_9": "I'll protect all citizens alike. That is my {job} and duty.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_10": "Did you know that rats are among the most dangerous animals in whole Tibia? Each day, they kill many people who are overestimating their powers. Don't be one of them!",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_11": "There are two types of spiders on this island: normal spiders and poison spiders. As their name says, the latter ones can poison you which will cause a constant loss of your health. Beware of them!",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_12": "Once you have upgraded your starter {equipment} a little - maybe leather stuff - and got a better weapon as well as a shield, you should be able to kill trolls.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_13": "You need a stronger weapon than the starter club to kill wolves. Maybe a {sabre} or a short {sword} will do.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_14": "Orcs are a constant menace. There are even stronger species of orcs on the main continent.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_15": "Minotaurs are very strong. You will need a group of people or at least level 6 and good equipment to be able to kill them.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_16": "They are a little tougher than they look like, but they're still good beginner monsters.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_17": "The skeletons on this island are usually fairly hidden. They are often found near graves and always underground. Beware of their evil life drain.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_18": "A bear can easily kill you if you don't pay attention.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_19": "Wasps are the fastest monsters on this island and they poison you. If you ever run into one and are already low of health, fear for your life!",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_20": "Snakes can poison you, too, but their poison is usually not as dangerous as that of poison spiders. Just be careful and kill them fast.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_21": "Premium warriors pay. They gain many advantages this way.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_22": "HAIL TO THE KING!",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_23": "All that theory won't help you without some real battle practice.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_24": "A place of protection. Nothing can harm you there.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_25": "I can mark you some dungeons on your map if you ask me about {monsters} suited for your level.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_26": "The sewers are crowded with {rats}. They make fine targets for young heroes.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_27": "There are {wolves}, {bears}, {snakes}, {deer}, and {spiders} in the wilderness past this bridge.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_28": "I'm a follower of {Banor}.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_29": "The heavenly warrior! Hail to him!",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_30": "I'm not interested in such party tricks.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_31": "A nice place for a hero, but nothing for whelps.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_32": "It's my duty to protect this village and its {citizens}.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_33": "It looks like you have mastered the drill.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_34": "Sorry, I don't trade. Ask the shop owners for a trade instead.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_35": "I don't approve of her opening a bar. Those drunken adventurers stumbling over the bridge at nighttime are not especially helpful in improving the situation.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_36": "Zerbrus tells me such strange stories about him. Well, he sees him all day from the west bridge.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_37": "He dedicated his life to welcoming newcomers to this island.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_38": "Nice old lady.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_39": "He has been on this island as long as me.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_40": "I don't trust her.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_41": "He guards the temple and can heal you if you are badly injured or poisoned, just like me.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_42": "She's {Obi's} granddaughter and deals with {armors} and {shields}. Her shop is south west of town, close to the temple.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_43": "Strange fellow, hides somewhere in the mountains of the isle.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_44": "Her shop is on the {premium} side of town. Best offers around.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_45": "Sometimes I wish I had an easy job like her, selling {potions} all day.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_46": "You can find the oracle on the top floor of the {academy}, just above Seymour. Go there when you are level 8.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_47": "The local bank clerk.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_48": "Leave me alone with this wimp.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_49": "He's the local tanner. You could try selling fresh corpses or leather to him.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_50": "At your service.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_51": "He's guarding the west bridge. Not that a real threat would lurk on the other side.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_52": "He is a fine cook and farmer. He buys and sells {food}.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_53": "You are poisoned. I will help you.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_54": "You are looking really bad. Let me heal your wounds.",
  "npc.dallheim.stdmod_55": "You aren't looking really bad. Eat some food to regain strength.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_1": "Just ask me for a {trade} to see what I buy from you. If you want to sell {blueberries}, ask me about them separately.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_2": "Just ask me for a {trade} to see my offers. If you want to sell {blueberries}, ask me about them separately.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_3": "How can I help you? If you like to buy something, just ask me for a {trade}. We can also chat about {Tibia}. Or, I could give you general {hints} about the game.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_4": "You definitely need a good {weapon}, an {armor} and a {shield}. Also, you should never leave for a {dungeon} without {rope}, {shovel} and {torch}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_5": "I'm in tune with myself and with nature. Thank you.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_6": "I'm a {druid}, bound to the spirit of nature. My {potions} will help you if you feel bad. I also buy {blueberries} and {cookies}. Just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_7": "My name is Lily, like the flower. It also stands for purity, just like my {potions} are!",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_8": "It's about |TIME|. But does it really matter? Don't rush yourself and enjoy all these little moments.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_9": "It's wise to store most of your gold at the bank below the academy. It's safer that way.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_10": "If you tell me the name of a citizen, I'll tell you what I know about him or her.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_11": "Antidote potions will cure {poisoning}. They also have a lovely {blueberry} taste. You only need them when you get poisoned deep down in a dungeon, else just go to the {temple} for a free heal!",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_12": "Some creatures like snakes or poison spiders can poison you. That will diminish your health over a certain amount of time, so be careful when dealing with those creatures!",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_13": "Being a druid is a wonderful profession. You control the forces of nature and can heal others.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_14": "There are many shops around here which are owned by local {citizens}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_15": "The temple is just to the right. You can get a healing for free there if you are badly injured or poisoned.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_16": "Tibia is our beautiful world, created by the gods. Being a {druid}, I'm a worshipper of {Crunor}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_17": "Crunor is the great lord of trees and the creator of all plants. Despite what some people believe, he didn't create the {monsters}, though.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_18": "Oh, I'm sorry honey, I don't sell food. If you are hungry, visit one of the farmers {Billy} and {Willie}. I buy {blueberries} and {cookies}, though.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_19": "I can offer you homemade {antidote} potions and small {health} potions. Ask me for a {trade} if you like to see them.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_20": "Health potions will heal you for about 75 hit points. It can't hurt to carry one with you, just in case.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_21": "I think Tibia would be a better place without authorities who lead others to war. Can't we just all live in peace?",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_22": "The academy is the big stone building in the town centre. If you're ready to leave Rookgaard, go there to see the {oracle}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_23": "Well, in this village and its surroundings you can {train} your skills until you are level 8. Then you should see the {oracle} and head to the {main} continent.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_24": "To train your skills, simply help us {fighting} monsters.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_25": " If you want to fight monsters, you should get better {equipment} from the {merchants}. You should also talk to one of the bridge {guards} to find suitable monsters for you.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_26": "To view the offers of a merchant, simply talk to him or her and ask for a {trade}. They will gladly show you their offers and also the things they buy from you.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_27": "The main continent is huge! The gods of Tibia created everything from great seas, deep jungles and large deserts.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_28": "Sadly, our little village of {Rookgaard} is invaded by monsters. From the {dungeons} they creep to the surface and attack the city. We always need adventurers helping us to {fight} them.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_29": "If you are looking for weapons, you should visit {Obi}'s shop east of here. Or, if you have a {premium} account, go to {Lee'Delle} for better offers.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_30": "Armors? Best buy them at {Dixi}'s little counter, just upstairs from {Obi}'s shop. Or, if you have a {premium} account, go to {Lee'Delle} for better offers.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_31": "Shields? Best buy them at {Dixi}'s little counter, just upstairs from {Obi}'s shop. Or, if you have a {premium} account, go to {Lee'Delle} for better offers.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_32": "If you need information about the dungeons here, you should talk to one of the bridge {guards}. They will show you where to go.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_33": "Our bridge guards are {Dallheim} and {Zerbrus}. You can find Dallheim if you follow the path to the right, then turn north at the {temple}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_34": "Yum, cookies! If you have some for me, just ask me for a trade.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_35": "Earn gold by fighting {monsters} and picking up what they carry. Sell it to {merchants} to make profit!",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_36": "I will pay you 5 gold for every empty vial and potion flask. Just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_37": "You best buy such equipment at {Al Dee}'s store in the North of the village. Or, if you have a {premium} account, go to {Lee'Delle} for better offers.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_38": "Oh yes, I love cookies! Will you accept 1 gold for it?",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_39": "Fine! Here's your gold.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_40": "Sorry, you do not have one.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_41": "Oh, what a pity.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_42": "Oh, do you have blueberries for sale? I need them for my {antidote potion}. I give you 1 gold for 5 of them, yes?",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_43": "Fine! Here's your gold.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_44": "Oh, I'm sorry. I'm not buying less than 5 blueberries.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_45": "As you wish.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_46": "He sells {weapons}. His shop is east of here.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_47": "I don't know what to think about all this new bar. {Rookgaard} needs a little peace!",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_48": "He used to help me gather blueberries. Then, one day, he suddenly stopped comming here. They say he went a little out of his mind.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_49": "We tried everything to fight that cockroach plague in his cellar, but natural anti-bug potions simply won't help. I guess those roaches need to be fought with stronger weapons.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_50": "That poor old woman. I wish I could help her.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_51": "Best tool shop in town, if you ask me.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_52": "I heard that she's recovering below the academy. She has been on an exciting expedition. I haven't talked to her yet, though.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_53": "Visiting Cipfried in the {temple} is a good idea if you are injured or poisoned. He can heal you.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_54": "She's {Obi}'s granddaughter and deals with {armors} and {shields}, just upstairs from Obi's shop.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_55": "Hyacinth also sells small health potions. He lives outside the village, in a hidden place.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_56": "If you are a {premium} adventurer, you should check out {Lee'Delle's} shop. She lives in the western part of town, just across the bridge.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_57": "You can find the oracle on the top floor of the {academy}, just above {Seymour}. Go there when you are level 8 to reach more areas of {Tibia}.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_58": "He takes care of the {bank}, keeping our money safe.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_59": "Seymour is a teacher running the {academy}. He has many important {information} about Tibia.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_60": "He's the local tanner. You could try selling fresh corpses or leather to him.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_61": "He is a great warrior. He can also tell you much about {monsters} and {dungeons} on this island.",
  "npc.lily.stdmod_62": "He's a farmer and sells {food}. Food will help you regain health when you are injured. Many {monsters} also carry food with them.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_1": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_2": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_3": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_4": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_5": "No problem.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_6": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_7": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_8": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_9": "No problem.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_10": "You don't even have that strange stake with you.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_11": "Brewster sent me a strange message about some strange hocus-pocus. I think it's nonsense, but since you have come that far, I'll play along. Are you ready?",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_12": "So receive my prayer: 'Your mind shall be a vessel for joy, light and wisdom' - uh, wow, something happened. Well, I guess that's it, but next time if you need some mumbo jumbo rather go to Chondur.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_13": "You don't even have that strange stake with you.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_14": "No problem, I have other things to do.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_15": "A blessed stake? I don't believe in things like that. If anyone does, it's probably old Quentin.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_16": "I won't do that rubbish again. Go pester Chondur with your hocus-pocus.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_17": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_18": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_19": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_20": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_21": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_22": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_23": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_24": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_25": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_26": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_27": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_28": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_29": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.tyrias.stdmod_30": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_1": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_2": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_3": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_4": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_5": "No problem.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_6": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_7": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_8": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_9": "No problem.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_10": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_11": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_12": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_13": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_14": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_15": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_16": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_17": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_18": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_19": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_20": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_21": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_22": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.cedrik.stdmod_23": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_1": "My name is Lee'Delle.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_2": "I'm a merchant. If you like to see my offers, just ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_3": "It's about |TIME|.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_4": "Well, it's a good idea to leave most of your money in the bank and only take what you need. That way your gold is safe.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_5": "Oh no! I've got to watch what I eat. {Lily} loves cookies, though.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_6": "There are many merchants in this village. Just ask them for a {trade} to see their offers. But I can promise you - my offers are the best around!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_7": "I'm fine. I'm delighted to welcome you as my customer.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_8": "What kind of information do you need? I could tell you about different topics such as {equipment}, {monsters} or {Rookgaard} in general.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_9": "How can I help you? Would you like to {trade} with me? I can also give you general {hints}. Or just ask me anything you'd like to know.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_10": "You should really take some time and travel around the marvellous areas of Tibia. There's everything - ice islands, deserts, jungles and mountains!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_11": "The temple is the place to go when you are very low on {health} or poisoned. Ask {Cipfried} for a heal - he usually notices emergencies by himself.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_12": "Health potions will heal you for about 75 hit points. It can't hurt to carry one with you, just in case.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_13": "Well, very important equipment would be a {backpack}, a {rope}, a {shovel}, a {weapon}, an {armor} and a {shield}. Maybe also a torch if you're heading into a dark {dungeon}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_14": "I sell fishing rods and worms in case you want to go fishing. Simply ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_15": "You could check out which weapons I offer by asking me for a {trade}. Don't be shy!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_16": "Oh, I'm sorry, that's one of the things I don't have for sale. But {Willie} or {Billy} surely have something to eat for you.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_17": "The king supports our little village very much!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_18": "In the academy you can get a lot of information from books. You can also try out a few things by yourself.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_19": "Isn't it lovely here? You'll be surprised once you reach the {mainland} -  so much to explore!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_20": "Well, the mainland also consists of several continents. You can go there once you've reached level 8 and talked to the {oracle}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_21": "Good monsters to start with are rats. They live in the {sewers} under the village of {Rookgaard}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_22": "Just ask me for a {trade} to see what I buy from you.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_23": "Be careful down there! Make sure you bought enough {torches} and a {rope} or you might get lost.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_24": "There are many sewer entrances throughout Rookgaard. If you want to know more details about monsters and dungeons, best talk to one of the guards.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_25": "Just ask me for a {trade} to see my offers. Apart from that, I also sell {footballs}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_26": "I really love flowers. My favourites are {honey flowers}. Sadly, they are very rare on this isle. If you can find one for me, I'll give you a little reward.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_27": "You could check out which armors or shields I offer by asking me for a {trade}. Don't be shy!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_28": "Yes, I'm selling that. Simply ask me for a {trade} to view all my offers.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_29": "Well, no gold, no deal. Earn gold by fighting {monsters} and picking up the things they carry. Sell it to {merchants} to make profit!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_30": "He sells {weapons}. However, I can offer you better deals than him!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_31": "I'm glad she stopped selling stuff. There was too much of a competition going on!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_32": "Sometimes, I see him walking outside the village near some hole.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_33": "He dedicated his life to welcome newcomers to this island.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_34": "Poor old woman, her son {Tom} never visits her.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_35": "Al Dee has a general {equipment} store in the north-western part of the village.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_36": "She lives under the {academy}. Always nice to chat with her!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_37": "He's a local farmer. If you need fresh {food} to regain health, it's a good place to go. He's only trading with premium adventurers, though.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_38": "He's a local farmer. If you need fresh {food} to regain your health, it's a good place to go. However, many monsters carry also food such as meat. Or you could simply pick {blueberries}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_39": "Visiting Cipfried in the {temple} is a good idea if you are injured or poisoned. He can heal you.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_40": "She's {Obi's} granddaughter and deals with {armors} and {shields}, just as I do.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_41": "He mostly stays by himself. He's a hermit outside of town - good luck finding him.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_42": "She buys all {blueberries} and {cookies} you can find.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_43": "You can find the oracle on the top floor of the {academy}, just above {Seymour}. Go there when you are level 8 to reach more areas of {Tibia}.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_44": "He is the {bank} clerk, just below the academy.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_45": "Seymour is a teacher running the {academy}. He has a lot of important {information} about Tibia.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_46": "He's the local tanner. You could try selling fresh corpses or leather to him.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_47": "He is a great warrior and our protector.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_48": "Do you want to buy a football for 111 gold?",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_49": "Here you go.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_50": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_51": "Oh, but it's fun to play!",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_52": "Oh, thank you so much! Please take this piece of armor as reward.",
  "npc.lee_delle.stdmod_53": "Honey flowers are my favourites <sighs>.",
  "npc.ferryman_kamil_meluna.stdmod_1": "You want me to transport you and your spouse back to {Fibula}?",
  "npc.ferryman_kamil_meluna.stdmod_2": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.lector.stdmod_1": "I can offer you ham or meat. If you'd like to check the quality of my wares, ask me for a {trade}.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_1": "Would you like to receive that protection for a sacrifice of |BLESSCOST| gold, child?",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_2": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_3": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_4": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_5": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_6": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_7": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_8": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_9": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_10": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_11": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_12": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_13": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.humphrey.stdmod_14": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_1": "I am the mistress of the hunt. At this place you may buy the food our hunts provide.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_2": "Hunting is an art, practiced too often by diletantes. Every fool with a bow or a spear considers himself a hunter.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_3": "Bow, arrow, and spear are the hunters' best friends. In the northeast of the town one of us may sell such tools.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_4": "Hunters live a life of freedom and closeness to nature, unlike a simple farmer or bugherder.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_5": "Nature is not a friend but an unforgiving teacher, and the lessons we have to learn are endless.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_6": "Watch the sky, it will tell you.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_7": "I guess it's a human god for the human sight of nature. I have not much knowledge of this entity.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_8": "If they ever existed they are gone now.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_9": "The Kuridai are too agressive not only to people but also to the enviroment. They lack any understanding of the balance that we know as nature.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_10": "The balance of nature, of course. It's everywhere, so don't ask but observe and learn.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_11": "We try to live in harmony with the forces of nature, may they be living or unliving.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_12": "The humans are a loud and ugly race. They lack any grace and are more kin to the orcs then to us.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_13": "Life and death are significant parts of the balance.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_14": "Life and death are significant parts of the balance.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_15": "I despise their presence in our town, but it may be a necessary evil.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_16": "That is the race to which I belong.",
  "npc.anerui.stdmod_17": "The magic they wield is all that matters to them.",
  "npc.old_adall.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a passage to the ",
  "npc.old_adall.stdmod_2": "Maybe another time.",
  "npc.old_adall.stdmod_3": "I can bring you either to the east end of Port Hope or to the west end of the town, where would you like to go?",
  "npc.nydala.stdmod_1": "Well, as you can see, I sell furniture. Ask me for a {trade} if you're interested to see my wares.",
  "npc.nydala.stdmod_2": "My name is Nydala. I run this store.",
  "npc.nydala.stdmod_3": "It is |TIME|. Do you need a clock for your house?",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_1": "I think the gods are too busy to care about us mortals, hmm... that makes me feel godlike, too.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_2": "I am honored to be the assistant of the great, the illustrious, the magnificent {Durin}!",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_3": "I am honored to be the assistant of the great, the illustrious, the magnificent {Durin}!",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_4": "I have a job of great responsibility, mostly I keep annoying persons away from my boss.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_5": "You better don't ask, you wouldn't like the answer.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_6": "Ah, yes, yes, hail to King {Tibianus}! Long live the king and so on...",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_7": "I overheard a conversation of officials, that magic will be forbidden soon.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_8": "My name is Oswald, but let's proceed, I am a very busy man.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_9": "Hey, I am not a shopkeeper, I am an important man!",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_10": "It is nearly tea time, so please hurry!",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_11": "It's rumoured that Sam does not forge all weapons himself, but buys them from his cousin, who is married to a cyclops.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_12": " If you want to see dungeons just don't pay your taxes.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_13": "It's beyond all doubt that certain sinister elements in our city have certain knowledge about this myth.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_14": "You are not the first one to ask about that. Am I the only one that preferes wine to such disgusting stuff?",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_15": "What do you expect from ex-soldiers? He is nuts! Hacked on the head far too often.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_16": "Isn't he the artist formerly known as the prince?",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_17": "I never found any rumour concerning him, isn't that odd?",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_18": "They say she killed over a dozen husbands already.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_19": "This man lives in the darkness like a rat and is also as handsome as one of them. He surely is up to no good and often consorts with sinister strangers.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_20": "Just last week a one eyed man, who had a room at Frodo's, met him in the middle of the night.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_21": "He sells his scrolls far too expensive.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_22": "I was told he lost a body part or two in duels... if you know what I mean.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_23": "He is rumoured to summon kinky demons to... well you know.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_24": "You know a rumour? TELL ME! TELL ME! TELL ME!",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_25": "Fascinating! Absolutely fascinating!",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_26": "I heard he was a ladies' man in younger days. In our days he is rumoured to wear women clothes now and then.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_27": "A simple shopkeeper with minor intelligence.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_28": "They say he isn't truly dead. He was... or is a necromant after all.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_29": " Some say he is Ferumbras in disguise.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_30": "What a shame. He claimed to be the king of thiefs and was caught stealing some fruit.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_31": "Just between you and me, he can be quite a tyrant.",
  "npc.oswald.stdmod_32": "AHHHH!!! WHERE??? WHERE???",
  "npc.oswald.say_33": "What? So why in the world should I give you an invitation? It's not as if you were someone important, are you?",
  "npc.oswald.say_34": "Well, rich and generous people are always welcome in the palace.If you donate 1000 gold to a fund I oversee, I'll give you an invitation, ok?",
  "npc.oswald.say_35": "Excellent! Here is your invitation!",
  "npc.oswald.say_36": "You don't have enough money.",
  "npc.oswald.say_37": "Not that I am bribeable but I doubt that you own 1000 gold pieces. Or do you?",
  "npc.carlson.stdmod_1": "Do you want to sail ",
  "npc.carlson.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.carlson.stdmod_3": "Where do you want to go? To {Folda}, {Senja} or {Tibia}?",
  "npc.buddel_okolnir.stdmod_1": "No, no, no, you even are no barb....barba...er.. one of us!!!! Talk to the Jarl first!",
  "npc.buddel_okolnir.stdmod_2": "Ohh, you got a nice ring there! Ya don't have to pay if you gimme the ring and I promise you I will bring you to the correct spot!*HICKS* Alright?",
  "npc.buddel_okolnir.stdmod_3": "Give me 50 gold and I bring you to ",
  "npc.buddel_okolnir.stdmod_4": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.buddel_okolnir.stdmod_5": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.buddel_okolnir.stdmod_6": "Where are we at the moment? Is this Svargrond? Ahh yes!*HICKS* Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.junkar_mines.stdmod_1": "Well, then you stay here, simple as that.",
  "npc.junkar_mines.stdmod_2": "Where do you want me to take you? To {Kazordoon}, {Thais} or to {Robsons Isle}?",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_1": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_2": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_3": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_4": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_5": "No problem.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_6": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_7": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_8": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_9": "No problem.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_10": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_11": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_12": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_13": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_14": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_15": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_16": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_17": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_18": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_19": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_20": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_21": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_22": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.lorietta.stdmod_23": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.a_ghostly_sage.stdmod_1": "You will now be travelled out of here. Are you sure that you want to face that teleport?",
  "npc.a_ghostly_sage.stdmod_2": "Then stay here in these ghostly halls.",
  "npc.a_ghostly_sage.stdmod_3": "I can offer you a {teleport}.",
  "npc.a_ghostly_sage.stdmod_4": "Dont mind me.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_1": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_2": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_3": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_4": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_5": "No problem.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_6": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_7": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_8": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_9": "No problem.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_10": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_11": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_12": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_13": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_14": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_15": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_16": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_17": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_18": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_19": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_20": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_21": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_22": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.alia.stdmod_23": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_1": "I'm sorry but I don't sail there.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_2": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_3": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_4": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_5": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_6": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_7": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_8": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_9": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.captain_harava.stdmod_10": "I'm ready to bring you to {Oramond}, {Krailos}, {Venore} or {Darashia}.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_1": "I am the archsorcerer of Carlin. I keep the secrets of our order.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_2": "My name is Lea.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_3": "Sorry, I only sell spells to sorcerers.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_4": "Time is a force we sorcerers will master one day.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_5": "Any sorcerer dedicates his whole life to the study of the arcane arts.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_6": "We sorcerers wield arcane powers beyond comprehension of men.",
  "npc.lea.stdmod_7": "We sorcerers wield arcane powers beyond comprehension of men.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_1": "Would you like to receive that protection for a sacrifice of |BLESSCOST| gold, child?",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_2": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_3": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_4": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_5": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_6": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_7": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_8": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_9": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_10": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_11": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_12": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_13": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.edala.stdmod_14": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a seek a passage to ",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_3": "Where do you want to go? To {Krailos}, {Thais}, {Carlin}, {Ab'Dendriel}, {Venore}, {Port Hope}, {Ankrahmun}, {Liberty Bay}, {Gray Island} or the isle {Cormaya}?",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_4": "Where do you want to go? To {Krailos}, {Thais}, {Carlin}, {Ab'Dendriel}, {Venore}, {Port Hope}, {Ankrahmun}, {Liberty Bay}, {Gray Island} or the isle {Cormaya}?",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_5": "My name is Captain Seahorse from the Royal Tibia Line.",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_6": "This is Edron. Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.captain_seahorse.stdmod_7": "I'm sorry, but we don't serve this route. However, I heard that Wyrdin here in Edron is looking for adventurers to go on a trip to Yalahar for him.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_1": "Never heard about a place like this.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_2": "Do you seek a ride to ",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_3": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_4": "I'm a licensed c...carpet pilot. I can {transport} you t...to a warm p...place.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_5": "I t...{transport} travellers to the continent of Darama for a small fee. It's w...warm there.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_6": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Edron}, to {Kazordoon}, to Z... Zao, to the F...{Femor Hills}, to {Issavi} or to M... {Marapur} if you like. W....Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_7": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Edron}, to {Kazordoon}, to Z... Zao, to the F...{Femor Hills}, to {Issavi} or to M... {Marapur} if you like. W....Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_8": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Edron}, to {Kazordoon}, to Z... Zao, to the F...{Femor Hills}, to {Issavi} or to M... {Marapur} if you like. W....Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_9": "I'm k...known as Iyad Ibn Abdul.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_10": "The thought of s...some mad sorcerer unleashing some f...fire magic is very tempting.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_11": "S...so close and s...still that far away.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_12": "For all its m...mistakes, Thais is warm at least.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_13": "I can fly you to {Darashia}, to {Edron}, to {Kazordoon}, to Z... Zao, to the F...{Femor Hills}, to {Issavi} or to M... {Marapur} if you like. W....Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_14": "I would t...trade it for some firewood.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_15": "This h...here is no continent. This is h...hell.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_16": "Even D...Drefia can't be worse than this land.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_17": "I d...don't care about any n...news unless it's the announcement of a h....heatwave.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_18": "It's p...probably the ice age.",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_19": "Th...there, in case you have {earmuffs}, I pay w...well!",
  "npc.iyad.stdmod_20": "Do you really have earmuffs f...for me?? If so, just ask me for a {trade}!",
  "npc.junkar_robsons.stdmod_1": "Well, then you stay here, simple as that.",
  "npc.junkar_robsons.stdmod_2": "Where do you want me to take you? To {Kazordoon} or to {Thais}? Occasionally we can even reach the {mines} if they are cleared.",
  "npc.lorek.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a passage to ",
  "npc.lorek.stdmod_2": "Maybe another time.",
  "npc.lorek.stdmod_3": "I heard he is some scary magician or so.",
  "npc.lorek.stdmod_4": "I can travel you to west, centre, darama, chor or banuta.",
  "npc.buddel_raider_camp.stdmod_1": "No, no, no, you even are no barb....barba...er.. one of us!!!! Talk to the Jarl first!",
  "npc.buddel_raider_camp.stdmod_2": "Ohh, you got a nice ring there! Ya don't have to pay if you gimme the ring and I promise you I will bring you to the correct spot!*HICKS* Alright?",
  "npc.buddel_raider_camp.stdmod_3": "Give me 50 gold and I bring you to ",
  "npc.buddel_raider_camp.stdmod_4": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.buddel_raider_camp.stdmod_5": "You shouldn't miss the experience.",
  "npc.buddel_raider_camp.stdmod_6": "Where are we at the moment? Is this Svargrond? Ahh yes!*HICKS* Where do you want to go?",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_1": "Alright, I guess you need a stake first. Maybe Gamon can help you, the leg of a chair or something could just do. Try asking him for a stake, and if you have one, bring it back to me.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_2": "I guess you couldn't convince Gamon to give you a stake, eh?",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_3": "Yes, I was informed what to do. Are you prepared to receive my line of the prayer?",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_4": "So receive my prayer: 'Light shall be near - and darkness afar'. Now, bring your stake to Tibra in the Carlin church for the next line of the prayer. I will inform her what to do.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_5": "I will wait for you.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_6": "You should visit Tibra in the Carlin church now.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_7": "You already received my line of the prayer.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_8": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_9": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_10": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_11": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_12": "No problem.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_13": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_14": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_15": "Sorry, you don't have enough money.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_16": "No problem.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_17": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_18": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_19": "Whenever you receive a lethal wound, your vital force is damaged and there is a chance that you lose some of your equipment. With every single of the five {blessings} you have, this damage and chance of loss will be reduced.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_20": "There are five blessings available in five sacred places: the {spiritual} shielding, the spark of the {phoenix}, the {embrace} of Tibia, the fire of the {suns} and the wisdom of {solitude}. Additionally, you can receive the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_21": "I see you received the spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_22": "I can sense that the druids north of Carlin have provided you with the Embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_23": "I can see you received the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_24": "I can sense that the spark of the phoenix already was given to you by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_25": "I can sense you already talked to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya and received this blessing.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_26": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_27": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_28": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_29": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.iptar_sin.stdmod_30": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.captain_jack.stdmod_1": "Do you seek a passage back to Tibia?",
  "npc.captain_jack.stdmod_2": "We would like to serve you some time.",
  "npc.captain_jack.stdmod_3": "I can travel you to {Tibia}.",
  "npc.captain_jack.stdmod_4": "I can travel you to {Tibia}.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_1": "I am able to grant you the heart of the mountain's blessing. But I must ask of you to sacrifice |BLESSCOST| gold. Are you willing to part with that amount of wealth?",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_2": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_3": "You are hurt, my child. I will heal your wounds.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_4": "You aren't looking that bad. Sorry, I can't help you. But if you are looking for additional protection you should go on the {pilgrimage} of ashes or get the protection of the {twist of fate} here.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_5": "Well, as I am quite in a {fix} currently, my only hope to escape this situation may be to grant you {healing} or an {enhanced} blessing if you wish. You must desire SOMETHING, right? Sure you do.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_6": "You can ask for the blessing of spiritual shielding in the whiteflower temple south of Thais.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_7": "You can ask for the blessing of the two suns in the suntower near Ab'Dendriel.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_8": "The spark of the phoenix is given by the dwarven priests of earth and fire in Kazordoon.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_9": "Talk to the hermit Eremo on the isle of Cormaya about this blessing.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_10": "The druids north of Carlin will provide you with the embrace of Tibia.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_11": "I know of a mysterious djinn, bound to an existence of slavery far to the north of Tiquanda's jungles. He is bound to tell you his secrets and offer you the 'blood of the mountain'. ...\nI do not know where exactly but I guess you must first dig that one out to actually talk to him.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_12": "I am one with nature, one with the ice and the cold. Names are of no worth out here. Out here, you face isolation and loneliness. Only your strength, willpower and {training} can keep you alive.",
  "npc.nomad.stdmod_13": "My life is one of hardship, hardship I chose freely. Endurance, strength and the power of the will are my only companions in this frigid wilderness. My strength comes from disciplined training and knowledge of the outdoors.",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_1": "Fine. You are free to decline my offer.",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_2": "Keep your adventurer's stone well.",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_3": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for free?",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_4": "Here you are. Take care.",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_5": "No problem.",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_6": "Ah, you want to replace your adventurer's stone for 30 gold?",
  "npc.prezil.stdmod_7": "Here you are. Take care."
}